PVD("malaysia_ndp_2021-2025",{"docs":["","Malaysia NDP 2021 25","Malaysia NDP 2021 25 1"],"s":{"1":[[1,"328","4","OGSE Industry Blueprint Establishment","Establishment of OGSE Industry Blueprint",""],[1,"329","1","Oil and Gas Industry Growth Support","This will include ensuring the healthy growth of the oil and gas industry.",""],[1,"329","8","Domestic Oil and Gas Subsector Development Initiatives","Several initiatives will be implemented to ensure progressive and sustainable development of the domestic oil and gas subsector.",""],[1,"329","8","Domestic Fuel Use Prioritisation Policy","The use of domestically produced petrol and diesel will be prioritised",""],[1,"329","8","Petrochemical High-Value Investment Promotion","high value investment in the petrochemical industry be promoted",""],[1,"329","8","Biofuel Usage Scale-Up","biofuel usage be scaled-up",""],[1,"329","8","Local Oil and Gas Services Company Capacity Enhancement","the capabilities of local OGSE companies will be enhanced",""],[1,"329","8","Natural Gas Roadmap Development","a natural gas roadmap will be developed",""],[1,"330","1","Local Petrol and Diesel Utilisation Prioritisation Mechanism","Efforts will be undertaken to develop a mechanism to prioritise the utilisation of locally produced petrol and diesel through engagement with stakeholders.",""],[1,"330","2","Petrochemical Industry Repositioning Initiative","The petrochemical industry will be repositioned to be more competitive and sustainable to attract and spur quality investments as well as reduce dependency on imported products.",""],[1,"330","2","Chemical Industry Roadmap Development","A chemical industry roadmap will be developed to ensure that the industry will leverage technology and innovation as well as establish a conducive ecosystem to produce specialty products.",""],[1,"330","2","Petrochemical Industry Readiness Assessment","Consequently, the industry readiness will be assessed in terms of infrastructure, feedstock and skilled workforce availability as well as R&D capability.",""],[1,"330","4","OGSE SME Capability Enhancement Programme","Concerted efforts will be undertaken to enhance the capability of local OGSE small and medium enterprises through establishing consortia, increasing collaborations and promoting strategic partnerships.",""],[1,"330","5","Comprehensive Natural Gas Roadmap Development","A comprehensive natural gas roadmap will be developed for this purpose to provide medium- and long-term directions, focusing on liberalising the gas market and increasing domestic gas demand.",""],[1,"330","5","Malaysia Gas Market Hub Strategy Study","A study will be carried out to formulate strategies in developing Malaysia as a gas market hub for the region, to attract new suppliers and increase competitiveness.",""],[2,"109","6","National Agricommodity Policy 2021-2030","The National Agricommodity Policy 2021-2030 (DAKN2030) is also being formulated to provide a new direction and targets to increase productivity, enhance downstream activities and promote the growth of new industries.",""],[2,"109","7","Natural Gas Industry Roadmap","A roadmap will be developed to chart the direction of the natural gas industry in optimising demand growth, ensuring security of supply and liberalising the market to enhance efficiency and competitiveness.",""],[2,"109","7","Gas Subsector Strategy for Regional Trading Hub Development","In addition, efforts will be undertaken to formulate strategies in capitalising potential of the gas subsector to position Malaysia as a regional gas trading hub.",""],[2,"329","8","Domestic Oil and Gas Subsector Development Initiatives","Several initiatives will be implemented to ensure progressive and sustainable development of the domestic oil and gas subsector.",""],[2,"329","8","Domestic Fuel Use Prioritisation Policy","The use of domestically produced petrol and diesel will be prioritised",""],[2,"329","8","Petrochemical High-Value Investment Promotion","high value investment in the petrochemical industry be promoted",""],[2,"329","8","Biofuel Usage Scale-Up","biofuel usage be scaled-up",""],[2,"329","8","Local OGSE Capacity Enhancement Programme","the capabilities of local OGSE companies will be enhanced",""],[2,"329","8","Natural Gas Roadmap Development","a natural gas roadmap will be developed",""],[2,"330","1","Local Fuel Utilisation Prioritisation Mechanism","Efforts will be undertaken to develop a mechanism to prioritise the utilisation of locally produced petrol and diesel through engagement with stakeholders.",""],[2,"330","2","Petrochemical Industry Repositioning Initiative","The petrochemical industry will be repositioned to be more competitive and sustainable to attract and spur quality investments as well as reduce dependency on imported products.",""],[2,"330","2","Chemical Industry Roadmap Development","A chemical industry roadmap will be developed to ensure that the industry will leverage technology and innovation as well as establish a conducive ecosystem to produce specialty products.",""],[2,"330","2","Petrochemical Industry Readiness Assessment","Consequently, the industry readiness will be assessed in terms of infrastructure, feedstock and skilled workforce availability as well as R&D capability.",""],[2,"330","4","Local OGSE SME Capability Enhancement Programme","Concerted efforts will be undertaken to enhance the capability of local OGSE small and medium enterprises through establishing consortia, increasing collaborations and promoting strategic partnerships.",""],[2,"330","5","Natural Gas Market Liberalisation and Roadmap Development","Malaysia is liberalising the gas market to create a sustainable gas industry and ensure the security of supply to become a regional gas market hub.",""],[2,"330","5","Gas Market Hub Strategy Study","A study will be carried out to formulate strategies in developing Malaysia as a gas market hub for the region, to attract new suppliers and increase competitiveness.",""]],"2":[[1,"23","3","Public Service Strengthening","Four catalytic policy enablers, namely developing future talent, accelerating technology adoption and innovation, enhancing connectivity and transport infrastructure as well as strengthening the public service will support the achievement of these themes.",""],[1,"33","8","Public Sector Digitalisation and Citizen-Centric Decision-Making","The public sector will further intensify digitalisation, citizen- centric decision-making, project implementation as well as collaboration and coordination between the three levels of government.",""],[1,"33","8","Public Sector Strengthening for Integrity and Transparency","In recognition of the current gaps in talent, governance ecosystem and project management, the public sector will be further strengthened with emphasis on integrity and transparency.",""],[1,"33","8","High-Performing Civil Service and Whole-of-Government Reform","In the Twelfth Plan, priorities will be given on developing a high-performing civil service, advancing the whole- of-government approach as well as enhancing budgeting and project management.",""],[1,"33","9","Whole-of-Government Public Service Transformation","Transforming the public service through the whole-of-government approach will be the game changer in ensuring a more efficient and effective public service delivery as well as optimising existing resources.",""],[1,"33","9","Public Service Leadership and Recruitment Improvement","In addition, enhancing the mechanism for selection of key leaders, improving the mechanism for recruitment of the professional and managerial officers as well as accelerating digitalisation will further enhance public service delivery.",""],[1,"33","9","Online Federal Government Service Digitalisation Target","The implementation of this policy enabler, among others, will improve Malaysia's performance to be among the top 30 in the Corruption Perceptions Index and top nine in the Government Efficiency sub-index of the IMD World Competitiveness Yearbook as well as ensure 80% of online Federal Government services will be available end-to-end by 2025.",""],[1,"38","6","Civil Service Institutional Streamlining and Governance Reform","The structures and functions of ministries and agencies will be reviewed and streamlined to establish a flatter organisation, thus reducing bureaucracy, increasing transparency as well as optimising the use of resources.",""],[1,"38","6","Public Service Act for Separation of Powers","A public service act will be introduced to reinforce the principle of separation of powers between the executive, legislative and judicial branches.",""],[1,"38","6","Civil Service Performance and Leadership Selection Reform","The Government will further enhance the performance-driven culture in the civil service as well as strengthen the mechanism for the selection of key leaders.",""],[1,"38","6","Professional and Managerial Officer Recruitment Improvement","The mechanism for recruitment of the professional and managerial officers will also be improved in attracting the best talent.",""],[1,"38","6","Public Sector Digitalisation and Malaysia Digital Economy Blueprint Implementation","accelerating digitalisation and implementation of the Malaysia Digital Economy Blueprint initiatives in the public sector will further enhance the public service delivery.",""],[1,"394","3","Public Sector Digital Transformation","Drive digital transformation in the public sector",""],[1,"395","3","MAMPU Digital Transformation Leadership Reform","The Malaysian Administrative Modernisation and Management Planning Unit (MAMPU) as the key agency will be transformed to respond proactively and drive the national digital agenda in the public sector.",""],[1,"395","3","National Digital Transformation Policy and Systems Development","MAMPU will formulate policies and strategies as well as propose nationwide systems and tools relating to digital transformation, for both Federal and state governments.",""],[1,"408","5","Government Digital Infrastructure and Tools Modernisation","Digital infrastructure and tools for modernisation of government operations and processes will be improved to ensure effective service delivery.",""],[1,"408","5","Civil Service Data Analytics and Technical Skills Development","Efforts will be intensified to develop interdisciplinary technical knowledge and data analytics skills of civil servants.",""],[1,"408","5","4IR Technology Integration in Public Services","Focus will also be given to embed 4IR technologies in healthcare services, public transport services as well as disaster management and prevention to improve the quality of life of the rakyat.",""],[2,"346","2","Public Sector Digitalisation and Malaysia Digital Economy Blueprint Implementation","accelerating digitalisation and implementation of the Malaysia Digital Economy Blueprint initiatives in the public sector will further enhance public service delivery.",""],[2,"351","7","Digital Technology Adoption Acceleration","Accelerate the adoption of digital technology.",""],[2,"351","15","Public Sector Digitalisation Acceleration","Accelerating digitalisation in the public sector.",""],[2,"393","2","Digital Governance Streamlining and Cybersecurity Strengthening","Measures will be undertaken to streamline digital governance, accelerate trade through eCommerce, expand the sharing economy and strengthen cyber security.",""],[2,"394","3","Public Sector Digital Transformation","Drive digital transformation in the public sector",""],[2,"395","1","National Digital Economy and 4IR Council Coordination Mechanism","The implementation of digital initiatives will be led by the National Digital Economy and 4IR Council.",""],[2,"395","2","Strategic Change Management Office for Digitalisation","The National Digital Economy and 4IR Council will be supported by the Strategic Change Management Office (SCMO) as a special entity to lead national level change management.",""],[2,"395","3","MAMPU Transformation for Public Sector Digital Agenda","The Malaysian Administrative Modernisation and Management Planning Unit (MAMPU) as the key agency will be transformed to respond proactively and drive the national digital agenda in the public sector.",""],[2,"395","3","National Digital Transformation Policy and Systems Development","MAMPU will formulate policies and strategies as well as propose nationwide systems and tools relating to digital transformation, for both Federal and state governments.",""],[2,"395","4","Trusted Government-Private Data Sharing Platform","A trusted platform for data sharing between the government and the private sectors as well as among government agencies will be developed to enable data-driven decision making.",""],[2,"395","5","Data Governance Strengthening Initiative","A lead body will be identified to enhance data governance including the development of big data analytics infrastructure, data security and human capital.",""],[2,"400","5","Digital Governance and Data Integration Improvement","Data integration and privacy will be improved for a more efficient service delivery.",""],[2,"400","6","Data Sharing Policy for Digitalisation","A policy on data sharing will be formulated to improve the decision-making process, while protecting data privacy.",""],[2,"400","6","Inter-Stakeholder Data Synchronisation and Sharing Mechanism","Data will be synchronised and shared among different stakeholders to promote data-driven activities including evidence-based decision making.",""],[2,"400","6","Targeted Socioeconomic Programme Delivery Mechanism","This will facilitate the targeted mechanisms for socioeconomic programmes as well as reduce inclusion and exclusion errors.",""],[2,"408","5","Government Digital Infrastructure and Tools Upgrade","Digital infrastructure and tools for modernisation of government operations and processes will be improved to ensure effective service delivery.",""],[2,"408","5","Civil Service Data Analytics and Technical Skills Development","Efforts will be intensified to develop interdisciplinary technical knowledge and data analytics skills of civil servants.",""],[2,"408","5","4IR Integration in Public Services","Focus will also be given to embed 4IR technologies in healthcare services, public transport services as well as disaster management and prevention to improve the quality of life of the rakyat.",""]],"3":[[1,"345","2","Whole-of-Government Coordination Enhancement","In addressing these issues, the adoption of the whole-of-government approach will be enhanced through better collaboration among Federal Government, state governments and local authorities to ensure the alignment of development priorities.",""],[1,"345","3","Public Service Transformation and Future Leaders Development","In the Twelfth Plan, the public service will be transformed and future leaders in the civil service will be developed.",""],[1,"345","3","Whole-of-Government Administrative Efficiency Enhancement","The whole-of-government approach will be enhanced in improving government administration and operational efficiency, enabling",""],[1,"346","1","Governance Ecosystem Strengthening","better decision-making and innovation as well as strengthening the governance ecosystem.",""],[1,"346","1","Budgeting Framework and Project Implementation Improvement","project management and budgeting will be improved by reviewing the budgeting framework and processes as well as improving the effectiveness of project implementation.",""],[1,"346","2","Public Service Structural Streamlining and Bureaucracy Reduction","the structures and functions of ministries and agencies will be reviewed and streamlined to establish a flatter organisation and reduce bureaucracy in the government administration.",""],[1,"346","2","Public Service Act for Clear Separation of Powers","A public service act will be introduced to ensure a clear demarcation of powers between Members of the Administration and civil servants.",""],[1,"346","2","Leadership Selection and Professional Recruitment Improvement","strengthening the mechanism for the selection of key leaders will improve the overall performance of the public service.",""],[1,"351","5","Clarification of Roles and Responsibilities Between Political Leaders and Civil Servants","Ensure the delineation of roles and responsibilities between Members of the Administration and civil servants.",""],[1,"351","6","Key Leader Selection Mechanism Strengthening","Strengthen the mechanism for the selection of key leaders in ensuring a more effective public service delivery.",""],[1,"351","8","Whole-of-Government Civil Service Strengthening","Strengthen the civil service through the whole-of-government approach.",""],[1,"351","11","Public Sector Administrative Streamlining Reform","Reviewing and streamlining structures and functions of ministries and agencies to establish a flatter organisation, reduce bureaucracy, increase transparency and optimise the use of resources.",""],[1,"351","12","Public Service Act for Checks and Balances","Introducing a public service act to ensure more effective checks and balances between executive, legislative and judicial powers.",""],[1,"351","13","Key Leader Selection Mechanism Strengthening","Strengthening the mechanism for the selection of key leaders.",""],[1,"351","14","Professional and Managerial Officer Recruitment Mechanism Improvement","Improving the mechanism for recruitment of professional and managerial officers in various schemes in attracting the best talents.",""],[1,"351","22","Civil Service Resource Optimization and Rights Preservation","Optimisation of existing resources as well as preservation of rights and obligations of civil servants.",""],[2,"345","2","Whole-of-Government Coordination Enhancement","In addressing these issues, the adoption of the whole-of-government approach will be enhanced through better collaboration among Federal Government, state governments and local authorities to ensure the alignment of development priorities.",""],[2,"345","3","Public Service Transformation and Future Leaders Development","In the Twelfth Plan, the public service will be transformed and future leaders in the civil service will be developed.",""],[2,"345","3","Whole-of-Government Administrative Efficiency Enhancement","The whole-of-government approach will be enhanced in improving government administration and operational efficiency, enabling",""],[2,"346","1","Project Management and Budgeting Improvement Reform","project management and budgeting will be improved by reviewing the budgeting framework and processes as well as improving the effectiveness of project implementation.",""],[2,"351","3","Public Service Delivery Efficiency Improvement","Ensure an efficient and effective public service delivery.",""],[2,"351","8","Whole-of-Government Civil Service Strengthening","Strengthen the civil service through the whole-of-government approach.",""]],"4":[[1,"430","2","Public Sector Service Delivery Strengthening","In this regard, efforts to strengthen public sector service delivery will focus on developing a high-performing civil service, advancing the whole-of-government approach as well as enhancing budgeting and project management.",""],[1,"437","6","High-Performing Civil Service Development","Moving forward, priority will be given to developing a high-performing civil service, advancing the whole-of-government approach as well as enhancing budgeting and project management.",""],[1,"437","6","Whole-of-Government Coordination Approach","Moving forward, priority will be given to developing a high-performing civil service, advancing the whole-of-government approach as well as enhancing budgeting and project management.",""],[1,"437","6","Budgeting and Project Management Enhancement","Moving forward, priority will be given to developing a high-performing civil service, advancing the whole-of-government approach as well as enhancing budgeting and project management.",""],[1,"440","1","Public Service Transformation and Civil Servant Leadership Development","focus will be given to develop high performing civil servants by transforming the public service and developing high calibre future leaders.",""],[1,"440","4","Human Resource Management Enhancement","human resource management will be enhanced",""],[1,"440","4","Central Agency Capacity and Capability Strengthening","the capacity and capability of central agencies will be strengthened",""],[1,"440","8","Public Service Transformation and Service Delivery Enhancement","Malaysia to transform the public service as well as enhance service delivery.","JPA | Malaysian Administrative Modernisation and Management Planning Unit (MAMPU) | Ministry of Finance (MOF) | Economic Planning Unit (EPU)"],[1,"442","5","Whole-of-Government Public Service Transformation","efforts will be undertaken to transform the public service through whole-of-government approach.",""],[1,"442","5","Public Sector Process and Systems Strengthening","The public sector will continue to be strengthened by improving processes and systems.",""],[1,"442","5","Government Administration and Service Delivery Improvement","Focus will be on improving government administration and efficiency of delivery, promoting better decision-making and innovation as well as strengthening the governance ecosystem.",""],[1,"442","9","Government Administration and Institutional Structure Improvement","government administration and institutional structure will be improved",""],[1,"442","9","Public Service Delivery Enhancement","public service delivery will be enhanced",""],[1,"443","2","Public Service Administrative Streamlining and Digitalisation","A flatter structure of administration will reduce bureaucracy, improve communication and promote a rakyat-centric and customer-focused culture.",""],[1,"443","2","Review and Streamlining of Ministry and Agency Functions","Structures and functions of ministries and agencies will be reviewed and streamlined to optimise resource allocation and enhance efficiency of the public service.",""],[1,"443","2","Special Committee on Overlapping Government Structures","In this regard, a special committee to coordinate and minimise various overlapping structures and functions between ministries and agencies will be established.",""],[1,"443","2","Public Service Sandbox","Meanwhile, the public service sandbox will be introduced to enhance innovation and produce solutions for better public service delivery.",""],[1,"449","1","Public Sector Reform Programme","In the Twelfth Plan, a number of reforms will be undertaken in the public sector to improve delivery.",""],[1,"449","1","High-Performing Civil Service Development","These include nurturing a high-performing civil service, advancing a whole-of-government approach as well as enhancing budgeting and project management.",""],[1,"449","1","Whole-of-Government Coordination Approach","These include nurturing a high-performing civil service, advancing a whole-of-government approach as well as enhancing budgeting and project management.",""],[1,"449","1","Budgeting and Project Management Enhancement","These include nurturing a high-performing civil service, advancing a whole-of-government approach as well as enhancing budgeting and project management.",""],[1,"454","5","Public Service Transformation","the public service will be transformed by further improving the mechanism for the selection of new officers and key leaders.",""],[1,"454","5","Public Service Coordination and Role Streamlining","Collaboration and coordination will be enhanced to streamline the public service, avoid duplication of roles and optimise resources.",""],[2,"33","8","Public Sector Digitalisation and Citizen-Centric Decision-Making","The public sector will further intensify digitalisation, citizen- centric decision-making, project implementation as well as collaboration and coordination between the three levels of government.",""],[2,"33","8","High-Performing Civil Service and Whole-of-Government Reform","In the Twelfth Plan, priorities will be given on developing a high-performing civil service, advancing the whole- of-government approach as well as enhancing budgeting and project management.",""],[2,"33","9","Whole-of-Government Public Service Transformation","Transforming the public service through the whole-of-government approach will be the game changer in ensuring a more efficient and effective public service delivery as well as optimising existing resources.",""],[2,"33","9","End-to-End Online Federal Government Services Expansion","The implementation of this policy enabler, among others, will improve Malaysia's performance to be among the top 30 in the Corruption Perceptions Index and top nine in the Government Efficiency sub-index of the IMD World Competitiveness Yearbook as well as ensure 80% of online Federal Government services will be available end-to-end by 2025.",""],[2,"38","6","Civil Service Governance and Streamlining Reform","The structures and functions of ministries and agencies will be reviewed and streamlined to establish a flatter organisation, thus reducing bureaucracy, increasing transparency as well as optimising the use of resources.",""],[2,"430","2","Public Sector Service Delivery Strengthening","In this regard, efforts to strengthen public sector service delivery will focus on developing a high-performing civil service, advancing the whole-of-government approach as well as enhancing budgeting and project management.",""],[2,"434","7","Public Sector Delivery Improvement Initiatives","Initiatives to enhance public sector delivery were focused on the improvement of talent, work processes, evaluation system, and work-life balance.",""],[2,"434","7","Government Service Digitalisation Expansion","Access to government services was expanded through enhancement of digitalisation, including at the local authority level.",""],[2,"437","6","High-Performing Civil Service Development","Moving forward, priority will be given to developing a high-performing civil service, advancing the whole-of-government approach as well as enhancing budgeting and project management.",""],[2,"437","6","Whole-of-Government Approach Advancement","Moving forward, priority will be given to developing a high-performing civil service, advancing the whole-of-government approach as well as enhancing budgeting and project management.",""],[2,"437","6","Budgeting and Project Management Enhancement","Moving forward, priority will be given to developing a high-performing civil service, advancing the whole-of-government approach as well as enhancing budgeting and project management.",""],[2,"440","8","Public Service Transformation and Service Delivery Enhancement","The transition towards a high-income economy requires Malaysia to transform the public service as well as enhance service delivery.",""],[2,"440","8","Public Service Support Ecosystem Strengthening","the ecosystem that supports an excellent public service, which includes human resources, work processes, technology, and financial resources need to be further strengthened.",""],[2,"440","8","Enhanced Central Agency Leadership for Public Sector Transformation","The role of central agencies, namely JPA, Malaysian Administrative Modernisation and Management Planning Unit (MAMPU), Ministry of Finance (MOF) and Economic Planning Unit (EPU) will be enhanced to effectively drive public sector transformation and ensure optimisation of resources.","JPA | Malaysian Administrative Modernisation and Management Planning Unit (MAMPU) | Ministry of Finance (MOF) | Economic Planning Unit (EPU)"],[2,"442","5","Whole-of-Government Public Service Transformation","efforts will be undertaken to transform the public service through whole-of-government approach.",""],[2,"442","5","Public Sector Process and Systems Strengthening","The public sector will continue to be strengthened by improving processes and systems.",""],[2,"442","5","Government Administration and Service Delivery Improvement","Focus will be on improving government administration and efficiency of delivery, promoting better decision-making and innovation as well as strengthening the governance ecosystem.",""],[2,"443","2","Public Service Administrative Streamlining and Digitalisation","A flatter structure of administration will reduce bureaucracy, improve communication and promote a rakyat-centric and customer-focused culture.",""],[2,"443","2","Inter-Ministerial Coordination Committee","a special committee to coordinate and minimise various overlapping structures and functions between ministries and agencies will be established.",""],[2,"443","2","Public Service Sandbox","the public service sandbox will be introduced to enhance innovation and produce solutions for better public service delivery.",""],[2,"449","1","Public Sector Reform Programme","In the Twelfth Plan, a number of reforms will be undertaken in the public sector to improve delivery.",""],[2,"449","1","High-Performing Civil Service Development","These include nurturing a high-performing civil service, advancing a whole-of-government approach as well as enhancing budgeting and project management.",""],[2,"449","1","Whole-of-Government Coordination Approach","These include nurturing a high-performing civil service, advancing a whole-of-government approach as well as enhancing budgeting and project management.",""],[2,"449","1","Budgeting and Project Management Enhancement","These include nurturing a high-performing civil service, advancing a whole-of-government approach as well as enhancing budgeting and project management.",""],[2,"454","5","Public Service Coordination and Role Streamlining Initiative","Collaboration and coordination will be enhanced to streamline the public service, avoid duplication of roles and optimise resources",""]],"5":[[1,"434","7","Public Sector Delivery Improvement Initiatives","Initiatives to enhance public sector delivery were focused on the improvement of talent, work processes, evaluation system, and work-life balance.",""],[1,"434","7","Public Sector Recruitment Process Improvement","efforts continued to be undertaken in improving the recruitment process to ensure talent selected is competent and possess the highest levels of integrity.",""],[1,"434","7","Ministry and Agency Talent Development Guidelines","A guideline was introduced to empower ministries and agencies to design talent development programmes based on needs and priorities.",""],[1,"434","7","Full-Pay Study Leave and Scholarship Programme","Continuous learning and capacity building among employees under the support group were encouraged through the introduction of a full-pay study leave with scholarship programme in 2017.",""],[1,"434","8","MyPortfolio Public Service Role Clarification System","The competencies of the public service was further enhanced with the introduction of MyPortfolio in 2018, as a reference document that contains, among others, job description, work processes and organisation structure.",""],[1,"434","8","Public Service Human Resource Management Policy Enhancement","Meanwhile, the improved Public Service Human Resource Management Policy enables ministries and agencies to customise performance evaluation based on the respective ministerial roles and functions.",""],[1,"434","8","MyPerformance Decentralised Performance Evaluation System","A new performance evaluation system, known as MyPerformance, was piloted at the Public Service Department (JPA) and the Public Works Department (JKR) in 2018.",""],[1,"440","6","Public Service Reform for Talent Attraction and Retention","reforms to create a more efficient and effective public service in better meeting public expectations.",""],[1,"440","7","Civil Servant Training Module Enhancement","Moving forward, the training modules for civil servants will be further improved to ensure civil servants possess the traits of excellence required in effectively managing domestic and global challenges.",""],[1,"440","7","Civil Servant Digital Literacy Initiative","With the acceleration of digital adoption, every civil servant is expected to be digitally literate by 2025.",""],[1,"440","9","Civil Service Talent Nurturing and Retention Programme","efforts will be intensified to nurture and retain top talent in the civil service.",""],[1,"440","10","Public Sector Talent Strengthening Reform","Talent in the public sector will be strengthened through improved recruitment procedures and retaining competent personnel.",""],[1,"441","1","Single-Window Public Service Recruitment Platform","a single-window recruitment platform for the public service will be developed to better coordinate recruitment systems.",""],[1,"441","1","Enhanced Civil Service Psychological Assessment Tool","The psychological assessment tool will also be enhanced to include integrity and competency evaluation components for all service schemes.",""],[1,"441","3","Priority Recruitment and Workplace Accommodation for Persons with Disabilities","PWDs will be given priority for a number of job categories in the recruitment process, consistent with the government policy of providing equal opportunities for all.",""],[1,"441","4","Public Sector Performance Appraisal Expansion","The MyPerformance system, which includes a 360-degree evaluation mechanism1 will be expanded across the public sector to improve the performance appraisal of civil servants, particularly at the management and professional levels.",""],[1,"441","4","Performance-Based Civil Service Promotion and Appointment Reform","This appraisal system will provide the basis for promotion as well as appointments to specialised positions that require skills and experience in critical areas.",""],[1,"441","4","Performance-Based Remuneration Enhancement","The existing remuneration system will be enhanced to provide better performance-based reward packages that are customised to the specific schemes of service.",""],[1,"441","4","Civil Service Exit Policy Improvement","the exit policy mechanism will be further improved to address the issue of low performance and promote a high performing culture in the public sector.",""],[1,"441","4","Public Pension Scheme Sustainability Review","The pension scheme will also be reviewed to be more sustainable.",""],[1,"441","5","Civil Service Leadership Selection Mechanism Strengthening","the mechanism for selection of civil servants with outstanding leadership skills and personality traits to lead ministries and agencies will be strengthened.",""],[1,"441","5","Professional and Managerial Officer Recruitment Improvement","The mechanism of recruiting professional and managerial officers in various schemes of service will be improved to attract the best talent from various backgrounds as well as to enhance public service excellence.",""],[1,"441","5","Future Leaders Development Training Programme","existing programmes to nurture future leaders such as the advanced professional development training will be strengthened.",""],[1,"441","6","Civil Service Values and Ethics Training","The good values, patriotism and preparedness to serve beyond expectations will be instilled in the early stages of recruitment and periodically through-out the service.",""],[1,"441","7","Enhanced Human Resource Development Programme for Civil Servants","the enhanced HRDP will be implemented to produce agile, resilient, creative, knowledgeable, and digitally skilled civil servants, who possess innovative and future-thinking skills.",""],[1,"441","7","Human Resource Management Information System Talent Repository Enhancement","the Human Resource Management Information System (HRMIS) will be enhanced with a sub-module on talent repository that incorporates the skills and expertise of civil servants.",""],[1,"442","3","Specialised Expert Development Programmes","More programmes will be undertaken to produce experts in specialised areas, such as in economic planning, finance, international relations and negotiations, procurement as well as project planning and management.",""],[1,"442","3","Customised Training and Secondment Programme","customised training and secondment programmes will be provided to enhance exposure and enable these personnel to acquire technical skills in the relevant areas.",""],[1,"442","3","Public-Private Cross-Fertilisation Programme","cross-fertilisation programmes between public and private sector personnel will be expanded to broaden knowledge-sharing and develop subject matter experts.",""],[1,"442","4","Civil Service Future-Readiness Training Programme","Appropriate training will be provided to enable civil servants to be future-ready especially in performing new tasks and responsibilities arising from the advancement of technology.",""],[1,"442","4","Centralised Civil Service Upskilling Coordination Platform","all existing upskilling and reskilling training initiatives by different agencies will be regulated and coordinated by a single agency using a centralised platform.",""],[1,"443","1","Public Service Act","A public service act will be introduced to ensure more effective checks and balances between executive, legislative and judicial powers.",""],[1,"443","3","Secretaries General KPI Improvement","The key performance indicators (KPIs) of Secretaries General will be improved to enhance the effectiveness of programmes and project implementation as well as to ensure efficiency of the public service delivery.",""],[1,"443","3","Malaysian Government Performance Index Evaluation","In achieving good governance, the organisational management and digitalisation of services by ministries will be evaluated through the Malaysian Government Performance Index (MyGPI).",""],[1,"443","3","SPB-PBT Indicator Expansion for Local Authorities","In addition, indicators in the SPB-PBT related to licensing, finance, enforcement and complaints will be expanded to provide vital information to local authorities in improving service delivery.",""],[1,"454","5","Public Service Digitalisation Infrastructure Upgrade","Digitalisation in the public service will be intensified by providing adequate infrastructure.",""],[1,"454","5","Public Service Act Introduction","The delineation of roles between Members of the Administration and civil servants through the introduction of Public Service Act will ensure integrity, accountability and transparency in public service delivery.",""],[2,"33","9","Public Service Leadership and Recruitment Reform","In addition, enhancing the mechanism for selection of key leaders, improving the mechanism for recruitment of the professional and managerial officers as well as accelerating digitalisation will further enhance public service delivery.",""],[2,"38","6","Public Service Act","A public service act will be introduced to reinforce the principle of separation of powers between the executive, legislative and judicial branches.",""],[2,"38","6","Civil Service Performance and Leadership Selection Reform","The Government will further enhance the performance-driven culture in the civil service as well as strengthen the mechanism for the selection of key leaders.",""],[2,"38","6","Professional and Managerial Officer Recruitment Improvement","The mechanism for recruitment of the professional and managerial officers will also be improved in attracting the best talent.",""],[2,"434","8","MyPortfolio Public Service Role Clarification System","The competencies of the public service was further enhanced with the introduction of MyPortfolio in 2018, as a reference document that contains, among others, job description, work processes and organisation structure.",""],[2,"434","8","Public Service Human Resource Management Policy Enhancement","Meanwhile, the improved Public Service Human Resource Management Policy enables ministries and agencies to customise performance evaluation based on the respective ministerial roles and functions.",""],[2,"434","8","MyPerformance Decentralised Performance Evaluation System","A new performance evaluation system, known as MyPerformance, was piloted at the Public Service Department (JPA) and the Public Works Department (JKR) in 2018.",""],[2,"440","1","Public Service Transformation and Civil Servant Leadership Development","focus will be given to develop high performing civil servants by transforming the public service and developing high calibre future leaders.",""],[2,"440","4","Public Service Human Resource Management Enhancement","human resource management will be enhanced",""],[2,"440","4","Central Agencies Capacity and Capability Strengthening","the capacity and capability of central agencies will be strengthened",""],[2,"440","6","Public Service Reform for Talent Attraction and Retention","reforms to create a more efficient and effective public service in better meeting public expectations.",""],[2,"440","9","Civil Service Talent Nurturing and Retention Programme","efforts will be intensified to nurture and retain top talent in the civil service.",""],[2,"440","10","Public Sector Talent Strengthening Reform","Talent in the public sector will be strengthened through improved recruitment procedures and retaining competent personnel.",""],[2,"441","1","Single-Window Public Service Recruitment Platform","a single-window recruitment platform for the public service will be developed to better coordinate recruitment systems.",""],[2,"441","1","Enhanced Psychological Assessment for Civil Service Recruitment","The psychological assessment tool will also be enhanced to include integrity and competency evaluation components for all service schemes.",""],[2,"441","3","Priority Recruitment and Workplace Accessibility for Persons with Disabilities","PWDs will be given priority for a number of job categories in the recruitment process, consistent with the government policy of providing equal opportunities for all.",""],[2,"441","4","Public Sector Performance Appraisal Expansion","The MyPerformance system, which includes a 360-degree evaluation mechanism1 will be expanded across the public sector to improve the performance appraisal of civil servants, particularly at the management and professional levels.",""],[2,"441","4","Performance-Based Civil Service Remuneration Reform","The existing remuneration system will be enhanced to provide better performance-based reward packages that are customised to the specific schemes of service.",""],[2,"441","4","Civil Service Exit Policy Improvement","the exit policy mechanism will be further improved to address the issue of low performance and promote a high performing culture in the public sector.",""],[2,"441","4","Public Pension Scheme Sustainability Review","The pension scheme will also be reviewed to be more sustainable.",""],[2,"441","5","Strengthening Civil Service Leadership Selection Mechanism","the mechanism for selection of civil servants with outstanding leadership skills and personality traits to lead ministries and agencies will be strengthened",""],[2,"441","5","Recruitment Reform for Professional and Managerial Officers","The mechanism of recruiting professional and managerial officers in various schemes of service will be improved to attract the best talent from various backgrounds as well as to enhance public service excellence",""],[2,"441","7","Enhanced Human Resource Development Programme for Civil Servants","the enhanced HRDP will be implemented to produce agile, resilient, creative, knowledgeable, and digitally skilled civil servants, who possess innovative and future-thinking skills.",""],[2,"441","7","Human Resource Management Information System Talent Repository Enhancement","the Human Resource Management Information System (HRMIS) will be enhanced with a sub-module on talent repository that incorporates the skills and expertise of civil servants.",""],[2,"454","5","Public Service Recruitment and Leadership Selection Reform","the public service will be transformed by further improving the mechanism for the selection of new officers and key leaders",""],[2,"454","5","Public Service Digitalisation Infrastructure Upgrade","Digitalisation in the public service will be intensified by providing adequate infrastructure",""]],"6":[[1,"36","5","Basic Development Projects","Examples of Basic DE projects are construction of schools, hospitals, roads, industrial areas and poverty eradication programmes.",""],[1,"75","1","Governance Improvement and Policy and Legislation Development","the strengthening of the country's economic foundation will be supported by improvement in overall governance and the development of comprehensive policies and legislations",""],[1,"82","2","Governance and Policy Improvement Reform","the focus will be on boosting productivity mainly through ... improving governance and policy.",""],[1,"82","2","Economic Sector Transformation Implementation Mechanism","Efforts to rejuvenate the economic sectors also require a major shift in approach and implementation mechanism that will transform the sectors and improve the performance of the economy.",""],[1,"90","7","Governance and Policy Improvement Measures","This will be achieved by boosting productivity growth, expanding exports markets, strengthening the effectiveness of financial intermediation ecosystem, enhancing the role of industrial estates and food production areas as well as improving governance and policy.",""],[1,"94","7","Evidence-Based Policy Making Promotion","Evidence-based policy (EBP) making will be promoted including, establishing a user-friendly data sharing framework.",""],[1,"94","7","Programme Evaluation and Monitoring Improvement","In addition, programme evaluation and monitoring will be improved to increase the effectiveness of productivity initiatives.",""],[1,"94","8","Evidence-Based Policy Adoption","The adoption of EBP approach will enhance the effectiveness of policies and programmes by leveraging available research and studies.",""],[1,"94","8","Productivity Research Network","The adoption of EBP will be supported by establishing a dedicated network to facilitate research on productivity.",""],[1,"94","8","Microdata Compilation and Data-Sharing Framework","In addition, the compilation of microdata will be strengthened, including developing a linked employer-employee dataset, to better identify the diverse and pertinent factors which stifle enterprise- level productivity.",""],[1,"94","9","Structured Programme Evaluation Framework","A structured programme evaluation framework will be developed to assess the effectiveness of all productivity programmes, particularly in ensuring more cost-effective interventions.",""],[1,"94","9","Strengthened Monitoring and Reporting Mechanisms","Monitoring and reporting mechanisms will be strengthened to ensure transparency and sustainability of intervention programmes.",""],[1,"94","9","Productivity Programme Improvement and Development Use of Evaluation Findings","the findings from the evaluation and monitoring efforts will be made as references in improving existing and developing new productivity- related programmes.",""],[1,"444","5","National Data Governance Framework","a national data governance framework will be established to bolster data sharing",""],[1,"444","6","National Open Data Framework","This framework will incorporate policies, guidelines, legal, and investment measures to obtain the data as well as the monetisation of data shared with the private sector.",""],[1,"444","7","Statistics Act 1965 Review and Statistical System Strengthening","The Statistics Act 1965 is being reviewed to empower the Department of Statistics Malaysia (DOSM) in collecting and coordinating data from the public and private sectors.","Department of Statistics Malaysia (DOSM)"],[1,"444","9","Public Service Delivery Innovation and Decision-Making Enhancement","In the Twelfth Plan, priority will be given to enhance quality decision-making and encourage innovation to ensure public service delivery meets the expectations of the rakyat.",""],[1,"444","9","Adoption of New Public Service Delivery Mechanisms","The adoption of new mechanisms and innovative approaches will foster efficiency in public service delivery.",""],[1,"444","10","Behavioural Insights Approach for Policy Formulation and Implementation","the Behavioural Insights (BI) approach will be introduced to enable effective policy formulation and implementation.",""],[1,"445","1","Behavioral Insights Policy Design and Implementation Approach","In the Twelfth Plan, the BI approach will be adopted as a complementary tool to enhance the Government's services to the rakyat.",""],[1,"445","1","Behavioral Insights for Public Policy Guidance","BI will be used to design and implement policies to guide the rakyat towards making better decisions.",""],[1,"445","4","Behavioral Insights in Policy Formulation and Implementation","Application of BI in policy formulation and implementation will enhance the effectiveness of policies and allow optimal resource allocation, as citizens are nudged and enabled towards better outcomes.",""],[1,"445","5","Public Sector Behavioral Insights Initiatives","The application of BI in the public sector will be introduced in the Twelfth Plan through several initiatives by the Malaysia Productivity Corporation.",""],[1,"446","2","Evidence-Based Policy Development","policy development will be driven by evidence-based data and supplemented with the outcomes from engagements with the rakyat.",""],[1,"446","2","Data Analytics for Policymaking","The usage of data analytics in policymaking will optimise the government's limited resources.",""],[1,"446","2","Malaysian Government Central Data Exchange Expansion","The expansion of Malaysian Government Central Data Exchange (MyGDX) services will enable the Government to optimise data for better decision-making, thus achieving better outcomes for the rakyat.",""],[1,"446","3","Central Depository System for Programme Coordination","A central depository system will be developed to coordinate information on selected programmes to enhance inclusivity.",""],[1,"452","5","Periodic Implementation Review of the Twelfth Plan","Throughout the five-year period, the implementation of the Plan will be reviewed periodically to take into account the dynamic and rapid changes in the domestic and global environment.",""]],"7":[[1,"432","3","Reintroduction of the Parliamentary Services Act 1963","Reintroduce Parliamentary Services Act 1963",""],[1,"446","5","Electoral System Improvement","In the Twelfth Plan, the focus will be to uphold integrity, transparency and neutrality at all levels, improve the electoral system, digitalise the judicial system as well as enhance corporate governance in SOEs.",""],[1,"446","8","Election Commission Strengthening and Electoral Process Reform","The Election Commission will be strengthened to ensure a fair, independent and transparent election process.",""],[1,"446","8","Digital Election Management Modernisation","Digitalisation of the election management will be further enhanced through a more systematic system integration and development of new applications.",""],[1,"446","8","Voter Age Eligibility and Automatic Voter Registration Implementation","This effort will enable more effective and efficient implementation of the 18 years old voter age eligibility and automatic voters' registration.",""],[2,"432","3","Reintroduction of the Parliamentary Services Act 1963","Reintroduce Parliamentary Services Act 1963",""],[2,"443","1","Public Service Act","A public service act will be introduced to ensure more effective checks and balances between executive, legislative and judicial powers.",""],[2,"446","1","Public Participation in Decision-Making Expansion","Public participation in decision-making processes will be expanded to ensure effective and impactful policies as well as to promote participatory governance.",""],[2,"446","5","Electoral System Improvement Reform","In the Twelfth Plan, the focus will be to uphold integrity, transparency and neutrality at all levels, improve the electoral system, digitalise the judicial system as well as enhance corporate governance in SOEs.",""],[2,"446","8","Election Commission Strengthening and Electoral System Reform","The Election Commission will be strengthened to ensure a fair, independent and transparent election process.",""],[2,"446","8","Digitalisation of Election Management","Digitalisation of the election management will be further enhanced through a more systematic system integration and development of new applications.",""],[2,"446","8","Voter Age Eligibility and Automatic Registration Implementation","This effort will enable more effective and efficient implementation of the 18 years old voter age eligibility and automatic voters' registration.",""],[2,"454","5","Public Service Act for Role Delineation and Accountability","The delineation of roles between Members of the Administration and civil servants through the introduction of Public Service Act will ensure integrity, accountability and transparency in public service delivery",""]],"8":[[1,"433","3","Special Cabinet Committee on Anti-Corruption Monitoring","These are monitored by the Special Cabinet Committee on Anti-Corruption (JKKMAR), which meets on a quarterly basis.",""],[1,"433","3","National Anti-Corruption Plan 2019-2023","The National Anti-Corruption Plan 2019-2023 (NACP) was launched in 2019, outlining six strategies and 115 initiatives.",""],[1,"433","4","Asset Declaration through MyDeclaration Portal","Members of the Administration and Members of Parliament have been required to declare assets through the MyDeclaration portal of the Malaysian Anti-Corruption Commission (MACC).","Malaysian Anti-Corruption Commission (MACC)"],[1,"446","5","Public Sector Integrity and Transparency Strengthening","Malaysia is committed to instil integrity, transparency and neutrality in the public sector to enhance trust among the rakyat.",""],[1,"446","6","Organisational Anti-Corruption Plan Implementation","all government agencies will implement the Organisational Anti-Corruption Plan as outlined under the NACP to address governance, integrity and corruption issues within each organisation.",""],[1,"446","6","Enhanced Enforcement of the Malaysian Anti-Corruption Commission Act 2009","Enforcement of the Malaysian Anti-Corruption Commission Act 2009 [Act 694] will be enhanced",""],[1,"446","6","Strategic Partnerships for Anti-Corruption Engagement","engagements through strategic partnerships with CSOs and political parties will be strengthened in combating corruption.",""],[1,"446","6","Ombudsman of Malaysia Legislation","a new legislation on Ombudsman of Malaysia will be introduced to enhance integrity and governance of public institutions.",""],[1,"446","7","ABMS Standard Intensification","The adoption of ABMS standard, which aims to reduce the risk of bribery and build trust among stakeholders, will be intensified.",""],[1,"446","7","Civil Service Confidentiality and Official Secrets Compliance","Moreover, in promoting integrity and to safeguard the sovereignty of the country, civil servants are required to strictly uphold confidentiality in handling sensitive documents and disseminating information as well as honour the pledge under the Official Secrets Act 1972.",""],[1,"446","7","Malaysian Governance Index Introduction","The Malaysian Governance Index will be introduced to measure the country's governance performance as well as to emphasise good governance among public institutions.",""],[2,"171","3","Anti-Bribery Management System Implementation","These include the mandatory implementation of the Anti-Bribery Management System standards, as outlined under the National Anti-Corruption Plan.",""],[2,"171","3","Recruitment Profiling System for Sensitive Positions","All enforcement agencies under the Ministry of Home Affairs will be required to implement the Recruitment Profiling System for high risk and sensitive positions to reduce corruption risks.","Ministry of Home Affairs"],[2,"171","3","Mandatory Job Rotation Policy","Job rotation will also be made mandatory.",""],[2,"433","3","Governance, Integrity and Anti-Corruption Coordination Centre","The National Centre for Governance, Integrity and Anti-Corruption (GIACC) was established in 2018 to coordinate and monitor measures involving governance and integrity across various agencies.",""],[2,"433","3","National Anti-Corruption Plan 2019-2023","The National Anti-Corruption Plan 2019-2023 (NACP) was launched in 2019, outlining six strategies and 115 initiatives.",""],[2,"433","3","Quarterly Anti-Corruption Oversight Committee","These are monitored by the Special Cabinet Committee on Anti-Corruption (JKKMAR), which meets on a quarterly basis.",""],[2,"433","4","Asset Declaration Requirement for Public Officials","Members of the Administration and Members of Parliament have been required to declare assets through the MyDeclaration portal of the Malaysian Anti-Corruption Commission (MACC).","Malaysian Anti-Corruption Commission"],[2,"446","5","Public Sector Integrity and Transparency Initiative","Malaysia is committed to instil integrity, transparency and neutrality in the public sector to enhance trust among the rakyat.",""],[2,"446","5","SOE Corporate Governance Enhancement Initiative","In the Twelfth Plan, the focus will be to uphold integrity, transparency and neutrality at all levels, improve the electoral system, digitalise the judicial system as well as enhance corporate governance in SOEs.",""],[2,"446","6","Organisational Anti-Corruption Plan Implementation","all government agencies will implement the Organisational Anti-Corruption Plan as outlined under the NACP to address governance, integrity and corruption issues within each organisation.",""],[2,"446","6","Enhanced Enforcement of the Malaysian Anti-Corruption Commission Act","Enforcement of the Malaysian Anti-Corruption Commission Act 2009 [Act 694] will be enhanced, while engagements through strategic partnerships with CSOs and political parties will be strengthened in combating corruption.",""],[2,"446","6","Strategic Partnerships for Anti-Corruption Engagement","engagements through strategic partnerships with CSOs and political parties will be strengthened in combating corruption.",""],[2,"446","6","Ombudsman of Malaysia Legislation","a new legislation on Ombudsman of Malaysia will be introduced to enhance integrity and governance of public institutions.",""],[2,"446","7","ABMS Standard Intensification","The adoption of ABMS standard, which aims to reduce the risk of bribery and build trust among stakeholders, will be intensified.",""],[2,"446","7","Civil Service Confidentiality and Official Secrets Compliance","Moreover, in promoting integrity and to safeguard the sovereignty of the country, civil servants are required to strictly uphold confidentiality in handling sensitive documents and disseminating information as well as honour the pledge under the Official Secrets Act 1972.",""],[2,"446","7","Malaysian Governance Index Introduction","The Malaysian Governance Index will be introduced to measure the country's governance performance as well as to emphasise good governance among public institutions.",""]],"9":[[1,"446","5","Judicial System Digitalisation","In the Twelfth Plan, the focus will be to uphold integrity, transparency and neutrality at all levels, improve the electoral system, digitalise the judicial system as well as enhance corporate governance in SOEs.",""],[1,"446","9","Digitalisation of Court Information Management Systems","The information management system and processes in all courts will be digitalised to provide transparent, efficient and effective legal and judicial services.",""],[1,"446","9","AI-Assisted Judicial Decision Support","In addition, AI will be used to assist judges and magistrates in making judgements for criminal trials.",""],[1,"447","1","Remote Hearings Pilot Projects","The Malaysian Judiciary has embarked on a number of pilot projects to evaluate the efficiency of remote hearings during the Movement Control Order.",""],[1,"447","1","Judicial Procedure and Remote Hearing Legal Reform","In view of the success and to facilitate remote hearings, the Courts of Judicature Act 1964, Subordinate Courts Act 1948, Subordinate Courts Rules Act 1955, Rules of the Federal Court 1995, Rules of the Court of Appeal 1994, and the Rules of Court 2012 will be reviewed and amended.",""],[2,"446","5","Judicial Digitalisation Programme","In the Twelfth Plan, the focus will be to uphold integrity, transparency and neutrality at all levels, improve the electoral system, digitalise the judicial system as well as enhance corporate governance in SOEs.",""],[2,"446","9","Digitalisation of Court Information Management Systems","The information management system and processes in all courts will be digitalised to provide transparent, efficient and effective legal and judicial services.",""],[2,"446","9","AI-Assisted Judicial Decision Support","In addition, AI will be used to assist judges and magistrates in making judgements for criminal trials.",""],[2,"447","1","Remote Hearings Pilot Projects","The Malaysian Judiciary has embarked on a number of pilot projects to evaluate the efficiency of remote hearings during the Movement Control Order.",""],[2,"447","1","Judicial Procedure and Court Rules Amendment","In view of the success and to facilitate remote hearings, the Courts of Judicature Act 1964, Subordinate Courts Act 1948, Subordinate Courts Rules Act 1955, Rules of the Federal Court 1995, Rules of the Court of Appeal 1994, and the Rules of Court 2012 will be reviewed and amended.",""]],"10":[[1,"433","7","Prudent Public Spending and Procurement Transparency","In the Eleventh Plan, the Government remained committed to ensuring prudent public spending and greater transparency in accordance with international good practices.",""],[1,"434","1","Public Procurement Governance Strengthening","process was reviewed to further enhance public procurement governance in achieving best value for money as well as ensuring transparency and effective spending.",""],[1,"434","1","ePerolehan Procurement System Upgrade and Mandatory Use","The ePerolehan (eP) system was upgraded and the government procurement mechanism through eP was made compulsory, effective January 2018.",""],[1,"434","1","Public Procurement Governance Circular Enforcement","the Pekeliling Perbendaharaan PK 1.1 2020 Punca Kuasa, Prinsip dan Dasar Perolehan Kerajaan was enforced in January 2020 to strengthen governance in public procurement and ensure value for money.",""],[1,"447","6","Government Procurement Legal Framework Review","Initiatives will be focused on enhancing budgeting transparency and aligning allocation priorities between various sectors, introducing the value gateway mechanism, reviewing the legal framework in government procurement, and improving PPP policy and governance.",""],[1,"448","3","Government Procurement Governance Reform Framework","A legal framework will be formulated to improve governance, transparency, efficiency and effectiveness of government procurement.",""],[1,"448","3","Independent Procurement Regulatory Body","Under this framework, an independent regulatory body will be formed to ensure compliance and proper monitoring of government procurement.",""],[1,"448","3","Online Procurement System for Physical Projects","An online procurement system for physical projects will be developed, while the existing eP system for supplies and services will be enhanced.",""],[1,"448","3","Procurement Complaints Review Mechanism","In addition, a complaints review mechanism will be established to address issues related to procurement.",""],[2,"33","8","Public Sector Strengthening for Integrity and Transparency","In recognition of the current gaps in talent, governance ecosystem and project management, the public sector will be further strengthened with emphasis on integrity and transparency.",""],[2,"433","7","Prudent Public Spending and Procurement Transparency","In the Eleventh Plan, the Government remained committed to ensuring prudent public spending and greater transparency in accordance with international good practices.",""],[2,"434","1","Public Procurement Governance Strengthening","process was reviewed to further enhance public procurement governance in achieving best value for money as well as ensuring transparency and effective spending.",""],[2,"434","1","ePerolehan Government Procurement System Upgrade and Mandatory Use","The ePerolehan (eP) system was upgraded and the government procurement mechanism through eP was made compulsory, effective January 2018.",""],[2,"434","1","Public Procurement Governance Circular Enforcement","the Pekeliling Perbendaharaan PK 1.1 2020 Punca Kuasa, Prinsip dan Dasar Perolehan Kerajaan was enforced in January 2020 to strengthen governance in public procurement and ensure value for money.",""],[2,"447","6","Government Procurement Legal Framework Review","Initiatives will be focused on enhancing budgeting transparency and aligning allocation priorities between various sectors, introducing the value gateway mechanism, reviewing the legal framework in government procurement, and improving PPP policy and governance.",""],[2,"448","3","Government Procurement Reform Framework","A legal framework will be formulated to improve governance, transparency, efficiency and effectiveness of government procurement.",""],[2,"448","3","Independent Procurement Regulatory Body","Under this framework, an independent regulatory body will be formed to ensure compliance and proper monitoring of government procurement.",""],[2,"448","3","Online Procurement System for Physical Projects","An online procurement system for physical projects will be developed, while the existing eP system for supplies and services will be enhanced.",""],[2,"448","3","Procurement Complaints Review Mechanism","In addition, a complaints review mechanism will be established to address issues related to procurement.",""]],"11":[[1,"434","3","Public Accounts Committee Oversight of Public Expenditure","PAC is one of the most important committees established by the Dewan Rakyat to review allocations approved by Parliament for public expenditure and to investigate non-compliance highlighted in the auditor general's reports.",""],[1,"434","4","Public Sector Comparator Mandate for Project Evaluation","the Public Sector Comparator (PSC) was also mandated to all ministries and agencies in enhancing the project evaluation and selection process.",""],[1,"447","3","Budgeting Process Review and Project Implementation Improvement","In the Twelfth Plan, a number of measures will be undertaken to review budgeting processes and to improve the effectiveness of project implementation.",""],[1,"447","6","Budgeting Framework and Process Improvement","The budgeting framework and process will be improved to promote good governance, transparency, efficiency, and effectiveness.",""],[1,"447","6","Budget Transparency and Sectoral Allocation Alignment Initiative","Initiatives will be focused on enhancing budgeting transparency and aligning allocation priorities between various sectors, introducing the value gateway mechanism, reviewing the legal framework in government procurement, and improving PPP policy and governance.",""],[1,"447","7","Budget Transparency Enhancement","Budget transparency will be improved in line with international good practices and standards to reduce leakages and ensure efficient public spending.",""],[1,"448","1","Fiscal Responsibility Act","the Fiscal Responsibility Act (FRA) will be introduced during the Twelfth Plan to enhance fiscal discipline as well as improve fiscal governance and transparency.",""],[1,"448","2","Value Gateway Mechanism for Development Project Appraisal","The value management initiative will be enhanced through the introduction of the value gateway mechanism.",""],[2,"70","2","Expansionary Fiscal Policy for Economic Revitalisation","Fiscal policy will be expansionary in the short-term to revitalise the economy after the COVID-19 pandemic.",""],[2,"70","2","Fiscal Consolidation for Long-Term Sustainability","Fiscal consolidation will resume once the economy is on a better footing to ensure long- term fiscal sustainability.",""],[2,"70","2","Twelfth Plan Development Expenditure Allocation","The total development expenditure allocation is estimated to be at RM400 billion in the Twelfth Plan period.",""],[2,"70","3","Fiscal Responsibility Act","Fiscal governance will be strengthened by institutionalising the fiscal sustainability principles throughccc the introduction of the Fiscal Responsibility Act, which is imperative to ensure long-term fiscal sustainability.",""],[2,"70","3","Medium-Term Revenue Strategy and Tax Administration Reform","Revenue will be enhanced by exploring new sources, expanding the revenue base, reviewing tax incentives, strengthening overall tax administration and adopting a medium- term revenue strategy.",""],[2,"70","3","Medium-Term Budgeting and Public Expenditure Review Reform","The management of expenditure will be strengthened by introducing medium-term budgeting and expenditure frameworks, undertaking public expenditure reviews and improving Government procurement management to ensure spending efficiency and effectiveness.",""],[2,"70","3","Debt and Liabilities Management Reform","The medium- and long-term debt and liabilities management will continue to be enhanced with the implementation of accrual accounting, introduction of medium-term debt strategy, establishment of the Debt Management Office as well as enhancement of the government guarantees framework.",""],[2,"447","7","Budget Transparency Enhancement","Budget transparency will be improved in line with international good practices and standards to reduce leakages and ensure efficient public spending.",""],[2,"447","7","Pre-Budget Statement and Mid-Year Review Publication","To enhance transparency, the Pre-Budget Statement and Mid-Year Review Report will be published.",""],[2,"448","1","Fiscal Responsibility Act","the Fiscal Responsibility Act (FRA) will be introduced during the Twelfth Plan to enhance fiscal discipline as well as improve fiscal governance and transparency.",""]],"12":[[1,"434","4","Pre-Approved Plan and Industrialised Building System Requirements for Government Projects","The requirement for Pre-Approved Plan (PAP) and Industrialised Building System (IBS) in government projects were enforced to expedite project implementation.",""],[1,"434","5","MyProjek Project Monitoring System Upgrade","were improved by upgrading MyProjek, formerly known as Sistem Pemantauan Projek II to better facilitate the implementation of Arahan Perbendaharaan 182 rujukan kepada Jabatan Teknik.",""],[1,"434","5","National Development Implementation Coordination Mechanism","Arahan No. 1 2020 Mekanisme Penyelarasan Pelaksanaan Pembangunan Negara was issued replacing Arahan No. 1 2018 Jentera Penyelarasan Pelaksanaan to strengthen the coordination mechanism at the federal, state and district levels in improving governance, minimising project mismanagement and reducing financial leakages.",""],[1,"443","9","National Development Implementation Coordination Mechanism","In this regard, Arahan No. 1 2020 Mekanisme Penyelarasan Pelaksanaan Pembangunan Negara will be leveraged.",""],[1,"448","6","Project Delivery Mechanism and Monitoring System Streamlining","The project delivery mechanism and monitoring system will be streamlined to ensure on-time completion, value-for-money and the fulfilment of intended outcomes.",""],[1,"448","7","Development Project Delivery Mechanism Improvement","The effectiveness of development projects in promoting socioeconomic development will be enhanced by improving the delivery mechanism and revising the regulatory framework.",""],[1,"448","7","Mandatory Evaluation Reports for Completed Projects","Evaluation reports for completed projects will be made mandatory across line ministries.","line ministries"],[1,"448","7","Project Compliance Enforcement and Remedial Action","Administrative and legal action will be taken against controlling officers who implemented projects which deviated from the approved scope.",""],[1,"448","8","MyProjek Planning, Monitoring, and Evaluation Enhancement","The MyProjek will be strengthened to facilitate better planning, monitoring, and evaluation of development programmes and projects.",""],[1,"448","8","MyProjek Project Submission Module Upgrade","The project submission module will be modified to allow state governments to directly submit proposals to ministries through the system.","state governments | ministries"],[1,"448","8","Integrated Government Planning Data Platform","The MyProjek will also be integrated with other systems to provide comprehensive and real-time data for planning and monitoring purposes.",""],[1,"455","15","Implementation Approach Transformation for Big, Fast Results","The goal will be to transform the implementation approach in achieving big, fast results.",""],[1,"455","16","Twelfth Plan Implementation Architecture Reform","These lessons will be incorporated into the implementation architecture so that the Twelfth Plan will be implemented in a way that is truly transformational.",""],[1,"455","16","Whole-of-Nation Twelfth Plan Delivery Approach","No stones will be left unturned when it comes to the implementation of the Twelfth Plan, in line with the adoption of the whole-of-nation approach.",""],[2,"434","4","Pre-Approved Plan and Industrialised Building System Requirements for Government Projects","The requirement for Pre-Approved Plan (PAP) and Industrialised Building System (IBS) in government projects were enforced to expedite project implementation.",""],[2,"434","4","Public Sector Comparator for Project Evaluation and Selection","the Public Sector Comparator (PSC) was also mandated to all ministries and agencies in enhancing the project evaluation and selection process.",""],[2,"434","5","National Development Implementation Coordination Mechanism","Arahan No. 1 2020 Mekanisme Penyelarasan Pelaksanaan Pembangunan Negara was issued replacing Arahan No. 1 2018 Jentera Penyelarasan Pelaksanaan to strengthen the coordination mechanism at the federal, state and district levels in improving governance, minimising project mismanagement and reducing financial leakages.",""],[2,"438","4","Budgeting Framework Review","Strategy C1 Reviewing Budgeting Framework and Process",""],[2,"438","4","Project Implementation Effectiveness Improvement","Strategy C2 Improving Effectiveness of Project Implementation",""],[2,"447","3","Budgeting Process Review and Project Implementation Improvement Measures","In the Twelfth Plan, a number of measures will be undertaken to review budgeting processes and to improve the effectiveness of project implementation.",""],[2,"447","6","Budgeting Framework and Process Improvement","The budgeting framework and process will be improved to promote good governance, transparency, efficiency, and effectiveness.",""],[2,"447","6","Budget Transparency and Sectoral Allocation Alignment Initiative","Initiatives will be focused on enhancing budgeting transparency and aligning allocation priorities between various sectors, introducing the value gateway mechanism, reviewing the legal framework in government procurement, and improving PPP policy and governance.",""],[2,"448","2","Value Gateway Mechanism for Development Project Appraisal","The value management initiative will be enhanced through the introduction of the value gateway mechanism.",""],[2,"448","6","Project Delivery and Monitoring System Streamlining","The project delivery mechanism and monitoring system will be streamlined to ensure on-time completion, value-for-money and the fulfilment of intended outcomes.",""],[2,"448","7","Development Project Delivery and Regulatory Reform","The effectiveness of development projects in promoting socioeconomic development will be enhanced by improving the delivery mechanism and revising the regulatory framework.",""],[2,"448","7","Mandatory Evaluation Reports for Completed Projects","Evaluation reports for completed projects will be made mandatory across line ministries.","line ministries"],[2,"448","7","Administrative and Legal Enforcement for Project Non-Compliance","Administrative and legal action will be taken against controlling officers who implemented projects which deviated from the approved scope.",""],[2,"448","8","MyProjek Planning, Monitoring, and Evaluation Enhancement","The MyProjek will be strengthened to facilitate better planning, monitoring, and evaluation of development programmes and projects.",""],[2,"455","15","Fourteen Game Changers for Plan Implementation","This commitment is exemplified by the 14 game changers.",""],[2,"455","16","Twelfth Plan Implementation Architecture Reform","The lessons will be incorporated into the implementation architecture so that the Twelfth Plan will be implemented in a way that is truly transformational.",""],[2,"455","16","Whole-of-Nation Implementation Approach","No stones will be left unturned when it comes to the implementation of the Twelfth Plan, in line with the adoption of the whole-of-nation approach.",""]],"13":[[1,"240","6","Federal-State Regional Development Coordination Mechanism","Strategic collaboration and coordination between the Federal Government and state governments will be strengthened to support effective regional development planning and implementation.",""],[1,"240","6","Regional Development Implementation and Data Sharing Improvement","Emphasis will be given to improve the implementation mechanism and enhance data sharing.",""],[1,"240","6","Priority Development Budget Allocation for Less Developed States","The six less developed states will continue to be prioritised in the development budget allocation.",""],[1,"241","1","Federal-State Regional Planning and Coordination Strengthening","Collaboration between the Federal Government and state governments will be strengthened to promote sustainable and balanced development across the regions.",""],[1,"241","1","State-Level Agency Rationalisation for Regional Planning","The role of key agencies at the state level will also be streamlined to support more effective regional planning and coordination, particularly in the six less developed states.",""],[1,"241","2","Alignment of State Development Plans with Federal Policies","The development plans of the state governments will be streamlined to support and complement the Federal development policies and strategies.",""],[1,"241","3","Development Composite Index 2.0","The Development Composite Index 2.0 (DCI 2.0) will be introduced as an instrument to measure the level of development at the state and regional levels.",""],[1,"241","4","Prioritised Development Funding for Less Developed States","The six less developed states comprising Kedah, Kelantan, Perlis, Sabah, Sarawak and Terengganu will continue to be prioritised with at least 50% of the Total Basic Development Expenditure3.",""],[1,"241","4","Federal-State Coordination for Development Implementation","Greater collaboration among Federal and states agencies will be undertaken to ensure the effective and efficient implementation of",""],[1,"241","5","Targeted Infrastructure and Development Projects","targeted programmes and development projects.",""],[1,"247","1","Regional Economic Development and Balanced Growth Initiative","The Twelfth Plan will optimise regional economic potential, develop sustainable cities and transform rural areas to bridge the development gap.",""],[1,"443","8","Strengthened Federal-State-Local Coordination Mechanism","collaboration and coordination between Federal, state and local authorities will be strengthened.",""],[1,"443","8","Cross-Ministerial Cluster Coordination Reform","the lead cluster will coordinate cross-ministerial issues within the clusters to reduce overlapping of functions.",""],[1,"443","8","Localisation of Agenda 2030 by Local Authorities","local authorities will be encouraged to localise Agenda 2030 by expanding activities and programmes on sustainable development.",""],[1,"443","8","Multi-Stakeholder Support for Sustainable Development Activities","This expansion will be undertaken by enhancing the involvement of the private sector, civil society organisations (CSOs) and local communities.",""],[1,"443","9","State Engagement for Development Programme Coordination","Concerted efforts will be undertaken in engaging states to streamline and coordinate development programmes and projects.",""],[1,"443","9","Public-Private and Civil Society Collaboration Strengthening","Similarly, collaborative efforts between the public and private sectors as well as CSOs will be strengthened to promote the whole of nation approach.",""],[1,"454","6","Public-Private Collaboration Enhancement","The Government is committed to further enhancing collaboration between the public and private sectors to ensure the goals of this Plan are realised.",""],[1,"455","16","Whole-of-Nation Twelfth Plan Delivery Approach","No stones will be left unturned when it comes to the implementation of the Twelfth Plan, in line with the adoption of the whole-of-nation approach.",""],[2,"240","6","Federal-State Regional Development Coordination and Data Sharing Mechanism","Strategic collaboration and coordination between the Federal Government and state governments will be strengthened to support effective regional development planning and implementation.",""],[2,"240","6","Priority Development Budget Allocation for Less Developed States","The six less developed states will continue to be prioritised in the development budget allocation.",""],[2,"241","1","Federal-State Regional Development Coordination Strengthening","Collaboration between the Federal Government and state governments will be strengthened to promote sustainable and balanced development across the regions.",""],[2,"241","1","State-Level Planning and Agency Rationalisation","The role of key agencies at the state level will also be streamlined to support more effective regional planning and coordination, particularly in the six less developed states.",""],[2,"241","1","Rationalisation of State Development and Corridor Authorities","This will involve rationalising the role of all state economic development corporations (SEDCs), state economic planning units, regional development authorities and regional economic corridor authorities.",""],[2,"241","2","Alignment of State Development Plans with Federal Policies","The development plans of the state governments will be streamlined to support and complement the Federal development policies and strategies.",""],[2,"241","2","Alignment of State Digital Plans with National Digital Transformation Objectives","State policies, such as the Smart Selangor Action Plan 2025, Pelan Induk Terengganu Sejahtera 2030 and Perlis Digital Plan 2021-2025 will be aligned to the national digital transformation objectives.",""],[2,"241","2","Alignment of State Initiatives with Federal Development Policies","State initiatives, such as the improvement of logistics services, river management and the development of the aerospace industry will also be mapped with the respective development policies at the Federal level.",""],[2,"241","3","Development Composite Index 2.0","The Development Composite Index 2.0 (DCI 2.0) will be introduced as an instrument to measure the level of development at the state and regional levels.",""],[2,"241","3","Federal-State Data Sharing Improvement","Meanwhile, data sharing between Federal and states agencies will be improved through better coordination and collaboration.",""],[2,"241","4","Prioritised Development Expenditure for Less Developed States","The six less developed states comprising Kedah, Kelantan, Perlis, Sabah, Sarawak and Terengganu will continue to be prioritised with at least 50% of the Total Basic Development Expenditure3.",""],[2,"241","4","Federal-State Collaboration for Development Implementation","Greater collaboration among Federal and states agencies will be undertaken to ensure the effective and efficient implementation of",""],[2,"241","5","Targeted Programmes and Development Projects for Less Developed States","targeted programmes and development projects.",""],[2,"443","7","Civil Service Communication and Information Dissemination Enhancement","Communication and dissemination of information within the civil service and to the rakyat will be enhanced to ensure effective service delivery.",""],[2,"443","8","Strengthened Federal-State-Local Coordination Mechanism","collaboration and coordination between Federal, state and local authorities will be strengthened.",""],[2,"443","8","Cross-Ministerial Cluster Coordination Arrangement","the lead cluster will coordinate cross-ministerial issues within the clusters to reduce overlapping of functions.",""],[2,"443","8","Local Agenda 2030 Localization and Sustainable Development Programme","local authorities will be encouraged to localise Agenda 2030 by expanding activities and programmes on sustainable development.",""],[2,"443","9","State Engagement for Development Programme Coordination","Concerted efforts will be undertaken in engaging states to streamline and coordinate development programmes and projects.",""],[2,"443","9","Public-Private and Civil Society Collaboration Strengthening","Similarly, collaborative efforts between the public and private sectors as well as CSOs will be strengthened to promote the whole of nation approach.",""],[2,"454","6","Regulatory Review to Reduce Bureaucracy","Rules and regulations will be reviewed to reduce bureaucracy at the Federal and state levels as well as at the local authority level in facilitating more robust private sector growth.",""],[2,"454","6","Public-Private Sector Collaboration Enhancement","The Government is committed to further enhancing collaboration between the public and private sectors to ensure the goals of this Plan are realised.",""]],"14":[[1,"180","5","Social Cohesion and National Unity Strengthening Measures","efforts will be concentrated on embracing diversity of society as a national asset, building a more tolerant society as well as strengthening governance for social cohesion and national unity",""],[1,"181","1","Social Interaction and Diversity Preservation Measures","Measures will be undertaken to promote social interaction and capitalise on various educational platforms in preserving diversity and fostering unity.",""],[1,"181","2","Unity Programme Expansion","Social interaction will be encouraged by improving and expanding unity programmes such as Kawasan Rukun Tetangga and Skim Rondaan Sukarela programmes.",""],[1,"181","2","Cultural Festivals and Heritage Awareness Programme","More cultural programmes and festivals will be organised to promote understanding and expose the rakyat, especially youth and children, to traditional customs and culture of various ethnic groups in Malaysia.",""],[1,"181","2","Museum and Heritage Site Engagement Activities","Activities in museums, memorials and art galleries as well as historical sites will be intensified to increase the understanding and exposure to the rich history and cultural diversity of the nation.",""],[1,"181","2","Sports for Unity Promotion","In addition, sports activities will also be promoted as a medium to foster unity.",""],[1,"181","3","National, State and Community Engagement and Dialogue Sessions","Engagement sessions at national, state and community levels will be intensified, including through town hall and dialogue sessions, to encourage discussions on unity and national integration.",""],[1,"181","3","Community Mediation Expansion and Mediator Certification","More community mediation avenues will be established by utilising existing facilities, while the number of certified community mediators will be increased nationwide.",""],[1,"181","4","Inter-Religious Harmony Advocacy Programme Expansion","advocacy programmes in promoting inter-religious harmony will be expanded",""],[1,"181","4","Use of Houses of Worship and Media for Religious Tolerance","houses of worship and religious activities, as well as mainstream and social media will be leveraged to enhance respect for different faiths",""],[1,"181","4","Inter-Religious Harmony Index Development","An index will also be developed to measure the level of inter- religious harmony in our multi-religious society and as a reference in formulating relevant strategies",""],[1,"182","3","Social Cohesion and National Unity Policy Formulation","Measures will be undertaken to formulate policies and strengthen stakeholders collaboration in improving governance of social cohesion and unity.",""],[1,"182","3","Unity Promotion Programmes for Leaders and CSOs","Leaders and CSOs will also be encouraged to actively participate in various programmes to promote unity.",""],[1,"182","4","National Unity Policy","A national policy on unity will be introduced to promote social cohesiveness and harmony as well as capitalise diversity as an asset to strengthen national unity.",""],[1,"182","4","Unity Action Plan","An action plan will also be introduced to translate the policy through the implementation of specific programmes and initiatives by multiple sectors and agencies to further foster, strengthen and preserve unity among Malaysians.",""],[1,"182","4","Unity Capacity Building Programme","More capacity building programmes will be organised to strengthen competency and develop subject matter experts on unity.",""],[1,"182","5","Whole-of-Nation Social Cohesion Partnership Programme","collaboration between government, the private sector and CSOs will be intensified to promote social cohesion, unity, patriotism and volunteerism.",""],[1,"182","5","Inclusive Engagement and Smart Partnership Programme","More engagement sessions and smart partnership programmes will be organised to ensure inclusive participation and promote better networking.",""],[1,"182","5","Community Facility Optimisation Initiative","Public facilities, such as Pusat Rukun Tetangga, Kompleks Perpaduan, Pusat Komuniti Desa, Pusat Khidmat Masyarakat and Pusat Aktiviti Warga Emas will be optimised to encourage social interaction.",""],[1,"182","6","Unity-Related Community Engagement Programmes","Local governments and CSOs will be encouraged to proactively organise unity-related programmes, such as dialogues, focus group meetings and public information campaigns.",""],[1,"182","6","Local Government and CSO Mediation Capacity Building Programme","Training and capacity building programmes for local government and CSOs will be intensified to equip them with relevant mediation, conciliation and negotiation skills.",""],[1,"182","6","CSO Diversified Funding Support Mechanism","CSOs will be encouraged to diversify funding sources from crowdfunding and private sector to conduct these programmes.",""],[1,"182","7","Community Mediation and Unity Promotion Venues","Community centres, offices of members of parliament and state assemblymen as well as places of worship will be utilised as venues to mediate community issues and promote unity programmes.",""],[1,"182","7","Religious Leader Engagement for Social Values","Religious leaders will be encouraged to play a more important role in instilling noble values and ensure the society behaves in a responsible and dignified manner.",""],[1,"183","1","National Unity Promotion Initiative","unity will further be given priority in building a united and prosperous nation as well as contribute to nation-building.",""]],"15":[[1,"213","3","Strengthening Bumiputera Institutions and Mandated Agencies","Governance and service delivery of Bumiputera institutions and mandated agencies will be enhanced to ensure the success of the Bumiputera socioeconomic development agenda.",""],[1,"213","3","Review of Bumiputera Institution Functions and Programmes","the functions and programmes of these institutions will be reviewed to ensure effectiveness and avoid duplication.",""],[1,"213","3","Coordination of the Bumiputera Database Across Institutions","The Bumiputera database across ministries, agencies and SOEs will be coordinated.",""],[1,"213","4","Government Mandate and Programme Review for Bumiputera Benefit","a review of the Government's mandate, functions, programmes and the role of Bumiputera institutions will be conducted to ensure Bumiputera derive maximum benefits.",""],[1,"213","4","Bumiputera Aspirations Rejuvenation Programme","programmes to rejuvenate the Bumiputera aspirations among leaders of Bumiputera institutions and mandated agencies will be introduced to ensure commitment in implementing the agenda.",""],[1,"213","5","Streamlining Ministry and Agency Mandates for Bumiputera Agenda Delivery","The mandate and functions of each ministry and agency will be streamlined to ensure effective implementation of the Bumiputera agenda.",""],[1,"213","5","Bumiputera Prosperity Division Establishment","a dedicated Bumiputera Prosperity Division (BKB) will be established in each ministry and agency through the redeployment of existing staff.",""],[1,"213","5","Bumiputera Agenda Monitoring and Evaluation Mechanism","This division is responsible for implementing the Bumiputera agenda within the ministries and agencies as well as in monitoring and evaluating equitable outcomes.",""],[1,"213","5","Corporate Leadership Appointment for EDOs and SOEs","boards of directors and top management of EDOs and SOEs will be appointed among qualified corporate and industry players in line with the Malaysia Code of Corporate Governance who can successfully execute the Bumiputera agenda.",""],[1,"213","6","MARA Institutional Strengthening and Expanded Economic Development Role","The role of MARA will be strengthened to exercise the power enacted under the MARA Act 1966.",""],[1,"213","6","New MARA Development Model for Bumiputera Advancement","MARA will explore a new development model to further accelerate progress in uplifting the Bumiputera socioeconomic position.",""],[1,"213","6","MARA Commercial and Industrial Activities for Bumiputera Entrepreneurs","MARA will continue to be involved in a number of commercial and industrial activities to create more opportunities for Bumiputera entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"213","6","TRM Economic Potential Unlocking Initiative","MARA will play an important role in unlocking the economic potential of the TRM.",""],[1,"213","7","Bumiputera Agenda Coordination and Monitoring Secretariat","TERAJU will continue to play a key role in implementing the Bumiputera agenda and serve as the secretariat to Majlis Kemakmuran Bumiputera in coordinating, monitoring and evaluating the implementation of strategic Bumiputera development programmes.",""],[1,"213","7","Bumiputera Participation Single Database","TERAJU will develop a single database related to Bumiputera participation in key socioeconomic activities.",""],[1,"213","7","Integrated Bumiputera Data Warehouse","Data collection and data sharing among stakeholders will be enhanced to facilitate the establishment of an integrated data warehouse.",""],[1,"213","7","Bumiputera Single Gateway for Services and Information","TERAJU will create a single gateway in providing information and services related to education and training, entrepreneurship as well as equity and property ownership of Bumiputera.",""],[1,"214","1","Outcome-Based Performance Assessment for EDOs and SOEs","The performance of the board of directors and CEOs of EDOs as well as and SOEs will be assessed on the outcome-based key performance indicators (KPIs).",""],[1,"214","1","Bumiputera Scorecard Reintroduction","The Bumiputera scorecard will be reintroduced to measure the achievement of Bumiputera socioeconomic outcomes.",""],[1,"214","1","Bumiputera Prosperity Index Development","A comprehensive Bumiputera Prosperity Index will be developed to measure Bumiputera progress and wellbeing.",""],[1,"214","2","Equitable Bumiputera Employment Initiatives","Initiatives will be introduced to encourage equitable employment for Bumiputera in the private sector to promote fair opportunities.",""],[1,"214","2","Government Procurement Policy and Regulation Review","Moreover, the Government procurement policies and regulations will be reviewed and strengthened in ensuring equitable distribution of Government contracts at every level.",""],[1,"214","2","Beneficial Ownership Disclosure Legal Amendments","Amendments and improvements will be made to the Companies Act 2016 and the Malaysian Anti-Corruption Commission Act 2009 to enable better identification of the beneficial owner of shares in companies and Government procurement.",""],[2,"212","1","Mainstreaming the Bumiputera Agenda Across Policies","The Bumiputera agenda will continue to be a national agenda in achieving fair, equitable and inclusive socioeconomic development in line with WKB 2030.",""],[2,"213","3","Enhancement of Bumiputera Institutions and Mandated Agencies","Governance and service delivery of Bumiputera institutions and mandated agencies will be enhanced to ensure the success of the Bumiputera socioeconomic development agenda.",""],[2,"213","3","Review of Bumiputera Institution Functions and Programmes","the functions and programmes of these institutions will be reviewed to ensure effectiveness and avoid duplication.",""],[2,"213","3","Coordination of the Bumiputera Database Across Institutions","The Bumiputera database across ministries, agencies and SOEs will be coordinated.",""],[2,"213","4","Review of Government Mandate, Functions, and Bumiputera Institutions","a review of the Government's mandate, functions, programmes and the role of Bumiputera institutions will be conducted to ensure Bumiputera derive maximum benefits",""],[2,"213","4","Bumiputera Aspirations Rejuvenation Programme","programmes to rejuvenate the Bumiputera aspirations among leaders of Bumiputera institutions and mandated agencies will be introduced to ensure commitment in implementing the agenda",""],[2,"213","5","Streamlining Ministry and Agency Mandates for Bumiputera Agenda Delivery","The mandate and functions of each ministry and agency will be streamlined to ensure effective implementation of the Bumiputera agenda.",""],[2,"213","5","Bumiputera Prosperity Division Establishment","a dedicated Bumiputera Prosperity Division (BKB) will be established in each ministry and agency through the redeployment of existing staff.",""],[2,"213","5","Bumiputera Agenda Monitoring and Evaluation Function","This division is responsible for implementing the Bumiputera agenda within the ministries and agencies as well as in monitoring and evaluating equitable outcomes.",""],[2,"213","5","Merit-Based Appointment of EDO and SOE Leadership","boards of directors and top management of EDOs and SOEs will be appointed among qualified corporate and industry players in line with the Malaysia Code of Corporate Governance who can successfully execute the Bumiputera agenda.",""],[2,"213","7","Bumiputera Agenda Coordination and Monitoring Secretariat","TERAJU will continue to play a key role in implementing the Bumiputera agenda and serve as the secretariat to Majlis Kemakmuran Bumiputera in coordinating, monitoring and evaluating the implementation of strategic Bumiputera development programmes.",""],[2,"213","7","Bumiputera Participation Single Database","TERAJU will develop a single database related to Bumiputera participation in key socioeconomic activities.",""],[2,"213","7","Integrated Bumiputera Data Warehouse","Data collection and data sharing among stakeholders will be enhanced to facilitate the establishment of an integrated data warehouse.",""],[2,"213","7","Bumiputera Information and Services Single Gateway","In addition, TERAJU will create a single gateway in providing information and services related to education and training, entrepreneurship as well as equity and property ownership of Bumiputera.",""],[2,"214","1","Outcome-Based Performance Assessment for EDOs and SOEs","The performance of the board of directors and CEOs of EDOs as well as and SOEs will be assessed on the outcome-based key performance indicators (KPIs).",""],[2,"214","1","Bumiputera Scorecard Reintroduction","The Bumiputera scorecard will be reintroduced to measure the achievement of Bumiputera socioeconomic outcomes.",""],[2,"214","1","Bumiputera Prosperity Index Development","A comprehensive Bumiputera Prosperity Index will be developed to measure Bumiputera progress and wellbeing.",""]],"16":[[1,"246","8","Rural Governance Strengthening and Delivery System Streamlining","Strategies will focus on strengthening rural governance and streamlining the delivery system to enhance rural development.",""],[1,"246","9","Rural Community Leadership Training Programme","Training development programmes for the Jawatankuasa Pembangunan dan Keselamatan Kampung (JPKK) and Jawatankuasa Pembangunan dan Keselamatan Kampung Persekutuan (JPKKP) will be strengthened to enhance the quality of grassroot leaders.",""],[1,"246","9","Rural Youth and Women Representation in Village Administration","More representatives among the rural youth and women will be appointed in JPKK and JPKKP to enhance their participation in village administration.",""],[1,"246","10","Strengthened Multi-Stakeholder Rural Development Implementation Collaboration","Strategic collaboration among government agencies, private sector and CSOs will be strengthened to undertake various rural development initiatives to ensure effective implementation of the Rural Development Policy 2030.",""],[1,"246","10","Continuous SPKPN Rural Development Database Updating","The data in SPKPN will be continuously updated to provide a comprehensive centralised database for better rural development planning.",""],[1,"246","10","Federal-State Rural Development Data Collaboration","Collaborations between the Federal Government and state governments will be enhanced in ensuring a complete and accurate database is available for all stakeholders.",""],[2,"246","8","Rural Governance Strengthening and Delivery System Streamlining","Strategies will focus on strengthening rural governance and streamlining the delivery system to enhance rural development.",""],[2,"246","9","Rural Community Leadership Training Programme","Training development programmes for the Jawatankuasa Pembangunan dan Keselamatan Kampung (JPKK) and Jawatankuasa Pembangunan dan Keselamatan Kampung Persekutuan (JPKKP) will be strengthened to enhance the quality of grassroot leaders.",""],[2,"246","9","Youth and Women Representation in Village Administration","More representatives among the rural youth and women will be appointed in JPKK and JPKKP to enhance their participation in village administration.",""],[2,"246","10","Strengthened Rural Development Collaboration and Implementation","Strategic collaboration among government agencies, private sector and CSOs will be strengthened to undertake various rural development initiatives to ensure effective implementation of the Rural Development Policy 2030.",""],[2,"246","10","Continuous Update of the SPKPN Rural Development Database","The data in SPKPN will be continuously updated to provide a comprehensive centralised database for better rural development planning.",""],[2,"246","10","Enhanced Federal-State Rural Development Data Collaboration","Collaborations between the Federal Government and state governments will be enhanced in ensuring a complete and accurate database is available for all stakeholders.",""]],"17":[[1,"271","1","Local Authority Capability Enhancement Roadmap","In this connection, a roadmap will be developed to enhance the capability of local authorities by incorporating new technology and digitalisation.",""],[1,"271","1","Local Authority Revenue Diversification Initiative","Meanwhile, local authorities in Sabah and Sarawak will also be encouraged to identify new sources of income for better revenue while addressing the needs of the growing urban population.",""],[1,"271","1","Local Authority Data Coordination and Sharing System","Efforts to strengthen data coordination and sharing among local authorities will ensure better planning and coordination.",""],[1,"271","1","Malaysian Urban-Rural National Indicators Network Adoption","In this regard, participation from local authorities in adopting the Malaysian Urban-Rural National Indicators Network for Sustainable Development system as a tool to measure sustainability of cities will help improve data readiness and support SDG's targets achievement.",""],[2,"245","1","Accelerated Local Agenda 21 Implementation","Meanwhile, the implementation of Local Agenda 21 (LA21) will be accelerated to achieve the 2030 Agenda.",""],[2,"245","3","LA21 Implementation Acceleration","The implementation of LA21 will be accelerated through greater collaboration among local authorities, communities and the private sector in championing urban sustainable development.",""],[2,"271","1","Urban Governance Improvement Roadmap","Urban governance will be improved to enhance service delivery among local authorities.",""],[2,"271","1","Local Authority Capability Enhancement Roadmap","In this connection, a roadmap will be developed to enhance the capability of local authorities by incorporating new technology and digitalisation.",""],[2,"271","1","Local Authority Revenue Diversification Initiative","Meanwhile, local authorities in Sabah and Sarawak will also be encouraged to identify new sources of income for better revenue while addressing the needs of the growing urban population.",""],[2,"271","1","Local Authority Data Coordination and Sharing Mechanism","Efforts to strengthen data coordination and sharing among local authorities will ensure better planning and coordination.",""],[2,"271","1","Urban Sustainability Indicators Adoption","In this regard, participation from local authorities in adopting the Malaysian Urban-Rural National Indicators Network for Sustainable Development system as a tool to measure sustainability of cities will help improve data readiness and support SDG's targets achievement.",""]],"18":[[1,"275","5","Federal-State Cooperation Supportive Ecosystem","Strategies will focus on establishing a supportive ecosystem for cooperation and enhancing public service delivery.",""],[1,"275","5","Public Service Delivery Enhancement in Sabah and Sarawak","Strategies will focus on establishing a supportive ecosystem for cooperation and enhancing public service delivery.",""],[1,"275","8","Public Service Strengthening for Efficient Service Delivery","The public service will need to be strengthened in ensuring efficient service delivery to the rakyat.",""],[1,"275","8","Review of Sabah and Sarawak Rights and Development Prioritisation","the rights of Sabah and Sarawak will be reviewed, talents will be strengthened and development allocations for the states will be prioritised.",""],[1,"275","9","Special Council on Malaysia Agreement 1963","The establishment of the Special Council on Malaysia Agreement 1963 in September 2020 replacing the Special Cabinet Committee further demonstrated the commitment of the Federal Government to ensure that the rights of Sabah and Sarawak under MA63 continue to be protected.",""],[1,"275","9","Coordination of Remaining MA63 Issues","Moving forward, efforts in coordinating and streamlining the remaining issues raised by Sabah and Sarawak will be continued.",""],[1,"275","9","Sabah and Sarawak Affairs Division Coordination Function","The Bahagian Hal Ehwal Sabah dan Sarawak, which was established under the Prime Minister's Department is tasked with coordinating all the issues relating to the implementation of MA63.","Prime Minister's Department"],[1,"276","2","Federal Department Capacity Strengthening in Sabah and Sarawak","Federal departments in Sabah and Sarawak will be strengthened by enhancing training and improving succession planning.",""],[1,"276","2","Public Service Talent Development Programme","Capacity and capability of talent in these two states will be improved by enhancing knowledge and skills in various fields, including leadership, digital technology, creativity and innovation.",""],[1,"276","2","Subject Matter Expert Identification and Grooming Initiative","Subject matter experts in the related fields will be identified and groomed in ensuring quality service delivery.",""],[1,"276","3","Priority Development Allocation for Sabah and Sarawak","The Federal Government is committed to ensuring the less developed states are given priority in the development allocation.",""],[1,"276","4","Inter-Agency Collaboration Strengthening in Sabah and Sarawak","Collaboration among all agencies in the two states will be strengthened by promoting synergies among the RECs with the Federal and state agencies.",""],[1,"276","4","Federal Support to SEDCO and SEDC","the Federal Government will work closely with both Sabah Economic Development Corporation (SEDCO) and Sarawak Economic Development Corporation (SEDC) to enhance their contribution in delivering better outcomes to the rakyat.","Federal Government | Sabah Economic Development Corporation (SEDCO) | Sarawak Economic Development Corporation (SEDC)"],[1,"276","4","State Role Support for Islamic Promotion and Native Courts","Support will also be given to enhance the states' role in a number of areas, including the promotion of Islam and strengthening the native courts.",""],[1,"276","5","Coordinated Regional Development Planning","Measures will be undertaken to promote more coordinated and integrated regional development planning through better collaboration with the relevant agencies, both at the Federal and state levels.",""],[1,"276","6","Regional Development Planning Coordination","Regional economic authorities in both states will streamline the development planning and initiatives introduced by all the relevant authorities.",""],[1,"276","6","SDC Blueprint Policy Alignment Review","SEDIA will need to align the review of the SDC Blueprint with all related policies at the national and state levels.",""],[1,"276","6","SCORE Area Development Acceleration","RECODA together with URDA, HDA and NRDA will collaborate with Federal and state agencies in accelerating development within the SCORE areas.",""],[1,"276","7","Strengthening of SEDCO and SEDC Roles for State Economic Planning","The roles of SEDCO and SEDC will be further enhanced to facilitate the planning of economic activities in Sabah and Sarawak, in line with the mandate given to these two agencies to correct economic imbalances at the state level.",""],[1,"276","7","Regional Planning, Coordination and Evaluation Committee","In this connection, a committee will be established comprising multiple key Federal and state agencies that are responsible for regional planning, coordination and evaluation.",""],[1,"276","7","Regional Coordination of Federal Programmes to Bridge Development Gaps","This committee will coordinate strategies with a number of Federal programmes at the regional level in bridging development gaps across regions and states.",""],[2,"275","5","Federal-State Cooperation Supportive Ecosystem","Strategies will focus on establishing a supportive ecosystem for cooperation and enhancing public service delivery.",""],[2,"275","5","Public Service Delivery Enhancement in Sabah and Sarawak","Strategies will focus on establishing a supportive ecosystem for cooperation and enhancing public service delivery.",""],[2,"275","8","Public Service Strengthening for Efficient Service Delivery","The public service will need to be strengthened in ensuring efficient service delivery to the rakyat.",""],[2,"276","2","Federal Department Capacity Strengthening in Sabah and Sarawak","Federal departments in Sabah and Sarawak will be strengthened by enhancing training and improving succession planning.",""],[2,"276","2","Public Service Talent Development Programme","Capacity and capability of talent in these two states will be improved by enhancing knowledge and skills in various fields, including leadership, digital technology, creativity and innovation.",""],[2,"276","2","Subject Matter Expert Development for Service Delivery","Subject matter experts in the related fields will be identified and groomed in ensuring quality service delivery.",""],[2,"276","4","Inter-Agency Collaboration Strengthening in Sabah and Sarawak","Collaboration among all agencies in the two states will be strengthened by promoting synergies among the RECs with the Federal and state agencies.",""],[2,"276","4","Support for State Roles in Islamic Promotion and Native Courts","Support will also be given to enhance the states' role in a number of areas, including the promotion of Islam and strengthening the native courts.",""]],"19":[[1,"443","2","Public Service Sandbox","Meanwhile, the public service sandbox will be introduced to enhance innovation and produce solutions for better public service delivery.",""],[1,"446","4","National Innovation Blueprint","In the Twelfth Plan, a national blueprint on innovation will be introduced to provide guidelines and strategies to promote innovation.",""],[1,"446","4","Public Sector Innovation Review and KPI Reform","Current circulars, KPIs, procedures and processes will be reviewed to encourage innovation in the public sector.",""],[1,"446","4","Public Sector Innovation Mainstreaming Initiative","Further efforts will be undertaken to inculcate innovation as a norm in the public sector, including by incorporating innovation as part of the KPIs for the top management of ministries, departments and agencies.",""],[1,"446","4","Public Sector Innovation Blueprint Development","The development of the public sector innovation blueprint will ensure a balance between the management and technology approaches in innovation.",""],[2,"444","9","Public Service Delivery Innovation and Decision-Making Enhancement","In the Twelfth Plan, priority will be given to enhance quality decision-making and encourage innovation to ensure public service delivery meets the expectations of the rakyat.",""],[2,"444","9","Adoption of New Public Service Delivery Mechanisms","The adoption of new mechanisms and innovative approaches will foster efficiency in public service delivery.",""],[2,"444","10","Behavioural Insights Approach for Policy Formulation and Implementation","the Behavioural Insights (BI) approach will be introduced to enable effective policy formulation and implementation.",""],[2,"445","1","Behavioral Insights Policy Design and Implementation","In the Twelfth Plan, the BI approach will be adopted as a complementary tool to enhance the Government's services to the rakyat.",""],[2,"445","4","Behavioral Insights in Policy Formulation and Implementation","Application of BI in policy formulation and implementation will enhance the effectiveness of policies and allow optimal resource allocation, as citizens are nudged and enabled towards better outcomes.",""],[2,"445","5","Public Sector Behavioral Insights Initiatives","The application of BI in the public sector will be introduced in the Twelfth Plan through several initiatives by the Malaysia Productivity Corporation.",""],[2,"446","4","National Innovation Blueprint","In the Twelfth Plan, a national blueprint on innovation will be introduced to provide guidelines and strategies to promote innovation.",""],[2,"446","4","Public Sector Innovation Review and KPI Reform","Current circulars, KPIs, procedures and processes will be reviewed to encourage innovation in the public sector.",""],[2,"446","4","Public Sector Innovation Mainstreaming","Further efforts will be undertaken to inculcate innovation as a norm in the public sector, including by incorporating innovation as part of the KPIs for the top management of ministries, departments and agencies.",""],[2,"446","4","Public Sector Innovation Blueprint Development","The development of the public sector innovation blueprint will ensure a balance between the management and technology approaches in innovation.",""]],"20":[[1,"447","6","Public-Private Partnership Policy and Governance Improvement","Initiatives will be focused on enhancing budgeting transparency and aligning allocation priorities between various sectors, introducing the value gateway mechanism, reviewing the legal framework in government procurement, and improving PPP policy and governance.",""],[1,"448","4","Public-Private Partnership Framework Improvement","The Government will continue to encourage private sector participation in the national development agenda via the PPP approach.",""],[1,"448","4","PPP Project Efficiency and Transparency Reform","the PPP framework will be improved to ensure efficiency and transparency in the implementation of PPP projects.",""],[1,"448","4","New PPP Blueprint","A new PPP blueprint will be introduced to replace the existing 1991 Privatisation Master",""],[1,"448","5","Public-Private Partnership Policy Framework Revision","The blueprint will provide a comprehensive PPP policy framework which includes the revision of implementation and financing models as well as terms and conditions to ensure a fairer sharing of risks and benefits between the public and private sectors.",""],[2,"447","2","State-Owned Enterprise Governance and Risk Management Review","The legal framework, policies and processes in managing SOEs including GLCs, government-linked investment companies and statutory bodies will be reviewed to minimise Government exposure to risks and enhance transparency.",""],[2,"447","2","Merit-Based Board Appointment Reform for Public Entities","more stringent processes will be put in place in the appointment of board members, based on merit, integrity, technical, financial and corporate governance skills.",""],[2,"447","6","Public-Private Partnership Policy and Governance Improvement","Initiatives will be focused on enhancing budgeting transparency and aligning allocation priorities between various sectors, introducing the value gateway mechanism, reviewing the legal framework in government procurement, and improving PPP policy and governance.",""],[2,"448","4","Public-Private Partnership Framework Improvement","The Government will continue to encourage private sector participation in the national development agenda via the PPP approach.",""],[2,"448","4","New Public-Private Partnership Blueprint","A new PPP blueprint will be introduced to replace the existing 1991 Privatisation Master",""],[2,"448","5","Comprehensive Public-Private Partnership Policy Framework","The blueprint will provide a comprehensive PPP policy framework which includes the revision of implementation and financing models as well as terms and conditions to ensure a fairer sharing of risks and benefits between the public and private sectors.",""]],"21":[[1,"22","4","6R1 Pandemic Mitigation Approach","the 6R1 approach was implemented to mitigate the impact of the pandemic.",""],[1,"22","4","National Recovery Plan","The National Recovery Plan (NRP) was introduced in June 2021 as a phased strategy to transition out from the Movement Control Order (MCO) in terms of the movement of people as well as the reopening of economic and social sectors.",""],[1,"23","1","Economic Stimulus Packages and Phased National Recovery Plan Transition","Twelfth Plan has taken into account the 6R approach that includes eight economic stimulus packages amounting to RM530 billion and the phased transition under the NRP.",""],[1,"42","2","Twelfth Plan Economic Recovery and Structural Transition Strategy","Macroeconomic strategies will focus on enhancing productivity, promoting quality investment, accelerating structural economic transition, increasing participation in the global value chain (GVC) and ensuring long-term fiscal sustainability.",""],[1,"48","11","COVID-19 Economic Stimulus Measures","Despite being affected by the COVID-19 pandemic, private consumption remains resilient supported by the stimulus measures, such as the Bantuan Prihatin Nasional, loan moratorium and the Employees",""],[1,"52","12","COVID-19 Economic Stimulus Packages","Fiscal expansionary measures were undertaken since 2020 to cushion the impact of the COVID-19 pandemic through four economic stimulus packages9, worth RM305 billion, which included direct fiscal injection of RM55 billion.",""],[1,"53","8","Expansionary Fiscal Stimulus Packages","Fiscal policy continues to be expansionary at the beginning of the Twelfth Plan in addressing the health and economic crises.",""],[1,"70","2","Expansionary Fiscal Policy for Economic Revitalisation","Fiscal policy will be expansionary in the short-term to revitalise the economy after the COVID-19 pandemic.",""],[2,"8","2","Comprehensive Policy Response Framework for the Twelfth Plan","This Plan paves the way forward for comprehensive policy responses in facing the challenging situation brought about by the COVID-19 pandemic.",""],[2,"22","4","National Recovery Plan","The National Recovery Plan (NRP) was introduced in June 2021 as a phased strategy to transition out from the Movement Control Order (MCO) in terms of the movement of people as well as the reopening of economic and social sectors.",""],[2,"22","4","6R1 Pandemic Mitigation Approach","As a Government that cares for the people, especially in times of crisis, the 6R1 approach was implemented to mitigate the impact of the pandemic.",""],[2,"23","1","Economic Stimulus Packages and Phased National Recovery Plan Transition","Twelfth Plan has taken into account the 6R approach that includes eight economic stimulus packages amounting to RM530 billion and the phased transition under the NRP.",""],[2,"39","1","Sustainable Economic Recovery and Social Protection Measures","The Plan strives to bring about sustainable economic recovery as well as provide better social protection to vulnerable segments of society.",""],[2,"42","2","Twelfth Plan Economic Recovery Strategy","The Twelfth Plan is a medium- and long-term economic recovery plan to address the impact of the COVID-19 pandemic and to put the economy back to its long-term growth trajectory.",""],[2,"48","11","COVID-19 Stimulus Support Measures","Despite being affected by the COVID-19 pandemic, private consumption remains resilient supported by the stimulus measures, such as the Bantuan Prihatin Nasional, loan moratorium and the Employees",""],[2,"53","8","Expansionary Fiscal Stimulus Packages","Fiscal policy continues to be expansionary at the beginning of the Twelfth Plan in addressing the health and economic crises.",""]],"22":[[1,"32","2","MSME Participation and Entrepreneurship Strengthening Programme","In addition, efforts will be undertaken to strengthen MSMEs participation in the economy and boosting entrepreneurial capabilities.",""],[1,"32","3","MSME Digital Adoption and Capability Enhancement Programme","Game Changer III will accelerate MSMEs development through technology and digital adoption in embracing new norms in business activities as well as enhancing the capabilities of Bumiputera entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"32","3","MSME Market Expansion and Cooperative Development Initiative","In addition, focus will be given to shift MSMEs from a domestic to the global market and leveraging cooperative movement in developing entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"35","12","MSME Digitalisation Skills and Business Process Transformation Programme","MSMEs will be equipped with the skills to enable these enterprises to digitalise their business process by the year 2025.",""],[1,"35","12","MSME Competitiveness and International Standards Support","To enhance competitiveness, MSMEs will also be assisted to produce products and services on par with international standards.",""],[1,"35","12","Conducive MSME Support Ecosystem","A conducive and holistic ecosystem will be created to support MSMEs.",""],[1,"35","12","Second-Chance Support for Failed Entrepreneurs","This includes giving a second chance to entrepreneurs who have tried and failed as success is very seldom achieved at the first-time attempt.",""],[1,"35","12","Small Business Payment Dispute Commissioner","A commissioner will be appointed to assist small businesses in securing payments on time and resolving payment disputes.",""],[1,"35","12","Cooperative Movement Entrepreneurship Development","In addition, cooperative movement will be leveraged in developing entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"69","8","MSME eCommerce Platform Adoption Initiative","intensifying eCommerce transactions by encouraging MSMEs to utilise digital platforms",""],[1,"75","4","Entrepreneur and Enterprise Capability-Building Programme","focused efforts will be undertaken to boost the capabilities of Malaysian entrepreneurs and enterprises, as well as cooperatives.",""],[1,"75","4","MSME Global Competitiveness Support","efforts will be undertaken to enable MSMEs to better compete in a globalised market.",""],[1,"75","4","Innovative and Sustainable Entrepreneurship Development","The development of innovative and sustainable entrepreneurs will be intensified through the adoption of advanced and digital technology.",""],[1,"75","4","Business Governance and Facilitative Regulatory Reform","governance and facilitative regulations will be further enhanced to ensure the continuity and sustainability of businesses.",""],[1,"78","5","Bumiputera Entrepreneur Capacity Enhancement","Enhance the capabilities of Bumiputera entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"78","9","National MSME Digitalisation Roadmap","Introducing a national MSMEs digitalisation roadmap.",""],[1,"78","11","Unified Entrepreneur Information Portal","Developing a unified portal to facilitate entrepreneurs to obtain essential information on financing resources and advisory services.",""],[1,"78","13","Second Chance Intervention Programme for Failed Entrepreneurs","Implementing the second chance intervention programme to assist failed entrepreneurs and mitigate the risk of bankruptcy.",""],[1,"78","14","Small Business Payment Commissioner","Appointing a commissioner to assist small businesses in securing payments on time and resolving payment disputes.",""],[1,"78","15","Cooperative Movement Entrepreneurship Development","Leveraging the cooperative movement in developing entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"114","2","MSME Capability Strengthening and Inclusive Growth Support","Efforts will also be undertaken to boost entrepreneurs capabilities and promote inclusive growth by strengthening MSMEs participation in the economy.",""],[1,"121","5","Entrepreneur and MSME Capability Enhancement","the capabilities of entrepreneurs and enterprises particularly MSMEs will be enhanced",""],[1,"136","5","Entrepreneur and MSME Capability Enhancement Measures","The Twelfth Plan will continue to boost the capabilities of entrepreneurs, cooperatives, agriculture-based associations, social enterprises and MSMEs.",""],[1,"137","1","Entrepreneurship Development and Innovation Promotion","Efforts to produce entrepreneurs that are competitive and resilient will include enhancing entrepreneurship development and promoting innovation-driven entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"137","2","Entrepreneurial Development Programmes","Entrepreneurial development programmes will be further enhanced to inculcate the right mindset among aspiring entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"137","2","Entrepreneurship Education and Training for Students","Education and training will also focus on developing students with entrepreneurial skills set to produce more job creators among graduates.",""],[1,"137","2","Triple Helix Entrepreneurship Collaboration","Triple Helix collaboration will be encouraged to enable entrepreneurs to acquire the necessary skills and competencies.",""],[1,"137","2","Entrepreneurship Outreach Programmes","the implementation of outreach programmes will be intensified in boosting entrepreneurial capability and skills among youth, Bumiputera and specific target groups.",""],[1,"137","2","Rural and Less Developed Area Incubation Spaces","Incubation spaces will be established in rural and less developed areas to support aspiring entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"137","2","Intrapreneurship Development within Organisations","Intrapreneurship development within organisations will be augmented to provide opportunities for employees to become entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"137","3","Support Programmes for Innovative Entrepreneurs","Support programmes will be implemented to increase the number of innovative entrepreneurs, including youth, Bumiputera and specific target groups in strategic and high impact industries, such as smart farming, halal, aerospace, biotechnology, medical devices and digital economy.",""],[1,"137","3","Entrepreneur-Researcher Collaboration for Innovation","Collaboration between entrepreneurs and researchers will be intensified to enhance innovation in creating more high value products and services that will boost competitiveness.",""],[2,"32","2","MSME Participation and Entrepreneurship Strengthening","In addition, efforts will be undertaken to strengthen MSMEs participation in the economy and boosting entrepreneurial capabilities.",""],[2,"32","3","MSME Digital Adoption and Capability Enhancement Programme","Game Changer III will accelerate MSMEs development through technology and digital adoption in embracing new norms in business activities as well as enhancing the capabilities of Bumiputera entrepreneurs.",""],[2,"32","3","MSME Market Expansion and Cooperative Entrepreneurship Support","In addition, focus will be given to shift MSMEs from a domestic to the global market and leveraging cooperative movement in developing entrepreneurs.",""],[2,"35","12","MSME Digitalisation Skills and Business Process Support","MSMEs will be equipped with the skills to enable these enterprises to digitalise their business process by the year 2025.",""],[2,"35","12","MSME Competitiveness and International Standards Support","To enhance competitiveness, MSMEs will also be assisted to produce products and services on par with international standards.",""],[2,"35","12","Supportive Ecosystem for MSMEs","A conducive and holistic ecosystem will be created to support MSMEs.",""],[2,"35","12","Second-Chance Support for Entrepreneurs","This includes giving a second chance to entrepreneurs who have tried and failed as success is very seldom achieved at the first-time attempt.",""],[2,"35","12","Small Business Payment Commissioner","A commissioner will be appointed to assist small businesses in securing payments on time and resolving payment disputes.",""],[2,"35","12","Cooperative Movement Support for Entrepreneurs","In addition, cooperative movement will be leveraged in developing entrepreneurs.",""],[2,"75","4","Entrepreneur and Enterprise Capability-Building Support","focused efforts will be undertaken to boost the capabilities of Malaysian entrepreneurs and enterprises, as well as cooperatives.",""],[2,"75","4","MSME Competitiveness Enhancement Initiative","efforts will be undertaken to enable MSMEs to better compete in a globalised market.",""],[2,"75","4","Digital and Sustainable Entrepreneurship Development","The development of innovative and sustainable entrepreneurs will be intensified through the adoption of advanced and digital technology.",""],[2,"75","4","Business Governance and Facilitative Regulatory Reform","governance and facilitative regulations will be further enhanced to ensure the continuity and sustainability of businesses.",""],[2,"78","5","Bumiputera Entrepreneur Capability Enhancement","Enhance the capabilities of Bumiputera entrepreneurs.",""],[2,"78","9","National MSMEs Digitalisation Roadmap","Introducing a national MSMEs digitalisation roadmap.",""],[2,"78","10","Digitalisation Drive through Community Internet Centers","Leveraging the Pusat Internet Komuniti (PIK) and Pusat Internet Desa (PID) as the one stop centres to drive digitalisation.",""],[2,"78","11","Unified Entrepreneur Information Portal","Developing a unified portal to facilitate entrepreneurs to obtain essential information on financing resources and advisory services.",""],[2,"78","13","Second Chance Intervention Programme for Failed Entrepreneurs","Implementing the second chance intervention programme to assist failed entrepreneurs and mitigate the risk of bankruptcy.",""],[2,"78","14","Small Business Payment Commissioner","Appointing a commissioner to assist small businesses in securing payments on time and resolving payment disputes.",""],[2,"101","5","Industry Capacity Strengthening and Collaboration Initiative","The capacity of industry will be strengthened to enhance competitiveness and sustainability of local industries.",""],[2,"101","6","Industry Collaboration and Smart Partnerships for Market Access","Efforts will be intensified to increase collaboration among industry players, including through smart partnerships, to enhance market access.",""],[2,"101","7","MNC-MSME Backward Linkage Incentive Programme","multinational companies (MNCs) will be incentivised to collaborate with MSMEs to strengthen backward linkages to assist MSMEs in participating in the global value chain.",""],[2,"101","7","Technology Transfer Collaboration Initiative for Domestic Firms","This collaboration will expedite technology transfer to domestic firms.",""],[2,"101","7","MSME Market Access Advisory Support","MSMEs will be encouraged to leverage industry associations to obtain marketing advisory services and information in increasing market access.",""],[2,"102","2","GLC Hand-Holding Programmes for SMPPs","GLCs will be encouraged to implement hand-holding programmes for SMPPs in the services sector, particularly the business and professional services subsector.",""],[2,"102","2","M&A Support for Multi-disciplinary SMPP Enterprises","SMPPs will be encouraged to form companies through M&A in establishing strong multi-disciplinary enterprises as well as digitalise and adopt advanced technology.",""],[2,"102","2","Tax Incentives for Digital Technology Adoption by M&A Companies","tax incentives will be considered for M&A companies to adopt digital technology.",""],[2,"121","5","Entrepreneur and MSME Capability Enhancement","the capabilities of entrepreneurs and enterprises particularly MSMEs will be enhanced.",""],[2,"136","5","Entrepreneur and MSME Capability-Building Measures","The Twelfth Plan will continue to boost the capabilities of entrepreneurs, cooperatives, agriculture-based associations, social enterprises and MSMEs.",""],[2,"137","1","Entrepreneurship Development and Innovation Promotion","Efforts to produce entrepreneurs that are competitive and resilient will include enhancing entrepreneurship development and promoting innovation-driven entrepreneurs.",""],[2,"137","2","Entrepreneurial Development Programmes","Entrepreneurial development programmes will be further enhanced to inculcate the right mindset among aspiring entrepreneurs.",""],[2,"137","2","Entrepreneurship Education and Training for Students","Education and training will also focus on developing students with entrepreneurial skills set to produce more job creators among graduates.",""],[2,"137","2","Triple Helix Entrepreneurship Collaboration","Triple Helix collaboration will be encouraged to enable entrepreneurs to acquire the necessary skills and competencies.",""],[2,"137","2","Entrepreneurial Outreach Programmes","the implementation of outreach programmes will be intensified in boosting entrepreneurial capability and skills among youth, Bumiputera and specific target groups.",""],[2,"137","2","Rural and Less Developed Area Incubation Spaces","Incubation spaces will be established in rural and less developed areas to support aspiring entrepreneurs.",""],[2,"137","2","Intrapreneurship Development within Organisations","Intrapreneurship development within organisations will be augmented to provide opportunities for employees to become entrepreneurs.",""],[2,"137","2","Entrepreneurship Training Module Enhancement","Training modules will incorporate skills, such as analytical thinking, emotional intelligence, reasoning, problem- solving, social influence and originality to assist entrepreneurs in their business.",""],[2,"137","3","Support Programmes for Innovative Entrepreneurs","Support programmes will be implemented to increase the number of innovative entrepreneurs, including youth, Bumiputera and specific target groups in strategic and high impact industries, such as smart farming, halal, aerospace, biotechnology, medical devices and digital economy.",""],[2,"137","3","Advanced and Digital Technology Adoption for Entrepreneurs","In addition, entrepreneurs will be encouraged to continuously innovate by adopting advanced and digital technology, including in their business operation and management.",""],[2,"137","3","Entrepreneur-Researcher Collaboration for Innovation","Collaboration between entrepreneurs and researchers will be intensified to enhance innovation in creating more high value products and services that will boost competitiveness.",""],[2,"137","4","MSME Participation and Market Access Strengthening Initiative","The participation of MSMEs, cooperatives and agriculture-based associations in the economy will be strengthened to ensure inclusive growth.",""],[2,"139","1","Social Enterprise Development Blueprint","Blueprint Perusahaan Sosial 2021-2025 will be introduced to further strengthen social enterprise development.",""],[2,"139","1","Social Enterprise Capacity Development and Market Expansion Support","continuous support and capacity development will be provided for business and market expansion.",""],[2,"139","1","Social Impact Government Procurement Programme","Program Perolehan Impak Sosial Kerajaan (PPISK) will be rolled out to enable the onboarding of social enterprises to the national e-procurement system.",""],[2,"139","1","Inclusive Business Model Expansion","The Inclusive Business (IB) model, which promotes the involvement of MSMEs in the supply chain of GLCs and MNCs, will also be expanded to facilitate the participation of social enterprises.",""],[2,"139","2","Entrepreneurship Ecosystem Support Initiatives","initiatives will be undertaken to enhance governance, regulations, institutional roles and financing to boost the performance of entrepreneurs.",""],[2,"139","4","Review and Improve Entrepreneurship Regulations","Existing legislations related to entrepreneurship will be reviewed to enhance the effectiveness and inclusiveness of entrepreneurship development.",""],[2,"139","4","Legal and Regulatory Support for Businesses and Cooperatives","relevant laws and regulations will be improved to ensure businesses and cooperatives remain vibrant.",""],[2,"139","4","Informal Sector Business Registration Promotion","Measures will continue to be undertaken to encourage registration of businesses in the informal sector.",""],[2,"139","5","Small Business Payment Commissioner","A commissioner will be appointed to provide support for small businesses in securing payments on time and will act as a mediator in resolving payment disputes thereby advocating better payment practices among government and businesses.",""],[2,"139","7","Alternative Financing Mechanisms for Entrepreneurs","A more diversified financing landscape for entrepreneurs will be promoted with greater involvement of the private sector through various alternative financing mechanisms.",""],[2,"139","7","Public-Private Co-funding Initiative for Entrepreneurs","Co-funding initiatives between the public and private sectors will be intensified, particularly for high-potential and innovative entrepreneurs and enterprises to",""],[2,"140","1","Development Financial Institutions Revitalisation for Inclusive Financing","The role of the Development Financial Institutions (DFIs) will be revitalised to ensure access to financing for different target groups at various stages of growth.",""],[2,"140","2","Startup Financing Access Improvement","Access to financing for new entrepreneurs, especially start-ups, will also be improved to encourage the development and adoption of emerging technology in businesses.",""],[2,"140","2","Entrepreneur Loan Processing Simplification","Financing procedures and processes will be simplified to expedite the approval and disbursement of funding to entrepreneurs.",""],[2,"140","2","Failed Entrepreneur Support Programme","In addition, intervention programmes will be introduced to assist failed entrepreneurs and mitigate the risk of bankruptcy.",""],[2,"140","3","Programme Monitoring Enhancement Mechanism","monitoring of programmes will be enhanced to ensure entrepreneurs are more successful and resilient.",""],[2,"140","3","Assessment, Implementation and Monitoring Mechanism","an appropriate mechanism for assessment, implementation and monitoring will be developed in the Plan period.",""],[2,"140","4","Invention-to-Innovation Ecosystem Development","Initiatives will be undertaken to develop an invention to innovation ecosystem that propagates IP registration among entrepreneurs, especially startups.",""],[2,"140","4","Performance-Based IP-Backed Loan and Incentive Scheme","Performance-based loans and incentives, including utilisation of IP as collateral, will be explored in providing financial assistance.",""]],"23":[[1,"34","4","Policy and Regulatory Reform for Investment Climate","The Government remains committed to ensure Malaysia continues to be an attractive investment destination by introducing policy and regulatory reforms as well as improving governance.",""],[1,"34","4","Private Sector Engagement and Consultation Mechanism","The ecosystems that support private sector participation in development will continue to be improved such as facilitating regulation as well as increasing engagement and consultation with the private sector in policy formulation.",""],[1,"34","4","Public Service Delivery Improvement for Business Operations","Public service delivery will be strengthened to ease business operation.",""],[1,"64","1","Macroeconomic Policy Package for Growth Restoration","The macroeconomic policies for the Twelfth Plan will focus on restoring the economic growth and strengthening the economic fundamentals.",""],[1,"64","1","Competitive Economic Environment Enhancement","Emphasis will be given to ensure a conducive and competitive economic environment towards achieving greater economic resilience.",""],[1,"65","10","National Investment Aspirations Reform Framework","The National Investment Aspirations (NIA) will be the basis for comprehensive reforms in all investment-linked initiatives and policies.",""],[1,"66","6","Public Service Delivery and Business Facilitation Regulatory Reform","regulations to enable more effective public service delivery and facilitate ease of doing business.",""],[1,"66","6","Investment Incentive Review and Reform","Existing investment incentives will also be reviewed to attract more investment, especially in strategic and high-impact industries.",""],[1,"66","6","Domestic Direct Investment Promotion for MSMEs","Domestic direct investment will be promoted, focusing on technology adoption and providing innovative business ecosystem, especially for MSMEs.",""],[1,"66","6","Foreign Direct Investment Attraction for Market Access and Technology Transfer","In efforts to attract FDI, focus will be given to companies that will facilitate market access as well as technology and knowledge transfer for domestic firms.",""],[1,"66","7","Private Investment Promotion Measures","Measures to further promote private investment will include leveraging on competitive advantages of industry clusters, enhancing competitiveness and promoting sustainable development.",""],[1,"66","7","Investment Institution Reform","Investment institutions will be reformed to focus on attracting quality investment that promote the development of complex products and services, create high-skilled and high-paying jobs, encourage high use of domestic inputs and improve development in underserved areas.",""],[1,"66","7","Incentives Administration Streamlining","In addition, the incentives administration framework will be streamlined and targeted to improve efficiency and effectiveness.",""],[1,"108","1","Investment Promotion and Facilitation Reform","Emphasis will be given on more targeted, relevant and effective investment promotion and facilitation strategies.",""],[1,"108","1","Regional Investment Hub Development Framework","this policy framework will act as a foundation for Malaysia to become a regional investment hub",""],[1,"108","2","Strengthened Incentives Coordination and Collaboration Mechanism","The implementation and coordination mechanism will be strengthened to improve transparency and minimise redundancies.",""],[1,"108","2","Enhanced i-Incentives One-Stop Application Portal","The effectiveness of the i-Incentives portal as a one-stop application portal for grants and funding provided by various ministries and agencies will be enhanced.",""],[1,"108","2","Single-Window MSME Service Facilitation through State and District Offices","Meanwhile, the existing state and district offices of the Ministry of Domestic Trade and Consumer Affairs will be leveraged as a single window to facilitate MSMEs in accessing services.","Ministry of Domestic Trade and Consumer Affairs"],[1,"454","6","Private Sector Growth Strengthening","the role of the private sector as an engine of economic growth will be strengthened to ensure more holistic and sustainable development.",""],[1,"454","6","Regulatory Simplification and Bureaucracy Reduction Reform","Rules and regulations will be reviewed to reduce bureaucracy at the Federal and state levels as well as at the local authority level in facilitating more robust private sector growth.",""],[2,"65","10","National Investment Aspirations Reform Framework","The National Investment Aspirations (NIA) will be the basis for comprehensive reforms in all investment-linked initiatives and policies.",""],[2,"66","6","Public Service Delivery and Business Facilitation Regulatory Reform","regulations to enable more effective public service delivery and facilitate ease of doing business.",""],[2,"66","6","Investment Incentive Review for Strategic Industries","Existing investment incentives will also be reviewed to attract more investment, especially in strategic and high-impact industries.",""],[2,"66","6","Domestic Direct Investment Promotion for MSMEs","Domestic direct investment will be promoted, focusing on technology adoption and providing innovative business ecosystem, especially for MSMEs.",""],[2,"66","6","Foreign Direct Investment Attraction for Market Access and Technology Transfer","In efforts to attract FDI, focus will be given to companies that will facilitate market access as well as technology and knowledge transfer for domestic firms.",""],[2,"66","7","Private Investment Promotion Measures","Measures to further promote private investment will include leveraging on competitive advantages of industry clusters, enhancing competitiveness and promoting sustainable development.",""],[2,"66","7","Investment Institution Reform","Investment institutions will be reformed to focus on attracting quality investment that promote the development of complex products and services, create high-skilled and high-paying jobs, encourage high use of domestic inputs and improve development in underserved areas.",""],[2,"66","7","Incentives Administration Framework Streamlining","In addition, the incentives administration framework will be streamlined and targeted to improve efficiency and effectiveness.",""],[2,"68","8","High Value-Added Industry Promotion and Investment Attraction","Efforts will be undertaken to promote high value-added economic activities and attract more investment in knowledge-intensive industries to spur the creation of skilled and high-paying jobs.",""],[2,"77","16","Private Sector Investment Promotion for Industrial Growth","Promoting greater private sector investments in driving industrial growth.",""],[2,"108","1","National Investment Aspirations Policy Reform Framework","In this regard, the National Investment Aspirations (NIA) policy was introduced in April 2021 to promote sustained flow of quality investments.",""],[2,"108","1","Comprehensive Reform of Investment Policies and Initiatives","NIA will be the basis for comprehensive reforms of all relevant national policies and initiatives related to investment.",""],[2,"108","1","Targeted Investment Promotion and Facilitation Strategy","Emphasis will be given on more targeted, relevant and effective investment promotion and facilitation strategies.",""],[2,"108","1","Malaysia Regional Investment Hub Initiative","this policy framework will act as a foundation for Malaysia to become a regional investment hub",""],[2,"108","2","Strengthened Incentives Coordination and Collaboration Office","The implementation and coordination mechanism will be strengthened to improve transparency and minimise redundancies.",""],[2,"108","2","Enhanced i-Incentives One-Stop Grant Portal","The effectiveness of the i-Incentives portal as a one-stop application portal for grants and funding provided by various ministries and agencies will be enhanced.",""],[2,"108","2","MSME Single-Window Service Facilitation","Meanwhile, the existing state and district offices of the Ministry of Domestic Trade and Consumer Affairs will be leveraged as a single window to facilitate MSMEs in accessing services.","Ministry of Domestic Trade and Consumer Affairs"]],"24":[[1,"74","5","Industrial Estates and Food Production Area Strengthening","The role of industrial estates and food production areas will be strengthened through the",""],[1,"75","1","Balanced Industrial Estates Development","development of balanced industrial estates",""],[1,"75","1","Green Industry Concept Implementation","the implementation of a green industry concept",""],[1,"82","2","Industrial Estates Enhancement Initiative","the focus will be on boosting productivity mainly through ... enhancing the role of industrial estates",""],[1,"90","7","Industrial Estates and Food Production Area Enhancement","This will be achieved by boosting productivity growth, expanding exports markets, strengthening the effectiveness of financial intermediation ecosystem, enhancing the role of industrial estates and food production areas as well as improving governance and policy.",""],[1,"100","4","GLC Role Enhancement and Competitive Market Reform","the role of GLCs will be enhanced while a more fair and healthy competitive environment will be encouraged to improve market efficiency for the private sector to expand into domestic and international markets.",""],[1,"101","2","Manufacturing Supply Chain Enhancement Initiative","The manufacturing sector supply chain will continue to be enhanced to produce basic inputs for manufacturing products.",""],[1,"101","2","Manufacturing Supply Chain Gap Mapping and Identification","initiatives will be undertaken in mapping and identifying gaps in the existing supply chain to ensure its sustainability.",""],[1,"106","1","Industrial Estates and Food Production Areas Enhancement Initiative","Under the Twelfth Plan, focus will be given on enhancing the role of industrial estates as growth catalyst and achieving a more balanced industrial development.",""],[1,"106","4","Industrial Estates and Food Production Areas Development Management","Measures will be undertaken to better plan, coordinate and manage the development of industrial estates and dedicated food production areas throughout the country.",""],[1,"106","4","Incentives and Financial Assistance Review for Industrial and Food Production Areas","Incentives and financial assistance will be reviewed to promote the development of these areas.",""],[1,"106","6","Industrial Estates Policy Framework","A policy framework will be formulated to guide the developers in the planning, development and operation of these estates.",""],[1,"106","6","Industrial Estate Feasibility and Market Study Requirement","Developers will be encouraged to conduct comprehensive feasibility and market studies to reduce the potential risks of underutilisation of industrial estates.",""],[1,"106","6","Review of Underutilised Industrial Estates","Meanwhile, a comprehensive review will be undertaken to revive the existing underutilised industrial estates.",""],[1,"107","2","Industrial Estate Development and Supporting Infrastructure","The development of industrial estates, particularly in less developed states will be complemented by a number of facilities and supporting infrastructure.",""],[1,"107","2","Industrialisation Roadmap Formulation for Sabah and Sarawak","industrialisation roadmaps will also be formulated including for Sabah and Sarawak to ensure the development of industrial estates is based on local strengths and capabilities.",""],[1,"107","2","Investment Incentive Mechanism Improvement","the existing investment incentive mechanism will be improved to ensure less developed regions or states are given priority in getting special incentives.",""],[1,"107","3","Regional Industrial Estate Development Mapping","In this regard, a mapping of potential industries based on local strengths and advantages will be undertaken.",""],[1,"138","2","Vendor Development Programme Expansion","The Vendor Development Programme (VDP) will be expanded in creating more competent Bumiputera vendors among MSMEs.",""],[1,"138","2","Anchor Company Development Initiative","Initiatives to develop more anchor companies through collaboration with GLCs and MNCs will be intensified in promoting an integrated supply chain and providing more business opportunities.",""],[1,"138","2","Vendor Support and Capability Enhancement Programmes","Other support programmes, such as certification, marketing and branding, packaging as well as product development will be enhanced to improve the capacity and capability of vendors in meeting industry requirements.",""],[1,"138","4","MSME-MNC Linkage Strengthening Initiative","Linkages with large firms, especially MNCs will be strengthened in enabling MSMEs to have access to a bigger market.",""],[1,"138","4","MSME Supply Chain Standards Capacity Building","For this purpose, the capacity and capability of MSMEs in producing products and services that comply with the global supply chain standards will be strengthened.",""],[1,"138","4","Enhanced MSME Capacity Building Programmes","Capacity building programmes will be enhanced with emphasis on 4IR, strategic management, certification, marketing and branding, packaging, product development and eCommerce.",""],[1,"138","5","Business-to-Business Local Sourcing Initiatives","business-to-business (B2B) opportunities will be expanded through initiatives that encourage large companies to source locally from MSMEs.",""],[1,"138","5","Buy Malaysia Campaign Intensification","The 'Buy Malaysia Campaign' will be intensified to support local MSMEs.",""],[1,"138","5","Anti-Monopoly Intervention Programmes","intervention programmes will be undertaken to break unhealthy monopolistic practices in certain industries.",""],[2,"75","1","Balanced Industrial Estates Development","development of balanced industrial estates",""],[2,"75","1","Green Industry Concept Implementation","the implementation of a green industry concept",""],[2,"82","2","Industrial Estates Enhancement Programme","enhancing the role of industrial estates",""],[2,"90","7","Industrial Estates and Food Production Area Enhancement","This will be achieved by boosting productivity growth, expanding exports markets, strengthening the effectiveness of financial intermediation ecosystem, enhancing the role of industrial estates and food production areas as well as improving governance and policy.",""],[2,"106","1","Industrial Estate and Food Production Area Upgrading Initiative","Under the Twelfth Plan, focus will be given on enhancing the role of industrial estates as growth catalyst and achieving a more balanced industrial development.",""],[2,"106","1","Industrial Estate Attractiveness and Investment Enhancement Initiative","Hence, initiatives will be intensified to improve the attractiveness and investments in these areas.",""],[2,"106","4","Industrial Estates and Dedicated Food Production Areas Development Management","Measures will be undertaken to better plan, coordinate and manage the development of industrial estates and dedicated food production areas throughout the country.",""],[2,"106","4","Incentives and Financial Assistance Review for Industrial and Food Production Areas","Incentives and financial assistance will be reviewed to promote the development of these areas.",""],[2,"106","6","Industrial Estates Policy Framework","A policy framework will be formulated to guide the developers in the planning, development and operation of these estates.",""],[2,"106","6","Industrial Estate Feasibility and Market Studies","Developers will be encouraged to conduct comprehensive feasibility and market studies to reduce the potential risks of underutilisation of industrial estates.",""],[2,"106","6","Review and Revitalisation of Underutilised Industrial Estates","Meanwhile, a comprehensive review will be undertaken to revive the existing underutilised industrial estates.",""],[2,"106","7","Strengthening Dedicated Food Production Areas","The role of dedicated food production areas will be strengthened to increase participation of agropreneurs in modern farming.",""],[2,"106","7","Comprehensive Management Mechanism for Food Production Areas","A comprehensive mechanism in developing and managing these food production areas, such as TKPM, Aquaculture Industrial Zones and Permanent Ruminant Production Parks will be formulated through collaboration between the Federal and state governments.",""],[2,"106","7","Public-Private Collaboration for Modern Farming Technology Adoption","Collaboration between the government, private sector service providers and agropreneurs will be intensified to facilitate adoption of modern technologies.",""]],"25":[[1,"95","3","Construction 4.0 Technology Intensification","in line with the Construction 4.0 Strategic Plan adoption of advanced technologies, including augmented reality (AR) and virtual reality (VR) in buildings and infrastructure projects will be intensified.",""],[1,"95","3","Real-Time Project Collaboration for Construction Delivery","Efforts will also be undertaken to increase the effectiveness of project implementation and monitoring by promoting real-time collaboration.",""],[1,"95","3","Online Construction Approval Process Simplification","The existing online application and approval mechanism will be improved to simplify and shorten the project approval process.",""],[1,"95","3","OSC 3 Plus Online and BIM E-Submission Integration","the existing One Stop Centre (OSC) 3 Plus Online platform at local authorities, will be integrated with the BIM e-submission system.",""],[1,"95","4","Expansion of Construction Quality Assessment Tools","The IBS Score and the use of Quality Assessment System in Construction in the evaluation of construction projects will be expanded, particularly in the private sector.",""],[1,"96","3","Green Construction Practices Promotion","Adopting and implementing green construction practices will create value, improve resource efficiency and cost effectiveness, while reducing environmental impact.",""],[1,"96","3","Green Building Design Uptake Incentive","The industry players in this sector will be further encouraged to uptake green building design that promotes resources, energy and water efficiency as well as incorporates measures to withstand extreme weather patterns and natural disasters.",""],[1,"96","4","Circular Economy Construction Materials Promotion","Implementation of the circular economy6 concept will increase the use of sustainable, durable, biodegradable and recycled construction materials, which will contribute to lower cost and higher product value.",""],[1,"96","4","Digital Construction Methods Promotion","Its implementation will be promoted through the application of the IBS concept and technologies, BIM, Prefabricated Prefinished Volumetric Construction (PPVC) and Modular Methods.",""],[1,"96","4","Green Procurement Initiative for Construction","The green procurement initiative in the construction sector will promote sustainable resource sourcing and increase demand for high value- added green construction materials.",""],[1,"96","4","Sustainable Construction Certification and Performance Tools Adoption","Developers will also be urged to adopt sustainable certification and performance tools, including the Sustainable Infrastructure Rating Tool (Sustainable INFRASTAR), Green Building Index (GBI) and GreenRE in ensuring environmental sustainability features are incorporated from the beginning of the design and construction phases to operation phase.",""],[1,"99","1","Construction Sector Technology Adoption Incentives","Incentives will be introduced in the construction sector to encourage adoption of technology, such as IBS, BIM and modular construction.",""],[1,"99","1","Construction Mechanisation and Automation Initiative","Mechanisation and automation in this sector will expedite project completion, ensure resource and cost efficiency while maintaining quality.",""],[1,"100","2","Government Green Procurement Guideline for Works","A short-term action plan and a guideline on government green procurement (GGP) on works will be introduced to encourage green practices in the construction sector.",""],[1,"100","2","Nationwide Green Government Procurement Implementation","A nationwide implementation of the GGP on works, including procurement of green labelled materials, will catalyse the shift towards more sustainable and green construction practices.",""],[1,"100","2","Green Certification and Performance Tools for Construction Projects","Industry players will be urged to adopt green certification and performance tools for new development projects as well as renovation and retrofitting works.",""],[2,"95","3","Construction 4.0 Technology Adoption in Buildings and Infrastructure","in line with the Construction 4.0 Strategic Plan adoption of advanced technologies, including augmented reality (AR) and virtual reality (VR) in buildings and infrastructure projects will be intensified.",""],[2,"95","3","Real-Time Collaboration for Project Implementation and Monitoring","Efforts will also be undertaken to increase the effectiveness of project implementation and monitoring by promoting real-time collaboration.",""],[2,"95","3","Online Project Approval Process Simplification","The existing online application and approval mechanism will be improved to simplify and shorten the project approval process.",""],[2,"95","3","OSC 3 Plus Online and BIM E-Submission Integration","the existing One Stop Centre (OSC) 3 Plus Online platform at local authorities, will be integrated with the BIM e-submission system.",""],[2,"95","4","Expansion of Construction Quality Assessment Tools","The IBS Score and the use of Quality Assessment System in Construction in the evaluation of construction projects will be expanded, particularly in the private sector.",""],[2,"97","9","Construction Sector Industrial Training Partnerships","Industry players in the construction sector will be encouraged to share resources and partner with training institutions in providing industrial training for workers and students on the latest applied technology.",""],[2,"97","9","University-Industry Linkage Strengthening","In addition, university-industry linkages will be strengthened by embedding industry input and expertise in the field of study and training to keep abreast with the rapid technological changes.",""],[2,"97","9","Construction Industry Development Board Training and Accreditation Uptake","Industry players will also be encouraged to leverage training and accreditation programmes offered by the Construction Industry Development Board to upskill existing workers, in producing qualified local talent in the sector.",""],[2,"99","1","Construction Sector Technology Adoption Incentives","Incentives will be introduced in the construction sector to encourage adoption of technology, such as IBS, BIM and modular construction.",""],[2,"99","1","Construction Sector Mechanisation and Automation","Mechanisation and automation in this sector will expedite project completion, ensure resource and cost efficiency while maintaining quality.",""],[2,"101","8","Construction Sector Industry Consortium","a consortium of industry players in the construction sector will be established to integrate various local industry players, including contractors,",""],[2,"102","1","Construction Industry Consortium Establishment","Establishment of the consortium will allow the industry players to capitalise on individual strengths and create synergistic value to enhance competitiveness.",""],[2,"109","3","Akademi Binaan Malaysia Upgrade","In the construction sector, Akademi Binaan Malaysia will be enhanced as an internationally recognised training institution to produce high skilled technical talent.",""],[2,"109","3","Construction R&D Institutional Collaboration","the roles and functions of the Construction Research Institute of Malaysia and the Centre of Excellence for Engineering and Technology will be streamlined through strategic collaboration to enhance the effectiveness of R&D in the construction sector.",""]],"26":[[1,"402","1","R&D&C&I Capacity and Capability Strengthening","The Twelfth Plan will continue to place high priority in developing and leveraging STI by strengthening R&D&C&I capacity and capability.",""],[1,"402","4","National STI Priority Streamlining and R&D&C&I Strengthening","efforts will be undertaken to streamline national STI priority areas, strengthen funding for R&D&C&I and translate R&D as well as intellectual property into high value-added products",""],[1,"402","5","R&D&C&I Incentive and Funding Streamlining","Consequently, all the incentives and funding for R&D&C&I will be streamlined based on the niche areas in line with the national development priorities.",""],[1,"403","15","Research Management Unit Coordination of R&D Financing","The newly formed Research Management Unit (RMU), under the Economic Planning Unit of the Prime Minister's Department will coordinate and harmonise the funding mechanism for all R&D&C&I activities in ensuring these activities are in line with national priorities.","Economic Planning Unit of the Prime Minister's Department"],[1,"403","15","Experimental Development Research Funding Allocation","The RMU will ensure at least 50% of total R&D expenditure in the Twelfth Plan is for experimental development research with high commercialisation potential.",""],[1,"403","15","Alternative R&D Financing Expansion","Measures will be undertaken to increase access to alternative financing including through venture capital and international funding.",""],[1,"403","16","STI Research and Development Endowment Fund","endowment fund will be established to source funds from industry, matching grants, crowdfunding and waqf, for STI-related R&D activities.",""],[1,"404","1","Technology Financing Evaluation Capacity Incentives","banks and local venture capital companies will be incentivised to increase capacity and capability in evaluating technology financing.",""],[2,"33","5","R&D Alignment and Commercialisation Initiative","This policy enabler outlines two game changers in accelerating technology adoption and innovation, which are enhancing digital connectivity for inclusive development as well as aligning R&D towards commercialisation, wealth generation and economic growth.",""],[2,"34","6","Research, Development, Commercialisation and Innovation Intensification","Focus will be given to gearing up for the 4IR, providing an enabling environment for the digital economy, intensifying R&D&C&I as well as developing the required talent.",""],[2,"38","1","Commercialisation-Focused Government Research Funding","During the Twelfth Plan, 50% of all Government research funding will be focused on encouraging experimental development with high commercialisation potential.","Economic Planning Unit of the Prime Minister's Department"],[2,"402","1","R&D&C&I Capacity and STI Talent Development","The Twelfth Plan will continue to place high priority in developing and leveraging STI by strengthening R&D&C&I capacity and capability.",""],[2,"402","4","National R&D and Innovation Capacity Scaling Initiative","Greater emphasis will be placed on scaling up capacity and capability in R&D&C&I to create greater wealth.",""],[2,"402","4","National STI Priority Streamlining and Funding Strengthening","efforts will be undertaken to streamline national STI priority areas, strengthen funding for R&D&C&I and translate R&D as well as intellectual property into high value-added products.",""],[2,"402","5","National Policy on Science, Technology and Innovation Implementation","The National Policy on Science, Technology and Innovation (NPSTI) 2021-2030 will be implemented to harness STI and strengthen the R&D&C&I ecosystem in building a scientifically advanced and progressive society.",""],[2,"402","5","Priority Research Area Identification under MySTIE Framework","Under NPSTI 2021-2030, niche areas for research will be identified based on the priority areas set under the 10-10 Malaysian Science, Technology, Innovation and Economy (MySTIE) Framework, as shown in Exhibit 11-2.",""],[2,"402","5","R&D&C&I Incentive and Funding Streamlining","Consequently, all the incentives and funding for R&D&C&I will be streamlined based on the niche areas in line with the national development priorities.",""],[2,"403","15","Research Management Unit Coordination of R&D Funding","The newly formed Research Management Unit (RMU), under the Economic Planning Unit of the Prime Minister's Department will coordinate and harmonise the funding mechanism for all R&D&C&I activities in ensuring these activities are in line with national priorities.","Economic Planning Unit of the Prime Minister's Department"],[2,"403","15","Experimental Development Research Funding Allocation","The RMU will ensure at least 50% of total R&D expenditure in the Twelfth Plan is for experimental development research with high commercialisation potential.",""],[2,"403","15","Alternative R&D Financing Expansion","Measures will be undertaken to increase access to alternative financing including through venture capital and international funding.",""],[2,"403","16","STI Research and Development Endowment Fund","endowment fund will be established to source funds from industry, matching grants, crowdfunding and waqf, for STI-related R&D activities.",""],[2,"403","17","Venture Capital Ecosystem Strengthening Measures","Private investors, including angel investors, corporate investors and multinational companies, will be encouraged to participate in the venture capital ecosystem to provide more funds for start-up companies.",""],[2,"403","17","Tax Incentive Reform for Venture Capital and R&D","An improved tax structure will be introduced to strengthen the venture capital ecosystem and increase joint R&D efforts among industry, academia, government and international research institutions.",""],[2,"404","1","Demand-Driven R&D Support and Technology Financing Capacity Incentives","demand-driven R&D activities.",""],[2,"404","1","Technology Financing Evaluation Capacity Incentives for Banks and Venture Capital Firms","banks and local venture capital companies will be incentivised to increase capacity and capability in evaluating technology financing.",""]],"27":[[1,"404","2","National Technology and Innovation Sandbox Rollout","Among others, the National Technology and Innovation Sandbox (NTIS) initiatives will be rolled out to allow researchers, innovators, start-up companies and high-tech entrepreneurs to test their innovation in a live environment.",""],[1,"404","2","Malaysia Commercialisation Year 2.0 Enhancement","In addition, the Malaysia Commercialisation Year 2.0 (MCY 2.0) programme will be enhanced to increase commercialisation as well as improve the transfer rate of R&D outputs from lab to market.",""],[1,"404","2","Standardised Intellectual Property Rights Valuation and Licensing Framework","A standardised intellectual property rights (IPR) valuation and licensing framework will be established to facilitate fair valuation.",""],[1,"404","3","Industrial Collaboration Programme Enhancement","The Industrial Collaboration Programme (ICP) will also be further improved to enhance the capacities and capabilities of local firms to compete in targeted markets and participate in supply chains.",""],[1,"404","3","Technology Commercialisation and Transfer One-Stop Centre","In addition, a one-stop centre for technology commercialisation and transfer will be established to scale up home-grown technologies.",""],[2,"404","2","National Technology and Innovation Sandbox","Among others, the National Technology and Innovation Sandbox (NTIS) initiatives will be rolled out to allow researchers, innovators, start-up companies and high-tech entrepreneurs to test their innovation in a live environment.",""],[2,"404","2","Malaysia Commercialisation Year 2.0 Enhancement","In addition, the Malaysia Commercialisation Year 2.0 (MCY 2.0) programme will be enhanced to increase commercialisation as well as improve the transfer rate of R&D outputs from lab to market.",""],[2,"404","2","Standardised Intellectual Property Rights Valuation and Licensing Framework","A standardised intellectual property rights (IPR) valuation and licensing framework will be established to facilitate fair valuation.",""],[2,"404","3","Industrial Collaboration Programme Enhancement","The Industrial Collaboration Programme (ICP) will also be further improved to enhance the capacities and capabilities of local firms to compete in targeted markets and participate in supply chains.",""],[2,"404","3","Technology Commercialisation and Transfer One-Stop Centre","a one-stop centre for technology commercialisation and transfer will be established to scale up home-grown technologies.",""],[2,"404","5","R&D Commercialisation and Wealth Creation Initiative","Technology transfer professionals will be leveraged to unlock the potentials of R&D output through commercialisation to create wealth and jobs.",""]],"28":[[1,"239","3","Industry Value Chain Upgrading and High-Value Activity Participation","Industry players, especially MSMEs in the key growth nodes and hotspot areas, will be encouraged to move up the value chain and participate in high value-added activities.",""],[1,"239","3","Industry 4IR Adoption Support","Efforts will be undertaken to facilitate industries to embrace the 4IR through the adoption of technology, automation and innovation, particularly in complex industrial processes.",""],[1,"239","6","Industry Facilitation and Value Chain Upgrading Initiative","efforts will be undertaken to move away from low-end economic activities to high value-added, advanced technology and knowledge-intensive activities.",""],[1,"239","6","Global Value Chain Participation Strengthening","This will be achieved by enhancing industry facilitation, strengthening participation in the global value chain, intensifying talent development and fortifying international collaboration.",""],[1,"239","6","Talent Development and International Collaboration Initiative","This will be achieved by enhancing industry facilitation, strengthening participation in the global value chain, intensifying talent development and fortifying international collaboration.",""],[1,"382","2","Digitalisation and Advanced Technology Adoption Initiatives","During the Twelfth Plan, initiatives to boost digitalisation and advanced technology adoption will be emphasised.",""],[1,"405","2","Fourth Industrial Revolution Technology Adoption and Deep Tech Development","Under the Twelfth Plan, efforts will be intensified to gear up for the 4IR, including adopting emerging technologies in new product development.",""],[1,"405","4","Fourth Industrial Revolution Opportunity-Seizing Initiatives","initiatives will be put in place to seize the economic growth opportunities arising from 4IR, create a conducive ecosystem to harness its potential as well as establish trust and build an inclusive digital society.",""],[1,"407","1","4IR Investment Attraction and MSME Capability Enhancement","Malaysia will capitalise on the strength of ASEAN to attract more investments in 4IR technologies, particularly from global unicorn companies.",""],[1,"407","2","Improved Coordination for Implementing Existing Programmes and Initiatives","improving the coordination in implementing existing programmes and initiatives.",""],[1,"407","2","Application of 4IR Technologies Across Priority Economic Sectors","For this purpose, 10 potential sectors will be given focus to facilitate a strategic shift in the economy, as shown in Exhibit 11-3.",""],[1,"408","1","National AI and Blockchain Strategy Development","National strategies on artificial intelligence (AI) and blockchain will be developed to guide the growth of every sector in the economy.",""],[1,"408","1","National Internet of Things Strategic Roadmap Reinforcement","The National Internet of Things (IoT) Strategic Roadmap will be reinvigorated to ensure its implementation can fully bring benefits to the rakyat.",""],[1,"408","1","4IR Innovation Parks Establishment","In addition, 4IR innovation parks will be established to provide a secure testbed and pool together 4IR technology providers to stimulate new technology breakthroughs.",""],[1,"408","2","WEF Centre for 4IR Establishment","The World Economic Forum (WEF) Centre for 4IR will be established in Malaysia using the quadruple helix model involving government, industry, academia and society to co-design the policy framework and governance mechanism through global collaboration.",""],[1,"408","2","Expanded Regulatory Sandbox for Emerging Technologies","The regulatory sandbox will be further expanded beyond fintech to other technologies in various sectors, which will allow start-up companies and innovators to test solutions under a controlled and supervised regulatory environment.",""],[1,"408","2","Performance-Linked Incentives for 4IR Adoption","In addition, performance-linked incentives related to 4IR technology adoption will be expanded to non-manufacturing sectors to reap the benefits of 4IR and capture economic growth opportunities.",""],[1,"408","2","Dedicated 4IR Technology Fund","A dedicated tech fund will be established to encourage companies, especially MSMEs to adopt 4IR technology.",""],[1,"409","1","Digitalisation and 4IR Technology Adoption Initiative","During the Twelfth Plan, concerted efforts will be undertaken to boost digitalisation and advance technology adoption to transform Malaysia into a high technology-based economy",""],[2,"405","2","Fourth Industrial Revolution Readiness and Emerging Technology Adoption","Under the Twelfth Plan, efforts will be intensified to gear up for the 4IR, including adopting emerging technologies in new product development.",""],[2,"405","4","Fourth Industrial Revolution Opportunity-Seizing Initiatives","initiatives will be put in place to seize the economic growth opportunities arising from 4IR, create a conducive ecosystem to harness its potential as well as establish trust and build an inclusive digital society.",""],[2,"407","2","Coordination Improvement for Existing Programmes and Initiatives","improving the coordination in implementing existing programmes and initiatives.",""],[2,"407","2","4IR Technology Application in Priority Economic Sectors","For this purpose, 10 potential sectors will be given focus to facilitate a strategic shift in the economy, as shown in Exhibit 11-3.",""],[2,"408","1","National Artificial Intelligence and Blockchain Strategies","National strategies on artificial intelligence (AI) and blockchain will be developed to guide the growth of every sector in the economy.",""],[2,"408","1","National Internet of Things Strategic Roadmap Reinforcement","The National Internet of Things (IoT) Strategic Roadmap will be reinvigorated to ensure its implementation can fully bring benefits to the rakyat.",""],[2,"408","1","4IR Innovation Parks Development","In addition, 4IR innovation parks will be established to provide a secure testbed and pool together 4IR technology providers to stimulate new technology breakthroughs.",""],[2,"408","2","WEF Centre for Fourth Industrial Revolution Establishment","The World Economic Forum (WEF) Centre for 4IR will be established in Malaysia using the quadruple helix model involving government, industry, academia and society to co-design the policy framework and governance mechanism through global collaboration.",""],[2,"408","2","Expanded Regulatory Sandbox for Emerging Technologies","The regulatory sandbox will be further expanded beyond fintech to other technologies in various sectors, which will allow start-up companies and innovators to test solutions under a controlled and supervised regulatory environment.",""],[2,"408","2","Performance-Linked Incentives for 4IR Adoption","In addition, performance-linked incentives related to 4IR technology adoption will be expanded to non-manufacturing sectors to reap the benefits of 4IR and capture economic growth opportunities.",""],[2,"408","2","Dedicated 4IR Technology Fund","A dedicated tech fund will be established to encourage companies, especially MSMEs to adopt 4IR technology.",""]],"29":[[1,"126","1","Electronics and Electrical Industry Upgrading Programme","During the Twelfth Plan, the E&E industry players will be encouraged to adopt advanced technologies and produce more sophisticated products, resulting in higher productivity and growth.",""],[1,"126","1","High-Value Electronics Investment Promotion","The E&E industry needs to be repositioned by boosting investments in high value activities such as design and development (D&D) and front-end manufacturing.",""],[1,"126","2","National E&E Roadmap","a national E&E roadmap will be formulated to provide strategic direction for the industry.",""],[1,"126","3","Enhanced Coordination and Public-Private Collaboration Mechanism","The roles of relevant organisations will be enhanced to better coordinate and create strong linkages and collaboration with research institutions as well as between the public and private sectors.",""],[1,"126","3","E&E Industry Incentive Restructuring","Incentives for the E&E industry will be restructured to be more impactful.",""],[1,"126","3","Streamlining of Government Support for E&E Initiatives","The implementation of these initiatives will enable the streamlining of Government funding, technical support and facilities.",""],[1,"126","4","E&E Industry Upgrading and Advanced Semiconductor Manufacturing Promotion","Efforts will be undertaken to move the E&E industry towards higher-value activities across the supply chain with greater automation and advanced technology utilisation.",""],[1,"126","4","Advanced Semiconductor Manufacturing Concentration Initiative","In this regard, industry players will be encouraged to concentrate on the manufacturing of advanced semiconductors.",""],[1,"126","5","MNC Support for Local MSME Capability Enhancement","Multinational companies (MNCs) will be encouraged to facilitate the enhancement of local MSMEs capabilities.",""],[1,"126","5","Lighthouse Project Intensification","The implementation of the Lighthouse Project, which was introduced in 2020, will be intensified to encourage MNCs to assist local MSMEs in embracing digitalisation and Globalization 4.05 in their business models.",""],[1,"126","5","4IR Business Platform Establishment","the establishment of the Fourth Industrial Revolution (4IR) business platform will provide opportunities to E&E companies and MSMEs to accelerate 4IR technology adoption and innovation.",""],[2,"126","1","Electronics and Electrical Industry Upgrading Initiative","During the Twelfth Plan, the E&E industry players will be encouraged to adopt advanced technologies and produce more sophisticated products, resulting in higher productivity and growth.",""],[2,"126","1","High-Value Electronics Investment Promotion","The E&E industry needs to be repositioned by boosting investments in high value activities such as design and development (D&D) and front-end manufacturing.",""],[2,"126","1","Electronics Manufacturing Ecosystem Strengthening","efforts will be focused on strengthening manufacturing ecosystems, promoting new technology adoption, uplifting the development of talent as well as enhancing R&D and D&D activities.",""],[2,"126","2","National E&E Roadmap","a national E&E roadmap will be formulated to provide strategic direction for the industry.",""],[2,"126","3","Institutional Coordination and Public-Private Collaboration Enhancement","The roles of relevant organisations will be enhanced to better coordinate and create strong linkages and collaboration with research institutions as well as between the public and private sectors.",""],[2,"126","3","E&E Industry Incentive Restructuring","Incentives for the E&E industry will be restructured to be more impactful.",""],[2,"126","3","Streamlining of Government Funding and Technical Support","The implementation of these initiatives will enable the streamlining of Government funding, technical support and facilities.",""],[2,"126","4","E&E Industry Upgrading and Advanced Semiconductor Manufacturing Promotion","Efforts will be undertaken to move the E&E industry towards higher-value activities across the supply chain with greater automation and advanced technology utilisation.",""]],"30":[[1,"32","2","Economic Sector Rejuvenation Programme","Over the next five years, concerted efforts will be undertaken to rejuvenate all the economic sectors, namely services, manufacturing, agriculture, mining and quarrying as well as construction.",""],[1,"32","2","Productivity Growth and Export Expansion Measures","Meanwhile, productivity growth will be boosted, export markets will be expanded, financial intermediation ecosystem effectiveness and role of industrial estates and food production areas will be enhanced, while governance and policies will be improved.",""],[1,"32","2","Strategic and High-Impact Industries Development Initiative","Focus will also be placed on accelerating the development of eight strategic and high impact industries and activities, namely electrical and electronics (E&E), global services (GS), aerospace, creative, tourism, halal, smart farming and biomass.",""],[1,"32","3","Strategic and High-Impact Industries Upgrade Initiative","Game Changer II aims to enhance the contribution of the strategic and high impact industries and activities to the economy by leveraging on advanced technologies, digitalisation and niche capabilities.",""],[1,"48","1","Productivity Improvement Measures","These included the review of regulatory policies and practices, benchmarking of best practices in reducing the cost of doing business as well as enhanced collaboration between the public and private sectors to boost competitiveness.",""],[1,"48","1","Malaysia Productivity Blueprint Implementation","Various initiatives were also implemented under the Malaysia Productivity Blueprint (MPB) to unlock the potential of productivity at the national, sectoral and enterprise levels.",""],[1,"65","1","National Productivity Planning Mechanism Strengthening","At the national level, the planning mechanism will be strengthened, the successful initiatives under the Productivity Nexus will be scaled up and the productivity gap between the large firms and MSMEs will be narrowed.",""],[1,"65","1","Productivity Nexus Scale-Up","At the national level, the planning mechanism will be strengthened, the successful initiatives under the Productivity Nexus will be scaled up and the productivity gap between the large firms and MSMEs will be narrowed.",""],[1,"65","1","Sectoral Productivity Ecosystem Strengthening","In addition, various strategies at the sectoral level will be implemented to strengthen the ecosystem to increase productivity, including uplifting research, development, commercialisation and innovation (R&D&C&I) in new technology and improving access to financing in supporting innovation and skills development.",""],[1,"65","1","Research, Development, Commercialisation and Innovation Support","In addition, various strategies at the sectoral level will be implemented to strengthen the ecosystem to increase productivity, including uplifting research, development, commercialisation and innovation (R&D&C&I) in new technology and improving access to financing in supporting innovation and skills development.",""],[1,"65","1","Innovation and Skills Development Financing Access","In addition, various strategies at the sectoral level will be implemented to strengthen the ecosystem to increase productivity, including uplifting research, development, commercialisation and innovation (R&D&C&I) in new technology and improving access to financing in supporting innovation and skills development.",""],[1,"82","2","Economic Sector Rejuvenation Programme","In the Twelfth Plan, concerted efforts will be undertaken to rejuvenate all economic sectors to ensure the growth momentum is restored.",""],[1,"82","2","Productivity Enhancement and Technology Adoption Initiative","the focus will be on boosting productivity mainly through accelerating technology adoption",""],[1,"90","7","Economic Rejuvenation and Productivity Enhancement Measures","In the Twelfth Plan, efforts will focus on rejuvenating the economy to ensure the momentum of growth is restored.",""],[1,"94","1","Productivity Planning, Evaluation and Monitoring Strengthening","Emphasis will be given to strengthening the planning, evaluation and monitoring mechanism",""],[1,"94","1","Productivity Nexus Initiative Scaling-Up","measures will be undertaken to scale up successful initiatives of the Productivity Nexus",""],[1,"99","3","Productivity Nexus Model Expansion","Under the Twelfth Plan, the Productivity Nexus model will be further leveraged to drive the implementation of productivity initiatives at the sectoral level.",""],[1,"99","3","Multi-Stakeholder Productivity Initiative Delivery","These initiatives will be undertaken through close collaboration among government, private sector and academia.",""],[1,"99","3","Scaling Up Existing Nexus Initiatives and Programmes","Successful initiatives and programmes under the existing nine Nexus will be scaled up to boost overall productivity.",""],[1,"99","4","Expansion of the Productivity Nexus Model","The Productivity Nexus model, where the private sector takes the lead in formulating and implementing productivity improvement programmes at the sector level will be extended to cover more sectors.",""],[1,"99","4","Establishment of New Productivity Nexus in Construction and Logistics","At least two new Productivity Nexus will be established during the Twelfth Plan, namely construction and logistics services.",""],[1,"99","5","Productivity Nexus Programme Review and Scaling Mechanism","A comprehensive review will be carried out to assess the effectiveness of initiatives and programmes under the nine Productivity Nexus.",""],[1,"141","1","Strategic and High-Impact Industry Development Programme","Moving forward, efforts will be undertaken to accelerate the development of strategic and high impact industries and enhance the capacity and capability of entrepreneurs as well as enterprises.",""],[1,"141","1","Entrepreneur and Enterprise Capacity-Building Initiative","Moving forward, efforts will be undertaken to accelerate the development of strategic and high impact industries and enhance the capacity and capability of entrepreneurs as well as enterprises.",""],[2,"32","2","Economic Sector Rejuvenation Programme","Over the next five years, concerted efforts will be undertaken to rejuvenate all the economic sectors, namely services, manufacturing, agriculture, mining and quarrying as well as construction.",""],[2,"32","2","Productivity Growth and Export Market Expansion Initiative","Meanwhile, productivity growth will be boosted, export markets will be expanded, financial intermediation ecosystem effectiveness and role of industrial estates and food production areas will be enhanced, while governance and policies will be improved.",""],[2,"32","2","Strategic and High-Impact Industry Development","Focus will also be placed on accelerating the development of eight strategic and high impact industries and activities, namely electrical and electronics (E&E), global services (GS), aerospace, creative, tourism, halal, smart farming and biomass.",""],[2,"32","3","Strategic and High-Impact Industries Development Initiative","Game Changer II aims to enhance the contribution of the strategic and high impact industries and activities to the economy by leveraging on advanced technologies, digitalisation and niche capabilities.",""],[2,"34","6","Productivity Acceleration and 4IR Readiness Programme","Efforts to accelerate productivity will continue under the Twelfth Plan, which will contribute to higher labour productivity growth.",""],[2,"42","2","Productivity and Quality Investment Enhancement Strategy","Macroeconomic strategies will focus on enhancing productivity, promoting quality investment, accelerating structural economic transition, increasing participation in the global value chain (GVC) and ensuring long-term fiscal sustainability.",""],[2,"64","1","Macroeconomic Policy Package for Growth Restoration","The macroeconomic policies for the Twelfth Plan will focus on restoring the economic growth and strengthening the economic fundamentals.",""],[2,"64","1","Competitive Economic Environment Enhancement","Emphasis will be given to ensure a conducive and competitive economic environment towards achieving greater economic resilience.",""],[2,"65","1","National Productivity Planning Mechanism Strengthening","At the national level, the planning mechanism will be strengthened, the successful initiatives under the Productivity Nexus will be scaled up and the productivity gap between the large firms and MSMEs will be narrowed.",""],[2,"65","1","Productivity Nexus Scale-Up","At the national level, the planning mechanism will be strengthened, the successful initiatives under the Productivity Nexus will be scaled up and the productivity gap between the large firms and MSMEs will be narrowed.",""],[2,"65","1","Sectoral Productivity Ecosystem Strengthening","In addition, various strategies at the sectoral level will be implemented to strengthen the ecosystem to increase productivity, including uplifting research, development, commercialisation and innovation (R&D&C&I) in new technology and improving access to financing in supporting innovation and skills development.",""],[2,"67","5","High-Potential Growth Industries Acceleration","Emphasis will also be placed on accelerating the development of high potential growth industries, including the halal, creative and tourism.",""],[2,"67","6","Manufacturing Sector Upgrading and Industry 4.0 Adoption","Efforts will also be undertaken to leverage digital technology and enhance mechanisms to boost productivity, in line with the National Policy on Industry 4.0 (Industry4WRD).",""],[2,"67","6","Value Chain Development in Shipbuilding, Pharmaceuticals, and Medical Devices","focus will also be given to growth along the value chain in shipbuilding, pharmaceutical and medical devices.",""],[2,"67","6","Manufacturing Diversification into Higher Value-Added Products","the manufacturing sector will continue to focus on shifting into higher value-added, diverse and complex products.",""],[2,"69","7","Product Substitution for Parts and Components","continuous efforts will be undertaken to enhance product substitution, especially for parts and components to reduce the import content",""],[2,"69","8","Resource-Based Downstream Industry Development Initiative","initiatives to strengthen resource- based downstream activities and related services will be escalated",""],[2,"69","8","Export Industry Technology Upgrading Initiative","boosting competitive advantage of main export industries through adoption of new technologies",""],[2,"74","4","Productivity and Value-Chain Upgrading Support","A key priority moving forward is to shift all sectors towards higher value-added activities.",""],[2,"75","3","Strategic and High-Impact Industry Development Programme","In the next five years, focus will be placed on accelerating the development of strategic and high impact industries, namely electrical and electronics (E&E), global services (GS), aerospace, creative, tourism, halal, biomass as well as smart farming activities.",""],[2,"75","3","High-Technology Adoption and Innovation Upgrading Initiative","Efforts will be aimed among others at promoting high technology adoption, governance reforms, talent upskilling, innovation and R&D to transform these industries into producing high value-added products and services, expanding global market and attracting quality investments.",""],[2,"77","3","Digitalisation and Advanced Technologies Investment Promotion","Spur investment in digitalisation and advanced technologies, build niche capabilities, and generate significant multiplier effects.",""],[2,"77","8","E&E Industry Upgrading through Design and Front-End Manufacturing","Boosting the E&E industry to move up the value chain through design and development (D&D), as well as front- end manufacturing activities.",""],[2,"77","11","Aerospace Industry Transformation Initiative","Transforming the aerospace industry with a focus on high-end, technology- driven manufacturing.",""],[2,"77","12","Regional Global Services Hub Attraction Initiative","Attracting multinational companies to position Malaysia as the regional GS hub.",""],[2,"77","13","Biomass Industry High Value-Added Product and Service Development","Accelerating the development of high value-added products and services in the biomass industry.",""],[2,"82","2","Economic Sector Rejuvenation Programme","In the Twelfth Plan, concerted efforts will be undertaken to rejuvenate all economic sectors to ensure the growth momentum is restored.",""],[2,"82","2","Technology Adoption Acceleration Initiative","the focus will be on boosting productivity mainly through accelerating technology adoption",""],[2,"86","4","High Value-Added and Complex Product Development Programme","The High Value-Added and Complex Product Development Programme was introduced in 2016 to improve capacities and competencies of industry players in developing high value- added complex products.",""],[2,"86","4","Automotive Vendor Development Programmes","various programmes were implemented to increase the number of vendors that meet the minimum requirements of original equipment manufacturers (OEMs) and participate in the supply chain.",""],[2,"95","1","Value Chain Upgrading and Productivity Enhancement Measures","Measures will be introduced to enable all economic sectors to move up the value chain by improving operational and production processes, adopting emerging technology in new product development, accelerating talent development as well as increasing high value-added activities.",""],[2,"95","5","Manufacturing Sector Modernisation and Digitalisation","Efforts will be undertaken to modernise and digitalise operations and processes in the manufacturing sector, which will propel the industry towards higher productivity.",""],[2,"95","5","Industry4WRD Implementation Intensification","The implementation of Industry4WRD will be intensified, particularly in developing local system integrator capabilities to provide innovative solutions related to digitalisation of production processes.",""],[2,"95","5","RAP Enhancement for Industry 4.0 Adoption","the implementation of RAP will be enhanced to facilitate more firms in adopting Industry 4.0 related technologies for productivity improvement.",""],[2,"96","5","High Value-Added Manufacturing Development Strategy","The growth strategy in the manufacturing sector will focus on producing high value-added and complex products, especially in the E&E, chemical and chemical products, machinery and equipment (M&E) and aerospace.",""],[2,"96","5","Manufacturing Value Chain Expansion Initiative","Meanwhile, avenues for growth along the value chain in the shipbuilding, pharmaceutical and medical devices will be explored.",""],[2,"96","5","Automotive High Value-Added Activities Support","Intensification of high value-added activities in the automotive industry will be supported through the implementation of the NAP 2020.",""],[2,"96","5","Industry4WRD Technology Adoption in Manufacturing","The manufacturing sector will also focus on developing and incorporating key technologies, including IoT, AI, sensor fusion as well as deep and machine learning into manufacturing products, in line with the implementation of the Industry4WRD.",""],[2,"96","5","Local Production of Advanced Critical Parts and Components","The sector also aims to increase the production of advanced critical parts and components locally to reduce imports, which includes using robotics application to cater for increasing demand.",""],[2,"97","3","Industrial Collaboration Programme Strengthening","The Industrial Collaboration Programme (ICP), a component of the Government Procurement policy will be promoted as a strategic tool to support the effort in moving up the value chain through high technology uptakes and innovation strategies.",""],[2,"97","4","Targeted Value Chain Upgrading and Technology Adoption","A more targeted approach will be taken to move the economic sectors up the value chain, producing high value, diverse and complex products through technology adoption.",""],[2,"97","4","Experimental Research and Commercialisation Prioritisation","Experimental research and commercialisation will be prioritised to encourage more demand-driven R&D activities.",""],[2,"97","6","Future Industries Centre of Excellence","a centre of excellence for future industries will be established to coordinate and integrate best practices and research as well as provide support and training",""],[2,"452","6","Industry Value Chain Upgrading Measures","During the Twelfth Plan, measures will be introduced to support all industries to move up the value chain.",""],[2,"452","6","4IR, Digitalisation, and Green Economy Adoption","The services, manufacturing, agriculture, mining and construction sectors will be rejuvenated by encouraging these sectors to move up the value chain by adopting 4IR technologies, digitalisation and the green economy.",""],[2,"452","6","High-Potential Industry Development Initiative","The electrical and electronics, global services, aerospace, creative, tourism, halal and biomass industries, as well as smart farming activities, will be enhanced as new sources of growth.",""],[2,"495","15","Malaysia Debt Venture Technology Acceleration and Commercialisation Scheme","Malaysia Debt Venture Technology Acceleration and Commercialisation Scheme",""]],"31":[[1,"67","5","Wholesale and Retail Trade Modernisation Strategy","The wholesale and retail trade subsector will continue to be the main contributor, supported by strategies to modernise the subsector as well as enhance the efficiency and effectiveness of the supply chain.",""],[1,"67","5","Technology Adoption for Services Sector Productivity","Concerted efforts will be undertaken to ensure higher adoption of technology to enhance efficiency and productivity within the sector in line with the Malaysia Digital Economy Blueprint.",""],[1,"87","3","Services Sector Transformation under the Services Sector Blueprint","Efforts to transform the services sector into more knowledge- intensive and innovation-led sector were undertaken in line with the Services Sector Blueprint, 2015-2020 (SSB) through 29 action plans.",""],[1,"95","6","Technology Adoption for Services Sector Efficiency","Concerted efforts will be undertaken to ensure higher adoption of technology to enhance efficiency and productivity across the services sector.",""],[1,"95","6","4IR Adoption in Modern Services Subsector","Modern services subsectors, such as financial, professional and private healthcare services, will focus on the adoption of 4IR technologies to increase efficiency and effectiveness in service delivery.",""],[1,"95","6","Wholesale and Retail Modernisation Initiative","In the wholesale and retail subsector, emphasis will be on modernising business activities that are mostly manually operated.",""],[1,"95","6","Retail Digital Systems Investment Support","Large scale retailers will be encouraged to invest in systems that are cost-effective and improve consumer experience, including self-check-out, and pick and pack.",""],[1,"95","6","Multichannel Payment Gateway Adoption for Hawkers and Petty Traders","Meanwhile, hawkers and petty traders will be encouraged to adopt multichannel payment gateways, including e-payment and e-wallet, as a step to modernising their business.",""],[1,"96","6","Modern Services Subsector Upgrading","the modern services subsector will focus on accelerating high value-added activities, adapting technological changes, improving labour productivity",""],[1,"97","1","Professional Services 4IR Adoption Roadmap","a comprehensive roadmap for all professional services to embrace 4IR will be developed.",""],[1,"97","1","4IR Technology Adoption for Local SMPPs","local SMPPs will be encouraged to provide high value- added services through the adoption of 4IR technology such as BDA, AI and IoT.",""],[1,"98","7","Modern Services Investment Incentive Enhancement","Initiatives to spur growth in the services sector will continue to focus on attracting quality investment, particularly in the modern services subsector by improving existing incentives.",""],[1,"110","3","Services Sector Blueprint","a new SSB, outlining the policy framework and strategic approaches will be implemented to further develop the sector",""],[1,"127","4","Global Services Hub Enabling Ecosystem Development","To create this environment, clear and supportive policies, a better regulatory and business environment, talent development, digital infrastructure and air connectivity to major cities are required.",""],[1,"127","5","Business Environment and Investment Facilitation Reforms","improvements will be made in enhancing the ease of doing business, facilitating the movement of talent, enabling supportive tax policies, greater flexibility in the movement of funds, intermediary liability protection as well as formalising alternative funding models and enhancing R&D.",""],[1,"127","7","Malaysia Digital Economy Blueprint Implementation","The implementation of the Malaysia Digital Economy Blueprint is expected to boost Malaysia's digital infrastructure and connectivity.",""],[1,"127","7","5G Network and Cloud Storage Services Expansion","In this regard, the 5G network and cloud storage services will be a catalyst to create a conducive ecosystem in enhancing Malaysia's attractiveness as an investment destination.",""],[1,"127","8","International Air Connectivity Enhancement","In this regard, collaboration with international airlines will be intensified to further improve air connectivity.",""],[2,"67","5","Wholesale and Retail Trade Modernisation Strategy","The wholesale and retail trade subsector will continue to be the main contributor, supported by strategies to modernise the subsector as well as enhance the efficiency and effectiveness of the supply chain.",""],[2,"67","5","Technology Adoption for Sector Productivity","Concerted efforts will be undertaken to ensure higher adoption of technology to enhance efficiency and productivity within the sector in line with the Malaysia Digital Economy Blueprint.",""],[2,"87","3","Services Sector Transformation under the Services Sector Blueprint","Efforts to transform the services sector into more knowledge- intensive and innovation-led sector were undertaken in line with the Services Sector Blueprint, 2015-2020 (SSB) through 29 action plans.",""],[2,"95","6","Technology Adoption for Services Sector Efficiency","Concerted efforts will be undertaken to ensure higher adoption of technology to enhance efficiency and productivity across the services sector.",""],[2,"95","6","4IR Adoption in Modern Services Subsections","Modern services subsectors, such as financial, professional and private healthcare services, will focus on the adoption of 4IR technologies to increase efficiency and effectiveness in service delivery.",""],[2,"95","6","Wholesale and Retail Business Modernisation","In the wholesale and retail subsector, emphasis will be on modernising business activities that are mostly manually operated.",""],[2,"95","6","Retail Digital Systems Investment Support","Large scale retailers will be encouraged to invest in systems that are cost-effective and improve consumer experience, including self-check-out, and pick and pack.",""],[2,"95","6","Multichannel Payment Adoption for Hawkers and Petty Traders","Meanwhile, hawkers and petty traders will be encouraged to adopt multichannel payment gateways, including e-payment and e-wallet, as a step to modernising their business.",""],[2,"96","6","Modern Services Subsector Upgrading","the modern services subsector will focus on accelerating high value-added activities, adapting technological changes, improving labour productivity",""],[2,"97","1","4IR Adoption Support for Local SMPPs in Professional Services","local SMPPs will be encouraged to provide high value- added services through the adoption of 4IR technology such as BDA, AI and IoT.",""],[2,"97","1","Comprehensive 4IR Roadmap for Professional Services","a comprehensive roadmap for all professional services to embrace 4IR will be developed.",""],[2,"109","2","Institutional Framework for Professional Services Development","A comprehensive institutional framework for professional services will be formulated to enhance SMPPs capacity and capability in expanding high value-added services.",""],[2,"110","3","Services Sector Blueprint","a new SSB, outlining the policy framework and strategic approaches will be implemented to further develop the sector",""],[2,"127","5","Business Services Investment Facilitation and Regulatory Reform Package","improvements will be made in enhancing the ease of doing business, facilitating the movement of talent, enabling supportive tax policies, greater flexibility in the movement of funds, intermediary liability protection as well as formalising alternative funding models and enhancing R&D.",""],[2,"127","6","Professional and Service Provider Capability Upgrading Programme","the capabilities of professionals and professional service providers need to be upgraded.",""],[2,"127","6","Public-Private Talent Development Partnership","Public- private collaboration in talent development especially upskilling and reskilling will be promoted to ensure a sustainable talent pipeline to meet industry demand.",""],[2,"127","6","Domestic Investment Strategic Fund Digitalisation Support","existing funds such as the Domestic Investment Strategic Fund (DISF) will be further leveraged to accelerate digitalisation and enhance local GS capabilities.",""]],"32":[[1,"67","6","Manufacturing Sector Industry 4.0 Productivity Enhancement","Efforts will also be undertaken to leverage digital technology and enhance mechanisms to boost productivity, in line with the National Policy on Industry 4.0 (Industry4WRD).",""],[1,"67","6","Adoption of Disruptive Technologies for Manufacturing Modernisation","Emphasis will also be given to capitalise on the benefits of disruptive technologies in gearing up for the 4IR.",""],[1,"68","8","High-Value Knowledge-Intensive Industry Promotion","Efforts will be undertaken to promote high value-added economic activities and attract more investment in knowledge-intensive industries to spur the creation of skilled and high-paying jobs.",""],[1,"69","7","Product Substitution for Parts and Components","continuous efforts will be undertaken to enhance product substitution, especially for parts and components to reduce the import content",""],[1,"74","4","Value-Added Industrial Upgrading and Productivity Enhancement","A key priority moving forward is to shift all sectors towards higher value-added activities.",""],[1,"75","3","Strategic and High-Impact Industry Development Initiative","In the next five years, focus will be placed on accelerating the development of strategic and high impact industries, namely electrical and electronics (E&E), global services (GS), aerospace, creative, tourism, halal, biomass as well as smart farming activities.",""],[1,"75","3","High Technology Adoption and Innovation Upgrade Measures","Efforts will be aimed among others at promoting high technology adoption, governance reforms, talent upskilling, innovation and R&D to transform these industries into producing high value-added products and services, expanding global market and attracting quality investments.",""],[1,"77","8","E&E Industry Value Chain Upgrading through Design and Front-End Manufacturing","Boosting the E&E industry to move up the value chain through design and development (D&D), as well as front- end manufacturing activities.",""],[1,"77","13","Biomass Industry High Value-Added Product and Service Development","Accelerating the development of high value-added products and services in the biomass industry.",""],[1,"94","1","Value Chain Upgrading Measures","moving up the value chain",""],[1,"95","1","Value Chain Upgrading Measures for Economic Sectors","Measures will be introduced to enable all economic sectors to move up the value chain by improving operational and production processes, adopting emerging technology in new product development, accelerating talent development as well as increasing high value-added activities.",""],[1,"95","5","Manufacturing Sector Modernisation and Digitalisation","Efforts will be undertaken to modernise and digitalise operations and processes in the manufacturing sector, which will propel the industry towards higher productivity.",""],[1,"95","5","Industry4WRD Implementation Intensification","The implementation of Industry4WRD will be intensified, particularly in developing local system integrator capabilities to provide innovative solutions related to digitalisation of production processes.",""],[1,"95","5","RAP Expansion for Industry 4.0 Adoption","the implementation of RAP will be enhanced to facilitate more firms in adopting Industry 4.0 related technologies for productivity improvement.",""],[1,"96","5","High Value-Added Manufacturing Growth Strategy","The growth strategy in the manufacturing sector will focus on producing high value-added and complex products, especially in the E&E, chemical and chemical products, machinery and equipment (M&E) and aerospace.",""],[1,"96","5","Manufacturing Value Chain Expansion in Shipbuilding, Pharmaceuticals, and Medical Devices","Meanwhile, avenues for growth along the value chain in the shipbuilding, pharmaceutical and medical devices will be explored.",""],[1,"96","5","Industry4WRD Technology Adoption in Manufacturing","The manufacturing sector will also focus on developing and incorporating key technologies, including IoT, AI, sensor fusion as well as deep and machine learning into manufacturing products, in line with the implementation of the Industry4WRD.",""],[1,"96","5","Local Production of Advanced Critical Parts and Components","The sector also aims to increase the production of advanced critical parts and components locally to reduce imports, which includes using robotics application to cater for increasing demand.",""]],"33":[[1,"108","5","Dedicated Mineral Subsector Authority","These include establishing a dedicated authority for mineral subsector and reforming existing institutions to enhance effectiveness and efficiency of service delivery.",""],[1,"108","5","Institutional Reform to Improve Service Delivery Efficiency","These include establishing a dedicated authority for mineral subsector and reforming existing institutions to enhance effectiveness and efficiency of service delivery.",""],[1,"108","6","Mineral Industry Development Board","a mineral industry development board will be established to systematically regulate and drive the development of a sustainable mineral subsector throughout the value chain.",""],[1,"109","1","Midstream and Downstream Mineral Investment Promotion","attracting investments in the midstream and downstream activities",""],[1,"109","1","Mineral Technology Adoption and R&D Collaboration Initiative","encouraging the adoption of technology and intensifying collaboration in mineral-related R&D between local and international industry players",""],[1,"310","3","Mineral Resources Management Enhancement","efforts will focus on strengthening the sustainable utilisation of natural resources, enhancing mineral resources management, diversifying conservation funding as well as ensuring fair and equitable sharing of benefits.",""],[1,"310","5","Strategic Minerals Geospatial Mapping","A more accurate geospatial map for strategic minerals will be prepared for states to optimise the utilisation of the resources and land-use planning.",""],[1,"310","5","Minerals and Mining Law Enforcement","Laws related to minerals and mining activities will be strictly enforced to minimise environmental degradation from these activities.",""],[1,"310","5","Sustainable Mining Standards and Rating Adoption","Standard operating procedures on sustainable mining practices will be developed, while mining operators will be further encouraged to subscribe to sustainability rating.",""],[1,"310","5","Digital Technologies for Mineral Planning and Monitoring","The adoption of new technologies will be encouraged to enhance efficiency in planning and monitoring as well as adopt best practices in mineral exploration and processing.",""],[1,"310","5","Minerals Subsector Governance Review","The governance of the minerals subsector will be reviewed to ensure the development of a sustainable industry throughout the entire value chain.",""],[1,"310","5","Mineral Industry Development Board","A mineral industry development board will be established to regulate and drive the development of a sustainable mineral subsector.",""],[2,"108","6","Mineral Industry Development Board","a mineral industry development board will be established to systematically regulate and drive the development of a sustainable mineral subsector throughout the value chain.",""],[2,"109","1","Mineral Sector Investment and R&D Collaboration Promotion","attracting investments in the midstream and downstream activities as well as encouraging the adoption of technology and intensifying collaboration in mineral-related R&D between local and international industry players.",""],[2,"310","5","Strategic Minerals Geospatial Mapping","A more accurate geospatial map for strategic minerals will be prepared for states to optimise the utilisation of the resources and land-use planning.",""],[2,"310","5","Minerals and Mining Law Enforcement","Laws related to minerals and mining activities will be strictly enforced to minimise environmental degradation from these activities.",""],[2,"310","5","Sustainable Mining Standards and Rating Promotion","Standard operating procedures on sustainable mining practices will be developed, while mining operators will be further encouraged to subscribe to sustainability rating.",""],[2,"310","5","Mineral Exploration Technology Adoption","The adoption of new technologies will be encouraged to enhance efficiency in planning and monitoring as well as adopt best practices in mineral exploration and processing.",""],[2,"310","5","Minerals Subsector Governance Review","The governance of the minerals subsector will be reviewed to ensure the development of a sustainable industry throughout the entire value chain.",""],[2,"310","5","Mineral Industry Development Board","A mineral industry development board will be established to regulate and drive the development of a sustainable mineral subsector.",""]],"34":[[1,"100","4","GLC Role Enhancement and Competitive Market Reform","the role of GLCs will be enhanced while a more fair and healthy competitive environment will be encouraged to improve market efficiency for the private sector to expand into domestic and international markets.",""],[2,"110","6","Wholesale and Retail Self-Regulation Framework","Self-regulation will be introduced to encourage adherence to legal and safety regulations, particularly in the wholesale and retail subsector.",""],[2,"110","6","Amendment of Regulations for Business Associations and Federations","Current regulations will be amended to fully empower the associations and federations to undertake the regulatory responsibility as well as enforce compulsory registration of businesses with the respective associations and federations.",""],[2,"111","1","Productivity Boosting and Market Access Expansion Strategy","Moving forward, the Twelfth Plan will give priority to boost productivity, expand market access, enhance financial intermediation, promote balanced industrial development as well as improve policy and governance.",""],[2,"111","1","Financial Intermediation Enhancement and Governance Improvement Measures","Moving forward, the Twelfth Plan will give priority to boost productivity, expand market access, enhance financial intermediation, promote balanced industrial development as well as improve policy and governance.",""]],"35":[[1,"101","6","Industry Collaboration and Smart Partnerships for Market Access","Efforts will be intensified to increase collaboration among industry players, including through smart partnerships, to enhance market access.",""],[1,"101","6","Expanded Contract Farming Scheme","The contract farming approach will be further expanded in the agriculture sector.",""],[1,"101","7","MNC-MSME Backward Linkage Collaboration Incentives","multinational companies (MNCs) will be incentivised to collaborate with MSMEs to strengthen backward linkages to assist MSMEs in participating in the global value chain.",""],[1,"101","7","Technology Transfer to Domestic Firms","This collaboration will expedite technology transfer to domestic firms.",""],[1,"101","7","MSME Marketing Advisory Support Through Industry Associations","MSMEs will be encouraged to leverage industry associations to obtain marketing advisory services and information in increasing market access.",""],[1,"101","8","Construction Sector Industry Consortium","a consortium of industry players in the construction sector will be established to integrate various local industry players, including contractors,",""],[1,"102","1","International Project Bidding Consortium","suppliers and financiers, to bid for international projects.",""],[1,"102","1","Industry Consortium Formation","Establishment of the consortium will allow the industry players to capitalise on individual strengths and create synergistic value to enhance competitiveness.",""],[1,"102","2","GLC Hand-Holding Programme for SMPPs","GLCs will be encouraged to implement hand-holding programmes for SMPPs in the services sector, particularly the business and professional services subsector.",""],[1,"102","2","M&A Support for Multi-disciplinary Enterprise Formation","SMPPs will be encouraged to form companies through M&A in establishing strong multi-disciplinary enterprises as well as digitalise and adopt advanced technology.",""],[2,"114","2","MSME Capability Strengthening and Inclusive Growth Support","Efforts will also be undertaken to boost entrepreneurs capabilities and promote inclusive growth by strengthening MSMEs participation in the economy.",""],[2,"126","5","MNC Support for Local MSME Capability Enhancement","Multinational companies (MNCs) will be encouraged to facilitate the enhancement of local MSMEs capabilities.",""],[2,"126","5","Lighthouse Project Intensification","The implementation of the Lighthouse Project, which was introduced in 2020, will be intensified to encourage MNCs to assist local MSMEs in embracing digitalisation and Globalization 4.05 in their business models.",""],[2,"126","5","Fourth Industrial Revolution Business Platform","the establishment of the Fourth Industrial Revolution (4IR) business platform will provide opportunities to E&E companies and MSMEs to accelerate 4IR technology adoption and innovation.",""],[2,"129","25","SME Development for Manufacturing Advancement","Develop SMEs for manufacturing advancement",""],[2,"138","2","Vendor Development Programme Expansion","The Vendor Development Programme (VDP) will be expanded in creating more competent Bumiputera vendors among MSMEs.",""],[2,"138","2","Anchor Company Development through GLC and MNC Collaboration","Initiatives to develop more anchor companies through collaboration with GLCs and MNCs will be intensified in promoting an integrated supply chain and providing more business opportunities.",""],[2,"138","2","Vendor Support Services Enhancement","Other support programmes, such as certification, marketing and branding, packaging as well as product development will be enhanced to improve the capacity and capability of vendors in meeting industry requirements.",""],[2,"138","3","Market Access Expansion for MSMEs","Measures to enhance market access and opportunities will be further expanded to assist MSMEs in increasing sales of goods and services domestically and internationally.",""],[2,"138","3","Government Procurement Support for MSMEs","Government Procurement (GP) will be fully leveraged as a means to support MSMEs in the domestic market, instil business confidence, drive innovation, and stimulate the development of products for local content requirements.",""],[2,"138","3","Accelerated MSME Participation in Government Procurement","efforts will be accelerated to ensure local MSMEs, including manufacturers to actively participate in GP.",""],[2,"138","4","MSME Capacity Building for Global Supply Chain Integration","For this purpose, the capacity and capability of MSMEs in producing products and services that comply with the global supply chain standards will be strengthened.",""],[2,"138","4","Enhanced MSME Capacity Building Programmes","Capacity building programmes will be enhanced with emphasis on 4IR, strategic management, certification, marketing and branding, packaging, product development and eCommerce.",""],[2,"138","6","MSME Export Internationalisation Support","MSMEs that demonstrate high export growth potential will be facilitated through the provision of advisory services, international market intelligence, IP registration as well as brand and product development.",""],[2,"138","6","Trade Facilitation and Cross-Border Regulatory Reform","Initiatives will also focus on trade facilitation measures, including reducing regulatory barriers to cross-border trade and business through G2G partnerships and collaboration among countries within ASEAN and APEC as well as with other international organisations.",""],[2,"138","6","FTA Utilisation for MSME Market Expansion","Efforts will also be undertaken to leverage the benefits of FTAs in widening market access and accelerating the internationalisation of MSMEs.",""]],"36":[[1,"103","1","Services Export Promotion and Brand Enhancement","In the services sector, efforts will be undertaken to increase export of local products and services to further reduce the services trade deficit.",""],[1,"103","1","Digital Marketing for Private Healthcare Brand Visibility","For private healthcare subsector, Malaysia healthcare brand visibility will be strengthened by intensifying marketing and promotion digitally.",""],[1,"103","1","High-Intensity Revenue Services Promotion Strategy","Moving forward the industry will shift its focus on promotion of high intensity revenue services such as fertility and oncology, as well as strengthening existing network and channels through strategic partners in identified key markets especially ASEAN and Middle East.",""],[1,"103","1","Niche Programme Development for International Student Attraction","The potential of private HEIs will be leveraged by introducing niche programmes to attract international students.",""],[1,"103","1","Private HEI-Corporate Strategic Partnership Scheme","Strategic collaboration between private HEIs, and large corporations as financial partners, will be encouraged.",""],[1,"103","1","Retail and F&B Export Initiative Enhancement","Meanwhile, the various export initiatives and programmes in the retail and F&B subsectors, including the Enhanced Franchise Development Programme and the Product Transformation and Distribution Programme will be enhanced to improve their effectiveness.",""],[1,"103","1","Local Product and Service Brand Image Uplift","Measures will also be implemented to uplift the brand image of local products and services to increase international market presence.",""],[1,"103","2","Expansion and Strengthening of the Services Export Fund","The existing services export fund will be expanded to cover the business services focusing on high potential activities, while the implementation and monitoring of the fund will be strengthened.",""]],"37":[[1,"110","1","National Construction Sector Policy","A national policy on construction sector will be formulated to increase the resilience of the sector in responding to fast-changing demand and technological development.",""],[1,"110","1","Construction Sector Implementation and Coordination Mechanism","An implementation mechanism will be put in place to enhance coordination and streamline governance at all levels of government.",""],[1,"110","5","Construction Law Amendment and Guideline Streamlining","In the construction sector, amendments will be made to relevant laws, while guidelines will be streamlined to realign the role of the Federal Government and local authorities.",""],[2,"110","1","National Construction Sector Policy","A national policy on construction sector will be formulated to increase the resilience of the sector in responding to fast-changing demand and technological development.",""],[2,"110","1","Construction Sector Governance Coordination Mechanism","An implementation mechanism will be put in place to enhance coordination and streamline governance at all levels of government.",""],[2,"110","5","Construction Law Amendment and Guideline Streamlining","In the construction sector, amendments will be made to relevant laws, while guidelines will be streamlined to realign the role of the Federal Government and local authorities.",""]],"38":[[1,"118","1","Integrated Domestic Halal Industry Development","During the Eleventh Plan, initiatives were undertaken to ensure an integrated and comprehensive development of the domestic halal industry.",""],[1,"133","1","Halal Industry Capacity and Competitiveness Enhancement","Measures will be undertaken to enhance the capacity and capability of the halal industry by uplifting the development of halal talent, establishing halal professional recognition, accelerating industry development including Bumiputera participation, increasing product competitiveness and positioning Malaysia as a global halal hub.",""],[1,"133","4","Halal Industry Master Plan 2030","The halal industry will be further developed by leveraging domestic strength, including by increasing the participation of Bumiputera companies through the implementation of the Halal Industry Master Plan 2030 (HIMP 2030).",""],[2,"133","1","Halal Industry Capacity and Competitiveness Enhancement","Measures will be undertaken to enhance the capacity and capability of the halal industry by uplifting the development of halal talent, establishing halal professional recognition, accelerating industry development including Bumiputera participation, increasing product competitiveness and positioning Malaysia as a global halal hub.",""],[2,"133","4","Halal Industry Master Plan 2030","The halal industry will be further developed by leveraging domestic strength, including by increasing the participation of Bumiputera companies through the implementation of the Halal Industry Master Plan 2030 (HIMP 2030).",""],[2,"133","5","MSME Halal Industry Upgrading Programme","High performing MSMEs will be groomed as home-grown halal local champions.",""],[2,"133","5","Local Company Supply Chain Participation Support","the capacity and capability of local companies will be strengthened to facilitate participation in the supply chain of MNCs.",""],[2,"133","5","Malaysia Halal Analysis Centre Enhancement","The Malaysia Halal Analysis Centre (MyHAC) will be enhanced to improve its function in conducting analysis and providing scientific evidence for halal authentication and traceability.",""],[2,"133","5","Halal Supply Chain Tracking and Monitoring Improvement","The tracking and monitoring mechanisms for halal integrity along the supply chain will be improved to be more transparent and further boost consumer confidence.",""],[2,"134","1","Halal Supply Chain Programme Expansion","Inclusive participation, particularly involving Bumiputera companies in the halal supply chain will be further promoted through the improvement of existing programmes and the creation of new programmes to facilitate the expansion of high value products.",""],[2,"134","1","Halal Innovation Business Incubator Programme","Halal innovation-focused business incubator programmes will also be implemented to grow local companies and connect with other business incubators globally for better networking, acceptance and recognition.",""],[2,"134","1","Dedicated Fund for Halal Exporters","A dedicated fund for halal exporters will be established to support the formation of consortiums, improve branding and promote business matching with global partners to capture a larger share of the halal market.",""],[2,"134","1","Halal Business Start-up Fundraising Initiative","In addition, fundraising activities through waqf and equity crowdfunding will be conducted to support halal business start-ups.",""],[2,"134","2","Halal Brand Promotion and Market Expansion Initiative","The Malaysian halal brand will be strengthened through targeted campaigns and promotions as well as strategic collaboration and partnerships to capture new growth opportunities in existing markets and penetrate new markets.",""],[2,"134","2","Halal Ecosystem Consultancy Services for Foreign Countries","Halal services, in terms of consultancy on halal ecosystem development, will also be offered to interested countries including non-Muslim majority countries to build Malaysia's halal brand recognition.",""],[2,"134","2","Halal Standard Accreditation and Certification Enhancement","The halal-related Malaysian Standard (MS), which includes accreditation and certification, will be enhanced as a key enabler to improve the competitiveness of products and services.",""],[2,"134","2","MSME Access to the Global Halal Market Programme","Access of MSMEs products to the global halal market will also be promoted through compliance with international standards and requirements, such as Hazard Analysis Critical Control Points (HACCP) and Good Manufacturing Practice (GMP), and utilisation of reputable online trading platforms.",""],[2,"134","2","Integrated Halal Database Enhancement","To enable data-driven decision-making, the integrated halal database comprising information on products, services, market trends and profiles will be enhanced.",""],[2,"134","3","Halal Supply Chain Improvement Initiative","The halal industry supply chain will be improved to position Malaysia as a global halal hub.",""],[2,"134","3","Halal Supply Chain Connectivity Enhancement","existing distribution centres, such as Digital Free Trade Zone (DFTZ), Port Klang Free Zone (PKFZ) and halal eCommerce platforms will be leveraged to promote seamless connectivity of the halal supply chain.",""],[2,"134","3","Halal Park Strengthening Programme","The role of halal parks will be strengthened to be more industry-friendly to attract new investments and expand existing businesses.",""],[2,"134","3","Revitalization of Underperforming Halal Parks","Existing underperforming halal parks will be revived through a holistic development approach to facilitate more integrated planning, coordination and implementation involving state authorities, investment promotion agencies and regional economic corridors authorities.",""],[2,"134","3","Halal Investment Incentive Enhancement","In addition, incentives will be improved to attract strategic partners to invest in halal promoted products and services.",""],[2,"134","4","Digital Advisory Platform for Financial Solutions","digital advisory platform will be established to provide financial solutions for local and international companies.",""],[2,"134","4","Halal Investment Promotion Initiative","Malaysia will also be promoted as a destination for halal investments through various international platforms, such as ASEAN, the Organisation of Islamic Cooperation (OIC) and chambers of commerce.",""],[2,"134","4","Export-Oriented Product and Service Promotion","The regional network and distribution channels of local large companies and MNCs will be leveraged in promoting export-oriented products and services.",""]],"39":[[1,"133","5","MSME Upgrading for Halal Industry Champions","High performing MSMEs will be groomed as home-grown halal local champions.",""],[1,"133","5","Local Company Capability Strengthening for MNC Supply Chains","the capacity and capability of local companies will be strengthened to facilitate participation in the supply chain of MNCs.",""],[1,"133","5","Malaysia Halal Analysis Centre Enhancement","The Malaysia Halal Analysis Centre (MyHAC) will be enhanced to improve its function in conducting analysis and providing scientific evidence for halal authentication and traceability.",""],[1,"133","5","Halal Integrity Tracking and Monitoring Improvement","the tracking and monitoring mechanisms for halal integrity along the supply chain will be improved to be more transparent and further boost consumer confidence.",""],[1,"134","1","Halal Supply Chain Participation and Programme Expansion","Inclusive participation, particularly involving Bumiputera companies in the halal supply chain will be further promoted through the improvement of existing programmes and the creation of new programmes to facilitate the expansion of high value products.",""],[1,"134","1","Halal Innovation Business Incubator Programme","Halal innovation-focused business incubator programmes will also be implemented to grow local companies and connect with other business incubators globally for better networking, acceptance and recognition.",""],[1,"134","1","Dedicated Fund for Halal Exporters","A dedicated fund for halal exporters will be established to support the formation of consortiums, improve branding and promote business matching with global partners to capture a larger share of the halal market.",""],[1,"134","1","Halal Business Start-up Fundraising Support","fundraising activities through waqf and equity crowdfunding will be conducted to support halal business start-ups.",""],[1,"134","2","Halal Brand Promotion and Market Expansion Campaigns","The Malaysian halal brand will be strengthened through targeted campaigns and promotions as well as strategic collaboration and partnerships to capture new growth opportunities in existing markets and penetrate new markets.",""],[1,"134","2","Halal Ecosystem Consultancy Services","Halal services, in terms of consultancy on halal ecosystem development, will also be offered to interested countries including non-Muslim majority countries to build Malaysia's halal brand recognition.",""],[1,"134","2","Halal Standard Accreditation and Certification Enhancement","The halal-related Malaysian Standard (MS), which includes accreditation and certification, will be enhanced as a key enabler to improve the competitiveness of products and services.",""],[1,"134","2","MSME Access to Global Halal Markets Programme","Access of MSMEs products to the global halal market will also be promoted through compliance with international standards and requirements, such as Hazard Analysis Critical Control Points (HACCP) and Good Manufacturing Practice (GMP), and utilisation of reputable online trading platforms.",""],[1,"134","2","Integrated Halal Database Enhancement","To enable data-driven decision-making, the integrated halal database comprising information on products, services, market trends and profiles will be enhanced.",""],[1,"134","3","Halal Supply Chain Enhancement Programme","The halal industry supply chain will be improved to position Malaysia as a global halal hub.",""],[1,"134","4","Digital Advisory Platform for Financial Solutions","digital advisory platform will be established to provide financial solutions for local and international companies.",""],[1,"134","4","Halal Investment Promotion Initiative","Malaysia will also be promoted as a destination for halal investments through various international platforms, such as ASEAN, the Organisation of Islamic Cooperation (OIC) and chambers of commerce.",""],[1,"134","4","Export-Oriented Product and Service Promotion","The regional network and distribution channels of local large companies and MNCs will be leveraged in promoting export-oriented products and services.",""],[1,"265","9","Halal Industry Strengthening in Sabah and Sarawak","The halal industry in Sabah and Sarawak will be strengthened to leverage the availability of resources and the growing global demand for halal products.",""],[1,"265","9","Bumiputera Entrepreneurship Development Programmes","Initiatives will be undertaken to increase participation of Bumiputera companies through entrepreneurship development programmes.",""],[1,"265","9","Halal Production Capacity and Market Access Upgrading","In addition, measures will be put in place to upscale the production capacity and quality, as well as improve access to the international market.",""],[1,"265","9","Halal Park Upgrading and Integrated Planning Approach","The existing halal parks including the Kota Kinabalu Industrial Park and Palm Oil Industrial Cluster Lahad Datu in Sabah, as well as Tanjung Manis Halal Hub in Sarawak, will be upgraded through a holistic development approach to enable more integrated planning, coordination and implementation in increasing the utilisation of the parks.",""]],"40":[[1,"127","2","Knowledge-Intensive Design Programmes for the E&E Subsector","Knowledge-intensive design programmes for the E&E subsector will be promoted to realise the importance of innovation and design activities thereby spurring growth in the industry.",""],[1,"127","2","Industry Design and Development Activity Promotion","Industry players will be encouraged to undertake D&D activities, particularly in integrated circuits (IC), IC packaging, embedded systems as well as test and engineering design services.",""],[1,"127","2","Design and Development Investment Incentives","Incentives will be provided to encourage companies to invest more in D&D activities.",""],[1,"127","3","Review of R&D Grants and Incentives","R&D grants and incentives will be reviewed to cater to advanced technology push and market pull activities.",""],[1,"127","3","Promotion of End-to-End R&D Activities","end-to- end R&D activities will be promoted to ensure the R&D outputs are able to go through extensive experimental development and testing programmes to meet the technology and product standards.",""],[1,"127","3","Streamlining of Research Institutions and Centres of Excellence","research institutions and centres of excellence will be streamlined to reduce redundancy and increase the effectiveness of conducting R&D activities.",""],[1,"127","3","Establishment of Dedicated Technology and Innovation Centres","Dedicated technology and innovation centres will be established to drive technology development, accelerate innovation and technology transfer as well as increase the development of home-grown technologies.",""],[1,"129","13","Industry 4.0 Technology Roadmap Development","Develop Industry 4.0 technology roadmap",""],[2,"127","2","Knowledge-Intensive Design Programmes for the E&E Subsector","Knowledge-intensive design programmes for the E&E subsector will be promoted to realise the importance of innovation and design activities thereby spurring growth in the industry.",""],[2,"127","2","Industry D&D Promotion in Integrated Circuits and Related Services","Industry players will be encouraged to undertake D&D activities, particularly in integrated circuits (IC), IC packaging, embedded systems as well as test and engineering design services.",""],[2,"127","2","Incentives for Corporate Design and Development Investment","Incentives will be provided to encourage companies to invest more in D&D activities.",""],[2,"127","3","Review of R&D Grants and Incentives","R&D grants and incentives will be reviewed to cater to advanced technology push and market pull activities.",""],[2,"127","3","Promotion of End-to-End R&D Activities","end-to- end R&D activities will be promoted to ensure the R&D outputs are able to go through extensive experimental development and testing programmes to meet the technology and product standards.",""],[2,"127","3","Streamlining of Research Institutions and Centres of Excellence","research institutions and centres of excellence will be streamlined to reduce redundancy and increase the effectiveness of conducting R&D activities.",""],[2,"127","3","Establishment of Dedicated Technology and Innovation Centres","Dedicated technology and innovation centres will be established to drive technology development, accelerate innovation and technology transfer as well as increase the development of home-grown technologies.",""],[2,"129","13","Industry 4.0 Technology Roadmap Development","Develop Industry 4.0 technology roadmap",""]],"41":[[1,"128","1","Aerospace Industry Transformation Initiative","The initiatives will include developing a sustainable ecosystem, clustering and zoning of aerospace activities, establishing an aerospace digital system and venturing into sustainable energy.",""],[1,"128","5","Enhanced Incentives and Financial Assistance for Industry Competitiveness","Incentives and financial assistance will be enhanced for the industry to remain competitive in the global value chain and promote sustainable growth.",""],[1,"128","5","Industrial Collaboration Programme Strengthening","the implementation of the Industrial Collaboration Programme (ICP) will be further strengthened to ensure more meaningful participation by local aerospace companies in Government procurement, particularly in the defence sector.",""],[1,"128","6","Aerospace Industry Clustering and Zoning Strategy","The development of the aerospace industry will be realigned to create specialised capabilities through the clustering and zoning of aerospace activities in selected economic areas.",""],[1,"129","15","Aerospace Industry Investment Roadmap","Develop aerospace industry investment roadmap",""],[1,"129","19","Business Jet MRO Expansion","Expand MRO activities for business jet",""],[1,"129","21","Fixed Based Operator Investment Attraction","Attract new Fixed Based Operator (FBO) investment",""],[1,"129","25","SME Development for Manufacturing Advancement","Develop SMEs for manufacturing advancement",""],[1,"266","6","Sabah Aerospace Industry Development","Thus, the development of the aerospace industry in Sabah will focus on maintenance, repair and overhaul (MRO), as well as becoming centre of excellence for skilled training.",""],[1,"266","6","Sarawak Helicopter Operations and MRO Development","the focus for Sarawak will be on helicopter operations and MRO.",""],[2,"128","1","Aerospace Industry Transformation Initiatives","The initiatives will include developing a sustainable ecosystem, clustering and zoning of aerospace activities, establishing an aerospace digital system and venturing into sustainable energy.",""],[2,"128","5","Enhanced Industrial Incentives and Financial Assistance","Incentives and financial assistance will be enhanced for the industry to remain competitive in the global value chain and promote sustainable growth.",""],[2,"128","5","R&D, Innovation, and High Value-Added Investment Incentive Review","incentives will be reviewed to accelerate R&D, innovation and high value-added investments.",""],[2,"128","5","Business Loan and Guarantee Liquidity Support","Loan and loan guarantees for businesses will be explored to enhance the industry access to liquidity in compensating for reduced cash flow due to the impact of the pandemic.",""],[2,"128","5","Industrial Collaboration Programme Strengthening","the implementation of the Industrial Collaboration Programme (ICP) will be further strengthened to ensure more meaningful participation by local aerospace companies in Government procurement, particularly in the defence sector.",""],[2,"128","6","Aerospace Industry Clustering and Zoning Strategy","The development of the aerospace industry will be realigned to create specialised capabilities through the clustering and zoning of aerospace activities in selected economic areas.",""],[2,"129","15","Aerospace Industry Investment Roadmap","Develop aerospace industry investment roadmap",""],[2,"129","19","Business Jet MRO Expansion","Expand MRO activities for business jet",""],[2,"129","21","Attract Fixed Based Operator Investment","Attract new Fixed Based Operator (FBO) investment",""],[2,"130","1","Bio-Jet Fuel Prototype Development Programme","a programme to produce Malaysia's first bio-jet fuel prototype using local research and technology will be initiated.",""]],"42":[[1,"137","3","Entrepreneur-Researcher Collaboration for Innovation","Collaboration between entrepreneurs and researchers will be intensified to enhance innovation in creating more high value products and services that will boost competitiveness.",""],[1,"140","4","Invention-to-Innovation Ecosystem Development","Initiatives will be undertaken to develop an invention to innovation ecosystem that propagates IP registration among entrepreneurs, especially startups.",""],[1,"140","4","Performance-Based IP-Backed Entrepreneur Financing","Performance-based loans and incentives, including utilisation of IP as collateral, will be explored in providing financial assistance.",""],[1,"239","8","R&D&C&I Intensification for MSME Productivity","Efforts to enhance R&D&C&I will be intensified to increase productivity, particularly among MSMEs.",""],[1,"239","8","Industry-HEI and Research Centre Collaboration Initiative","Industries will be encouraged to collaborate with HEIs and research centres to embark on research that focuses on the specific needs of the industries and communities in each region.",""],[1,"239","8","Anchor Company Support for MSMEs in Less Developed Regions","Anchor companies will be identified to assist MSMEs in the less developed regions.",""],[1,"239","8","Agribusiness Anchor Company Technical Assistance and Market Access","In the agribusiness industry, anchor companies will take up an active role in providing technical assistance and greater market access to small scale agropreneurs to provide wider growth opportunities to MSMEs.",""]],"43":[[1,"137","4","MSME, Cooperative, and Social Enterprise Support Initiatives","In realising this, initiatives will include increasing MSMEs contribution to the economy, widening market access and international trade opportunities as well as capitalising cooperatives, agriculture-based associations and social enterprise in developing entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"138","7","Malaysian Cooperative Transformation Plan (TRANSKOM) 2021-2025","The governance structure and legal framework that govern the cooperative movement will be improved through the implementation of the Malaysian Cooperative Transformation Plan (TRANSKOM) 2021-2025.",""],[1,"138","7","Promotion of Cooperative Movement Among B40 and Rural Communities","The cooperative movement among the B40 and rural communities will be further promoted to encourage them to pool their limited resources to achieve economies of scale.",""],[1,"138","7","Extension of MSME Support to Cooperatives","The support provided to MSMEs will be extended to cooperatives, including access to programmes, assistance and business opportunities.",""],[1,"139","1","Social Enterprise Development Blueprint","Blueprint Perusahaan Sosial 2021-2025 will be introduced to further strengthen social enterprise development.",""],[1,"139","1","Social Enterprise Capacity Development and Market Expansion Support","continuous support and capacity development will be provided for business and market expansion.",""],[1,"139","1","Social Impact Government Procurement Onboarding Programme","Program Perolehan Impak Sosial Kerajaan (PPISK) will be rolled out to enable the onboarding of social enterprises to the national e-procurement system.",""],[1,"139","1","Inclusive Business Model Expansion","The Inclusive Business (IB) model, which promotes the involvement of MSMEs in the supply chain of GLCs and MNCs, will also be expanded to facilitate the participation of social enterprises.",""],[1,"139","2","Entrepreneurship Support Ecosystem Enhancement","initiatives will be undertaken to enhance governance, regulations, institutional roles and financing to boost the performance of entrepreneurs.",""]],"44":[[1,"138","3","MSME Market Access Expansion Measures","Measures to enhance market access and opportunities will be further expanded to assist MSMEs in increasing sales of goods and services domestically and internationally.",""],[1,"138","3","Government Procurement Support for MSMEs","Government Procurement (GP) will be fully leveraged as a means to support MSMEs in the domestic market, instil business confidence, drive innovation, and stimulate the development of products for local content requirements.",""],[1,"138","3","Accelerated MSME Participation in Government Procurement","efforts will be accelerated to ensure local MSMEs, including manufacturers to actively participate in GP.",""]],"45":[[1,"193","2","Bumiputera Development Agenda","The Bumiputera development agenda continues to be one of the national priorities in uplifting the socioeconomic status and ensuring the success of the BEC.",""],[1,"193","2","Human Capital Capacity and Capability Enhancement","Initiatives undertaken included enhancing the capacity and capability of human capital, raising effective control of corporate equity ownership, increasing wealth ownership and building a resilient and sustainable BEC.",""],[1,"193","2","Corporate Equity Ownership and Wealth Ownership Expansion","Initiatives undertaken included enhancing the capacity and capability of human capital, raising effective control of corporate equity ownership, increasing wealth ownership and building a resilient and sustainable BEC.",""],[1,"194","5","Bumiputera Business Participation Programmes","TERAJU was also mandated to increase Bumiputera participation by implementing a number of programmes such as Syarikat Bumiputera Berprestasi Tinggi (TERAS), Skim Usahawan Permulaan Bumiputera (SUPERB), Dana Pembangunan Usahawan Bumiputera, Skim Jejak Jaya Bumiputera as well as carve-out and compete initiative.",""],[1,"194","5","Bumiputera Socioeconomic Coordination Mechanism","TERAJU acted as the secretariat to the Majlis Ekonomi Bumiputera which is responsible for coordinating Bumiputera socioeconomic development.",""],[1,"194","5","EKUINAS Bumiputera Equity, Employment, and Talent Development Mandate","Meanwhile, the role of EKUINAS was realigned not only to increase corporate equity ownership, but also to generate more significant Bumiputera outcomes through job creation, professional and managerial participation as well as talent development.",""],[1,"212","1","Mainstreaming the Bumiputera Agenda Across Policies","This agenda will be embedded in all existing and new policies.",""],[1,"212","1","Bumiputera Socioeconomic Development Support","Bumiputera socioeconomic development will be given priority through enhancing the governance, service delivery and human capital development as well as strengthening access to education.",""],[1,"212","1","Bumiputera Business Resilience and Sustainability Support","Bumiputera businesses will be empowered to be resilient and sustainable.",""],[1,"212","1","Wealth Creation and Equity Ownership Measures","In addition, concerted efforts will be undertaken in increasing wealth creation, optimising TRM and waqf instruments as well as ensuring sustainable corporate equity ownership.",""],[1,"213","1","Targeted Socioeconomic Assistance for Poor Bumiputera Households","Strategic and targeted efforts will be implemented to obtain more equitable socioeconomic benefits among Bumiputera households.",""],[1,"213","1","Basic Necessities Support for Poor Bumiputera Households","Assistance in the form of basic necessities such as housing, education and health will continue to be provided to poor Bumiputera households.",""],[1,"213","1","Income Diversification and Training for B40 Bumiputera Households","Furthermore, the B40 Bumiputera households will be encouraged to diversify their sources of income to improve their standard of living through the provision of appropriate training.",""],[1,"213","2","Bumiputera Household Empowerment Programme","The M40 Bumiputera households will continue to be empowered towards increasing their potential to attain a better standard of living.",""],[1,"213","2","Bumiputera Entrepreneurship and Financial Literacy Support","This income group will be encouraged to venture into entrepreneurship, enhance financial literacy and investment management as well as participate in additional income-generating activities, including leveraging on digital platforms.",""],[1,"213","2","Bumiputera Community Contribution Initiative","The T20 Bumiputera households will be encouraged to actively contribute back to the Bumiputera community.",""],[1,"213","2","Bumiputera EDO-SOE-Private Sector Collaboration Initiative","collaboration between Bumiputera EDOs, SOEs and private sectors with successful icons will be initiated to create value and trickle-down effects to the community.",""],[1,"214","3","Bumiputera Human Capital Development Initiatives","Efforts will be intensified in expanding educational access and opportunities, improving the quality of skills programmes, increasing the participation in certified professional programmes as well as improving huffaz skills and marketability.",""],[1,"214","4","Bumiputera Education Access Expansion","Access to quality education opportunities from pre-school to tertiary level will be the main focus in enhancing the socioeconomic status of Bumiputera.",""],[1,"214","4","MARA Future Skills Education Programme","MARA education institutes will be leveraged to equip Bumiputera human capital with skills of the future including artificial intelligence (AI), advanced digital skills, critical thinking as well as spiritual and positive values to enhance creativity and competency.",""],[1,"214","4","Bumiputera Nurturing and Development Programmes","The Bumiputera education institutions will also be encouraged to implement the nurturing and development programmes18 in complementing the academic and technical training received by students and trainees.",""],[1,"214","5","Intensified Structured TVET Skills Training","Structured skills training in TVET programmes will be intensified by MARA to increase the supply of Bumiputera talents in meeting industrial demands as well as to address the high Bumiputera unemployment rate particularly among youth.","MARA"],[1,"214","5","HEI-Industry Digital Employability Platform","a digital platform will be developed through collaboration between HEIs and industry to improve the employability of Bumiputera graduates.",""],[1,"214","5","New Skills Development Programme for Emerging Jobs","a programme to develop new skill sets related to the solution of complex problems, technology design and programming will be introduced to equip the Bumiputera for newly emerging skilled jobs.",""],[1,"214","6","Bumiputera Graduate Professional Development Support","More eligible Bumiputera graduates will be supported to increase the number of Bumiputera professionals such as accountants, architects and engineers.",""],[1,"214","6","Bumiputera Future Careers Strategy for 4IR Occupations","specific strategies will be formulated to increase Bumiputera participation in future careers such as analysts, data scientists and big data experts through strategic collaboration with industry and skills training institutions.",""],[1,"214","6","Bumiputera Specialist Training Support","more Bumiputera professionals will be trained to become specialists in various fields such as medicine and engineering.",""],[1,"214","6","Diversified Financing for Bumiputera Professional Development","Funds will be sourced from SOEs and the private sector as well as individuals through crowdfunding to reduce dependency on government.",""],[1,"214","7","Student and Trainee Skills and Values Development Programme","This programme will help students and trainees to acquire relevant skills and values such as industry relevant soft skills, financial literacy, employment readiness, leadership and spiritual values to complement technical competencies in creating balanced and competitive individuals.",""],[1,"215","1","Tahfiz Programme Accreditation and Curriculum Alignment","Concerted efforts will continue to be implemented to accredit tahfiz19 programmes, particularly in private institutions to provide better routes for huffaz to enter into mainstream education.",""],[1,"215","1","Huffaz Technical, Professional, and Lifelong Learning Training","In addition, YPPB and MARA will continue to train more huffaz in technical and professional fields as well as program pembelajaran sepanjang hayat (PSH) in enhancing their employability.",""],[1,"215","2","Bumiputera Business Resilience and Sustainability Enhancement","Increasing the resilience and sustainability of Bumiputera businesses will be the main focus in strengthening entrepreneurship culture.",""],[1,"215","2","Bumiputera Participation Expansion in High-Impact and Strategic Sectors","Bumiputera participation in high impact and the emerging strategic sectors will be enhanced.",""],[1,"215","3","Bumiputera Entrepreneur Capacity and Capability Enhancement Programme","The capacity and capability of Bumiputera entrepreneurs will be enhanced by inculcating self-reliance, a competitive mindset and a high-performance culture.",""],[1,"215","3","Merit- and Needs-Based Financial and Non-Financial Assistance","Financial and non-financial assistances will be provided based on merit and needs.",""],[1,"215","3","Structured Coaching and Mentoring Programme for Bumiputera Entrepreneurs","Structured coaching and mentoring programmes will be strengthened through the involvement of successful entrepreneurs in sharing business ethics and best practices.",""],[1,"215","3","Bumiputera Digital Economy Participation Initiative","More Bumiputera entrepreneurs will be encouraged to venture into the digital economy.",""],[1,"215","4","Start-up Entrepreneurship Programme Intensification","Start-up entrepreneurship programmes including for youth and professionals will be intensified to enhance Bumiputera participation by providing more training and advisory services in innovative and knowledge-based businesses.",""],[1,"215","5","Bumiputera Participation Facilitation in High-Potential Industries","Bumiputera participation in these high potential industries will be facilitated through the acquisition of local and foreign technologies as well as intellectual properties (IP).",""],[1,"215","5","Bumiputera Crowdfunding for Entrepreneurs","Moreover, the corporate sector will be encouraged to create Bumiputera crowdfunding aimed at providing alternative financing to Bumiputera entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"215","6","Vendor Development Programme Strengthening","The involvement of Bumiputera MSMEs in the Vendor Development Programme will be further intensified.",""],[1,"215","6","Carve-Out and Compete Initiative Expansion","Meanwhile, the carve-out and compete initiative will be extended to various sectors in increasing effective Bumiputera participation in the economy.",""],[1,"215","6","Bumiputera MSME Consortium and Cooperative Formation Support","Bumiputera MSMEs will also be encouraged to form consortiums and cooperatives in enhancing their capacity and capability to compete along the supply chain.",""],[1,"215","6","VentureTECH Capital Injection for Bumiputera Companies","Meanwhile, VentureTECH will be injecting capital into Bumiputera companies with potential.",""],[1,"215","6","Bumiputera MSME Exit Policy Framework","A clear exit policy will be formulated to encourage successful Bumiputera MSMEs to be more independent and resilient.",""],[1,"215","7","Bumiputera MSME Global Market Expansion Support","Bumiputera MSMEs will be encouraged to grow and penetrate the global market.",""],[1,"215","7","SOE Partnership Support for Bumiputera MSMEs","SOEs will enhance collaboration with MNCs and global companies in identifying and assisting potential Bumiputera MSMEs.",""],[1,"215","7","Smart Partnership Commercialisation Initiative","Smart partnerships between SOEs, R&D institutions and Bumiputera MSMEs will be intensified to develop and commercialise IPs as well as innovative products and services to penetrate new markets.",""],[1,"215","7","Bumiputera Business Promotion in New Growth Areas","Bumiputera businesses will be promoted in new growth areas across the country, while Development Financial Institutions (DFIs) will be urged to expand financial assistance, coaching and mentoring to support potential Bumiputera entrepreneurs venturing into high value-added activities.",""],[1,"216","1","Bumiputera Property Ownership Support Initiatives","Various initiatives will be undertaken to further increase property ownership of Bumiputera.",""],[1,"216","1","Improved Property Purchase Financing Terms","Better terms of financing for the purchase of properties will be introduced through collaboration between financial institutions, private developers and investors.",""],[1,"216","1","Rent-to-Own Asset Acquisition Scheme for Bumiputera Entrepreneurs","EDOs will be encouraged to acquire and develop commercial and industrial assets under the Rent-to-Own scheme for Bumiputera entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"216","2","Bumiputera Housing Finance Scheme","a dedicated fund will be explored to provide a financing scheme for eligible Bumiputera households",""],[1,"216","2","Suburban Township Development Initiative","new townships in sub-urban areas with good connectivity and infrastructure will be developed by the private sector and Bumiputera mandated agencies",""],[1,"216","2","Bumiputera Home Ownership Quota Coordination","the policy on Bumiputera quota in home ownership will be coordinated between Federal, state and local governments",""],[1,"216","3","Bumiputera Asset Ownership Expansion through New Business Models","PHB will explore new business models to enable participation in government privatisation projects as part of its real estate investment trust portfolio.",""],[1,"216","3","AHB Fund Injection and Dividend Reinvestment Scheme","A new model of property ownership will be introduced through the injection of funds in the AHB to generate dividends, which will be reinvested as long-term investment instruments.",""],[1,"216","3","Post-COVID Business Model Innovation for Commercial Premises Ownership","EDOs and SOEs will explore innovative new business models to retain and enhance the ownership of the commercial and business premises.",""],[1,"216","4","TRM and Waqf Development Optimisation","the development of TRM and waqf instruments will be optimised.",""],[1,"216","4","State-Federal Collaboration for TRM and Waqf Land Development","state authorities will be encouraged to develop TRM and waqf lands through collaboration with the Federal agencies.",""],[1,"216","4","Integrated Master Plan for TRM and Waqf Development","An integrated master plan on the development of TRM, waqf land and waqf instruments will be formulated to provide a framework for socioeconomic development at state and local levels.",""],[1,"216","4","Expanded TRM Land Data Steering Committee Mandate","The role and scope of the Jawatankuasa Pemandu Pengurusan Data Tanah Rizab Melayu Semenanjung Malaysia will be expanded to provide guidelines relating to land development and value creation.",""],[1,"216","5","Waqf Land Development Coordination Committee","A committee comprising representatives of Federal and state governments will be set up to provide overall direction in planning, implementation and monitoring of waqf land development.",""],[1,"216","5","Expansion of Waqf for Socioeconomic Development","the possibility of expanding the concept of waqf as an instrument for broader socioeconomic development will be explored.",""],[1,"216","5","Federal Waqf Fund Establishment","A waqf fund at the Federal level will be established to mobilise resources from individuals and corporate bodies to fund socioeconomic activities.",""],[1,"217","1","Bumiputera Corporate Equity Ownership Strengthening","Bumiputera effective control of corporate organisations will be strengthened to ensure sustainable corporate equity ownership.",""],[1,"217","1","State-Owned Enterprise Role Enhancement for Bumiputera Equity","Furthermore, the role of SOEs as development enablers in increasing Bumiputera equity ownership will be further enhanced.",""],[1,"217","2","Revision of Bumiputera Mandated Institutions Investment Model","The investment model in the Bumiputera mandated institutions will be revisited to ensure optimal returns from strategic investments and divestments to the Bumiputera companies.",""],[1,"217","2","Bumiputera Equity Reallocation to Eligible Consortiums and Companies","In ensuring sustainable Bumiputera corporate sector equity ownership, shares of companies divested by Bumiputera mandated agencies will be offered to eligible Bumiputera consortiums and companies.",""],[1,"217","2","Bumiputera Divestment Return Distribution Mechanism","Returns from the divestment will be distributed and shared with other Bumiputera mandated agencies to improve the Bumiputera wealth distribution.",""],[1,"217","2","Monitoring of Bumiputera-Owned Company Disposal","Disposal of Bumiputera-owned companies will be monitored by the sector regulators to maintain the Bumiputera corporate equity ownership.",""],[1,"217","2","Equity Safety-Net Exploration","The possibility of establishing an equity safety-net will be explored to ensure disposal of Bumiputera equity will be made to other qualified Bumiputera individuals and entities.",""],[1,"217","2","Committee on Equity Ownership Oversight Mandate","the Committee on Equity Ownership established under the EPU, JPM will be tasked to oversee the implementation of policies and strategies to further strengthen Bumiputera corporate sector equity ownership.",""],[1,"217","3","Investment Literacy and IPO Outreach Programme","Bumiputera institutions, such as PNB, MARA and EKUINAS will collaborate with the Securities Commission and Bursa Malaysia in promoting investment literacy.",""],[1,"217","4","Strategic Reallocation of GLC and GLIC Investments","Investment of GLCs and GLICs will be prioritised in the strategic sectors while participation in non-strategic sectors will be gradually reduced.",""],[1,"217","4","Coordinated Disposal of Non-Strategic GLC and GLIC Assets","The disposal of assets owned by the GLCs and GLICs in the non-strategic sectors will be coordinated in ensuring priority will be given to qualified Bumiputera entrepreneurs and entities.",""],[1,"217","4","Bumiputera Corporate Ownership Enhancement Requirement","GLCs and GLICs will be required to enhance the Bumiputera agenda to ensure the sustainability of Bumiputera corporate sector ownership.",""],[1,"217","4","Expansion of Bumiputera Company Listing Programmes","Programmes to facilitate more Bumiputera companies to be listed will be expanded through improvements to the existing programmes.",""],[1,"217","4","Strategic Collaboration for Bumiputera MSME and PLC Financing","Strategic collaboration with foreign investors and fund managers will be facilitated to raise funds for Bumiputera MSMEs and PLCs to become global players.",""],[1,"217","5","Digital Financial Planning and Investment Participation Expansion","PNB will facilitate to increase the participation of Bumiputera community in digital-based financial planning and investment services.",""],[1,"217","5","New Foreign Market Unit Trust Products","PNB will introduce new unit trust products that have investment exposure in the foreign market.",""],[1,"217","5","Domestic and International Investment Diversification Strategy","PNB will continue to invest in high performing PLCs in Bursa Malaysia as well as diversify its investment portfolio at the domestic and international market.",""],[1,"217","5","Bumiputera Empowerment Collaboration Initiative","Khazanah Nasional Berhad (KHAZANAH), as the national sovereign wealth fund, will also continue to lead collaboration with selected GLCs and GLICs to support and strengthen the Bumiputera Empowerment Agenda in increasing the Bumiputera corporate equity ownership.",""],[1,"217","5","VentureTECH Performance-Based Investment Programme","Bumiputera companies in high value-added, green and emerging industries will be developed through the VentureTECH performance-based investment programme.",""],[2,"193","2","Bumiputera Development Agenda","The Bumiputera development agenda continues to be one of the national priorities in uplifting the socioeconomic status and ensuring the success of the BEC.",""],[2,"194","5","Bumiputera Business Participation Programmes","TERAJU was also mandated to increase Bumiputera participation by implementing a number of programmes such as Syarikat Bumiputera Berprestasi Tinggi (TERAS), Skim Usahawan Permulaan Bumiputera (SUPERB), Dana Pembangunan Usahawan Bumiputera, Skim Jejak Jaya Bumiputera as well as carve-out and compete initiative.",""],[2,"194","5","Bumiputera Socioeconomic Coordination Mechanism","TERAJU acted as the secretariat to the Majlis Ekonomi Bumiputera which is responsible for coordinating Bumiputera socioeconomic development.",""],[2,"194","5","EKUINAS Bumiputera Equity and Talent Development Mandate","Meanwhile, the role of EKUINAS was realigned not only to increase corporate equity ownership, but also to generate more significant Bumiputera outcomes through job creation, professional and managerial participation as well as talent development.",""],[2,"212","1","Mainstreaming the Bumiputera Agenda Across Policies","The Bumiputera agenda will continue to be a national agenda in achieving fair, equitable and inclusive socioeconomic development in line with WKB 2030.",""],[2,"212","1","Bumiputera Socioeconomic Development Support","Bumiputera socioeconomic development will be given priority through enhancing the governance, service delivery and human capital development as well as strengthening access to education.",""],[2,"212","1","Bumiputera Business Resilience and Sustainability Support","Bumiputera businesses will be empowered to be resilient and sustainable.",""],[2,"213","2","Bumiputera Entrepreneurship and Financial Literacy Support","This income group will be encouraged to venture into entrepreneurship, enhance financial literacy and investment management as well as participate in additional income-generating activities, including leveraging on digital platforms.",""],[2,"213","2","Bumiputera EDO-SOE-Private Sector Collaboration Initiative","In addition, collaboration between Bumiputera EDOs, SOEs and private sectors with successful icons will be initiated to create value and trickle-down effects to the community.",""],[2,"213","6","Strengthening MARA's Development and Entrepreneur Support Role","The role of MARA will be strengthened to exercise the power enacted under the MARA Act 1966.",""],[2,"213","6","New Development Model for Bumiputera Socioeconomic Advancement","MARA will explore a new development model to further accelerate progress in uplifting the Bumiputera socioeconomic position.",""],[2,"213","6","MARA Commercial and Industrial Participation Programme","MARA will continue to be involved in a number of commercial and industrial activities to create more opportunities for Bumiputera entrepreneurs.",""],[2,"213","6","TRM Economic Potential Development Initiative","MARA will play an important role in unlocking the economic potential of the TRM.",""],[2,"215","2","Bumiputera Business Resilience and Sustainability Enhancement","Increasing the resilience and sustainability of Bumiputera businesses will be the main focus in strengthening entrepreneurship culture.",""],[2,"215","2","Bumiputera Participation in High-Impact and Emerging Strategic Sectors","Bumiputera participation in high impact and the emerging strategic sectors will be enhanced.",""],[2,"215","3","Bumiputera Entrepreneur Capacity-Building Support","The capacity and capability of Bumiputera entrepreneurs will be enhanced by inculcating self-reliance, a competitive mindset and a high-performance culture.",""],[2,"215","3","Merit- and Needs-Based Entrepreneur Assistance Scheme","Financial and non-financial assistances will be provided based on merit and needs.",""],[2,"215","3","Structured Coaching and Mentoring Programme for Entrepreneurs","Structured coaching and mentoring programmes will be strengthened through the involvement of successful entrepreneurs in sharing business ethics and best practices.",""],[2,"215","3","Bumiputera Digital Economy Participation Initiative","More Bumiputera entrepreneurs will be encouraged to venture into the digital economy.",""],[2,"215","4","Start-up Entrepreneurship Support Programme","Start-up entrepreneurship programmes including for youth and professionals will be intensified to enhance Bumiputera participation by providing more training and advisory services in innovative and knowledge-based businesses.",""],[2,"215","5","Bumiputera Participation Facilitation in High-Potential Industries","Bumiputera participation in these high potential industries will be facilitated through the acquisition of local and foreign technologies as well as intellectual properties (IP).",""],[2,"215","5","Bumiputera Crowdfunding for Entrepreneurs","Moreover, the corporate sector will be encouraged to create Bumiputera crowdfunding aimed at providing alternative financing to Bumiputera entrepreneurs.",""]],"46":[[1,"238","7","Growth Node and Hotspot Area Development","Regional development will be driven by the development of key growth nodes and hotspot areas.",""],[1,"238","7","Promotion of Niche Economic Activities","several niche economic activities will be promoted in these areas.",""],[1,"238","7","High Value-Added and Green Growth Acceleration Initiative","Efforts will be focused on accelerating the implementation of high value-added activities and green growth initiatives, which will contribute to economic growth and ensure inclusive regional development.",""],[1,"238","8","Regional Key Growth Node Development Programme","Key growth nodes will be developed in each region as hubs for economic activities, allowing for economies of scale, agglomeration of economic activities, optimisation of resources and the creation of a conducive ecosystem.",""],[1,"238","8","Hotspot Area Development Initiative","Hotspot areas, which refer to the areas surrounding key growth nodes that have the potential to be developed on a smaller scale, will be established to complement the key growth nodes.",""],[1,"238","8","Strategic Investment and Entrepreneurship Attraction Strategy","Synergistic development in the key growth nodes and hotspot areas will attract strategic and quality investment as well as create more employment and entrepreneurship opportunities.",""],[1,"239","7","Enhanced Investment Incentive Packages","Incentive packages will be enhanced to attract more quality investment to catalyse key economic activities across key growth nodes and hotspot areas.",""],[1,"239","7","Investment Incentives for Less Developed Areas","Attractive incentive packages will also be extended to encourage investments in less developed areas.",""]],"47":[[1,"239","1","Techpark@Enstek Phase Three Development","The development of phase three of the Techpark@Enstek in Negeri Sembilan will expand the development of halal-related activities, particularly in food and beverages, pharmaceuticals and cosmetics industries.",""],[1,"239","1","Pagoh Special Economic Zone Development","the proposed Pagoh Special Economic Zone will attract both local and foreign investment, offering huge potential for the area's future development.",""],[2,"264","7","Conducive Economic Growth Ecosystem Measures","measures will be undertaken to provide a conducive ecosystem for economic growth.",""],[2,"265","6","Equitable Industrial Development in Sabah and Sarawak","In promoting growth in Sabah and Sarawak, the focus will be given on more equitable industrial development, modernising the agriculture sector, strengthening the oil and gas subsector, enhancing the services",""],[2,"265","8","Industrial Estates Development in Sabah and Sarawak","The development of industrial estates in Sabah and Sarawak will be accelerated through better provision of infrastructure, namely roads, electricity and water supply, as well as internet connectivity.",""],[2,"265","8","National Industrialisation Roadmap Formulation","The formulation of a new national industrialisation roadmap will take into account the local strength of Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[2,"265","8","Investment Incentive Mechanism Review","Existing investment incentive mechanisms will be reviewed focusing on selected quality industries and addressing regional imbalance in industrial development.",""],[2,"265","9","Halal Industry Strengthening in Sabah and Sarawak","The halal industry in Sabah and Sarawak will be strengthened to leverage the availability of resources and the growing global demand for halal products.",""],[2,"265","9","Halal Park Upgrading and Integrated Development","the existing halal parks including the Kota Kinabalu Industrial Park and Palm Oil Industrial Cluster Lahad Datu in Sabah, as well as Tanjung Manis Halal Hub in Sarawak, will be upgraded through a holistic development approach to enable more integrated planning, coordination and implementation in increasing the utilisation of the parks.",""],[2,"268","2","Regional Economic Corridor Development","efforts will be focused on leveraging regional economic corridors to play a more important role as an engine of growth.",""],[2,"268","2","Sabah and Sarawak Investment Promotion Initiative","concerted efforts will also be undertaken in making Sabah and Sarawak as preferred investment destinations in BIMP-EAGA by leveraging on comparative advantages in both states.",""],[2,"268","3","Strengthening Regional Development Strategies","Measures will be undertaken to strengthen regional development strategies in ensuring a higher development impact.",""],[2,"268","3","Acceleration of Strategic Development Projects","SEDIA and RECODA will intensify efforts in expediting the implementation of strategic development projects.",""],[2,"268","3","Investment Attraction Collaboration Mechanism","SEDIA and RECODA will be actively collaborating with various agencies to create a conducive environment in attracting quality investment.",""],[2,"268","4","SDC Blueprint Review and Alignment","As SEDIA is currently reviewing the SDC Blueprint, 2008-2025, it will be aligned to the policies and strategies at national and state levels.",""],[2,"268","4","Quality Investment Attraction for Regional Jobs and Entrepreneurship","The review, which will be finalised in 2021, is expected to provide a more strategic development approach, particularly in attracting quality investment to create jobs and entrepreneurship opportunities in the region.",""],[2,"268","5","Sarawak Regional Development Area Expansion","In accelerating development in Sarawak, the SCORE area was extended beyond the central region with the establishment of the URDA, HDA and NRDA in ensuring a comprehensive development of the rural and interior areas of Sarawak.",""],[2,"268","6","Acceleration of Strategic Projects in SCORE Growth Nodes","The implementation of strategic projects in the five key growth nodes in the SCORE areas, namely Tanjung Manis, Mukah, Samalaju, Baram and Tunoh will be accelerated.",""],[2,"268","6","Infrastructure, Facilities, and Services Provision for Economic Activities","The provision of infrastructure, facilities and services will support economic activities, which in turn will result in spillover effects to the surrounding areas.",""],[2,"268","7","Strengthening Investment Promotion and Facilitation in Sabah and Sarawak","The investment promotion and facilitation functions of the RECs and other investment promotion agencies in Sabah and Sarawak will be strengthened to promote both states as preferred investment destinations for BIMP-EAGA.",""],[2,"268","7","Local Business Environment and Incentive Enhancement","The state governments will play a proactive role in creating a conducive environment for businesses, including efforts to complement national investment incentives with local incentives.",""],[2,"268","7","Industrial Zone Infrastructure Upgrading","Measures will be undertaken to ensure adequate electricity and water supply, proper waste management facilities, as well as sufficient digital infrastructure and services at strategic industrial zones and growth nodes.",""],[2,"268","7","Special Fiscal and Non-Fiscal Investment Incentive Schemes","Special fiscal and non-fiscal incentive schemes to attract investment originated from BIMP-EAGA and elsewhere will be explored, particularly schemes that promote green growth and green infrastructure.",""],[2,"276","4","Federal Support to Sabah and Sarawak Economic Development Corporations","the Federal Government will work closely with both Sabah Economic Development Corporation (SEDCO) and Sarawak Economic Development Corporation (SEDC) to enhance their contribution in delivering better outcomes to the rakyat.",""],[2,"276","5","Coordinated Regional Development Planning","Measures will be undertaken to promote more coordinated and integrated regional development planning through better collaboration with the relevant agencies, both at the Federal and state levels.",""],[2,"276","6","Regional Development Planning Coordination","Regional economic authorities in both states will streamline the development planning and initiatives introduced by all the relevant authorities.",""],[2,"276","6","SDC Blueprint Policy Alignment Review","SEDIA will need to align the review of the SDC Blueprint with all related policies at the national and state levels.",""],[2,"276","6","SCORE Area Development Acceleration Initiative","RECODA together with URDA, HDA and NRDA will collaborate with Federal and state agencies in accelerating development within the SCORE areas.",""],[2,"276","7","Strengthening of SEDCO and SEDC Roles for State Economic Planning","The roles of SEDCO and SEDC will be further enhanced to facilitate the planning of economic activities in Sabah and Sarawak, in line with the mandate given to these two agencies to correct economic imbalances at the state level.",""],[2,"276","7","Regional Planning Coordination and Evaluation Committee","In this connection, a committee will be established comprising multiple key Federal and state agencies that are responsible for regional planning, coordination and evaluation.",""],[2,"276","7","Coordination of Federal Programmes for Regional Development Gap Reduction","This committee will coordinate strategies with a number of Federal programmes at the regional level in bridging development gaps across regions and states.",""]],"48":[[1,"239","4","Green Growth Initiatives for Industry","Industries will also be encouraged to implement green growth initiatives by adopting green technology and best practices.",""],[1,"300","6","Green Market Expansion and Green Procurement Promotion","the green market will be expanded by increasing demand for local green products, services and technologies as well as encouraging the private sector to undertake green procurement.",""],[1,"300","6","Green Industry Development Support Programme for MSMEs","local industries, especially micro, small and medium-sized enterprises (MSMEs), will be encouraged to participate in green industry development programmes, including capacity building, certification, dissemination of information and business matching.",""],[1,"300","6","Green Label Facilitation Mechanism","initiatives to facilitate industries to obtain green labels will be enhanced by providing appropriate financial mechanisms and technical expertise.",""],[1,"300","7","Green Government Procurement Expansion","The GGP initiative will be expanded to state governments and local authorities.",""],[1,"300","7","Green Procurement for Construction and Renovation Works","The GGP implementation will also be expanded to include procurement of works for construction and renovation.",""],[1,"300","7","Green Building Materials and Design Promotion","Green labels, designs and methods as well as the use of green and recycled materials will be promoted.",""],[1,"300","8","Green Government Procurement Guidelines and Short-Term Action Plan","a short-term action plan and guidelines for GGP works will be developed",""],[1,"300","8","Promotion of Green Products and Services","the promotion of green products and services, including green buildings and infrastructure, will be intensified to boost demand from the private sector and the general public",""],[1,"300","8","Sustainable Consumption and Production Blueprint Implementation","the sustainable consumption and production (SCP) blueprint will be implemented to encourage sustainable business practices and lifestyles",""],[1,"300","9","Triple Helix Innovation Collaboration","Collaboration among three key players, namely academia, industry and government, working together to foster and accelerate innovation to address challenges faced by society.",""],[2,"75","1","Green Industry Concept Implementation","the implementation of a green industry concept",""],[2,"100","3","Circular Economy Promotion Mechanism for Manufacturing","the circular economy model will be promoted through a structured mechanism to enable industries in adopting sustainable manufacturing processes, reducing the use of raw materials and increasing the use of recycled materials.",""],[2,"100","3","National Policy of Remanufacturing","The implementation of the National Policy of Remanufacturing will help industries to embark on the circular economy through the remanufacturing of products.",""],[2,"100","3","Eco-Industrial Parks Requirement","the adoption of the eco-industrial parks concept which embodies the circular economy model will be made a pre-requisite for the development or new industrial parks.",""],[2,"100","3","Eco-Industrial Park Collaboration for Existing Parks","Existing industrial parks will also be encouraged to adopt the model, by promoting collaboration among tenants in these parks in managing resources and environmental issues efficiently.",""],[2,"100","3","Mandatory ESG Adoption in Manufacturing","industry players will be required to adopt the environment, social and governance (ESG) elements in their business practices.",""],[2,"106","5","Green Industry Development for Industrial Estates","the development of industrial estates will be promoted based on the green industry concept.",""],[2,"106","5","Eco-Industrial Parks Guideline","A comprehensive guideline on eco-industrial parks will be introduced to be adopted by industrial estates.",""],[2,"106","8","Industrial Estate Incentives and Financial Assistance Enhancement","The provision of incentives and financial assistance for players in industrial estates, particularly those investing in advanced technology will be enhanced.",""],[2,"106","8","Industrial Automation and Technology Utilisation Promotion","Greater automation and technology utilisation along the value chain will drive productivity growth and reduce reliance on low-skilled foreign workers.",""],[2,"106","8","Clean Technology Investment Incentive Redesign","Incentives will be redesigned to attract quality investments that utilise clean technology to ensure sustainable practices.",""],[2,"291","3","Sustainable Business Adoption and Market Integration Programme","programme included enhancing the adoption of sustainability best practices, identifying new niche markets for sustainable businesses and products as well as integrating Malaysian companies into the global sustainable supply change.",""],[2,"300","1","Green Labelling Uptake Promotion","the private sector will also be encouraged to uptake recognised green labelling for next generation vehicles and technologies.",""],[2,"300","6","Green Market Expansion and Green Procurement Promotion","the green market will be expanded by increasing demand for local green products, services and technologies as well as encouraging the private sector to undertake green procurement.",""],[2,"300","6","Green Industry Development Support for MSMEs","local industries, especially micro, small and medium-sized enterprises (MSMEs), will be encouraged to participate in green industry development programmes, including capacity building, certification, dissemination of information and business matching.",""],[2,"300","6","Green Labelling Facilitation Mechanism","initiatives to facilitate industries to obtain green labels will be enhanced by providing appropriate financial mechanisms and technical expertise.",""],[2,"300","8","Green Government Procurement Guidelines and Short-Term Action Plan","a short-term action plan and guidelines for GGP works will be developed",""],[2,"300","8","Promotion of Green Products and Services","the promotion of green products and services, including green buildings and infrastructure, will be intensified",""],[2,"300","8","Sustainable Consumption and Production Blueprint Implementation","the sustainable consumption and production (SCP) blueprint will be implemented to encourage sustainable business practices and lifestyles",""],[2,"300","9","Triple Helix Innovation Collaboration","Collaboration among three key players, namely academia, industry and government, working together to foster and accelerate innovation to address challenges faced by society.",""]],"49":[[1,"267","3","Business Registration Regulatory Reform","Business registration regulations will be reviewed and reformed to improve the ease of doing business.",""],[1,"267","3","eCommerce Adoption and Business Digitalisation Support","Businesses will be encouraged to leverage eCommerce platforms and modernise business processes through digitalisation.",""],[1,"267","3","Road, Last-Mile, and Digital Infrastructure Expansion","Roads and last-mile connectivity, as well as digital infrastructure will allow businesses to grow and permeate into rural areas, as well as access to reasonably priced goods and services.",""],[1,"267","7","MSME Ecosystem Support Initiatives in Sabah and Sarawak","For this purpose, efforts will be undertaken towards improving access to financing, enhancing resource-based activities, facilitating ease of doing business and boosting the market access of MSMEs.",""],[1,"267","8","Special Financing Fund for MSMEs in Sabah and Sarawak","Access to financing will be improved for MSMEs by allocating a special fund for Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[1,"267","8","MSME Financing Awareness Programmes","Special programmes will be implemented to increase awareness of available financing for MSMEs.",""],[1,"267","8","Mobile Banking Expansion for MSME Access","In addition, mobile banking will be expanded to provide better access to financing.",""],[1,"267","9","MSME Resource-Based Value-Added Enterprise Support","MSMEs in Sabah and Sarawak will be encouraged to utilise domestic natural resources in producing high value-added products and services.",""],[1,"267","9","MSME Participation in Resource-Based Industry Supply Chains","In this regard, MSMEs participation in industries such as oil and gas, ecotourism, agri-business and palm oil will be further strengthened.",""],[1,"267","9","Entrepreneurship Training and Development Programme","comprehensive entrepreneurship training and development programmes will be developed.",""],[1,"267","10","Expansion of Business Registration Counters and Innovative Registration Mechanisms","The existing network of business registration counters across Sabah and Sarawak will be expanded and innovative registration mechanisms will be introduced to facilitate business registration.",""],[1,"267","10","District Office Information Dissemination Focal Point Arrangement","Districts offices will be encouraged to act as the focal point to disseminate information on programmes offered by the Federal and state governments as well as financial institutions.",""],[1,"267","11","MSME Product Aggregation and Market Access Mechanism","A mechanism for aggregation of MSME products will be introduced to provide wider market access through utilisation of existing platforms at the district, municipal and local leader levels in small and mid-",""],[2,"395","7","National eCommerce Strategic Roadmap 2.0 Implementation","The National eCommerce Strategic Roadmap 2.0, 2021-2025 will be implemented to spur eCommerce activities.",""],[2,"395","7","National e-Invoicing Framework Development","A national e-Invoicing framework will also be developed to enable trade partners to seamlessly transact using digital mechanisms, particularly in the export of digital products and services.",""],[2,"395","8","Integrated One-Stop Centre Support for MSME E-Commerce","Local MSMEs will be encouraged to increase eCommerce trading through integration of existing one-stop centres to enable better access to funding, facilities and stewardship.",""],[2,"395","8","Coordination of Digital Business and Cross-Border Trade Support","The centre will also coordinate intervention related to digital businesses and cross border trading to encourage local businesses in penetrating the global market.",""],[2,"395","8","Regional Cooperation for Cross-Border Data Flow","Additionally, regional collaboration and cooperation will be leveraged to encourage seamless cross border data flow, without compromising the sovereignty and security of the data.",""],[2,"396","1","Sharing Economy Standards Adoption and Accreditation","To address these challenges and accelerate growth of the sharing economy, standards based on ISO International Workshop Agreement: Guiding principles and framework for the sharing economy (ISO-IWA 27:2017) will be adopted.",""],[2,"396","1","Local Sharing Economy Platform Accreditation Support","In addition, local platforms will be facilitated to be accredited with international sharing economy industry standards and platform certifications, for example ISO TC 324 on Sharing Economy and Fairwork Certification.",""],[2,"396","2","Cross-Border Sharing Economy Partnership Initiative","The growth of the sharing economy will be further expedited by fostering interregional collaboration and cooperation through cross border partnerships.",""],[2,"396","2","International Knowledge Exchange on Sharing Economy Regulation","Partnerships with international agencies will also be established for the exchange of knowledge and best practices, especially on regulations and standards.",""],[2,"396","2","Global Expansion Support for Local Sharing Platforms","Local sharing platforms will also be encouraged to go global and attract foreign investment.",""],[2,"396","3","Sharing Economy Awareness and Participation Campaign","In the Twelfth Plan, efforts to increase awareness and participation of the rakyat in the sharing economy will be intensified.",""],[2,"396","3","Industry Adoption of Sharing Economy Models","Industries including tourism, transportation and manufacturing will also be encouraged to adopt and leverage sharing economy models to improve productivity and competitiveness.",""],[2,"396","3","Local Community Sharing Economy and Gig Economy Initiatives","Initiatives will also be implemented to promote sharing economy activities, including the gig economy among local communities to supplement their incomes.",""],[2,"396","3","Sharing Economy and TVET Training Partnerships","Partnerships between sharing economy players and TVET institutions will be developed to provide training programmes for the rural population.",""],[2,"400","2","eCommerce Expansion for Vulnerable Groups","eCommerce activities will be expanded to scale up digital opportunities for vulnerable groups to exploit digital platforms.",""],[2,"400","2","MSME One-Stop Service Centres","One-stop service centres will be established to guide and facilitate the on-boarding of the MSMEs to venture into business and go global.",""],[2,"400","2","Comprehensive MSME Database Development","a comprehensive database will be developed to enhance the planning and monitoring of the MSMEs development.",""],[2,"400","4","Sharing Economy Promotion Initiatives","Several initiatives will be undertaken to facilitate the growth of this economy, including developing standards, setting up new platforms and fostering cross border activities.",""],[2,"400","4","Sharing Economy Awareness Programme","Awareness programmes will be implemented to further promote participation in the sharing economy, especially among the vulnerable groups.",""]],"50":[[1,"399","5","MSME Digital Adoption Support Programme","In the Twelfth Plan, MSMEs will be encouraged to adopt digital technologies in production, processes and business services, mainly in the back-end of business operations.",""],[1,"399","5","MSME Digital Readiness Training and Awareness Programme","Training and awareness programmes will be implemented for MSMEs to enhance readiness to digitalise and compete in the international market.",""],[1,"399","5","Digital Adoption Incentive Scheme","Appropriate digital solutions will be identified and proposed to match the level of business readiness through digital adoption incentives.",""],[1,"399","6","Holistic Financing Mechanism for MSME Digital Adoption","A holistic financing mechanism will be provided to accelerate the adoption of digital solutions by MSMEs.",""],[1,"399","6","eBerkat3 MSME and B40 Microfinance Support Initiative","The eBerkat3 initiative will be further promoted to assist the MSMEs as well as entrepreneurs among the B40 households in acquiring knowledge, securing insurance and accessing micro-financing services.",""],[1,"399","6","MSME Digitalisation Needs and Peer-to-Peer Financing Assessment","MSMEs and entrepreneurs digitalisation needs and peer-to-peer financing will be identified.",""],[1,"399","9","MSME Access to Finance Facilitation Initiative","Initiative to facilitate MSMEs to financial sources in expanding businesses.",""],[1,"400","1","Digital Inclusion and Online Business Development Initiatives","The emphasis will be on facilitating digital opportunities and creating more online business ventures.",""],[1,"400","1","Digital Economy Participation Expansion Initiative","The initiatives will promote greater participation of the rakyat in the digital economy.",""],[1,"400","2","MSME One-Stop Service Centres","One-stop service centres will be established to guide and facilitate the on-boarding of the MSMEs to venture into business and go global.",""],[1,"400","2","Comprehensive MSME Database Development","a comprehensive database will be developed to enhance the planning and monitoring of the MSMEs development.",""],[1,"400","3","New Business Venture Promotion Initiatives","Initiatives to promote the creation of new business ventures including solopreneur4 as well as global microenterprises will be enhanced.",""],[1,"400","3","eRezeki and eUsahawan Programme Expansion","The coverage and effectiveness of eRezeki and eUsahawan programmes will be improved to increase the digital skills and opportunities for the targeted groups, including those involved in the sharing economy.",""],[1,"400","3","Business Model Innovation and Programme Evaluation Mechanism","Performance of existing programmes will be evaluated, while new business models and approaches will be introduced.",""],[1,"400","3","Programme Monitoring and Evaluation Mechanism","An effective monitoring and evaluation mechanism will be utilised to ensure more effective implementation.",""],[1,"400","6","Targeted Socioeconomic Programme Delivery Mechanism","This will facilitate the targeted mechanisms for socioeconomic programmes as well as reduce inclusion and exclusion errors.",""],[2,"399","5","MSME Digital Adoption Incentives","In the Twelfth Plan, MSMEs will be encouraged to adopt digital technologies in production, processes and business services, mainly in the back-end of business operations.",""],[2,"399","5","MSME Digital Readiness Training and Awareness Programme","Training and awareness programmes will be implemented for MSMEs to enhance readiness to digitalise and compete in the international market.",""],[2,"399","5","Digital Solutions Identification and Matching Initiative","Appropriate digital solutions will be identified and proposed to match the level of business readiness through digital adoption incentives.",""],[2,"399","6","Holistic Financing Mechanism for MSME Digital Adoption","A holistic financing mechanism will be provided to accelerate the adoption of digital solutions by MSMEs.",""],[2,"399","6","eBerkat3 MSME and B40 Entrepreneur Support Initiative","The eBerkat3 initiative will be further promoted to assist the MSMEs as well as entrepreneurs among the B40 households in acquiring knowledge, securing insurance and accessing micro-financing services.",""],[2,"399","6","MSME Digitalisation Needs and Peer-to-Peer Financing Assessment","MSMEs and entrepreneurs digitalisation needs and peer-to-peer financing will be identified.",""],[2,"399","9","MSME Access to Finance Facilitation Initiative","Initiative to facilitate MSMEs to financial sources in expanding businesses.",""],[2,"400","3","New Business Venture Promotion Initiatives","Initiatives to promote the creation of new business ventures including solopreneur4 as well as global microenterprises will be enhanced.",""],[2,"400","3","eRezeki and eUsahawan Programme Expansion","The coverage and effectiveness of eRezeki and eUsahawan programmes will be improved to increase the digital skills and opportunities for the targeted groups, including those involved in the sharing economy.",""],[2,"400","3","Business Model Innovation and Programme Evaluation","Performance of existing programmes will be evaluated, while new business models and approaches will be introduced.",""],[2,"400","3","Programme Monitoring and Evaluation Mechanism","An effective monitoring and evaluation mechanism will be utilised to ensure more effective implementation.",""],[2,"453","1","MSME Digitalisation Priority","digitalisation of MSMEs will be a priority to enhance their competitiveness and resilience.",""],[2,"453","1","Entrepreneurship Support Ecosystem Development","The creation of a conducive and holistic ecosystem to support entrepreneurs and enterprises, as well as expansion of market access and international trade opportunities will enable MSMEs to be global, export-oriented and innovation-driven players.",""]],"51":[[1,"398","7","Strategic Investment Facilitation and MSME Digitalisation","Efforts to position Malaysia as the ASEAN digital centre will focus on facilitating strategic and quality investment as well as digitalising MSMEs to broaden market access.",""],[1,"398","8","Investment Climate and Venture Capital Promotion for the Digital Economy","Measures will be undertaken to improve the investment climate and encourage local and foreign venture capital in supporting a niche digital economy market.",""],[1,"398","8","MSC Bill of Guarantees Review","These include reviewing the current MSC Bill of Guarantees to further increase competitiveness, promote a more vibrant digital ecosystem, and attract prospective high-technology and high-value investments.",""],[1,"398","8","Regulatory and Real-Life Testing Sandboxes","Additionally, sandboxes will be established to create a conducive environment for real-life testing, including regulatory sandboxes to drive investment and the adoption of catalytic technology.",""],[1,"399","2","Fintech Accelerator Programmes","These will include the introduction of fintech accelerator programmes to encourage the setting up of fintech businesses in Malaysia.",""],[1,"403","17","Venture Capital Ecosystem Strengthening","Private investors, including angel investors, corporate investors and multinational companies, will be encouraged to participate in the venture capital ecosystem to provide more funds for start-up companies.",""],[1,"403","17","Tax Incentives for Venture Capital and Joint R&D","An improved tax structure will be introduced to strengthen the venture capital ecosystem and increase joint R&D efforts among industry, academia, government and international research institutions.",""]],"52":[[1,"399","1","Digital Content Industry Development Programme","The digital ecosystem will be improved to accelerate the growth of the digital content industry.",""],[1,"399","1","Inter-Agency Investment Promotion Coordination","Additionally, inter-agency collaboration will be strengthened to promote and attract high quality investments.",""],[1,"399","1","Digital Content Awareness Programme","Awareness programmes will be undertaken to promote digital content related opportunities, particularly among youth.",""],[1,"399","3","Regional Cyber Security Centre Development Initiative","Initiatives will also be intensified to establish Malaysia as a regional cyber security centre.",""],[1,"399","4","Malaysia Regional Digital Centre Branding and Promotion","Branding and extensive promotional activities will be undertaken to position Malaysia as the regional digital centre.",""],[1,"399","4","Digital Technology Investment Database","A single and transparent database of investment opportunities in digital technology will be developed to provide comprehensive information to local and foreign investors.",""],[1,"399","4","International Event Participation for Digital Firms","Moreover, local digital technology players will be encouraged to participate in international events to promote networking and for local businesses to go global.",""],[2,"398","7","ASEAN Digital Centre Positioning Initiative","Efforts to position Malaysia as the ASEAN digital centre will focus on facilitating strategic and quality investment as well as digitalising MSMEs to broaden market access.",""],[2,"398","8","Digital Economy Investment Climate Improvement Measures","Measures will be undertaken to improve the investment climate and encourage local and foreign venture capital in supporting a niche digital economy market.",""],[2,"398","8","Strategic Investment Promotion for the Digital Economy","New value propositions to drive strategic investment in the digital economy will be created.",""],[2,"398","8","MSC Bill of Guarantees Review","These include reviewing the current MSC Bill of Guarantees to further increase competitiveness, promote a more vibrant digital ecosystem, and attract prospective high-technology and high-value investments.",""],[2,"398","8","Regulatory Sandbox Establishment","Additionally, sandboxes will be established to create a conducive environment for real-life testing, including regulatory sandboxes to drive investment and the adoption of catalytic technology.",""],[2,"399","1","Digital Content Industry Development Initiative","The digital ecosystem will be improved to accelerate the growth of the digital content industry.",""],[2,"399","1","Digital Content Talent and Value-Chain Strengthening","The focus will be on developing talent, strengthening the industry value-chain and commercialising intellectual property to brand Malaysia as the digital content regional centre.",""],[2,"399","1","Inter-Agency Investment Promotion Collaboration","Additionally, inter-agency collaboration will be strengthened to promote and attract high quality investments.",""],[2,"399","1","Digital Content Awareness Programme for Youth","Awareness programmes will be undertaken to promote digital content related opportunities, particularly among youth.",""],[2,"399","2","Fintech Accelerator Programme","These will include the introduction of fintech accelerator programmes to encourage the setting up of fintech businesses in Malaysia.",""],[2,"399","3","Regional Cyber Security Centre Development Initiative","Initiatives will also be intensified to establish Malaysia as a regional cyber security centre.",""],[2,"399","3","Cyber Security Investment Attraction and Business Facilitation Package","Attractive packages and business facilitation will be provided to attract investment in cyber security.",""],[2,"399","3","International Certification Support for Local Digital Businesses","Local businesses will be encouraged to obtain international certification to better commercialise digital products and solutions globally.",""],[2,"399","4","Malaysia Regional Digital Centre Branding and Promotion Initiative","Branding and extensive promotional activities will be undertaken to position Malaysia as the regional digital centre.",""],[2,"399","4","Digital Technology Investment Opportunity Database","A single and transparent database of investment opportunities in digital technology will be developed to provide comprehensive information to local and foreign investors.",""],[2,"399","4","International Market Access Support for Local Digital Firms","Moreover, local digital technology players will be encouraged to participate in international events to promote networking and for local businesses to go global.",""],[2,"407","1","4IR Investment Attraction and MSME Capability Enhancement","Malaysia will capitalise on the strength of ASEAN to attract more investments in 4IR technologies, particularly from global unicorn companies.",""]],"53":[[1,"452","6","Sector Upgrading Through 4IR, Digitalisation, and Green Economy Measures","The services, manufacturing, agriculture, mining and construction sectors will be rejuvenated by encouraging these sectors to move up the value chain by adopting 4IR technologies, digitalisation and the green economy.",""],[1,"452","6","High-Potential Industry Development Initiative","The electrical and electronics, global services, aerospace, creative, tourism, halal and biomass industries, as well as smart farming activities, will be enhanced as new sources of growth.",""],[1,"455","15","Malaysia Economy Transformation Game Changers","The Government is committed to transform the Malaysian economy over the next five years.",""]],"54":[[2,"208","6","B40 Income Diversification and Support Programme","Several strategies will be implemented to empower the B40 in increasing their standard of living and income.",""],[2,"209","4","B40 Income Diversification Support Programme","The B40 will be encouraged to diversify sources of income so that they will enjoy a decent standard of living.",""],[2,"209","4","B40 High Value-Added Livelihoods and Technology Adoption Initiative","They will be encouraged to focus on high value-added activities through the application of best practices and adoption of technology such as smart farming, online businesses and outsourcing.",""],[2,"209","5","B40 Entrepreneurship and Online Business Support","Efforts to create more income-generating opportunities through entrepreneurship activities among the B40 will be enhanced.",""],[2,"209","5","B40 Online Business Participation Initiative","In addition, opportunities will be provided for the B40 to engage in online business.",""],[2,"209","5","Local Resource-Based Social Enterprise Promotion","The SE approach will be intensified by leveraging local resources to create business opportunities.",""],[2,"209","5","Inclusive Supply Chain Participation Initiative","An inclusive business approach will be promoted to enable the B40 to be involved in the supply chain.",""]],"55":[[1,"148","13","Unity, Sports, and Religious Activities Programme","Promoting social interaction through unity programmes, sports and religious activities.",""],[1,"148","14","Patriotism and Volunteerism Promotion through Media Platforms","Strengthening patriotism and volunteerism through the utilisation of digital and other media platforms.",""],[1,"162","1","Arts and Culture Unity Programmes","Efforts to increase understanding and tolerance among ethnics were undertaken through various arts and culture programmes.",""],[2,"148","13","Social Cohesion and Unity Programmes","Promoting social interaction through unity programmes, sports and religious activities.",""],[2,"148","14","Patriotism and Volunteerism Promotion through Media Platforms","Strengthening patriotism and volunteerism through the utilisation of digital and other media platforms.",""],[2,"154","3","National Unity Enhancement Initiative","Sports will be leveraged to build an active nation while unity among the rakyat will be enhanced.",""],[2,"155","1","Social Cohesion and National Unity Promotion","In addition, social cohesion and national unity were further promoted among Malaysians.",""],[2,"164","6","National Unity Strengthening Initiative","This will be achieved by ensuring national security and sovereignty, enhancing the healthcare service delivery, increasing the supply of quality and liveable affordable housing, leveraging sports in building an active nation as well as strengthening national unity.",""],[2,"180","5","Social Cohesion and National Unity Strengthening Measures","efforts will be concentrated on embracing diversity of society as a national asset, building a more tolerant society as well as strengthening governance for social cohesion and national unity.",""],[2,"181","1","Social Interaction and Diversity Preservation Measures","Measures will be undertaken to promote social interaction and capitalise on various educational platforms in preserving diversity and fostering unity.",""],[2,"181","2","Sports for Unity Promotion","In addition, sports activities will also be promoted as a medium to foster unity.",""],[2,"181","3","National and Community Engagement for Unity and Integration","Engagement sessions at national, state and community levels will be intensified, including through town hall and dialogue sessions, to encourage discussions on unity and national integration.",""],[2,"181","4","Inter-Religious Harmony Advocacy Programme Expansion","advocacy programmes in promoting inter-religious harmony will be expanded",""],[2,"181","4","Interfaith Respect and Harmony Outreach through Worship and Media","houses of worship and religious activities, as well as mainstream and social media will be leveraged to enhance respect for different faiths",""],[2,"181","5","Unity-Related Syllabus and Academic Programme Review","Unity-related syllabus and academic programmes in schools and HEIs will be reviewed and streamlined to enhance effectiveness and relevancy.",""],[2,"181","5","Bahasa Melayu Promotion and Proficiency Strengthening Initiative","Programmes and initiatives to promote the usage as well as to strengthen the proficiency of Bahasa Melayu, as the national language, in society will be further intensified.",""],[2,"181","5","Local Language Learning Diversification Through Digital Technology","Learning methods for other local languages will be diversified by leveraging digital technology.",""],[2,"181","5","Educational Programmes, Campaigns and Engagements for Noble Values","More educational programmes, campaigns and engagements will be undertaken to cultivate noble values.",""],[2,"181","6","Patriotism, Volunteerism, and Values Promotion Measures","Measures will be undertaken to strengthen patriotism and volunteerism as well as leverage the digital platform in instilling noble values.",""],[2,"181","7","Federal Constitution and Rukun Negara Awareness Campaigns","Understanding and appreciation of the Federal Constitution and Rukun Negara will be enhanced through wider awareness campaigns by leveraging digital media and other platforms.",""],[2,"181","7","Patriotism Icon Appointment Initiative","constitutional experts and social media influencers will be appointed as icons to raise the level of awareness on patriotism.",""],[2,"181","7","Patriotism Index Development","A new index will also be developed to assess the level of patriotism among Malaysians and assist in designing patriotism programmes.",""],[2,"181","7","National History Dissemination Initiative","Efforts will be intensified in disseminating knowledge on Malaysia's history to every citizen.",""],[2,"181","7","Short Documentary and Interactive Patriotism Programmes","Initiatives such as short documentaries and interactive programmes will be increased through collaboration with relevant stakeholders.",""],[2,"181","7","Overseas Patriotism Awareness Expansion","Awareness programmes, including Kelas Bimbingan Malaysia will be expanded to all major diplomatic missions to enhance patriotism and nationalism among Malaysians residing overseas.",""],[2,"182","1","Youth Volunteerism Promotion and Social Cohesion Programme","Volunteerism will be further promoted, especially among youth to strengthen social cohesion in society.",""],[2,"182","1","Expansion of Youth Volunteer Participation Programmes","Existing programmes will be expanded to enable youth to actively participate in voluntary activities.",""],[2,"182","1","Volunteer Icon Awards Scheme","Volunteer icon awards will be introduced to recognise outstanding youth volunteers and social media influencers in helping the government to inculcate volunteerism and fostering national unity.",""],[2,"182","1","Digital Platforms for Volunteerism and Unity","Digital platforms will be leveraged to boost the spirit of volunteerism and unity among youth as well as promote activities to build social cohesion and unity.",""],[2,"182","3","Social Cohesion and National Unity Policy Formulation","Measures will be undertaken to formulate policies and strengthen stakeholders collaboration in improving governance of social cohesion and unity.",""],[2,"182","3","Unity Promotion Programmes for Leaders and CSOs","Leaders and CSOs will also be encouraged to actively participate in various programmes to promote unity.",""],[2,"182","4","National Unity Policy","A national policy on unity will be introduced to promote social cohesiveness and harmony as well as capitalise diversity as an asset to strengthen national unity.",""],[2,"182","4","Unity Action Plan","An action plan will also be introduced to translate the policy through the implementation of specific programmes and initiatives by multiple sectors and agencies to further foster, strengthen and preserve unity among Malaysians.",""],[2,"182","4","Unity Capacity Building Programme","More capacity building programmes will be organised to strengthen competency and develop subject matter experts on unity.",""],[2,"182","5","Whole-of-Nation Social Cohesion Partnership Programme","collaboration between government, the private sector and CSOs will be intensified to promote social cohesion, unity, patriotism and volunteerism.",""],[2,"182","5","Inclusive Engagement and Smart Partnership Programmes","More engagement sessions and smart partnership programmes will be organised to ensure inclusive participation and promote better networking.",""],[2,"182","5","Public Facility Optimisation for Social Interaction","Public facilities, such as Pusat Rukun Tetangga, Kompleks Perpaduan, Pusat Komuniti Desa, Pusat Khidmat Masyarakat and Pusat Aktiviti Warga Emas will be optimised to encourage social interaction.",""],[2,"182","6","Unity-Related Community Engagement Programmes","Local governments and CSOs will be encouraged to proactively organise unity-related programmes, such as dialogues, focus group meetings and public information campaigns.",""],[2,"182","6","Mediation and Negotiation Capacity Building for Local Governments and CSOs","Training and capacity building programmes for local government and CSOs will be intensified to equip them with relevant mediation, conciliation and negotiation skills.",""],[2,"182","6","Diversified Funding for CSO Programmes","CSOs will be encouraged to diversify funding sources from crowdfunding and private sector to conduct these programmes.",""],[2,"182","7","Community Mediation and Unity Programmes","Community centres, offices of members of parliament and state assemblymen as well as places of worship will be utilised as venues to mediate community issues and promote unity programmes.",""],[2,"182","7","Religious Leader Engagement for Social Values","Religious leaders will be encouraged to play a more important role in instilling noble values and ensure the society behaves in a responsible and dignified manner.",""]],"56":[[1,"22","2","Poverty Alleviation and Living Standards Improvement Programmes","These include programmes to alleviate the poor and uplift the standard of living of the rakyat.",""],[1,"32","4","Poverty Reduction and Disparity Narrowing Measures","Addressing poverty as well as narrowing disparities among low income groups, inequitable Bumiputera socioeconomic outcomes, the low socioeconomic development of Orang Asli and social deprivation of specific target groups will be emphasised.",""],[1,"32","5","Hardcore Poverty Eradication and Livelihood Upliftment","Addressing poverty holistically and uplifting the standard of living of the rakyat is one of the game changers in strengthening inclusivity and uplifting the livelihood especially of the hardcore poor, B40 and vulnerable groups.",""],[1,"36","3","Dedicated Poverty Units and Centralized Poverty Database","These initiatives include establishing dedicated poverty units at the Federal and district levels as well as integrating and centralising a database on poverty.",""],[1,"36","3","Dedicated Tax for Poverty Alleviation Programmes","The possibility of introducing a dedicated tax to finance poverty alleviation programmes will be explored.",""],[1,"65","9","Targeted Cash Assistance and Minimum Wage Support","The increase will be supported by higher household income arising from expected stable labour market conditions in tandem with the post-COVID-19 economic recovery, higher minimum wage and cash assistance to the targeted groups.",""],[1,"150","6","Hardcore Poverty Elimination Mechanism","A more effective mechanism of eliminating hardcore poverty will encompass the following:",""],[1,"150","7","Dedicated Poverty Units at Federal and District Levels","Establishing dedicated poverty units at Federal and district levels.",""],[1,"150","8","Data-Driven Poverty Policy Formulation","Formulating poverty policies based on data-driven approach.",""],[1,"150","12","Dedicated Tax Financing for Poverty Alleviation Programmes","Exploring the possibility of introducing dedicated tax as a financing source for poverty alleviation programmes.",""],[1,"186","2","Hardcore Poverty Reduction and Inclusivity Initiatives","concerted efforts will be undertaken in further reducing hardcore poverty incidence, achieving equitability for all, while addressing current and future challenges, including the impact of COVID-19 pandemic.",""],[1,"200","6","Poverty Reduction and Inclusive Society Initiatives","Moving forward, the Twelfth Plan will focus on addressing poverty and building an inclusive society to achieve a decent standard of living and social justice.",""],[1,"200","6","Wellbeing Improvement Strategies and Initiatives","This will be undertaken through various strategies and initiatives to improve the wellbeing of the rakyat.",""],[1,"200","6","B40 Income and Living Standards Improvement","Concerted efforts will be geared towards addressing poverty, increasing income and the standard of living of the B40, supporting the M40 and achieving an equitable outcome for Bumiputera.",""],[1,"204","1","Multidimensional Poverty Eradication Programme","Poverty eradication programmes will be undertaken through coordinated efforts within the public sector, between the public and private sectors, CSOs and communities with special attention given to the poorest districts and locations in urban and rural areas.",""],[1,"204","1","Essential Services Access Improvement","The strategies include improving access to essential services, increasing income and uplifting the standard of living of the poor, addressing urban poverty, strengthening the service delivery mechanism and narrowing household inequality.",""],[1,"204","1","Urban Poverty Reduction Strategy","The strategies include improving access to essential services, increasing income and uplifting the standard of living of the poor, addressing urban poverty, strengthening the service delivery mechanism and narrowing household inequality.",""],[1,"204","1","Service Delivery Mechanism Strengthening","The strategies include improving access to essential services, increasing income and uplifting the standard of living of the poor, addressing urban poverty, strengthening the service delivery mechanism and narrowing household inequality.",""],[1,"205","1","Enhancement of Social Welfare Programmes for the Hardcore Poor and Poor","Existing social welfare programmes for the hardcore poor and poor will be enhanced.",""],[1,"205","1","Need-Based Cash Transfer and Healthcare Support","Assistance such as cash transfers and healthcare support will continue to be provided on a need basis.",""],[1,"205","1","Productive Welfare, Entrepreneurship and Microfinance Programme","Productive welfare programmes, including entrepreneurship and micro financing will be intensified to provide economic opportunities for the poor.",""],[1,"205","1","Training and Upskilling for Poor Households","In addition, training and upskilling will be strengthened among members of poor households to increase employability and capacity in venturing into income-generating activities.",""],[1,"205","1","Basic Financial Education for Poor Households","Basic financial education will be enhanced to improve their financial literacy.",""],[1,"205","2","Structured Private Sector Support for Poor Households","The private sector will be encouraged to offer structured and targeted assistance to poor households by providing scholarships and training, entrepreneurship and job opportunities as well as organising public benefit programmes through in situ development.",""],[1,"205","2","Promotion of Social Enterprises and Cooperatives","Social enterprises and cooperatives will be further promoted among the poor to increase household income.",""],[1,"205","2","Community-Based Income-Generating Activities","Community-based economic activities will be pursued as part of income-generating programmes.",""],[1,"205","2","Inclusive Business Approach for Poor Participation in Supply Chains","The inclusive business approach15 will be introduced to increase the involvement of the poor in the supply chain.",""],[1,"205","3","Essential Services Access Improvement Initiative","improving access to quality education and skills training as well as improving healthcare services will be given priority",""],[1,"205","4","Expanded Quality Education Support for Poor Households","Provision for quality education will be expanded to enhance the education level among members of poor households.",""],[1,"205","4","Subsidised Early Childhood Care and Education","subsidised ECCE will be continued and expanded to offer more affordable and high-quality childcare services for the poor.",""],[1,"205","4","Universal Early Childhood Education Access","Steps will be taken to provide early childhood education for all, while efforts will be intensified to ensure children from poor families will complete compulsory schooling of 11 years.",""],[1,"205","4","Targeted Scholarships for Poor Households","targeted interventions such as scholarships will be provided to reduce the number of school dropouts among poor households.",""],[1,"205","4","Scholarship Support for Skills Training and Higher Education","Scholarship opportunities will also be provided in easing the financial burden to pursue skills training, TVET and higher education.",""],[1,"205","5","Expanded Community Health Outreach for the Poor","Efforts to uplift the health of the poor will focus on improving the outreach of pre-natal care to geriatric services to the community.",""],[1,"205","5","Balanced Nutrition Awareness Promotion","In addition, awareness of the importance of good health will be further promoted by ensuring balanced nutrients intake at all stages of life.",""],[1,"205","5","Food Basket Programme for the Poor","Initiatives will be intensified to promote a balanced diet through the food basket programme for the poor according to the optimum minimum requirement based on the Malaysia Food Pyramid.",""],[1,"205","6","Base-of-the-Pyramid Business Inclusion Initiative","Businesses that engage people living at the base of the economic pyramid (B1) to provide goods and services, making them part of the value chain.",""],[1,"206","1","Basic Amenities and Housing Improvement for the Poor","These efforts include improving basic amenities and infrastructure as well as upgrading the living conditions of the poor.",""],[1,"206","2","Systematic Garbage Collection and Transportation Service Improvement","Access to systematic garbage collection and transportation services will be improved.",""],[1,"206","2","Basic Utilities and Broadband Connectivity Expansion","Basic utilities and communication services such as treated water, electricity and broadband connectivity will be enhanced, particularly in remote areas.",""],[1,"206","3","Housing Assistance Programme for Poor Households","the housing assistance programme will be continued.",""],[1,"206","4","Urban Poverty Support and Livelihood Improvement Measures","Efforts to address urban poverty will focus on improving access to social support in maintaining a certain level of quality of life and uplift the wellbeing of urban poor communities.",""],[1,"206","5","Entrepreneurship Training and Microfinancing Expansion for the Urban Poor","Access to entrepreneurship training and microfinancing will be expanded to increase and diversify income of the urban poor.",""],[1,"206","5","Social Enterprise Initiatives for the Urban Poor","SE initiatives will be promoted to address social and economic issues faced by the urban poor.",""],[1,"206","5","Community-Based Urban Livelihood Activities","Community-based activities in producing goods and services such as urban farming,",""],[1,"206","6","Childcare Services and Home-Based Food Business Promotion","childcare services and home-based food business will also be promoted to generate additional income.",""],[1,"206","6","Urban Poor Gig Economy Job Exposure Initiative","the urban poor will be exposed to job opportunities in the gig economy.",""],[1,"206","7","Expanded Early Childhood Care and Education Access for Urban Poor Households","Early childhood programmes will be made more accessible for children from urban poor households.",""],[1,"206","7","Community-Based ECCE Facility Expansion in Low-Cost Housing Areas","CBOs will be encouraged to provide ECCE facilities at public and private low-cost housing areas.",""],[1,"206","7","Enhanced Tuition Support for Urban Poor Students","the provision of tuition classes to the urban poor students residing in low-cost housing projects will be enhanced.",""],[1,"206","7","Online Tuition Delivery Through Digital Platforms","Digital platforms will be leveraged to provide online tuition.",""],[1,"206","7","Child Nutrition Awareness and Balanced Diet Promotion","A balanced nutrient intake will also be promoted to address malnutrition issues among children.",""],[1,"206","7","TVET Awareness Campaign for Urban Poor Youth","awareness of TVET programmes will be intensified among youth from urban poor households.",""],[1,"206","8","Service Delivery Mechanism Strengthening for Poverty Alleviation","The service delivery mechanism will be strengthened by enhancing the delivery system, improving poverty measurement and policy implementation as well as exploring new funding mechanisms.",""],[1,"206","9","Comprehensive Poverty Alleviation Service Delivery Reform","Service delivery will be strengthened through a comprehensive action plan and clear exit policy to improve efficiency and optimise resources.",""],[1,"206","9","Integrated Poverty Assistance Coordination Approach","Policies and initiatives will be streamlined, while an integrated approach will be adopted in providing assistance to various target groups.",""],[1,"206","9","Special Poverty Alleviation Unit","a special unit staffed by competent personnel will be established to address poverty in a holistic manner.",""],[1,"206","9","Central Poverty Alleviation Coordination and Monitoring Unit","The unit will function as the central body to plan, coordinate, implement and monitor measures in poverty alleviation.",""],[1,"206","9","Dedicated Tax Financing for Poverty Alleviation","The possibility of introducing dedicated tax to finance poverty alleviation programmes will be explored.",""],[1,"206","9","Expanded Poverty Alleviation Funding Sources","In addition, additional sources will also be considered from zakat and waqf, contributions from GLC, private entities and individuals.",""],[1,"206","9","Targeted Social Assistance and Poverty Alleviation Mapping","Social assistance and poverty alleviation programmes will be mapped out according to the different categories of the poor and vulnerable, focusing on the hardcore poor and poor from the B116 income decile.",""],[1,"208","1","eKasih Poverty Alleviation System Strengthening","The eKasih system will be reviewed and strengthened in identifying, implementing and monitoring poverty alleviation programmes to enhance transparency and accuracy of the data.",""],[1,"208","1","Poverty and Social Assistance Data Integration Platform","Databases related to poverty eradication and social assistance will be integrated through the development of Pangkalan Data Perlindungan Sosial (PDPS) to eliminate redundancies as well as inclusion and exclusion errors.",""],[1,"208","1","Big Data Analytics for Poverty Eradication","Big data analytics and data-driven policies will also be adopted in enhancing poverty eradication initiatives.",""],[1,"208","1","Bottom-Up Poverty Alleviation Approach","In addition to existing programmes, the bottom-up approach will be enhanced with the involvement of CSOs and CBOs.",""],[1,"208","1","Local Poverty Identification and Community Support","Local authorities and community leaders will also be empowered to identify and alleviate pockets of poverty at the community level.",""],[1,"208","1","Grassroots Poverty Coordination and Implementation Mechanism","Designated government officials at the local level will be assigned to coordinate and implement the grassroots approach to ensure the success of poverty alleviation initiatives.",""],[1,"208","2","Multidimensional Poverty Index Expansion and Adoption","The MPI dimensions and indicators will be expanded to be more comprehensive in better reflecting the measurement of multidimensional poverty.",""],[1,"208","3","Cost of Living Relief and Purchasing Power Support","Initiatives to reduce inequality include addressing the rising cost of living and increasing purchasing power as well as strengthening social protection.",""],[1,"208","3","Social Protection Strengthening","Initiatives to reduce inequality include addressing the rising cost of living and increasing purchasing power as well as strengthening social protection.",""],[1,"208","4","Enhanced Price Control Enforcement","enforcement of price control on goods and services will be enhanced to address price manipulation.",""],[1,"208","4","Food Bank Initiative","The Food Bank initiative and corporate social responsibility (CSR) programmes will help reduce the financial burden of poor households.",""],[1,"208","4","Corporate Social Responsibility Support Programmes","The Food Bank initiative and corporate social responsibility (CSR) programmes will help reduce the financial burden of poor households.",""],[1,"208","4","Financial Education and Literacy Promotion","financial education and literacy will be promoted among all age groups.",""],[1,"208","5","Merged Social Protection Coordination Council","The Malaysia Social Protection Council (MySPC) and Jawatankuasa Khas Kabinet Menangani Kemiskinan (JKKMK) have been merged to become a single entity.",""],[1,"208","6","B40 Income Diversification and Support Measures","Several strategies will be implemented to empower the B40 in increasing their standard of living and income.",""],[1,"208","6","Basic Services Access Improvement for Low-Income Households","efforts will be undertaken to improve access to basic services such as education, healthcare, housing and social protection.",""],[1,"209","4","B40 Income Diversification and Capability Support Programme","The B40 will be encouraged to diversify sources of income so that they will enjoy a decent standard of living.",""],[1,"209","4","B40 Education, Training, and Skills Support Initiative","Members of the households will be supported in terms of education, training and skills to enhance their capacity and capability through a bottom-up and community-based approach.",""],[1,"209","4","B40 High Value-Added Livelihoods and Technology Adoption Initiative","They will be encouraged to focus on high value-added activities through the application of best practices and adoption of technology such as smart farming, online businesses and outsourcing.",""],[1,"209","5","B40 Entrepreneurship and Online Business Support","Efforts to create more income-generating opportunities through entrepreneurship activities among the B40 will be enhanced.",""],[1,"209","5","Online Business Opportunities for B40 Households","In addition, opportunities will be provided for the B40 to engage in online business.",""],[1,"209","5","Local Resource-Based Social Enterprise Expansion","The SE approach will be intensified by leveraging local resources to create business opportunities.",""],[1,"209","5","Inclusive Supply Chain Participation for B40","An inclusive business approach will be promoted to enable the B40 to be involved in the supply chain.",""],[1,"209","6","Household Income Categorisation Review","The existing household income category will be reviewed to enable more targeted assistance.",""],[1,"209","7","Quality Education and Skills Training Support for B40 Households","Access to quality education and skills training will be strengthened to increase capacity and capability among the B40 household members.",""],[1,"209","7","Community-Based Early Childhood Education Expansion","ECCE will be further enhanced by encouraging CBOs to provide facilities in areas where such services are lacking.",""],[1,"209","7","Priority Scholarships and School Intake for B40 Children","Children of the B40 will continue to be given priority for scholarships and intakes into SBP and MRSM.",""],[1,"209","7","Financial Assistance for Skills Training and Higher Education","Financial assistance will be extended to pursue skills training including TVET and higher education.",""],[1,"209","8","Rural and Remote Primary Healthcare Enhancement","Access to quality healthcare and primary health facilities in rural and remote areas will be enhanced to provide affordable and better healthcare services.",""],[1,"209","8","PeKa B40 Health Assistance Expansion","The Skim Peduli Kesihatan untuk Kumpulan B40 (PeKa B40) initiative will be strengthened by widening the coverage and increasing the target group's awareness of Peka B40 benefits.",""],[1,"209","8","Waqf-Based Healthcare Support Scheme","The waqf model will be utilised as an alternative to ease the burden of B40 in meeting healthcare expenses.",""],[1,"209","8","Community Healthcare Services through Cooperatives","In addition, cooperatives will be encouraged to provide affordable healthcare services for their members.",""],[1,"210","1","Affordable Housing Support for the B40","Existing housing policies and programmes to assist the B40 will be continued.",""],[1,"210","1","Affordable Homeownership Priority for the B1 Income Decile","priority will be given to the B1 income decile to own affordable homes.",""],[1,"210","1","Rent-to-Own Housing Programme","housing programmes such as Rent-to-Own (RTO), Rumah Mesra Rakyat and Program Perumahan Penjawat Awam Malaysia will continue to be implemented.",""],[1,"210","2","B40 Poverty Alleviation and Empowerment Initiatives","Strategies and initiatives for addressing poverty and empowerment of the B40 will be implemented irrespective of ethnicity.",""],[1,"223","1","Integrated Poverty Reduction and Inclusivity Measures","During the Twelfth Plan period, more emphasis will be given towards efforts in addressing poverty and strengthening inclusivity, as well as in achieving a decent standard of living and social justice.",""],[1,"223","1","Education, Training, Entrepreneurship, and Social Protection Support","Measures will focus on education and training, entrepreneurship, social protection for all households, particularly the poor, B40, M40, Bumiputera, Orang Asli and specific target groups.",""],[1,"223","1","Holistic and Integrated Poverty Reduction Implementation","Holistic efforts and integrated implementation in addressing poverty and building an inclusive society will steer Malaysia to become a developed, inclusive and prosperous nation by 2030.",""],[1,"453","4","Targeted Poverty Alleviation Programmes","initiatives will be implemented to uplift the standard of living of the rakyat through specific and targeted programmes, irrespective of gender, ethnicity, socioeconomic status and location.",""],[1,"453","4","Dedicated Poverty Units","These will include the establishment of dedicated poverty units at the Federal and district levels as well as grassroot level poverty eradication solutions.",""],[1,"453","4","Grassroots Poverty Eradication Solutions","These will include the establishment of dedicated poverty units at the Federal and district levels as well as grassroot level poverty eradication solutions.",""],[1,"453","4","Bumiputera Socioeconomic Development Agenda","The socioeconomic development of Bumiputera will continue to be given priority as a national agenda.",""],[1,"453","4","Bumiputera Human Capital Development","Focus will be given in strengthening human capital development, enhancing business resilience and wealth creation as well as increasing sustainable Bumiputera corporate equity ownership.",""],[1,"453","4","Bumiputera Business Resilience and Wealth Creation Support","Focus will be given in strengthening human capital development, enhancing business resilience and wealth creation as well as increasing sustainable Bumiputera corporate equity ownership.",""],[1,"453","4","Sustainable Bumiputera Corporate Equity Ownership Expansion","Focus will be given in strengthening human capital development, enhancing business resilience and wealth creation as well as increasing sustainable Bumiputera corporate equity ownership.",""],[2,"22","2","Poverty Alleviation and Living Standards Improvement Programmes","Various game-changing and radical initiatives will be implemented.",""],[2,"24","5","Inclusive Economic Growth and Distribution Strategy","It is a commitment to achieve sustainable economic growth accompanied by fair, equitable and inclusive economic distribution, across all income groups, ethnicities, regions and supply chains.",""],[2,"32","4","Poverty Reduction and Disparity Narrowing Measures","Addressing poverty as well as narrowing disparities among low income groups, inequitable Bumiputera socioeconomic outcomes, the low socioeconomic development of Orang Asli and social deprivation of specific target groups will be emphasised",""],[2,"32","5","Hardcore Poverty Eradication and Livelihood Upliftment","Addressing poverty holistically and uplifting the standard of living of the rakyat is one of the game changers in strengthening inclusivity and uplifting the livelihood especially of the hardcore poor, B40 and vulnerable groups.",""],[2,"36","3","Dedicated Poverty Units and Centralized Poverty Database","These initiatives include establishing dedicated poverty units at the Federal and district levels as well as integrating and centralising a database on poverty.",""],[2,"36","3","Dedicated Tax for Poverty Alleviation","The possibility of introducing a dedicated tax to finance poverty alleviation programmes will be explored.",""],[2,"186","2","Hardcore Poverty Reduction and Inclusivity Initiatives","In this regard, concerted efforts will be undertaken in further reducing hardcore poverty incidence, achieving equitability for all, while addressing current and future challenges, including the impact of COVID-19 pandemic.",""],[2,"200","6","Inclusive Poverty Reduction and Wellbeing Initiatives","This will be undertaken through various strategies and initiatives to improve the wellbeing of the rakyat.",""],[2,"200","6","Poverty, Income, and Living Standards Improvement Measures","Concerted efforts will be geared towards addressing poverty, increasing income and the standard of living of the B40, supporting the M40 and achieving an equitable outcome for Bumiputera.",""],[2,"204","1","Multidimensional Poverty Eradication Programme","Poverty eradication programmes will be undertaken through coordinated efforts within the public sector, between the public and private sectors, CSOs and communities with special attention given to the poorest districts and locations in urban and rural areas.",""],[2,"204","1","Essential Services Access Improvement","The strategies include improving access to essential services, increasing income and uplifting the standard of living of the poor, addressing urban poverty, strengthening the service delivery mechanism and narrowing household inequality.",""],[2,"204","1","Income Upliftment for the Poor","The strategies include improving access to essential services, increasing income and uplifting the standard of living of the poor, addressing urban poverty, strengthening the service delivery mechanism and narrowing household inequality.",""],[2,"204","1","Service Delivery Mechanism Strengthening","The strategies include improving access to essential services, increasing income and uplifting the standard of living of the poor, addressing urban poverty, strengthening the service delivery mechanism and narrowing household inequality.",""],[2,"204","1","Household Inequality Reduction Measures","The strategies include improving access to essential services, increasing income and uplifting the standard of living of the poor, addressing urban poverty, strengthening the service delivery mechanism and narrowing household inequality.",""],[2,"206","9","Comprehensive Poverty Alleviation Action Plan","Service delivery will be strengthened through a comprehensive action plan and clear exit policy to improve efficiency and optimise resources.",""],[2,"206","9","Expanded Poverty Alleviation Funding Sources","In addition, additional sources will also be considered from zakat and waqf, contributions from GLC, private entities and individuals.",""],[2,"453","4","Targeted Poverty Alleviation Programmes","initiatives will be implemented to uplift the standard of living of the rakyat through specific and targeted programmes, irrespective of gender, ethnicity, socioeconomic status and location.",""],[2,"453","4","Dedicated Poverty Units","These will include the establishment of dedicated poverty units at the Federal and district levels as well as grassroot level poverty eradication solutions.",""],[2,"453","4","Grassroot Poverty Eradication Solutions","These will include the establishment of dedicated poverty units at the Federal and district levels as well as grassroot level poverty eradication solutions.",""],[2,"453","4","Bumiputera Socioeconomic Development Agenda","The socioeconomic development of Bumiputera will continue to be given priority as a national agenda.",""],[2,"453","4","Bumiputera Human Capital Development","Focus will be given in strengthening human capital development, enhancing business resilience and wealth creation as well as increasing sustainable Bumiputera corporate equity ownership.",""],[2,"453","4","Bumiputera Business Resilience and Wealth Creation Support","Focus will be given in strengthening human capital development, enhancing business resilience and wealth creation as well as increasing sustainable Bumiputera corporate equity ownership.",""],[2,"453","4","Sustainable Bumiputera Corporate Equity Ownership Expansion","Focus will be given in strengthening human capital development, enhancing business resilience and wealth creation as well as increasing sustainable Bumiputera corporate equity ownership.",""]],"57":[[1,"145","1","Poverty Reduction and Social Inclusion Strategies","Addressing poverty will be given higher priority during the Twelfth Plan period, consistent with the principle of leaving no one behind, in ensuring social justice and a decent standard of living for the rakyat.",""],[1,"145","1","B40 Empowerment Measures","Several strategies will be implemented to empower the B40 in increasing their standard of living and income, while support will be provided to the M40 to improve their quality of life.",""],[1,"145","1","Bumiputera Human Capital and Asset Ownership Agenda","The Bumiputera Agenda will be pursued by further enhancing human capital development, expanding business opportunities and increasing their share of equity and property ownership.",""],[1,"145","1","Comprehensive Development Approach for Orang Asli Wellbeing","A more comprehensive development approach will be introduced to enhance the wellbeing of the Orang Asli community.",""],[1,"145","1","Wellbeing Support for Children, Youth, Women, Older Persons, Persons with Disabilities and Families","Synergistic efforts will be mobilised in improving the wellbeing of children, youth, women, older persons, persons with disabilities (PWDs) and family institutions.",""],[2,"145","1","Poverty Reduction and Social Inclusion Strategies","Addressing poverty will be given higher priority during the Twelfth Plan period, consistent with the principle of leaving no one behind, in ensuring social justice and a decent standard of living for the rakyat.",""],[2,"145","1","B40 Empowerment Measures","Several strategies will be implemented to empower the B40 in increasing their standard of living and income, while support will be provided to the M40 to improve their quality of life.",""],[2,"145","1","Bumiputera Human Capital and Asset Ownership Development","The Bumiputera Agenda will be pursued by further enhancing human capital development, expanding business opportunities and increasing their share of equity and property ownership.",""],[2,"145","1","Orang Asli Comprehensive Development Approach","A more comprehensive development approach will be introduced to enhance the wellbeing of the Orang Asli community.",""],[2,"145","1","Integrated Wellbeing Support for Vulnerable Groups","Synergistic efforts will be mobilised in improving the wellbeing of children, youth, women, older persons, persons with disabilities (PWDs) and family institutions.",""],[2,"150","7","Dedicated Poverty Units","Establishing dedicated poverty units at Federal and district levels.",""],[2,"150","8","Data-Driven Poverty Policy Formulation","Formulating poverty policies based on data-driven approach.",""],[2,"150","10","Bottom-Up Approach Programmes","Enhancing bottom-up approach programmes.",""],[2,"150","12","Dedicated Tax Financing for Poverty Alleviation Programmes","Exploring the possibility of introducing dedicated tax as a financing source for poverty alleviation programmes.",""],[2,"220","1","Target Group Wellbeing Empowerment Initiatives","Synergistic efforts will be mobilised in empowering specific target groups to improve their wellbeing and achieve a higher standard of living based on the principle of leaving no one behind.",""]],"58":[[2,"222","4","Family Institution Strengthening through Community Empowerment","the family institution will be strengthened through community empowerment.",""],[2,"222","4","Redesign of Pre-marital Education and Parenting Skills Programmes","Pre-marital education and parenting skills programmes will be redesigned to leverage the digital platform and be more relevant to the current issues and challenges.",""],[2,"222","5","Flexible Working Arrangements and Work-Life Balance Measures","Work-life balance will be enhanced by promoting flexible working hours.",""],[2,"222","5","Expansion of Adaptable Working Arrangements","Adaptable working arrangements will be expanded while the private sector will be encouraged to provide paternity leave and better care centres.",""],[2,"222","5","Sexual and Reproductive Health Programme Expansion","Sexual and reproductive health programmes will be enhanced by expanding the role of Lembaga Penduduk dan Pembangunan Keluarga Negara (LPPKN) Subfertility Centre.",""],[2,"222","5","Financial Literacy and Debt Advisory Services","Financial literacy and debt advisory services will be improved, particularly for families from the B40.",""],[2,"222","5","Parental Digital Literacy Awareness Campaign","Awareness on digital literacy among parents will be expanded to address digital addiction, while child cyber protection programmes will be incorporated in the school curriculum to increase understanding of cyber threats.",""],[2,"222","5","Child Cyber Protection Curriculum Integration","child cyber protection programmes will be incorporated in the school curriculum to increase understanding of cyber threats.",""]],"59":[[2,"195","1","Expansion of the Child Care Needs and Child Protection Unit","The Child Care Needs and Child Protection Unit (CCNCPU) was expanded to protect the interest of children.",""],[2,"195","1","Training of Child Protectors Nationwide","244 child protectors were trained nationwide.",""],[2,"195","1","Child Protection and Rehabilitation Programme","411 schools participated in the Child Protection and Rehabilitation Programme that benefitted 96,512 students.",""],[2,"195","1","Expansion of Early Childhood Care and Education Facilities","To strengthen early childhood care and education (ECCE), 30 new Taman Asuhan Kanak-kanak (TASKA) were set up in government premises with an allocation of RM4.6 million in 2020.",""],[2,"221","1","Child Development Governance and Implementation Mechanisms","governance and implementation mechanisms for children development and protection will be enhanced.",""],[2,"221","1","National Child Development Index","A national child development index will be formulated as a tool to improve policies related to the biological and psychological growth of children.",""],[2,"221","1","Child Justice Process Review","The child judicial process will be reviewed to further strengthen children protection.",""],[2,"221","1","Juvenile Offender Separation and Reintegration Programme","programmes to separate children with minor crimes from those committing more serious offences will be undertaken to assist the reintegration of the young offenders into the community.",""],[2,"221","1","National Strategy Plan to Address Child Marriage","the issue of child marriage will continue to be addressed through the implementation of the National Strategy Plan in Handling the Causes of Child Marriage.",""]],"60":[[1,"195","6","Disability Accessibility Action Plan","The Disability Accessibility Action Plan endorsed in 2019 served as a guideline to local authorities in improving accessibility to public facilities.",""],[1,"195","6","Disability Equality Training Programme","Meanwhile, 85 Disability Equality Training programmes were organised to ensure active participation of PWDs in society.",""],[1,"195","6","Community Rehabilitation Programme for Persons with Disabilities","The Pemulihan Dalam Komuniti (PDK) programme was implemented to develop capacity and capability of PWDs.",""],[1,"195","6","PDKNet ICT Upgrade Initiative","A total of 240 PDKs out of 560 were upgraded with information and communication technology (ICT) facilities and rebranded as PDKNet.",""],[1,"195","6","Study on Economic and Job Opportunities for Persons with Disabilities","A study to explore more economic and job opportunities for PWDs as well as to strengthen the support system for carers of PWDs was initiated in 2019 and is expected to be completed in 2021.",""],[1,"196","1","PWD Registration Outreach and Targeted Assistance Programme","Various outreach programmes were conducted to increase the registration of PWDs in Sistem Maklumat Orang Kurang Upaya (SMOKU), including through the Santuni OKU programme.",""],[1,"196","1","Job Coach Service Employment Support Programme","Under the Job Coach Service programme, a total of 1,397 PWDs were trained and facilitated in securing employment.",""],[1,"196","1","PWD Representation in the Dewan Negara","One PWD representative continues to be a member of Dewan Negara.",""],[1,"222","3","PWD Registration System Improvement","The registration of PWDs in SMOKU will be improved through strategic collaboration among various agencies and CSOs as well as through the integration with the Malaysian Government Central Data Exchange (MyGDX) system.",""],[1,"222","3","PWD Inclusion in Education, Training, Employment, Financing and Sports","The inclusiveness of PWDs in education and training, employment, financing as well as sports will be enhanced.",""],[1,"222","3","Economic Opportunity Expansion for PWDs","More economic opportunities will be made available for PWDs through various platforms, including the sharing and digital economies.",""],[1,"222","3","Universal Design Promotion for Public Facilities","Adoption of universal design principle will be further encouraged among local authorities to improve accessibility to public facilities for PWDs.",""],[1,"222","3","PWD Social Protection Strengthening","Social protection for PWDs will also be strengthened by reviewing insurance protection coverage, including for the caregivers.",""],[2,"195","6","Disability Accessibility Action Plan","The Disability Accessibility Action Plan endorsed in 2019 served as a guideline to local authorities in improving accessibility to public facilities.",""],[2,"195","6","Disability Equality Training Programmes","Meanwhile, 85 Disability Equality Training programmes were organised to ensure active participation of PWDs in society.",""],[2,"195","6","Community-Based Rehabilitation Programme","The Pemulihan Dalam Komuniti (PDK) programme was implemented to develop capacity and capability of PWDs.",""],[2,"195","6","PDKNet ICT Upgrade Initiative","A total of 240 PDKs out of 560 were upgraded with information and communication technology (ICT) facilities and rebranded as PDKNet.",""],[2,"196","1","PWD Representation in Dewan Negara","One PWD representative continues to be a member of Dewan Negara.",""],[2,"222","3","PWD Registration System Integration and Collaboration","The registration of PWDs in SMOKU will be improved through strategic collaboration among various agencies and CSOs as well as through the integration with the Malaysian Government Central Data Exchange (MyGDX) system.",""],[2,"222","3","PWD Inclusion in Education, Training, Employment, Financing, and Sports","The inclusiveness of PWDs in education and training, employment, financing as well as sports will be enhanced.",""],[2,"222","3","PWD Economic Opportunity Expansion through Sharing and Digital Economies","More economic opportunities will be made available for PWDs through various platforms, including the sharing and digital economies.",""],[2,"222","3","Universal Design Promotion for Public Facility Accessibility","Adoption of universal design principle will be further encouraged among local authorities to improve accessibility to public facilities for PWDs.",""],[2,"222","3","PWD Social Protection and Insurance Coverage Review","Social protection for PWDs will also be strengthened by reviewing insurance protection coverage, including for the caregivers.",""]],"61":[[1,"200","6","Orang Asli and Target Group Wellbeing Uplift","Focus will also be given to uplift the wellbeing of Orang Asli and specific target groups.",""],[1,"218","1","Comprehensive Orang Asli Development Approach","a comprehensive development approach with a focus on education will be introduced.",""],[1,"218","1","Orang Asli Socioeconomic Development Plan","A socioeconomic development plan for Orang Asli will be formulated focusing on poverty reduction as well as expanding basic infrastructure, amenities and services.",""],[1,"218","1","Inter-Agency Service Delivery Coordination","Inter-agency collaboration will also be strengthened to improve service delivery.",""],[1,"218","4","Orang Asli Education Access Improvement Programme","Access to education will be improved to facilitate social and economic mobility of Orang Asli.",""],[1,"218","5","Streamlining Ongoing Education Programmes","Efforts in strengthening ongoing programmes on education will be streamlined.",""],[1,"218","5","ECCE Access Improvement for Orang Asli Communities","Access to ECCE for the Orang Asli community will be improved to better prepare them in acquiring the basic skills of reading, writing and counting (3M).",""],[1,"218","5","Student Dropout Reduction and School Retention Measures","Student dropouts during the transition from ECCE level to primary and from primary to secondary will be reduced while teaching and learning methods will be improved to ensure that Orang Asli students remain in school and progress towards higher levels of education.",""],[1,"218","5","TVET and Tertiary Education Enrollment Expansion","In addition, enrolment in TVET programmes and tertiary education will be increased.",""],[1,"218","6","Community Learning and Attendance Improvement Programme","The Program Jom Belajar will be further expanded within the community to improve student attendance through innovative teaching and suitable learning methods in reducing illiteracy.",""],[1,"218","6","Teacher Accommodation Support","In ensuring a conducive living environment for the teachers, adequate decent accommodation will be provided.",""],[1,"218","6","Community Basic Literacy and Numeracy Classes","The Program Kelas Komuniti will continue to ensure the community is able to master the basic 3M skills.",""],[1,"219","1","Expanded Access to Orang Asli Education","Access to education will be improved to encourage social and economic mobility of Orang Asli.",""],[1,"219","1","Comprehensive Special Model School 9 Expansion","The Comprehensive Special Model School 9 (K9) which offers schooling up to Form 3 will be made accessible to more Orang Asli students in facilitating the transition from primary to secondary schools.",""],[1,"219","1","Comprehensive Special Model School 11 Implementation","A Comprehensive Special Model School 11 (K11) that provides 11 years of schooling will be implemented to ensure Orang Asli students remain in school until they sit for the SPM examination.",""],[1,"219","1","K11 TVET-Oriented Secondary Education Programme","In order to motivate the Orang Asli students to attend secondary education, K11 schools will focus on TVET programmes with specific training skills taking into account the local as well as national requirements.",""],[1,"219","2","Bringing School to Community Programme","a special programme, Bringing School to Community, will be introduced through collaboration between government, universities and CSOs.",""],[1,"219","3","Orang Asli Integrated Socioeconomic Development Plan","a development plan will be formulated, encompassing education and training, increasing income, provision of basic infrastructure, land development, healthcare services and housing.",""],[1,"219","3","Inter-Agency Coordination for Orang Asli Service Delivery","Inter-agency collaboration will be strengthened to enhance the efficiency and effectiveness of the delivery system in improving the wellbeing of Orang Asli.",""],[1,"219","3","Capacity Building for Jabatan Kemajuan Orang Asli and Relevant Agencies","The capacity and capability of Jabatan Kemajuan Orang Asli and other relevant agencies will be enhanced.",""],[1,"219","4","Income-Generating Poverty Eradication Programme","Poverty eradication programmes will focus on income-generating activities.",""],[1,"219","4","Commercial Crop and Handicraft Development Initiative","Potential crops that have commercial value and traditional handicrafts will be further developed to fully exploit their potential.",""],[1,"219","4","Orang Asli Microfinance and Skills Training Support","microfinancing facilities and skills training will be provided for Orang Asli to become entrepreneurs, particularly in ecotourism, agrotourism as well as arts and handicrafts.",""],[1,"219","4","Land Gazettement for Economic Activities","State governments will be encouraged to enhance the gazettement of land for economic activities.",""],[1,"219","5","Orang Asli Basic Infrastructure and Services Expansion","Efforts will be intensified to improve the livelihood of Orang Asli by expanding basic infrastructure, amenities and services.",""],[2,"218","1","Comprehensive Development Approach for Orang Asli","a comprehensive development approach with a focus on education will be introduced.",""],[2,"218","1","Orang Asli Socioeconomic Development Plan","A socioeconomic development plan for Orang Asli will be formulated focusing on poverty reduction as well as expanding basic infrastructure, amenities and services.",""],[2,"218","1","Inter-Agency Service Delivery Coordination for Orang Asli","Inter-agency collaboration will also be strengthened to improve service delivery.",""],[2,"219","3","Orang Asli Integrated Socioeconomic Development Plan","In this regard, a development plan will be formulated, encompassing education and training, increasing income, provision of basic infrastructure, land development, healthcare services and housing.",""],[2,"219","5","Orang Asli Livelihood Improvement Programme","Efforts will be intensified to improve the livelihood of Orang Asli by expanding basic infrastructure, amenities and services.",""]],"62":[[1,"370","10","Mandatory Employer Childcare Facilities Law","a new law will be introduced to mandate employers to provide childcare facilities, of which penalties will be imposed for those who failed to comply.",""]],"63":[[1,"370","12","Gig Worker Social Protection Expansion","Measures will also be undertaken to introduce social protection for gig workers and increase compliance with labour laws and regulations.",""],[1,"370","12","Labour Law Compliance Enforcement","Measures will also be undertaken to introduce social protection for gig workers and increase compliance with labour laws and regulations.",""],[1,"372","4","Enhanced Social Protection Scheme for Informal Workers","a social protection scheme, which includes unemployment and health benefits, as well as retirement savings, will be enhanced.",""],[1,"372","4","Gig Worker Information Capture and Legal Provision Reform","an innovative approach by leveraging existing intermediaries or platform providers to capture information on gig workers will be explored.",""],[1,"372","4","Gig Worker Training Fund","A training fund for gig workers will be established to assist in upgrading their skills in order to move to a more favourable employment.",""],[1,"372","5","Gig Worker Psychosocial Risk Mitigation Measures","Psychosocial risks, especially work-related stress faced by gig workers, including those working in international platforms in different time zones, will be addressed.",""],[2,"370","9","Strengthened Labour Rights and Anti-Trafficking Enforcement","Efforts will continue to be undertaken to ensure employers in all economic sectors protect the welfare of the workers and comply with the international obligations related to labour.",""],[2,"370","12","Gig Worker Social Protection Expansion","Measures will also be undertaken to introduce social protection for gig workers",""],[2,"370","12","Labour Law Compliance Enforcement","increase compliance with labour laws and regulations",""],[2,"372","4","Enhanced Social Protection Scheme for Informal Workers","a social protection scheme, which includes unemployment and health benefits, as well as retirement savings, will be enhanced",""],[2,"372","4","Gig Worker Information Capture and Legal Provision Reform","an innovative approach by leveraging existing intermediaries or platform providers to capture information on gig workers will be explored",""],[2,"372","4","Gig Worker Training Fund","A training fund for gig workers will be established to assist in upgrading their skills in order to move to a more favourable employment",""],[2,"372","5","Gig Worker Psychosocial Risk Mitigation Measures","Psychosocial risks, especially work-related stress faced by gig workers, including those working in international platforms in different time zones, will be addressed.",""],[2,"372","6","Labour Law Compliance Capacity and Collaboration Strengthening","The capacity of and collaboration among employers, employees and enforcement officers will be strengthened to promote shared responsibility in complying with labour laws and regulations.",""],[2,"372","6","Dedicated Labour Training Hub Upgrade","An existing facility will be upgraded as a dedicated training hub for learning, knowledge sharing, and capacity building for the employers, employees and enforcement officers.",""]],"64":[[2,"206","9","Integrated Poverty Coordination Unit","In this regard, a special unit staffed by competent personnel will be established to address poverty in a holistic manner.",""],[2,"206","9","Poverty Alleviation Financing Options Review","The possibility of introducing dedicated tax to finance poverty alleviation programmes will be explored.",""],[2,"206","9","Expanded Poverty Alleviation Funding Sources","In addition, additional sources will also be considered from zakat and waqf, contributions from GLC, private entities and individuals.",""],[2,"206","9","Targeted Social Assistance and Poverty Mapping","Social assistance and poverty alleviation programmes will be mapped out according to the different categories of the poor and vulnerable, focusing on the hardcore poor and poor from the B116 income decile.",""],[2,"208","1","eKasih Poverty Programme Review and Strengthening","The eKasih system will be reviewed and strengthened in identifying, implementing and monitoring poverty alleviation programmes to enhance transparency and accuracy of the data.",""],[2,"208","1","Integrated Social Protection Database Development","Databases related to poverty eradication and social assistance will be integrated through the development of Pangkalan Data Perlindungan Sosial (PDPS) to eliminate redundancies as well as inclusion and exclusion errors.",""],[2,"208","1","Big Data Analytics for Poverty Eradication","Big data analytics and data-driven policies will also be adopted in enhancing poverty eradication initiatives.",""],[2,"208","1","Bottom-Up Poverty Alleviation Approach","In addition to existing programmes, the bottom-up approach will be enhanced with the involvement of CSOs and CBOs.",""],[2,"208","1","Local Poverty Identification and Community-Level Support","Local authorities and community leaders will also be empowered to identify and alleviate pockets of poverty at the community level.",""],[2,"208","1","Grassroots Poverty Coordination and Implementation","Designated government officials at the local level will be assigned to coordinate and implement the grassroots approach to ensure the success of poverty alleviation initiatives.",""],[2,"208","2","Multidimensional Poverty Index Expansion and Application","The MPI dimensions and indicators will be expanded to be more comprehensive in better reflecting the measurement of multidimensional poverty.",""],[2,"208","5","Merged Social Protection Coordination Council","The Malaysia Social Protection Council (MySPC) and Jawatankuasa Khas Kabinet Menangani Kemiskinan (JKKMK) have been merged to become a single entity.",""],[2,"209","6","Household Income Categorisation Review","The existing household income category will be reviewed to enable more targeted assistance.",""],[2,"223","1","Inclusive Poverty Reduction and Social Protection Measures","During the Twelfth Plan period, more emphasis will be given towards efforts in addressing poverty and strengthening inclusivity, as well as in achieving a decent standard of living and social justice.",""],[2,"223","1","Holistic Poverty Reduction and Inclusive Society Implementation","Holistic efforts and integrated implementation in addressing poverty and building an inclusive society will steer Malaysia to become a developed, inclusive and prosperous nation by 2030.",""]],"65":[[1,"274","3","Poverty Reduction Programmes for Sabah and Sarawak","The incidence of poverty in both states will be reduced through programmes and projects that focus on income-generating activities.",""],[1,"274","3","Employment and High-Value Economic Activity Expansion for Indigenous Communities","The socioeconomic status of Anak Negeri Sabah and Bumiputera Sarawak will be improved by creating more employment opportunities and high value economic activities.",""],[1,"274","6","Poverty Alleviation and Income Diversification Measures","Efforts to address poverty, as well as increase and diversify sources of income will be intensified.",""],[1,"274","6","Bumiputera Socioeconomic Development Measures","measures to alleviate poverty and strengthen Bumiputera socioeconomic development will be escalated.",""],[1,"274","6","Employability and Entrepreneurship Promotion","Efforts will also be undertaken to increase employability and promote entrepreneurship as well as facilitate the development of NCR land.",""],[1,"274","7","Poverty Alleviation Programmes Enhancement","Poverty alleviation programmes will be enhanced to uplift the wellbeing of poor households.",""],[1,"274","7","Education, Skills Training, and Healthcare Access Expansion","Efforts will be intensified to improve quality education and skills training as well as access to healthcare services.",""],[1,"274","7","Basic Infrastructure and Services Expansion for Poor Households","the provision of basic infrastructure and services including roads, treated water, electricity and broadband connectivity will be enhanced.",""],[1,"274","8","Poor Household Income Diversification and Skills Development Programme","Sources of income of the poor households will be increased and diversified through participation in high value-added economic activities as well as human capital and entrepreneurship development.",""],[1,"274","8","High-Value Indigenous Product Commercialisation Initiative","The rich natural resources and culture will be leveraged to commercialise high value-added indigenous products, including arts and crafts as well as venturing into agriculture, aquaculture and ecotourism industries.",""],[1,"274","8","TVET Upskilling Programme","The upskilling programmes, especially TVET, will be intensified.",""],[1,"274","8","Customised Community Skills Training Programme","Untapped ancestral skills and talent of local communities will be unleashed by providing customised skills training.",""],[1,"274","9","Entrepreneurship Ecosystem Strengthening for Community Development","The entrepreneurship ecosystem such as financing assistance and marketing through digital platforms will be strengthened to facilitate entrepreneurs in accelerating the socioeconomic development of these communities.",""],[1,"274","9","Federal-State and Multi-Stakeholder Service Delivery Cooperation","In improving service delivery to the target groups, cooperation between the Federal and state governments, the private sector, community-based organisations and communities will be strengthened.",""],[1,"274","9","Bottom-Up Delivery Mechanism Enhancement","Delivery mechanisms will be enhanced through a bottom-up approach and involvement of social enterprises in alleviating pockets of poverty at the community level.",""],[1,"275","1","Socioeconomic Empowerment of Anak Negeri Sabah and Bumiputera Sarawak","The socioeconomic development of Anak Negeri Sabah and Bumiputera Sarawak will continue to be given priority to uplift their wellbeing.",""],[1,"275","1","Capacity and Capability Enhancement for Employability and Entrepreneurship","In this regard, the capacity and capability of these communities will be enhanced to improve employability and entrepreneurship.",""],[1,"275","2","Education and Training Support for Anak Negeri Sabah and Bumiputera Sarawak","Education and training will be pursued to enhance the capacity and capability of these communities, starting from early childhood care and education until tertiary level.",""],[1,"275","2","Entrepreneurship and Market Access Support for Indigenous Communities","Entrepreneurship will be inculcated among these communities by providing necessary support such as financing facilities, logistic services and access to market, including through digital platform.",""],[1,"275","3","Human Resources Development Fund Access Improvement","Access to the human resources development fund programmes will be improved to enhance the employability of youth by providing dedicated reskilling and upskilling programmes to leverage local economic opportunities.",""],[1,"275","3","Youth Soft Skills Development Courses","Youth will also be provided courses on self- discipline, interpersonal and communication skills, adaptability and self-confidence to better compete with more experienced workers.",""],[1,"275","3","Youth Entrepreneurship Support Programme","In addition, youth who are inclined towards entrepreneurship will be channelled to specific programmes in developing their ability to venture into business.",""],[1,"277","1","Sabah and Sarawak Socioeconomic Development Enhancement","In the Twelfth Plan, greater emphasis will be given in enhancing socioeconomic development in Sabah and Sarawak by providing better infrastructure, optimising economic potential, improving access to social services, enhancing inclusive development and strengthening cooperation between the Federal agencies and state governments.",""],[2,"274","3","Income-Generating Poverty Reduction Programmes and Projects","The incidence of poverty in both states will be reduced through programmes and projects that focus on income-generating activities.",""],[2,"274","3","Employment and High-Value Economic Activity Expansion for Indigenous Communities","The socioeconomic status of Anak Negeri Sabah and Bumiputera Sarawak will be improved by creating more employment opportunities and high value economic activities.",""],[2,"274","6","Poverty Alleviation and Income Diversification Measures","Efforts to address poverty, as well as increase and diversify sources of income will be intensified.",""],[2,"274","6","Bumiputera Socioeconomic Development Measures","measures to alleviate poverty and strengthen Bumiputera socioeconomic development will be escalated.",""],[2,"274","6","Employability, Entrepreneurship, and NCR Land Development Support","Efforts will also be undertaken to increase employability and promote entrepreneurship as well as facilitate the development of NCR land.",""],[2,"274","7","Poverty Alleviation Programme Enhancement","Poverty alleviation programmes will be enhanced to uplift the wellbeing of poor households.",""],[2,"274","7","Education, Skills Training, and Healthcare Access Expansion","Efforts will be intensified to improve quality education and skills training as well as access to healthcare services.",""],[2,"274","7","Basic Infrastructure and Services Expansion for Poor Households","the provision of basic infrastructure and services including roads, treated water, electricity and broadband connectivity will be enhanced.",""],[2,"274","8","Income Diversification for Poor Households","Sources of income of the poor households will be increased and diversified through participation in high value-added economic activities as well as human capital and entrepreneurship development.",""],[2,"274","8","High-Value Indigenous Product Commercialisation Initiative","The rich natural resources and culture will be leveraged to commercialise high value-added indigenous products, including arts and crafts as well as venturing into agriculture, aquaculture and ecotourism industries.",""],[2,"274","9","Entrepreneurship Ecosystem Strengthening for Community Development","The entrepreneurship ecosystem such as financing assistance and marketing through digital platforms will be strengthened to facilitate entrepreneurs in accelerating the socioeconomic development of these communities.",""],[2,"274","9","Multi-Stakeholder Service Delivery Coordination","In improving service delivery to the target groups, cooperation between the Federal and state governments, the private sector, community-based organisations and communities will be strengthened.",""],[2,"274","9","Bottom-Up Community Poverty Alleviation Delivery Mechanism","Delivery mechanisms will be enhanced through a bottom-up approach and involvement of social enterprises in alleviating pockets of poverty at the community level.",""],[2,"275","1","Socioeconomic Empowerment of Anak Negeri Sabah and Bumiputera Sarawak","The socioeconomic development of Anak Negeri Sabah and Bumiputera Sarawak will continue to be given priority to uplift their wellbeing.",""],[2,"275","1","Capacity and Employability Enhancement for Indigenous Communities","In this regard, the capacity and capability of these communities will be enhanced to improve employability and entrepreneurship.",""],[2,"275","2","Education and Training Support for Anak Negeri Sabah and Bumiputera Sarawak","Education and training will be pursued to enhance the capacity and capability of these communities, starting from early childhood care and education until tertiary level.",""],[2,"275","2","Economic Diversification Support for Indigenous Communities","These communities will also be encouraged to venture into ecotourism, agriculture and aquaculture as well as indigenous arts and crafts activities.",""],[2,"275","2","Entrepreneurship Support Package for Indigenous Communities","Entrepreneurship will be inculcated among these communities by providing necessary support such as financing facilities, logistic services and access to market, including through digital platform.",""]],"66":[[1,"226","2","Regional and Rural Development Gap Reduction Initiative","In the Twelfth Plan, efforts will be intensified to accelerate the development of states and regions and further narrow the development gap between rural and urban areas for greater inclusion.",""],[1,"226","2","Regional Economic Potential Optimisation Initiative","These will include optimising regional economic potential, developing sustainable cities1 and transforming rural areas to bridge the development gap.",""],[1,"226","2","Sustainable Cities Development Initiative","These will include optimising regional economic potential, developing sustainable cities1 and transforming rural areas to bridge the development gap.",""],[1,"226","2","Rural Transformation Programme","These will include optimising regional economic potential, developing sustainable cities1 and transforming rural areas to bridge the development gap.",""],[1,"231","4","Rural Development and Urban-Rural Linkage Improvement","Efforts to accelerate rural development especially in pockets of hinterland continue to be implemented.",""],[1,"234","2","Balanced and Inclusive Regional Development Programme","The Twelfth Plan will continue to focus on accelerating balanced and inclusive regional development.",""],[1,"238","1","Regional Growth Node and Hotspot Development Initiatives","Initiatives will focus on accelerating development based on key growth nodes and hotspot areas, attracting quality investment, improving the business ecosystem, enhancing strategic collaboration and coordination as well as enhancing cooperation under IMT-GT and BIMP-EAGA.",""],[2,"32","4","Regional and State Development Acceleration","Efforts will be intensified to accelerate the development of regions and states as well as narrow the development gap between rural and urban areas for greater inclusion",""],[2,"32","4","Sabah and Sarawak Development Acceleration","The development in Sabah and Sarawak will be further accelerated for better growth and wellbeing of the rakyat",""],[2,"32","5","Less Developed States Growth and Connectivity Enhancement","The potential of less developed states will be optimised.",""],[2,"36","4","Priority Development Funding for Less Developed States","Priority will be given to Kedah, Kelantan, Perlis, Sabah, Sarawak and Terengganu by allocating at least 50% of the Total Basic Development Expenditure2 (Basic DE).",""],[2,"36","4","Growth Node and Hotspot Area Development","The development of these states will be driven by key growth nodes and hotspot areas as hubs for economic activities.",""],[2,"36","4","Rural Industrialisation and Economic Diversification Programme","Rural areas will be further developed by intensifying industrialisation and diversifying economic activities through smart and cluster farming.",""],[2,"36","4","Cross-Border Economic Development Promotion","In addition, cross-border economic activities will be promoted to accelerate border development.",""],[2,"36","4","Infrastructure and Connectivity Improvement Projects","A number of projects for infrastructure and connectivity improvement will be implemented.",""],[2,"42","2","Regional Balance and Green Growth Strategy","Achieving greater regional balance will remain a priority to reduce disparity among states and green growth will be further emphasised in line with the 2030 Agenda.",""],[2,"68","4","Balanced Regional Development Planning and Coordination","Priority will continue to be given to bridging the development gap among states to ensure balanced regional development.",""],[2,"68","4","Federal-State-Local Regional Development Collaboration","Collaboration between the Federal, state and local governments, including regional development authorities, will be further strengthened for better regional development planning, implementation and coordination.",""],[2,"68","4","Rural Infrastructure Upgrade and Rural Economic Revitalisation","Initiatives will be undertaken to upgrade infrastructure and re-energise economic activities in rural areas as well as improve the rural-urban linkages.",""],[2,"107","1","Equitable Industrial Development and Regional Distribution Initiative","In the Twelfth Plan, efforts will be undertaken to promote equitable development and improve industrial distribution in narrowing development gaps across regions and states as well as between urban and rural areas.",""],[2,"107","2","Industrial Estate Development and Supporting Infrastructure","The development of industrial estates, particularly in less developed states will be complemented by a number of facilities and supporting infrastructure.",""],[2,"107","2","Industrialisation Roadmap Formulation for Sabah and Sarawak","industrialisation roadmaps will also be formulated including for Sabah and Sarawak to ensure the development of industrial estates is based on local strengths and capabilities.",""],[2,"107","2","Investment Incentive Mechanism Improvement for Less Developed Regions","the existing investment incentive mechanism will be improved to ensure less developed regions or states are given priority in getting special incentives.",""],[2,"107","3","Regional Industrial Estate Development Mapping","In this regard, a mapping of potential industries based on local strengths and advantages will be undertaken.",""],[2,"226","2","Regional Development Acceleration and Urban-Rural Gap Reduction","In the Twelfth Plan, efforts will be intensified to accelerate the development of states and regions and further narrow the development gap between rural and urban areas for greater inclusion.",""],[2,"226","2","Regional Economic Potential Optimization","These will include optimising regional economic potential, developing sustainable cities1 and transforming rural areas to bridge the development gap.",""],[2,"226","2","Sustainable Cities Development Initiative","These will include optimising regional economic potential, developing sustainable cities1 and transforming rural areas to bridge the development gap.",""],[2,"226","2","Rural Transformation Programme","These will include optimising regional economic potential, developing sustainable cities1 and transforming rural areas to bridge the development gap.",""],[2,"226","2","Development Support for Less Developed States","Greater emphasis will be placed on the development of the less developed states.",""],[2,"231","4","Rural Development Acceleration Measures","Efforts to accelerate rural development especially in pockets of hinterland continue to be implemented.",""],[2,"234","2","Balanced and Inclusive Regional Development Measures","The Twelfth Plan will continue to focus on accelerating balanced and inclusive regional development.",""],[2,"238","1","Regional Growth Node and Hotspot Development Initiative","Initiatives will focus on accelerating development based on key growth nodes and hotspot areas, attracting quality investment, improving the business ecosystem, enhancing strategic collaboration and coordination as well as enhancing cooperation under IMT-GT and BIMP-EAGA.",""],[2,"238","7","Key Growth Nodes and Hotspot Area Development","Regional development will be driven by the development of key growth nodes and hotspot areas.",""],[2,"238","7","Promotion of Niche Economic Activities","several niche economic activities will be promoted in these areas.",""],[2,"238","7","High Value-Added Activities and Green Growth Initiative Acceleration","Efforts will be focused on accelerating the implementation of high value-added activities and green growth initiatives, which will contribute to economic growth and ensure inclusive regional development.",""],[2,"238","8","Regional Key Growth Nodes Development","Key growth nodes will be developed in each region as hubs for economic activities, allowing for economies of scale, agglomeration of economic activities, optimisation of resources and the creation of a conducive ecosystem.",""],[2,"238","8","Hotspot Area Development Initiative","Hotspot areas, which refer to the areas surrounding key growth nodes that have the potential to be developed on a smaller scale, will be established to complement the key growth nodes.",""],[2,"238","8","Synergistic Regional Economic Development","Synergistic development in the key growth nodes and hotspot areas will attract strategic and quality investment as well as create more employment and entrepreneurship opportunities.",""],[2,"238","9","State-Driven Regional and State Development Programmes","strategic development programmes at the regional and state levels will be implemented through state-driven initiatives and private sector-led projects.",""],[2,"238","9","Private-Sector-Led New Township Development","The development of new townships led by the private sector, including in the Setia Fontaines, Pulau Pinang as well as Seriemas in Ampangan and Rantau, Negeri Sembilan, are expected to provide additional job and business opportunities.",""],[2,"238","10","Integrated Mixed Development Projects","Integrated and comprehensive mixed development projects, including the catalytic development of Malaysia Vision Valley 2.0 (MVV 2.0) in Negeri Sembilan and the proposed Pagoh Special Economic Zone in Johor will provide new opportunities for growth.",""],[2,"239","1","Techpark@Enstek Phase Three Development","The development of phase three of the Techpark@Enstek in Negeri Sembilan will expand the development of halal-related activities, particularly in food and beverages, pharmaceuticals and cosmetics industries.",""],[2,"239","1","Pagoh Special Economic Zone Development","the proposed Pagoh Special Economic Zone will attract both local and foreign investment, offering huge potential for the area's future development.",""],[2,"239","2","Sarawak Corridor of Renewable Energy Boundary Expansion","The extended and new demarcation of the Sarawak Corridor of Renewable Energy area, which covers the Upper Rajang, Northern and Highland areas will ensure a more comprehensive development to accelerate economic growth in the rural and interior areas of Sarawak.",""],[2,"239","2","Regional Corridor Boundary Extension Initiative","Similarly, the proposed extension of other regional corridor boundaries to include a number of additional districts and mukim will promote development and more economic activities in these areas.",""]],"67":[[1,"32","4","Regional and Rural-Urban Development Gap Reduction","Efforts will be intensified to accelerate the development of regions and states as well as narrow the development gap between rural and urban areas for greater inclusion.",""],[1,"32","4","Sabah and Sarawak Development Acceleration","The development in Sabah and Sarawak will be further accelerated for better growth and wellbeing of the rakyat.",""],[1,"32","5","Less Developed States Growth and Connectivity Enhancement","The potential of less developed states will be optimised.",""],[1,"36","4","Priority Development Funding for Less Developed States","Priority will be given to Kedah, Kelantan, Perlis, Sabah, Sarawak and Terengganu by allocating at least 50% of the Total Basic Development Expenditure2 (Basic DE).",""],[1,"36","4","Growth Node and Hotspot Area Development","The development of these states will be driven by key growth nodes and hotspot areas as hubs for economic activities.",""],[1,"36","4","Rural Industrialisation and Smart Cluster Farming Programme","Rural areas will be further developed by intensifying industrialisation and diversifying economic activities through smart and cluster farming.",""],[1,"36","4","Cross-Border Economic Development Promotion","In addition, cross-border economic activities will be promoted to accelerate border development.",""],[1,"36","4","Infrastructure and Connectivity Improvement Projects","A number of projects for infrastructure and connectivity improvement will be implemented.",""],[1,"68","4","Balanced Regional Development and State Gap Bridging Initiative","Priority will continue to be given to bridging the development gap among states to ensure balanced regional development.",""],[1,"68","4","Federal-State-Local Regional Development Coordination Strengthening","Collaboration between the Federal, state and local governments, including regional development authorities, will be further strengthened for better regional development planning, implementation and coordination.",""],[1,"68","4","Rural Infrastructure Upgrading and Economic Revitalisation Initiative","Initiatives will be undertaken to upgrade infrastructure and re-energise economic activities in rural areas as well as improve the rural-urban linkages.",""],[1,"146","1","Regional Development Gap Reduction Initiative","Efforts will also be intensified to accelerate the development of less developed states and regions, and further narrow the development gap between rural and urban areas.",""],[1,"146","1","Border Area Growth Triangle Cooperation Initiative","The subregional cooperation under the Indonesia-Malaysia-Thailand Growth Triangle (IMT-GT) and Brunei Darussalam-Indonesia-Malaysia-Philippines East ASEAN Growth Area (BIMP-EAGA) will be leveraged to catalyse growth in border areas.",""],[1,"146","2","Regional Inclusion and Socioeconomic Development in Sabah and Sarawak","Socioeconomic development in Sabah and Sarawak will be intensified to promote regional inclusion.",""],[1,"146","2","Federal-State Coordination Mechanism for Programme Implementation","Cooperation between Federal agencies and state governments will be strengthened to effectively implement programmes and projects.",""],[1,"146","2","Infrastructure, Connectivity, and Social Services Upgrading","The provision of infrastructure and connectivity will be enhanced, while economic potential optimised by creating a conducive ecosystem for economic growth.",""],[1,"151","6","Regional Development Expenditure Allocation","Allocating at least 50% of Total Basic Development Expenditure1 for the six less developed states, especially Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[1,"151","9","Investment Incentive Packages for Target States","Providing attractive incentive packages to entice investments to these states.",""],[1,"151","12","Rural Industrial Park Development and Revitalization","Intensifying rural industrialisation by developing new industrial parks and reinvigorating existing ones.",""],[1,"447","8","Development Expenditure Allocation to Less-Developed States","At least 50% of the development expenditure will be allocated to six less- developed states, namely Sabah, Sarawak, Kelantan, Terengganu, Kedah and Perlis, to ensure a more balanced regional growth and reduce development gaps.",""],[1,"447","8","Connectivity and Basic Infrastructure Improvement","Most of the allocations will be channelled to improve connectivity and provide better access to basic infrastructure, amenities and services.",""],[1,"453","5","Regional Inclusion Funding Prioritisation","In allocating Federal Government funds, special attention will be given to Sabah, Sarawak and other less developed states to promote regional inclusion.",""],[1,"453","5","Infrastructure and Connectivity Upgrading","The provision of better infrastructure and connectivity, as well as improved access to social services and enhancement of defence, security and public safety will contribute towards uplifting the socioeconomic status of the rakyat.",""],[1,"453","5","Social Services Access Expansion","The provision of better infrastructure and connectivity, as well as improved access to social services and enhancement of defence, security and public safety will contribute towards uplifting the socioeconomic status of the rakyat.",""]],"68":[[1,"239","2","Sarawak Corridor of Renewable Energy Area Expansion","The extended and new demarcation of the Sarawak Corridor of Renewable Energy area, which covers the Upper Rajang, Northern and Highland areas will ensure a more comprehensive development to accelerate economic growth in the rural and interior areas of Sarawak.",""],[1,"239","2","Regional Corridor Boundary Extension Initiative","Similarly, the proposed extension of other regional corridor boundaries to include a number of additional districts and mukim will promote development and more economic activities in these areas.",""]],"69":[[1,"245","4","Rural Infrastructure and Basic Amenities Upgrading","Rural areas will be further developed to narrow the development gap between rural and urban areas by upgrading infrastructure and basic amenities, providing better connectivity and expanding socioeconomic activities.",""],[1,"245","4","Rural Economic Diversification and Governance Improvement","The rural areas will be further transformed by accelerating the provision of infrastructure and services, diversifying and boosting economic activities as well as improving governance.",""],[1,"245","7","Rural Infrastructure and Basic Services Expansion","These measures include increasing the provision of rural infrastructure, improving basic services and enhancing connectivity and mobility.",""],[1,"246","1","Rural Basic Services Improvement","The coverage and accessibility to basic services will be continuously improved.",""],[1,"246","1","Rural Waste Management and Sanitation Enhancement","Waste management and sanitation services in rural areas will be enhanced to ensure a sustainable environment.",""],[1,"246","1","Komuniti Sihat Pembina Negara Programme Expansion","The Komuniti Sihat Pembina Negara programme will be expanded to increase health awareness among rural communities.",""],[1,"246","1","Older Persons Rural Care Support","Rural development planning will also address the needs of older persons, including the provision of healthcare and home caregiver services.",""],[1,"246","1","Program Bantuan Rumah Continuation","The Program Bantuan Rumah will be continued to provide quality and affordable housing in rural areas.",""]],"70":[[1,"246","3","Rural Economic Diversification and Cottage Industry Revitalization","Initiatives to diversify and boost the rural economy will focus on optimising land use and re-energising the rural cottage industry.",""],[1,"246","3","Rural Income-Generating Activities Expansion","Income-generating activities will also be intensified to reduce the rural-urban income disparity.",""],[1,"246","7","Rural Cottage Industry Revitalisation Initiatives","Efforts will be intensified to re-energise the rural cottage industry through various initiatives in supporting MSMEs.",""],[1,"246","7","Rural Natural Resource-Based Enterprise Development","Natural endowments and resources will be leveraged to create business and employment opportunities as well as generate additional income for the rural population.",""],[1,"246","7","Multi-Stakeholder Coordination for Rural Cottage Industries","Greater collaboration will be fostered among relevant ministries, regional development agencies and state governments to promote rural cottage industries.","relevant ministries | regional development agencies | state governments"],[1,"246","7","Private Sector and Social Enterprise Participation in Rural Economy","The private sector and social enterprises will be encouraged to participate in rural economic activities.",""],[1,"269","9","Rural Development Acceleration in Sabah and Sarawak","The development of rural areas in Sabah and Sarawak will be accelerated to close the gap between rural and urban areas.",""],[1,"269","9","Rural Growth Enablers and Economic Revitalisation Measures","Measures include strengthening growth enablers, re-energising rural economic activities and providing access to online businesses.",""],[2,"246","3","Rural Economic Diversification and Cottage Industry Revitalization","Initiatives to diversify and boost the rural economy will focus on optimising land use and re-energising the rural cottage industry.",""],[2,"246","3","Rural Income-Generating Activities Expansion","Income-generating activities will also be intensified to reduce the rural-urban income disparity.",""],[2,"246","7","Rural Cottage Industry Revitalization Initiative","Efforts will be intensified to re-energise the rural cottage industry through various initiatives in supporting MSMEs.",""],[2,"246","7","Rural Natural Endowment-Based Enterprise Development","Natural endowments and resources will be leveraged to create business and employment opportunities as well as generate additional income for the rural population.",""],[2,"246","7","Multi-Stakeholder Coordination for Rural Cottage Industries","Greater collaboration will be fostered among relevant ministries, regional development agencies and state governments to promote rural cottage industries.","relevant ministries | regional development agencies | state governments"],[2,"246","7","Private Sector and Social Enterprise Participation in Rural Economy","The private sector and social enterprises will be encouraged to participate in rural economic activities.",""]],"71":[[1,"32","7","Integrated Water Resources Management Acceleration","accelerating adoption of the Integrated Water Resources Management (IWRM)",""],[1,"37","2","Integrated Water Resources Management Adoption","The Twelfth Plan will lay the foundation for a comprehensive water transformation agenda by accelerating the adoption of IWRM.",""],[1,"37","2","Whole-of-Nation Water Stewardship Approach","The whole-of-nation approach involving all stakeholders will be adopted to instil a sense of ownership and responsibility in protecting and conserving this precious resource.",""],[1,"37","2","Water Governance and Legal Reform","Governance of water resources will be strengthened to manage water resources effectively through revising existing laws and establishing an integrated centre for water data and R&D&C&I.",""],[1,"37","2","Financial Sustainability Improvement for Water Service Providers","Financial sustainability of water service providers will be improved to enhance efficient service delivery.",""],[1,"281","2","Integrated Water Resources Management Adoption","accelerating the adoption of Integrated Water Resources Management (IWRM) will be the key priority.",""],[1,"284","9","Water Sector Transformation 2040 Agenda","Introducing the Water Sector Transformation 2040 (WST 2040) agenda.",""],[1,"284","10","Single Water Management Agency","Establishing single water management agency.",""],[1,"284","11","Governance and Enforcement Legal Reform","Revising existing laws and formulating new ones to strengthen governance and enforcement.",""],[1,"284","12","Innovative Financing Mechanisms with Private Sector Participation","Promoting innovative financing mechanisms with more involvement of the private sector.",""],[1,"284","13","Integrated Water Data and R&D Centre","Establishing an integrated centre for water data and R&D&C&I to enhance data-driven decision-making.",""],[1,"284","14","Tariff Setting Mechanism","Introducing Tariff Setting Mechanism to ensure financial sustainability.",""],[1,"296","8","Integrated River Basin Management Plan Implementation","Implementation of the Integrated River Basin Management (IRBM) Plans",""],[1,"311","4","Water Catchment and Riparian Habitat Protection","The gazetting and protection of water catchment areas will be intensified, while riparian forests and wetland habitats will be conserved and protected to ensure sustainability of water resources as well as reduce disaster risks.",""],[1,"311","4","Integrated River Basin Management Acceleration","Furthermore, the adoption of the IRBM approach will be accelerated in line with the Integrated Water Resources Management (IWRM) to maximise socioeconomic benefits, while conserving the freshwater ecosystem.",""],[1,"311","4","Water Resources Legislation Harmonisation","In this regard, states will be encouraged to review and harmonise their respective water- related legislation based on the Water Resources Bill 2016 to ensure coherence and comprehensiveness of water resources management.",""],[1,"311","4","Federal Water Agency Governance Improvement","Governance of water-related agencies at the Federal level will be improved to strengthen the implementation of IWRM.",""],[1,"318","2","Integrated Water Resource Management Adoption","Accelerating the adoption of the Integrated Water Resource Management (IWRM) will be the foundation in transforming the water sector",""],[1,"326","2","Water Sector Management Transformation","Management of the water sector will be improved by encompassing multidimensional approaches.",""],[1,"332","2","Water Sector Transformation Agenda","The water sector transformation agenda will be introduced in the Twelfth Plan through the adoption of the whole-of-nation approach to increase efficiency in water management, realise the potential of the water sector to generate wealth and create new job opportunities as described in Box 9-1.",""],[1,"332","2","Integrated Water Resources Management Acceleration Phase","The first phase of the water sector transformation will focus on accelerating the adoption of IWRM, while laying the foundation for the execution of the remaining phases.",""],[1,"332","2","Water Sector Governance, Data, Financing, and Infrastructure Strategy Package","In this regard, five strategies will be employed which include empowering people as drivers of water sector transformation, strengthening governance, enhancing data- driven decision-making, ensuring sustainable financing as well as developing sustainable and cost-effective infrastructure.",""],[1,"333","1","Water Sector Transformation 2040","The Water Sector Transformation 2040 (WST 2040) will be developed to set the strategic direction towards positioning the sector as a dynamic growth engine, while ensuring water security for all.",""],[1,"333","7","IWRM Adoption Acceleration Roadmap","A roadmap will be developed to outline strategies, initiatives and programmes for each phase to ensure the success of the transformation.",""],[1,"333","8","WST 2040 Task Force","A dedicated task force comprising members from the public and private sectors will be established under the National Water Council.",""],[1,"334","2","State and District Public Consultation Platforms for Water Management","Public consultation platforms will be established at the state and district levels for active engagement as part of the water management system.",""],[1,"334","2","National Water Council Decision Support Mechanism","These platforms will be leveraged to support the National Water Council decisions.",""],[1,"334","2","Capacity Building for Water Platform Members","Capabilities and skills of members will be enhanced, particularly in conflict resolution and negotiation to ensure the effectiveness of the platforms.",""],[1,"334","2","Strategic Communication Plan for Water Sector Transformation","A strategic communication plan will also be developed for the effective implementation of the water sector transformation.",""],[1,"334","3","Integrated Water Resources Management Awareness and Capacity-Building Programmes","Efforts to enhance understanding of the IWRM will be intensified through the implementation of comprehensive AACB programmes.",""],[1,"334","6","Water Sector Governance Strengthening","Governance of the water sector at the Federal, state and district levels will be strengthened to ensure more integrated and effective water management.",""],[1,"334","6","Water Legislation Harmonisation and Pollution Control Enhancement","water-related legislations will be harmonised, pollution control measures enhanced and the water- energy-food nexus institutionalised.",""],[1,"334","6","Water-Energy-Food Nexus Institutionalisation","water- energy-food nexus institutionalised.",""],[1,"334","7","State Water Legislation Review and Harmonization","States will be encouraged to review the respective water- related legislation in line with the Water Resources Bill 2016.",""],[1,"334","7","State Water Resources Management Authorities","The revision will also provide a legal basis for the establishment of a water resources management authority in all states.",""],[1,"334","7","Federal Single Water Management Agency","To strengthen the implementation of IWRM and to integrate existing water-related agencies, single water management agency at the Federal level will be established.",""],[1,"334","7","Water Resources Accounting and Auditing Improvement","The accounting and auditing methods for water resources management will also be improved.",""],[1,"334","7","Expanded Regional Planning Committee for Water Resource Management","In addition, the scope of the Regional Planning Committee, established to look into the commonalities of inter-state or inter-sectoral policies, planning, implementation and monitoring of development activities, will be expanded to incorporate water resource management.",""],[1,"335","2","Water-Energy-Food Nexus Institutionalisation","Going forward, the water-energy-food nexus approach will be institutionalised, while technical expertise of relevant ministries and agencies will be enhanced to ensure effective implementation.",""],[1,"339","1","Integrated Water Resources Management Acceleration","The water sector will be strengthened through the adoption of the whole-of-nation approach by accelerating the implementation of IWRM which lays the foundation in achieving water sector transformation by 2040.",""],[1,"454","1","Water Sector Transformation 2040 Agenda","the Water Sector Transformation 2040 agenda will be introduced in the Twelfth Plan to transform this sector from being an economic enabler to a dynamic growth engine",""],[1,"454","1","Integrated Water Resources Management Adoption","Accelerating the adoption of the Integrated Water Resources Management (IWRM) will be the starting point in transforming this sector",""],[1,"454","1","Rakyat-Led Water Sector Transformation","The rakyat will be empowered to actively drive the water sector transformation",""],[2,"32","6","Integrated Energy and Water Management","Energy and water will be managed holistically and sustainably, taking into account the supply and demand of these resources.",""],[2,"32","6","Water Security for All Initiative","the water sector will focus on ensuring water security for all.",""],[2,"32","7","Integrated Water Resources Management Adoption","Two game changers will be implemented under Theme 3, namely embracing the circular economy and accelerating adoption of the Integrated Water Resources Management (IWRM).",""],[2,"37","2","Integrated Water Resources Management Acceleration","The Twelfth Plan will lay the foundation for a comprehensive water transformation agenda by accelerating the adoption of IWRM.",""],[2,"37","2","Whole-of-Nation Water Stewardship Approach","The whole-of-nation approach involving all stakeholders will be adopted to instil a sense of ownership and responsibility in protecting and conserving this precious resource.",""],[2,"37","2","Water Governance and Legal Reform","Governance of water resources will be strengthened to manage water resources effectively through revising existing laws and establishing an integrated centre for water data and R&D&C&I.",""],[2,"37","2","Water Service Provider Financial Sustainability Improvement","Financial sustainability of water service providers will be improved to enhance efficient service delivery.",""],[2,"281","2","Integrated Water Resources Management Adoption","In the water sector, accelerating the adoption of Integrated Water Resources Management (IWRM) will be the key priority.",""],[2,"284","9","Water Sector Transformation 2040 Agenda","Introducing the Water Sector Transformation 2040 (WST 2040) agenda.",""],[2,"284","10","Single Water Management Agency","Establishing single water management agency.",""],[2,"284","11","Governance and Enforcement Legal Reform","Revising existing laws and formulating new ones to strengthen governance and enforcement.",""],[2,"284","12","Innovative Financing Mechanisms with Private Sector Participation","Promoting innovative financing mechanisms with more involvement of the private sector.",""],[2,"284","13","Integrated Water Data and R&D&C&I Centre","Establishing an integrated centre for water data and R&D&C&I to enhance data-driven decision-making.",""],[2,"284","14","Tariff Setting Mechanism","Introducing Tariff Setting Mechanism to ensure financial sustainability.",""],[2,"332","2","Water Sector Transformation Agenda","The water sector transformation agenda will be introduced in the Twelfth Plan through the adoption of the whole-of-nation approach to increase efficiency in water management, realise the potential of the water sector to generate wealth and create new job opportunities as described in Box 9-1.",""],[2,"332","2","Integrated Water Resources Management Acceleration","The first phase of the water sector transformation will focus on accelerating the adoption of IWRM, while laying the foundation for the execution of the remaining phases.",""],[2,"332","2","Water Sector Governance, Data, Financing, and Infrastructure Strategy Package","In this regard, five strategies will be employed which include empowering people as drivers of water sector transformation, strengthening governance, enhancing data- driven decision-making, ensuring sustainable financing as well as developing sustainable and cost-effective infrastructure.",""],[2,"333","1","Water Sector Transformation 2040","The Water Sector Transformation 2040 (WST 2040) will be developed to set the strategic direction towards positioning the sector as a dynamic growth engine, while ensuring water security for all.",""],[2,"333","7","Integrated Water Resources Management Roadmap","A roadmap will be developed to outline strategies, initiatives and programmes for each phase to ensure the success of the transformation.",""],[2,"333","8","WST 2040 Task Force Establishment","A dedicated task force comprising members from the public and private sectors will be established under the National Water Council.",""],[2,"333","8","WST 2040 Coordination, Monitoring, and Review Mechanism","The task force will guide, coordinate, monitor and report progress as well as review, realign and provide recommendations for the successful implementation of the WST 2040 agenda.",""],[2,"334","6","Integrated Water Sector Governance Reform","Governance of the water sector at the Federal, state and district levels will be strengthened to ensure more integrated and effective water management.",""],[2,"334","6","Water Legislation Harmonisation and Pollution Control Enhancement","water-related legislations will be harmonised, pollution control measures enhanced and the water- energy-food nexus institutionalised.",""],[2,"334","6","Integrated Water Resources Management Mainstreaming","physical development will be streamlined with IWRM.",""],[2,"334","7","State Water Legislation Review and Harmonization","States will be encouraged to review the respective water- related legislation in line with the Water Resources Bill 2016.",""],[2,"334","7","State Water Resources Management Authority Establishment","The revision will also provide a legal basis for the establishment of a water resources management authority in all states.",""],[2,"334","7","Federal Single Water Management Agency","To strengthen the implementation of IWRM and to integrate existing water-related agencies, single water management agency at the Federal level will be established.",""],[2,"334","7","Water Resources Accounting and Auditing Improvement","The accounting and auditing methods for water resources management will also be improved.",""],[2,"334","7","Expanded Regional Planning Committee Mandate for Water Resource Management","In addition, the scope of the Regional Planning Committee, established to look into the commonalities of inter-state or inter-sectoral policies, planning, implementation and monitoring of development activities, will be expanded to incorporate water resource management.",""],[2,"335","2","Water-Energy-Food Nexus Institutionalization","Going forward, the water-energy-food nexus approach will be institutionalised, while technical expertise of relevant ministries and agencies will be enhanced to ensure effective implementation.","relevant ministries and agencies"],[2,"339","1","Integrated Water Resources Management Acceleration","The water sector will be strengthened through the adoption of the whole-of-nation approach by accelerating the implementation of IWRM which lays the foundation in achieving water sector transformation by 2040.",""],[2,"454","1","Water Sector Transformation 2040 Agenda","For the water sector, the Water Sector Transformation 2040 agenda will be introduced in the Twelfth Plan to transform this sector from being an economic enabler to a dynamic growth engine.",""],[2,"454","1","Integrated Water Resources Management Acceleration","Accelerating the adoption of the Integrated Water Resources Management (IWRM) will be the starting point in transforming this sector.",""],[2,"454","1","Public Empowerment for Water Sector Transformation","The rakyat will be empowered to actively drive the water sector transformation.",""]],"72":[[1,"311","6","Integrated Wastewater Treatment Plant Construction","Integrated wastewater treatment plants will be constructed to improve the management and control of effluent discharge, especially in newly developed industrial areas.",""],[1,"311","6","Review of Environmental Laws for Emerging Pollutants","Existing laws, including Act 127, will be reviewed to incorporate provisions on emerging pollutants, mainly chemicals found in pharmaceuticals, pesticides, industrial and household products.",""],[1,"311","6","Expanded TMDL Studies for River Basin Planning","TMDL studies, which determine the loading capacity of river segments, will be expanded to cover more river basins in guiding state governments and local authorities to evaluate existing and new development proposals along river corridors.",""],[1,"311","6","Smart River Monitoring and Early Warning System","A smart monitoring system will also be put in place to enable real- time monitoring and early warning as well as in strengthening enforcement.",""],[1,"311","6","River Trail Construction for Encroachment Prevention","River trails will be built as a nature-based solution to prevent encroachment and pollution of rivers.",""],[1,"334","8","Water Pollution Control and Pollution Penalty Reform","Existing legislation will be strengthened to intensify measures in reducing water pollution.",""],[1,"334","8","Total Maximum Daily Load Studies","In addition, 10 Total Maximum Daily Load (TMDL) studies will be carried out to determine the loading capacity of river segments.",""],[1,"335","1","River Corridor Development Evaluation and River Protection Measures","and local authorities in evaluating existing development and new development proposals along river corridors.",""],[1,"335","1","Strengthening Enforcement Capacity for River Protection","The enforcement capacity of relevant Federal and state agencies will be fortified through various measures, including the use of smart technologies.","relevant Federal and state agencies"],[1,"335","1","Inter-Agency Coordination for Enforcement","Coordination between enforcement agencies will be enhanced.","enforcement agencies"],[1,"335","1","Sewage Connection and Septic Tank Desludging Programme","To contain pollution from sewage, efforts will be intensified to connect premises to existing regional sewage treatment plants and undertake periodic desludging of individual septic tanks.",""],[1,"335","1","Mandatory Compliance with Effluent Discharge Standards","Sewerage services operators will also be mandated to comply with existing effluent discharge standards.","Sewerage services operators"],[2,"311","6","Integrated Wastewater Treatment Plant Construction","Integrated wastewater treatment plants will be constructed to improve the management and control of effluent discharge, especially in newly developed industrial areas.",""],[2,"311","6","Review of Environmental Laws for Emerging Pollutants","Existing laws, including Act 127, will be reviewed to incorporate provisions on emerging pollutants, mainly chemicals found in pharmaceuticals, pesticides, industrial and household products.",""],[2,"311","6","Expanded TMDL Studies for River Basin Planning","TMDL studies, which determine the loading capacity of river segments, will be expanded to cover more river basins in guiding state governments and local authorities to evaluate existing and new development proposals along river corridors.",""],[2,"311","6","Smart River Monitoring and Early Warning System","A smart monitoring system will also be put in place to enable real- time monitoring and early warning as well as in strengthening enforcement.",""],[2,"311","6","River Trail Construction for Encroachment Prevention","River trails will be built as a nature-based solution to prevent encroachment and pollution of rivers.",""],[2,"322","4","Resource Recovery Facilities for Sewage Treatment Plants","The requirement for resource recovery facilities was also incorporated into the development of regional and centralised sewage treatment plants.",""],[2,"322","4","Waste-to-Wealth Initiative for Closed-Loop Water Cycle Management","This is to encourage the implementation of waste-to-wealth initiative that complements the closed-loop water cycle management.",""],[2,"334","8","Water Pollution Control and Regulatory Strengthening","Existing legislation will be strengthened to intensify measures in reducing water pollution.",""],[2,"334","8","Total Maximum Daily Load Studies","In addition, 10 Total Maximum Daily Load (TMDL) studies will be carried out to determine the loading capacity of river segments.",""],[2,"335","1","River Corridor Development Review and River Protection Measures","and local authorities in evaluating existing development and new development proposals along river corridors. It will also facilitate authorities in undertaking actions to protect rivers.",""],[2,"335","1","Strengthening Enforcement Capacity of Federal and State Agencies","The enforcement capacity of relevant Federal and state agencies will be fortified through various measures, including the use of smart technologies.",""],[2,"335","1","Inter-Agency Enforcement Coordination Enhancement","Coordination between enforcement agencies will be enhanced.",""],[2,"335","1","Sewage Connection and Septic Tank Desludging Programme","To contain pollution from sewage, efforts will be intensified to connect premises to existing regional sewage treatment plants and undertake periodic desludging of individual septic tanks.",""],[2,"335","1","Mandatory Compliance with Effluent Discharge Standards","Sewerage services operators will also be mandated to comply with existing effluent discharge standards.",""],[2,"337","4","Constructed Wetlands for Wastewater Treatment","In CWs, specific vegetation will be planted for different treatment purposes, such as for the removal of pollutants, purification of water, control of erosion, filtration of sediments and reduction of water flow.",""]],"73":[[1,"328","10","Integrated Centre for Water Data and R&D&C&I","Establishment of an Integrated Centre for Water Data and R&D&C&I",""],[1,"334","5","Periodic Water Resources Status Reporting","Reports on the status of water resources will be published periodically.",""],[1,"335","3","Data-Driven Water Sector Decision-Making Enhancement","Data-driven decision-making capabilities will be enhanced to support strategic planning and management of the water sector.",""],[1,"335","3","Water Research Institute Strengthening","The water research institute will be strengthened to serve as a one-stop centre for water-related data and R&D&C&I.",""],[1,"335","3","Water Technology Capacity Development","Furthermore, the capacity of water industry players and the scientific community will be heightened to support the development of indigenous water technology.",""],[1,"335","4","Strengthening of the Water Research Institute","The water research institute will be strengthened as a centre to undertake comprehensive water-related analysis and provide accessibility to appropriate data that meets the needs of stakeholders.",""],[1,"335","4","Water-Related Research, Development and Innovation Programme","The centre will also actively conduct water-related R&D&C&I activities as well as coordinate and provide strategic direction to other relevant organisations.",""],[1,"335","4","National Water Balance Management System Utilisation","The utilisation of the National Water Balance Management System (NAWABS) will be",""],[1,"335","5","Local Data-Driven Water Decision Support System","The long-term goal of these initiatives is to develop local data-driven decision-making support system (DMSS) based on comprehensive data as well as innovative water technologies",""],[1,"335","6","Water-Related Professional Capacity Building and Certification Programme","The capacity of professionals, skilled workers and the scientific community will be improved to enable data-driven decision-making in embracing the 4IR.",""],[1,"335","6","Competency Certification and Tertiary Education Development for Water Professionals","Competency certification and relevant tertiary education programmes will be continuously developed to increase the competency of water-related professionals in the public and private sectors.",""],[1,"335","6","Water-Related TVET Programme Introduction","Similarly, water-related TVET programmes will also be introduced to meet the future demand for skilled workers in the industry.",""],[1,"335","6","Home-Grown Water Technology Innovation Support","Local scientists will be encouraged to keep abreast with current research to develop home-grown and innovative water technologies that are on par with international standards.",""],[1,"335","6","Strategic Collaboration for Water Research","Strategic collaboration among scientists at regional and international levels will be intensified.",""],[2,"335","3","Data-Driven Water Sector Planning and Management","Data-driven decision-making capabilities will be enhanced to support strategic planning and management of the water sector.",""],[2,"335","3","Strengthening of the Water Research Institute","The water research institute will be strengthened to serve as a one-stop centre for water-related data and R&D&C&I.",""],[2,"335","3","Capacity Building for Indigenous Water Technology Development","Furthermore, the capacity of water industry players and the scientific community will be heightened to support the development of indigenous water technology.",""],[2,"335","4","Strengthening of the Water Research Institute","The water research institute will be strengthened as a centre to undertake comprehensive water-related analysis and provide accessibility to appropriate data that meets the needs of stakeholders.",""],[2,"335","4","Water-Related Research, Development, Commercialisation and Innovation Activities","The centre will also actively conduct water-related R&D&C&I activities as well as coordinate and provide strategic direction to other relevant organisations.",""],[2,"335","5","Local Data-Driven Water Decision Support System","The long-term goal of these initiatives is to develop local data-driven decision-making support system (DMSS) based on comprehensive data as well as innovative water technologies",""],[2,"335","6","Professional Capacity and Competency Development for Water Sector 4IR Transition","The capacity of professionals, skilled workers and the scientific community will be improved to enable data-driven decision-making in embracing the 4IR.",""],[2,"335","6","Water-Related Competency Certification and Tertiary Education Programme","Competency certification and relevant tertiary education programmes will be continuously developed to increase the competency of water-related professionals in the public and private sectors.",""],[2,"335","6","Water-Related TVET Programme Introduction","Similarly, water-related TVET programmes will also be introduced to meet the future demand for skilled workers in the industry.",""],[2,"335","6","Home-Grown Water Technology Innovation Support","Local scientists will be encouraged to keep abreast with current research to develop home-grown and innovative water technologies that are on par with international standards.",""],[2,"335","6","Regional and International Scientific Collaboration","Strategic collaboration among scientists at regional and international levels will be intensified.",""]],"74":[[1,"319","1","Water Service Provider Financial Sustainability Strengthening","In the water sector, the financial sustainability of service providers was strengthened.",""],[1,"335","7","Water Services Financial Sustainability Strengthening","the financial sustainability of water services providers will be strengthened and innovative financing mechanisms will be introduced",""],[1,"335","7","Strategic Investment in the Water Industry","This will also encourage strategic investments to strengthen the water industry",""],[1,"335","8","Tariff Setting Mechanism for Water Supply and Sewerage Services","The Tariff Setting Mechanism (TSM) for water supply and sewerage services will be implemented to achieve operating costs recovery and improve the financial capabilities of service providers.",""],[1,"335","8","Alternative Non-Tariff Revenue Development for Water Services Providers","Water services providers will also be urged to explore alternative non-tariff revenues, particularly from water recycling and wastewater treatment by-products.",""],[1,"336","1","Water Sector Cost Recovery and Benchmarking Reform","The economic potential of the water sector will be harnessed to achieve cost recovery and economies of scale.",""],[1,"336","1","Water Services Industry Strategy Benchmarking","The water services industry will adopt relevant strategies and be benchmarked against the energy sector, which is financially independent, market-driven and technologically efficient.",""],[1,"336","2","Innovative Water Sector Financing Mechanisms","Innovative financing mechanisms will be explored to reduce dependence on government funds for water sector development.",""],[1,"336","2","Licensed Sewerage Infrastructure Delivery Entity","The establishment of a licensed entity to build new sewerage infrastructure through alternative financing models will be considered.",""],[1,"336","2","Private Sector Investment in Water Sector Transformation Projects","The private sector will also be encouraged to invest in water sector transformation projects such as wastewater resource recovery, R&D&C&I and smart technology applications.",""],[2,"335","7","Water Services Financial Sustainability Strengthening","the financial sustainability of water services providers will be strengthened and innovative financing mechanisms will be introduced.",""],[2,"335","8","Tariff Setting Mechanism for Water Supply and Sewerage Services","The Tariff Setting Mechanism (TSM) for water supply and sewerage services will be implemented to achieve operating costs recovery and improve the financial capabilities of service providers.",""],[2,"335","8","Alternative Non-Tariff Revenue Development for Water Services Providers","Water services providers will also be urged to explore alternative non-tariff revenues, particularly from water recycling and wastewater treatment by-products.",""],[2,"336","1","Water Sector Cost Recovery and Benchmarking Reform","The economic potential of the water sector will be harnessed to achieve cost recovery and economies of scale.",""],[2,"336","1","Water Services Industry Strategy Benchmarking","The water services industry will adopt relevant strategies and be benchmarked against the energy sector, which is financially independent, market-driven and technologically efficient.",""],[2,"336","1","International Best Practice Review for Water Services","Best practices from other countries in the water services industry will also be considered.",""],[2,"336","2","Innovative Water Sector Financing Mechanisms","Innovative financing mechanisms will be explored to reduce dependence on government funds for water sector development.",""],[2,"336","2","Licensed Sewerage Infrastructure Delivery Entity","The establishment of a licensed entity to build new sewerage infrastructure through alternative financing models will be considered.",""],[2,"336","2","Private Sector Water Sector Transformation Investment","The private sector will also be encouraged to invest in water sector transformation projects such as wastewater resource recovery, R&D&C&I and smart technology applications.",""]],"75":[[1,"319","1","Water Infrastructure Upgrading and Expansion","Existing infrastructure was upgraded, while new ones were built to support increasing demand and improving access in rural areas.",""],[1,"326","2","Sustainable Energy and Water Utilisation Initiative","In the Twelfth Plan, emphasis will be given to the sustainable utilisation of energy and water to ensure security of supply as well as to create more economic opportunities.",""],[1,"336","4","Sustainable Water Infrastructure Development","Sustainable infrastructure with cost-effective technology will be further developed to optimise resources in the water sector.",""],[1,"336","4","Alternative Water Services Systems","The initiatives that will be implemented include adopting alternative systems for water services, optimising cost-effective water infrastructure, emphasising the nature-based approach as well as implementing the circular economy concept.",""],[1,"336","5","Clean Water and Sanitation Access Improvement Programme","Access to clean and safe water supply as well as sanitation systems will be improved to achieve 98% coverage especially for rural and island communities.",""],[1,"336","5","Locally Suited Water Reticulation and Alternative Systems","Reticulation and alternative systems with locally suited technology will be adopted.",""],[1,"336","5","National Water Supply and Sanitation Coordination Committee","A national committee will be established to coordinate and oversee the overall implementation of water supply and sanitation projects in achieving the provision of water services for all.",""],[1,"336","6","Non-Revenue Water Reduction Programme","NRW reduction programme will be prioritised by providing financial assistance to state governments based on the current NRW level.",""],[1,"336","6","Leak Detection and Pressure Management Infrastructure","Infrastructure for preventive measures including leak sensors and pressure management tools to reduce water loss will be installed, particularly in the new distribution systems.",""],[1,"336","6","Water Auditing in Agencies and Public Institutions","agencies and public institutions will be encouraged to implement water auditing to identify the amount of water loss within the premises, such as military camps, universities and schools.",""],[1,"337","1","Groundwater Resource Development and Management Programme","The utilisation of groundwater as an alternative water source will be increased, especially in water-stressed areas to ensure water security.",""],[1,"337","1","Groundwater Aquifer Mapping Initiative","groundwater aquifers based on river basins will be mapped out.",""],[1,"337","1","Advanced Groundwater Exploration and Underground Dam Development","Advanced techniques and technologies will be utilised for the exploration, development and management of groundwater sources, including underground dams.",""],[1,"337","1","Underground Dam Feasibility Study","Detailed feasibility studies on underground dams will be undertaken to identify potential, risks and cost-effectiveness.",""],[1,"337","2","Multi-use Water Infrastructure Development","Development of multi-use water infrastructure will be promoted to ensure optimisation of resources.",""],[2,"336","4","Sustainable Water Infrastructure Development","Sustainable infrastructure with cost-effective technology will be further developed to optimise resources in the water sector.",""],[2,"336","4","Alternative Water Services Systems","The initiatives that will be implemented include adopting alternative systems for water services, optimising cost-effective water infrastructure, emphasising the nature-based approach as well as implementing the circular economy concept.",""],[2,"336","5","Clean Water and Sanitation Access Expansion","Access to clean and safe water supply as well as sanitation systems will be improved to achieve 98% coverage especially for rural and island communities.",""],[2,"336","5","Locally Suited Water Reticulation and Alternative Systems","Reticulation and alternative systems with locally suited technology will be adopted.",""],[2,"336","5","National Water Supply and Sanitation Coordination Committee","A national committee will be established to coordinate and oversee the overall implementation of water supply and sanitation projects in achieving the provision of water services for all.",""],[2,"336","6","Non-Revenue Water Reduction Programme","NRW reduction programme will be prioritised by providing financial assistance to state governments based on the current NRW level.",""],[2,"336","6","Leak Detection and Pressure Management Infrastructure","Infrastructure for preventive measures including leak sensors and pressure management tools to reduce water loss will be installed, particularly in the new distribution systems.",""],[2,"336","6","Water Auditing in Agencies and Public Institutions","agencies and public institutions will be encouraged to implement water auditing to identify the amount of water loss within the premises, such as military camps, universities and schools.",""],[2,"337","1","Groundwater Resource Development and Management Programme","The utilisation of groundwater as an alternative water source will be increased, especially in water-stressed areas to ensure water security.",""],[2,"337","1","River Basin Groundwater Aquifer Mapping","groundwater aquifers based on river basins will be mapped out.",""],[2,"337","1","Advanced Groundwater Exploration and Underground Dam Development","Advanced techniques and technologies will be utilised for the exploration, development and management of groundwater sources, including underground dams.",""],[2,"337","1","Underground Dam Feasibility Study","Detailed feasibility studies on underground dams will be undertaken to identify potential, risks and cost-effectiveness.",""],[2,"337","2","Multi-use Water Infrastructure Development","Development of multi-use water infrastructure will be promoted to ensure optimisation of resources.",""],[2,"337","3","Nature-Based Water Management and Eco-Friendly Construction Policy","Application of nature-based technology in addressing various water-related issues, such as water pollution, floods and droughts will be promoted.",""]],"76":[[1,"68","1","Agricommodity Entrepreneur Development for Specialty Products","The development of agricommodity entrepreneurs in speciality products, including tocotrienols, will be promoted to diversify into higher value-added products.",""],[1,"70","1","Internationalisation and Destination Promotion Initiative","measures will be undertaken to reduce the deficit, including greater internationalisation and continued promotion of Malaysia as a preferred destination for tourism, education and healthcare.",""],[1,"74","5","Export Market Expansion and Trade Facilitation","The Twelfth Plan also aims to expand export markets by improving market efficiency, empowering the role of industry players and strengthening trade facilitation.",""],[1,"77","12","Regional Global Services Hub Attraction Initiative","Attracting multinational companies to position Malaysia as the regional GS hub.",""],[1,"77","14","Tourism Industry Re-energisation and Promotion Initiative","Re-energising the tourism industry by strengthening brand positioning and aggressive promotion.",""],[1,"82","2","Export Market Expansion Initiative","the focus will be on boosting productivity mainly through ... expanding market exports",""],[1,"90","7","Export Market Expansion Initiative","This will be achieved by boosting productivity growth, expanding exports markets, strengthening the effectiveness of financial intermediation ecosystem, enhancing the role of industrial estates and food production areas as well as improving governance and policy.",""],[1,"97","2","Premium Healthcare Tourism Package Promotion","exclusive high-end medical tourism packages for premium healthcare travellers will be promoted.",""],[1,"100","4","Domestic and Export Market Expansion Measures","Measures to expand domestic and export markets will focus on improving market efficiency, empowering role of industry players and strengthening trade facilitation.",""],[1,"100","8","Digital Direct-to-Consumer Market Access Initiative","Initiatives to improve market efficiency will encompass connecting suppliers directly to consumers through digital platforms and enhancing supply chain sustainability.",""],[1,"100","8","Supply Chain Sustainability Enhancement Initiative","Initiatives to improve market efficiency will encompass connecting suppliers directly to consumers through digital platforms and enhancing supply chain sustainability.",""],[1,"102","4","Trade Facilitation and Export Promotion Initiative","During the Plan period, focus will be on leveraging trade agreements, and intensifying marketing and export promotion.",""],[1,"102","5","Trade Agreement Utilization and Market Access Support","MSMEs, SMPPs and mid-tier companies in all sectors of the economy will be encouraged to maximise opportunities from existing FTAs, bilateral agreements and economic partnerships with other countries.",""],[1,"102","5","Foreign Market Advisory and Intelligence Services","Industry players will be provided with advisory services and comprehensive information relating to foreign market as well as market intelligence.",""],[1,"102","5","New Bilateral and Multilateral Trade Agreement Negotiation","In addition, new bilateral and multilateral agreements with potential trading partners will be explored.",""],[1,"102","5","Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Ratification and Implementation","The Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership agreement, which potentially provides preferential market access to 45% of the world's population, is expected to be ratified and implemented in the Twelfth Plan period.",""],[1,"102","5","Priority Negotiation of Potential Free Trade Agreements","Several potential FTAs are currently being negotiated and will be among the priorities to be leveraged.",""],[1,"102","6","Trade Mission Streamlining and Export Promotion","Trade missions will be further streamlined to play an effective role in intensifying marketing and promotion efforts.",""],[1,"102","7","Manufacturing Export Market Penetration Support","Continuous efforts will be undertaken to facilitate industry players in the manufacturing sector to penetrate into markets of major trading partners.",""],[1,"102","7","National Trade Blueprint","The National Trade Blueprint (RTPN) is designed to improve the business ecosystem and enhance the competitiveness of Malaysian exporting companies by focusing on trade regulations, logistics and market access.",""],[1,"102","7","Mid-Tier Companies Export Development Programme","In addition, the Mid-Tier Companies Development Programme and Going Export (GoEx) Programme will be enhanced to enable local companies to export high value-added products.",""],[1,"102","7","National Product Branding Promotion","Manufacturers will also be encouraged to create strong brand propositions for local products to increase international recognition.",""],[1,"102","7","Global Promotion of Malaysian Brand","The Malaysian brand will be promoted globally as a brand for quality products.",""]],"77":[[1,"350","10","Single Border Agency for Trade Facilitation","Enhancing trade facilitation by establishing a single border agency.",""],[2,"38","3","Single Border Agency for Trade Facilitation","A single border agency for trade facilitation will be created, while a national regulatory framework for warehousing and the maritime economy will be formulated.",""],[2,"350","10","Single Border Agency for Trade Facilitation","Enhancing trade facilitation by establishing a single border agency.",""]],"78":[[1,"241","6","Subregional Cooperation for Cross-Border Economic Development","Regional development will continue to leverage the subregional cooperation platform to promote and accelerate socioeconomic growth.",""],[1,"241","7","Cross-Border Economic Activity Diversification and Modernisation Programme","Cross-border economic activities will be promoted through the diversification of production and supply chain activities across neighbouring countries.",""],[1,"241","7","MSME Cross-Border Diversification and Downstream Industry Support","MSMEs will be encouraged to diversify and modernise cross-border economic activities as well as venture into downstream industries.",""],[1,"241","7","Digital Cross-Border Trade Platform and Talent Upskilling Initiative","Cross-border economic activities will be accelerated by adopting the digital platform, promoting private sector participation and developing talent through upskilling and reskilling.",""],[1,"241","8","Cross-Border Value Chain Development Strategic Action Plan","A strategic action plan will be formulated to accelerate cross- border value chain development.",""],[2,"241","7","Cross-Border Economic Activity Diversification and Modernisation","Cross-border economic activities will be promoted through the diversification of production and supply chain activities across neighbouring countries.",""],[2,"241","7","MSME Cross-Border Modernisation and Downstream Upgrading Support","MSMEs will be encouraged to diversify and modernise cross-border economic activities as well as venture into downstream industries.",""],[2,"241","7","Digital Cross-Border Trade Platform and Talent Upskilling Initiative","Cross-border economic activities will be accelerated by adopting the digital platform, promoting private sector participation and developing talent through upskilling and reskilling.",""],[2,"241","8","Cross-Border Value Chain Development Strategic Action Plan","A strategic action plan will be formulated to accelerate cross- border value chain development.",""],[2,"241","8","Catalytic Cross-Border Development Projects","at least 30 catalytic projects with a strong focus on enhancing local economic activities will be identified.",""],[2,"241","8","Public-Private Coordination for Cross-Border Investment","The implementation of the strategic action plan will involve close collaboration and coordination between the public and private stakeholders.",""]],"79":[[1,"144","2","Crime Prevention, Rehabilitation and Emergency Preparedness","Efforts will be intensified in crime prevention, rehabilitation and emergency preparedness, as well as improve the welfare of security personnel.",""],[1,"158","5","Crime Prevention and Police Omnipresence Programmes","Crime prevention efforts were intensified through various programmes involving PDRM omnipresence and public participation.",""],[1,"169","3","Crime Prevention and Anti-Trafficking Measures","Measures to strengthen public safety and security will focus on improving crime prevention efforts, combatting drug abuse and trafficking as well as curbing trafficking in persons.",""],[1,"169","4","Crime Prevention Programme Intensification","Crime prevention efforts will be further intensified through the implementation of various programmes involving PDRM, CSOs, the private sector and the rakyat at large.",""],[1,"169","4","PDRM Omnipresence Programme Enhancement","The PDRM omnipresence programmes, including URB and MPV will be enhanced, while Community Policing will be strengthened through collaboration with CSOs, the private sector and local communities.",""],[1,"169","4","Safe City Programme Continuation","The Safe City Programme, which incorporates the environmental design approach in crime prevention, such as the installation of streetlamps, anti-crime safety mirrors and closed-circuit television, will be continued.",""],[1,"169","4","Inter-Agency Information Sharing for Crime Reduction","Greater cooperation among enforcement agencies, ATM, local authorities and communities will be enhanced for more effective information sharing to reduce crime and public disorder.",""],[1,"169","5","Crime Prevention Public Awareness Campaigns","Public awareness and campaigns through social media will be increased to create better awareness of crime prevention.",""],[1,"169","5","Public-Agency Crime Information Exchange Platform","Social media will also be utilised as a platform between the public and enforcement agencies to promote information exchange related to crime.",""],[1,"169","5","Enforcement Personnel Capacity Building Programme","Capacity building programmes for enforcement personnel will also be strengthened, especially in the areas of intelligence, investigation and prosecution.",""],[2,"168","1","Crime Prevention, Rehabilitation, and Emergency Preparedness","Emphasis will be given on safeguarding national sovereignty, intensifying efforts in crime prevention, rehabilitation and emergency preparedness as well as the welfare of ATM and enforcement personnel.",""],[2,"169","3","Crime Prevention and Anti-Trafficking Measures","Measures to strengthen public safety and security will focus on improving crime prevention efforts, combatting drug abuse and trafficking as well as curbing trafficking in persons.",""],[2,"169","4","Crime Prevention Programme Intensification","Crime prevention efforts will be further intensified through the implementation of various programmes involving PDRM, CSOs, the private sector and the rakyat at large.",""],[2,"169","4","PDRM Omnipresence Programme Enhancement","The PDRM omnipresence programmes, including URB and MPV will be enhanced, while Community Policing will be strengthened through collaboration with CSOs, the private sector and local communities.",""],[2,"169","4","Safe City Programme Continuation","The Safe City Programme, which incorporates the environmental design approach in crime prevention, such as the installation of streetlamps, anti-crime safety mirrors and closed-circuit television, will be continued.",""],[2,"169","4","Inter-Agency Crime Information Sharing Coordination","Greater cooperation among enforcement agencies, ATM, local authorities and communities will be enhanced for more effective information sharing to reduce crime and public disorder.",""],[2,"169","5","Public Crime Prevention Awareness Campaigns","Public awareness and campaigns through social media will be increased to create better awareness of crime prevention.",""],[2,"169","5","Social Media Information Exchange Platform for Crime Prevention","Social media will also be utilised as a platform between the public and enforcement agencies to promote information exchange related to crime.",""],[2,"169","5","Enforcement Personnel Capacity Building Programme","Capacity building programmes for enforcement personnel will also be strengthened, especially in the areas of intelligence, investigation and prosecution.",""]],"80":[[1,"169","3","Welfare Support for ATM and Enforcement Personnel","The welfare of ATM and enforcement personnel will be taken care off to enhance personnel performance in implementing duties.",""],[1,"170","6","Personnel Housing Construction, Upgrade, and Maintenance","the quarters will be built, upgraded and maintained to create a condusive environment for the personnel.",""],[1,"170","6","Healthcare Programme Improvement for ATM and Enforcement Personnel","Meanwhile, healthcare programmes for ATM and enforcement personnel will be improved to increase health and fitness.",""]],"81":[[1,"273","10","Border and Maritime Security Strengthening","These include strengthening border and maritime security, as well as implementing a holistic plan to manage illegal immigrants.",""],[1,"273","10","Holistic Illegal Immigrant Management Plan","These include strengthening border and maritime security, as well as implementing a holistic plan to manage illegal immigrants.",""],[1,"274","1","Border Security Post Expansion","Border security will be enhanced by increasing the number of security posts along the international border of Sabah and Sarawak to prevent the entry of illegal immigrants and combat unlawful activities.",""],[1,"274","1","Maritime Patrolling and Joint Operations Intensification","In addition, maritime patrolling and joint operations will be intensified to make maritime zones safer and more secure.",""],[1,"274","1","Defence Surveillance and Enforcement Capacity Strengthening","Defence capacity and capability will be strengthened especially in surveillance, enforcement and show of presence to protect the state's socioeconomic interests and security.",""],[1,"274","1","Advocacy Programmes on Unlawful Activities","Advocacy programmes will be expanded to increase awareness on unlawful activities, such as illegal fishing, maritime border crossing and drug trafficking.",""],[1,"274","2","Illegal Immigrant Management Plan","A holistic plan will be implemented to manage illegal immigrants.",""],[2,"273","10","Border and Maritime Security Strengthening","These include strengthening border and maritime security, as well as implementing a holistic plan to manage illegal immigrants.",""],[2,"273","10","Holistic Illegal Immigrant Management Plan","These include strengthening border and maritime security, as well as implementing a holistic plan to manage illegal immigrants.",""],[2,"274","1","Border Security Enhancement","Border security will be enhanced by increasing the number of security posts along the international border of Sabah and Sarawak to prevent the entry of illegal immigrants and combat unlawful activities.",""],[2,"274","1","Maritime Patrolling and Joint Operations","maritime patrolling and joint operations will be intensified to make maritime zones safer and more secure.",""],[2,"274","1","Defence Capacity and Capability Strengthening","Defence capacity and capability will be strengthened especially in surveillance, enforcement and show of presence to protect the state's socioeconomic interests and security.",""],[2,"274","1","Advocacy Programmes on Unlawful Activities","Advocacy programmes will be expanded to increase awareness on unlawful activities, such as illegal fishing, maritime border crossing and drug trafficking.",""],[2,"274","2","Holistic Illegal Immigrant Management Plan","A holistic plan will be implemented to manage illegal immigrants.",""]],"82":[[1,"149","3","Health Crisis Preparedness Strengthening","Increase preparedness in meeting future health crises.",""],[1,"149","9","Whole-of-Nation Future Health Crisis Response Approach","Implementing a whole-of-nation approach in handling future health crises.",""],[1,"149","16","Healthcare Preparedness Enhancement for Infectious Disease and Health Crisis Management","Enhancement of healthcare preparedness in managing infectious diseases and health crises.",""],[1,"159","1","Malaysia Strategy Framework for Emerging Diseases and Public Health Emergencies II Workplan","efforts to address emerging diseases were intensified through the implementation of the Malaysia Strategy Framework for Emerging Diseases and Public Health Emergencies II (MYSED II) Workplan (2017-2021).",""],[1,"159","1","COVID-19 Pandemic Preparedness and Control Measures","This work plan has proven to be extremely beneficial in battling the COVID-19 pandemic in terms of preparedness whereby swift control measures were put in place to contain the outbreak as well as save lives and resources.",""],[1,"159","2","Healthcare Capacity Support Through Civil Society and Private Sector Contributions","Meanwhile, contributions were received from various civil society organisations (CSOs), the corporate sector and the community to enhance healthcare capacity and capability during the COVID-19 pandemic.",""],[1,"172","3","Health Crisis Preparedness and Response Capacity Enhancement","The capability in handling health crises will be enhanced in ensuring quality and accessibility to healthcare services.",""],[1,"172","6","Communicable Disease Prevention and Intervention Programme Intensification","The prevention and intervention programmes will be intensified to combat CDs, especially during an outbreak or pandemic.",""],[1,"172","6","Disease Awareness and Mitigation Campaigns","Awareness and mitigation programmes on disease transmission, especially COVID-19, HIV, dengue, TB, rabies, hepatitis B and C, will be heightened, focusing on targeted groups.",""],[1,"172","6","Wolbachia Dengue Control Programme Expansion","The Wolbachia8 programme will be expanded to control the dengue endemic, particularly in the red zone areas.",""],[1,"172","6","National Immunisation Communication Plan","Effective communication plans for the national immunisation programme will be implemented to avoid vaccine preventable diseases.",""],[1,"172","6","National Immunisation Registry Establishment","a national immunisation registry will be established",""],[1,"172","6","Expanded National Immunisation Coverage","the immunisation programme will be expanded to include children in private schools, older persons, Orang Asli and underserved communities in Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[1,"172","6","Local Authority Public Health Management Enhancement","the role of local authorities in public health management will be enhanced by incorporating health aspects in the development planning as well as the provision of public sanitation services and disease control measures.",""],[1,"172","6","Food Hygiene Regulation and Legal Framework Reform","The Food Hygiene Regulation 2009 will be amended, while other related legal and regulatory frameworks will be refined to reduce the incidences of food borne diseases caused by home-based food businesses.",""],[1,"173","4","Healthcare Crisis Preparedness Strengthening","Healthcare services will be strengthened with better facilities, pharmaceutical services, health personnel and medical equipment to increase the preparedness level in handling health crises.",""],[1,"173","4","Clinical Laboratory Safety Compliance Upgrade","The safety measures at the clinical laboratories will also be improved to fully comply with the standard requirements set by the WHO to ensure the safety of personnel.",""],[1,"173","4","Multi-Hazard Public Emergency Response Team Strengthening","Furthermore, the multi-hazard public emergency response team will be strengthened in terms of health personnel and medical equipment at a number of selected entry points, particularly at the Kuala Lumpur International Airport, Sepang.",""],[1,"173","4","Emergency Department Equipment Upgrading","All emergency departments, particularly in state hospitals will be better equipped to improve service delivery efficiency.",""],[1,"173","6","Post-COVID-19 Healthcare Facility Design Refinement","The design for new healthcare facilities will be refined to fulfil post COVID-19 requirements.",""],[2,"149","3","Health Crisis Preparedness Enhancement","Increase preparedness in meeting future health crises.",""],[2,"149","9","Whole-of-Nation Health Crisis Response Approach","Implementing a whole-of-nation approach in handling future health crises.",""],[2,"149","16","Healthcare Preparedness Enhancement for Infectious Disease and Health Crisis Management","Enhancement of healthcare preparedness in managing infectious diseases and health crises.",""],[2,"159","1","Malaysia Strategy Framework for Emerging Diseases and Public Health Emergencies II Workplan","efforts to address emerging diseases were intensified through the implementation of the Malaysia Strategy Framework for Emerging Diseases and Public Health Emergencies II (MYSED II) Workplan (2017-2021)",""],[2,"159","2","COVID-19 Healthcare Capacity Support through Civil Society and Corporate Contributions","Meanwhile, contributions were received from various civil society organisations (CSOs), the corporate sector and the community to enhance healthcare capacity and capability during the COVID-19 pandemic.",""],[2,"159","3","Community Health Literacy Programmes","Efforts to improve health literacy among the population were continued through community-based programmes and user engagement.",""],[2,"172","3","Health Crisis Preparedness and Response Capacity Enhancement","The capability in handling health crises will be enhanced in ensuring quality and accessibility to healthcare services.",""],[2,"172","6","Communicable Disease Prevention and Intervention Programme Intensification","The prevention and intervention programmes will be intensified to combat CDs, especially during an outbreak or pandemic.",""],[2,"172","6","Disease Transmission Awareness and Mitigation Campaigns","Awareness and mitigation programmes on disease transmission, especially COVID-19, HIV, dengue, TB, rabies, hepatitis B and C, will be heightened, focusing on targeted groups.",""],[2,"172","6","Wolbachia Dengue Control Expansion","The Wolbachia8 programme will be expanded to control the dengue endemic, particularly in the red zone areas.",""],[2,"172","6","National Immunisation Communication Plan","Effective communication plans for the national immunisation programme will be implemented to avoid vaccine preventable diseases.",""],[2,"172","6","National Immunisation Registry Establishment","In addition, a national immunisation registry will be established, while the immunisation programme will be expanded to include children in private schools, older persons, Orang Asli and underserved communities in Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[2,"172","6","Expanded Immunisation Coverage for Underserved Groups","In addition, a national immunisation registry will be established, while the immunisation programme will be expanded to include children in private schools, older persons, Orang Asli and underserved communities in Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[2,"172","6","Local Authority Public Health Management Enhancement","The role of local authorities in public health management will be enhanced by incorporating health aspects in the development planning as well as the provision of public sanitation services and disease control measures.",""],[2,"172","6","Food Hygiene Regulation Amendment and Regulatory Refinement","The Food Hygiene Regulation 2009 will be amended, while other related legal and regulatory frameworks will be refined to reduce the incidences of food borne diseases caused by home-based food businesses.",""],[2,"172","9","Wolbachia Dengue Mosquito Replacement Programme","The objective of the Wolbachia programme is to replace wild dengue-transmitting mos- quito population with population that is unable to transmit dengue, zika or chikungunya viruses to people.",""],[2,"173","4","Healthcare Crisis Preparedness Strengthening","Healthcare services will be strengthened with better facilities, pharmaceutical services, health personnel and medical equipment to increase the preparedness level in handling health crises.",""],[2,"173","4","Clinical Laboratory Safety Compliance Upgrade","The safety measures at the clinical laboratories will also be improved to fully comply with the standard requirements set by the WHO to ensure the safety of personnel.",""],[2,"173","4","Multi-Hazard Public Emergency Response Team Strengthening","Furthermore, the multi-hazard public emergency response team will be strengthened in terms of health personnel and medical equipment at a number of selected entry points, particularly at the Kuala Lumpur International Airport, Sepang.",""]],"83":[[1,"170","1","Drug Law Revision and De-listing Reform","Drug-related laws will be reviewed to expand the definition of drugs and substances to cover NPS and ketum.",""],[1,"170","1","Integrated Drug Trafficking Surveillance and Enforcement Operations","Integrated and coordinated surveillance as well as operations by related enforcement agencies will be intensified to combat drug trafficking.",""],[1,"170","1","Alternative Service Delivery Programme Enhancement","The alternative service delivery (ASD) programme will be enhanced by empowering CSOs and the private sector to improve the effectiveness of drug prevention programmes.",""],[1,"170","1","Drug Prevention Awareness Campaigns","Awareness programmes targeting families, schools, HEIs, workplaces and communities will be intensified.",""],[1,"170","1","Drug Issues Index Development","An index to measure drug related issues will be introduced for better decision making in combatting drug abuse and trafficking.",""],[1,"173","1","Expansion of Cure and Care Clinics Rehabilitation Services","The role of the Cure and Care Clinics as a One Stop Centre for Addiction will be expanded to include alcohol addiction in the rehabilitation programme.",""],[2,"170","1","Drug Law Review and De-listing Reform","Drug-related laws will be reviewed to expand the definition of drugs and substances to cover NPS and ketum.",""],[2,"170","1","Integrated Drug Trafficking Surveillance and Enforcement Operations","Integrated and coordinated surveillance as well as operations by related enforcement agencies will be intensified to combat drug trafficking.",""],[2,"170","1","Alternative Service Delivery Programme Enhancement","The alternative service delivery (ASD) programme will be enhanced by empowering CSOs and the private sector to improve the effectiveness of drug prevention programmes.",""],[2,"170","1","Drug Prevention Awareness Campaigns","Awareness programmes targeting families, schools, HEIs, workplaces and communities will be intensified.",""],[2,"170","1","Drug Issues Index Development","An index to measure drug related issues will be introduced for better decision making in combatting drug abuse and trafficking.",""],[2,"173","1","Expansion of Cure and Care Clinics Rehabilitation Services","The role of the Cure and Care Clinics as a One Stop Centre for Addiction will be expanded to include alcohol addiction in the rehabilitation programme.",""]],"84":[[1,"149","10","Healthcare Service Redesign through Public-Private-CSO Collaboration","Consolidating resources and responsibilities, and redesigning healthcare service through collaboration among public and private sectors as well as civil society organisations (CSOs).",""],[1,"158","9","Cluster Hospitals Concept","2 Cluster hospitals concept aims to optimise the use of healthcare facilities and overcome the shortage of specialists in non-specialist hospitals.",""],[2,"144","2","Healthcare Sector Reform","In addition, healthcare service delivery will be enhanced by reforming the healthcare sector.",""],[2,"149","4","Equal Access to Healthcare Services","Ensure rakyat have equal access to healthcare services.",""],[2,"149","10","Healthcare Service Redesign through Multi-Sector Collaboration","Consolidating resources and responsibilities, and redesigning healthcare service through collaboration among public and private sectors as well as civil society organisations (CSOs).",""],[2,"149","11","Sustainable Health Financing Model","Introducing a more sustainable health financing model.",""],[2,"149","12","Digital Healthcare Services Digitalisation","Digitalising healthcare services by leveraging emerging technologies.",""],[2,"154","3","Healthcare Service Delivery Improvement","Meanwhile, healthcare service delivery, provision of quality and liveable affordable houses will be improved.",""],[2,"155","1","Healthcare Service Delivery Improvement","Priority was given to ensure the nation is safer and more secure, enhance healthcare service delivery and increase the supply and quality of affordable housing to poor, low- and middle- income households.",""],[2,"158","9","Cluster Hospitals Concept","2 Cluster hospitals concept aims to optimise the use of healthcare facilities and overcome the shortage of specialists in non-specialist hospitals.",""],[2,"159","2","National Health Waqf Fund Establishment","The plan was initiated to establish tabung wakaf kesihatan negara which focus on the development of waqf properties and products.",""]],"85":[[1,"159","3","Community Health Literacy and Engagement Programmes","Efforts to improve health literacy among the population were continued through community-based programmes and user engagement.",""],[1,"172","7","Non-Communicable Disease Control and Awareness Expansion","Efforts will be intensified to combat NCDs, focussing on cancer, cardiovascular diseases, diabetes mellitus and mental illness.",""],[1,"172","7","Healthy Lifestyle Awareness Programme Expansion","Various awareness programmes on a healthy lifestyle will be expanded to cover a wider population.",""],[1,"172","7","Mobile Cancer Screening and Diagnosis Service Expansion","The screening and diagnosis services for colorectal, oral, breast and cervical cancers will be strengthened by increasing the number of mobile health clinics.",""],[1,"172","7","Cancer Awareness Outreach for High-Risk Groups","In addition, cancer awareness programmes will be conducted at more health clinics and hospitals, targeting high-risk groups for early detection.",""],[1,"172","8","Nutrition Advocacy for Women of Reproductive Age","Nutrition advocacy activities for women of reproductive age will be heightened to control and prevent double burden9 of malnutrition.",""],[1,"172","9","Wolbachia Mosquito Replacement Programme","This will be done using bacteria called Wolbachia, which is naturally found inside many insects, including mosquitoes and are passed to the offspring through eggs.",""],[1,"173","2","National Mental Health Strategic Plan","A national strategic plan will be formulated to address mental health issues, covering among others, measures for prevention, intervention and treatment.",""],[1,"173","2","Mental Health Awareness Campaigns and Services","Campaigns and services related to mental health will be enhanced to educate and increase awareness through concerted efforts with related agencies, volunteers, community- based organisations (CBOs) and CSOs.",""],[1,"173","2","National Suicide Registry","the national suicide registry10 will be established to assist in formulating effective measures in addressing the rising suicide rate.",""],[1,"173","3","Domiciliary Oral Healthcare Services for Older Persons","In addition, domiciliary healthcare will incorporate oral healthcare services to prevent and treat oral cancer among older persons.",""],[1,"173","3","Strategic Partnerships for Preventive and Self-Care Programmes","Strategic partnerships with the private sector, HEIs, CBOs and CSOs will be enhanced to implement preventive and self-care programmes.",""],[1,"173","3","Healthy Ageing and Eating Awareness Programmes","Awareness programmes on healthy ageing and eating will be strengthened, including at the Pusat Aktiviti Warga Emas to maintain good health among older persons.",""],[1,"174","1","Public Health Literacy and Awareness Programmes","health literacy and awareness among the public will be enhanced through the implementation of various programmes at all levels.",""],[1,"174","5","National Health Literacy Policy","A national health literacy policy will be introduced to improve the knowledge and understanding of the public on the basic health information and services needed.",""],[1,"174","5","Health Literacy Surveillance System","The health literacy surveillance system will be developed to support the implementation of this policy.",""],[1,"174","5","Expanded Health Awareness Programmes","In line with Agenda Nasional Malaysia Sihat, healthcare awareness programmes will be intensified through various platforms at all levels.",""],[1,"174","5","KOSPEN Workplace Intensification","The implementation of KOSPEN will be invigorated at workplaces including government agencies to reduce the number of NCDs cases.",""],[1,"174","5","Wellness Facilities Utilization and Community Leader Capacity Building","In addition, wellness facilities under various agencies will be leveraged, while capacity building programmes for community leaders will be enhanced to improve health literacy and awareness.",""],[1,"174","6","Health Agents and National Health Icons Programme","More school children, HEIs students, local leaders and community members will be appointed as health agents and national health icons to promote health awareness at various levels.",""],[1,"174","6","Health Volunteer Coordination Alliance","A health alliance will be formed to better organise the content and activities of health volunteers to improve effectiveness.",""],[1,"174","6","Digital Health Literacy and Misinformation Countering Initiative","Social media platforms will be leveraged to invigorate health literacy and counter misleading information that exacerbates health issues.",""],[2,"172","7","Non-Communicable Disease Control Intensification","Efforts will be intensified to combat NCDs, focussing on cancer, cardiovascular diseases, diabetes mellitus and mental illness.",""],[2,"172","7","Healthy Lifestyle Awareness Expansion","Various awareness programmes on a healthy lifestyle will be expanded to cover a wider population.",""],[2,"172","7","Cancer Screening and Diagnosis Strengthening","The screening and diagnosis services for colorectal, oral, breast and cervical cancers will be strengthened by increasing the number of mobile health clinics.",""],[2,"172","7","Cancer Awareness Outreach for High-Risk Groups","In addition, cancer awareness programmes will be conducted at more health clinics and hospitals, targeting high-risk groups for early detection.",""],[2,"172","8","School, Workplace, and Community Obesity Intervention Programmes","The obesity intervention programmes at schools, HEIs, workplaces and local community centres will be intensified to increase awareness of the risks of poor dietary habits.",""],[2,"172","8","Expanded Sugar Tax on Premix Drink Products","The scope of sugar tax will also be expanded to include premix drink products.",""],[2,"172","8","Nutrition Advocacy for Women of Reproductive Age","Nutrition advocacy activities for women of reproductive age will be heightened to control and prevent double burden9 of malnutrition.",""],[2,"173","2","National Mental Health Strategic Plan","A national strategic plan will be formulated to address mental health issues, covering among others, measures for prevention, intervention and treatment.",""],[2,"173","2","Mental Health Awareness Campaigns and Services","Campaigns and services related to mental health will be enhanced to educate and increase awareness through concerted efforts with related agencies, volunteers, community- based organisations (CBOs) and CSOs.",""],[2,"173","2","National Suicide Registry","the national suicide registry10 will be established to assist in formulating effective measures in addressing the rising suicide rate.",""],[2,"173","8","Integrated Suicide and Fatal Injury Case Database","An integrated database between agencies to record cases of suicide and fatal injuries as a result of suicide.",""],[2,"174","1","Public Health Literacy and Awareness Programmes","health literacy and awareness among the public will be enhanced through the implementation of various programmes at all levels.",""],[2,"174","5","National Health Literacy Policy","A national health literacy policy will be introduced to improve the knowledge and understanding of the public on the basic health information and services needed.",""],[2,"174","5","Health Literacy Surveillance System","The health literacy surveillance system will be developed to support the implementation of this policy.",""],[2,"174","5","Expanded Health Awareness Campaigns","In line with Agenda Nasional Malaysia Sihat, healthcare awareness programmes will be intensified through various platforms at all levels.",""],[2,"174","5","KOSPEN Workplace Intensification","The implementation of KOSPEN will be invigorated at workplaces including government agencies to reduce the number of NCDs cases.",""],[2,"174","5","Wellness Facilities Utilization and Community Leader Capacity Building","In addition, wellness facilities under various agencies will be leveraged, while capacity building programmes for community leaders will be enhanced to improve health literacy and awareness.",""],[2,"174","6","Health Agents and National Health Icons Initiative","More school children, HEIs students, local leaders and community members will be appointed as health agents and national health icons to promote health awareness at various levels.",""],[2,"174","6","Health Volunteer Coordination Alliance","A health alliance will be formed to better organise the content and activities of health volunteers to improve effectiveness.",""],[2,"174","6","Digital Health Literacy and Misinformation Countering Campaign","Social media platforms will be leveraged to invigorate health literacy and counter misleading information that exacerbates health issues.",""]],"86":[[1,"173","4","Clinical Skills Laboratory Capacity Improvement","The capacity of clinical skills laboratory will be improved to enhance competencies of health personnel in providing the best quality care.",""],[1,"173","4","Clinical Laboratory Safety Compliance Upgrade","The safety measures at the clinical laboratories will also be improved to fully comply with the standard requirements set by the WHO to ensure the safety of personnel.",""],[1,"173","6","Healthcare Facilities and Human Resources Master Plan","A master plan on healthcare facilities and human resources will be formulated to strengthen the capacity and capability of healthcare personnel as well as improve facilities.",""],[1,"173","6","Cluster Hospital Expansion","The cluster hospital concept will be expanded to include more public hospitals, including teaching hospitals and health clinics, in increasing accessibility to specialists' services.",""],[1,"173","6","National Postgraduate Medical Training Enhancement","The curriculum of the National Postgraduate Training Programme will be enhanced to improve the quality and increase the number of medical specialists.",""],[1,"173","6","Healthcare Facility Repair, Replacement and Restoration Programme","Focus will also be given to the maintenance aspect through repair, replace and restore approach to improve aged healthcare facilities especially those above 50 years, as well as obsolete medical equipment.",""],[1,"173","6","Medical Equipment Leasing Pilot","In addition, leasing of medical equipment approach will be explored to enable rapid technology adoption in medical equipment procurement.",""],[1,"173","6","Accelerated Healthcare Facility Construction through Federal-State Collaboration","The construction of healthcare facilities will be accelerated through better collaboration between the Federal and state governments in meeting the health needs of the rakyat.",""],[1,"173","6","Expanded Mobile Health Services","the mobile health services will be expanded to include laboratory, x-ray and mammogram services.",""],[2,"173","4","Clinical Skills Laboratory Capacity Improvement","The capacity of clinical skills laboratory will be improved to enhance competencies of health personnel in providing the best quality care.",""],[2,"173","4","Clinical Laboratory Safety Compliance Upgrade","The safety measures at the clinical laboratories will also be improved to fully comply with the standard requirements set by the WHO to ensure the safety of personnel.",""],[2,"173","4","Emergency Department Equipment Upgrade","All emergency departments, particularly in state hospitals will be better equipped to improve service delivery efficiency.",""],[2,"173","6","Healthcare Facilities and Human Resources Master Plan","A master plan on healthcare facilities and human resources will be formulated to strengthen the capacity and capability of healthcare personnel as well as improve facilities.",""],[2,"173","6","Post-COVID-19 Healthcare Facility Design Upgrade","The design for new healthcare facilities will be refined to fulfil post COVID-19 requirements.",""],[2,"173","6","Cluster Hospital Expansion","The cluster hospital concept will be expanded to include more public hospitals, including teaching hospitals and health clinics, in increasing accessibility to specialists' services.",""],[2,"173","6","National Postgraduate Medical Training Enhancement","The curriculum of the National Postgraduate Training Programme will be enhanced to improve the quality and increase the number of medical specialists.",""],[2,"173","6","Healthcare Facility Repair, Replacement and Restoration Programme","Focus will also be given to the maintenance aspect through repair, replace and restore approach to improve aged healthcare facilities especially those above 50 years, as well as obsolete medical equipment.",""],[2,"173","6","Medical Equipment Leasing Pilot","In addition, leasing of medical equipment approach will be explored to enable rapid technology adoption in medical equipment procurement.",""],[2,"173","6","Accelerated Healthcare Facility Construction through Federal-State Collaboration","The construction of healthcare facilities will be accelerated through better collaboration between the Federal and state governments in meeting the health needs of the rakyat.",""],[2,"173","6","Expanded Mobile Health Services","the mobile health services will be expanded to include laboratory, x-ray and mammogram services.",""]],"87":[[1,"97","2","Big Data Analytics Adoption and Holistic Private Healthcare Care","measures will be undertaken to increase the adoption of BDA as well as strengthen the provision of holistic end-to-end care in the private healthcare subsector.",""],[1,"97","2","Digital Innovation in Healthcare Delivery and Aged Care","Emphasis will also be given on digital innovation in healthcare delivery and solutions to ensure better quality of healthcare services including aged care services.",""],[1,"97","7","Private Healthcare Subsector Research Coordination","a more coordinated research in T&CM will be conducted through private sector led collaboration with the research institutions.",""],[1,"98","7","Private Healthcare Tax Incentive Revision for Clinical Research Investment","In the private healthcare subsector, existing tax incentives will be revised to attract involvement of more research-based organisations and increase foreign direct investment (FDI) in clinical research.",""],[1,"98","7","Pharmaceutical R&D Commercialisation and Domestic Investment Promotion","At the same time, efforts will be undertaken to increase domestic investment in the pharmaceutical industry through commercialisation of R&D findings to secure sustainable medicine supply in Malaysia.",""],[1,"99","2","Financial Incentives for Advanced Healthcare Technology Adoption","financial incentives will be introduced to promote adoption of advanced healthcare technology among private aged healthcare facility providers.",""],[1,"175","1","Healthcare Research, Development and Innovation Support","research, development and innovation will be leveraged to ensure better provision of healthcare services.",""],[1,"175","4","Digital Health Research and Innovation Centre","A centre for digital health research and innovation will be established at the National Institute of Health (NIH) to accelerate the development of innovative digital healthcare products and services.",""],[1,"175","4","Researcher Capacity-Building Training Programmes","the capabilities of researchers will be enhanced through quality training programmes in improving their competency and performance.",""],[1,"175","4","External Quality Assurance Providers Centre","The role of the existing National Public Health Laboratory in Sungai Buloh will be strengthened by developing a centre for External Quality Assurance (EQA) providers.",""],[1,"175","5","Scientific Research Enhancement Programme","Efforts will also be undertaken to enhance scientific research by conducting birth cohort studies, vulnerability and adaptation assessment as well as human biomonitoring programme.",""],[1,"175","5","Healthcare R&D Partnership Strengthening","Collaboration and strategic partnerships, including with the private sector and foreign partners will be enhanced to strengthen the capacity and capability of research and development in the healthcare subsector.",""],[2,"173","5","Medicine Track-and-Trace System","track and trace system will be introduced to ensure sufficient supply and efficient distribution of medicines to all healthcare facilities.",""],[2,"175","1","Healthcare Research, Development and Innovation Support","research, development and innovation will be leveraged to ensure better provision of healthcare services",""],[2,"175","2","Environmental Health and WASH Information Systems","A number of dedicated information systems will be introduced, particularly on environmental health, water, sanitation and hygiene to gather information for health surveillance and auditing purposes.",""],[2,"175","2","Health Data Analytics and Precision Medicine Initiative","In this regard, big data analytics (BDA), business intelligence and precision medicine will be utilised for better planning and decision-making.",""],[2,"175","2","Integrated Food Safety Information and Nutrition Labelling System","In addition, an integrated food safety information system and a healthier choice logo system for food and beverages as well as a food composition database will be developed to provide information on food safety, ingredients composition and nutrition content.",""],[2,"175","4","Health Research and Innovation Capacity Strengthening","Research, development and innovation capacity will be intensified to improve the healthcare system.",""],[2,"175","4","Digital Health Research and Innovation Centre","A centre for digital health research and innovation will be established at the National Institute of Health (NIH) to accelerate the development of innovative digital healthcare products and services.",""],[2,"175","4","Researcher Training and Competency Development Programme","the capabilities of researchers will be enhanced through quality training programmes in improving their competency and performance.",""],[2,"175","4","External Quality Assurance Centre for Public Health Laboratories","The role of the existing National Public Health Laboratory in Sungai Buloh will be strengthened by developing a centre for External Quality Assurance (EQA) providers.",""],[2,"175","5","Birth Cohort Studies and Human Biomonitoring Programme","Efforts will also be undertaken to enhance scientific research by conducting birth cohort studies, vulnerability and adaptation assessment as well as human biomonitoring programme.",""],[2,"175","5","Healthcare Research Collaboration and Strategic Partnerships","Collaboration and strategic partnerships, including with the private sector and foreign partners will be enhanced to strengthen the capacity and capability of research and development in the healthcare subsector.",""]],"88":[[1,"159","2","National Health Waqf Fund Establishment","The plan was initiated to establish tabung wakaf kesihatan negara which focus on the development of waqf properties and products.",""],[1,"174","1","Sustainable Healthcare Financing and Health Protection Coverage","Initiatives will be introduced to ensure sustainable healthcare financing and strengthen health protection coverage for targeted groups.",""],[1,"174","2","Strengthening of the Malaysia National Health Accounts Report","The Malaysia National Health Accounts report will be strengthened by incorporating a more detailed analysis of public health expenditure as a tool to identify cost drivers within the health system.",""],[1,"174","2","Healthcare Charges Review for Higher-Income Patients","Current healthcare charges will be reviewed so that higher income patients will be required to pay higher charges.",""],[1,"174","2","Means-Tested Healthcare Subsidy Streamlining","Subsidies for healthcare services will be streamlined based on a means test11.",""],[1,"174","2","National Health Endowment Fund","a national health endowment fund, particularly from waqf will be introduced as a measure to diversify sources of funding and create alternative financing for healthcare.",""],[1,"174","2","Alternative Healthcare Financing through Public-Private Partnerships and Asset-Sharing","Several approaches including public-private partnership, rent-to-own, leasing and sharing of facilities will be explored in reducing the dependency on Government allocations.",""],[1,"174","3","Expansion of Pooled Procurement for Medicines and Medical Equipment","The existing strategic purchasing initiative will be enhanced through the expansion of the pooled procurement approach in purchasing pharmaceutical products and medical equipment.",""],[1,"174","3","Medicine Price Control Mechanism","a price control mechanism for medicines will be introduced to protect consumers from unfair pricing.",""],[1,"174","4","Health Insurance and Takaful Promotion","Efforts will be undertaken to encourage the rakyat to have insurance and takaful in financing healthcare expenses.",""],[1,"174","4","SOCSO Informal Sector Coverage Expansion","The existing social protection scheme under the Social Security Organisation (SOCSO) will be expanded to cover workers in the informal sector, including those in agriculture and retail trade.",""],[1,"174","4","PeKa B40 Health Financing Expansion","Meanwhile, the PeKa B40 programme will be expanded to cover the cost of treatment and services at private healthcare facilities through strategic purchasing and service level agreements to ensure sustainable health financing.",""],[2,"174","1","Sustainable Healthcare Financing and Health Protection Coverage","Initiatives will be introduced to ensure sustainable healthcare financing and strengthen health protection coverage for targeted groups.",""],[2,"174","2","Strengthening of Malaysia National Health Accounts Reporting","The Malaysia National Health Accounts report will be strengthened by incorporating a more detailed analysis of public health expenditure as a tool to identify cost drivers within the health system.",""],[2,"174","2","Revision of Healthcare Charges for Higher-Income Patients","Current healthcare charges will be reviewed so that higher income patients will be required to pay higher charges.",""],[2,"174","2","Means-Tested Healthcare Subsidy Rationalisation","Subsidies for healthcare services will be streamlined based on a means test11.",""],[2,"174","2","National Health Endowment Fund","a national health endowment fund, particularly from waqf will be introduced as a measure to diversify sources of funding and create alternative financing for healthcare.",""],[2,"174","2","Alternative Healthcare Financing Approaches","Several approaches including public-private partnership, rent-to-own, leasing and sharing of facilities will be explored in reducing the dependency on Government allocations.",""],[2,"174","3","Expanded Pooled Procurement for Pharmaceuticals and Medical Equipment","The existing strategic purchasing initiative will be enhanced through the expansion of the pooled procurement approach in purchasing pharmaceutical products and medical equipment.",""],[2,"174","3","Medicine Price Control Mechanism","a price control mechanism for medicines will be introduced to protect consumers from unfair pricing.",""],[2,"174","4","Health Insurance and Takaful Promotion","Efforts will be undertaken to encourage the rakyat to have insurance and takaful in financing healthcare expenses.",""],[2,"174","4","SOCSO Informal Sector Coverage Expansion","The existing social protection scheme under the Social Security Organisation (SOCSO) will be expanded to cover workers in the informal sector, including those in agriculture and retail trade.",""],[2,"174","4","PeKa B40 Healthcare Cost Expansion","Meanwhile, the PeKa B40 programme will be expanded to cover the cost of treatment and services at private healthcare facilities through strategic purchasing and service level agreements to ensure sustainable health financing.",""]],"89":[[1,"273","3","Healthcare Service Improvement in Sabah and Sarawak","Healthcare services will be improved to ensure better access and efficient delivery in Sabah and Sarawak, particularly in remote and rural areas.",""],[1,"273","3","Healthcare Personnel Strengthening Initiative","Among the efforts to be undertaken are strengthening healthcare personnel and improving facilities for healthcare services.",""],[1,"273","3","Healthcare Facilities Upgrading Programme","Among the efforts to be undertaken are strengthening healthcare personnel and improving facilities for healthcare services.",""],[1,"273","4","National Healthcare Facilities and Human Resource Master Plan","A national master plan for healthcare facilities and human resource development will be introduced to address inadequate healthcare facilities and personnel, including in Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[1,"273","4","Patient Transport Service Vehicle Expansion","In improving access to healthcare facilities among underserved communities, the number of patient transport service vehicle, used by health district offices will be increased.",""],[1,"273","4","Medical Equipment Provision for Sabah and Sarawak","more medical equipment will be provided to both states.",""],[1,"273","4","Teaching Hospital Construction for Universiti Malaysia Sabah and Universiti Malaysia Sarawak","the construction of teaching hospitals for Universiti Malaysia Sabah and Universiti Malaysia Sarawak will complement efforts to produce specialists in Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[1,"273","5","Cluster Hospital Expansion","The cluster hospital concept will be expanded to increase accessibility to specialists' services.",""],[1,"273","5","Mobile Health Services Expansion","The number of mobile health services will be increased, while existing healthcare facilities will be upgraded.",""],[1,"273","5","Healthcare Facility Upgrading Programme","The number of mobile health services will be increased, while existing healthcare facilities will be upgraded.",""],[1,"273","5","New Health Clinic Construction in Sabah and Sarawak","New health clinics will be built in Penampang and Beaufort in Sabah, as well as in Samarahan, Sarikei and Miri in Sarawak.",""],[1,"273","6","Regional Blood Centre and Public Health Laboratory Construction","A new regional blood centre will be built in Sabah, while in Sarawak, state public health and food safety laboratories will be built.",""],[2,"273","3","Healthcare Service Improvement in Sabah and Sarawak","Healthcare services will be improved to ensure better access and efficient delivery in Sabah and Sarawak, particularly in remote and rural areas.",""],[2,"273","3","Healthcare Personnel Strengthening Initiative","Among the efforts to be undertaken are strengthening healthcare personnel and improving facilities for healthcare services.",""],[2,"273","3","Healthcare Facilities Improvement Programme","Among the efforts to be undertaken are strengthening healthcare personnel and improving facilities for healthcare services.",""],[2,"273","4","National Healthcare Facilities and Human Resource Development Master Plan","A national master plan for healthcare facilities and human resource development will be introduced to address inadequate healthcare facilities and personnel, including in Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[2,"273","4","Patient Transport Service Vehicle Expansion","the number of patient transport service vehicle, used by health district offices will be increased.",""],[2,"273","4","Medical Equipment Provision for Sabah and Sarawak","more medical equipment will be provided to both states.",""],[2,"273","4","Teaching Hospital Construction for Universiti Malaysia Sabah and Universiti Malaysia Sarawak","the construction of teaching hospitals for Universiti Malaysia Sabah and Universiti Malaysia Sarawak will complement efforts to produce specialists in Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[2,"273","5","Cluster Hospital Expansion","The cluster hospital concept will be expanded to increase accessibility to specialists' services.",""],[2,"273","5","Expansion of Mobile Health Services","The number of mobile health services will be increased, while existing healthcare facilities will be upgraded.",""],[2,"273","5","Healthcare Facility Upgrading Programme","The number of mobile health services will be increased, while existing healthcare facilities will be upgraded.",""],[2,"273","5","New Health Clinic Construction in Sabah and Sarawak","New health clinics will be built in Penampang and Beaufort in Sabah, as well as in Samarahan, Sarikei and Miri in Sarawak.",""],[2,"273","6","Regional Blood Centre Construction in Sabah","A new regional blood centre will be built in Sabah",""],[2,"273","6","State Public Health and Food Safety Laboratory Construction in Sarawak","in Sarawak, state public health and food safety laboratories will be built",""]],"90":[[2,"208","6","Basic Services Access Expansion for Low-Income Households","efforts will be undertaken to improve access to basic services such as education, healthcare, housing and social protection.",""],[2,"209","8","Rural and Remote Primary Healthcare Access Expansion","Access to quality healthcare and primary health facilities in rural and remote areas will be enhanced to provide affordable and better healthcare services.",""],[2,"209","8","PeKa B40 Health Assistance Expansion","The Skim Peduli Kesihatan untuk Kumpulan B40 (PeKa B40) initiative will be strengthened by widening the coverage and increasing the target group's awareness of Peka B40 benefits.",""],[2,"209","8","Waqf-Based Healthcare Support Mechanism","The waqf model will be utilised as an alternative to ease the burden of B40 in meeting healthcare expenses.",""],[2,"209","8","Ambulance, Dialysis, and Elderly Care Centre Provision","It will also provide ambulance services as well as set up dialysis and elderly care centres.",""],[2,"209","8","Cooperative Affordable Healthcare Services","In addition, cooperatives will be encouraged to provide affordable healthcare services for their members.",""]],"91":[[2,"173","3","Regulation of Private Aged Healthcare Facility Design","The design of private healthcare facilities shall comply with the Private Aged Healthcare Facilities and Services Act 2018 and Care Centres (Amendment) Act 2018 to cater for the needs of older persons.",""],[2,"173","3","Domiciliary Oral Healthcare Services for Older Persons","domiciliary healthcare will incorporate oral healthcare services to prevent and treat oral cancer among older persons.",""],[2,"173","3","Strategic Partnerships for Preventive and Self-Care Programmes","Strategic partnerships with the private sector, HEIs, CBOs and CSOs will be enhanced to implement preventive and self-care programmes.",""],[2,"173","3","Healthy Ageing and Eating Awareness Programmes","Awareness programmes on healthy ageing and eating will be strengthened, including at the Pusat Aktiviti Warga Emas to maintain good health among older persons.",""],[2,"222","1","Older Persons Rights Protection Laws","This will include introducing laws to protect the rights of older persons, establishing a comprehensive long-term care framework, enhancing quality and services of caregivers as well as invigorating the social care industry.",""],[2,"222","1","Comprehensive Long-Term Care Framework","This will include introducing laws to protect the rights of older persons, establishing a comprehensive long-term care framework, enhancing quality and services of caregivers as well as invigorating the social care industry.",""],[2,"222","1","Healthy Ageing Awareness Campaigns","Awareness campaigns on healthy ageing will be intensified, while care givers for the aged will be promoted as a professional career.",""],[2,"222","1","Professionalization of Elder Caregivers","Awareness campaigns on healthy ageing will be intensified, while care givers for the aged will be promoted as a professional career.",""],[2,"222","1","Expanded Palliative Care Collaboration","In addition, collaboration between public and private healthcare providers in broadening palliative care services will be strengthened to ensure the effectiveness of intervention programmes.",""],[2,"222","1","Digital Homecare Monitoring and Virtual Consultations","New initiatives will also be introduced to modernise healthcare services by utilising internet of things (IoT) in homecare monitoring and virtual medical consultations.",""]],"92":[[1,"32","4","Healthcare Service Delivery Expansion","Healthcare service delivery will continue to be a focus in increasing the health status of the rakyat.",""],[1,"32","4","Disease Preparedness and Healthcare Coverage Expansion","Endeavours to improve preparedness in battling various diseases and the expansion of healthcare coverage will be continued.",""],[1,"32","5","Healthcare System Revitalisation","Thus, revitalising healthcare system is critical in order to ensure the rakyat have equal access to healthcare services as well as be well-prepared in meeting future health crises.",""],[1,"34","2","National COVID-19 Immunisation Programme","the rollout of the National COVID-19 Immunisation Programme",""],[1,"36","2","Healthcare Service Revitalisation","Lessons learnt from managing the pandemic will be leveraged to revitalise healthcare services.",""],[1,"36","2","Whole-of-Nation Outbreak and Health Crisis Management","the need to embrace the whole-of- nation approach in ensuring better management of future outbreaks and health crises.",""],[1,"36","2","Public-Private and CSO Healthcare Service Redesign","healthcare services will be redesigned through collaboration between public and private sectors as well as CSOs.",""],[1,"36","2","Sustainable Health Financing Model","a more sustainable health financing model will be introduced",""],[1,"36","2","Digitalisation of Healthcare Services","healthcare services will be digitalised to accelerate delivery.",""],[1,"53","8","COVID-19 Vaccination Programme Acceleration","These packages aimed to protect the welfare of the rakyat, support businesses and strengthen the economy as well as accelerate the implementation of the vaccination programme to contain and break the chain of COVID-19 infection.",""],[1,"453","3","Healthcare Preparedness Masterplan for Infectious Diseases","strengthening healthcare preparedness for infectious diseases will be accorded high priority.",""],[1,"453","3","Healthcare Facilities and Human Resource Management Masterplan","a healthcare facilities and human resource management masterplan will be developed",""],[1,"453","3","National Centre for Disease Control and Infectious Disease Hospital","the National Centre for Disease Control and Infectious Disease Hospital will be built.",""],[1,"453","3","Whole-of-Nation Healthcare System Revitalisation","The healthcare system will be revitalised through the adoption of a whole-of-nation approach, optimising resources, redesigning and digitalising healthcare services, as well as introducing a more sustainable health financing model in promoting a healthy and productive nation.",""],[1,"455","9","Healthcare System Revitalization for Future Health Crises","revitalising the healthcare system in handling future health crises;",""],[2,"32","4","Healthcare Service Delivery Continuation","Healthcare service delivery will continue to be a focus in increasing the health status of the rakyat",""],[2,"32","4","Disease Preparedness and Healthcare Coverage Expansion","Endeavours to improve preparedness in battling various diseases and the expansion of healthcare coverage will be continued",""],[2,"32","5","Healthcare System Revitalisation","Thus, revitalising healthcare system is critical in order to ensure the rakyat have equal access to healthcare services as well as be well-prepared in meeting future health crises.",""],[2,"36","2","Healthcare Service Revitalisation","Lessons learnt from managing the pandemic will be leveraged to revitalise healthcare services.",""],[2,"36","2","Whole-of-Nation Future Outbreak and Health Crisis Management","the need to embrace the whole-of- nation approach in ensuring better management of future outbreaks and health crises.",""],[2,"36","2","Public-Private and CSO Healthcare Service Redesign","Resources and responsibilities will be consolidated and healthcare services will be redesigned through collaboration between public and private sectors as well as CSOs.",""],[2,"36","2","Sustainable Health Financing Model","a more sustainable health financing model will be introduced",""],[2,"36","2","Healthcare Digitalisation Initiative","healthcare services will be digitalised to accelerate delivery.",""],[2,"453","3","Healthcare Facilities and Human Resource Management Masterplan","a healthcare facilities and human resource management masterplan will be developed",""],[2,"453","3","National Centre for Disease Control and Infectious Disease Hospital","the National Centre for Disease Control and Infectious Disease Hospital will be built",""],[2,"453","3","Whole-of-Nation Healthcare System Revitalisation","The healthcare system will be revitalised through the adoption of a whole-of-nation approach, optimising resources, redesigning and digitalising healthcare services, as well as introducing a more sustainable health financing model in promoting a healthy and productive nation",""],[2,"455","9","Healthcare System Revitalization for Future Health Crises","revitalising the healthcare system in handling future health crises;",""]],"93":[[1,"32","4","Affordable Housing Supply Expansion","The supply of quality affordable housing will be increased by improving access to affordable housing and governance as well as ensuring inclusive housing development.",""],[1,"68","2","Affordable Housing Development Programme","More affordable housing will be developed in strategic locations.",""],[1,"273","7","New Public Housing Model for Affordable Housing","A new public housing model will be adopted to encourage more private developers to build affordable houses.",""],[1,"273","7","Expansion of Affordable Housing Supply","Concurrently, supply of affordable housing will be increased for the targeted groups.",""],[1,"273","8","Rumah Malaysia Affordable Housing Programme","The PPR has been rebranded as Rumah Malaysia to ensure the provision of affordable houses is more sustainable in the long run.",""],[1,"273","8","Low-Cost Housing Completion in Sabah and Sarawak","A total of seven projects involving 3,202 low-cost houses under the Program Perumahan Rakyat (PPR) in Sabah and Sarawak will be completed during the Twelfth Plan period.",""],[1,"273","8","Request for Proposal Housing Collaboration Model","The Rumah Malaysia concept will adopt the request for proposal approach to provide a platform for collaboration among the Federal Government, state governments and private developers.",""],[1,"273","9","Affordable Housing Construction for Targeted Groups in Sabah and Sarawak","More affordable houses will be constructed for the targeted groups in Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[1,"273","9","Rumah Mesra Rakyat Housing Support Programme","The RMR will assist poor and low-income households that own land to build their own houses.",""],[1,"274","7","Housing Assistance Programme","The housing assistance programme will be continued in building new and repairing dilapidated houses to improve the living conditions of poor households in rural and urban areas.",""],[1,"453","3","Affordable Housing Construction Programme","More quality and affordable housing will be constructed.",""],[2,"68","2","Affordable Housing Development Programme","More affordable housing will be developed in strategic locations.",""]],"94":[[1,"144","2","Affordable Housing Supply Expansion","the supply of quality and affordable houses will be increased.",""],[1,"154","3","Affordable Housing Provision Improvement","Meanwhile, healthcare service delivery, provision of quality and liveable affordable houses will be improved.",""],[1,"159","7","Affordable Housing Access and Public Housing Management Improvement","Among the initiatives undertaken included increased access to affordable houses, enhancement of planning and implementation for better management of public affordable houses and provision of user-friendly facilities for enhanced liveability.",""],[1,"160","1","Affordable Housing Financing Facilities for First-Time Buyers","Access to affordable housing was enhanced through the provision of financing facilities for first time home buyers and the Rent-to-Own (RTO) housing programme for poor and low-income households.",""],[1,"160","1","Rent-to-Own Housing Programme for Low-Income Households","Access to affordable housing was enhanced through the provision of financing facilities for first time home buyers and the Rent-to-Own (RTO) housing programme for poor and low-income households.",""],[1,"160","1","My First Home and First House Deposit Financing Schemes","Special financing schemes, namely, My First Home Scheme (MyHome) and First House Deposit Financing Scheme (MyDeposit) were provided.",""],[1,"164","6","Affordable Housing Supply Expansion","This will be achieved by ensuring national security and sovereignty, enhancing the healthcare service delivery, increasing the supply of quality and liveable affordable housing, leveraging sports in building an active nation as well as strengthening national unity.",""],[1,"176","1","Affordable Housing Access and Home Ownership Support","This will be achieved by ensuring the provision of affordable housing for target groups, increasing access to financing and managing housing construction costs to facilitate home ownership.",""],[1,"176","3","Housing Financing Scheme Improvement","The existing housing financing schemes will be improved to assist the B40 and M40 households to own houses.",""],[1,"176","3","Rent-to-Own Housing Programme Expansion","the RTO programme will be expanded to cover houses priced up to RM500,000 with an option to purchase the property within five years of renting.",""],[1,"176","3","Affordable Homes and Youth Housing Financing Support","the Fund for Affordable Homes and Youth Housing Scheme will continue to be provided in financing the purchase of the first house.",""],[1,"176","4","Housing Loan Support and Affordable Home Construction Scheme","The Skim Pinjaman Perumahan will be strengthened to assist households that own land to build affordable houses.",""],[1,"176","4","Homeowner Auction Prevention Assistance","Efforts will also be undertaken to assist home owners in preventing their houses from being auctioned due to financial difficulties.",""],[1,"176","4","Murabaha to Ijarah to Murabaha Home Repurchase Programme","the murabaha to ijarah to murabaha programme (own-to-rent-to-own) will be introduced to allow home owners to repurchase the property acquired by banks.",""],[2,"144","2","Affordable Housing Supply Expansion","Meanwhile, the supply of quality and affordable houses will be increased.",""],[2,"154","3","Affordable Housing Provision","Meanwhile, healthcare service delivery, provision of quality and liveable affordable houses will be improved.",""],[2,"155","1","Affordable Housing Supply and Quality Expansion","Priority was given to ensure the nation is safer and more secure, enhance healthcare service delivery and increase the supply and quality of affordable housing to poor, low- and middle- income households.",""],[2,"159","7","Affordable Housing Access and Management Improvement","Among the initiatives undertaken included increased access to affordable houses, enhancement of planning and implementation for better management of public affordable houses and provision of user-friendly facilities for enhanced liveability.",""],[2,"160","1","First-Time Homebuyer Financing Facilities","Access to affordable housing was enhanced through the provision of financing facilities for first time home buyers and the Rent-to-Own (RTO) housing programme for poor and low-income households.",""],[2,"160","1","Rent-to-Own Housing Programme","Access to affordable housing was enhanced through the provision of financing facilities for first time home buyers and the Rent-to-Own (RTO) housing programme for poor and low-income households.",""],[2,"160","1","My First Home Scheme","Special financing schemes, namely, My First Home Scheme (MyHome) and First House Deposit Financing Scheme (MyDeposit) were provided.",""],[2,"160","1","First House Deposit Financing Scheme","Special financing schemes, namely, My First Home Scheme (MyHome) and First House Deposit Financing Scheme (MyDeposit) were provided.",""],[2,"176","1","Affordable Housing Access and Home Ownership Support","This will be achieved by ensuring the provision of affordable housing for target groups, increasing access to financing and managing housing construction costs to facilitate home ownership.",""],[2,"176","3","Housing Financing Scheme Improvement for B40 and M40 Households","The existing housing financing schemes will be improved to assist the B40 and M40 households to own houses.",""],[2,"176","3","Rent-to-Own Housing Programme Expansion","the RTO programme will be expanded to cover houses priced up to RM500,000 with an option to purchase the property within five years of renting.",""],[2,"176","3","Affordable Homes and Youth Housing Financing Support","the Fund for Affordable Homes and Youth Housing Scheme will continue to be provided in financing the purchase of the first house.",""],[2,"176","4","Affordable Housing Loan Support Scheme Strengthening","The Skim Pinjaman Perumahan will be strengthened to assist households that own land to build affordable houses.",""],[2,"176","4","Enhanced Housing Loan Package Reform","A new financial model with more attractive loan packages will be introduced to increase take-up rate.",""],[2,"176","4","Homeowner Auction Prevention Assistance","Efforts will also be undertaken to assist home owners in preventing their houses from being auctioned due to financial difficulties.",""],[2,"176","4","Murabaha to Ijarah to Murabaha Home Repurchase Programme","the murabaha to ijarah to murabaha programme (own-to-rent-to-own) will be introduced to allow home owners to repurchase the property acquired by banks.",""],[2,"210","1","Continuation of Housing Assistance Programmes for the B40","Existing housing policies and programmes to assist the B40 will be continued.",""],[2,"210","1","Affordable Homeownership Priority for the B1 Income Decile","priority will be given to the B1 income decile to own affordable homes.",""],[2,"210","1","Affordable Housing Programme Continuation","housing programmes such as Rent-to-Own (RTO), Rumah Mesra Rakyat and Program Perumahan Penjawat Awam Malaysia will continue to be implemented.",""],[2,"210","1","Federal-State-Local Housing Policy Coordination","Coordination between the Federal and state governments as well as local authorities in integrating and streamlining overall housing policies will be strengthened.",""],[2,"210","4","Education Access Improvement and Affordable Home Ownership Facilitation","In this regard, access to education will be improved while affordable home ownership will be facilitated.",""],[2,"211","4","Affordable Home Ownership Facilitation","Ownership of affordable homes by the M40 will be facilitated.",""]],"95":[[1,"175","6","Affordable Housing Governance and Inclusive Housing Development","Emphasis will be given to improving access to affordable housing by enhancing affordable housing governance and ensuring inclusive housing development.",""],[1,"176","1","Use of Government-Owned and Waqf Land for Affordable Housing","Efforts will continue to be undertaken to capitalise on government-owned and waqf land to enable higher ownership of affordable housing for selected target groups.",""],[1,"176","2","Affordable Housing Construction Programme","More affordable housing will be constructed for the selected target groups.",""],[1,"176","2","Affordable Housing Purchase Restriction Regulation","A regulation will be introduced to limit the purchase of only one affordable house per eligible citizen.",""],[1,"176","2","Affordable Homeowner Database System","A comprehensive database of affordable homeowners will be established to monitor home ownership.",""],[1,"176","2","Affordable Housing Ceiling Price Regulation","Ceiling prices of affordable housing will also be introduced in the secondary market to control house prices, especially in the urban areas.",""],[1,"176","2","PPR Errant Tenant Exit Enforcement","the exit policy on errant tenants of PPR will be strictly enforced to ensure this programme only benefits deserving households.",""],[1,"176","5","Affordable Housing Construction Cost Management Measures","Initiatives will be undertaken to manage the construction cost of affordable houses.",""],[1,"176","5","Affordable Housing Cost-Sharing Development Model","A model for affordable housing development based on a cost-sharing mechanism will be introduced through collaboration between the Federal Government and state governments, and private developers.",""],[1,"176","5","Industrialised Building System Incentive Review","The existing Industrialised Building System (IBS) incentives will be reviewed to encourage developers to use IBS technology to manage costs and improve efficiency.",""],[1,"176","6","Affordable Housing Land Capitalisation Initiative","Efforts will be undertaken to capitalise land owned by the Federal Government and state governments, waqf land and utility providers for the development of affordable housing.",""],[1,"176","6","Waqf Land Development Law","A law on waqf land development will be introduced at the Federal level which will serve as a guide for waqf land development throughout the country.",""],[1,"176","6","Waqf Land Identification and Housing Development Coordination","The Federal Government will continue working closely with the state Islamic religious councils and other stakeholders to identify suitable waqf land to be developed for housing purposes.",""],[1,"176","6","Public Utility Land Identification for Affordable Housing","In addition, suitable land owned by public utility companies will be identified to develop affordable housing, particularly in the urban and peripheral areas.",""],[1,"176","7","Housing Redevelopment Guideline","A housing redevelopment guideline will be formulated, using the public-private partnership model, to rebuild public housing, especially dilapidated flats, and old or abandoned government quarters that are beyond economic repair.",""],[1,"176","7","Affordable Housing Development Near Transport Terminals","In addition, affordable housing will be built close to transport terminals to improve mobility and connectivity.",""],[1,"176","7","Affordable Housing Provision in New Township Planning","In this regard, the provision of affordable housing will be included in the development planning of new townships.",""],[1,"177","1","Affordable Housing Governance Enhancement","The governance of affordable housing will be enhanced to improve planning, coordination and execution of affordable housing projects at the Federal, state and local levels.",""],[1,"177","1","Affordable Housing Institutional Capacity Strengthening","Institutional capability in building affordable houses, enforcing houses standards, and strengthening rules and regulations to safeguard homebuyers and tenants will be enhanced.",""],[1,"177","2","Housing Data Centre Establishment","A data centre on housing, integrating relevant data from the Federal and state governments as well as private developers will be established to strengthen the institutional capability.",""],[1,"177","2","Evidence-Based Housing Policy Support","BDA will be leveraged to facilitate evidence-based policy formulation in developing housing projects.",""],[1,"177","2","Housing Integrated Management System","a housing integrated management system will be developed to serve as a single-entry platform for the application and processing of advertisement and sale permits.",""],[1,"177","3","Quality Affordable Housing Standards Enforcement","The Piawaian Perumahan Berkualiti (PPB) will be enforced to ensure the quality of affordable houses.",""],[1,"177","5","Inclusive Affordable Housing Requirement in New Township Development","the construction of affordable houses will be made a prerequisite in new township development",""],[1,"177","6","Affordable Housing Priority in New Townships","The construction of affordable houses will be made a priority in the development of new townships, making them accessible to low-income groups.",""],[1,"177","6","National Affordable Housing Guideline for State Governments","A national guideline will be formulated to serve as a reference for state governments in the development of affordable housing in new townships.",""],[1,"177","7","Affordable Housing Quality Standard","The standard provides minimum quality standards for housing in Malaysia and serves as a guideline in the planning, design and construction of affordable housing projects.",""],[2,"164","6","Affordable Housing Supply Expansion","This will be achieved by ensuring national security and sovereignty, enhancing the healthcare service delivery, increasing the supply of quality and liveable affordable housing, leveraging sports in building an active nation as well as strengthening national unity.",""],[2,"175","6","Affordable Housing Governance and Inclusive Development","Emphasis will be given to improving access to affordable housing by enhancing affordable housing governance and ensuring inclusive housing development.",""],[2,"176","1","Use of Government-Owned and Waqf Land for Affordable Housing","Efforts will continue to be undertaken to capitalise on government-owned and waqf land to enable higher ownership of affordable housing for selected target groups.",""],[2,"176","2","Affordable Housing Construction Programme","More affordable housing will be constructed for the selected target groups.",""],[2,"176","2","Affordable Housing Purchase Restriction Regulation","A regulation will be introduced to limit the purchase of only one affordable house per eligible citizen.",""],[2,"176","2","PPR Errant Tenant Exit Enforcement","the exit policy on errant tenants of PPR will be strictly enforced to ensure this programme only benefits deserving households.",""],[2,"176","5","Affordable Housing Construction Cost Management Measures","Initiatives will be undertaken to manage the construction cost of affordable houses.",""],[2,"176","5","Affordable Housing Cost-Sharing Development Model","A model for affordable housing development based on a cost-sharing mechanism will be introduced through collaboration between the Federal Government and state governments, and private developers.",""],[2,"176","5","Industrialised Building System Incentive Review","The existing Industrialised Building System (IBS) incentives will be reviewed to encourage developers to use IBS technology to manage costs and improve efficiency.",""],[2,"176","6","Affordable Housing Land Development Initiative","Efforts will be undertaken to capitalise land owned by the Federal Government and state governments, waqf land and utility providers for the development of affordable housing.",""],[2,"176","6","Waqf Land Development Law","A law on waqf land development will be introduced at the Federal level which will serve as a guide for waqf land development throughout the country.",""],[2,"176","6","Waqf Land Identification for Housing","The Federal Government will continue working closely with the state Islamic religious councils and other stakeholders to identify suitable waqf land to be developed for housing purposes.",""],[2,"176","6","Public Utility Land Identification for Affordable Housing","suitable land owned by public utility companies will be identified to develop affordable housing, particularly in the urban and peripheral areas.",""],[2,"177","5","Inclusive Affordable Housing Provision Measures","Measures will be undertaken to ensure the provision of affordable housing is inclusive.",""],[2,"177","5","Affordable Housing Requirement in New Township Development","the construction of affordable houses will be made a prerequisite in new township development.",""],[2,"177","6","Affordable Housing Development in New Townships","The construction of affordable houses will be made a priority in the development of new townships, making them accessible to low-income groups.",""],[2,"177","6","National Affordable Housing Guideline for State Governments","A national guideline will be formulated to serve as a reference for state governments in the development of affordable housing in new townships.",""],[2,"183","1","Affordable Housing Supply Expansion","The wellbeing and unity of the rakyat will be enhanced through improving healthcare service delivery as well as increasing the supply of quality affordable housing.",""],[2,"206","6","Affordable Housing Construction Programme","An additional 500,000 affordable houses will be constructed to provide quality and decent housing for poor households.",""]],"96":[[1,"245","1","Affordable Housing and Urban Infrastructure Improvement","Efforts to improve the liveability in urban areas will include the provision of affordable housing and better infrastructure.",""],[1,"245","2","Affordable Urban Housing Provision","The provision of affordable housing for urban dwellers will be continued as part of the initiatives under the NAHP.",""],[1,"245","2","Mixed-Use Transit-Oriented Development Promotion","More mixed-use development that incorporates affordable housing with commercial development, including TOD, will be encouraged in realising a more inclusive development.",""],[1,"245","2","Inclusive Urban Public Infrastructure Upgrade","The quality of life of urban dwellers will be improved with the provision of better public infrastructure, especially to suit the needs of older persons and persons with disabilities.",""],[2,"245","1","Affordable Housing and Urban Infrastructure Improvement","Efforts to improve the liveability in urban areas will include the provision of affordable housing and better infrastructure.",""],[2,"245","2","Urban Affordable Housing and Liveability Measures","Measures to enhance liveability in cities will be intensified by providing better access to quality and affordable housing as well as programmes to improve household income, particularly for the urban poor.",""],[2,"245","2","Continued Affordable Housing Provision under NAHP","The provision of affordable housing for urban dwellers will be continued as part of the initiatives under the NAHP.",""],[2,"245","2","Mixed-Use Transit-Oriented Development Promotion","More mixed-use development that incorporates affordable housing with commercial development, including TOD, will be encouraged in realising a more inclusive development.",""],[2,"245","2","Accessible Urban Public Infrastructure Improvement","The quality of life of urban dwellers will be improved with the provision of better public infrastructure, especially to suit the needs of older persons and persons with disabilities.",""],[2,"270","6","Urban Development Acceleration Measures","measures to accelerate urban development will focus on improving the development potential of cities, upgrading urban services and enhancing liveability.",""],[2,"273","7","New Public Housing Model for Affordable Housing","A new public housing model will be adopted to encourage more private developers to build affordable houses.",""],[2,"273","7","Expansion of Affordable Housing Supply for Targeted Groups","Concurrently, supply of affordable housing will be increased for the targeted groups.",""],[2,"273","8","Affordable Housing Delivery under Rumah Malaysia","A total of seven projects involving 3,202 low-cost houses under the Program Perumahan Rakyat (PPR) in Sabah and Sarawak will be completed during the Twelfth Plan period.",""],[2,"273","8","Rumah Malaysia Public-Private Housing Collaboration Model","The Rumah Malaysia concept will adopt the request for proposal approach to provide a platform for collaboration among the Federal Government, state governments and private developers.",""],[2,"273","9","Affordable Housing Construction for Targeted Groups in Sabah and Sarawak","More affordable houses will be constructed for the targeted groups in Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[2,"273","9","Rumah Mesra Rakyat Housing Support Programme","The RMR will assist poor and low-income households that own land to build their own houses.",""]],"97":[[2,"216","1","Improved Property Financing Terms for Bumiputera Ownership","Better terms of financing for the purchase of properties will be introduced through collaboration between financial institutions, private developers and investors.",""],[2,"216","1","Rent-to-Own Commercial and Industrial Asset Development for Bumiputera Entrepreneurs","Furthermore, EDOs will be encouraged to acquire and develop commercial and industrial assets under the Rent-to-Own scheme for Bumiputera entrepreneurs.",""],[2,"216","2","Bumiputera Housing Finance Scheme","a dedicated fund will be explored to provide a financing scheme for eligible Bumiputera households",""],[2,"216","2","Suburban New Township Development","new townships in sub-urban areas with good connectivity and infrastructure will be developed by the private sector and Bumiputera mandated agencies",""],[2,"216","2","Bumiputera Home Ownership Quota Coordination","the policy on Bumiputera quota in home ownership will be coordinated between Federal, state and local governments",""],[2,"216","3","Bumiputera Asset Ownership Expansion through New Business Models","In increasing Bumiputera assets ownership, PHB will explore new business models to enable participation in government privatisation projects as part of its real estate investment trust portfolio.",""],[2,"216","3","AHB Fund Injection and Dividend Reinvestment Scheme","A new model of property ownership will be introduced through the injection of funds in the AHB to generate dividends, which will be reinvested as long-term investment instruments.",""],[2,"216","3","Post-COVID Business Model Innovation for Commercial Property Ownership","In adjusting to the post COVID-19 pandemic new normal, EDOs and SOEs will explore innovative new business models to retain and enhance the ownership of the commercial and business premises.",""]],"98":[[1,"33","3","TVET Ecosystem Improvement Initiative","Improving technical and vocational education and training (TVET) ecosystem to produce future-ready talent will be introduced as a game changer that can better meet industry demand.",""],[1,"33","3","Emerging Technologies for TVET Teaching and Research","Emerging technologies such as virtual reality, augmented reality and artificial intelligence will be leveraged to complement existing hands-on teaching and learning activities as well as research and development conducted in laboratories and workshop.",""],[1,"37","3","TVET Quality Enhancement and Accreditation Reform","the attractiveness and the quality of delivery and training of TVET will be enhanced through improvement in accreditation, recognition and certification.",""],[1,"37","3","TVET Institution Ranking and Performance-Based Funding System","A ranking system for TVET institutions will be introduced whereby the allocation of funds will be based on a number of components including employability, wage levels of graduates, industrial engagement and the implementation of social initiatives in the rural areas.",""],[1,"343","1","TVET Ecosystem Strengthening and Modernization","In this regard, emerging technologies such as virtual reality (VR), augmented reality (AR) and arti fi cial intelligence (AI) will be leveraged to complement existing hands-on teaching and learning activities as well as research and development conducted in laboratories and workshops.",""],[1,"343","1","TVET Institution Ranking and Performance-Based Funding System","A ranking system for TVET institutions will be introduced whereby the allocation of funds will be based on a number of components in this ranking system including employability, wage levels of graduates, industrial engagement and the implementation of social initiatives in the rural areas.",""],[1,"347","4","TVET Institute Quality Improvement and Industry Collaboration","Increase the quality of TVET institutes and encourage more industry collaboration.",""],[1,"347","6","TVET Promotion Initiative","Enable TVET to become the preferred choice for students.",""],[1,"347","9","National TVET Council Establishment","Establishing a National TVET Council.",""],[1,"347","10","Unified Public and Private TVET Branding Initiative","Promoting a single brand to represent all public TVET institutions and private providers.",""],[1,"347","12","Graduate Employability Ranking System","Introducing ranking system based on employability, wage levels of graduates, industrial engagement and the implementation of social initiatives in the rural areas.",""],[1,"362","4","TVET Governance and Programme Quality Enhancement","During the Plan period, TVET was transformed to develop quality human capital by strengthening governance as well as enhancing the quality and delivery of programmes.",""],[1,"362","4","TVET Rebranding and Attractiveness Campaign","TVET was also rebranded to increase attractiveness, particularly among SPM leavers.",""],[1,"362","5","TVET Quality Assurance Harmonisation and Accreditation Reform","Efforts were undertaken by the Malaysian Qualifications Agency (MQA) and Department of Skills Development (DSD) through the Joint Technical Committee on Single Quality Assurance of TVET to harmonise the accreditation systems and to improve the learning pathways for TVET graduates.","Malaysian Qualifications Agency (MQA) | Department of Skills Development (DSD)"],[1,"362","5","National Dual Training System Mainstreaming","The quality and delivery of TVET programmes were enhanced by mainstreaming the National Dual Training System (NDTS) and Special NDTS.",""],[1,"362","5","Extended TVET Training Duration","Changes were made to the structure of programmes, in which period of training was extended to enable trainees to complete Malaysian Skills Certificate level 1 to 3 and Malaysian Skills Diploma.",""],[1,"362","6","TVET Instructor Quality and Professionalism Rebranding","TVET programmes were rebranded to focus on improving the quality of instructors and recognising TVET professionalism.",""],[1,"378","5","TVET Governance Alignment and Consolidation Reform","efforts will be undertaken to align the diverse systems of TVET institutions to ensure students' pathways to higher education and future careers are streamlined.",""],[1,"378","5","TVET Governance Revamp and Industry Demand Database","The TVET governance will also be revamped by coordinating and consolidating various TVET governance systems, promoting the TVET brand, enhancing quality programmes and creating a TVET database to meet industry demand.",""],[1,"378","6","TVET Ecosystem Framework Reform","A TVET ecosystem framework will be formulated to revamp the current fragmented TVET governance while safeguarding the interests of various stakeholders.",""],[1,"378","6","National TVET Council Establishment","Under this framework, an establishment of National TVET Council will optimise the utilisation of resources and minimise duplication of programmes as well as to coordinate and consolidate various TVET governing systems.",""],[1,"378","9","TVET Programme Quality Enhancement and Accreditation Reform","The quality of programmes at all TVET institutions will be enhanced through accreditation, recognition and certification from related professional and industry lead bodies, locally and internationally.",""],[1,"378","9","TVET Upskilling and Reskilling Expansion","Upskilling and reskilling programmes will be expanded to include micro credentials, industrial attachments, training and cross- fertilisation.",""],[1,"378","9","TVET Professional Status Recognition Pathway","TVET graduates will be provided with the opportunity to acquire professional status by MBOT, thus enabling them to pursue professional career pathways.",""],[1,"378","9","TVET Institutional Ranking and Performance-Based Allocation System","In addition, a ranking system will be introduced to categorise the TVET institutions based on a number of components, including employability, wage levels of graduates, industrial engagement and the implementation of social initiatives in the rural areas.",""],[1,"378","9","Performance Improvement Requirements for Underperforming TVET Institutions","Underperforming TVET institutions will be required to rapidly implement best practices to improve their rankings.",""],[1,"378","10","TVET Database Development Platform","A TVET database will be developed to enable BDA to support effective policy formulation and programme development and delivery.",""],[1,"379","1","Future Talent Development and Labour Market Realignment","The Twelfth Plan will focus on developing future talent by realigning the labour market and improving the quality of education and training programmes.",""],[2,"33","3","TVET Ecosystem Improvement Initiative","Improving technical and vocational education and training (TVET) ecosystem to produce future-ready talent will be introduced as a game changer that can better meet industry demand.",""],[2,"33","3","Emerging Technologies for TVET Teaching and Research","Emerging technologies such as virtual reality, augmented reality and artificial intelligence will be leveraged to complement existing hands-on teaching and learning activities as well as research and development conducted in laboratories and workshop.",""],[2,"37","3","TVET Quality Enhancement and Accreditation Reform","the attractiveness and the quality of delivery and training of TVET will be enhanced through improvement in accreditation, recognition and certification.",""],[2,"37","3","TVET Institution Ranking and Performance-Based Funding System","A ranking system for TVET institutions will be introduced whereby the allocation of funds will be based on a number of components including employability, wage levels of graduates, industrial engagement and the implementation of social initiatives in the rural areas.",""],[2,"343","1","TVET Ecosystem Strengthening and Digital Learning Enhancement","In this regard, emerging technologies such as virtual reality (VR), augmented reality (AR) and arti fi cial intelligence (AI) will be leveraged to complement existing hands-on teaching and learning activities as well as research and development conducted in laboratories and workshops.",""],[2,"343","1","TVET Institution Ranking and Performance-Based Funding System","A ranking system for TVET institutions will be introduced whereby the allocation of funds will be based on a number of components in this ranking system including employability, wage levels of graduates, industrial engagement and the implementation of social initiatives in the rural areas.",""],[2,"343","1","Expansion of TVET Intake, 4IR Courses, and Entrepreneurship Jobs","Among the key outcomes expected are an increase in TVET programme intake from Sijil Pelajaran Malaysia (SPM) leavers and equivalent qualifications, an increase in the number of Fourth Industrial Revolution (4IR) related courses offered and the creation of new jobs through entrepreneurship.",""],[2,"347","4","TVET Institute Quality Improvement and Industry Collaboration","Increase the quality of TVET institutes and encourage more industry collaboration.",""],[2,"347","5","Rural Community Upskilling Programme","Upskill communities in the rural areas.",""],[2,"347","9","National TVET Council Establishment","Establishing a National TVET Council.",""],[2,"347","10","Unified Public and Private TVET Branding Initiative","Promoting a single brand to represent all public TVET institutions and private providers.",""],[2,"347","12","Graduate Employability Ranking System","Introducing ranking system based on employability, wage levels of graduates, industrial engagement and the implementation of social initiatives in the rural areas.",""],[2,"362","4","TVET Governance and Programme Quality Enhancement","During the Plan period, TVET was transformed to develop quality human capital by strengthening governance as well as enhancing the quality and delivery of programmes.",""],[2,"362","4","TVET Rebranding and Attractiveness Campaign","TVET was also rebranded to increase attractiveness, particularly among SPM leavers.",""],[2,"362","5","TVET Quality Assurance Harmonisation and Accreditation Reform","Efforts were undertaken by the Malaysian Qualifications Agency (MQA) and Department of Skills Development (DSD) through the Joint Technical Committee on Single Quality Assurance of TVET to harmonise the accreditation systems and to improve the learning pathways for TVET graduates.","Malaysian Qualifications Agency (MQA) | Department of Skills Development (DSD)"],[2,"362","5","National Dual Training System Mainstreaming","The quality and delivery of TVET programmes were enhanced by mainstreaming the National Dual Training System (NDTS) and Special NDTS.",""],[2,"362","6","TVET Instructor Quality and Professionalism Rebranding","TVET programmes were rebranded to focus on improving the quality of instructors and recognising TVET professionalism.",""],[2,"362","6","eProfiling System for TVET Instructors","The eProfiling System, which was established to collect information on skills and competencies of TVET instructors, registered 33,458 instructors across 675 public training institutions at the end of 2020.",""],[2,"372","8","Education and Training Quality Improvement Measures","Emphasis will be given to raise the quality of education and training programmes, strengthen governance, leverage emerging technology, ensure equitable learning outcomes and address overlap TVET governance.",""],[2,"373","1","TVET Programme Enhancement","TVET programmes enhanced while industry collaboration and enculturation of LLL strengthened",""],[2,"375","3","Teaching Factory Rollout for TVET Institutions","the Teaching Factory model that provides real production or manufacturing environment will be rolled out to more TVET institutions to enable students to use industry equipment in campuses.",""],[2,"375","3","Industry Exposure and Experience Linkages for TVET Students","Industry within the proximity of TVET institutions will be leveraged to provide students with better exposure to the latest technology as well as gain industrial experience.",""],[2,"376","5","TVET Institution Funding Diversification","TVET institutions will also be encouraged to diversify and expand funding sources, which include waqf and endowment.",""],[2,"378","5","TVET Governance Alignment and Consolidation Reform","efforts will be undertaken to align the diverse systems of TVET institutions to ensure students' pathways to higher education and future careers are streamlined.",""],[2,"378","5","TVET Governance Coordination and Consolidation Mechanism","The TVET governance will also be revamped by coordinating and consolidating various TVET governance systems, promoting the TVET brand, enhancing quality programmes and creating a TVET database to meet industry demand.",""],[2,"378","6","TVET Ecosystem Framework Reform","A TVET ecosystem framework will be formulated to revamp the current fragmented TVET governance while safeguarding the interests of various stakeholders.",""],[2,"378","6","National TVET Council Establishment","Under this framework, an establishment of National TVET Council will optimise the utilisation of resources and minimise duplication of programmes as well as to coordinate and consolidate various TVET governing systems.",""],[2,"378","7","TVET Promotion and Buddy Programme","Concerted efforts will be undertaken to promote TVET as a preferred choice for students.",""],[2,"378","8","National TVET Brand Introduction","A single TVET brand representing both public and private TVET providers will be introduced.",""],[2,"378","9","TVET Programme Quality Enhancement and Accreditation","The quality of programmes at all TVET institutions will be enhanced through accreditation, recognition and certification from related professional and industry lead bodies, locally and internationally.",""],[2,"378","9","TVET Upskilling and Reskilling Expansion","Upskilling and reskilling programmes will be expanded to include micro credentials, industrial attachments, training and cross- fertilisation.",""],[2,"378","9","MBOT Professional Status Pathway for TVET Graduates","TVET graduates will be provided with the opportunity to acquire professional status by MBOT, thus enabling them to pursue professional career pathways.",""],[2,"378","9","TVET Institution Ranking and Performance-Based Allocation System","a ranking system will be introduced to categorise the TVET institutions based on a number of components, including employability, wage levels of graduates, industrial engagement and the implementation of social initiatives in the rural areas.",""],[2,"378","9","Performance-Based TVET Funding Allocation","Allocations for TVET institutions will be based on their performance in this ranking system.",""],[2,"378","9","Rapid Improvement Measures for Underperforming TVET Institutions","Underperforming TVET institutions will be required to rapidly implement best practices to improve their rankings.",""]],"99":[[1,"97","2","Virtual Teaching and Experiential Learning Enhancement","virtual teaching and experiential learning will be further strengthened to enhance the learning experience, thus improving the quality of education.",""],[1,"97","2","Education Technology and Learning Materials Innovation","This will drive innovation in the production of education technologies and tools, such as educational applications as well as audio and video materials.",""],[1,"98","8","Digitalisation Support for Private Higher Education Institutions","the private HEIs, particularly MSMEs will be encouraged to utilise existing financing facilities to upgrade and modernise ICT assets as well as digitise teaching content.",""],[1,"348","6","Support for Vulnerable Groups in Remote Learning","Address the issue of vulnerable groups who are unable to participate in remote learning.",""],[1,"348","12","Digital Devices and Complimentary Data Packages for Students","Expanding access to digital devices and complimentary data packages for students from selected groups through a people, private and public partnership approach.",""],[1,"360","6","Digital Learning Platform Expansion in Schools","Several initiatives were carried out to improve teaching and learning by encouraging the use of digital platforms for online learning and expanding access to the virtual learning environment (VLE) in schools.",""],[1,"360","6","DELIMa Continuous Learning Access Support","This platform was used extensively to ensure continuous access to learning during pandemic.",""],[2,"348","6","Support for Vulnerable Groups in Remote Learning","Address the issue of vulnerable groups who are unable to participate in remote learning.",""],[2,"348","12","Digital Devices and Data Package Support for Students","Expanding access to digital devices and complimentary data packages for students from selected groups through a people, private and public partnership approach.",""],[2,"360","6","Digital Learning Platform Expansion","Several initiatives were carried out to improve teaching and learning by encouraging the use of digital platforms for online learning and expanding access to the virtual learning environment (VLE) in schools.",""]],"100":[[1,"372","8","Education and Training Quality Improvement Measures","Emphasis will be given to raise the quality of education and training programmes, strengthen governance, leverage emerging technology, ensure equitable learning outcomes and address overlap TVET governance.",""],[1,"373","1","Education Quality Improvement and TVET Enhancement","the quality of education will be elevated by improving learning outcomes and promoting flexible higher education system.",""],[1,"373","1","Assessment Method Review","The method of assessment will be reviewed,",""],[1,"373","5","Curriculum and Assessment Review for Holistic Learning","The current education system will be continuously reviewed to allow more opportunities for exploratory and project-based learning as well as to provide a holistic assessment of students' performance.",""],[1,"373","5","Enhanced School-Based Assessment Reform","The abolishment of Ujian Pencapaian Sekolah Rendah (UPSR) in 2021 will be a significant milestone towards more holistic assessment based on the enhanced School-based Assessment (PBS).",""],[1,"373","5","Lower Secondary School-Based Assessment System","Thus, the lower secondary students will be assessed based on their performance in the PBS which comprised Classroom Assessment (PBD), Psychometric Assessment (PPsi) and Physical Activities, Sports and Co-curricular Assessment (PAJSK).",""],[1,"373","5","Participation in International Education Assessments","Malaysia will continue to participate in international assessments such as PISA and TIMSS to further improve the quality of education at all levels.",""],[1,"374","2","School Quality Assurance and Inspectorate Strengthening","Quality assurance will be enhanced to ensure effective delivery of teaching and learning in schools.",""],[1,"374","3","Values-Based Teaching Across the Curriculum","good values will be incorporated in all subjects beyond Islamic Education, Moral Education as well as Civic and Citizenship Education.",""],[1,"374","3","Value-Based Teaching for Character Development","Value-based teaching will be applied to inculcate character building and social interaction among students.",""],[1,"374","3","Review of Strategic Plans for Student Values and Character","the related short- and long-term strategic plans will be reviewed to instil values and develop student character holistically.",""],[1,"374","3","Student Participation in Co-Curricular Activities","Student participation in sports, associations and uniform bodies will be promoted to foster greater unity and understanding among students.",""],[2,"373","1","Assessment Method Review","The method of assessment will be reviewed",""],[2,"373","3","Extension of Compulsory Schooling to 11 Years","Compulsory schooling will be extended from six to 11 years by making secondary education compulsory for all Malaysian citizens.",""],[2,"373","5","Curriculum and Assessment Reform for Holistic Learning","The current education system will be continuously reviewed to allow more opportunities for exploratory and project-based learning as well as to provide a holistic assessment of students' performance.",""],[2,"373","5","Enhanced School-Based Assessment System","In this respect, curriculum as well as the assessment standard will be reviewed to nurture critical thinking, creative learning and problem- solving skills.",""],[2,"373","5","Participation in International Student Assessments","Malaysia will continue to participate in international assessments such as PISA and TIMSS to further improve the quality of education at all levels.",""],[2,"375","1","Alternative Assessment Reform for Higher Education Institutions","Measures will be undertaken to strengthen assessment of students in HEIs by introducing an alternative assessment to produce holistic, entrepreneurial and balanced graduates.",""]],"101":[[1,"373","7","Continuous Professional Development for Teachers and Lecturers","the emphasis will be on continuous professional development among school teachers and lecturers at IPG",""],[1,"373","7","English Language Proficiency Requirement for Teachers and Lecturers","All English language teachers will be required to attain at least C1 level in the Common European Framework of Reference for Languages (CEFR)24 whilst lecturers of English language at IPG will be required to obtain C2 level in CEFR.",""],[1,"373","8","Structured Monitoring System for English Language Education Reform","A structured monitoring system will be developed to evaluate the effectiveness of the programmes under the English Language Education Reform in Malaysia: The Roadmap 2015-2025.",""],[1,"373","8","Expansion of CEFR Across All Education Stages","In addition, the CEFR will be expanded to all stages of education.",""],[1,"373","8","CEFR-Aligned English Proficiency Assessment Reform","The evaluation of English proficiency at the end of secondary and primary school levels will be aligned to the CEFR starting 2021 and 2022, respectively.",""],[1,"373","9","Tahfiz Teacher Professional Development and Pedagogy Training","Professional development and pedagogy training will be extended to tahfiz teachers through a standardised teaching curriculum offered by IPG.",""],[1,"374","1","Tahfiz Teacher Training Hub","a training hub to produce qualified and quality tahfiz teachers.",""],[2,"373","7","Continuous Professional Development for Teachers and Lecturers","the emphasis will be on continuous professional development among school teachers and lecturers at IPG",""],[2,"373","8","Structured Monitoring System for English Language Education Reform","A structured monitoring system will be developed to evaluate the effectiveness of the programmes under the English Language Education Reform in Malaysia: The Roadmap 2015-2025.",""],[2,"373","8","CEFR Expansion Across All Education Stages","In addition, the CEFR will be expanded to all stages of education.",""],[2,"373","8","CEFR-Aligned English Proficiency Assessment Reform","The evaluation of English proficiency at the end of secondary and primary school levels will be aligned to the CEFR starting 2021 and 2022, respectively.",""]],"102":[[1,"375","4","Lifelong Learning Programme Strengthening and Innovation","Greater emphasis will be given to strengthen the enculturation and implementation of LLL programmes to develop a learned society.",""],[1,"375","4","Innovative Lifelong Learning Programme Expansion","Focus will be given to develop and enhance innovative LLL programmes in ensuring more opportunities for the rakyat.",""],[1,"375","4","Lifelong Learning Branding and Outreach Campaign","Efforts will also be intensified on promoting impactful branding to ensure better perception of LLL.",""],[2,"375","4","Lifelong Learning Programme Strengthening and Implementation","Greater emphasis will be given to strengthen the enculturation and implementation of LLL programmes to develop a learned society.",""],[2,"375","4","Innovative Lifelong Learning Programme Development","Focus will be given to develop and enhance innovative LLL programmes in ensuring more opportunities for the rakyat.",""],[2,"375","4","Lifelong Learning Branding and Perception Campaign","Efforts will also be intensified on promoting impactful branding to ensure better perception of LLL.",""]],"103":[[1,"272","9","Expansion of Special Education Service Centres","the Special Education Service Centres, which provide screening, intervention, rehabilitation and consultation services to students with SEN and parents, will be expanded to more locations",""],[1,"272","9","GENIUS Kurnia Centre Establishment in Sabah and Sarawak","the GENIUS Kurnia centre will be established in Sabah and Sarawak to ensure children with autism receive early intervention and education",""],[1,"272","9","Basic Disability Facilities in District Schools","at least one school in every district will be equipped with a set of basic facilities for the disabled",""],[1,"377","7","Inclusive Education Access and Learning Environment Improvement","Efforts will be undertaken to ensure equal access to quality education for students with SEN, Orang Asli students and those residing in remote areas.",""],[1,"377","7","Teaching, Learning, and Education Infrastructure Upgrading","Initiatives will include improving teaching and learning as well as providing the necessary infrastructure.",""],[1,"377","8","Education for All Policy Implementation","Accessibility to inclusive and quality education will be improved through the implementation of Education for All Policy including students with SEN.",""],[1,"377","8","Zero Reject Policy for Students with Special Educational Needs","The Zero Reject Policy, which was introduced in 2019, assures that students with SEN are provided placement in either public schools or SEN-ready public schools, depending on their level of disabilities and will be assisted with necessary intervention, rehabilitation and support.",""],[1,"377","9","Special Education Teacher and Aide Competency Enhancement","Quality of education for students with SEN will be improved by enhancing competency of teachers and student aides.",""],[1,"377","9","Special Needs Early Detection and Support System Strengthening","Support systems for these students will be strengthened to improve early detection and intervention.",""],[1,"377","9","Special Education Curriculum and TVET Disability Guideline","a specific guideline covering different categories and levels of disability will be introduced to enhance the implementation of the Special Education Curriculum and TVET programme.",""],[1,"377","9","Assistive Learning Tools Provision for SEN Students","Efforts will be undertaken to provide age-appropriate learning tools such as sensory-processing tools, gym balls and Braille to promote effective intervention programmes.",""],[1,"377","9","Vocational Colleges Expansion for Students with SEN","At the same time, vocational colleges for students with SEN will be expanded.",""],[1,"377","9","Special Needs Co-curriculum Improvement","The co-curriculum for students with SEN will also be improved based on student potential in non-academic fields.",""],[1,"378","1","Special Education Service Centre Upgrading and Expansion","Special Education Service Centres, which provide screening, intervention, rehabilitation and consultation services to students with SEN and parents, will be upgraded to provide better services and expanded to cover more areas.",""],[1,"378","2","GENIUS Kurnia Centre Expansion","the GENIUS Kurnia Centre will be established in every state.",""],[2,"272","9","Expansion of Special Education Service Centres","the Special Education Service Centres, which provide screening, intervention, rehabilitation and consultation services to students with SEN and parents, will be expanded to more locations.",""],[2,"272","9","GENIUS Kurnia Centre Establishment in Sabah and Sarawak","the GENIUS Kurnia centre will be established in Sabah and Sarawak to ensure children with autism receive early intervention and education.",""],[2,"272","9","Basic Disability Facilities in District Schools","at least one school in every district will be equipped with a set of basic facilities for the disabled.",""],[2,"377","7","Inclusive Education Access and Learning Environment Improvement","Efforts will be undertaken to ensure equal access to quality education for students with SEN, Orang Asli students and those residing in remote areas.",""],[2,"377","7","Teaching and Learning Improvement Initiative","Initiatives will include improving teaching and learning as well as providing the necessary infrastructure.",""],[2,"377","8","Education for All Policy for Inclusive Education","Accessibility to inclusive and quality education will be improved through the implementation of Education for All Policy including students with SEN.",""],[2,"377","8","Zero Reject Policy for Students with Special Educational Needs","The Zero Reject Policy, which was introduced in 2019, assures that students with SEN are provided placement in either public schools or SEN-ready public schools, depending on their level of disabilities and will be assisted with necessary intervention, rehabilitation and support.",""],[2,"377","9","Special Education Teacher and Aide Capacity Building","Quality of education for students with SEN will be improved by enhancing competency of teachers and student aides.",""],[2,"377","9","Special Needs Early Detection and Intervention Support Systems","Support systems for these students will be strengthened to improve early detection and intervention.",""],[2,"377","9","Disability-Specific Special Education Implementation Guideline","a specific guideline covering different categories and levels of disability will be introduced to enhance the implementation of the Special Education Curriculum and TVET programme.",""],[2,"377","9","Age-Appropriate Learning Tools for Special Education","Efforts will be undertaken to provide age-appropriate learning tools such as sensory-processing tools, gym balls and Braille to promote effective intervention programmes.",""],[2,"377","9","Expansion of Vocational Colleges for Students with SEN","At the same time, vocational colleges for students with SEN will be expanded.",""],[2,"377","9","Special Education Co-curriculum Improvement","The co-curriculum for students with SEN will also be improved based on student potential in non-academic fields.",""],[2,"377","10","Disabled-Friendly School Facilities Improvement","The accessibility for students with SEN in schools will be enhanced through improvement of disabled-friendly facilities.",""],[2,"378","1","Special Education Service Centre Upgrading and Expansion","Special Education Service Centres, which provide screening, intervention, rehabilitation and consultation services to students with SEN and parents, will be upgraded to provide better services and expanded to cover more areas.",""],[2,"378","2","GENIUS Kurnia Centre Establishment in Every State","the GENIUS Kurnia Centre will be established in every state",""],[2,"378","2","Autism Daily Programme","Each GENIUS Kurnia Centre will provide three programmes to assist the development of children with autism, namely Daily Programme, Family Support Programme and Community Education Programme.",""],[2,"378","2","Autism Family Support Programme","Each GENIUS Kurnia Centre will provide three programmes to assist the development of children with autism, namely Daily Programme, Family Support Programme and Community Education Programme.",""],[2,"378","2","Autism Community Education Programme","Each GENIUS Kurnia Centre will provide three programmes to assist the development of children with autism, namely Daily Programme, Family Support Programme and Community Education Programme.",""]],"104":[[1,"126","1","E&E Manufacturing Ecosystem and Talent Development Initiative","In this regard, efforts will be focused on strengthening manufacturing ecosystems, promoting new technology adoption, uplifting the development of talent as well as enhancing R&D and D&D activities.",""],[1,"126","6","Micro-Credentials Programme Expansion","the various micro-credentials programmes will be expanded based on the Triple Helix model.",""],[1,"126","6","Skills Training in Coding and Data Analytics","Additional skills sets, including software coding and data analytics modelling, will be provided by various training institutions to meet market demand.",""],[1,"126","7","Industry-Led 4IR Skills Development Centres","These include establishing industry-led 4IR skills development centres, incentivising industry to reskill and upskill employees in 4IR areas, and establishing an AI-enabled data platform to facilitate manpower planning.",""],[1,"126","7","4IR Employee Reskilling and Upskilling Incentives","These include establishing industry-led 4IR skills development centres, incentivising industry to reskill and upskill employees in 4IR areas, and establishing an AI-enabled data platform to facilitate manpower planning.",""],[1,"126","7","AI-Enabled Manpower Planning Data Platform","These include establishing industry-led 4IR skills development centres, incentivising industry to reskill and upskill employees in 4IR areas, and establishing an AI-enabled data platform to facilitate manpower planning.",""],[1,"126","7","High-End Manufacturing Design Skills Upgrading","To accelerate the development of the high-end manufacturing industry, employees will be upskilled and reskilled in the field of designing.",""],[1,"126","7","Dedicated Centre for Design Engineer Training","A dedicated centre will be identified to train highly skilled design engineers to meet industry demand.",""],[1,"127","1","STEM Enrolment Expansion Programme","Enrolment in science, technology, engineering and mathematics (STEM) education programmes will be increased in providing talent to support the production of high value and high-tech products in the E&E industry.",""],[1,"127","1","University Software Engineering Alignment Initiative","Programmes in software engineering and programming in public universities will be aligned with industry requirements.",""],[2,"126","6","Micro-Credentials Expansion Programme","the various micro-credentials programmes will be expanded based on the Triple Helix model.",""],[2,"126","6","Software Coding and Data Analytics Skills Training","Additional skills sets, including software coding and data analytics modelling, will be provided by various training institutions to meet market demand.",""],[2,"126","7","Industry-Led 4IR Skills Development Centres","These include establishing industry-led 4IR skills development centres, incentivising industry to reskill and upskill employees in 4IR areas, and establishing an AI-enabled data platform to facilitate manpower planning.",""],[2,"126","7","4IR Employee Reskilling and Upskilling Incentives","These include establishing industry-led 4IR skills development centres, incentivising industry to reskill and upskill employees in 4IR areas, and establishing an AI-enabled data platform to facilitate manpower planning.",""],[2,"126","7","AI-Enabled Manpower Planning Data Platform","These include establishing industry-led 4IR skills development centres, incentivising industry to reskill and upskill employees in 4IR areas, and establishing an AI-enabled data platform to facilitate manpower planning.",""],[2,"126","7","High-End Manufacturing Design Skills Upskilling","To accelerate the development of the high-end manufacturing industry, employees will be upskilled and reskilled in the field of designing.",""],[2,"126","7","Dedicated Centre for Design Engineer Training","A dedicated centre will be identified to train highly skilled design engineers to meet industry demand.",""],[2,"127","1","STEM Enrolment Expansion Programme","Enrolment in science, technology, engineering and mathematics (STEM) education programmes will be increased in providing talent to support the production of high value and high-tech products in the E&E industry.",""],[2,"127","1","University Software Engineering Alignment Initiative","Programmes in software engineering and programming in public universities will be aligned with industry requirements.",""],[2,"141","1","Entrepreneur and Enterprise Capacity-Building","Moving forward, efforts will be undertaken to accelerate the development of strategic and high impact industries and enhance the capacity and capability of entrepreneurs as well as enterprises.",""]],"105":[[1,"131","5","Tourism Talent Attraction and Retention Initiative","initiatives will be undertaken to attract and retain talented individuals by providing a better working environment, quality training and upskilling, as well as adopting international best practices in the food and hospitality industry.",""],[1,"131","5","Industry-Government-Academia Collaboration for Tourism Skills","Collaboration between industry, government and academia will be strengthened to produce talent with the right skills in meeting industry needs.",""],[2,"131","5","Tourism Talent Attraction and Retention Initiative","initiatives will be undertaken to attract and retain talented individuals by providing a better working environment, quality training and upskilling, as well as adopting international best practices in the food and hospitality industry.",""],[2,"131","5","Industry-Government-Academia Tourism Skills Collaboration","Collaboration between industry, government and academia will be strengthened to produce talent with the right skills in meeting industry needs.",""]],"106":[[1,"240","4","Regional Talent Development and Skills Matching Programme","Efforts will be undertaken to intensify talent development and reduce skills mismatch to meet industry demand as well as enhance entrepreneurship development in every region.",""],[1,"240","4","Continuous Revision of Talent Development Programmes","Talent development programmes will continuously be revised, emphasising 4IR knowledge and skills to keep pace with the dynamic requirements of industry.",""],[1,"240","4","Regional Tailored Training Collaboration with HEIs and TVET Institutions","Tailored training concerning the identified key economic activities in each region will be undertaken through collaboration with respective HEIs and TVET institutions.",""],[1,"240","4","Industry Internship Promotion Initiative","Industries will also be encouraged to provide internship programmes.",""],[1,"240","4","Regional Entrepreneurship Development Programme","Entrepreneurship programmes will also be enhanced to spur new businesses and produce more job creators at the regional level.",""],[2,"240","1","Talent and Entrepreneurship Development Programme","Measures will also be undertaken to enhance the provision of basic infrastructure and services, intensify talent and entrepreneurship development as well as promote collaboration for broader production networks.",""],[2,"240","4","Regional Talent Development and Skills Mismatch Reduction Programme","Efforts will be undertaken to intensify talent development and reduce skills mismatch to meet industry demand as well as enhance entrepreneurship development in every region.",""],[2,"240","4","Continuous Revision of Talent Development Programmes","Talent development programmes will continuously be revised, emphasising 4IR knowledge and skills to keep pace with the dynamic requirements of industry.",""],[2,"240","4","Regional Tailored Training Collaboration with HEIs and TVET Institutions","Tailored training concerning the identified key economic activities in each region will be undertaken through collaboration with respective HEIs and TVET institutions.",""],[2,"240","4","Industry Internship Programme Promotion","Industries will also be encouraged to provide internship programmes.",""],[2,"240","4","Regional Entrepreneurship Programme Enhancement","Entrepreneurship programmes will also be enhanced to spur new businesses and produce more job creators at the regional level.",""]],"107":[[1,"371","11","Graduate Bridging and Employability Support Programme","The issue of underemployment of graduates will be addressed through the continuous support for bridging programmes that enhance the employability of graduates.",""],[1,"371","11","Graduate Skills and Thinking Courses Intensification","Courses that focus on creative and analytical thinking, organisational adaptability as well as communication and networking skills will be intensified.",""],[1,"371","11","Graduate Entrepreneurship Nurturing Programme","those with affinity towards entrepreneurship will also be nurtured based on their interest.",""],[2,"371","11","Graduate Bridging Programmes for Employability","The issue of underemployment of graduates will be addressed through the continuous support for bridging programmes that enhance the employability of graduates.",""],[2,"371","11","Graduate Skills and Adaptability Training","Courses that focus on creative and analytical thinking, organisational adaptability as well as communication and networking skills will be intensified.",""],[2,"371","11","Graduate Entrepreneurship Nurturing Support","Besides bridging programmes to gain employment, those with affinity towards entrepreneurship will also be nurtured based on their interest.",""]],"108":[[1,"373","2","Education Access and School Environment Improvement","Efforts to improve learning outcomes will include widening access to education, enhancing teaching and learning as well as improving school environment.",""],[1,"373","2","Preschool Enrolment Incentive Review and Awareness Campaigns","Existing incentives will be reviewed and awareness programmes will be enhanced to increase preschool enrolment.",""],[1,"373","2","ECCE Teacher Qualification Upgrade","The quality of ECCE teachers will be upgraded to improve teaching and learning.",""],[1,"373","2","Mandatory Diploma Qualification for ECCE Teachers","Towards this end, all public and private ECCE teachers will be required to have at least a diploma qualification in ECCE by 2025.",""],[1,"373","2","Expanded Diploma in ECCE Provision","The Diploma in ECCE offered by IPG will be extended to these teachers.",""],[1,"375","6","Preschool Education Quality and Management Improvement Initiative","Efforts will be undertaken to improve the quality and management of preschool education by strengthening collaboration among various service providers.",""],[1,"375","6","Preschool Education Streamlining Initiative","the implementation of initiatives to streamline preschool education will be expedited.",""],[1,"375","6","National Preschool Curriculum and Quality Review","The current national committee on preschool education will be tasked to review the curriculum standard, student outcomes, teaching and learning materials, infrastructure and quality of teachers for all Taman Asuhan Kanak-kanak (TASKA) and TABIKA under KEMAS, JPNIN and JAKOA.",""],[2,"365","13","Early Childhood Education Programmes","Education programmes involving preschools for children aged 4+ to 5+ years old and daycare centres for younger children.",""],[2,"373","2","Education Access and Learning Improvement Measures","Efforts to improve learning outcomes will include widening access to education, enhancing teaching and learning as well as improving school environment.",""],[2,"373","2","Preschool Enrolment Incentive Review and Awareness Campaigns","Existing incentives will be reviewed and awareness programmes will be enhanced to increase preschool enrolment.",""],[2,"373","2","ECCE Teacher Qualification Upgrade","The quality of ECCE teachers will be upgraded to improve teaching and learning.",""],[2,"373","2","Mandatory Diploma Qualification for ECCE Teachers","Towards this end, all public and private ECCE teachers will be required to have at least a diploma qualification in ECCE by 2025.",""],[2,"373","2","Extension of the IPG Diploma in ECCE","The Diploma in ECCE offered by IPG will be extended to these teachers.",""],[2,"375","6","Preschool Education Quality and Management Improvement Initiative","Efforts will be undertaken to improve the quality and management of preschool education by strengthening collaboration among various service providers.",""],[2,"375","6","Preschool Education Streamlining Initiative","the implementation of initiatives to streamline preschool education will be expedited.",""],[2,"375","6","National Preschool Curriculum and Quality Review","The current national committee on preschool education will be tasked to review the curriculum standard, student outcomes, teaching and learning materials, infrastructure and quality of teachers for all Taman Asuhan Kanak-kanak (TASKA) and TABIKA under KEMAS, JPNIN and JAKOA.",""]],"109":[[1,"374","6","Flexible Higher Education System Reform","Concerted efforts will be undertaken to promote a more flexible higher education system.",""],[1,"374","7","Higher Education Entrepreneurship Education Initiative","HEIs will be encouraged to enhance entrepreneurship education to inculcate entrepreneurial values among students.",""],[1,"374","8","Industrial Training Policy Review","The policy on industrial training will be reviewed to ensure optimal industrial exposure for students.",""],[1,"374","8","Professional Qualifications and Certification Promotion","Students will also be encouraged to pursue professional qualifications and certification programmes.",""],[1,"375","1","Alternative Assessment Reform for Higher Education Institutions","Measures will be undertaken to strengthen assessment of students in HEIs by introducing an alternative assessment to produce holistic, entrepreneurial and balanced graduates.",""],[2,"361","2","Work-Based and Virtual Higher Education Programmes","Measures were also undertaken to enhance access to quality higher education by introducing diverse learning and teaching approaches.",""],[2,"361","3","MOOC Credit Transfer in Public Universities","Seven public universities agreed to offer MOOCs with credit transfer.",""],[2,"373","1","Education Quality Improvement and Flexible Higher Education Reform","the quality of education will be elevated by improving learning outcomes and promoting flexible higher education system",""],[2,"374","6","Flexible Higher Education System Reform","Concerted efforts will be undertaken to promote a more flexible higher education system.",""]],"110":[[1,"374","9","Innovative Learning and Teaching Enhancement","the current learning and teaching delivery will be strengthened by incorporating self-determined, peer- oriented, virtual-based and experiential learning approaches.",""],[1,"374","9","Academic Staff Professional Qualification and Certification Programme","Academic staff will also be encouraged to pursue professional qualifications or certification programmes to stay abreast with the latest standards and technology.",""],[1,"374","9","Cross-Sector Academic Mobility Programme","cross-sector academic mobility programmes will be expanded to enrich the knowledge of academic staff.",""],[1,"374","9","Academic Staff Capacity Building and Progress Tracking","Capacity building and progress tracking of academic staff will be enhanced to improve their competency in emerging technologies.",""],[2,"374","9","Innovative Learning and Teaching Delivery Enhancement","the current learning and teaching delivery will be strengthened by incorporating self-determined, peer- oriented, virtual-based and experiential learning approaches.",""],[2,"374","9","Academic Staff Professional Qualification and Certification Support","Academic staff will also be encouraged to pursue professional qualifications or certification programmes to stay abreast with the latest standards and technology.",""],[2,"374","9","Cross-Sector Academic Mobility Programme Expansion","cross-sector academic mobility programmes will be expanded to enrich the knowledge of academic staff.",""],[2,"374","9","Academic Staff Capacity Building and Progress Tracking","Capacity building and progress tracking of academic staff will be enhanced to improve their competency in emerging technologies.",""],[2,"374","10","HEI Infrastructure and Equipment Upgrading Programme","Various measures will be undertaken to upgrade outdated and unsafe infrastructure and equipment to ensure a conducive environment in HEIs.",""]],"111":[[1,"376","3","Higher Education Policy and Legislation Reform","Concerted efforts will be undertaken to review, streamline and formulate relevant policies and legislations that govern the higher education ecosystem to increase the efficiency and effectiveness of HEIs.",""],[1,"376","3","International Student Management Guidelines","Guidelines on Good Practices (GGP) on international students in HEIs will be formulated to improve the management of international students.",""],[1,"376","3","International Accreditation Guidelines for Higher Education","GGP on international accreditation will be developed as an initiative to improve quality and strengthen niche programmes.",""],[1,"376","4","Higher Education Financial Sustainability Strengthening","The financial sustainability of HEIs will be strengthened.",""],[1,"376","6","Student Funding Policy Review and Sustainability Reform","The PTPTN will review its policy on student funding to be more sustainable in the long term, including funding for courses that have high employability to ensure higher loan repayment rate by borrowers.",""],[1,"376","6","Education Loan Repayment Enforcement Measures","The repayment collection strategies will be strengthened to address defaulters and those who have yet to pay their loans, including enforcement of the law, reintroduction of travel bans and data sharing with other government agencies.",""],[1,"376","6","Savings Promotion for Prospective Borrowers","Efforts will be taken to promote higher savings among potential borrowers to reduce the burden of repaying education loans after graduation.",""],[1,"376","6","Alternative Higher Education Financing Initiatives","PTPTN will explore other initiatives for higher education funding such as educational waqf and endowment.",""],[2,"376","3","Higher Education Policy and Legislation Review and Streamlining","Concerted efforts will be undertaken to review, streamline and formulate relevant policies and legislations that govern the higher education ecosystem to increase the efficiency and effectiveness of HEIs.",""],[2,"376","3","Guidelines on Good Practices for International Students in Higher Education Institutions","Guidelines on Good Practices (GGP) on international students in HEIs will be formulated to improve the management of international students.",""],[2,"376","3","International Accreditation Guidelines for Higher Education Programmes","In addition, GGP on international accreditation will be developed as an initiative to improve quality and strengthen niche programmes.",""],[2,"376","4","Higher Education Financial Sustainability Measures","The financial sustainability of HEIs will be strengthened.",""],[2,"376","6","Student Funding Policy Review","The PTPTN will review its policy on student funding to be more sustainable in the long term, including funding for courses that have high employability to ensure higher loan repayment rate by borrowers.",""],[2,"376","6","Education Loan Repayment Enforcement Measures","The repayment collection strategies will be strengthened to address defaulters and those who have yet to pay their loans, including enforcement of the law, reintroduction of travel bans and data sharing with other government agencies.",""],[2,"376","6","Borrower Savings Promotion Initiative","Efforts will be taken to promote higher savings among potential borrowers to reduce the burden of repaying education loans after graduation.",""],[2,"376","6","Alternative Higher Education Financing Exploration","Apart from that, PTPTN will explore other initiatives for higher education funding such as educational waqf and endowment.",""]],"112":[[1,"402","1","STI Talent Development Initiative","It will also nurture quality STI talent to improve R&D&C&I outcomes.",""],[1,"404","4","STI Talent Pool Development Initiative","Malaysia will build a sufficient and competent STI talent pool to meet industry demand.",""],[1,"404","4","STEM Learning Expansion and Awareness Programme","Efforts will be undertaken to increase the supply of quality STI talent, and champion effective and fun non-formal STEM learning.",""],[1,"404","4","STI Communication and Awareness Programme Improvement","The effectiveness of communication and awareness programmes will be improved.",""],[1,"404","5","STI Career Path and Remuneration Improvement","The career path for STI talent including remuneration will be improved to make STI careers the preferred choice.",""],[1,"404","5","STI Occupation Remuneration Scheme Enhancement","schemes for STI related occupations such as researchers, technology transfer officers and research managers will be improved to provide a competitive remuneration package.",""],[1,"404","5","Structured Technology Transfer Professional Capacity-Building Programme","structured capacity-building programmes will be implemented to produce accredited and registered technology transfer professionals.",""],[1,"404","6","STI Talent Public-Private Partnership Strengthening","Public-private partnerships will be strengthened to increase the supply of STI talent.",""],[1,"404","6","Technology Assembly Partnership Programme","The technology assembly programme will be introduced to forge partnerships with companies to bridge the skills mismatch of graduates and the needs of the industry.",""],[1,"404","6","2u2i Industry Readiness Programme","the existing two years in university and two years in industry (2u2i) programme will be leveraged to improve industry readiness of graduates.",""],[1,"404","6","STI Workforce Reskilling and Upskilling Programme","Continuous learning through cross-fertilisation programmes will be further enhanced to reskill and upskill the existing STI workforce.",""],[1,"404","6","Researcher-Industry Scientific Exchange Programme Enhancement","the effectiveness of the Researcher-Industry Scientific Exchange (RISE) programme will be improved by extending the duration and number of public sector secondees.",""],[1,"404","7","STEM Outreach and Non-Formal Learning Programmes","This includes providing a non-formal learning environment through outreach programmes, thematic exhibitions and interactive educational activities.",""],[1,"404","7","Transformation of Science Centres and STI Enculturation Spaces","Non- formal learning centres and STI enculturation spaces, particularly the National Science Centre and the National Planetarium will be transformed to be fully utilised in delivering effective and fun STEM learning.",""],[1,"404","7","Regional Science Centre Expansion","This transformation will also involve the establishment of more regional science centres.",""],[1,"404","7","Innovative and Creative Kids STEM Programme","In addition, innovative and creative kids programmes, which provide hands-on non-formal learning will be introduced to foster creative thinking as well as instil inventing and entrepreneurial skills among school students.",""],[1,"405","1","STI Communications Coordination Committee","The effectiveness of STI communications and awareness programmes will be enhanced through the establishment of a coordination committee that will streamline and integrate all public awareness messages produced by different agencies.",""],[1,"405","1","STEM Education Advocacy Partnerships","Strategic engagements between government agencies, social enterprises and civil society organisations will be intensified to advocate the benefits of STEM education among the rakyat.",""],[1,"405","1","STEM Education Promotion Expansion","promotion of STEM education through various platforms including social media, virtual reality programmes and gamification will be expanded to reach a wider audience.",""],[1,"405","1","Youth Science Ambassador Programme Expansion","Meanwhile, the Youth Science Ambassador programme will be up scaled to encourage the take- up of STEM among youth.",""],[1,"405","1","Science Communicator Training and Ambassador Appointment","More young people will be trained as science communicators and appointed as ambassadors to stimulate and strengthen the development of peer mentoring and aspiration in STEM learning.",""],[2,"404","4","STI Talent Pool Development Initiative","Malaysia will build a sufficient and competent STI talent pool to meet industry demand.",""],[2,"404","4","STI Talent Supply Expansion and STEM Learning Promotion","Efforts will be undertaken to increase the supply of quality STI talent, and champion effective and fun non-formal STEM learning.",""],[2,"404","4","STI Communication and Awareness Programme Improvement","The effectiveness of communication and awareness programmes will be improved.",""],[2,"404","5","STI Career Remuneration Improvement Scheme","The career path for STI talent including remuneration will be improved to make STI careers the preferred choice.",""],[2,"404","5","Structured Technology Transfer Professional Capacity-Building Programme","Furthermore, structured capacity-building programmes will be implemented to produce accredited and registered technology transfer professionals.",""],[2,"404","6","STI Talent Public-Private Partnership Strengthening","Public-private partnerships will be strengthened to increase the supply of STI talent.",""],[2,"404","6","Technology Assembly Partnership Programme","The technology assembly programme will be introduced to forge partnerships with companies to bridge the skills mismatch of graduates and the needs of the industry.",""],[2,"404","6","2u2i Industry Readiness Programme","the existing two years in university and two years in industry (2u2i) programme will be leveraged to improve industry readiness of graduates.",""],[2,"404","6","STI Workforce Reskilling and Upskilling Programme","Continuous learning through cross-fertilisation programmes will be further enhanced to reskill and upskill the existing STI workforce.",""],[2,"404","6","Researcher-Industry Scientific Exchange Programme Enhancement","Meanwhile, the effectiveness of the Researcher-Industry Scientific Exchange (RISE) programme will be improved by extending the duration and number of public sector secondees.",""],[2,"404","7","STEM Outreach and Non-Formal Learning Programmes","This includes providing a non-formal learning environment through outreach programmes, thematic exhibitions and interactive educational activities.",""],[2,"404","7","Transformation of Science Centres for STEM Learning","Non- formal learning centres and STI enculturation spaces, particularly the National Science Centre and the National Planetarium will be transformed to be fully utilised in delivering effective and fun STEM learning.",""],[2,"404","7","Regional Science Centre Expansion","This transformation will also involve the establishment of more regional science centres.",""],[2,"404","7","Innovative Kids STEM Learning Programme","In addition, innovative and creative kids programmes, which provide hands-on non-formal learning will be introduced to foster creative thinking as well as instil inventing and entrepreneurial skills among school students.",""],[2,"405","1","STI Communications Coordination Committee","The effectiveness of STI communications and awareness programmes will be enhanced through the establishment of a coordination committee that will streamline and integrate all public awareness messages produced by different agencies.",""],[2,"405","1","STEM Advocacy Engagements with Government, Social Enterprises, and Civil Society","Strategic engagements between government agencies, social enterprises and civil society organisations will be intensified to advocate the benefits of STEM education among the rakyat.",""],[2,"405","1","STEM Education Promotion through Digital and Interactive Platforms","promotion of STEM education through various platforms including social media, virtual reality programmes and gamification will be expanded to reach a wider audience.",""],[2,"405","1","Youth Science Ambassador Programme Expansion","the Youth Science Ambassador programme will be up scaled to encourage the take- up of STEM among youth.",""],[2,"405","1","Science Communicator Training and Ambassador Appointment Initiative","More young people will be trained as science communicators and appointed as ambassadors to stimulate and strengthen the development of peer mentoring and aspiration in STEM learning.",""],[2,"405","2","Local Technology Talent Development Initiative","A key component of this is to empower more local talent from merely being technology adopters to becoming technology developers and creators, focusing on the development and application of advanced technologies, including deep technology.",""]],"113":[[1,"454","2","Digital Education Enhancement","the country's education system will be further improved by enhancing digital education and strengthening the technical and vocational education and training (TVET) ecosystem.",""],[1,"454","2","TVET Ecosystem Strengthening","the country's education system will be further improved by enhancing digital education and strengthening the technical and vocational education and training (TVET) ecosystem.",""],[2,"454","2","Digital Education Enhancement","the country's education system will be further improved by enhancing digital education and strengthening the technical and vocational education and training (TVET) ecosystem",""],[2,"454","2","TVET Ecosystem Strengthening","the country's education system will be further improved by enhancing digital education and strengthening the technical and vocational education and training (TVET) ecosystem",""]],"114":[[2,"66","7","Business and Higher Education Skills Partnership","Collaboration between businesses and higher education institutions will also be enhanced to address skills shortages.",""],[2,"68","8","Labour Productivity Enhancement through Technology and Skills Upgrading","Labour productivity initiatives will be further emphasised through greater adoption of advanced technology as well as upskilling and reskilling the workforce.",""],[2,"98","1","Industry-Training Institution Customised Training Collaboration","Industries in the manufacturing sector will be encouraged to collaborate with skills training institutions in designing customised training programmes to accommodate their respective needs in moving up the value chain.",""],[2,"98","1","Micro-Credentials Expansion Programme","Efforts to uplift talent will also focus on expanding the provision of micro-credentials programmes to meet the current reskilling and future skills requirements.",""],[2,"98","2","Services Sector Talent Development Strategies","a new SSB will provide the strategies for talent development programmes in the services sector.",""],[2,"98","2","Business and Professional Services Upskilling Blueprint","A holistic blueprint for business and professional services will also be formulated to guide the relevant stakeholders in upskilling the talent with automation tools and advanced technology in embracing 4IR.",""],[2,"98","3","Technology Adoption Financing and Incentive Support","Measures will include enhancing existing incentives and introducing new financing mechanisms for technology adoption.",""]],"115":[[2,"209","7","Quality Education and Skills Training Support for B40 Households","Access to quality education and skills training will be strengthened to increase capacity and capability among the B40 household members.",""],[2,"209","7","Community-Based Early Childhood Education Expansion","ECCE will be further enhanced by encouraging CBOs to provide facilities in areas where such services are lacking.",""],[2,"209","7","Scholarship and Priority Intake Support for B40 Children","Children of the B40 will continue to be given priority for scholarships and intakes into SBP and MRSM.",""],[2,"209","7","Financial Assistance for Skills Training and Higher Education","Financial assistance will be extended to pursue skills training including TVET and higher education.",""]],"116":[[2,"360","7","School Administration Decentralization and Coaching Support","Administration of schools was further decentralised to improve the quality of delivery and governance.",""],[2,"360","12","SISC+ Teacher Coaching for Curriculum Alignment","SISC+ is responsible to coach teachers to ensure dimensions of curriculum, assessment and pedagogy are aligned.",""],[2,"360","13","School Leadership Coaching Programme","SIPartner+ is responsible to coach the school leadership team on effective school administration and management.",""],[2,"375","9","Continuous Professional Development for Education Leaders","Continuous professional development will be maintained to improve leadership quality.",""],[2,"375","9","Structured Training Programme for Education Leaders","Education leaders from schools, JPNs, PPDs and divisions will be trained under a structured programme to improve capacity and capability to manage education institutions.",""],[2,"375","9","National Professional Qualification for System Leaders","the National Professional Qualification for System Leaders (NPQSL)26 programme will be introduced.",""],[2,"375","10","NPQSL Training Programme for System Leaders","NPQSL is a training programme for system leaders to ensure officers appointed at district education officers, state officer and division officers are competent.",""],[2,"376","1","Educational Leaders Qualification Strengthening Programme","Qualification for Educational Leaders (NPQEL)27 programme will also be strengthened and tailored for different types of schools, particularly Orang Asli, special education, religious schools as well as technical and vocational education.",""],[2,"376","2","Parent-Teacher Association School Governance Strengthening","The role of Parent-Teacher Associations (PTAs) will be strengthened to play more active role in supporting the school governance.",""],[2,"376","2","PTA Community and Private Sector Engagement Initiative","Engagements with the broader community, private sector, civil society organisations and education training providers will be spearheaded by PTAs based on programmes identified by schools.",""],[2,"376","2","PTA External Resource Mobilization Support","This empowerment of PTAs will facilitate sourcing of external funding, provision of additional manpower and expertise to improve the quality of schools.",""]],"117":[[2,"373","6","Student Tracking and Early Intervention System","A student tracking system from preschool to upper secondary levels will be developed to monitor the mobility of students throughout the school system.",""],[2,"373","6","Student Support Programmes for At-Risk Learners","student support programmes such as parental and community involvement for poor students and students at risk will be enhanced to ensure students remain in the school system.",""],[2,"373","6","Social and Emotional Support for Students","focus will be given in providing social and emotional support for students as well as assisting those with learning difficulties, in order to build an inclusive school environment.",""]],"118":[[1,"23","3","Future Talent Development","Four catalytic policy enablers, namely developing future talent, accelerating technology adoption and innovation, enhancing connectivity and transport infrastructure as well as strengthening the public service will support the achievement of these themes.",""],[1,"33","2","Future Talent Development through Labour Market, Education and Training Realignment","Hence, the Twelfth Plan will focus on developing future talent by realigning the labour market, education and training.",""],[1,"33","2","Equitable Compensation and Labour Participation Promotion","Among the key initiatives for realigning the labour market are promoting equitable CE and labour participation, as well as strengthening labour market support.",""],[1,"33","2","Labour Market Support Strengthening","Among the key initiatives for realigning the labour market are promoting equitable CE and labour participation, as well as strengthening labour market support.",""],[1,"33","2","Education and Training Quality Enhancement","In addition, elevating the quality of education and leveraging emerging technologies will be the key initiatives to improve the education and training system.",""],[1,"66","7","Business-Higher Education Skills Collaboration","Collaboration between businesses and higher education institutions will also be enhanced to address skills shortages.",""],[1,"68","8","Labour Productivity Enhancement and Workforce Upskilling","Labour productivity initiatives will be further emphasised through greater adoption of advanced technology as well as upskilling and reskilling the workforce.",""],[1,"68","8","Reduction of Dependence on Low-Skilled Foreign Workers","In addition, measures will be taken to reduce dependency on low-skilled foreign workers.",""]],"119":[[1,"272","7","School Infrastructure Upgrading and Rebuilding Programme","efforts will be undertaken to further improve school infrastructure.",""],[1,"272","7","Comprehensive Special Model School Expansion and Upgrade Programme","The number of Comprehensive Special Model School 9 (K9) will be increased, while several existing K9 schools will be upgraded to Comprehensive Special Model School 11 (K11) to provide the remotely located students a complete 11 years of schooling, increasing opportunities to pursue tertiary education.",""],[1,"272","7","K11 Skills Development and TVET Strengthening Initiative","The K11 schools will focus on enhancing skills development by strengthening the TVET programme.",""],[1,"272","7","Student Hostel and Teachers' Quarters Upgrading Programme","Students' hostels, as well as teachers' quarters will be upgraded to provide better access for students and liveable conditions for the teachers.",""],[1,"272","8","Digital Infrastructure Upgrade for Education","Digital infrastructure including internet connectivity will be improved to facilitate better teaching and learning in line with the new norms.",""],[1,"272","8","Provision of Fit-for-Purpose Digital Devices for Students","To narrow the digital divide, 'fit-for-purpose' digital devices will be provided for students from the selected group.",""],[1,"272","8","School and Education Office Network Upgrade","Concurrently, efforts will be taken to upgrade the local area network in schools and education offices and expand MyGov*Net to provide wide area network to education offices.",""],[1,"272","11","Remote Learning Strengthening Initiative","Remote learning approaches will be strengthened to improve learning and teaching processes, which will increase access for students in HEIs and TVET institutions.",""],[1,"272","11","Education Infrastructure Enhancement in Sabah and Sarawak","Infra- and info-structure facilities in Sabah and Sarawak will be enhanced to create a conducive learning",""],[2,"272","2","Education and Training Access Improvement and Industry Collaboration","efforts will focus on improving access to education and training, as well as enhancing collaboration with industry.",""],[2,"272","7","School Infrastructure Upgrading and Reconstruction Programme","efforts will be undertaken to further improve school infrastructure.",""],[2,"272","7","Comprehensive Special Model School Expansion and Upgrade Programme","The number of Comprehensive Special Model School 9 (K9) will be increased, while several existing K9 schools will be upgraded to Comprehensive Special Model School 11 (K11) to provide the remotely located students a complete 11 years of schooling, increasing opportunities to pursue tertiary education.",""],[2,"272","7","TVET Strengthening in K11 Schools","The K11 schools will focus on enhancing skills development by strengthening the TVET programme.",""],[2,"272","7","Student Hostel and Teachers' Quarters Upgrading Programme","Students' hostels, as well as teachers' quarters will be upgraded to provide better access for students and liveable conditions for the teachers.",""],[2,"272","8","Digital Infrastructure Improvement for Education","Digital infrastructure including internet connectivity will be improved to facilitate better teaching and learning in line with the new norms.",""],[2,"272","8","Provision of Fit-for-Purpose Digital Devices for Students","To narrow the digital divide, 'fit-for-purpose' digital devices will be provided for students from the selected group.",""],[2,"272","8","School and Education Office Network Upgrade","Concurrently, efforts will be taken to upgrade the local area network in schools and education offices and expand MyGov*Net to provide wide area network to education offices.",""],[2,"272","10","Higher Education Access Expansion in Sabah and Sarawak","Access to higher education will be enhanced to increase opportunities in human capital development.",""],[2,"272","10","Improvement of Existing Higher Education Institutions in Sabah and Sarawak","Infrastructure, equipment and academic programmes in the existing HEIs in Sabah and Sarawak will be improved according to local needs.",""],[2,"272","11","Remote Learning Strengthening Initiative","Remote learning approaches will be strengthened to improve learning and teaching processes, which will increase access for students in HEIs and TVET institutions.",""],[2,"272","11","Sabah and Sarawak Learning Infrastructure Enhancement","Infra- and info-structure facilities in Sabah and Sarawak will be enhanced to create a conducive learning",""],[2,"274","7","Education, Skills Training, and Healthcare Access Expansion","Efforts will be intensified to improve quality education and skills training as well as access to healthcare services.",""],[2,"275","2","Education and Training Support for Anak Negeri Sabah and Bumiputera Sarawak","Education and training will be pursued to enhance the capacity and capability of these communities, starting from early childhood care and education until tertiary level.",""],[2,"276","8","Enhancement of Islamic Training Programmes at Institut Pengajian Islam dan Dakwah Sabah","The role of Institut Pengajian Islam dan Dakwah Sabah in providing more comprehensive Islamic training programmes will be enhanced by upgrading its physical infrastructure.",""],[2,"276","8","Upgrading of Institut Kemahiran Islam Malaysia Sarawak","The ongoing upgrading of Institut Kemahiran Islam Malaysia Sarawak is expected to be completed in 2023.",""]],"120":[[1,"374","1","Tahfiz Teacher Training Hub","a training hub to produce qualified and quality tahfiz teachers.",""],[1,"374","1","Integrated Tahfiz Curriculum Adoption Expansion","Efforts will also be undertaken to increase the adoption of the Integrated Curriculum Tahfiz among tahfiz schools nationwide to enhance the quality of teaching and learning as well as improve student outcomes.",""],[1,"375","7","Public-Private Tahfiz School Coordination Platform","A coordination platform between the public and private providers of tahfiz schools will be established to promote the adoption of standardised curriculum as well as improve the quality of teachers.",""],[1,"375","7","Tahfiz School Registration as SABK Programme","Efforts will also be undertaken to encourage more tahfiz schools to register as Sekolah Agama Bantuan Kerajaan (SABK).",""],[1,"375","7","Government Assistance for SABK Schools","These SABKs will receive government assistance to enhance the quality of education as well as ensure adherence to the building safety guidelines and provision of proper living conditions.",""],[2,"373","9","Tahfiz Teacher Professional Development and Pedagogy Training","Professional development and pedagogy training will be extended to tahfiz teachers through a standardised teaching curriculum offered by IPG.",""],[2,"374","1","Tahfiz Teacher Training Hub","a training hub to produce qualified and quality tahfiz teachers.",""],[2,"374","1","Integrated Tahfiz Curriculum Adoption Expansion","Efforts will also be undertaken to increase the adoption of the Integrated Curriculum Tahfiz among tahfiz schools nationwide to enhance the quality of teaching and learning as well as improve student outcomes.",""],[2,"375","7","Public-Private Tahfiz School Coordination Platform","A coordination platform between the public and private providers of tahfiz schools will be established to promote the adoption of standardised curriculum as well as improve the quality of teachers.",""],[2,"375","7","Tahfiz School Registration as SABK Programme","Efforts will also be undertaken to encourage more tahfiz schools to register as Sekolah Agama Bantuan Kerajaan (SABK).",""],[2,"375","7","Government Assistance for SABK Schools","These SABKs will receive government assistance to enhance the quality of education as well as ensure adherence to the building safety guidelines and provision of proper living conditions.",""]],"121":[[1,"137","3","Entrepreneur Digital and Advanced Technology Adoption Initiative","In addition, entrepreneurs will be encouraged to continuously innovate by adopting advanced and digital technology, including in their business operation and management.",""],[1,"137","5","Targeted MSME Transformation and Innovation Support","Concerted efforts will be undertaken to increase the contribution of MSMEs to the economy.",""],[1,"137","6","Technology Adoption and Innovation Support Programme","Technology adoption and innovation will be promoted by increasing R&D uptake and strengthening research collaboration between MSMEs, industry experts and academia.",""],[1,"137","6","Targeted Technology Development Financing Support","Targeted assistance and access to financing will be improved for the development and adoption of new technology.",""],[1,"137","6","Automation and Digital Skills Upskilling Programme","Training and development programmes related to automation, digitalisation and 4IR technologies will be strengthened to upskill and reskill talent in supporting technology adoption and automation.",""],[1,"137","7","MSME Digitalisation Roadmap","A national MSMEs digitalisation roadmap will be introduced to drive the adoption of digitalisation.",""],[1,"137","7","MSME Digitalisation Support Mechanism","A mechanism to assist and guide MSMEs in the digitalisation process will be strengthened, among others through the Digital On-Boarding for Micro Businesses (DigitalNiaga), Digital Transformation Acceleration Programme (DTAP), and Warongku initiatives.",""],[1,"137","7","Digital Compass Enhancement","The Digital Compass will be enhanced to help assess MSMEs readiness and capabilities to adopt",""],[1,"138","1","MSME Digitalisation and eCommerce Adoption Support","technology-based business processes and 4IR-related technologies.",""],[1,"138","1","Cyber Health Checks for MSMEs","This will also include cyber health checks to assess the vulnerability of MSMEs to potential threats and attacks.",""],[1,"138","1","Outcome-Based KPI Framework for Digitalisation Funds","Outcome-based KPIs for all funds provided for digitalisation and eCommerce adoption will be established to track the effectiveness of the programmes.",""],[1,"138","1","Digital and Technological Transformation Funding","Out of this total, more than RM20 billion is dedicated to drive the digital and technological transformation agenda.",""],[2,"137","5","Targeted MSME Automation and Digitalisation Assistance","Initiatives to accelerate the creation of high growth and innovative firms will include enhancement of targeted assistance for automation, digitalisation, AI and other 4IR technologies.",""],[2,"137","5","Technology and Digital Entrepreneurial Cluster Development","Focus will also be given to strengthening the ecosystem for future industry start-ups by creating technology and digital entrepreneurial cluster.",""],[2,"137","5","Innovation-Driven Start-Up Financial Assistance Streamlining","Financial assistance will also be streamlined to meet the specific needs of innovation-driven and high-tech start-ups.",""],[2,"137","6","R&D Uptake and Research Collaboration Promotion","Technology adoption and innovation will be promoted by increasing R&D uptake and strengthening research collaboration between MSMEs, industry experts and academia.",""],[2,"137","6","Targeted Technology Adoption Financing Support","Targeted assistance and access to financing will be improved for the development and adoption of new technology.",""],[2,"137","6","Automation and Digital Skills Upskilling Programme","Training and development programmes related to automation, digitalisation and 4IR technologies will be strengthened to upskill and reskill talent in supporting technology adoption and automation.",""],[2,"137","7","MSME Digitalisation Roadmap","A national MSMEs digitalisation roadmap will be introduced to drive the adoption of digitalisation.",""],[2,"137","7","MSME Digitalisation Support and Guidance Mechanism","A mechanism to assist and guide MSMEs in the digitalisation process will be strengthened, among others through the Digital On-Boarding for Micro Businesses (DigitalNiaga), Digital Transformation Acceleration Programme (DTAP), and Warongku initiatives.",""],[2,"137","7","Digital Compass MSME Readiness Assessment Tool","The Digital Compass will be enhanced to help assess MSMEs readiness and capabilities to adopt",""],[2,"138","1","MSME Digitalisation and 4IR Technology Adoption Support","technology-based business processes and 4IR-related technologies.",""],[2,"138","1","Cyber Health Checks for MSMEs","This will also include cyber health checks to assess the vulnerability of MSMEs to potential threats and attacks.",""],[2,"138","1","Outcome-Based KPI Framework for Digitalisation and eCommerce Funds","Outcome-based KPIs for all funds provided for digitalisation and eCommerce adoption will be established to track the effectiveness of the programmes.",""],[2,"138","1","Digital and Technological Transformation Funding","more than RM20 billion is dedicated to drive the digital and technological transformation agenda.",""],[2,"139","3","MSME Corporate Governance Toolkit Development","A corporate governance toolkit for MSMEs will be developed to improve business efficiency and performance through fair practices, good ethics and the right corporate and management culture.",""],[2,"265","9","Bumiputera Entrepreneurship Development Programmes","Initiatives will be undertaken to increase participation of Bumiputera companies through entrepreneurship development programmes.",""],[2,"265","10","MSME Digital Technology Adoption Support","MSMEs will be encouraged to adopt digital technologies in production and business services.",""],[2,"265","10","MSME Digital Readiness Training and Mentoring Programme","Training, mentoring and awareness programmes will be implemented for MSMEs in enhancing readiness to digitalise and compete in the local and global market.",""],[2,"265","10","Local MSME One-Stop Support Centres","One-stop centres with connections to other parts of the country will be established to assist local MSMEs to have better access to funding, facilities and stewardship.",""],[2,"265","10","eRezeki and eUsahawan Programme Expansion","The eRezeki and eUsahawan programmes will be improved and expanded to increase the skills and opportunities of the rakyat in Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[2,"265","10","National Digital Economy and 4IR Council Support","The National Digital Economy and 4IR Council, which was established in 2020 will also be leveraged in solving digitalisation issues in Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[2,"266","5","MSME Capability and Competitiveness Enhancement in Resource-Based Manufacturing","the capabilities and competitiveness of MSMEs in resource- based manufacturing activity will be enhanced with greater adoption of automation and technology.",""],[2,"267","3","Business Registration Regulatory Reform","Business registration regulations will be reviewed and reformed to improve the ease of doing business.",""],[2,"267","3","eCommerce Adoption and Business Digitalisation Support","Businesses will be encouraged to leverage eCommerce platforms and modernise business processes through digitalisation.",""],[2,"267","7","MSME Ecosystem Support Initiatives in Sabah and Sarawak","efforts will be undertaken towards improving access to financing, enhancing resource-based activities, facilitating ease of doing business and boosting the market access of MSMEs.",""],[2,"267","9","MSME Resource-Based Value-Added Production Support","MSMEs in Sabah and Sarawak will be encouraged to utilise domestic natural resources in producing high value-added products and services.",""],[2,"267","9","MSME Participation Strengthening in Resource-Based Industries","In this regard, MSMEs participation in industries such as oil and gas, ecotourism, agri-business and palm oil will be further strengthened.",""],[2,"267","9","MSME Supply Chain Participation in Downstream Activities","The growth of these industries will increase the opportunities for capable MSMEs to participate in the supply chain for downstream activities.",""],[2,"267","9","Entrepreneurship Training and Development Programmes for Resource-Based MSMEs","comprehensive entrepreneurship training and development programmes will be developed.",""],[2,"267","10","Expansion of Business Registration Counters and Innovative Registration Mechanisms","The existing network of business registration counters across Sabah and Sarawak will be expanded and innovative registration mechanisms will be introduced to facilitate business registration.",""],[2,"267","10","District Office Information Dissemination Role for Government and Financial Programmes","Districts offices will be encouraged to act as the focal point to disseminate information on programmes offered by the Federal and state governments as well as financial institutions.",""],[2,"267","11","MSME Product Aggregation and Market Access Mechanism","A mechanism for aggregation of MSME products will be introduced to provide wider market access through utilisation of existing platforms at the district, municipal and local leader levels in small and mid-",""],[2,"268","1","MSME Technology and Digitalisation Sales Expansion","MSMEs will be encouraged to increase the sales of products and services through adoption of technology and digitalisation.",""]],"122":[[1,"23","3","Technology Adoption and Innovation Acceleration","Four catalytic policy enablers, namely developing future talent, accelerating technology adoption and innovation, enhancing connectivity and transport infrastructure as well as strengthening the public service will support the achievement of these themes.",""],[1,"33","4","Digitalisation Acceleration and 4IR Technology Adoption Programme","The digitalisation process will be accelerated and the adoption of advanced technology, particularly the Fourth Industrial Revolution (4IR) technologies, will be promoted in achieving a high technology-based economy.",""],[1,"33","4","R&D, Commercialisation and Innovation Intensification Programme","The talent and skills required to drive both the digital economy and 4IR will be enhanced, while R&D&C&I will be intensified.",""],[1,"33","4","Digital Economy Investment Attraction Initiative","Malaysia will also aggressively attract investment in the digital economy to become the regional leader.",""],[1,"33","5","Digital Connectivity Expansion for Inclusive Development","This policy enabler outlines two game changers in accelerating technology adoption and innovation, which are enhancing digital connectivity for inclusive development",""],[1,"33","5","R&D Alignment for Commercialisation and Economic Growth","This policy enabler outlines two game changers in accelerating technology adoption and innovation, which are aligning R&D towards commercialisation, wealth generation and economic growth.",""],[1,"34","6","Productivity Acceleration and 4IR Readiness Programme","Efforts to accelerate productivity will continue under the Twelfth Plan",""],[1,"34","6","Digital Economy Enabling Environment Initiative","providing an enabling environment for the digital economy",""],[1,"34","6","Research, Development, Commercialisation and Innovation Intensification","intensifying R&D&C&I",""],[1,"34","6","Talent Development for the Fourth Industrial Revolution","developing the required talent",""],[1,"38","1","Commercialisation-Focused Government Research Funding","During the Twelfth Plan, 50% of all Government research funding will be focused on encouraging experimental development with high commercialisation potential.","Economic Planning Unit of the Prime Minister's Department"],[1,"67","4","National Fourth Industrial Revolution Policy Implementation","The implementation of the National Fourth Industrial Revolution (4IR) Policy will be pivotal to boost growth across all sectors.",""],[1,"77","3","Digitalisation and Advanced Technology Investment Promotion","Spur investment in digitalisation and advanced technologies, build niche capabilities, and generate significant multiplier effects.",""],[1,"97","4","Targeted Value Chain Upgrading through Technology Adoption","A more targeted approach will be taken to move the economic sectors up the value chain, producing high value, diverse and complex products through technology adoption.",""],[1,"97","4","Research Management Unit Establishment","The establishment of the Research Management Unit (RMU) will enhance management, facilitation and monitoring of research activities by industry and research institutions.",""],[1,"97","4","Experimental Research and Commercialisation Prioritisation","Experimental research and commercialisation will be prioritised to encourage more demand-driven R&D activities.",""],[1,"97","6","Future Industries Centre of Excellence","a centre of excellence for future industries will be established to coordinate and integrate best practices and research as well as provide support and training",""],[1,"98","3","Technology Adoption Financing and Incentive Support","Measures will include enhancing existing incentives and introducing new financing mechanisms for technology adoption.",""],[1,"98","9","High-Potential Industries Financing and Incentive Mechanism","A new financing mechanism and incentive structure will be introduced to accelerate the development of high potential industries across the economic sectors, particularly in adopting 4IR technologies.",""],[2,"33","4","Digitalisation Acceleration and 4IR Technology Adoption Programme","The digitalisation process will be accelerated and the adoption of advanced technology, particularly the Fourth Industrial Revolution (4IR) technologies, will be promoted in achieving a high technology-based economy.",""],[2,"33","4","Digital Infrastructure and Services Expansion","In doing so, Malaysia will address the issues of insufficient digital infrastructure and services, fragmented governance, widening digital divide, low research, development, commercialisation and innovation (R&D&C&I) capacity and capability, and slow adoption of technologies.",""],[2,"33","4","Digital Economy Investment Attraction Initiative","Malaysia will also aggressively attract investment in the digital economy to become the regional leader.",""],[2,"33","5","Digital Connectivity Expansion for Inclusive Development","This policy enabler outlines two game changers in accelerating technology adoption and innovation, which are enhancing digital connectivity for inclusive development as well as aligning R&D towards commercialisation, wealth generation and economic growth.",""],[2,"34","6","Productivity Acceleration and 4IR Readiness Programme","Efforts to accelerate productivity will continue under the Twelfth Plan, which will contribute to higher labour productivity growth.",""],[2,"34","6","Digital Economy Enabling Environment Initiative","Focus will be given to gearing up for the 4IR, providing an enabling environment for the digital economy, intensifying R&D&C&I as well as developing the required talent.",""],[2,"34","6","Research, Development, Commercialisation and Innovation Intensification","Focus will be given to gearing up for the 4IR, providing an enabling environment for the digital economy, intensifying R&D&C&I as well as developing the required talent.",""],[2,"37","4","Telecommunication Services as a Public Utility","The Government's decision to introduce telecommunication services as a public utility will enhance internet connectivity, enabling the rakyat to have equitable access to more affordable, reliable and quality broadband services.",""],[2,"37","4","Digital Device Access for Students and Vulnerable Groups","In narrowing the digital divide, the Government will also ensure that students and vulnerable groups have access to digital devices.",""],[2,"37","4","JENDELA Digital Connectivity Programme","The implementation of the Pelan Jalinan Digital Negara (JENDELA) will enhance digital connectivity and achieve full 4G coverage in populated areas, as well as enable 100% households' subscription to the internet.",""],[2,"37","4","Digital Nasional Berhad 5G Rollout","The establishment of Digital Nasional Berhad (DNB) will further accelerate the provision of 5G coverage for a better user experience.",""],[2,"343","3","Digitalisation and Advanced Technology Adoption Acceleration","the adoption and application of digital and advanced technology will be accelerated in creating and unlocking new opportunities to reap the benefits of the digital economy as well as to achieve inclusive, responsible and sustainable growth.",""],[2,"344","1","Digital Skills and 4IR Talent Development","The supply of talent and skills required to drive both the digital economy and 4IR technology adoption will be increased, while R&D&C&I will be intensified.",""],[2,"344","1","Digitalisation Mainstreaming for Inclusive Development","Malaysia will also focus on mainstreaming digitalisation for inclusive development and attracting more investments to become the regional champion in the digital economy.",""],[2,"344","1","Digital Economy Infrastructure and Innovation Targets","This policy enabler will realise the targets of 25.5% contribution of digital economy and 10.5% contribution of eCommerce to GDP, 100% 4G coverage in populated areas, wider 5G coverage, 2.5% gross expenditure on R&D (GERD) to GDP, 50 locally accredited sharing economy platforms and 2,000 patent applications by Malaysians in 2025.",""],[2,"349","9","Experimental Development Research Funding Allocation","Ensuring 50% of research funding will be focused on experimental development with high commercialisation potential.",""],[2,"349","10","Research Management Unit for Priority-Aligned R&D&C&I","Ensuring R&D&C&I activities are in line with national priorities with the newly established Research Management Unit (RMU).",""],[2,"349","11","Technology Commercialisation and Transfer One-Stop Centre","Establishing a one-stop centre for technology commercialisation and transfer to scale up home-grown technologies.",""],[2,"349","12","Private Sector R&D and Innovation Investment Support","Increasing investment by the private sector in R&D&C&I and access to alternative financing.",""]],"123":[[1,"149","12","Digital Healthcare Services Digitalisation","Digitalising healthcare services by leveraging emerging technologies.",""],[1,"171","7","Digital Health Technology Support for Healthcare Services","Emerging technologies will be leveraged to support the initiatives for better provision of healthcare services.",""],[1,"173","5","Medicine Track-and-Trace System","track and trace system will be introduced to ensure sufficient supply and efficient distribution of medicines to all healthcare facilities.",""],[1,"173","7","E-Hailing Supported Home Healthcare Services","The e-hailing service will be further leveraged to provide better home healthcare services.",""],[1,"173","7","Expansion of Virtual Clinic Services","Virtual clinic services will be expanded to 250 clinics over five years to provide better access to online medical consultations.",""],[1,"173","7","Patient Mobile Health Application","A mobile application, will be introduced, enabling patients to register for appointments as well as view their medical history and prescriptions online.",""],[1,"173","7","National E-Wallet Payment Expansion for Public Health Clinics","the e-wallet service, which is currently available at four clinics, namely the Klinik Kesihatan Kuala Lumpur, Klinik Kesihatan Cheras, Klinik Kesihatan Seremban and Klinik Kesihatan Putrajaya Presint 18, will be expanded nationwide.",""],[1,"173","8","Integrated Suicide and Fatal Injury Case Database","An integrated database between agencies to record cases of suicide and fatal injuries as a result of suicide.",""],[1,"175","1","Healthcare Service Digitalisation Initiative","more healthcare services will be digitalised to ensure seamless utilisation of information and solve the issue of fragmented health information systems.",""],[1,"175","2","Electronic Medical Record Rollout","The Electronic Medical Record (EMR) initiative will be rolled out in phases to ensure seamless flow of information among healthcare facilities and will create a lifetime health record.",""],[1,"175","2","Environmental Health, Water, Sanitation and Hygiene Information Systems","A number of dedicated information systems will be introduced, particularly on environmental health, water, sanitation and hygiene to gather information for health surveillance and auditing purposes.",""],[1,"175","2","Health Planning Analytics and Precision Medicine Tools","In this regard, big data analytics (BDA), business intelligence and precision medicine will be utilised for better planning and decision-making.",""],[1,"175","2","Integrated Food Safety and Nutrition Information Systems","In addition, an integrated food safety information system and a healthier choice logo system for food and beverages as well as a food composition database will be developed to provide information on food safety, ingredients composition and nutrition content.",""],[1,"175","3","Integrated Health Data Sharing Platform","A virtual platform will be established and integrated with the Malaysian Health Data Warehouse (MyHDW) to allow data sharing across government agencies.",""],[2,"171","7","Digital Technology Support for Healthcare Delivery","Emerging technologies will be leveraged to support the initiatives for better provision of healthcare services.",""],[2,"173","7","Digital Home Healthcare Service Expansion","The e-hailing service will be further leveraged to provide better home healthcare services.",""],[2,"173","7","Virtual Clinic Expansion Programme","Virtual clinic services will be expanded to 250 clinics over five years to provide better access to online medical consultations.",""],[2,"173","7","Patient Mobile Health Application","A mobile application, will be introduced, enabling patients to register for appointments as well as view their medical history and prescriptions online.",""],[2,"173","7","Public Health Clinic E-Wallet Payment Expansion","The e-payment platform will be leveraged to allow e-wallet usage for payment of medical bills in public health clinics.",""],[2,"175","1","Healthcare Service Digitalisation Initiative","more healthcare services will be digitalised to ensure seamless utilisation of information and solve the issue of fragmented health information systems",""],[2,"175","2","Electronic Medical Record Rollout","The Electronic Medical Record (EMR) initiative will be rolled out in phases to ensure seamless flow of information among healthcare facilities and will create a lifetime health record.",""],[2,"175","3","Integrated Health Data Sharing Platform","A virtual platform will be established and integrated with the Malaysian Health Data Warehouse (MyHDW) to allow data sharing across government agencies.",""]],"124":[[1,"33","4","Digital Infrastructure and Services Strengthening Initiative","In doing so, Malaysia will address the issues of insufficient digital infrastructure and services, fragmented governance, widening digital divide, low research, development, commercialisation and innovation (R&D&C&I) capacity and capability, and slow adoption of technologies.",""],[1,"33","5","Digital Connectivity Expansion for Inclusive Development","This policy enabler outlines two game changers in accelerating technology adoption and innovation, which are enhancing digital connectivity for inclusive development",""],[1,"37","4","Telecommunication Services as Public Utility","The Government's decision to introduce telecommunication services as a public utility will enhance internet connectivity, enabling the rakyat to have equitable access to more affordable, reliable and quality broadband services.",""],[1,"37","4","Digital Device Access for Students and Vulnerable Groups","In narrowing the digital divide, the Government will also ensure that students and vulnerable groups have access to digital devices.",""],[1,"37","4","JENDELA Digital Connectivity Implementation","The implementation of the Pelan Jalinan Digital Negara (JENDELA) will enhance digital connectivity and achieve full 4G coverage in populated areas, as well as enable 100% households' subscription to the internet.",""],[1,"37","4","Digital Nasional Berhad 5G Rollout","The establishment of Digital Nasional Berhad (DNB) will further accelerate the provision of 5G coverage for a better user experience.",""],[1,"78","10","Community and Village Internet Centers as Digitalization One-Stop Centers","Leveraging the Pusat Internet Komuniti (PIK) and Pusat Internet Desa (PID) as the one stop centres to drive digitalisation.",""],[1,"348","3","Digital Connectivity and Affordability Improvement","Address the issue of low quality digital connectivity, unaffordable broadband services and digital devices as well as inequitable access.",""],[1,"348","4","Harmonization of Digital Infrastructure Policies and Procedures Across States","Narrow the differences in policies and procedures related to the provision of digital infrastructure among states.",""],[1,"348","5","Gigabit Broadband Access for Out-of-Zone Industries","Address the problem of industries outside selected industrial zones which do not have access to gigabit-speed broadband connectivity to adopt emerging and the 4IR technologies.",""],[1,"348","9","Telecommunication Services Public Utility Regulation","Introducing telecommunication services as a public utility under the Uniform Building By-laws and other relevant laws.",""],[1,"348","10","Digital Infrastructure Investment Promotion","Accelerating digital infrastructure development by encouraging more private sector investment.",""],[1,"348","11","Pay-Per-Use Concept Feasibility Study","Exploring the feasibility of introducing the pay-per-use concept.",""],[1,"393","1","Digital Economy Enabling Environment","Under the Twelfth Plan, efforts will focus on providing an enabling environment for the growth of the digital economy, strengthening the provision of digital infrastructure and services, developing future-ready digital talent as well as positioning Malaysia as the ASEAN digital centre.",""],[1,"393","1","Digital Infrastructure and Services Strengthening","Under the Twelfth Plan, efforts will focus on providing an enabling environment for the growth of the digital economy, strengthening the provision of digital infrastructure and services, developing future-ready digital talent as well as positioning Malaysia as the ASEAN digital centre.",""],[1,"394","5","Enabling Digital Infrastructure Development","Build enabling digital infrastructure",""],[1,"396","6","Nationwide Digital Infrastructure Provision","A nationwide provision of digital infrastructure will enhance digital connectivity as well as unlock new economic potential and opportunities.",""],[1,"397","1","JENDELA Digital Infrastructure Implementation","The implementation of JENDELA will enable the development of a sustainable, inclusive and high quality digital infrastructure as well as a wider fifth generation technology standard (5G) coverage.",""],[1,"397","1","Broadband Network Capacity Expansion through Private Investment","The capacity and capability of the broadband network will be improved by attracting private capital to complement public investments.",""],[1,"397","1","Telecommunication Regulation Streamlining and Utility Reform","In this regard, rules and regulations will be streamlined to facilitate crowding-in private investment and the creation of new network infrastructure.",""],[1,"397","1","Telecommunication Services Public Utility Reform","Steps will be undertaken to introduce telecommunication services as a public utility, similar to water and electricity under the Uniform Building By-laws and other relevant laws.",""],[1,"397","1","Pay-Per-Use Telecommunication Access Feasibility Study","The feasibility of introducing the pay-per-use concept will be explored to increase accessibility and affordability of telecommunication services.",""],[1,"397","2","Digital Infrastructure Policy Realignment","Policies on the planning and provision of digital infrastructure by both the Federal and state governments will be realigned to facilitate investment in state-of-the-art digital infrastructure and to ensure its optimum deployment.",""],[1,"397","2","Digital-by-Default Laws","Meanwhile, digital-by-default laws will be introduced to enable the provision of digital services, protect consumers and promote innovation and competition.",""],[1,"397","2","Universal Service Provision Programme Restructuring","The Universal Service Provision programme will be restructured to increase transparency, flexibility and participation by a wider range of firms in network deployment.",""],[1,"397","2","Innovative Digital Infrastructure Financing Mechanisms","In addition, innovative funding mechanisms will be introduced by both commercial banks and government agencies to encourage more investment in the development of digital infrastructure.",""],[1,"397","3","Digital Infrastructure Development with Emerging Technologies","Digital infrastructure development and provision will incorporate elements of innovation as well as emerging and alternative technologies, while ensuring sustainability, aesthetics and future compatibility.",""],[1,"397","3","Industry Incentives for Emerging Technology Adoption","In line with the National 4IR Policy, incentives will be provided for industries to share best practices, conduct trials and adopt the sandbox approach in encouraging the adoption of emerging and alternative technologies.",""],[1,"397","4","Digital-by-Default Laws for Digital Infrastructure Development","The digital-by-default laws will be introduced to promote the development of digital infrastructure.",""],[1,"397","4","Dedicated Digital Infrastructure Expansion Fund","The dedicated fund to expedite the expansion of digital infrastructure will continue to be allocated to state governments and local authorities while collaboration between Federal and state governments will be strengthened.",""],[1,"397","4","Accelerated Approval Process for Digital Infrastructure Projects","Measures will also be undertaken to expedite the approval process at all levels in addition to soliciting cooperation from industry players to ensure effective implementation of digital infrastructure projects.",""],[1,"397","4","Submarine Cable Landing Station Investment Promotion","Efforts to encourage investments in submarine cable landing stations will be intensified to improve fixed broadband services and promote the establishment of high-end data centres.",""],[2,"348","3","Digital Connectivity and Affordability Improvement","Address the issue of low quality digital connectivity, unaffordable broadband services and digital devices as well as inequitable access.",""],[2,"348","4","Harmonization of Digital Infrastructure Policies and Procedures","Narrow the differences in policies and procedures related to the provision of digital infrastructure among states.",""],[2,"348","5","Gigabit Broadband Access for Industries Outside Selected Industrial Zones","Address the problem of industries outside selected industrial zones which do not have access to gigabit-speed broadband connectivity to adopt emerging and the 4IR technologies.",""],[2,"348","9","Telecommunication Services Public Utility Regulation","Introducing telecommunication services as a public utility under the Uniform Building By-laws and other relevant laws.",""],[2,"348","10","Digital Infrastructure Investment Promotion","Accelerating digital infrastructure development by encouraging more private sector investment.",""],[2,"348","11","Pay-Per-Use Feasibility Study","Exploring the feasibility of introducing the pay-per-use concept.",""],[2,"393","1","Digital Economy Enabling Environment","Under the Twelfth Plan, efforts will focus on providing an enabling environment for the growth of the digital economy, strengthening the provision of digital infrastructure and services, developing future-ready digital talent as well as positioning Malaysia as the ASEAN digital centre.",""],[2,"393","1","Digital Infrastructure and Services Expansion","Under the Twelfth Plan, efforts will focus on providing an enabling environment for the growth of the digital economy, strengthening the provision of digital infrastructure and services, developing future-ready digital talent as well as positioning Malaysia as the ASEAN digital centre.",""],[2,"394","5","Enabling Digital Infrastructure Development","Build enabling digital infrastructure",""],[2,"396","6","Nationwide Digital Infrastructure Provision","A nationwide provision of digital infrastructure will enhance digital connectivity as well as unlock new economic potential and opportunities.",""],[2,"397","1","JENDELA Digital Connectivity Infrastructure Programme","The implementation of JENDELA will enable the development of a sustainable, inclusive and high quality digital infrastructure as well as a wider fifth generation technology standard (5G) coverage.",""],[2,"397","1","Broadband Network Public-Private Investment Mobilization","The capacity and capability of the broadband network will be improved by attracting private capital to complement public investments.",""],[2,"397","1","Telecommunications Regulatory Streamlining Reform","In this regard, rules and regulations will be streamlined to facilitate crowding-in private investment and the creation of new network infrastructure.",""],[2,"397","1","Telecommunications Public Utility Legal Reform","Steps will be undertaken to introduce telecommunication services as a public utility, similar to water and electricity under the Uniform Building By-laws and other relevant laws.",""],[2,"397","1","Telecommunications Pay-Per-Use Access Study","The feasibility of introducing the pay-per-use concept will be explored to increase accessibility and affordability of telecommunication services.",""],[2,"397","2","Digital Infrastructure Planning Realignment","Policies on the planning and provision of digital infrastructure by both the Federal and state governments will be realigned to facilitate investment in state-of-the-art digital infrastructure and to ensure its optimum deployment.",""],[2,"397","2","Digital-By-Default Legal Framework","Meanwhile, digital-by-default laws will be introduced to enable the provision of digital services, protect consumers and promote innovation and competition.",""],[2,"397","2","Universal Service Provision Programme Restructuring","The Universal Service Provision programme will be restructured to increase transparency, flexibility and participation by a wider range of firms in network deployment.",""],[2,"397","2","Innovative Digital Infrastructure Financing Mechanisms","In addition, innovative funding mechanisms will be introduced by both commercial banks and government agencies to encourage more investment in the development of digital infrastructure.",""],[2,"397","3","Digital Infrastructure Development with Emerging Technologies","Digital infrastructure development and provision will incorporate elements of innovation as well as emerging and alternative technologies, while ensuring sustainability, aesthetics and future compatibility.",""],[2,"397","3","Smart City Development Initiative","the development of smart cities will take into consideration these elements in order to address issues pertaining to energy consumption, public transport as well as waste and disaster management.",""],[2,"397","3","Industry Incentives for Emerging Technology Adoption","In line with the National 4IR Policy, incentives will be provided for industries to share best practices, conduct trials and adopt the sandbox approach in encouraging the adoption of emerging and alternative technologies.",""],[2,"397","4","Digital-by-Default Laws for Digital Infrastructure Development","The digital-by-default laws will be introduced to promote the development of digital infrastructure.",""],[2,"397","4","Dedicated Fund for Digital Infrastructure Expansion","The dedicated fund to expedite the expansion of digital infrastructure will continue to be allocated to state governments and local authorities while collaboration between Federal and state governments will be strengthened.",""],[2,"397","4","Accelerated Approval and Industry Coordination for Digital Infrastructure Projects","Measures will also be undertaken to expedite the approval process at all levels in addition to soliciting cooperation from industry players to ensure effective implementation of digital infrastructure projects.",""],[2,"397","4","Submarine Cable Landing Station Investment Promotion","Efforts to encourage investments in submarine cable landing stations will be intensified to improve fixed broadband services and promote the establishment of high-end data centres.",""]],"125":[[1,"376","7","Digital Learning Ecosystem Optimization Initiative","During the Twelfth Plan, initiatives to leverage emerging technology in education will focus on optimising the digital learning ecosystem, strengthening TVET through digital learning and strengthening industry collaboration for greater innovation.",""],[1,"376","7","TVET Digital Learning Strengthening Programme","During the Twelfth Plan, initiatives to leverage emerging technology in education will focus on optimising the digital learning ecosystem, strengthening TVET through digital learning and strengthening industry collaboration for greater innovation.",""],[1,"376","7","Industry Collaboration for Innovation Initiative","During the Twelfth Plan, initiatives to leverage emerging technology in education will focus on optimising the digital learning ecosystem, strengthening TVET through digital learning and strengthening industry collaboration for greater innovation.",""],[1,"376","8","Digital Education Strategy","The Digital Education Strategy will be introduced to accelerate digitalisation in the education agenda.",""],[1,"376","9","Remote Learning Methods and Materials Expansion","The standardised remote learning methods and materials will be extended.",""],[1,"377","1","Online Classroom Audit and Quality Assurance Initiative","The school inspectorate will actively conduct online classroom audits to ensure quality teaching and to improve the participation of students in the virtual classroom.",""],[1,"377","1","Device Assistance for B40 Students","Students from the B40 group will be given assistance in obtaining devices.",""],[1,"377","3","School Digital Infrastructure Provision","Digital infrastructure will be provided to schools to support digital teaching and learning.",""],[1,"377","3","MyGov*Net Expansion for Education Offices","The MyGov*Net, a Government shared initiative by the Malaysian Administrative Modernisation and Management Planning Unit (MAMPU) will be expanded to provide wide area network (WAN) to education offices.","Malaysian Administrative Modernisation and Management Planning Unit (MAMPU)"],[1,"377","3","Broadband Connectivity for Schools Through JENDELA","Schools will be provided with access to broadband connectivity through the Pelan Jalinan Digital Negara (JENDELA) initiative.",""],[1,"377","4","Remote Learning Strengthening for Higher Education Institutions","The HEIs will strengthen remote learning approaches to ensure continuity in learning and teaching.",""],[1,"377","4","Digital Skills Development for Academic Staff and Students","Academic staff and students of HEIs will be equipped with digital skills to further improve learning outcomes.",""],[1,"377","4","Higher Education Quality Assessment Reform","Measures will also be undertaken to improve the Rating for Higher Education Institutions (SETARA) and Malaysian Quality Evaluation System for Private College (MyQUEST), by incorporating technology indicator in the assessment criteria.",""],[1,"398","4","Digital Curriculum Integration","Emerging digital technology will be incorporated into the school curriculum to mould digital talent from an early age.",""],[1,"398","4","School Digital Facilities Upgrade","digital facilities in schools will be upgraded to ensure quality digital education and learning.",""],[1,"398","4","Digital Creativity and Innovation Activities","Adaptability skills, creative thinking and innovative mindset will be nurtured through activities and competitions related to digital making.",""],[1,"398","4","Digital Accountability and Ethics Education","efforts will be undertaken to incorporate digital accountability, ethics and cultural values in building a well-rounded and responsible talent.",""],[1,"398","6","Digital Devices and Data Plan Support for Students","During the Twelfth Plan, digital devices will be provided targeting students from selected groups through a people-private-public partnerships approach.",""],[2,"376","7","Digital Learning Ecosystem Optimization Initiative","During the Twelfth Plan, initiatives to leverage emerging technology in education will focus on optimising the digital learning ecosystem, strengthening TVET through digital learning and strengthening industry collaboration for greater innovation.",""],[2,"376","7","TVET Digital Learning Strengthening Programme","During the Twelfth Plan, initiatives to leverage emerging technology in education will focus on optimising the digital learning ecosystem, strengthening TVET through digital learning and strengthening industry collaboration for greater innovation.",""],[2,"376","7","Industry Collaboration for Innovation Initiative","During the Twelfth Plan, initiatives to leverage emerging technology in education will focus on optimising the digital learning ecosystem, strengthening TVET through digital learning and strengthening industry collaboration for greater innovation.",""],[2,"376","8","Digital Education Strategy","The Digital Education Strategy will be introduced to accelerate digitalisation in the education agenda.",""],[2,"376","8","Expansion of Digital Teaching, Learning and Assessment","Teaching, learning and assessment using digital technology will be expanded by strengthening the capabilities and knowledge of teachers.",""],[2,"376","8","DELIMa Digital Learning Platform Enhancement","The DELIMa, a digital platform for teachers to share educational content and resources will be enhanced.",""],[2,"376","8","Computational Thinking and Computer Science Curriculum Integration","Under this platform, computational thinking and computer science skills that enable students to deal with complex problems will be integrated to the curriculum.",""],[2,"376","9","Standardised Remote Learning Expansion","The standardised remote learning methods and materials will be extended.",""],[2,"376","9","Teacher Training for Remote Learning","Teachers will be trained and",""],[2,"377","1","Online Classroom Audit and Device Assistance Programme","The school inspectorate will actively conduct online classroom audits to ensure quality teaching and to improve the participation of students in the virtual classroom.",""],[2,"377","1","Device Support for B40 Students","Students from the B40 group will be given assistance in obtaining devices.",""],[2,"377","1","Community Monitoring through Parent-Teacher Associations","The PTAs will be empowered to assist community monitoring initiatives.",""],[2,"377","2","RBT Workshop Digital Equipment Upgrade","RBT workshops will be equipped with the required equipment including portable computers and robotics components.",""],[2,"377","2","Hands-on RBT Project-Based Learning Enhancement","Hands-on activities will be emphasised to nurture creativity and innovative learning among students in carrying out projects and PBS.",""],[2,"377","3","School Digital Infrastructure Provision","Digital infrastructure will be provided to schools to support digital teaching and learning.",""],[2,"377","3","MyGov*Net Expansion for Education Offices","The MyGov*Net, a Government shared initiative by the Malaysian Administrative Modernisation and Management Planning Unit (MAMPU) will be expanded to provide wide area network (WAN) to education offices.","Malaysian Administrative Modernisation and Management Planning Unit (MAMPU)"],[2,"398","4","Digital Curriculum Integration","Emerging digital technology will be incorporated into the school curriculum to mould digital talent from an early age.",""],[2,"398","4","School Digital Facilities Upgrade","digital facilities in schools will be upgraded to ensure quality digital education and learning.",""],[2,"398","4","Digital Making Activities and Competitions","Adaptability skills, creative thinking and innovative mindset will be nurtured through activities and competitions related to digital making.",""],[2,"398","4","Digital Accountability and Ethics Integration","efforts will be undertaken to incorporate digital accountability, ethics and cultural values in building a well-rounded and responsible talent.",""],[2,"398","6","Digital Devices and Data Support for Students","During the Twelfth Plan, digital devices will be provided targeting students from selected groups through a people-private-public partnerships approach.",""]],"126":[[1,"395","4","Trusted Data Sharing Platform","A trusted platform for data sharing between the government and the private sectors as well as among government agencies will be developed to enable data-driven decision making.",""],[1,"395","5","Data Governance Lead Body and Big Data Analytics Infrastructure Development","A lead body will be identified to enhance data governance including the development of big data analytics infrastructure, data security and human capital.",""],[1,"395","6","Data Sharing Regulatory Framework","Relevant regulations pertaining to data sharing will be put in place to address concerns relating to system interoperability, cyber security and technical standards.",""],[1,"400","5","Improved Digital Governance and Data Integration","Improved digital governance will provide a comprehensive digital ecosystem for the rakyat to reap opportunities from the digital economy.",""],[1,"400","6","Data Sharing Policy for Digitalisation","A policy on data sharing will be formulated to improve the decision-making process, while protecting data privacy.",""],[1,"400","6","Inter-Stakeholder Data Synchronisation and Sharing Mechanism","Data will be synchronised and shared among different stakeholders to promote data-driven activities including evidence-based decision making.",""],[1,"400","7","National Digital Identification Policy","A national digital identification policy will be developed to provide a comprehensive framework for building trust and security for digital transactions and movement of data.",""],[1,"400","7","Personal Data Protection Act Review","The Personal Data Protection Act will be reviewed to provide greater rights and control over personal data as well as clarity on personal data management using technology.",""],[1,"401","2","National Digital Identification Roll-out","The envisaged roll-out of the NDI in the Twelfth Plan will create value in the economy and further drive the digital inclusion agenda.",""],[1,"408","4","Open Data Sharing Infrastructure Upgrade","Open data sharing infrastructure will be upgraded to enable accessibility of digital information by the public and private sectors, academia and the rakyat.",""],[1,"408","4","Personal Data Protection and Data Sharing Regulatory Strengthening","Meanwhile, guidelines and regulations on personal data protection and data sharing will be strengthened to ensure data is safeguarded against cyber-attacks and unethical uses.",""],[2,"171","6","National Digital Identification Policy","A national digital identification policy will be introduced to enable a trusted, secured and transparent movement of data.",""],[2,"444","5","National Data Governance Framework","a national data governance framework will be established to bolster data sharing",""],[2,"444","6","National Data Governance and Open Data Framework","This framework will incorporate policies, guidelines, legal, and investment measures to obtain the data as well as the monetisation of data shared with the private sector.",""],[2,"444","7","Statistics Act Review to Strengthen Official Statistics","The Statistics Act 1965 is being reviewed to empower the Department of Statistics Malaysia (DOSM) in collecting and coordinating data from the public and private sectors.",""],[2,"446","2","Evidence-Based Policy Development","policy development will be driven by evidence-based data and supplemented with the outcomes from engagements with the rakyat.",""],[2,"446","2","Data Analytics for Policymaking","The usage of data analytics in policymaking will optimise the government's limited resources.",""],[2,"446","2","MyGDX Service Expansion","The expansion of Malaysian Government Central Data Exchange (MyGDX) services will enable the Government to optimise data for better decision-making, thus achieving better outcomes for the rakyat.",""],[2,"446","3","Central Depository System for Programme Coordination","A central depository system will be developed to coordinate information on selected programmes to enhance inclusivity.",""]],"127":[[1,"434","7","Digitalisation of Government Services","Access to government services was expanded through enhancement of digitalisation, including at the local authority level.",""],[1,"435","2","Expansion of Online Government Services","In this regard, an additional 222 mobile applications were developed and uploaded into the Gallery of Malaysian Government Mobile Applications to increase accessibility to public services and expand outreach.",""],[1,"444","2","Expansion of End-to-End Online Public Services","Measures will be undertaken to expand end-to-end online services to provide greater accessibility and convenience for the rakyat.",""],[1,"444","2","Single Sign-On Digital Service Initiative","Single sign-on initiatives will be accelerated to provide seamless online services, including through mobile platforms.",""],[1,"444","2","Land Administration System Expansion and Upgrade","The existing land administration system will be further improved and expanded to states that have yet to adopt the system.",""],[1,"444","2","Spatial Data Sharing System Development","In addition, a system that enables spatial data sharing will be developed.",""],[1,"444","2","Chatbot-Based Customer Service Enhancement","Meanwhile, chatbot applications will be utilised to allow interaction between customers and systems in providing real-time responses to enhance service delivery.",""],[1,"444","2","SISPAA Centralised Complaint Management Upgrade","Moreover, the Sistem Pengurusan Aduan Awam (SISPAA) will be further enhanced by introducing a holistic and centralised system featuring chatbot and smart mobile application as well as cloud computing.",""],[1,"444","3","National Digital Identification Project","the national digital identification project will be introduced in early 2022 to accelerate the realisation of digital governance, promote inclusivity, reduce cost of access to services and enhance service delivery to the rakyat.",""],[1,"444","3","Government Digital Footprint Enhancement","The digital footprint will also be enhanced to ensure integrity, accountability and transparency are not compromised while accessing and sharing government documents online.",""],[1,"444","4","Local Authority Digital Service Delivery Upgrade","Local authorities will be encouraged to leverage on the existing MyGovernment portal to improve service delivery.",""],[1,"444","4","Local Authority Digital Infrastructure and Online Services Upgrade","In this regard, it is important for local authorities to upgrade their digital infrastructure and online services.",""],[1,"444","4","E-Payment Adoption by Federal and State Agencies","Agencies at both the federal and state levels will be encouraged to adopt e-payment methods.",""],[1,"444","4","Cashless Transaction Security Awareness Campaign","In addition, awareness on the security of cashless transactions will be enhanced to gain public trust.",""],[2,"435","2","Expansion of Online Public Services","In this regard, an additional 222 mobile applications were developed and uploaded into the Gallery of Malaysian Government Mobile Applications to increase accessibility to public services and expand outreach.",""],[2,"435","2","MyGovCloud@PDSA Government Cloud Sharing System","In addition, a total of 1,303 systems utilised MyGovCloud@PDSA, which enables facility sharing with secured access across government agencies.",""],[2,"435","2","MyGov*Net Educational Connectivity Upgrade","The MyGov*Net network in 375 educational institutions was upgraded to higher bandwidth with speed up to 100 Mbps, enabling secure and reliable connectivity.",""],[2,"442","9","Government Digitalisation and Public Service Modernisation","In achieving this, government administration and institutional structure will be improved, public service delivery will be enhanced, collaboration and coordination will be strengthened, while digitalisation initiatives will be expanded.",""],[2,"444","1","Public Sector and MSME Digitalisation Acceleration","the Government will take the lead in accelerating digitalisation in the public sector and MSMEs.",""],[2,"444","1","National Digital Economy and 4IR Council","the establishment of the National Digital Economy and 4IR Council will strengthen the digital governance structure and spur growth of the digital economy.",""],[2,"444","1","Public-Private Partnerships for Malaysia Digital Economy Blueprint Implementation","More smart partnerships between the public and private sectors will also be forged to boost the implementation of the Malaysia Digital Economy Blueprint initiatives.",""],[2,"444","2","Expansion of End-to-End Online Public Services","Measures will be undertaken to expand end-to-end online services to provide greater accessibility and convenience for the rakyat.",""],[2,"444","2","Acceleration of Single Sign-On Services","Single sign-on initiatives will be accelerated to provide seamless online services, including through mobile platforms.",""],[2,"444","2","Expansion of the Land Administration System","The existing land administration system will be further improved and expanded to states that have yet to adopt the system.",""],[2,"444","2","Spatial Data Sharing System Development","In addition, a system that enables spatial data sharing will be developed.",""],[2,"444","2","Chatbot-Based Service Delivery Enhancement","Meanwhile, chatbot applications will be utilised to allow interaction between customers and systems in providing real-time responses to enhance service delivery.",""],[2,"444","2","SISPAA Enhancement with Centralised Digital Complaint System","Moreover, the Sistem Pengurusan Aduan Awam (SISPAA) will be further enhanced by introducing a holistic and centralised system featuring chatbot and smart mobile application as well as cloud computing.",""],[2,"444","8","National Cloud Hub Policy","The National Cloud Hub Policy will be introduced to ensure successful cloud adoption.",""],[2,"444","8","Government Hybrid Cloud Development","A government hybrid cloud will be developed, combining both MyGovCloud@PDSA and other cloud services to leverage the latest technology in providing better services in the public sector.",""],[2,"444","8","Government Cloud Storage Promotion","Furthermore, the usage of cloud storage provided by the Government will be promoted in accessing and reviewing documents through the Digital Document Management System.",""],[2,"454","5","Public Service Digitalisation Infrastructure Upgrade","Digitalisation in the public service will be intensified by providing adequate infrastructure",""]],"128":[[1,"435","2","Government Cloud Sharing Platform","In addition, a total of 1,303 systems utilised MyGovCloud@PDSA, which enables facility sharing with secured access across government agencies.",""],[1,"435","2","MyGov*Net Bandwidth Upgrade in Educational Institutions","The MyGov*Net network in 375 educational institutions was upgraded to higher bandwidth with speed up to 100 Mbps, enabling secure and reliable connectivity.",""],[1,"444","8","National Cloud Hub Policy","The National Cloud Hub Policy will be introduced to ensure successful cloud adoption.",""],[1,"444","8","Government Hybrid Cloud Development","A government hybrid cloud will be developed, combining both MyGovCloud@PDSA and other cloud services to leverage the latest technology in providing better services in the public sector.",""],[1,"444","8","Government Cloud Storage Promotion for Digital Document Management","Furthermore, the usage of cloud storage provided by the Government will be promoted in accessing and reviewing documents through the Digital Document Management System.",""]],"129":[[1,"148","8","Advanced Technology for Threat Identification and Enforcement","Expanding the use of advanced technology in identifying threats and enforcement activities.",""],[1,"148","9","National Cybersecurity and Cyber Defence Strengthening","Strengthening national cybersecurity and cyber defence.",""],[1,"169","7","Integrated Cybercrime Sharing Platform","An integrated sharing platform among ATM and other enforcement agencies will be developed to improve cybercrime investigations performance.",""],[1,"169","7","Cybercrime Investigation and Cyber-Defence Capacity Building","The capabilities of personnel will be enhanced to combat cybercrime, focusing on criminal investigation, cyber- intelligence, cyber-defence and online surveillance.",""],[1,"169","7","Cybercrime Enforcement Intensification","The involvement of security and enforcement agencies will be intensified, particularly ATM and PDRM, in curbing cybercrime threats such as the Macau Scam, eCommerce fraud and online gambling.",""],[1,"169","7","Cross-Border Cybercrime Cooperation Arrangements","Cooperation through bilateral and multilateral arrangements will also be strengthened in addressing cross-border cybercrime.",""],[1,"169","7","Public Cybercrime Awareness Campaigns","Advocacy programmes among the public will be intensified to increase awareness of cybercrime and cyber safety.",""],[1,"393","2","Cyber Security Strengthening","Measures will be undertaken to streamline digital governance, accelerate trade through eCommerce, expand the sharing economy and strengthen cyber security.",""],[1,"395","6","Cyber Security Ecosystem Strengthening","The cyber security ecosystem will be strengthened by reviewing and streamlining policies and initiatives across authorities.",""],[1,"396","4","Malaysia Cyber Security Strategy Implementation","the Malaysia Cyber Security Strategy (MCSS) will be implemented to spearhead efforts to manage cyber threats",""],[1,"396","4","Strengthening of the Cyber Security Legal Framework","The cyber security legal framework will continue to be strengthened and the Cyber Security Act will be enacted",""],[1,"408","4","National Cyber Security Response Strengthening","The implementation of the national cyber security response, surveillance and supervision will also be strengthened to protect the nation against any possible cyber threats.",""],[2,"169","7","Integrated Cybercrime Sharing Platform","An integrated sharing platform among ATM and other enforcement agencies will be developed to improve cybercrime investigations performance.",""],[2,"169","7","Cybercrime Investigation and Defence Capacity Building","The capabilities of personnel will be enhanced to combat cybercrime, focusing on criminal investigation, cyber- intelligence, cyber-defence and online surveillance.",""],[2,"169","7","Strengthened Enforcement Action Against Cybercrime","The involvement of security and enforcement agencies will be intensified, particularly ATM and PDRM, in curbing cybercrime threats such as the Macau Scam, eCommerce fraud and online gambling.",""],[2,"169","7","Bilateral and Multilateral Cybercrime Cooperation","Cooperation through bilateral and multilateral arrangements will also be strengthened in addressing cross-border cybercrime.",""],[2,"169","7","Public Cybercrime and Cyber Safety Awareness Campaigns","Advocacy programmes among the public will be intensified to increase awareness of cybercrime and cyber safety.",""]],"130":[[1,"182","2","Ethical and Responsible Digital Media Advocacy Programme","Advocacy programmes on ethical and responsible digital media usage will be expanded at all levels of society to maintain harmony.",""],[1,"182","2","Ethical Digital Media Education in Schools and Higher Education Institutions","Ethical digital media usage will be incorporated in relevant academic programmes as well as co-curricular activities in schools and HEIs.",""],[1,"182","2","Multi-Stakeholder Positive Content for Unity Initiative","In addition, collaboration with celebrities, social media influencers and content creators will be enhanced to not only advocate ethical and responsible media usage but to also create positive and meaningful content on unity.",""],[1,"182","2","Legal Review and Strengthening Against Malicious and Seditious Content","Several provisions in existing laws such as the Penal Code, Sedition Act 1948 and Communications and Multimedia Act 1998 will be reviewed and strengthened to curb the proliferation of malicious and seditious materials as well as fake news that threaten national unity and harmony.",""],[2,"182","2","Ethical Digital Media Advocacy Programme","Advocacy programmes on ethical and responsible digital media usage will be expanded at all levels of society to maintain harmony.",""],[2,"182","2","Ethical Digital Media Education Integration","Ethical digital media usage will be incorporated in relevant academic programmes as well as co-curricular activities in schools and HEIs.",""],[2,"182","2","Positive Unity Content Collaboration Initiative","collaboration with celebrities, social media influencers and content creators will be enhanced to not only advocate ethical and responsible media usage but to also create positive and meaningful content on unity.",""],[2,"182","2","Legal Review and Strengthening Against Malicious Content","Several provisions in existing laws such as the Penal Code, Sedition Act 1948 and Communications and Multimedia Act 1998 will be reviewed and strengthened to curb the proliferation of malicious and seditious materials as well as fake news that threaten national unity and harmony.",""]],"131":[[1,"454","3","Research Management Unit for R&D&C&I Investment Intensification","The newly established Research Management Unit (RMU) will play an important role to intensify investments in R&D&C&I.",""],[1,"454","3","High-Value Research Commercialisation and 4IR Talent Development","Priority will be given to commercialising high-value research, capitalising on emerging technologies and developing the required talent and skills for the digital economy and adoption of 4IR technologies.",""],[1,"454","3","Digital Inclusion Support through Devices and Telecom Utility Designation","Digital inclusion will be enhanced through the provision of digital devices and the designation of telecommunication services as a public utility.",""],[2,"454","3","Research Management Unit for R&D&C&I Investment Intensification","The newly established Research Management Unit (RMU) will play an important role to intensify investments in R&D&C&I.",""],[2,"454","3","Commercialisation of High-Value Research and Emerging Technologies","Priority will be given to commercialising high-value research, capitalising on emerging technologies and developing the required talent and skills for the digital economy and adoption of 4IR technologies.",""],[2,"454","3","Digital Inclusion Support through Devices and Telecom Public Utility Designation","Digital inclusion will be enhanced through the provision of digital devices and the designation of telecommunication services as a public utility.",""]],"132":[[2,"245","8","Rural Fixed Broadband Expansion","Digital infrastructure will be expanded to increase fixed broadband coverage in rural areas, targeting at least 20% of premises with up to 500Mbps.",""],[2,"246","2","Rural Internet and Telecommunications Coverage Expansion","Measures to widen internet and telecommunication coverage will also be undertaken for better connectivity in rural areas.",""],[2,"246","2","Rural Government and Business Service Hubs","PKDs will be leveraged to be the hub for services in rural areas in facilitating the delivery of government and business services.",""],[2,"246","2","Rural Digitalisation Promotion through PIDs","PIDs will be enhanced to promote digitalisation among the rural population.",""],[2,"263","4","Broadband Expansion in Populated Areas and Rural Schools","Besides the expansion of broadband coverage in populated areas, broadband connectivity to rural schools will also be provided.",""],[2,"263","7","JENDELA Broadband Coverage Expansion in Sabah and Sarawak","Broadband coverage in Sabah and Sarawak will be further enhanced under the Pelan Jalinan Digital Negara (JENDELA), to widen the coverage of broadband services in the effort to provide equitable digital opportunities to the population.",""],[2,"263","8","School and Rural Broadband Connectivity Expansion","Measures will be undertaken to improve broadband connectivity in schools, as well as the surrounding areas.",""],[2,"269","11","Rural Broadband Expansion","Broadband coverage in rural areas will be improved to enhance internet connectivity, thus facilitating socioeconomic activities and business expansion through the digital platform.",""],[2,"269","11","Village Community Centre Upgrade and Service Expansion","Pusat Komuniti Desa (PKD) will be upgraded to be hubs for services in rural areas.",""],[2,"269","11","New Community Centre Services","New services will be introduced in PKD, such as courier services, disaster alerts and co-working space.",""],[2,"270","5","Rural Entrepreneur Digitalisation and Online Market Access Programme","Access to online business platforms will be capitalised to elevate competitiveness and capacity of rural entrepreneurs of Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[2,"270","5","Pusat Internet Optimisation for Rural Digitalisation","The 133 Pusat Internet in Sabah and 138 in Sarawak, comprising of PKD, Pusat Internet Desa and Pusat Internet, will be optimised as platforms to promote digitalisation among rural entrepreneurs.",""],[2,"270","5","DesaMall@KPLB Expansion for Rural E-Commerce Transition","The DesaMall@KPLB programme will be expanded to assist rural entrepreneurs in migrating from traditional business methods to online businesses for better market access.",""]],"133":[[1,"144","2","Sports for Active Nation Initiative","Sports will be leveraged as a means to build an active nation",""],[1,"154","3","Sports for Active Nation Initiative","Sports will be leveraged to build an active nation while unity among the rakyat will be enhanced.",""],[1,"160","4","Mass Sports and High-Performance Sports Promotion Programme","Efforts in promoting an active lifestyle were undertaken through the implementation of programmes and initiatives in encouraging mass sports and high-performance sports (HPS).",""],[1,"164","6","Sports-Based Active Nation Initiative","This will be achieved by ensuring national security and sovereignty, enhancing the healthcare service delivery, increasing the supply of quality and liveable affordable housing, leveraging sports in building an active nation as well as strengthening national unity.",""],[1,"178","3","National Sports Vision 2030","The National Sports Vision 2030 (VSN 2030), which is a continuation of the National Sports Policy 2009 will be introduced to set a new direction to build Malaysia as a sporting nation by 2030.",""],[1,"178","3","Sports for Active and Healthy Living Promotion","This will be undertaken by promoting sports for active and healthy living, enhancing sports excellence and developing the sports industry as a new source of growth.",""],[1,"178","7","Sports Culture Promotion and Inclusive Participation Initiative","Concerted efforts will be undertaken to promote sports culture in building an active and healthy society.",""],[1,"178","7","Sports Facilities Accessibility Enhancement","These efforts include enhancing accessibility to sports facilities, strengthening community- based sports bodies and promoting inclusive participation in sports.",""],[1,"178","7","Community-Based Sports Body Strengthening","These efforts include enhancing accessibility to sports facilities, strengthening community- based sports bodies and promoting inclusive participation in sports.",""],[1,"179","2","Inclusive Sports Facilities and Participation Programmes","Specific facilities to cater for the needs of target groups such as PWDs, older persons and women will be provided in the development of new sports facilities and recreational areas.",""],[1,"179","2","Dedicated Sports Participation Programmes for Target Groups","Sports event organisers will also be required to organise dedicated programmes to encourage participation of these target groups.",""],[1,"179","2","Community-Level Sports Activities for Target Groups","Local authorities will also be encouraged to organise more sports activities for these groups at the community level.",""],[1,"179","2","National Action Plan to Increase Women’s Sports Participation","In addition, a national plan of action to boost participation of women in sports will be introduced.",""],[1,"179","2","Women’s Sports Awareness and Safety Support Measures","This plan will not only promote sports awareness among women, but also facilitate specific needs of women, including enhancing safety and security at the sports facilities.",""],[1,"179","2","School and Higher Education Sports Culture Promotion","Intensive efforts will also be undertaken to instil sports culture among children and youth by improving sports programmes and syllabi in schools and HEIs.",""],[1,"179","2","Digital and Event-Based Sports Awareness Campaigns","Awareness campaigns, particularly through digital platforms and sports events will be implemented to encourage sports participation among the targeted groups.",""],[2,"160","4","Mass Sports and High-Performance Sports Promotion Programmes","Efforts in promoting an active lifestyle were undertaken through the implementation of programmes and initiatives in encouraging mass sports and high-performance sports (HPS).",""],[2,"164","6","Sports for Active Nation Initiative","This will be achieved by ensuring national security and sovereignty, enhancing the healthcare service delivery, increasing the supply of quality and liveable affordable housing, leveraging sports in building an active nation as well as strengthening national unity.",""],[2,"178","3","National Sports Vision 2030","The National Sports Vision 2030 (VSN 2030), which is a continuation of the National Sports Policy 2009 will be introduced to set a new direction to build Malaysia as a sporting nation by 2030.",""],[2,"178","7","Sports Culture Promotion and Inclusive Participation Initiative","Concerted efforts will be undertaken to promote sports culture in building an active and healthy society.",""],[2,"179","1","Community-Based Sports Body Strengthening Programme","Community-based sports bodies will be strengthened to conduct sports events and promote an active lifestyle more effectively.",""],[2,"179","1","Sports Body Capacity Building Programme","The management of these sports bodies will be enhanced through capacity building programmes to improve leadership, financial management and administrative skills.",""],[2,"179","1","Community Sports Body Rating System","A rating system will be introduced to promote management excellence among community-based sports bodies.",""]],"134":[[1,"178","3","Sports Excellence Enhancement Initiative","This will be undertaken by promoting sports for active and healthy living, enhancing sports excellence and developing the sports industry as a new source of growth.",""],[1,"179","3","National Athletes Performance and Support Enhancement Initiative","A number of initiatives will be undertaken to ensure national athletes continue to excel in sports competitions.",""],[1,"179","5","High-Performance Sports Athlete Support Enhancement","Support for HPS athletes will be further enhanced to ensure consistent performance.",""],[1,"179","5","Specialised Training and Competitive Tournament Expansion for HPS Athletes","The participation of HPS athletes in specialised training programmes and competitive tournaments at local and international levels will be increased.",""],[1,"179","5","International Standard Tournament Collaboration Mechanism","Collaboration with the NSA will be strengthened to organise more tournaments of international standard to provide national athletes with adequate exposure to compete.",""],[1,"179","5","Dedicated High-Performance Sports Training Facilities","More dedicated training facilities for HPS will be built to increase accessibility and availability of training avenues for athletes.",""],[1,"179","5","School and Higher Education Talent Identification Programmes","In increasing the pool of sports talent, specific programmes to identify talent will be conducted at schools and HEIs.",""],[1,"179","5","State Sports Council Talent Development Empowerment","State Sports Councils will be empowered in identifying and training new talent through the re-establishment of the HPS unit.",""],[1,"179","6","Sports Science and Medicine Services Enhancement","A holistic approach will be undertaken to improve sports science and medicine services to support the overall development of sports.",""],[1,"179","7","Athlete Education and Career Development Support","The wellbeing of athletes will be given greater importance by providing better opportunities in education, career development and social protection.",""],[1,"179","7","Higher Education Collaboration for Athletes","Collaboration with HEIs will be strengthened to provide more opportunities for athletes to pursue higher education.",""],[1,"179","7","Athlete Capacity Building for Sports-Related Livelihoods","Capacity building programmes will be intensified to enable athletes to be involved in sports-related businesses and pursue vocations such as coaches, personal trainers and technical officials.",""],[1,"179","7","Athlete Social Protection Study","A study will be undertaken to introduce social protection for athletes in enhancing their wellbeing, including after retirement.",""],[2,"179","3","National Athletes Performance and Support Enhancement","A number of initiatives will be undertaken to ensure national athletes continue to excel in sports competitions.",""],[2,"179","5","High-Performance Sports Athlete Support Programme","Support for HPS athletes will be further enhanced to ensure consistent performance.",""],[2,"179","5","Specialised Training and Competitive Tournament Expansion","The participation of HPS athletes in specialised training programmes and competitive tournaments at local and international levels will be increased.",""],[2,"179","5","International-Standard Sports Tournament Collaboration","Collaboration with the NSA will be strengthened to organise more tournaments of international standard to provide national athletes with adequate exposure to compete.",""],[2,"179","5","Dedicated High-Performance Sports Training Facilities","More dedicated training facilities for HPS will be built to increase accessibility and availability of training avenues for athletes.",""],[2,"179","5","School and Higher Education Sports Talent Identification Programme","specific programmes to identify talent will be conducted at schools and HEIs.",""],[2,"179","5","State Sports Council Talent Development Empowerment","State Sports Councils will be empowered in identifying and training new talent through the re-establishment of the HPS unit.",""],[2,"179","6","Sports Science and Medicine Services Enhancement","A holistic approach will be undertaken to improve sports science and medicine services to support the overall development of sports.",""],[2,"179","7","Athlete Education and Career Development Support","The wellbeing of athletes will be given greater importance by providing better opportunities in education, career development and social protection.",""],[2,"179","7","University Collaboration for Athlete Higher Education","Collaboration with HEIs will be strengthened to provide more opportunities for athletes to pursue higher education.",""],[2,"179","7","Athlete Capacity Building for Sports-Related Livelihoods","Capacity building programmes will be intensified to enable athletes to be involved in sports-related businesses and pursue vocations such as coaches, personal trainers and technical officials.",""],[2,"179","7","Athlete Social Protection Study","A study will be undertaken to introduce social protection for athletes in enhancing their wellbeing, including after retirement.",""]],"135":[[1,"178","3","Sports Industry Development Initiative","This will be undertaken by promoting sports for active and healthy living, enhancing sports excellence and developing the sports industry as a new source of growth.",""],[1,"180","1","Sports Industry Ecosystem and Sports Tourism Development","Measures will focus on improving the sports industry ecosystem and developing the sports tourism segment.",""],[1,"180","2","Sports Industry Policy and Regulatory Reform","The sports industry ecosystem will be improved by introducing appropriate policies as well as formulating related laws and regulations to facilitate the sustainable development of this industry.",""],[1,"180","2","Sports Industry Coordination Committee","A coordinating committee will be established to promote the sports industry as a new source of growth.",""],[1,"180","2","BDA-Based Sports Industry Decision Support","The BDA approach will be adopted to facilitate informed decision-making in developing the industry.",""],[1,"180","3","Local Sports Entrepreneurship Support Programme","Efforts will be undertaken to encourage local entrepreneurs to venture into sports goods manufacturing and marketing industry as well as sports event management and sports facility management.",""],[1,"180","3","Sports Business Financing and Competitiveness Support","These entrepreneurs will be supported by creating a conducive environment, including providing access to financing, for the businesses to grow and increase competitiveness.",""],[1,"180","3","Sports Trade Exhibition Participation Initiative","The local sports businesses, particularly small and medium enterprises will be encouraged to participate in various local and international trade exhibitions and sports events to showcase their products and services.",""],[1,"180","3","Promotion of Local Sports Products and Services","Promotional activities will also be intensified to create consumer awareness of local sports products and services.",""],[1,"180","3","Private Sector Sports Event Organisation Initiative","Also, the private sector will be encouraged to play a bigger role in organising sports events as a platform to provide business opportunities for local entrepreneurs.",""],[2,"180","1","Sports Industry Promotion and Sports Tourism Development","The sports industry will be promoted as a new source of growth to aid the socioeconomic development of the rakyat.",""],[2,"180","2","Sports Industry Policy and Regulatory Reform","The sports industry ecosystem will be improved by introducing appropriate policies as well as formulating related laws and regulations to facilitate the sustainable development of this industry.",""],[2,"180","2","Sports Industry Coordination Committee","A coordinating committee will be established to promote the sports industry as a new source of growth.",""],[2,"180","2","BDA-Based Sports Industry Decision Support","The BDA approach will be adopted to facilitate informed decision-making in developing the industry.",""],[2,"180","3","Local Sports Entrepreneurship and Market Development Support","Efforts will be undertaken to encourage local entrepreneurs to venture into sports goods manufacturing and marketing industry as well as sports event management and sports facility management.",""],[2,"180","3","Sports Business Financing and Competitiveness Support","These entrepreneurs will be supported by creating a conducive environment, including providing access to financing, for the businesses to grow and increase competitiveness.",""],[2,"180","3","Sports Trade Exhibition Participation Support","The local sports businesses, particularly small and medium enterprises will be encouraged to participate in various local and international trade exhibitions and sports events to showcase their products and services.",""],[2,"180","3","Promotion of Local Sports Products and Services","Promotional activities will also be intensified to create consumer awareness of local sports products and services.",""],[2,"180","3","Private Sector Sports Event Organisation Initiative","Also, the private sector will be encouraged to play a bigger role in organising sports events as a platform to provide business opportunities for local entrepreneurs.",""],[2,"180","4","Sports Tourism Promotion and Event Hosting Initiative","Sports tourism will be promoted to spur growth in the industry by hosting or organising sports events, such as recreational sports, e-sports and extreme sports.",""],[2,"180","4","International Sports Events Attraction Effort","In this regard, efforts will be intensified for international sports events to be held in Malaysia to attract both local and foreign participants and spectators.",""],[2,"180","4","Special Tourism Package Development for Sports Visitors","Special tourism packages will also be developed for them to experience local culture and hospitality.",""],[2,"180","4","Private Investment in International-Standard Sports Facilities","The private sector will also be encouraged to invest in sports facilities that comply with international standards.",""]],"136":[[1,"280","2","Whole-of-Nation Green Growth Implementation Approach","In advancing green growth, the whole-of-nation approach will be adopted.",""],[1,"280","2","Circular Economy Transition Acceleration","In this regard, adoption of the circular economy, which represents a systemic shift will be accelerated to create more responsible businesses and investments as well as to expand the green market and generate new economic opportunities.",""],[1,"280","2","Natural Capital Conservation and Sustainable Use Management","In addition, natural capital will continue to be managed efficiently through conservation and sustainable utilisation, while ensuring equitable benefit sharing.",""],[1,"280","2","Green Growth Enabling Environment and Behaviour Change Support","The green growth will be strengthened by a robust enabling environment and supported by a mindset change as well as behavioural shift of the rakyat.",""],[1,"283","8","Integration of SDGs and ESG Principles into Decision-Making","Integrating the SDGs and environmental, social and governance (ESG) principles into decision-making.",""],[1,"283","9","Green Policy, Regulatory, and Financing Instruments","Enhancing policies, regulations, green financing and economic instruments.",""],[1,"283","10","Circular Economy and Sharing Economy Business Development","Encouraging businesses to develop the circular economy design and the sharing economy model.",""],[1,"288","2","Clean, Green and Resilient Development Agenda","This will be undertaken by implementing a clean, green and resilient development agenda through the whole-of-nation approach.",""],[1,"289","1","Green Growth Policy and Legislative Alignment Review","Several policies and legislation were reviewed to ensure coherence and alignment with current developments and future needs.",""],[1,"289","1","Environmental Governance Capacity Strengthening","Institutional capacities were also strengthened to enable more effective environmental governance.",""],[1,"289","1","Protected Area Conservation and Ecosystem Rehabilitation","There was greater emphasis placed on conserving protected areas and rehabilitating degraded ecosystems of terrestrial and marine areas as well as enhancing the livelihood of indigenous and local communities (ILCs).",""],[1,"289","1","Climate Change Mitigation and Adaptation Actions","Priority was also given to climate change mitigation and adaptation actions as well as disaster risk reduction measures.",""],[1,"291","3","Sustainable Business Adoption and Market Integration Programme","programme included enhancing the adoption of sustainability best practices, identifying new niche markets for sustainable businesses and products as well as integrating Malaysian companies into the global sustainable supply change.",""],[1,"291","4","Stakeholder Collaboration and Monitoring of Environment-Related Initiatives","Various efforts were also undertaken to enhance stakeholder collaboration and monitor the implementation of environment- related initiatives.",""],[1,"294","5","Clean, Green and Resilient Development Agenda","The Twelfth Plan will advance green growth by implementing the clean, green and resilient development agenda through the whole- of-nation approach.",""],[1,"294","5","Circular Economy Transition","The strategies to be implemented include accelerating transition to the circular economy, promoting green and resilient cities and townships, enhancing green mobility, augmenting low-carbon energy and extending producer's responsibility as well as implementing evidence-based and risk- informed actions to increase resilience against climate change and disasters.",""],[1,"294","5","Natural Capital Protection and Green Financing Scale-Up","Emphasis will also be placed on efforts to safeguard natural capital, ensure sustainable utilisation of resources and benefit sharing, strengthening of environmental governance, scaling-up green financing and instilling a sense of shared responsibility.",""],[1,"297","5","Whole-of-Nation Environmental Sustainability Coordination Approach","The whole-of-nation approach is a holistic means to hold all stakeholders accountable in implementing the clean, green and resilient development agenda.",""],[1,"297","5","Sustainable Finance Mobilization for Green Business Practices","the financial services sector will play a key role in channelling capital to accelerate the adoption of sustainable business practices.",""],[1,"298","1","Low-Carbon, Clean and Resilient Development Plan","A low-carbon, clean and resilient development plan that gives due emphasis on planetary health and sustainability as well as resilience of the nation will be implemented to achieve sustained socioeconomic growth.",""],[1,"298","1","Low-Carbon Nation Transition and Circular Economy Acceleration","Focus will be placed on efforts to attain a low-carbon nation status, accelerate transition to the circular economy and share responsibility in reducing pollution.",""],[1,"298","6","Cross-Sector Climate Action and Low-Carbon Transition","The Government will continue to address climate change across all sectors.",""],[1,"298","6","Climate Action Enabling Instruments and Carbon Pricing","the focus will be on developing enabling instruments for climate action, including carbon pricing.",""],[1,"298","6","Private Sector Net-Zero Emissions Commitment Campaign","More private sector companies will be encouraged to declare their aspiration to achieve net zero carbon emissions by 2050.",""],[1,"298","7","Nationally Determined Contribution Roadmap","a Nationally Determined Contribution roadmap will be developed to devise specific mitigation action plans in fulfilling the country's commitment to the Paris Agreement.",""],[1,"298","7","Low-Emission Development Strategy Formulation","Multi-scenario analyses and detailed studies will also be undertaken to formulate long-term low emission development strategies as well as assessing the cost and implications to the country in achieving carbon neutrality.",""],[1,"298","7","Carbon Pricing Feasibility Study","a feasibility study will be conducted on carbon pricing, such as carbon tax and the Emission Trading Scheme.",""],[1,"299","1","Carbon Trading Instruments","carbon trading.",""],[2,"271","3","Green Growth Promotion and Green Initiatives Acceleration","Green growth will be promoted by accelerating green initiatives and conserving natural capital.",""],[2,"271","4","Acceleration of Green Initiatives","Implementation of green initiatives will be accelerated to ensure sustainable, responsible and resilient socioeconomic growth.",""],[2,"271","4","Circular Economy Adoption Along Value Chains","Businesses will be encouraged to implement the circular economy along their value chain, particularly using recycled materials to produce green products.",""],[2,"271","4","Private Sector Energy Efficiency and Renewable Energy Promotion","The private sector will also be encouraged to implement energy efficiency initiatives in their operation and premises, as well as intensify development and utilisation of renewable energy sources, including hydrogen.",""],[2,"271","4","Government Green Procurement Initiative in Sabah and Sarawak","Government green procurement initiative will also be implemented in Sabah and Sarawak as a catalyst in expanding the green market, including the green construction sector.",""],[2,"271","5","Extended Producer Responsibility and Circular Economy Measures","the adoption of the extended producer responsibility approach, user-pay and polluter-pay principles, as well as self-regulation among industries will be further promoted.",""],[2,"271","5","Waste Separation and 3R Intensification","Waste separation at source and the reduce, reuse and recycle (3R) initiatives will also be intensified.",""],[2,"271","5","Green Financing and Economic Incentives for Business Greening","Economic instruments, environmentally motivated subsidies and the existing green financing incentives will be leveraged to support businesses in greening their activities.",""],[2,"280","2","Whole-of-Nation Green Growth Implementation Approach","the whole-of-nation approach will be adopted",""],[2,"280","2","Circular Economy Adoption Acceleration","adoption of the circular economy, which represents a systemic shift will be accelerated",""],[2,"280","2","Natural Capital Conservation and Sustainable Utilisation Management","natural capital will continue to be managed efficiently through conservation and sustainable utilisation",""],[2,"280","2","Green Growth Enabling Environment Strengthening","The green growth will be strengthened by a robust enabling environment and supported by a mindset change as well as behavioural shift of the rakyat.",""],[2,"283","10","Circular Economy and Sharing Economy Business Promotion","Encouraging businesses to develop the circular economy design and the sharing economy model.",""],[2,"288","2","Clean, Green and Resilient Development Agenda","This will be undertaken by implementing a clean, green and resilient development agenda through the whole-of-nation approach.",""],[2,"294","5","Clean, Green and Resilient Development Agenda","The Twelfth Plan will advance green growth by implementing the clean, green and resilient development agenda through the whole- of-nation approach.",""],[2,"294","5","Circular Economy Transition","The strategies to be implemented include accelerating transition to the circular economy, promoting green and resilient cities and townships, enhancing green mobility, augmenting low-carbon energy and extending producer's responsibility as well as implementing evidence-based and risk- informed actions to increase resilience against climate change and disasters.",""],[2,"294","5","Natural Capital Conservation and Environmental Governance Strengthening","Emphasis will also be placed on efforts to safeguard natural capital, ensure sustainable utilisation of resources and benefit sharing, strengthening of environmental governance, scaling-up green financing and instilling a sense of shared responsibility.",""],[2,"297","5","Whole-of-Nation Environmental Sustainability Coordination","The whole-of-nation approach is a holistic means to hold all stakeholders accountable in implementing the clean, green and resilient development agenda.",""],[2,"297","5","Sustainable Finance Mobilization for Green Business Practices","In addition, the financial services sector will play a key role in channelling capital to accelerate the adoption of sustainable business practices.",""],[2,"298","1","Low-Carbon, Clean and Resilient Development Plan","A low-carbon, clean and resilient development plan that gives due emphasis on planetary health and sustainability as well as resilience of the nation will be implemented to achieve sustained socioeconomic growth.",""],[2,"298","6","Cross-Sector Climate Action and Low-Carbon Transition","The Government will continue to address climate change across all sectors.",""],[2,"298","6","Climate Action Enabling Instruments and Carbon Pricing","the focus will be on developing enabling instruments for climate action, including carbon pricing.",""],[2,"298","6","Private Sector Net Zero Carbon Commitment Promotion","More private sector companies will be encouraged to declare their aspiration to achieve net zero carbon emissions by 2050.",""],[2,"302","1","Circular Economy Transition","The circular economy will be achieved through improved product design and manufacturing, innovative sharing economy models2 and enhanced recycling mechanisms.",""],[2,"315","1","Clean, Green and Resilient Development Agenda","The Twelfth Plan will advance green growth by implementing the clean, green and resilient development agenda through the whole-of-nation approach.",""]],"137":[[1,"32","3","ESG-Oriented Green Economy Investment Promotion","Private sector investments particularly with environmental, social and governance (ESG) elements will be encouraged to support green economy agenda.",""],[1,"32","6","National Green Growth Transition","The next five years will see a nationwide shift to more sustainable economic practices and lifestyles that value natural endowments and environmental health.",""],[1,"32","6","Low-Carbon Nation Responsibility Sharing","the need to share responsibility in moving towards a low-carbon nation will be emphasised, while more equal benefit sharing from the utilisation of natural resources will be promoted.",""],[1,"70","4","Green Economy Economic Model","an economic model on the green economy will be introduced to complement existing macroeconomic planning and impact analysis",""],[1,"70","4","Socioeconomic Impact Assessment for Resource Use","the assessment of socioeconomic impact on utilisation of limited resources such as water, energy, land use and raw materials will be conducted to support the formulation of development policies",""],[1,"77","4","Green Economy Investment Prioritization","Implementing the green economy agenda by prioritising environmental, social and governance (ESG) elements in investment.",""],[2,"32","3","Green Economy ESG Investment Promotion","Private sector investments particularly with environmental, social and governance (ESG) elements will be encouraged to support green economy agenda.",""],[2,"32","6","Green Growth and Sustainable Lifestyles Transition","The next five years will see a nationwide shift to more sustainable economic practices and lifestyles that value natural endowments and environmental health.",""],[2,"32","6","Low-Carbon Nation Responsibility Sharing Initiative","the need to share responsibility in moving towards a low-carbon nation will be emphasised",""]],"138":[[1,"32","7","Circular Economy Transition","Two game changers will be implemented under Theme 3, namely embracing the circular economy",""],[1,"37","1","Circular Economy Transition Framework","the circular economy model will be embraced.",""],[1,"94","1","Green Practices Scaling for Resource and Environmental Management","Green practices will also be scaled up in managing resources and environmental issues",""],[1,"96","7","Reuse, Waste Reduction, and Waste Prevention Initiatives","Emphasises on putting resources back into environmental and economic systems through reuse end waste and waste prevention initiatives, thus reducing material loss.",""],[1,"99","6","Acceleration of Green Practices Adoption Across Industries","focus will be given in accelerating the adoption of green practices among industries and enhancing the related implementation mechanisms.",""],[1,"99","7","Industrial Green Practices Adoption Programme","Industries will be encouraged to accelerate the adoption and implementation of green practices, particularly sustainable consumption and production (SCP) practices.",""],[1,"99","7","Green Public Procurement Expansion","The expansion of green procurement initiatives will increase demand for green products and services, and catalyse the industries to shift towards green practices.",""],[1,"99","7","Local Green Product Procurement Initiative","Industries will be urged to procure and utilise local green products and services, which will contribute in expanding the green market.",""],[1,"99","7","Circular Economy Implementation Across Value Chains","In addition, industries will be encouraged to implement the circular economy concept throughout the products and services value chain.",""],[1,"99","7","Triple Helix Green R&D Collaboration","The triple helix collaboration in R&D will be strengthened to increase innovation and commercialisation of green products as well as transfer best practices into mass-production for higher productivity.",""],[2,"96","7","Reuse, Waste Reduction, and Waste Prevention Initiatives","Emphasises on putting resources back into environmental and economic systems through reuse end waste and waste prevention initiatives, thus reducing material loss.",""],[2,"99","6","Acceleration of Green Practices Adoption Across Industries","focus will be given in accelerating the adoption of green practices among industries and enhancing the related implementation mechanisms.",""],[2,"99","6","Green Practices Implementation Mechanism Enhancement","focus will be given in accelerating the adoption of green practices among industries and enhancing the related implementation mechanisms.",""],[2,"99","7","Green Practices Adoption and Sustainable Consumption and Production Promotion","Industries will be encouraged to accelerate the adoption and implementation of green practices, particularly sustainable consumption and production (SCP) practices.",""],[2,"99","7","Green Procurement Expansion Initiative","The expansion of green procurement initiatives will increase demand for green products and services, and catalyse the industries to shift towards green practices.",""],[2,"99","7","Circular Economy Implementation Across Product and Service Value Chains","In addition, industries will be encouraged to implement the circular economy concept throughout the products and services value chain.",""],[2,"99","7","Triple Helix Green R&D Collaboration Strengthening","The triple helix collaboration in R&D will be strengthened to increase innovation and commercialisation of green products as well as transfer best practices into mass-production for higher productivity.",""],[2,"100","1","Green Agriculture Practices Adoption Initiative","Efforts to inculcate green practices in the agriculture sector will be intensified by encouraging farmers to adopt good agriculture practices such as myGAP, MSPO and Malaysian Organic (myOrganic).",""],[2,"100","1","Contract Farming Procurement for Green Practices","In addition, agriculture procurement for contract farming will be leveraged to promote adoption of green practices.",""],[2,"100","1","Smart and Environment-Friendly Farming Support","This initiative will enable agricultural cooperatives and associations to facilitate farmers in adopting smart farming and environment-friendly farming practices.",""]],"139":[[1,"151","11","Green City Action Plan Expansion","Promoting sustainable cities by extending the Green City Action Plan (GCAP).",""],[1,"177","5","Community Adoption of National Liveability Policies","communities will be encouraged to adopt best practices under the National Community Policy, National Cleanliness Policy and Separation at Source to enhance liveability",""],[1,"178","1","National Community Policy Rollout","The NCP initiatives will be rolled out nationwide to encourage communities to be more active in keeping the surroundings safe and clean.",""],[1,"178","1","Community Skills Development for Local Management Bodies","The local communities and residential management bodies will be equipped with the necessary skills to undertake and organise community programmes effectively.",""],[1,"178","1","Strata Management Act Amendment","The roles of joint management bodies and management corporations will be strengthened by amending the Strata Management Act 2013.",""],[1,"178","2","Expansion of Best Practices under the National Cleanliness Policy and Separation at Source","A more conducive living environment will be provided through the expansion of best practices as outlined in the NCP, National Cleanliness Policy and Separation at Source.",""],[1,"178","2","Universal Design Adoption in Housing Projects","Private developers will be encouraged to adopt the universal design concept in housing projects to cater for the needs of specific target groups, particularly PWDs and older persons.",""],[1,"178","2","Environment-Friendly Public Facilities and Green Space Development","Local authorities will also be encouraged to build more environment-friendly facilities, including public parks and recreational spaces, particularly in high-density residential areas.",""],[1,"242","1","Green City Action Plan Expansion","Specific measures will be undertaken to create liveable towns and cities in the subregions.",""],[2,"244","6","Green City Action Plan Implementation","Green initiatives in cities will also be accelerated through the implementation of the Green City Action Plan under the IMT-GT and BIMP-EAGA platforms.",""],[2,"244","7","Green Mobility Promotion and Public Transport Improvement","The adoption of the green mobility approach to facilitate the movement of people via public transport and active mobility will be promoted.",""],[2,"244","8","Urban Green and Blue Space Expansion","Green and blue spaces, such as recreational parks, urban forests and lakes, will be expanded to improve microclimate and enhance biodiversity in urban areas.",""],[2,"244","8","Urban Biodiversity Action Plan","An action plan for urban biodiversity will be developed to guide local authorities in enhancing liveability.",""],[2,"244","8","Endemic Plant Urban Greening and Community Farming Initiative","Developers of residential and commercial projects will be encouraged to revive the green and blue spaces with endemic plant species as well as facilitate community-based urban farming.",""],[2,"270","7","CCMP Action Plan Implementation for Kota Kinabalu and Kuching","Focus will be given to improve the competitiveness of major cities through the implementation of action plans identified under the CCMP for Kota Kinabalu and Kuching.",""],[2,"270","7","Urban Ecosystem Improvement for Liveability","Meanwhile, the efficiency of the urban ecosystem will be enhanced to promote liveability in the major cities through better access to digital infrastructure, affordable housing and entrepreneurial opportunities.",""],[2,"271","2","Green City Action Plan Implementation","Measures will be undertaken to enhance the liveability of cities and ecological resilience of Sabah and Sarawak.",""]],"140":[[1,"244","3","Green and Resilient Urban Development","Green and resilient urban development will be prioritised to address environmental issues and climate change as well as promote efficient usage of resources.",""],[1,"244","3","Urban Waste Management Strengthening","efforts will be intensified to strengthen waste management, increase energy efficiency, promote green mobility and enhance biodiversity.",""],[1,"244","3","Urban Energy Efficiency Improvement","efforts will be intensified to strengthen waste management, increase energy efficiency, promote green mobility and enhance biodiversity.",""],[1,"244","4","Waste Separation at Source and 3R Initiative","Waste will be managed holistically and sustainably by enforcing waste separation at source and intensifying the reduce, reuse and recycle (3R) initiative.",""],[1,"244","4","Waste Separation and Recycling Facilities Enhancement","In supporting this, facilities for waste separation and recycling will be enhanced, particularly in residential, institutional and commercial areas.",""],[1,"244","4","Single-Use Plastics Reduction Measures","Additionally, efforts will be strengthened to reduce single-use plastics, especially at",""],[1,"244","6","Green and Resilient City Framework and Certification Adoption","Focus will be given to the adoption of a green and resilient city framework and certification to enhance energy efficiency and resilience of cities.",""],[1,"244","6","Green City Action Plan Implementation","Green initiatives in cities will also be accelerated through the implementation of the Green City Action Plan under the IMT-GT and BIMP-EAGA platforms.",""],[2,"244","3","Green and Resilient Urban Development Initiative","Green and resilient urban development will be prioritised to address environmental issues and climate change as well as promote efficient usage of resources.",""],[2,"244","3","Urban Waste Management Strengthening","In addition, efforts will be intensified to strengthen waste management, increase energy efficiency, promote green mobility and enhance biodiversity.",""],[2,"244","3","Urban Energy Efficiency and Green Mobility Promotion","In addition, efforts will be intensified to strengthen waste management, increase energy efficiency, promote green mobility and enhance biodiversity.",""],[2,"244","4","Waste Separation and Recycling Facilities Enhancement","facilities for waste separation and recycling will be enhanced, particularly in residential, institutional and commercial areas.",""],[2,"244","4","Source Waste Separation and 3R Initiative","Waste will be managed holistically and sustainably by enforcing waste separation at source and intensifying the reduce, reuse and recycle (3R) initiative.",""],[2,"244","4","Single-Use Plastics Reduction Measures","Additionally, efforts will be strengthened to reduce single-use plastics, especially at",""],[2,"244","6","Green and Resilient City Framework and Certification","Focus will be given to the adoption of a green and resilient city framework and certification to enhance energy efficiency and resilience of cities.",""],[2,"244","6","Local Authority Implementation of Urban Planning Guidelines","This will be undertaken by advocating local authorities to implement the LCCF, MSCF and Planning Guideline for Disaster Resilient City.",""],[2,"244","6","Green Building Certification Incentive","In addition, developers will be encouraged to adopt accredited green certification tools, such as the Green Building Index and the Malaysian Carbon Reduction and Environmental Sustainability Tool (MyCREST) during the construction and operation phases.",""],[2,"244","6","Land Use Compliance for Climate-Resilient Development","developers of public and private development projects will be urged to adhere to the land use policies in designated development areas as prescribed in the NPP4, State Structure Plans, Local Plans or Special Area Plans.",""],[2,"244","6","Green City Action Plan Implementation","Green initiatives in cities will also be accelerated through the implementation of the Green City Action Plan under the IMT-GT and BIMP-EAGA platforms.",""]],"141":[[1,"292","1","Wildlife Conservation Programmes","Numerous programmes were implemented as part of wildlife conservation initiatives, including the establishment of wildlife sanctuaries and conservation centres.",""],[1,"292","2","Integrated Wildlife Enforcement Operation","Operasi Bersepadu Khazanah, launched in 2019, is a strategic collaborative operation between the Royal Malaysian Police (PDRM) and the Department of Wildlife and National Parks (PERHILITAN).",""],[1,"310","1","Strategic Joint Enforcement Against Wildlife Crime","Strategic joint enforcement programmes at the national and state levels will be intensified to combat poaching and illegal wildlife trade.",""],[1,"310","1","Regional Enforcement Collaboration on Cross-Border Wildlife Protection","Regional enforcement collaboration to control cross-border encroachment and poaching as well as conservation programmes will be strengthened.",""],[1,"310","1","Enforcement Capacity and Capability Enhancement","In supporting these efforts, the capacity and capability of enforcement agencies will be enhanced to combat illegal activities related to wild fauna and flora, including online illegal trading as well as unreported and unregulated fishing activities.",""],[2,"310","1","National and State Joint Wildlife Enforcement Programme","Strategic joint enforcement programmes at the national and state levels will be intensified to combat poaching and illegal wildlife trade.",""],[2,"310","1","Regional Cross-Border Enforcement Collaboration","Regional enforcement collaboration to control cross-border encroachment and poaching as well as conservation programmes will be strengthened.",""],[2,"310","1","Enforcement Agency Capacity Enhancement for Wildlife Protection","In supporting these efforts, the capacity and capability of enforcement agencies will be enhanced to combat illegal activities related to wild fauna and flora, including online illegal trading as well as unreported and unregulated fishing activities.",""]],"142":[[1,"308","2","Natural Resource Management and Conservation Programme","focus will be on conserving ecosystems, protecting species and genetic resources, ensuring sustainable utilisation and benefits sharing of resources as well as enhancing conservation of water resources.",""],[1,"308","7","Ecosystem Conservation and Habitat Connectivity Programme","conservation of terrestrial, inland water, coastal and marine areas will be enhanced through habitat protection, rehabilitation and connectivity as well as mainstreaming ecosystem considerations into planning and development",""],[1,"308","8","Protected Areas Gazetting Task Force","The gazetting of protected areas for terrestrial and inland waters will be intensified through the establishment of a special task force.",""],[1,"308","8","Other Effective Area-Based Conservation Measures Framework","a framework for other effective area-based conservation measures18 (OECM) will be developed to increase conservation of natural areas, including geoparks and inland waters",""],[1,"308","8","Forest Restoration, Rehabilitation and Enrichment Programme","Forest restoration, rehabilitation and enrichment will be intensified through multi- stakeholder collaboration.",""],[1,"308","8","Private Sector Forest Rehabilitation Participation","The private sector will be encouraged to actively participate in forest rehabilitation programmes.",""],[1,"308","8","Project RELeaf Tree Planting Initiative","Other companies are encouraged to emulate the lead taken by Nestlé to commit the planting of three million trees by 2023 through Project RELeaf.",""],[1,"308","8","Ecological Corridor Establishment under CFS Initiative","connectivity of four major forest complexes19 in Peninsular Malaysia will be improved by accelerating the establishment of ecological corridors under the CFS initiative.",""],[1,"308","8","HoB Forest Management and Conservation Initiative","the management and conservation of forested areas in Sabah and Sarawak will be further enhanced through the ongoing HoB initiative.",""],[1,"308","8","Public Hearing Requirement for Forest Degazetting","State governments will be urged to conduct public hearings before any degazetting of Permanent Reserved Forest (PRF) and Permanent Forest Estate (PFE).",""],[1,"309","2","Mainstream Natural Ecosystem Science in Development Planning","Natural ecosystem science and approaches will be mainstreamed into development planning and decision-making to ensure uninterrupted ecosystem services.",""],[1,"309","2","Protection of High Conservation Value and Sensitive Areas","vital natural areas, such as High Conservation Value areas21, Important Bird and Biodiversity Areas and Particularly Sensitive Sea Areas22 will be recognised and protected.",""],[1,"309","2","Spatial Mapping of Vulnerable Ecosystems","Spatial mapping of the vital areas and vulnerable ecosystems, such as peatlands, inland waters and riverine areas will be undertaken to facilitate conservation efforts.",""],[1,"309","2","Ecosystem Services Valuation in Decision-Making","The value of ecosystem services will be incorporated into the decision-making process by adopting appropriate approaches, including The Economics of Ecosystems and Biodiversity (TEEB).",""],[1,"309","2","Strengthened Ecosystem Health Monitoring","efforts to monitor ecosystem health, including soil fertility will be intensified to conserve the affected ecosystems.",""],[1,"309","2","Strategic Environmental Assessment for Early Planning","SEA will also be introduced to mainstream environmental considerations at the earliest stages of decision making, while coastal development and land reclamation activities will be reviewed to assess the environmental and ecological impact on the ecosystem.",""],[1,"309","3","Urban Green and Blue Space Expansion","Green spaces, such as urban forests and recreational parks, as well as blue spaces, including wetlands and lakes, in urban areas will be continuously expanded to regulate microclimate and support biodiversity.",""],[1,"309","3","Urban Biodiversity Conservation Action Plan","an action plan for urban biodiversity conservation will be formulated to guide local authorities in enhancing the liveability of urban areas.",""],[1,"309","3","Endemic Species Green Area Development in New Townships","New townships will be encouraged to establish more green areas with endemic plant species to rehabilitate their biodiversity.",""],[2,"308","2","Natural Resource Management and Conservation Programme","Therefore, it is important to strike a balance between utilising resources for socioeconomic development and safeguarding natural capital.",""],[2,"308","7","Ecosystem Conservation and Habitat Connectivity Programme","conservation of terrestrial, inland water, coastal and marine areas will be enhanced through habitat protection, rehabilitation and connectivity as well as mainstreaming ecosystem considerations into planning and development",""],[2,"308","8","Special Task Force for Protected Area Gazetting","The gazetting of protected areas for terrestrial and inland waters will be intensified through the establishment of a special task force.",""],[2,"308","8","OECM Framework for Conservation Areas","a framework for other effective area-based conservation measures18 (OECM) will be developed to increase conservation of natural areas, including geoparks and inland waters",""],[2,"308","8","Forest Restoration and Rehabilitation Programme","Forest restoration, rehabilitation and enrichment will be intensified through multi- stakeholder collaboration.",""],[2,"308","8","Private Sector Forest Rehabilitation Participation","The private sector will be encouraged to actively participate in forest rehabilitation programmes.",""],[2,"308","8","Project RELeaf Tree Planting Commitment","Other companies are encouraged to emulate the lead taken by Nestlé to commit the planting of three million trees by 2023 through Project RELeaf.",""],[2,"308","8","Ecological Corridor Expansion under CFS Initiative","connectivity of four major forest complexes19 in Peninsular Malaysia will be improved by accelerating the establishment of ecological corridors under the CFS initiative.",""],[2,"308","8","HoB Forest Management and Conservation Initiative","the management and conservation of forested areas in Sabah and Sarawak will be further enhanced through the ongoing HoB initiative.",""],[2,"308","8","Public Hearings for Forest Degazetting","State governments will be urged to conduct public hearings before any degazetting of Permanent Reserved Forest (PRF) and Permanent Forest Estate (PFE).",""],[2,"309","2","Mainstream Natural Ecosystem Science in Development Planning","Natural ecosystem science and approaches will be mainstreamed into development planning and decision-making to ensure uninterrupted ecosystem services.",""],[2,"309","2","Protection of High Conservation Value and Sensitive Areas","vital natural areas, such as High Conservation Value areas21, Important Bird and Biodiversity Areas and Particularly Sensitive Sea Areas22 will be recognised and protected.",""],[2,"309","2","Spatial Mapping of Vulnerable Ecosystems","Spatial mapping of the vital areas and vulnerable ecosystems, such as peatlands, inland waters and riverine areas will be undertaken to facilitate conservation efforts.",""],[2,"309","2","Ecosystem Services Valuation in Decision-Making","The value of ecosystem services will be incorporated into the decision-making process by adopting appropriate approaches, including The Economics of Ecosystems and Biodiversity (TEEB).",""],[2,"309","2","Strengthened Ecosystem Health Monitoring","efforts to monitor ecosystem health, including soil fertility will be intensified to conserve the affected ecosystems.",""],[2,"309","2","Strategic Environmental Assessment for Early Decision-Making","SEA will also be introduced to mainstream environmental considerations at the earliest stages of decision making, while coastal development and land reclamation activities will be reviewed to assess the environmental and ecological impact on the ecosystem.",""],[2,"309","3","Urban Green and Blue Space Expansion","Green spaces, such as urban forests and recreational parks, as well as blue spaces, including wetlands and lakes, in urban areas will be continuously expanded to regulate microclimate and support biodiversity.",""],[2,"309","3","Urban Biodiversity Conservation Action Plan","an action plan for urban biodiversity conservation will be formulated to guide local authorities in enhancing the liveability of urban areas.",""],[2,"309","3","Endemic Species Green Area Development in New Townships","New townships will be encouraged to establish more green areas with endemic plant species to rehabilitate their biodiversity.",""]],"143":[[1,"309","1","Coastal and Marine Area Rehabilitation Programme","The conservation and management of coastal and marine areas will be enhanced through rehabilitation programmes, such as beach nourishment, mangrove planting and deploying artificial reefs, particularly through multi-stakeholder collaboration.",""],[1,"309","1","Marine Protected Areas Management Planning and Identification Studies","Conservation of these areas will also be intensified by developing, implementing and reviewing management plans for marine protected areas (MPAs) as well as undertaking studies to identify potential MPAs.",""],[1,"309","1","Other Effective Area-Based Conservation Measures Framework","An OECM framework will also be developed for coastal and marine areas.",""],[1,"309","1","Coral Triangle Initiative Regional Plan Review","The Regional Plan of Action on Coral Triangle Initiative will be reviewed to focus on improving the health of coastal and marine ecosystems, ensuring food security and increasing climate resilience.",""],[1,"309","1","Blue Economy Blueprint","A blue economy20 blueprint will also be introduced to govern coastal and marine areas as well as related socioeconomic sectors.",""],[1,"309","1","Blue Economy Resource Optimization and Risk Assessment Measures","The blueprint will incorporate measures to optimise ocean resources and create alternative sources of income as well as undertake risk assessments, including the impact of climate change and disaster on people and businesses.",""],[1,"309","1","Marine Debris and Pollution Control Measures","In addition, measures to address marine debris and pollution will be introduced to protect the marine ecosystems.",""],[2,"309","1","Coastal and Marine Area Conservation and Management Programme","The conservation and management of coastal and marine areas will be enhanced through rehabilitation programmes, such as beach nourishment, mangrove planting and deploying artificial reefs, particularly through multi-stakeholder collaboration.",""],[2,"309","1","Marine Protected Areas Planning and Review Programme","Conservation of these areas will also be intensified by developing, implementing and reviewing management plans for marine protected areas (MPAs) as well as undertaking studies to identify potential MPAs.",""],[2,"309","1","OECM Framework Development for Coastal and Marine Areas","An OECM framework will also be developed for coastal and marine areas.",""],[2,"309","1","Coral Triangle Initiative Regional Plan Review","The Regional Plan of Action on Coral Triangle Initiative will be reviewed to focus on improving the health of coastal and marine ecosystems, ensuring food security and increasing climate resilience.",""],[2,"309","1","Blue Economy Blueprint","A blue economy20 blueprint will also be introduced to govern coastal and marine areas as well as related socioeconomic sectors.",""],[2,"309","1","Marine Debris and Pollution Reduction Measures","In addition, measures to address marine debris and pollution will be introduced to protect the marine ecosystems.",""]],"144":[[1,"309","4","Species and Genetic Resources Conservation Programme","Therefore, species and genetic resources will be protected by strengthening management and enhancing conservation.",""],[1,"309","5","Revision and Expansion of Species Action Plans","The management and conservation of key terrestrial and marine species will be improved through the revision of existing action plans as well as the introduction of new plans.",""],[1,"309","5","Species Inventory and Vulnerability Assessment","In supporting this, a comprehensive inventory and vulnerability assessment on species and their habitat, particularly the national red list species, will be conducted through multi-stakeholder collaboration to provide baseline information for species distribution mapping.",""],[1,"309","5","In-situ and Ex-situ Conservation Enhancement","In addition, in-situ and ex-situ conservation measures will be enhanced, among others, through the establishment of new sanctuaries as well as enhancement of existing wildlife conservation centres and prey recovery programmes.",""],[1,"309","5","Strengthening Wildlife and Marine Resources Assessment in EIA","The component of wildlife and marine resources assessment in the existing EIA will be strengthened to minimise the impact of new development projects on the natural habitat.",""],[1,"310","2","Integrated Gene and Specimen Centre","The current cryopreservation efforts and the existing gene banks to conserve the diverse biological and genetic resources will be strengthened by establishing an integrated gene and specimen centre.",""],[1,"310","2","Botanical Garden Network for Flora Conservation","a botanical garden network for flora conservation and genetic preservation will be established.",""],[1,"310","2","Biosafety Act Review and Enforcement Capacity Strengthening","The Biosafety Act 2007 will be reviewed to incorporate liability and redress elements, while the capacity and capability of relevant agencies will be enhanced in strengthening the management and enforcement of biosafety.",""],[1,"310","2","GMO Awareness Programmes","Awareness programmes will be stepped up to increase understanding on GMO.",""],[1,"310","2","Alien Species Management Improvement","Emphasis will also be given to improve the management of alien species to prevent the species from being invasive.",""],[1,"310","2","Alien Species Impact Studies","studies on the ecological and economic impact of alien species on the ecosystem will be undertaken.",""],[1,"311","2","Biological Resources and Traditional Knowledge Benefit-Sharing Enforcement","Act 795 will be enforced to ensure revenues generated from the commercialisation of biological resources and traditional knowledge are fairly and equitably shared among resource providers.",""],[1,"311","2","Competent Authorities Capacity Enhancement","the capacity and capability of the Competent Authorities at all levels will be enhanced.",""],[1,"311","2","Access and Benefit-Sharing Awareness Programme for ILCs","education and awareness programmes on access and benefits sharing will be enhanced for ILCs.",""],[1,"311","2","Traditional Knowledge Documentation Initiative","Existing traditional knowledge will be documented to safeguard the rights of the ILCs, while R&D&C&I and investment in bioprospecting activities will be encouraged to realise the value of traditional knowledge.",""],[2,"309","4","Species and Genetic Resources Protection and Conservation Programme","Therefore, species and genetic resources will be protected by strengthening management and enhancing conservation.",""],[2,"309","5","Revision and Expansion of Species Conservation Action Plans","The management and conservation of key terrestrial and marine species will be improved through the revision of existing action plans as well as the introduction of new plans.",""],[2,"309","5","Species Inventory and Vulnerability Assessment","a comprehensive inventory and vulnerability assessment on species and their habitat, particularly the national red list species, will be conducted through multi-stakeholder collaboration to provide baseline information for species distribution mapping.",""],[2,"309","5","In-situ and Ex-situ Wildlife Conservation Enhancement","in-situ and ex-situ conservation measures will be enhanced, among others, through the establishment of new sanctuaries as well as enhancement of existing wildlife conservation centres and prey recovery programmes.",""],[2,"309","5","Strengthening Wildlife and Marine Resources Assessment in EIA","The component of wildlife and marine resources assessment in the existing EIA will be strengthened to minimise the impact of new development projects on the natural habitat.",""],[2,"310","2","Integrated Gene and Specimen Centre","The current cryopreservation efforts and the existing gene banks to conserve the diverse biological and genetic resources will be strengthened by establishing an integrated gene and specimen centre.",""],[2,"310","2","Botanical Garden Network for Flora Conservation","a botanical garden network for flora conservation and genetic preservation will be established.",""],[2,"310","2","Biosafety Act Review and Enforcement Capacity Strengthening","The Biosafety Act 2007 will be reviewed to incorporate liability and redress elements, while the capacity and capability of relevant agencies will be enhanced in strengthening the management and enforcement of biosafety.",""],[2,"310","2","GMO Awareness Programme","Awareness programmes will be stepped up to increase understanding on GMO.",""],[2,"310","2","Alien Species Management Improvement","Emphasis will also be given to improve the management of alien species to prevent the species from being invasive.",""],[2,"310","2","Alien Species Impact Studies","studies on the ecological and economic impact of alien species on the ecosystem will be undertaken.",""]],"145":[[1,"310","3","Sustainable Natural Resources Utilisation Initiative","efforts will focus on strengthening the sustainable utilisation of natural resources, enhancing mineral resources management, diversifying conservation funding as well as ensuring fair and equitable sharing of benefits.",""],[1,"310","3","Conservation Funding Diversification Mechanism","efforts will focus on strengthening the sustainable utilisation of natural resources, enhancing mineral resources management, diversifying conservation funding as well as ensuring fair and equitable sharing of benefits.",""],[1,"310","4","Strengthening Sustainable Forest Management Systems","Sustainable forest management will be strengthened by improving existing plans and systems, while the inventory of forest resources will be updated.",""],[1,"310","4","Sustainable Fisheries Management Plan","a sustainable fisheries management plan will be developed to ensure ocean resources are used sustainably and the livelihood of the fishing communities is improved.",""],[1,"310","4","Periodic Marine Resources Assessment","Periodic assessments of marine resources will be undertaken to support the plan.",""],[1,"310","4","Carrying Capacity Assessment for Tourism Sites","an assessment on the carrying capacity of terrestrial and marine tourism sites will be conducted.",""],[1,"310","4","Green Practices Adoption in Tourism","Industry players will be encouraged to adopt green practices to ensure the tourism activities are sustainable.",""],[1,"310","4","Sustainable Geopark Management Plan","A sustainable geopark management plan will also be formulated to optimise geological resources.",""],[2,"310","3","Sustainable Natural Resources Utilisation and Benefit-Sharing Initiatives","In this respect, efforts will focus on strengthening the sustainable utilisation of natural resources, enhancing mineral resources management, diversifying conservation funding as well as ensuring fair and equitable sharing of benefits.",""],[2,"310","4","Strengthening Sustainable Forest Management Systems","Sustainable forest management will be strengthened by improving existing plans and systems, while the inventory of forest resources will be updated.",""],[2,"310","4","Sustainable Fisheries Management Plan","a sustainable fisheries management plan will be developed to ensure ocean resources are used sustainably and the livelihood of the fishing communities is improved.",""],[2,"310","4","Tourism Carrying Capacity Assessment","an assessment on the carrying capacity of terrestrial and marine tourism sites will be conducted.",""],[2,"310","4","Green Practices Adoption in Tourism Industry","Industry players will be encouraged to adopt green practices to ensure the tourism activities are sustainable.",""],[2,"310","4","Sustainable Geopark Management Plan","A sustainable geopark management plan will also be formulated to optimise geological resources.",""]],"146":[[1,"305","1","Strengthened Solid Waste Management and Zero-Waste Compliance","solid waste management will be strengthened to ensure compliance with existing standards.",""],[1,"305","1","Waste Separation at Source and 3R Intensification","The enforcement of waste separation at source and the implementation of the 3R initiatives will be intensified, especially in urban areas.",""],[1,"305","1","Expansion of Waste Collection, Separation and Recycling Facilities","The provision of waste collection, separation and recycling facilities will be increased, particularly in residential, institutions and commercial areas.",""],[1,"305","1","State By-law Reform for Integrated Waste Management","States which have not adopted the Solid Waste Management and Public Cleansing Act 2007 will be encouraged to formulate or amend the relevant by-laws or ordinance to ensure all types of waste are managed holistically.",""],[1,"305","1","Enforcement of Solid Waste and Public Cleansing Regulations","Enforcement of the Solid Waste and Public Cleansing Management (Scheme for Commercial, Industrial and Institutional Solid Waste) Regulations 2018 and the Solid Waste and Public Cleansing Management (Scheme for Construction Solid Waste) Regulations 2018 will ensure all waste are separated at source to enable proper treatment, recycling and disposal.",""],[1,"305","1","National Waste Database for Monitoring and Circular Economy Support","A comprehensive database for all types of waste will also be developed for better monitoring and to support the circular economy initiatives.",""],[1,"305","2","Integrated Waste Management Facilities Construction","a number of integrated waste management facilities will be constructed.",""],[1,"305","2","Waste Eco-Parks and Waste Management Technology Development","the establishment of waste eco parks and development of waste management technologies will be encouraged.",""],[1,"305","2","Open Landfill Closure and Waste Import Cessation","Over time, all open landfills will be safely closed and import of waste will be ceased.",""],[1,"305","3","Single-Use Product Reduction Initiative","Single-use products, including plastics and packaging materials will be discouraged, particularly in eateries and at public events through collaboration with relevant stakeholders, including restaurants and shopping complex owners as well as public event organisers.",""],[1,"305","4","Review of Waste Import and Export Enforcement Legislation","Existing legislation, including Act 127 and the Customs Act 1967, will be reviewed to enable stringent and robust enforcement, monitoring and control of waste imports and exports.",""],[1,"305","5","Transboundary Waste Import Control and Enforcement","Following this, exporting countries will have to attain prior informed consent from importing countries before transboundary shipping of waste takes place.",""],[1,"305","5","Enhanced Inspection and Verification for Imported Waste","In addition, on-site inspections and verification for all types of imported waste will be enhanced.",""],[1,"305","5","Illegal Waste Operator Tracking and Penalty Enforcement","Simultaneously, efforts to track and weed out illegal waste operators will be escalated and stiffer penalties imposed to curb illegal operations.",""],[2,"305","1","Strengthened Solid Waste Management and Zero-Waste Enforcement","solid waste management will be strengthened to ensure compliance with existing standards.",""],[2,"305","1","Waste Separation at Source and 3R Intensification","The enforcement of waste separation at source and the implementation of the 3R initiatives will be intensified, especially in urban areas.",""],[2,"305","1","Expansion of Waste Collection, Separation and Recycling Facilities","The provision of waste collection, separation and recycling facilities will be increased, particularly in residential, institutions and commercial areas.",""],[2,"305","1","State By-law Reform for Solid Waste Management","States which have not adopted the Solid Waste Management and Public Cleansing Act 2007 will be encouraged to formulate or amend the relevant by-laws or ordinance to ensure all types of waste are managed holistically.",""],[2,"305","1","Enforcement of Solid Waste and Public Cleansing Regulations","Enforcement of the Solid Waste and Public Cleansing Management (Scheme for Commercial, Industrial and Institutional Solid Waste) Regulations 2018 and the Solid Waste and Public Cleansing Management (Scheme for Construction Solid Waste) Regulations 2018 will ensure all waste are separated at source to enable proper treatment, recycling and disposal.",""],[2,"305","1","National Waste Database Development","A comprehensive database for all types of waste will also be developed for better monitoring and to support the circular economy initiatives.",""],[2,"305","2","Integrated Waste Management Facilities Construction","a number of integrated waste management facilities will be constructed.",""],[2,"305","2","Waste Eco-Parks and Waste Management Technology Development","the establishment of waste eco parks and development of waste management technologies will be encouraged.",""],[2,"305","2","Open Landfill Closure and Waste Import Cessation","all open landfills will be safely closed and import of waste will be ceased.",""],[2,"305","3","Single-Use Product Reduction Initiative","Single-use products, including plastics and packaging materials will be discouraged, particularly in eateries and at public events through collaboration with relevant stakeholders, including restaurants and shopping complex owners as well as public event organisers.",""]],"147":[[1,"306","3","Accelerated HCFC Phase-Out Management Plan Implementation","The implementation of the Malaysia Hydrochlorofluorocarbons (HCFC) Phased-Out Management Plan (HPMP Stage 2) (2017-2022) will be expedited to eventually eliminate the use of ozone depleting substances in foam, refrigerant and air conditioning production.",""],[1,"306","3","Hydrofluorocarbon Phase-Down Regulatory Framework","processes and procedures will be put in place to phase- down hydrofluorocarbons (HFC) use.",""],[1,"306","4","Chemical and Hazardous Substances Management Task Force","a dedicated task force will be established to coordinate and oversee the overall management of chemical and hazardous substances, from the production to disposal stages.",""],[1,"306","4","Comprehensive Chemical Safety Regulatory Framework Study","A detailed study will be undertaken to formulate a comprehensive regulatory framework and strengthen its governance to be at par with international best practices.",""],[1,"306","4","New Regulation for Chemical and Hazardous Substances","a new regulation will be introduced, while relevant legislation, including Act 127, the Occupational Safety and Health Act 1994 and the Poison Act 1952 will be reviewed.",""],[1,"306","5","Chemical and Hazardous Waste Movement Regulation","movement of chemical and hazardous substances and their waste will also be introduced.",""],[1,"306","5","Integrated Scheduled Waste Treatment and Disposal Facilities","Integrated scheduled waste treatment and disposal facilities will be constructed to enable recovery, treatment, recycling and sound management of the waste, therefore minimising illegal dumping.",""],[1,"306","6","Chemical Management Strategy and Action Plan Acceleration","Implementation of the Strategy and Action Plan for Chemical Management will be accelerated.",""],[1,"306","6","Ban on Selected Mercury-Containing Product Trade","The import and export of selected mercury-containing products will be banned.",""],[1,"306","6","Phase-Out of Mercury, Toxic Chemicals, and Harmful Pesticides","The use of mercury and its compounds in manufacturing processes as well as the use of environmentally harmful pesticides and toxic chemicals will be phased-out.",""],[1,"306","6","Promotion of Environment-Friendly Alternatives","These substances will be replaced with environment- friendly alternatives.",""],[1,"306","6","Triple-Helix R&D&C&I Collaboration for Green Products","Triple-helix collaboration will be further encouraged to undertake R&D&C&I in developing more environment- friendly products.",""],[2,"306","3","Accelerated HCFC Phase-Out Management Plan Implementation","The implementation of the Malaysia Hydrochlorofluorocarbons (HCFC) Phased-Out Management Plan (HPMP Stage 2) (2017-2022) will be expedited to eventually eliminate the use of ozone depleting substances in foam, refrigerant and air conditioning production.",""],[2,"306","3","Hydrofluorocarbon Phase-Down Regulatory Framework","With the ratification of the Kigali Amendment to the Montreal Protocol on Substances that Deplete the Ozone Layer, processes and procedures will be put in place to phase- down hydrofluorocarbons (HFC) use.",""],[2,"306","4","Chemical and Hazardous Substances Management Task Force","a dedicated task force will be established to coordinate and oversee the overall management of chemical and hazardous substances, from the production to disposal stages.",""],[2,"306","4","Comprehensive Chemical Safety Regulatory Framework Study","A detailed study will be undertaken to formulate a comprehensive regulatory framework and strengthen its governance to be at par with international best practices.",""],[2,"306","4","Chemical and Hazardous Substances Regulation and Legal Review","a new regulation will be introduced, while relevant legislation, including Act 127, the Occupational Safety and Health Act 1994 and the Poison Act 1952 will be reviewed.",""],[2,"306","5","Regulation of Chemical and Hazardous Substance Movement","movement of chemical and hazardous substances and their waste will also be introduced.",""],[2,"306","5","Integrated Scheduled Waste Treatment and Disposal Facilities","Integrated scheduled waste treatment and disposal facilities will be constructed to enable recovery, treatment, recycling and sound management of the waste, therefore minimising illegal dumping.",""],[2,"306","6","Chemical Management Strategy and Action Plan Acceleration","Implementation of the Strategy and Action Plan for Chemical Management will be accelerated.",""],[2,"306","6","Mercury-Containing Products Import and Export Ban","The import and export of selected mercury-containing products will be banned.",""],[2,"306","6","Phase-Out of Mercury, Toxic Chemicals, and Harmful Pesticides","The use of mercury and its compounds in manufacturing processes as well as the use of environmentally harmful pesticides and toxic chemicals will be phased-out.",""],[2,"306","6","Substitution of Hazardous Substances with Environment-Friendly Alternatives","These substances will be replaced with environment- friendly alternatives.",""],[2,"306","6","Triple-Helix R&D&C&I for Environment-Friendly Products","Triple-helix collaboration will be further encouraged to undertake R&D&C&I in developing more environment- friendly products.",""]],"148":[[1,"311","7","Environmental Governance Strengthening","The Twelfth Plan will focus on strengthening environmental governance, scaling- up green financing and investments as well as instilling a sense of ownership and shared responsibility.",""],[1,"312","1","Environmental Governance Strengthening Initiative","Environmental governance will be strengthened to enable better management of the environment and natural resources.",""],[1,"312","2","Policy Review and Benchmarking for Environmental Coherence","New policies, legislation and blueprints will be formulated, while existing ones will be reviewed and benchmarked against international standards and best practices.",""],[1,"312","2","Review of National Environmental and Climate Policies","The National Policy on the Environment 2002, the National Policy on Climate Change 2009 and the National Policy on Biological Diversity 2016-2025 will be reviewed to ensure coherence and comprehensiveness.",""],[1,"312","2","Climate Change Legislation Development","A legislation on climate change will also be formulated to enable more coordinated and effective climate action at all levels.",""],[1,"312","2","Strengthened Environmental Enforcement","environment-related enforcement activities will be strengthened to ensure effective implementation of legislation in deterring activities that are damaging to the environment and biodiversity.",""],[1,"312","3","State Sustainable Development Task Forces","State governments will be recommended to establish a task force on sustainable development to monitor, assess and report the implementation and performance of sustainable development initiatives, including conserving biodiversity, addressing climate change and pollution as well as reducing disaster risks.",""],[1,"312","3","Climate Change Governance Strengthening and UNFCCC Alignment","In addition, climate change governance will be strengthened and aligned with Malaysia's obligations to the UNFCCC as well as the 2030 Agenda.",""],[2,"290","4","Environmental Protection Enhancement Act","Formulation of an Act to Enhance Environmental Protection",""],[2,"311","7","Environmental Governance Strengthening","The Twelfth Plan will focus on strengthening environmental governance, scaling- up green financing and investments as well as instilling a sense of ownership and shared responsibility.",""],[2,"312","1","Environmental Governance Strengthening Initiative","Environmental governance will be strengthened to enable better management of the environment and natural resources.",""],[2,"312","2","Policy Review and Benchmarking for Environmental Frameworks","New policies, legislation and blueprints will be formulated, while existing ones will be reviewed and benchmarked against international standards and best practices.",""],[2,"312","2","Climate Change Legislation Development","A legislation on climate change will also be formulated to enable more coordinated and effective climate action at all levels.",""],[2,"312","2","Strengthened Environmental Enforcement","In addition, environment-related enforcement activities will be strengthened to ensure effective implementation of legislation in deterring activities that are damaging to the environment and biodiversity.",""],[2,"312","3","State Sustainable Development Task Forces","State governments will be recommended to establish a task force on sustainable development to monitor, assess and report the implementation and performance of sustainable development initiatives, including conserving biodiversity, addressing climate change and pollution as well as reducing disaster risks.",""],[2,"312","3","Climate Change Governance Strengthening","In addition, climate change governance will be strengthened and aligned with Malaysia's obligations to the UNFCCC as well as the 2030 Agenda.",""]],"149":[[1,"313","8","Expansion of Environmental Economic Instruments","The application of environmental economic instruments based on the user-pay and polluter-pay principles will be augmented to promote the circular economy, minimise environmental pollution and prevent ecosystems damage.",""],[1,"313","8","Study of Economic Instruments for Environmental Policy","a comprehensive study on the options of economic instruments, including PES and carbon pricing, as well as related costs and benefits will be carried out.",""],[1,"313","8","Revision of Environment-Related Fees and Charges","Existing environment-related fees and charges will also be revised to reflect fair value and the proceeds will be utilised to support environmental protection and conservation efforts.",""],[1,"313","8","Replacement of Environmentally Harmful Subsidies","Meanwhile, environmentally harmful subsidies will be replaced with subsidies that promote environmental sustainability.",""],[1,"336","3","Ecological Fiscal Transfer Mechanism Institutionalisation","The ecological fiscal transfer mechanism will be institutionalised by providing adequate funds and introducing an appropriate distribution mechanism.",""],[1,"336","3","River Ecosystem Services Assessment Requirement","state governments and local authorities will be encouraged to conduct assessments of the river ecosystem services8 before decisions are made on land-use change.",""],[1,"336","3","Payment for Ecosystem Services Mechanism","a mechanism will be established to ensure the payment for ecosystem services commensurates with the benefits derived and costs incurred from the services.",""],[1,"336","3","Green Technology Financing Scheme for Water Saving and Circular Economy","The existing Green Technology Financing Scheme will also be leveraged to inculcate water saving habit and promote circular economy practices among water-intensive industries.",""]],"150":[[1,"314","2","Behavioral Insights for Environmental Sustainability","efforts will focus on steering behavioural changes, including adopting the behavioural insights27 approach.",""],[1,"314","2","Stakeholder Collaboration for Environmental Protection","stakeholder collaboration will be increased in protecting and conserving the environment.",""],[1,"314","3","Communication, Education and Public Awareness (CEPA) Initiatives","Communication, education and public awareness (CEPA) initiatives will be intensified to encourage mindset and behavioural changes as well as enhance shared responsibility in environmental protection, biodiversity conservation and disaster risk reduction.",""],[1,"314","3","Environmental Champions Empowerment Initiative","environmental champions will be identified and empowered as agents of change.",""],[1,"314","3","Environment-Related Curriculum Expansion","Experiential learning among students will be enhanced through the expansion of environment-related curriculum",""],[1,"314","4","Youth Environmental Awareness and Sustainability Participation Programme","Youth will be encouraged to actively participate in advocating environmental awareness and sustainability programmes",""],[1,"314","4","Training of Trainers for Teachers and Community Leaders","teachers and local community leaders will be equipped with appropriate skills through training of trainers' programmes",""],[1,"314","5","Amanah Lestari Alam Environmental Education Support Initiative","Amanah Lestari Alam, a company limited by guarantee, will be leveraged to support the implementation of environment and sustainability-related education initiatives in schools and higher education institutions as well as awareness programmes.",""],[1,"314","6","Behavioural Insights for Environmental Awareness and Sustainable Lifestyles","The behavioural insights approach will be adopted to steer mindset and behavioural changes, mainly through the provision of appropriate facilities, product labelling and reward system as well as incorporation in faith practices.",""],[1,"314","6","Stakeholder Collaboration for Behavioural Insights Adoption","Collaboration with various stakeholders will be strengthened to promote the adoption of behavioural insights.",""],[1,"314","7","Environmental Dialogue and Knowledge-Sharing Platforms","Existing dialogues and knowledge-sharing platforms will be enhanced, and new ones will be created to promote a shared vision on environmental protection and conservation.",""],[1,"314","7","Community and Private Sector Environmental Participation Initiative","the involvement of communities and the private sector in environmental protection and conservation programmes will be further encouraged, including via technological innovations and social media.",""],[1,"314","7","Community-Based Natural Area Monitoring and Citizen Science","The ILCs will also be empowered in the conservation of natural areas through community-based resource monitoring and citizen science28.",""],[1,"314","7","Friends of River Initiative Replication","The success of the Friends of River initiative by the community in supporting the protection, restoration and sustainable use of rivers will be replicated.",""],[1,"314","7","Private Sector Conservation Financing Coordination","Contributions from the private sector, including financial institutions will be better coordinated to support efforts in implementing various conservation activities.",""],[1,"334","1","Public Consultation Platforms for Water Sector Transformation","Rakyat will be empowered to drive the transformation through the establishment of public consultation platforms, implementation of awareness-raising, advocacy and capacity-building (AACB) programmes as well as expansion of community-driven conservation activities.",""],[1,"334","1","Awareness-Raising, Advocacy and Capacity-Building Programmes for Water Conservation","Rakyat will be empowered to drive the transformation through the establishment of public consultation platforms, implementation of awareness-raising, advocacy and capacity-building (AACB) programmes as well as expansion of community-driven conservation activities.",""],[1,"334","1","Community-Driven Water Conservation Activities","Rakyat will be empowered to drive the transformation through the establishment of public consultation platforms, implementation of awareness-raising, advocacy and capacity-building (AACB) programmes as well as expansion of community-driven conservation activities.",""],[1,"334","4","Community-Driven Environmental Conservation Programmes","Community-driven programmes in environmental conservation will be increased to empower people to protect and conserve water resources as well as create socioeconomic activities.",""],[1,"334","4","Expansion of Tagal and FoR Programmes","Various successful initiatives including the Tagal system and FoR programmes will also be expanded.",""],[1,"334","4","Water-Saving Behavior Change Campaigns","Campaigns to inculcate water-saving habits and precise water use among domestic users",""],[1,"334","5","Environmental-Related Experiential Learning Enhancement","Environmental-related education, especially experiential learning, will be further enhanced through collaboration among educational institutions, civil society organisations (CSOs), the private sector and government agencies.",""]],"151":[[1,"453","6","Whole-of-Nation Green Growth Transition","The third theme, Advancing Sustainability, focuses on efforts to advance green growth through the whole-of- nation approach by leveraging green technology as well as sustainable consumption and production practices, whilst ensuring environmental protection, addressing climate change and conserving natural resources for future generations.",""],[1,"453","6","Circular Economy Transition","The transition to circular economy enables a systemic shift to generate more sustainable and responsible businesses and investments, create new economic opportunities and expand the green market.",""],[1,"453","6","Comprehensive Energy Policy Formulation","To ensure continuous access and affordable energy costs, the energy sector will be managed efficiently through the formulation of a comprehensive policy.",""],[2,"453","6","Whole-of-Nation Green Growth Transition","The third theme, Advancing Sustainability, focuses on efforts to advance green growth through the whole-of- nation approach by leveraging green technology as well as sustainable consumption and production practices, whilst ensuring environmental protection, addressing climate change and conserving natural resources for future generations.",""],[2,"453","6","Circular Economy Transition","The transition to circular economy enables a systemic shift to generate more sustainable and responsible businesses and investments, create new economic opportunities and expand the green market.",""],[2,"453","6","Comprehensive Energy Policy Formulation","To ensure continuous access and affordable energy costs, the energy sector will be managed efficiently through the formulation of a comprehensive policy.",""]],"152":[[2,"289","1","Climate Change Mitigation and Adaptation Actions","Priority was also given to climate change mitigation and adaptation actions as well as disaster risk reduction measures.",""],[2,"289","1","Disaster Risk Reduction Measures","Priority was also given to climate change mitigation and adaptation actions as well as disaster risk reduction measures.",""]],"153":[[2,"32","7","Circular Economy Transition","Two game changers will be implemented under Theme 3, namely embracing the circular economy and accelerating adoption of the Integrated Water Resources Management (IWRM).",""],[2,"37","1","Circular Economy Transition Framework","the circular economy model will be embraced.",""],[2,"37","1","Green Economy and Low-Carbon Transition Measures","All these initiatives will expand the green economy and facilitate the attainment of a low-carbon future.",""]],"154":[[1,"290","4","Environmental Protection Enhancement Act","Formulation of an Act to Enhance Environmental Protection",""],[1,"305","6","Planetary Health Mainstreaming in Policy and Planning","In preventing pollution, planetary health will be mainstreamed in policies, and development planning and implementation.",""],[1,"305","6","Environmental Health Prioritization and Hazardous Substances Management","Accordingly, efforts will be intensified to prioritise environmental health as well as implement environmentally sound management of chemical and hazardous substances.",""],[1,"305","7","Review and Strengthen Environmental Regulations and Guidelines","In addressing environmental issues effectively, including emerging issues, Act 127 will be reviewed.",""],[1,"305","7","Household E-Waste Regulation and Clean Air Master Plan","These include the introduction of regulation on household e-waste, master plan on clean air and guidelines for managing end-of-life vehicles as well as green practice modules for chemical and scheduled waste industries.",""],[1,"305","7","Environmental Enforcement Modernization System","Environmental enforcement efforts will be intensified and improved through smart surveillance and enforcement systems, online system for self-regulation among industries, hydrocarbon fingerprinting to address marine oil spills and environment geospatial information system.",""],[1,"305","7","Empowerment of Environmental Crime Enforcement Task Force","the task force will be empowered to enforce Act 127 and the Water Services Industry Act 2006.",""],[1,"305","7","Pollution Carrying Capacity Studies","studies to determine the carrying capacity of the atmosphere, river and soil in absorbing pollutants, particularly in high-risk areas will be undertaken to facilitate enforcement efforts.",""],[1,"306","1","Environmental Impact Assessment Enhancement","The prescribed activities under the Environmental Impact Assessment (EIA) will be enhanced to strengthen environmental management.",""],[1,"306","1","Strategic Environmental Assessment Introduction","studies on the effectiveness of the EIA and the introduction of the Strategic Environmental Assessment17 (SEA) will be undertaken.",""],[1,"306","1","Fisheries Act Revision for Coastal Impact Assessment","The Fisheries Act 1985 will be revised to incorporate impact assessment of coastal area development on the fisheries ecosystem.",""],[1,"306","1","Health and Social Impact Assessment Enhancement","health and social impact assessments will be enhanced to support evidence-based and risk-informed decision-making.",""],[1,"306","2","Environmental Pollution Prevention Requirements","premise owners and developers will be required to prevent pollution or reduce its emissions at source through better preventive and emission control measures.",""],[1,"306","2","Environmental Compliance Reporting Requirements","They will also be required to submit regular reports to the relevant authorities.",""],[1,"306","2","Technical Training and Professional Certification for Environmental Compliance","technical training in relevant fields as well as professional certification programmes for the industry players will be enhanced.",""]],"155":[[1,"67","4","Agriculture Sector Reinvigoration for Food Security","The agriculture sector will be reinvigorated to support the downstream activities and to enhance food security.",""],[1,"67","7","Smart Farming Transformation","the emphasis will be on expediting the transformation of the agriculture sector into a modern, dynamic and competitive sector, supported by greater R&D&C&I.",""],[1,"67","7","National Food Security and Agrofood Policy Implementation","the strategies and initiatives under the National Food Security Framework and the National Agrofood Policy 2021-2030 will be implemented to meet food self-sufficiency targets and comply with international food safety standards.",""],[1,"77","15","Smart Farming Technology Adoption Programme","Intensifying smart farming activities by accelerating the adoption of modern technologies.",""],[1,"95","2","Digital Transformation of Agriculture Operations","The operation and production process in the agriculture sector will be transformed to minimise costs, reduce processing time and optimise the usage of resources through adoption of digital technologies.",""],[1,"95","2","Digital Applications for Farm and Fishery Management","Farmers will be encouraged to adopt digital applications in farm and fishery management practices, production and marketing.",""],[1,"95","2","Agricultural Big Data Decision Support System","The sector will utilise BDA that enable farmers to access granular data, such as on agricultural land, farm inputs, incentives and financial assistance as well as market demand in making smart decisions on production.",""],[1,"95","2","Sonar-Based Fish Detection System","The utilisation of sonar-based fish detection system will encourage efficient marine fishery activities.",""],[1,"95","2","Agricultural eCommerce Marketing Platform","Meanwhile, farmers as well as agricultural cooperatives and associations will be encouraged to leverage eCommerce platforms to improve marketing of agriculture produce, reducing over dependency on intermediaries.",""],[1,"95","2","Agricultural Machinery and Equipment Outsourcing Platform","In addition, these platforms will be leveraged to outsource farming machinery and equipment services to optimise resources and achieve cost efficiency.",""],[1,"95","2","Agricultural Technology Resilience for Health Crises","The adoption of technology in the agriculture sector will also minimise farming operations risk from health-related crises to ensure uninterrupted production.",""],[1,"96","1","High-Value Agricultural Production Upgrading","efforts to increase high value-added products will be intensified in the upstream and midstream activities by producing premium agricultural products, high-yielding crop varieties and breeds as well as internationally accepted by-products.",""],[1,"96","1","Smart Farming and Precision Agriculture Scale-Up","Smart farming and precision agriculture technologies will be adopted on a wider scale for both agrofood and agricommodity subsectors.",""],[1,"96","1","Agricultural Machinery and Equipment Customization","Focus will also be given to developing and customising agricultural machineries and equipment to suit local conditions, such as terrain features, weather and crop requirements.",""],[1,"96","1","Smart Indoor Vertical Farming Expansion","smart indoor vertical farming or plant factory will be expanded by leveraging on existing Permanent Food Production Parks (TKPM), idle land and abandoned buildings.",""],[1,"96","1","Organic Farming Adoption Promotion","Farmers will be encouraged to adopt organic farming practices in meeting increasing demand for organic products and generating higher income.",""],[1,"96","1","Deep Sea and High Sea Fishing Modernization","agricultural cooperatives and associations will be encouraged to venture into deep sea and high sea fishing utilising modern vessels and innovative equipment to enhance competitiveness as well as promote a sustainable fishing industry.",""],[1,"97","7","Agricultural Research and Innovation Programme","In the agriculture sector, research will focus on developing new crop varieties, livestock and fish breeds, methods of planting and niche export products, as well as ensuring affordable, healthy and safe agriculture produce.",""],[1,"97","7","Collaborative Agricultural Research Strengthening","Research will be intensified through greater collaboration between local and international research institutions.",""],[1,"97","8","Agricultural Training Curriculum Review","In the agriculture sector, the training curricula and modules will be reviewed to produce certified and highly knowledgeable agriculturists to meet current and future demand.",""],[1,"97","8","Professional Body for Agriculturists","A professional body will be established to recognise trained and experienced farmers, farm experts, agricultural technicians and scientists, as professional agriculturists to elevate the standing, image and recognition of the agriculture sector workforce.",""],[1,"98","4","Agricultural Modernisation Incentive Review","In the agriculture sector, financial incentives for investment, including in building, machinery, training and utilities will be reviewed to catalyse the transition from traditional to modern agriculture.",""],[1,"98","4","Skim Tanam Semula Implementation","The Skim Tanam Semula (STS)7 will be implemented and an endowment fund will be",""],[1,"98","9","Smart Farming Fund","A dedicated smart farming fund will be established to accelerate the adoption of modern technology in the agriculture",""],[1,"99","1","Agricultural Modernisation Fund","This fund will offer opportunities for farmers, especially for youth agropreneurs and smallholders to modernise farming activities along the value chain in ensuring food security.",""],[2,"67","4","Agriculture Sector Reinvigoration for Food Security","The agriculture sector will be reinvigorated to support the downstream activities and to enhance food security.",""],[2,"67","7","Smart Farming Transformation","Adoption of smart farming through modern and new technologies is vital in reinvigorating growth in the agriculture sector.",""],[2,"67","7","Agriculture Sector Modernisation and Competitiveness Drive","the emphasis will be on expediting the transformation of the agriculture sector into a modern, dynamic and competitive sector, supported by greater R&D&C&I.",""],[2,"67","7","National Food Security Framework and Agrofood Policy Implementation","the strategies and initiatives under the National Food Security Framework and the National Agrofood Policy 2021-2030 will be implemented to meet food self-sufficiency targets and comply with international food safety standards.",""],[2,"68","1","Agricommodity Entrepreneur Development for Specialty Products","The development of agricommodity entrepreneurs in speciality products, including tocotrienols, will be promoted to diversify into higher value-added products.",""],[2,"77","15","Smart Farming Technology Adoption Initiative","Intensifying smart farming activities by accelerating the adoption of modern technologies.",""],[2,"95","2","Digital Transformation of Agricultural Operations and Production","The operation and production process in the agriculture sector will be transformed to minimise costs, reduce processing time and optimise the usage of resources through adoption of digital technologies.",""],[2,"95","2","Digital Agriculture Applications for Farm and Fishery Management","Farmers will be encouraged to adopt digital applications in farm and fishery management practices, production and marketing.",""],[2,"95","2","Agricultural Big Data Decision Support System","The sector will utilise BDA that enable farmers to access granular data, such as on agricultural land, farm inputs, incentives and financial assistance as well as market demand in making smart decisions on production.",""],[2,"95","2","Sonar-Based Fish Detection System","The utilisation of sonar-based fish detection system will encourage efficient marine fishery activities.",""],[2,"95","2","Agricultural eCommerce Marketing Platform","Meanwhile, farmers as well as agricultural cooperatives and associations will be encouraged to leverage eCommerce platforms to improve marketing of agriculture produce, reducing over dependency on intermediaries.",""],[2,"95","2","Agricultural Machinery and Equipment Outsourcing Platform","In addition, these platforms will be leveraged to outsource farming machinery and equipment services to optimise resources and achieve cost efficiency.",""],[2,"95","2","Climate-Resilient Agricultural Technology Adoption","The adoption of technology in the agriculture sector will also minimise farming operations risk from health-related crises to ensure uninterrupted production.",""],[2,"96","1","High-Value Agricultural Production and Smart Farming Expansion","In the agriculture sector, efforts to increase high value-added products will be intensified in the upstream and midstream activities by producing premium agricultural products, high-yielding crop varieties and breeds as well as internationally accepted by-products.",""],[2,"96","1","Smart Farming and Precision Agriculture Adoption","Smart farming and precision agriculture technologies will be adopted on a wider scale for both agrofood and agricommodity subsectors.",""],[2,"96","1","High-Tech Farming Methods Deployment","These initiatives will include adopting high-tech farming methods utilising BDA, AI and IoT as well as precision tools, such as drones, robotics and sensors.",""],[2,"96","1","Agricultural Machinery and Equipment Customisation","Focus will also be given to developing and customising agricultural machineries and equipment to suit local conditions, such as terrain features, weather and crop requirements.",""],[2,"96","1","Smart Indoor Vertical Farming Expansion","In addition, smart indoor vertical farming or plant factory will be expanded by leveraging on existing Permanent Food Production Parks (TKPM), idle land and abandoned buildings.",""],[2,"96","1","Organic Farming Adoption Promotion","Farmers will be encouraged to adopt organic farming practices in meeting increasing demand for organic products and generating higher income.",""],[2,"96","1","Deep Sea and High Sea Fishing Modernisation","In the area of marine fishery, agricultural cooperatives and associations will be encouraged to venture into deep sea and high sea fishing utilising modern vessels and innovative equipment to enhance competitiveness as well as promote a sustainable fishing industry.",""],[2,"97","7","Agricultural Research and Crop Improvement Programme","In the agriculture sector, research will focus on developing new crop varieties, livestock and fish breeds, methods of planting and niche export products, as well as ensuring affordable, healthy and safe agriculture produce.",""],[2,"97","7","Agricultural Research Collaboration Strengthening","Research will be intensified through greater collaboration between local and international research institutions.",""],[2,"97","8","Agricultural Training Curriculum Review","In the agriculture sector, the training curricula and modules will be reviewed to produce certified and highly knowledgeable agriculturists to meet current and future demand.",""],[2,"97","8","Professional Body for Agriculturists","A professional body will be established to recognise trained and experienced farmers, farm experts, agricultural technicians and scientists, as professional agriculturists to elevate the standing, image and recognition of the agriculture sector workforce.",""],[2,"98","4","Agricultural Investment Incentive Review","In the agriculture sector, financial incentives for investment, including in building, machinery, training and utilities will be reviewed to catalyse the transition from traditional to modern agriculture.",""],[2,"98","4","Skim Tanam Semula Implementation","The Skim Tanam Semula (STS)7 will be implemented and an endowment fund will be",""],[2,"98","5","Replanting Financing Mechanism Improvement Scheme","established to improve the replanting financing mechanism.",""],[2,"98","9","Smart Farming Fund","A dedicated smart farming fund will be established to accelerate the adoption of modern technology in the agriculture",""],[2,"99","1","Agricultural Modernisation Fund","This fund will offer opportunities for farmers, especially for youth agropreneurs and smallholders to modernise farming activities along the value chain in ensuring food security.",""],[2,"101","6","Expanded Contract Farming Scheme","The contract farming approach will be further expanded in the agriculture sector.",""],[2,"101","6","Smallholder Market Access Support through Anchor Companies and Cooperatives","Through this approach, anchor companies or agricultural cooperatives and associations will provide greater market access for smallholders, particularly for high value agricultural products.",""],[2,"108","3","Agricultural Sector Coordination Mechanism Enhancement","Existing coordination mechanisms in the agriculture sector will be further leveraged to create better synergy among agencies involved in agricultural development to increase efficiency and effectiveness in service delivery.",""],[2,"108","3","State-Level Agricultural Business Development Centres","Business Development Centre will be set up in all states as a one-stop centre to provide multiple agricultural related services, such as agronomic advisory, licence and permit approvals as well as certification and marketing services.",""],[2,"108","3","Agricultural Marketing Collaboration and eCommerce Promotion","Strategic collaboration among ministries, state governments and agencies will be strengthened to improve efficiency in the marketing of agriculture products.",""],[2,"109","3","Agriculture Sector Agency Realignment","The roles and functions of several agencies in the agriculture sector related to training, research and marketing will be reviewed and realigned in modernising the sector.",""],[2,"109","3","IR4.0-Ready Agricultural Modernisation Support","This includes taking into account the needs for IR4.0 technology adaptation, extension services and private sector investment.",""],[2,"109","6","National Agrofood Policy 2021-2030","the National Agrofood Policy 2021-2030 (DAN 2.0), which is being formulated will focus on the application of modern technology in the agrofood subsector to attain higher productivity and income.",""],[2,"109","6","National Food Security Action Plan","An action plan on national food security is also being formulated and is expected to be finalised by the end of 2021.",""]],"156":[[1,"134","5","Smart Farming Framework and Technology Adoption Programme","Smart farming approach will be implemented across all subsectors in the agriculture sector including crops, aquaculture and marine fishery as well as livestock.",""],[1,"134","6","Smart Farming Implementation Framework","A comprehensive framework will be developed as a guideline to support the implementation of smart farming.",""],[1,"134","6","Federal-State Smart Farming Policy Coordination","Collaboration among agencies at Federal and state levels will be enhanced to ensure policies on smart farming are consistent.",""],[1,"134","7","Modern Technology Adoption for Smart Farming","Efforts to accelerate the adoption of modern technologies among farmers will be implemented by encouraging utilisation of big data analytic (BDA), IoT and AI as well as intensifying usage of drones, robotics and sensors.",""],[1,"134","7","Smart Farming Demonstration Projects in Dedicated Food Production Areas","Several dedicated food production areas such as Permanent Food Production Parks and Aquaculture Industrial Zone will be leveraged for the implementation of demonstration projects.",""],[1,"135","1","Smart Farming Investment Incentives","Existing incentives will be improved to promote investments in smart farming that utilise modern technologies and apply green practices.",""],[1,"135","1","Mechanisation and Automation Fund Expansion","The mechanisation and automation fund will be expanded to encourage participation from private companies as well as agricultural cooperatives and associations.",""],[1,"135","1","Dedicated Smart Farming Fund","A dedicated smart farming fund will also be introduced to support the acceleration of modern technology adoption in the agriculture sector.",""],[1,"135","1","Precision Agriculture Rollout in FELDA Plantations","The application of precision agriculture technology in plantations under FELDA through geospatial information systems will be rolled out to improve operational efficiency.",""],[1,"135","2","Smart Farming Information Dissemination and AgF Strengthening","Effective dissemination of information pertaining to modern technologies will be one of the important factors to increase application of smart farming.",""],[1,"135","3","Smart Farming Technology Training Curriculum Review","In this regard, training curricula and modules will be reviewed to incorporate elements of modern technology.",""],[1,"135","3","Farmer Participation in Technological Research","The involvement of farmers including young agropreneurs in technological research will be intensified to ensure farmers are always kept abreast of new developments.",""],[1,"135","3","Agricultural Extension Service Enhancement","Extension services will also be enhanced by appointing successful farmers as technical partners to provide advisory services and guidance in adopting technologies.",""],[1,"135","4","eLadang Programme Enhancement","programmes such as eLadang will be enhanced to encourage participation of technology providers in introducing modern technology and digital solutions to farmers, including ranchers, fishers and smallholders.",""],[1,"135","4","Technology Provider-Farmer Collaboration Promotion","Collaboration between technology providers and farmers will be promoted to inculcate modern technology usage as well as increase accessibility and adoption of affordable smart technology along the agriculture sector value chain.",""],[1,"135","4","Agricultural Outsourcing Services Expansion","Efforts in establishing more agricultural outsourcing services will also be intensified to reduce high capital expenditure and the cost of production incurred by farmers.",""],[2,"134","5","Smart Farming Framework and Adoption Programme","Smart farming approach will be implemented across all subsectors in the agriculture sector including crops, aquaculture and marine fishery as well as livestock.",""],[2,"134","6","Smart Farming Implementation Framework","A comprehensive framework will be developed as a guideline to support the implementation of smart farming.",""],[2,"134","7","Smart Farming Technology Adoption Programme","Efforts to accelerate the adoption of modern technologies among farmers will be implemented by encouraging utilisation of big data analytic (BDA), IoT and AI as well as intensifying usage of drones, robotics and sensors.",""],[2,"134","7","Demonstration Projects in Dedicated Food Production Areas","Several dedicated food production areas such as Permanent Food Production Parks and Aquaculture Industrial Zone will be leveraged for the implementation of demonstration projects.",""],[2,"135","1","Smart Farming Investment Incentives","Existing incentives will be improved to promote investments in smart farming that utilise modern technologies and apply green practices.",""],[2,"135","1","Mechanisation and Automation Fund Expansion","The mechanisation and automation fund will be expanded to encourage participation from private companies as well as agricultural cooperatives and associations.",""],[2,"135","1","Dedicated Smart Farming Fund","A dedicated smart farming fund will also be introduced to support the acceleration of modern technology adoption in the agriculture sector.",""],[2,"135","1","Precision Agriculture Rollout in FELDA Plantations","The application of precision agriculture technology in plantations under FELDA through geospatial information systems will be rolled out to improve operational efficiency.",""],[2,"135","2","Smart Farming Information Dissemination and AgF Strengthening","Effective dissemination of information pertaining to modern technologies will be one of the important factors to increase application of smart farming.",""],[2,"135","3","Smart Farming Technology Training Curriculum Review","training curricula and modules will be reviewed to incorporate elements of modern technology.",""],[2,"135","3","Farmer Participation in Agricultural Technology Research","The involvement of farmers including young agropreneurs in technological research will be intensified to ensure farmers are always kept abreast of new developments.",""],[2,"135","3","Agricultural Extension Service Enhancement Through Technical Partners","Extension services will also be enhanced by appointing successful farmers as technical partners to provide advisory services and guidance in adopting technologies.",""],[2,"135","4","eLadang Enhancement Programme","programmes such as eLadang will be enhanced to encourage participation of technology providers in introducing modern technology and digital solutions to farmers, including ranchers, fishers and smallholders.",""],[2,"135","4","Technology Provider-Farmer Collaboration Promotion","Collaboration between technology providers and farmers will be promoted to inculcate modern technology usage as well as increase accessibility and adoption of affordable smart technology along the agriculture sector value chain.",""],[2,"135","4","Agricultural Outsourcing Services Expansion","Efforts in establishing more agricultural outsourcing services will also be intensified to reduce high capital expenditure and the cost of production incurred by farmers.",""],[2,"135","5","Smart Farming Expansion under FELDA Settlements","The smart farming initiatives through technology providers will also be expanded under the FELDA Program Pembangunan Peneroka to increase the productivity and income of settlers.",""],[2,"135","5","FELDA Smart Farming Pilot Expansion","In this regard, the smart farming pilot project through modern agricultural activities including cash crop, aquaculture and livestock initiated in FELDA Bukit Rokan will be expanded to several other FELDA settlements.",""],[2,"135","5","Modern Agriculture Information, Capacity Building, and Advisory Services","This expansion will involve dissemination of information on modern technologies as well as capacity building and provision of advisory services to the settlers.",""],[2,"135","6","Community Farming Enhancement Incentives","In this regard, incentives will be provided to assist local communities in intensifying the implementation of community farming.",""],[2,"135","6","Smart Farming Adoption for Community Food Production","Food production through community farming will be enhanced by adopting smart farming.",""],[2,"135","6","Public-Private Smart Farming Advisory Services","In addition, public-private collaboration in providing advisory services and suitable smart farming technology for local communities will be enhanced.",""],[2,"146","1","Smart and Cluster Farming on Idle Land","Rural areas will be transformed by optimising idle land for smart and cluster farming activities, as well as employing advanced technology to increase farm produce.",""],[2,"151","13","Idle Land Optimization and Smart Cluster Farming Initiative","Optimising idle land and utilising advanced technology for smart and cluster farming.",""]],"157":[[1,"246","4","Rural Economic Diversification through Idle Land Development","Rural economic activities will be diversified and re-energised, particularly through the development of underutilised land.",""],[1,"246","4","Smart and Cluster Farming Initiative","Smart and cluster farming activities will be undertaken by optimising idle land to increase economies of scale.",""],[1,"246","4","Advanced Technology Adoption for Farm Productivity","This initiative will be implemented by utilising advanced technology to increase the quantity and quality of farm produce.",""],[1,"270","1","Smart and Cluster Farming Initiative","Smart and cluster farming activities will be undertaken by utilising idle land to increase economies of scale, while village cooperatives will be strengthened.",""],[1,"270","2","Modern Agrofood Participation Expansion Measures","Measures will be undertaken to increase participation in the modern agricultural activities to attain higher income.",""],[1,"270","3","Land Management Consolidation and Intercropping Support","Efforts to expand land management consolidation will be undertaken through collaboration between smallholders, cooperatives and associations to generate economies of scale through optimisation of resources.",""],[1,"270","4","Agricultural Input and Financial Support Incentives for Agropreneurs","Incentives including the provision of agricultural inputs, such as seeds, breeds and fertilisers, as well as financial support will be provided to assist agropreneurs in venturing into agricultural activities.",""],[1,"270","4","Agricultural Capacity Building Programme","Capacity building programmes will be provided to improve technical capabilities whilst technical expert teams will be formed through public-private partnership to provide advisory services in increasing agricultural produce.",""],[1,"270","4","Rural Adoption of Modern Agricultural Technologies","Farmers in rural areas will also be encouraged to adopt modern technologies in the production process.",""],[1,"270","4","Agricultural Producer Distribution and Marketing Collaboration","Collaboration between farmers, cooperatives and associations will be strengthened to leverage eCommerce platforms in improving the distribution and marketing of agricultural produce.",""],[2,"246","4","Rural Economic Diversification through Underutilised Land Development","Rural economic activities will be diversified and re-energised, particularly through the development of underutilised land.",""],[2,"246","4","Smart and Cluster Farming Initiative","Smart and cluster farming activities will be undertaken by optimising idle land to increase economies of scale.",""],[2,"246","4","Advanced Technology Adoption for Farm Productivity","This initiative will be implemented by utilising advanced technology to increase the quantity and quality of farm produce.",""],[2,"266","1","High-Value Agrofood and Aquaculture Development in Sabah","Agricultural activities in Sabah will focus on producing high value agrofood, aquaculture, deep sea fishing and dairy produce.",""],[2,"266","1","Ranau and Keningau Vegetable and Dairy Production Development","Ranau and Keningau will be further developed as the main producer of vegetables and dairy products, while Kota Belud has been identified to undertake large scale paddy and fruit farming.",""],[2,"266","1","Upgrade of Dedicated Food Production Areas","Dedicated food production areas such as the Taman Kekal Pengeluaran Makanan (TKPM) and Zon Industri Akuakultur (ZIA) will be upgraded to encourage modern agriculture.",""],[2,"266","1","Modernization of the Deep Sea Fishing Industry","The deep sea fishing industry utilising high-tech fishing vessels will be further encouraged to leverage the availability of resources and competitive advantage.",""],[2,"266","2","Modern Agriculture Transformation in Sarawak Integrated Agricultural Development Areas","The Integrated Agricultural Development Areas of Kalaka Saribas and Samarahan in Sarawak will be transformed into modern agriculture areas.",""],[2,"266","2","Fishery Complex Utilisation and Downstream Development Support","the utilisation of fishery complexes in Tanjung Manis and Tanjong Bako will be optimised in supporting the development of downstream activities.",""],[2,"266","3","Smart Farming and Precision Agriculture Adoption","The utilisation of digital technology will be enhanced through the application of smart farming and precision agriculture along the production value chain.",""],[2,"266","3","Modern Agriculture Capacity Building and Advisory Services","Capacity building and advisory services will be provided to accelerate the adoption of modern agriculture.",""],[2,"266","3","Good Agricultural Practices Promotion","farmers will be encouraged to adopt good agricultural practices such as Malaysian Good Agricultural Practice, Malaysian Sustainable Palm Oil and Malaysian Organic for sustainable agriculture and food safety.",""],[2,"266","3","Agricultural R&D Capacity Enhancement","The capabilities of state agricultural departments and agencies in undertaking research and development activities will be enhanced.",""],[2,"266","3","Agricultural Research Collaboration with HEIs","Collaboration with HEIs in the area of research will also be intensified, focusing on soil testing, production of seeds and breeds, as well as biosecurity control.",""],[2,"266","3","Federal-State Agricultural Development Coordination","collaboration between the Federal and state governments of Sabah and Sarawak in implementing agricultural development will be strengthened.",""],[2,"270","1","Smart and Cluster Farming on Idle Land","Smart and cluster farming activities will be undertaken by utilising idle land to increase economies of scale, while village cooperatives will be strengthened.",""],[2,"270","2","Modern Agrofood Participation Expansion Measures","Measures will be undertaken to increase participation in the modern agricultural activities to attain higher income.",""],[2,"270","2","Land Consolidation and Agricultural Support Package","These measures include expansion of land management consolidation, provision of incentives and financial assistance, enhancement of capacity building and advisory services, as well as the adoption of modern technologies.",""],[2,"270","3","Land Management Consolidation through Smallholder Collaboration","Efforts to expand land management consolidation will be undertaken through collaboration between smallholders, cooperatives and associations to generate economies of scale through optimisation of resources.",""],[2,"270","3","High-Yield Crop Variety Cultivation Support","This approach will also facilitate efforts to cultivate high-yielding and high-demand crop varieties.",""],[2,"270","3","Smallholder Intercropping Income Diversification Programme","Smallholders in the agricommodity subsector, namely oil palm and rubber will also be encouraged to implement intercropping by cultivating pineapples, corn and other cash crops during the replanting period to generate additional income.",""],[2,"270","4","Agricultural Input and Financial Support Incentives","Incentives including the provision of agricultural inputs, such as seeds, breeds and fertilisers, as well as financial support will be provided to assist agropreneurs in venturing into agricultural activities.",""],[2,"270","4","Agricultural Capacity Building Programme","Capacity building programmes will be provided to improve technical capabilities whilst technical expert teams will be formed through public-private partnership to provide advisory services in increasing agricultural produce.",""],[2,"270","4","Modern Agricultural Technology Adoption Support","Farmers in rural areas will also be encouraged to adopt modern technologies in the production process.",""],[2,"270","4","Agricultural eCommerce Collaboration Initiative","Collaboration between farmers, cooperatives and associations will be strengthened to leverage eCommerce platforms in improving the distribution and marketing of agricultural produce.",""]],"158":[[1,"246","5","Program Pembangunan Peneroka Intensification","The Program Pembangunan Peneroka in the FELDA settlements, will be further intensified to increase the income of settlers.",""],[1,"246","6","FELDA Agricultural Technology Support Expansion","technology, will be provided for settlers to venture into agricultural activities, such as cash crop and herbs, cultivation through fertigation method, horticulture, livestock as well as aquaculture.",""],[1,"246","6","FELDA Pilot Project Expansion","The pilot project in FELDA Bukit Rokan, Negeri Sembilan will be expanded to other FELDA settlements nationwide.",""],[1,"246","6","FELDA Transformation Support","the Government will continue supporting FELDA's transformation efforts in moving towards achieving operational and financial sustainability.",""],[2,"246","5","Program Pembangunan Peneroka Intensification","The Program Pembangunan Peneroka in the FELDA settlements, will be further intensified to increase the income of settlers.",""],[2,"246","6","FELDA Settler Agricultural Technology Support","technology, will be provided for settlers to venture into agricultural activities, such as cash crop and herbs, cultivation through fertigation method, horticulture, livestock as well as aquaculture.",""],[2,"246","6","Expansion of FELDA Bukit Rokan Pilot Project","The pilot project in FELDA Bukit Rokan, Negeri Sembilan will be expanded to other FELDA settlements nationwide.",""],[2,"246","6","FELDA Transformation Support","the Government will continue supporting FELDA's transformation efforts in moving towards achieving operational and financial sustainability.",""]],"159":[[1,"117","5","MyDigital Content Programme","The MyDigital Content programme has helped local animation companies to market creative products with intellectual properties (IP), such as Upin & Ipin, Ejen Ali, and Didi and Friends in penetrating local and global markets.",""],[1,"117","5","Culture, Arts and Heritage Sector Support Efforts","Efforts to boost the culture, arts and heritage segment were undertaken to strengthen the contribution of this segment to support the creative industry.",""],[1,"130","2","Creative Industry Ecosystem Development and Growth Acceleration","Measures to accelerate the creative industry growth include developing a holistic ecosystem, upskilling talent to match industry needs as well as strengthening product development and promotion.",""],[1,"130","3","Creative Industry Policy and Governance Framework Review","Existing policies, mainly DIKN and institutional framework will be reviewed to chart a new direction for the industry and support the expansion of local companies into regional and global markets.",""],[1,"130","3","Digital Content Development Framework Improvement","The framework for digital content development will be improved to increase exports, attract investments, by fully utilising local talent and strengthening public- private partnerships.",""],[1,"130","4","National Creative Industry Development Council","The National Creative Industry Development Council, led by the Ministry of Communications and Multimedia Malaysia and Ministry of Tourism, Arts and Culture (MOTAC), will be the overarching platform to drive the creative industry development.","Ministry of Communications and Multimedia Malaysia | Ministry of Tourism, Arts and Culture (MOTAC)"],[1,"130","4","Creative Industry Satellite Account","A satellite account for the creative industry will be developed to facilitate data collection and analysis, further augmenting evidence-based decision-making in realising the industry's potential.",""],[1,"130","4","Creative Industry Database Development","A comprehensive database will also be established to facilitate better planning, monitoring and assessment.",""],[1,"130","4","Creative Industry Financing Incentives","Financing mechanisms, including incentives, will be enhanced to accelerate the growth of the creative industry.",""],[1,"130","4","Public Facility Access for Creative Products and Services","Existing government facilities, including those for cultural programmes under the Jabatan Kebudayaan dan Kesenian Negara (JKKN) and Istana Budaya, will be made available for private entities to optimise, in promoting and showcasing creative products and services.",""],[1,"130","4","Intellectual Property Awareness Campaign for Creative Content","Concerted efforts will be undertaken to increase awareness of the importance of IP in improving creative content production and protection as well as increasing income-generating capability.",""],[1,"130","5","Creative Industry Talent Development Programme","more focus will be given to developing talent in the creative space, by aligning it with the national science, technology and innovation agenda.",""],[1,"130","5","Specialised Creative Industry Training and Learning Opportunities","Efforts will include establishing specialised training and learning opportunities that meet industry requirements.",""],[1,"130","5","Creative Talent Upskilling and Reskilling Initiative","Upskilling and reskilling of talent will be accelerated in various areas, including animation, movie-making and gaming.",""],[1,"130","5","Regional eSports and Digital Content Hub","A regional platform for eSports, digital content regional hub and the Creator's Studio will be established to meet the demand of the evolving creative content industry.",""],[1,"130","5","Continuous Updating of Creative Talent Training Programmes","institutions related to talent development will be encouraged to continuously update training programmes to produce quality talent in various fields such as music, fashion and design.",""],[1,"130","5","Expansion of Creative Industry Subjects in TVET Institutions","The teaching and learning of creative industry-related subjects, particularly multimedia, digital technology and fashion design, will be expanded to more TVET institutions nationwide.",""],[1,"130","6","Creative Industry R&D Capacity Enhancement","R&D capacity will be augmented to ensure sustainability and maximise the potential of creative goods and services.",""],[1,"130","6","Digital Promotion Platforms for Creative Goods and Services","Mobile applications and online platforms will be further leveraged to strengthen product development and promotion.",""],[1,"130","6","Digital Enhancement of Cultural and Heritage Attractions","Cultural and heritage products, including museums and galleries, will be enhanced by utilising technology, comprising among others, infographics and information-sharing tools, to provide a wholesome experience.",""],[1,"130","6","Digital Platforms for Malaysian Brand Promotion and Export","Digital platforms will be adopted to promote and export the Malaysian brand, capitalising on unique local destinations, food and culture.",""]],"160":[[2,"162","1","Arts and Culture Unity Programmes","Efforts to increase understanding and tolerance among ethnics were undertaken through various arts and culture programmes.",""],[2,"181","2","Unity Programme Expansion","Social interaction will be encouraged by improving and expanding unity programmes such as Kawasan Rukun Tetangga and Skim Rondaan Sukarela programmes.",""],[2,"181","2","Cultural Festivals and Heritage Awareness Programme","More cultural programmes and festivals will be organised to promote understanding and expose the rakyat, especially youth and children, to traditional customs and culture of various ethnic groups in Malaysia.",""],[2,"181","2","Museum, Memorial, Art Gallery, and Heritage Site Activities","Activities in museums, memorials and art galleries as well as historical sites will be intensified to increase the understanding and exposure to the rich history and cultural diversity of the nation.",""]],"161":[[1,"131","1","Tourism Industry Re-energisation Programme","During the Twelfth Plan period, the tourism industry will be re-energised to cater to tourists needs amid higher demands for improved safety and hygiene measures.",""],[1,"131","3","Tourism Product Value-Addition and Packaging Initiative","The value and impact of tourism products and services will be strengthened by capitalising on content, storytelling and packaging, to cater to changing demands of tourists who seek experiential- based tourism activities.",""],[1,"131","3","Ecotourism Product Promotion Initiative","Ecotourism products and services, which distinctly portray Malaysian experiences, will be promoted as premier products targeting high value tourists.",""],[1,"131","3","Community-Based Homestay and Handicraft Participation Programme","Local communities will be engaged to increase their participation in providing unique homestay experiences, producing handicrafts and offering tour guide services, which will improve their economic wellbeing.",""],[1,"131","4","Cultural Heritage Tourism Promotion","Malaysian culture, arts and heritage will be leveraged to further boost tourism promotional efforts.",""],[1,"131","4","Heritage and Culture Showcase Campaign","These efforts will focus on showcasing Malaysia's unique heritage and culture, such as festivals, traditional dances and gastronomic experiences.",""],[1,"131","4","Private Sector Tourism Services Enhancement","The role of the private sector in providing enhanced tourist services at government- owned facilities such as museums, galleries and JKKN complexes will be strengthened.",""],[1,"131","4","Agile Tourism Business Model Reform","In this regard, a more agile and effective business model will be introduced to enable the private sector to complement government efforts.",""],[1,"131","4","MICE and Shopping Destination Promotion","Measures will also be undertaken to promote Malaysia as the first-choice destination for MICE events and shopping.",""],[1,"132","7","Domestic Tourism Incentives and Promotional Campaigns","Incentives and promotional campaigns will be intensified, ensuring the tourism industry is revived to be robust and capable of withstanding any shocks.",""],[1,"132","7","Digital Platforms for Domestic Tourism Promotion","Digital platforms will be aggressively utilised to entice domestic travellers to explore local sights and scenes.",""],[1,"132","7","Community-Based Tourism Homestay Packages","In addition, community-based tourism that offers a homestay experience will be aggressively promoted through attractive and unique packages such as living as a fisherman, living in a longhouse and living a kampung life.",""],[2,"131","1","Tourism Industry Re-energisation Programme","During the Twelfth Plan period, the tourism industry will be re-energised to cater to tourists needs amid higher demands for improved safety and hygiene measures.",""],[2,"131","2","Tourism Safety and Hygiene Branding Campaign","a campaign to inculcate socially responsible culture and restore tourist confidence will be launched.",""],[2,"131","2","Technology Adoption for Contact-Minimizing Business Operations","Businesses will be encouraged to adopt advanced technology, such as automation, robotics and AI, to minimise physical interaction with customers thus reducing risks in the spread of infectious diseases.",""],[2,"131","3","Tourism Product Value Enhancement and Ecotourism Promotion","The value and impact of tourism products and services will be strengthened by capitalising on content, storytelling and packaging, to cater to changing demands of tourists who seek experiential- based tourism activities.",""],[2,"131","3","Community-Based Homestay, Handicraft, and Tour Guide Support","Local communities will be engaged to increase their participation in providing unique homestay experiences, producing handicrafts and offering tour guide services, which will improve their economic wellbeing.",""],[2,"131","4","Cultural Heritage Tourism Promotion","Malaysian culture, arts and heritage will be leveraged to further boost tourism promotional efforts.",""],[2,"131","4","Heritage and Cultural Experience Promotion Campaign","These efforts will focus on showcasing Malaysia's unique heritage and culture, such as festivals, traditional dances and gastronomic experiences.",""],[2,"131","4","Review of Compensation for Art Practitioners","In ensuring the sustainability of the local heritage and culture, compensation and appreciation to art practitioners will be reviewed.",""],[2,"131","4","Private Sector Tourism Services Partnership Model","The role of the private sector in providing enhanced tourist services at government- owned facilities such as museums, galleries and JKKN complexes will be strengthened.",""],[2,"131","4","Agile Tourism Business Model Reform","In this regard, a more agile and effective business model will be introduced to enable the private sector to complement government efforts.",""],[2,"131","4","Malaysia MICE and Shopping Destination Promotion","Measures will also be undertaken to promote Malaysia as the first-choice destination for MICE events and shopping.",""],[2,"132","1","Digital Innovation and Virtual Tourism Promotion","Industry players will be encouraged to innovate and adopt digital technology in enhancing the sustainability of tourism products.",""],[2,"132","1","Online Cultural and Handicraft Market Expansion","Online marketplaces will also be utilised to complement arts and handicraft complexes including Kompleks Kraftangan and Balai Seni to enable wider market access and increase the visibility of local arts and crafts globally.",""],[2,"132","3","Malaysia National Brand Positioning Strategy","Efforts to enhance Malaysia as a brand that incorporates the identity, essence, image and culture of the nation, will be implemented through distinct brand positioning strategies.",""],[2,"132","3","Aggressive National Marketing and Promotional Campaigns","Aggressive marketing and promotional campaigns, which focus on differentiating Malaysia from its competitors and building a distinct market, will be pursued.",""],[2,"132","4","Malaysia Truly Asia Brand Revitalisation","The Malaysia Truly Asia tagline will be revitalised to leverage the brand recognition and value built through past efforts.",""],[2,"132","4","Tour Package Development and Marketing","Attractive tour packages will continue to be developed and marketed, showcasing destinations and activities that include culture, arts and heritage elements to provide a unique experience.",""],[2,"132","4","Digital Tourism Platform Enablement","Digital platforms will be harnessed to realise tourism-related aspirations.",""],[2,"132","5","Travel Facilitation and Air Connectivity Enhancement","travel to and from Malaysia will be made more efficient by improving travel facilitation and enhancing air connectivity.",""],[2,"132","7","Domestic Tourism Incentives and Promotional Campaigns","Incentives and promotional campaigns will be intensified, ensuring the tourism industry is revived to be robust and capable of withstanding any shocks.",""],[2,"132","7","Digital Platforms for Domestic Tourism Promotion","Digital platforms will be aggressively utilised to entice domestic travellers to explore local sights and scenes.",""],[2,"132","7","Community-Based Homestay Tourism Promotion","community-based tourism that offers a homestay experience will be aggressively promoted through attractive and unique packages such as living as a fisherman, living in a longhouse and living a kampung life.",""]],"162":[[1,"131","2","Tourism Safety and Hygiene Branding Campaign","a campaign to inculcate socially responsible culture and restore tourist confidence will be launched.",""],[1,"131","2","Business Adoption of Automation, Robotics, and AI","Businesses will be encouraged to adopt advanced technology, such as automation, robotics and AI, to minimise physical interaction with customers thus reducing risks in the spread of infectious diseases.",""],[1,"131","3","Ecotourism Site Monitoring Mechanism","Specific monitoring mechanisms will be established at ecotourism destinations, such as Kilim Geoforest Park in Kedah, Royal Belum State Park in Perak, Danum Valley in Sabah and Mulu National Park in Sarawak to ensure the sanctity and sustainability of these sites.",""],[1,"131","3","Private Sector Ecotourism Management Improvement Measures","Measures will also be undertaken to encourage the private sector to improve management and profitability, and ultimately ensuring the preservation and conservation of such sites.",""],[1,"132","2","Green Tourism Sustainability and Carrying Capacity Measures","Sustainable consumption and production practices, including the adoption of green labels, will be further encouraged.",""],[1,"132","2","Tourism Pricing Mechanism Review","The pricing mechanisms for tourism products and services will be reviewed to commensurate with the value offered.",""]],"163":[[1,"266","7","Replication of Sustainable Ecotourism Management Practices","The successful public-private partnership and carrying capacity practice at the Mulu Caves of Sarawak and the Sipadan Island of Sabah will be replicated across other local sites in the interest of preservation, thereby improving the livelihoods of the local community and improving the sites' long-term economic viability.",""],[1,"266","7","Tourism Facilities and Infrastructure Improvement","specific initiatives will be undertaken to improve tourism facilities and infrastructure to increase accessibility to the major attractions in these states.",""],[1,"266","8","Tailored Tourism Promotional Campaigns for Sabah and Sarawak","Promotional campaigns will also be tailored to celebrate the unique qualities of Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[1,"266","8","Tourism Safety and Hygiene Confidence Restoration Initiative","Efforts to restore confidence among tourists following the effects of COVID-19, will be carried out with strong commitment from the industry in applying the best safety and hygiene standards.",""],[1,"266","8","Tourism Governance and Implementation Mechanism Improvement","The overall governance and implementation mechanism of tourism development will also be improved to ensure that planned strategies and initiatives come to fruition.",""],[1,"266","8","New Tourism Markets and Route Development","In addition, identifying and establishing new markets and routes, along with targeted promotional efforts in specific markets will boost tourist arrivals in Sarawak.",""],[1,"266","8","Strategic Airline and Foreign Travel Agent Partnerships","Strategic partnerships with airlines and foreign travel agents will be strengthened to establish more international",""],[2,"266","7","Replication of Ecotourism Public-Private Partnership and Carrying Capacity Practices","The successful public-private partnership and carrying capacity practice at the Mulu Caves of Sarawak and the Sipadan Island of Sabah will be replicated across other local sites in the interest of preservation, thereby improving the livelihoods of the local community and improving the sites' long-term economic viability.",""],[2,"266","7","Tourism Facilities and Infrastructure Improvement Initiative","specific initiatives will be undertaken to improve tourism facilities and infrastructure to increase accessibility to the major attractions in these states.",""],[2,"266","8","Tailored Tourism Promotional Campaigns for Sabah and Sarawak","Promotional campaigns will also be tailored to celebrate the unique qualities of Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[2,"266","8","Tourism Confidence Restoration and Safety Standards Initiative","Efforts to restore confidence among tourists following the effects of COVID-19, will be carried out with strong commitment from the industry in applying the best safety and hygiene standards.",""],[2,"266","8","Tourism Governance and Implementation Mechanism Improvement","The overall governance and implementation mechanism of tourism development will also be improved to ensure that planned strategies and initiatives come to fruition.",""],[2,"266","8","New Tourism Markets and Route Development","In addition, identifying and establishing new markets and routes, along with targeted promotional efforts in specific markets will boost tourist arrivals in Sarawak.",""],[2,"266","8","Strategic Airline and Foreign Travel Agent Partnerships","Strategic partnerships with airlines and foreign travel agents will be strengthened to establish more international",""],[2,"267","1","Tourism Industry Expansion in Sarawak","This will expand the tourism industry in Sarawak, benefitting not only local communities and the state but also the nation at large.",""],[2,"270","7","Urban Waterfront Tourism and Economic Activity Promotion","The uniqueness of these two cities with a vibrant waterfront area will be leveraged to promote tourism and economic activities.",""],[2,"270","8","Secondary City Economic Development and Investment Attraction Initiative","Efforts to increase the potential of cities in other division areas in the states will focus on enhancing economic activities to spur development.",""]],"164":[[1,"135","7","Comprehensive Biomass Policy and High-Value Biomass Industry Development","The measures will include formulating a comprehensive biomass policy, developing local technology through R&D&C&I, accelerating the development of high value-added products and services and promoting utilisation of high value-added biomass products.",""],[1,"135","8","National Biomass Policy Framework","A national biomass policy will be formulated as a comprehensive framework to ensure the sustainable development of the industry and unlock its economic potential.",""],[1,"135","8","Biomass Agency Coordination and Collaboration Measures","The policy will prescribe measures to strengthen collaboration and coordination among related agencies to ensure effective implementation.",""],[1,"135","8","Biomass Value Chain Business Model Development","In addition, an effective business model will be developed to facilitate better profit-sharing mechanisms among stakeholders along the value chain.",""],[1,"135","8","Holistic Biomass Database Development","A holistic biomass database will be developed to integrate biomass information along the value chain, from bio-resource supply to bio-energy and bio-product markets.",""],[1,"136","1","Advanced Biomass Conversion Technology Development","Local capabilities in the biomass industry need to be enhanced in developing and adopting advanced biomass conversion technologies that are sustainable, reliable and cost-effective.",""],[1,"136","1","Biomass Research, Development, Commercialisation and Innovation Intensification","R&D&C&I activities by research institutions, HEIs and Government-linked companies (GLCs) will be intensified to further create value from biomass resources.",""],[1,"136","1","Biomass Research Investment Support and Advisory Services","The private sector will also be encouraged to invest in research-driven activities related to biomass through financial assistance and advisory services.",""],[1,"136","1","Green Financing and Tax Incentive Enhancement","Additionally, existing incentives, such as the Green Technology Financing Scheme, Green Investment Tax Allowance, and Green Income Tax Exemption will be enhanced to attract more investors including MSMEs.",""],[1,"136","2","Biomass Industry Commercialisation and Innovation Programme","Commercialisation and innovation in the biomass industry will be intensified to produce a diverse range of high value-added products and services.",""],[1,"136","2","Government-Private Sector Collaboration for Biomass Industry Development","Collaboration between the government and the private sector will be strengthened to support the development of this industry.",""],[1,"136","3","Biomass Logistics Financial Assistance Scheme","Financial assistance for logistics will be provided to attract companies and cooperatives to actively participate in biomass logistics services.",""],[1,"136","3","Biomass Supply Consistency Support Measures","These initiatives will facilitate efforts in ensuring consistency of feedstock supply.",""],[1,"136","3","Biomass Industry Financial Institution Engagement","Meanwhile, financial institutions will be actively engaged to increase awareness of the prospects in the biomass industry.",""],[1,"136","4","Domestic Biomass Utilisation and Export Promotion","efforts will be intensified to increase the domestic utilisation of biomass- related products as well as leverage its potential in generating high value exports.",""],[1,"136","4","Biomass Strategic Communication Plan","A strategic communication plan will be crafted to streamline all biomass public awareness and education programmes as well as advocacy efforts.",""],[1,"136","4","Biomass Public Awareness and Education Campaign","social awareness activities will be strengthened to increase public awareness of the benefits and contributions of biomass products to environmental sustainability.",""],[1,"136","4","Public-Private Biomass Market Expansion Partnerships","public-private collaborations will be intensified to explore and penetrate new markets.",""],[2,"135","7","Comprehensive Biomass Policy and Industry Upgrading","The measures will include formulating a comprehensive biomass policy, developing local technology through R&D&C&I, accelerating the development of high value-added products and services and promoting utilisation of high value-added biomass products.",""],[2,"135","8","National Biomass Policy Framework","A national biomass policy will be formulated as a comprehensive framework to ensure the sustainable development of the industry and unlock its economic potential.",""],[2,"135","8","Biomass Value Chain Profit-Sharing Business Model","In addition, an effective business model will be developed to facilitate better profit-sharing mechanisms among stakeholders along the value chain.",""],[2,"135","8","Holistic Biomass Database Development","A holistic biomass database will be developed to integrate biomass information along the value chain, from bio-resource supply to bio-energy and bio-product markets.",""],[2,"136","1","Biomass Technology Development and Adoption Programme","Local capabilities in the biomass industry need to be enhanced in developing and adopting advanced biomass conversion technologies that are sustainable, reliable and cost-effective.",""],[2,"136","1","Biomass Research, Development, Commercialisation and Innovation Intensification","R&D&C&I activities by research institutions, HEIs and Government-linked companies (GLCs) will be intensified to further create value from biomass resources.",""],[2,"136","1","Private Sector Biomass Research Investment Support","The private sector will also be encouraged to invest in research-driven activities related to biomass through financial assistance and advisory services.",""],[2,"136","1","Green Financing and Tax Incentive Enhancement","Additionally, existing incentives, such as the Green Technology Financing Scheme, Green Investment Tax Allowance, and Green Income Tax Exemption will be enhanced to attract more investors including MSMEs.",""],[2,"136","2","Biomass Industry Commercialisation and Innovation Programme","Commercialisation and innovation in the biomass industry will be intensified to produce a diverse range of high value-added products and services.",""],[2,"136","2","Biomass Industry Government-Private Sector Collaboration Mechanism","Collaboration between the government and the private sector will be strengthened to support the development of this industry.",""],[2,"136","3","Biomass Feedstock Collection and Pre-treatment Facility Incentives","Incentives will be introduced to encourage the development of collection, aggregation and pre-treatment facilities for biomass feedstock to strengthen the value chain.",""],[2,"136","3","Biomass Logistics Financial Assistance Scheme","Financial assistance for logistics will be provided to attract companies and cooperatives to actively participate in biomass logistics services.",""],[2,"136","3","Biomass Industry Financial Institution Engagement","Meanwhile, financial institutions will be actively engaged to increase awareness of the prospects in the biomass industry.",""],[2,"136","4","Biomass Domestic Utilisation and Export Promotion","efforts will be intensified to increase the domestic utilisation of biomass- related products as well as leverage its potential in generating high value exports",""],[2,"136","4","Biomass Strategic Communication Plan","A strategic communication plan will be crafted to streamline all biomass public awareness and education programmes as well as advocacy efforts",""],[2,"136","4","Biomass Public Awareness and Education Campaign","social awareness activities will be strengthened to increase public awareness of the benefits and contributions of biomass products to environmental sustainability",""],[2,"136","4","Biomass Public-Private Market Expansion Partnerships","public-private collaborations will be intensified to explore and penetrate new markets",""]],"165":[[1,"109","7","Natural Gas Industry Roadmap Development","A roadmap will be developed to chart the direction of the natural gas industry in optimising demand growth, ensuring security of supply and liberalising the market to enhance efficiency and competitiveness.",""],[1,"109","7","Gas Subsector Strategy Formulation","efforts will be undertaken to formulate strategies in capitalising potential of the gas subsector to position Malaysia as a regional gas trading hub.",""]],"166":[[1,"263","9","Sabah Electricity Supply System Augmentation","The Sabah electricity supply system will be further augmented through the construction and upgrading of generation facilities, as well as transmission and distribution networks.",""],[1,"263","9","Sabah East-West Grid Power Station and Transmission Upgrade","The issue of insufficient power generation in the east coast of Sabah will be resolved through the construction of a new power station and transmission upgrading works in the Sabah East-West Grid.",""],[1,"263","9","Southern Link Transmission Network Project","Additionally, the Southern Link transmission network project will start with initial work in the Twelfth Plan.",""],[1,"263","9","Incentive-Based Regulation Framework for Electricity Supply","The Incentive-Based Regulation framework will be introduced to improve the quality and efficiency of electricity supply.",""],[1,"263","10","Baleh Hydroelectric Project","The Sarawak electricity system will be further strengthened with the implementation of the 1,285 megawatt Baleh hydroelectric project that is expected to be completed in 2025.",""],[1,"263","10","Sarawak 500 KV Transmission Line Expansion","Sarawak will expand its 500 KV transmission line as the second transmission backbone.",""],[1,"263","10","Northern Grid Development","In addition, the Northern Grid will be developed to expand the State",""],[1,"264","1","Statewide Grid System Expansion","Grid System to cover the whole state.",""],[2,"263","9","Sabah Electricity Supply System Augmentation","The Sabah electricity supply system will be further augmented through the construction and upgrading of generation facilities, as well as transmission and distribution networks.",""],[2,"263","9","Sabah East-West Grid Power Station and Transmission Upgrade","The issue of insufficient power generation in the east coast of Sabah will be resolved through the construction of a new power station and transmission upgrading works in the Sabah East-West Grid.",""],[2,"263","9","Southern Link Transmission Network Project","Additionally, the Southern Link transmission network project will start with initial work in the Twelfth Plan.",""],[2,"263","9","Incentive-Based Regulation Framework for Electricity Supply","The Incentive-Based Regulation framework will be introduced to improve the quality and efficiency of electricity supply.",""],[2,"263","10","Baleh Hydroelectric Project","The Sarawak electricity system will be further strengthened with the implementation of the 1,285 megawatt Baleh hydroelectric project that is expected to be completed in 2025.",""],[2,"263","10","Sarawak 500 KV Transmission Line Expansion","Sarawak will expand its 500 KV transmission line as the second transmission backbone.",""],[2,"263","10","Northern Grid Development","In addition, the Northern Grid will be developed to expand the State",""],[2,"264","1","Grid System Expansion","Grid System to cover the whole state.",""]],"167":[[1,"276","1","Transfer of Gas and Electricity Regulatory Powers under MA63","The process of handing over the regulatory power for gas and electricity under MA63 will be continued in the Twelfth Plan.",""],[1,"276","1","Amendment of Existing Energy Regulatory Laws and Establishment of a Regulatory Body","a number of provisions in the existing law will be amended while a regulatory body will be established.",""],[1,"276","1","Federal Financial Support for Existing Grid Infrastructure Projects","the Federal Government will continue to provide financial support in the implementation of existing infrastructure projects.",""],[1,"276","1","Reduction of Sabah's Dependence on Tariff Support Subsidies","Efforts will also be undertaken to gradually reduce dependency of the State Government of Sabah on the tariff support subsidies.",""],[2,"259","4","Transfer of Gas and Electricity Regulatory Powers to Sabah","The Federal Government has agreed in principle on the handing over of regulatory power for gas and electricity supply to the State Government of Sabah.",""],[2,"263","9","Incentive-Based Regulation Framework for Electricity Supply","The Incentive-Based Regulation framework will be introduced to improve the quality and efficiency of electricity supply.",""],[2,"276","1","Transfer of Gas and Electricity Regulatory Powers under MA63","The process of handing over the regulatory power for gas and electricity under MA63 will be continued in the Twelfth Plan.",""],[2,"276","1","Amendment of Existing Energy Laws and Establishment of Regulatory Body","a number of provisions in the existing law will be amended while a regulatory body will be established.",""],[2,"276","1","Federal Financial Support for Existing Grid Infrastructure Projects","the Federal Government will continue to provide financial support in the implementation of existing infrastructure projects.",""],[2,"276","1","Reduction of Sabah Tariff Support Subsidy Dependence","Efforts will also be undertaken to gradually reduce dependency of the State Government of Sabah on the tariff support subsidies.",""]],"168":[[1,"281","1","National Energy Policy Formulation","A comprehensive national energy policy will be formulated to streamline and harmonise all energy-related policies, thus providing an overarching framework to address issues across energy-consuming sectors.",""],[1,"281","1","Renewable Energy Expansion and Energy Efficiency Measures","Furthermore, renewable energy as an alternative energy source will be augmented to complement energy efficiency measures.",""],[1,"281","1","Energy Demand-Side Management","These measures will focus on demand side management, resulting in the prudent and efficient management of energy.",""],[1,"290","16","Energy Demand Side Management Master Plan","Formulation of an Energy Demand Side Management (DSM) Master Plan",""],[1,"300","2","Low-Carbon Energy Scale-Up through Renewable Energy and Energy Efficiency","Efforts to pursue low-carbon energy through RE and EE will be scaled-up to reduce GHG emissions.",""],[1,"300","2","Renewable Energy Industry Diversification into Floating Solar and Waste-to-Energy","The RE industry will be encouraged to venture into floating solar and waste-to-energy projects.",""],[1,"300","2","Promotion of Renewable Energy Technologies and Certificates","The use of existing and new technologies, namely cogeneration, solar thermal and fuel cell will be further promoted to expand options available to the industry.",""],[1,"300","3","Energy Efficiency and Conservation Act","the use of energy by high-intensity consumers in the industrial and commercial sectors will be regulated through the introduction of the EE and conservation act",""],[1,"300","3","Energy Audit Conditional Grants","Energy Audit Conditional Grants will continue to be provided to selected industrial and commercial sectors",""],[1,"300","4","PETRONAS Net Zero and Low-Carbon Transition Initiatives","PETRONAS has declared its target to achieve net zero carbon emissions by 2050.",""],[1,"300","4","Clean Energy and Low-Carbon Solutions Delivery","The company has put in place plans to deliver clean energy and low-carbon solutions globally.",""],[1,"300","4","Methane Reduction and Production Optimization Measures","PETRONAS will also undertake several initiatives, including reducing hydrocarbon flaring and venting, capturing methane emissions and optimising production and operations.",""],[1,"300","5","Low-Carbon Energy and Solutions Development","providing low-carbon energy and solutions, such as natural gas and RE; developing low and zero carbon fuels, products and solutions; and investing in nature-based solutions by preserving and restoring the capacity of forest ecosystems to act as carbon sinks.",""],[1,"326","2","Institutional and Regulatory Framework Improvement","Efforts will be undertaken to improve institutional and regulatory frameworks.",""],[1,"326","2","National Energy Policy Development","A comprehensive national energy policy will be introduced to strengthen the oil and gas and electricity ecosystems.",""],[1,"329","1","Energy Sector Sustainability Initiatives","Initiatives will be focused to enhance the sustainability of the energy sector.",""],[1,"329","1","Market Liberalisation Communication Plan","A comprehensive communication plan on market liberalisation will also be developed to provide clear information to the energy fraternity and the rakyat.",""],[1,"329","5","Comprehensive Single Energy Policy","Two key initiatives will be implemented to address the energy cross-sectoral predicaments, namely the formulation of a comprehensive single energy policy",""],[1,"329","5","Systematic Energy Sector Communication Plan","Two key initiatives will be implemented to address the energy cross-sectoral predicaments, namely ... the establishment of a systematic communication plan.",""],[1,"329","6","Single Energy Policy Formulation","The existing energy-related policies will be streamlined and harmonised to formulate a long-term comprehensive single energy policy.",""],[1,"329","7","Energy Reform Communication Plan","Thus, a comprehensive communication plan will be developed to strengthen collaboration with stakeholders as well as facilitate efforts to educate consumers and increase awareness of the rationale for market liberalisation.",""],[1,"339","1","Energy Market Liberalisation and Electricity Supply Resilience Reform","In the Twelfth Plan, priority will be given to transform the energy market through market liberalisation of the gas and enhance the resilience of the electricity supply industry to be future-proof.",""],[2,"266","4","National Natural Gas Roadmap","Initiatives under both plans will be taken into account in formulating the national natural gas roadmap.",""],[2,"281","1","Comprehensive National Energy Policy","A comprehensive national energy policy will be formulated to streamline and harmonise all energy-related policies, thus providing an overarching framework to address issues across energy-consuming sectors.",""],[2,"281","1","Renewable Energy Expansion and Energy Efficiency Measures","Furthermore, renewable energy as an alternative energy source will be augmented to complement energy efficiency measures.",""],[2,"281","1","Demand-Side Energy Management Measures","These measures will focus on demand side management, resulting in the prudent and efficient management of energy.",""],[2,"283","9","Green Policy, Regulatory, and Financing Instruments","Enhancing policies, regulations, green financing and economic instruments.",""],[2,"329","5","Comprehensive Single Energy Policy","Two key initiatives will be implemented to address the energy cross-sectoral predicaments, namely the formulation of a comprehensive single energy policy",""],[2,"329","5","Systematic Energy Sector Communication Plan","Two key initiatives will be implemented to address the energy cross-sectoral predicaments, namely ... the establishment of a systematic communication plan",""],[2,"329","6","Single Comprehensive Energy Policy","The existing energy-related policies will be streamlined and harmonised to formulate a long-term comprehensive single energy policy.",""],[2,"329","7","Energy Reform Communication Plan","Thus, a comprehensive communication plan will be developed to strengthen collaboration with stakeholders as well as facilitate efforts to educate consumers and increase awareness of the rationale for market liberalisation.",""]],"169":[[1,"319","2","Energy Efficiency and Conservation Bill","The plan to introduce a demand side management (DSM) masterplan was replaced with the formulation of the energy efficiency and conservation bill.",""],[1,"320","5","Comprehensive Demand Side Management Master Plan","Formulation of a Comprehensive Demand Side Management (DSM) Master Plan",""],[1,"321","5","Energy Efficiency and Conservation Bill","Several initiatives were undertaken to improve energy efficiency (EE), including the formulation of the Energy Efficiency and Conservation bill in 2020 to regulate energy demand on electricity and thermal use.",""],[1,"321","5","Minimum Energy Performance Standard Expansion","The EE labelling initiatives were intensified through the expansion of the Minimum Energy Performance Standard (MEPS) and the National Building Energy Intensity (BEI).",""],[1,"321","5","National Building Energy Intensity Labelling Programme","The EE labelling initiatives were intensified through the expansion of the Minimum Energy Performance Standard (MEPS) and the National Building Energy Intensity (BEI).",""],[1,"332","1","Energy Efficiency and Conservation Regulation","the use of energy by high-intensity consumers in the industrial and commercial sectors will be regulated through the formulation of an act related to energy efficiency and conservation.",""],[1,"332","1","Energy Audit Conditional Grants","the Energy Audit Conditional Grants (EACG) will continue to be given to selected industrial and commercial sectors to enhance energy efficiency.",""],[1,"332","1","Energy Performance Contracting for Government Buildings","the energy audit and retrofitting activities will be expanded to more government buildings through the Energy Performance Contracting (EPC) initiative to accelerate the implementation of EE programmes.",""],[2,"290","16","Energy Demand Side Management Master Plan","Formulation of an Energy Demand Side Management (DSM) Master Plan",""],[2,"292","5","Minimum Energy Performance Standard and Building Energy Intensity Programmes","As for energy-efficient related initiatives, the Minimum Energy Performance Standard and the National Building Energy Intensity (BEI) programmes were intensified.",""],[2,"292","5","Expansion of Energy Efficiency Labelling for Domestic Appliances","The EE labelling for domestic appliances was extended to include microwave ovens and electric rice cookers, increasing the number to eight appliances.",""],[2,"300","3","Energy Efficiency and Conservation Act","the use of energy by high-intensity consumers in the industrial and commercial sectors will be regulated through the introduction of the EE and conservation act",""],[2,"300","3","Energy Audit Conditional Grants","Energy Audit Conditional Grants will continue to be provided to selected industrial and commercial sectors",""],[2,"319","2","Energy Efficiency and Conservation Bill","The plan to introduce a demand side management (DSM) masterplan was replaced with the formulation of the energy efficiency and conservation bill.",""],[2,"320","5","Comprehensive Demand Side Management Master Plan","Formulation of a Comprehensive Demand Side Management (DSM) Master Plan",""],[2,"321","5","Energy Efficiency and Conservation Bill","Several initiatives were undertaken to improve energy efficiency (EE), including the formulation of the Energy Efficiency and Conservation bill in 2020 to regulate energy demand on electricity and thermal use.",""],[2,"321","5","Minimum Energy Performance Standard Expansion","The EE labelling initiatives were intensified through the expansion of the Minimum Energy Performance Standard (MEPS) and the National Building Energy Intensity (BEI).",""],[2,"321","5","National Building Energy Intensity Labelling Programme","The EE labelling initiatives were intensified through the expansion of the Minimum Energy Performance Standard (MEPS) and the National Building Energy Intensity (BEI).",""],[2,"332","1","Energy Efficiency and Conservation Act","the use of energy by high-intensity consumers in the industrial and commercial sectors will be regulated through the formulation of an act related to energy efficiency and conservation.",""],[2,"332","1","Energy Audit Conditional Grants","the Energy Audit Conditional Grants (EACG) will continue to be given to selected industrial and commercial sectors to enhance energy efficiency.",""],[2,"332","1","Energy Performance Contracting for Government Buildings","the energy audit and retrofitting activities will be expanded to more government buildings through the Energy Performance Contracting (EPC) initiative to accelerate the implementation of EE programmes.",""]],"170":[[1,"321","3","Cleaner Fuels Promotion Programme","Cleaner fuels continued to be promoted towards reducing greenhouse gas emissions to combat climate change.",""],[1,"329","8","Biofuel Usage Scale-Up","biofuel usage be scaled-up",""],[1,"330","3","Transportation Sector Biodiesel Blend Upgrade","The biodiesel blend for the transportation sector will be continuously upgraded from B153 to B204 and eventually to B305.",""],[1,"330","3","B30 Biodiesel Depot Upgrade Assessment","Assessment will be conducted to identify the gaps and costs required to upgrade blending depots to be B30-compliant.",""],[1,"330","3","Stakeholder Engagement on B30 Biodiesel Acceptance","more engagement with stakeholders will be held to address issues of manufacturers' acceptance of B30.",""],[1,"330","3","Industry Sector Biodiesel Programme Expansion","For the industry sector, the biodiesel programme will be expanded from B7 to B10.",""],[2,"330","3","Transport Sector Biodiesel Blend Upgrade","The biodiesel blend for the transportation sector will be continuously upgraded from B153 to B204 and eventually to B305.",""],[2,"330","3","B30 Biodiesel Depot Upgrade Assessment","Assessment will be conducted to identify the gaps and costs required to upgrade blending depots to be B30-compliant.",""],[2,"330","3","Stakeholder Engagement on B30 Acceptance","more engagement with stakeholders will be held to address issues of manufacturers' acceptance of B30.",""],[2,"330","3","Industry Biodiesel Programme Expansion","For the industry sector, the biodiesel programme will be expanded from B7 to B10.",""]],"171":[[1,"330","6","Electricity Subsector Enhancement Initiatives","The electricity subsector will be enhanced by implementing various initiatives.",""],[1,"331","1","Electricity Supply Industry Digitalisation and Future-Proofing Reform","The electricity supply industry will be enhanced to be more digitalised and future-proof.",""],[1,"331","2","Sabah Electricity Supply Reinforcement Programme","The electricity supply system in Sabah will be further reinforced through the construction and upgrading of generation facilities as well as transmission and distribution networks.",""],[1,"331","2","East Coast Power Plant Construction","This will include construction of a new power plant on the east coast.",""],[1,"331","2","Southern Link Project","Initial work for the Southern Link Project will begin under the Twelfth Plan.",""],[1,"331","2","Incentive-Based Regulation Framework","Moreover, the Incentive-based Regulation (IBR) framework will be introduced to improve the quality and efficiency of electricity supply.",""],[1,"331","3","Electricity Generation Capacity Expansion and Grid Reinforcement","Investment in generation capacity and reinforcement of transmission and distribution networks will be continued to ensure the security of electricity supply.",""],[1,"331","3","Gas-Fired Power Plant Commissioning Programme","New gas-fired power plants with a total capacity of 3,441 MW will be commissioned in Peninsular Malaysia to replace power plants that will be decommissioned.",""],[1,"331","3","Sarawak Hydroelectric Plant Completion","A 1,285 MW hydroelectric plant in Sarawak, which is under construction, will be completed by the end of the Twelfth Plan to increase installed capacity.",""],[1,"331","3","High-Voltage Transmission Line Construction","The construction of 500 KV and 275 kV transmission lines will be undertaken in Peninsular Malaysia and Sarawak, which will support future load growth.",""],[1,"331","3","ASEAN Power Grid Interconnection Expansion","In addition, the existing Lao PDR-Thailand-Malaysia power transfer under the ASEAN Power Grid (APG) and new transboundary interconnections will be explored to ensure better connectivity.",""],[1,"331","4","Rural Electrification Programme","The rural electrification programme will be continued to provide electricity to an additional 28,000 houses towards achieving the 99% target of electricity coverage in rural areas.",""],[2,"330","6","Electricity Subsector Enhancement Initiatives","The electricity subsector will be enhanced by implementing various initiatives.",""],[2,"331","1","Electricity Supply Industry Digitalisation and Future-Proofing Review","The electricity supply industry will be enhanced to be more digitalised and future-proof.",""],[2,"331","1","Electricity Market and Grid Access Reform","The current industry structure will be reviewed, which includes improving the energy market under the New Enhanced Dispatch Arrangement (NEDA) as well as enhancing the transparency of the Single Buyer and Grid System Operator.",""],[2,"331","2","Sabah Electricity Supply System Reinforcement","The electricity supply system in Sabah will be further reinforced through the construction and upgrading of generation facilities as well as transmission and distribution networks.",""],[2,"331","2","New East Coast Power Plant Construction","This will include construction of a new power plant on the east coast.",""],[2,"331","2","Southern Link Project Initial Works","Initial work for the Southern Link Project will begin under the Twelfth Plan.",""],[2,"331","2","Incentive-Based Regulation Framework for Electricity Supply","Moreover, the Incentive-based Regulation (IBR) framework will be introduced to improve the quality and efficiency of electricity supply.",""],[2,"331","3","Electricity Generation Capacity Expansion and Grid Reinforcement","Investment in generation capacity and reinforcement of transmission and distribution networks will be continued to ensure the security of electricity supply.",""],[2,"331","3","New Gas-Fired Power Plant Commissioning","New gas-fired power plants with a total capacity of 3,441 MW will be commissioned in Peninsular Malaysia to replace power plants that will be decommissioned.",""],[2,"331","3","Hydroelectric Plant Completion in Sarawak","A 1,285 MW hydroelectric plant in Sarawak, which is under construction, will be completed by the end of the Twelfth Plan to increase installed capacity.",""],[2,"331","3","Transmission Line Construction Programme","The construction of 500 KV and 275 kV transmission lines will be undertaken in Peninsular Malaysia and Sarawak, which will support future load growth.",""],[2,"331","3","ASEAN Power Grid Interconnection Expansion","In addition, the existing Lao PDR-Thailand-Malaysia power transfer under the ASEAN Power Grid (APG) and new transboundary interconnections will be explored to ensure better connectivity.",""],[2,"339","1","Energy Market Liberalisation and Electricity Supply Resilience Reform","In the Twelfth Plan, priority will be given to transform the energy market through market liberalisation of the gas and enhance the resilience of the electricity supply industry to be future-proof.",""]],"172":[[1,"329","6","Clean Energy and Hydrogen Exploration Initiative","Under this policy, the prospect of future growth related to energy, particularly on the potential of new energy from clean and sustainable sources including hydrogen will be explored.",""],[1,"331","5","Renewable Energy Development and Utilisation Intensification","The development and utilisation of RE resources will be intensified to meet the target of 31% RE of the total installed capacity.",""],[1,"331","5","Renewable Energy Technology Diversification","Existing and new technologies such as cogeneration, solar thermal and fuel cells will be leveraged to provide more options for the industry.",""],[1,"331","5","Bioenergy Cluster Development","Several bioenergy clusters will be established as centralised collection points to ensure sustainable supply of feedstock and to enable electricity generators to minimise cost.",""],[1,"331","6","Direct Green Energy Purchasing Mechanism","A new mechanism for green energy will be explored to encourage corporate consumers to buy energy directly from RE generators to meet their environmental, social and governance (ESG) commitment.",""],[1,"331","6","Promotion of Green Tariff Rider and Renewable Energy Certificates","The implementation of existing mechanisms such as Green Tariff Rider6 and Renewable Energy Certificate7 will be further promoted to create more options for consumers and industries as well as spur investment.",""],[1,"331","6","Waste-to-Energy and Floating Solar Expansion","Efforts will be intensified to encourage waste-to-energy generation and development of floating solar projects as well as to deploy more rooftop solar PV through existing financing options, including solar leasing programme and PPA.",""],[1,"331","6","Energy Storage Technology Promotion","The adoption of new technologies comprising the energy storage system will be further promoted to address the intermittency issue in RE.",""],[1,"331","8","Green Tariff Renewable Energy Procurement Mechanism","Mechanism that enables consumers to have a choice to procure RE through green tariff offerings, known as MyGreen+ as well as the opportunity to track and trade RE through Malaysia Green Attribute Tracking System platform.",""],[2,"300","2","Low-Carbon Energy Scale-Up Programme","Efforts to pursue low-carbon energy through RE and EE will be scaled-up to reduce GHG emissions.",""],[2,"300","2","Renewable Energy Development and Utilisation Expansion","The development and utilisation of RE sources will be intensified to meet the 31% RE target of total installed capacity.",""],[2,"300","2","Renewable Energy Industry Diversification Initiative","The RE industry will be encouraged to venture into floating solar and waste-to-energy projects.",""],[2,"300","2","Renewable Energy Source Diversification Programme","Apart from large hydro and solar, focus will also be on increasing the contribution from other renewable sources, such as biomass and biogas.",""],[2,"300","2","Clean Energy Technology Promotion Initiative","The use of existing and new technologies, namely cogeneration, solar thermal and fuel cell will be further promoted to expand options available to the industry.",""],[2,"300","2","Renewable Energy Certificate Promotion Mechanism","In addition, the Renewable Energy Certificate14 will be promoted to enable procurement and trading of RE.",""],[2,"300","4","PETRONAS Net Zero and Low-Carbon Transition Initiatives","PETRONAS has declared its target to achieve net zero carbon emissions by 2050.",""],[2,"300","5","Low-Carbon Energy and Nature-Based Solutions Investment","providing low-carbon energy and solutions, such as natural gas and RE; developing low and zero carbon fuels, products and solutions; and investing in nature-based solutions by preserving and restoring the capacity of forest ecosystems to act as carbon sinks.",""],[2,"300","10","Green Tariff Renewable Energy Procurement Mechanism","Mechanism that enables consumers to have a choice to procure RE through green tariff offerings, known as MyGreen+ as well as the opportunity to track and trade RE through Malaysia Green Attribute Tracking System platform.",""],[2,"331","5","Renewable Energy Development and Utilisation Intensification","The development and utilisation of RE resources will be intensified to meet the target of 31% RE of the total installed capacity.",""],[2,"331","5","Renewable Technology Diversification for Industry","Existing and new technologies such as cogeneration, solar thermal and fuel cells will be leveraged to provide more options for the industry.",""],[2,"331","5","Bioenergy Cluster Establishment","Several bioenergy clusters will be established as centralised collection points to ensure sustainable supply of feedstock and to enable electricity generators to minimise cost.",""],[2,"331","6","Corporate Direct Renewable Energy Purchasing Mechanism","A new mechanism for green energy will be explored to encourage corporate consumers to buy energy directly from RE generators to meet their environmental, social and governance (ESG) commitment.",""],[2,"331","6","Promotion of Green Tariff Rider and Renewable Energy Certificate Mechanisms","The implementation of existing mechanisms such as Green Tariff Rider6 and Renewable Energy Certificate7 will be further promoted to create more options for consumers and industries as well as spur investment.",""],[2,"331","6","Waste-to-Energy and Floating Solar Development","Efforts will be intensified to encourage waste-to-energy generation and development of floating solar projects as well as to deploy more rooftop solar PV through existing financing options, including solar leasing programme and PPA.",""],[2,"331","6","Energy Storage Technology Promotion","The adoption of new technologies comprising the energy storage system will be further promoted to address the intermittency issue in RE.",""],[2,"331","7","Consumer Energy Mix Customization Mechanism","Mechanism that enables consumers to customise the energy mix attributed to RE sources.",""],[2,"331","8","Green Tariff Renewable Energy Procurement Mechanism","Mechanism that enables consumers to have a choice to procure RE through green tariff offerings, known as MyGreen+ as well as the opportunity to track and trade RE through Malaysia Green Attribute Tracking System platform.",""]],"173":[[2,"331","4","Rural Electrification Programme","The rural electrification programme will be continued to provide electricity to an additional 28,000 houses towards achieving the 99% target of electricity coverage in rural areas.",""],[2,"331","4","Federal-State and Utility Company Coordination for Rural Electrification","Collaboration between the Federal and state governments as well as utility companies will be intensified to ensure holistic planning and effective implementation.",""],[2,"331","4","Remote Area Renewable Electrification Deployment","Most of the rural electrification projects will involve grid connection, while alternative systems such as small hydro, solar hybrid as well as solar PV will be deployed in remote areas.",""]],"174":[[1,"169","3","Emergency Response and Preparedness Improvement","Efforts will also be undertaken to improve emergency response and preparedness.",""],[1,"170","5","Emergency Services Capacity Upgrading","The capability of agencies in providing emergency services will be enhanced through the upgrading of facilities and assets.",""],[1,"170","5","Community Emergency Response Volunteer Programme","Voluntary participation by local communities in the Civil Defence Emergency Response Team-Community (CDERT-C) will be encouraged by promoting awareness on the importance of volunteerism.",""],[1,"170","5","Certified Emergency Responder Training","These volunteers will be trained to be certified emergency responders.",""],[1,"170","5","Emergency Response and Public Warning System Upgrade","Meanwhile, the emergency response system and the Public Warning System will be upgraded to improve response time.",""],[1,"170","5","Voluntary Firefighter Service Expansion","Voluntary firefighter services will also be expanded to include FELDA areas.",""],[1,"306","7","Early Warning and Disaster Response Strengthening","Early warning systems as well as disaster response, preparedness and recovery measures will be strengthened.",""],[1,"307","3","Intensified Research on Climate-Sensitive Diseases","As such, research will be intensified on climate-sensitive diseases, especially vector-, water- and air-borne diseases as well as illnesses due to the deteriorating environmental quality.",""],[1,"307","6","AI-Enabled Disaster Response Systems","Technologies, including artificial intelligence sensors and alert systems, will be leveraged to ensure more effective disaster response.",""],[1,"307","7","Enhanced Early Warning and Disaster Response Systems","Early warning systems and disaster response will be enhanced to ensure at-risk communities are better prepared to take action ahead of impact, thus saving lives and minimising property losses.",""],[1,"307","7","Big Data and Artificial Intelligence for Disaster Forecasting","The use of big data analytics and artificial intelligence in forecasting and early warning systems will enable better prediction and mitigation of disaster risks.",""],[1,"307","7","Expanded Flood Forecasting and Early Warning Coverage","The integrated weather and flood forecasting and early warning system for floods will be expanded to cover more high-risk river basins.",""],[1,"307","7","Enhanced Earthquake and Tsunami Monitoring and Warning Systems","The earthquake monitoring system and early warning system for tsunamis will also be enhanced for better response.",""],[1,"307","7","Stakeholder Collaboration for Early Warning Dissemination","Collaboration with all stakeholders, particularly the private sector, will be intensified to effectively disseminate early warning information to the public.",""],[1,"307","8","Strengthened Disaster Response Coordination","Coordination among disaster management-related agencies will be strengthened to further improve the efficiency of disaster response measures, including health-related disasters.",""],[1,"307","8","Disaster Response Technical Training and Simulation Exercises","This will be supported by increasing the number of technical training and simulation exercises, including with regional and international disaster response teams.",""],[1,"307","8","Community-Based Disaster Risk Management and Civil Defence Emergency Response Programmes","Community-based Disaster Risk Management and Civil Defence Emergency Response Team for Community programmes, led by disaster management-related agencies as well as local stakeholders, will continue to be implemented to empower local communities to undertake early disaster response.",""],[1,"307","8","Community Disaster Preparedness Drills and Knowledge Sharing","The capability of communities living in disaster-prone areas will be strengthened through sharing of knowledge and practical approaches as well as by organising more regular drills.",""],[1,"308","1","Disaster Recovery and Community Resilience Support","The build back better approach will also be adopted to facilitate affected communities to recover from the aftermath of disasters.",""],[2,"169","3","Emergency Response and Preparedness Enhancement","Efforts will also be undertaken to improve emergency response and preparedness.",""],[2,"170","5","Emergency Services Capability Upgrade","The capability of agencies in providing emergency services will be enhanced through the upgrading of facilities and assets.",""],[2,"170","5","Community Emergency Response Volunteer Programme","Voluntary participation by local communities in the Civil Defence Emergency Response Team-Community (CDERT-C) will be encouraged by promoting awareness on the importance of volunteerism.",""],[2,"170","5","Emergency Responder Training and Certification","These volunteers will be trained to be certified emergency responders.",""],[2,"170","5","Emergency Response and Public Warning System Upgrade","Meanwhile, the emergency response system and the Public Warning System will be upgraded to improve response time.",""],[2,"170","5","Voluntary Firefighter Service Expansion","Voluntary firefighter services will also be expanded to include FELDA areas.",""]],"175":[[1,"292","7","Seismic Hazard Mapping and Fault Monitoring","Seismic hazard areas are being mapped out to identify active faults, enabling appropriate measures to be put in place, thus enhancing preparedness and resilience to earthquakes.",""],[1,"296","9","Disaster Risk Management Policy","Introduction of the Policy on Disaster Risk Management (DRM)",""],[1,"306","7","Evidence-Based Climate Adaptation and Disaster Risk Reduction Planning","evidence-based and risk-informed actions as well as integrated approaches for climate change adaptation and disaster risk reduction will be undertaken in development planning.",""],[1,"306","7","Early Warning and Disaster Response Strengthening","Early warning systems as well as disaster response, preparedness and recovery measures will be strengthened.",""],[1,"306","8","Climate- and Disaster-Risk-Informed Policy Planning","Climate change impacts and disaster risks will be taken into account in policy planning and implementation to enable evidence-based and risk-informed actions.",""],[1,"306","8","Expanded Vulnerability Assessment Programme","Vulnerability assessments will be expanded, covering more high-risk and sensitive areas, communities and sectors, including flood-prone areas, human health and the agriculture sector.",""],[1,"306","8","Cross-Sectoral Climate Coordination Mechanism","Cross-sectoral collaboration between government agencies and all other stakeholders will be strengthened for a more coordinated",""],[1,"307","1","Data Sharing and Integration Protocol Development","relevant data will be made available to the stakeholders, while data sharing processes and protocols will be developed to ensure better data integration.",""],[1,"307","2","Natural Hazard Monitoring and Assessment Enhancement","Monitoring and assessment of natural hazards will be enhanced to further improve disaster preparedness and response measures.",""],[1,"307","2","Multi-Hazard Data Centre and Risk Register Platform","A multi-hazard data centre and risk register platform will be established for efficient data and information sharing.",""],[1,"307","2","Hydroclimate Model Enhancement and Integration","The ability of hydroclimate models to represent the dynamical process and project precipitation variation will be enhanced.",""],[1,"307","2","Multi-Scale Hazard and Risk Map Expansion","In addition, multi-scale hazard and risk maps will be expanded to cover more areas, in order to mitigate the impact on vulnerable communities and sectors.",""],[1,"307","4","National Disaster Risk Management Policy and Resilience Plans","A national policy on disaster risk management and multi-level disaster resilience plans as well as a national adaptation action plan will be developed.",""],[1,"307","4","Integration of Climate and Disaster Measures into Development Plans","These will be integrated into the local, structural and sectoral development plans to improve planning and implementation of appropriate measures.",""],[1,"307","4","Geological Hazard Adaptation and Risk Reduction Framework","A framework will be developed to outline adaptation and risk reduction measures for geological hazards, including earthquake and submarine landslides.",""],[1,"307","4","Revision of Spatial Plans for Disaster Risk Measures","These measures will be incorporated in the revision of all relevant spatial plans.",""],[1,"307","4","Integration of Scientific and Indigenous Knowledge in Disaster Planning","In addition, scientific and indigenous knowledge will be assimilated to improve planning and implementation of measures, which will address the complexity and dynamicity of the impact of climate change and disasters.",""],[1,"307","5","Integrated Resilience and Sustainability Approaches","Adoption of integrated approaches, combining structural and non- structural initiatives, will be expanded to enhance resilience as well as ensure sustainability and cost effectiveness.",""],[1,"307","5","Developer Hazard Mapping and Disaster Preparedness Requirements","developers will be further encouraged to include site hazard mapping, disaster preparedness plans and disaster insurance in project implementation.",""],[1,"307","5","Climate and Disaster Socioeconomic Impact Assessment","the socioeconomic impact of climate change and disasters will be quantified to better understand and manage the implications of such events.",""],[1,"307","6","Climate Adaptation and Disaster Risk Reduction Measures","based adaptation and risk reduction measures will also be enhanced through green cover expansion and coastal improvement as well as watershed, wetlands and river conservation.",""],[1,"307","6","AI-Enabled Disaster Response Systems","Technologies, including artificial intelligence sensors and alert systems, will be leveraged to ensure more effective disaster response.",""],[1,"307","9","Build Back Better Disaster Recovery and Resilient Reconstruction Measures","The build back better approach will continue to be adopted as one of the disaster preparedness and recovery measures in enhancing resilience against climate change and disasters, hence protecting development gains.",""],[2,"292","7","Seismic Hazard Mapping and Fault Monitoring","Seismic hazard areas are being mapped out to identify active faults, enabling appropriate measures to be put in place, thus enhancing preparedness and resilience to earthquakes.",""],[2,"306","7","Evidence-Based Risk-Informed Development Planning","evidence-based and risk-informed actions as well as integrated approaches for climate change adaptation and disaster risk reduction will be undertaken in development planning.",""],[2,"306","7","Early Warning and Disaster Response Strengthening","Early warning systems as well as disaster response, preparedness and recovery measures will be strengthened.",""],[2,"306","8","Climate- and Disaster-Risk-Informed Policy Planning","Climate change impacts and disaster risks will be taken into account in policy planning and implementation to enable evidence-based and risk-informed actions.",""],[2,"306","8","Expanded Vulnerability Assessment Programme","Vulnerability assessments will be expanded, covering more high-risk and sensitive areas, communities and sectors, including flood-prone areas, human health and the agriculture sector.",""],[2,"306","8","Cross-Sectoral Disaster Risk Coordination","Cross-sectoral collaboration between government agencies and all other stakeholders will be strengthened for a more coordinated",""],[2,"307","1","Data Sharing and Integration Protocol Development","relevant data will be made available to the stakeholders, while data sharing processes and protocols will be developed to ensure better data integration.",""],[2,"307","2","Enhanced Natural Hazard Monitoring and Assessment System","Monitoring and assessment of natural hazards will be enhanced to further improve disaster preparedness and response measures.",""],[2,"307","2","Multi-Hazard Data Centre and Risk Register Platform","A multi-hazard data centre and risk register platform will be established for efficient data and information sharing.",""],[2,"307","2","Hydroclimate Model Enhancement and Integration","The ability of hydroclimate models to represent the dynamical process and project precipitation variation will be enhanced.",""],[2,"307","2","Expansion of Multi-Scale Hazard and Risk Maps","In addition, multi-scale hazard and risk maps will be expanded to cover more areas, in order to mitigate the impact on vulnerable communities and sectors.",""],[2,"307","3","Intensified Research on Climate-Sensitive Diseases","As such, research will be intensified on climate-sensitive diseases, especially vector-, water- and air-borne diseases as well as illnesses due to the deteriorating environmental quality.",""],[2,"307","6","Climate Adaptation and Disaster Risk Reduction Measures","based adaptation and risk reduction measures will also be enhanced through green cover expansion and coastal improvement as well as watershed, wetlands and river conservation.",""],[2,"307","6","AI-Enabled Disaster Response Systems","Technologies, including artificial intelligence sensors and alert systems, will be leveraged to ensure more effective disaster response.",""],[2,"307","7","Enhanced Early Warning and Disaster Response Systems","Early warning systems and disaster response will be enhanced to ensure at-risk communities are better prepared to take action ahead of impact, thus saving lives and minimising property losses.",""],[2,"307","7","Big Data and Artificial Intelligence for Disaster Forecasting","The use of big data analytics and artificial intelligence in forecasting and early warning systems will enable better prediction and mitigation of disaster risks.",""],[2,"307","7","Expanded Integrated Weather and Flood Forecasting System","The integrated weather and flood forecasting and early warning system for floods will be expanded to cover more high-risk river basins.",""],[2,"307","7","Enhanced Earthquake and Tsunami Monitoring and Warning Systems","The earthquake monitoring system and early warning system for tsunamis will also be enhanced for better response.",""],[2,"307","7","Stakeholder Collaboration for Public Early Warning Dissemination","Collaboration with all stakeholders, particularly the private sector, will be intensified to effectively disseminate early warning information to the public.",""]],"176":[[1,"182","1","Youth Volunteerism Promotion Programme","Volunteerism will be further promoted, especially among youth to strengthen social cohesion in society.",""],[1,"182","1","Expansion of Youth Volunteer Activities","Existing programmes will be expanded to enable youth to actively participate in voluntary activities.",""],[1,"182","1","Volunteer Icon Awards Scheme","Volunteer icon awards will be introduced to recognise outstanding youth volunteers and social media influencers in helping the government to inculcate volunteerism and fostering national unity.",""],[1,"182","1","Digital Volunteerism and Social Cohesion Platforms","Digital platforms will be leveraged to boost the spirit of volunteerism and unity among youth as well as promote activities to build social cohesion and unity.",""],[1,"221","2","Youth Economic Empowerment Plan","A national plan on youth economic empowerment will be introduced to provide strategic direction in improving youth employability.",""],[1,"221","2","Youth Financial Education Network","a youth financial education network will be initiated as a platform to promote financial literacy and credit management programmes.",""],[1,"221","2","Youth Leadership and Volunteerism Programmes","Youth leadership and volunteerism programmes",""],[1,"221","3","Youth Participation and Civic Awareness Programmes","at school, HEIs and community levels will be streamlined to enhance youth participation in community activities.",""],[1,"221","3","Patriotism and Constitutional Literacy Initiative","focus will be given to inculcate patriotism, increase awareness on politics as well as improve knowledge on the Federal Constitution and the role of the legislative system in the country's administration.",""],[1,"221","3","Digital Ethics Awareness Programmes","more awareness programmes will be undertaken to elevate ethical usage of technology, including the digital platform.",""],[2,"221","2","Youth Economic Empowerment Plan","A national plan on youth economic empowerment will be introduced to provide strategic direction in improving youth employability.",""],[2,"221","2","Youth Financial Education Network","a youth financial education network will be initiated as a platform to promote financial literacy and credit management programmes.",""],[2,"221","2","Youth Leadership and Volunteerism Programmes","Youth leadership and volunteerism programmes",""],[2,"221","3","Youth Participation Streamlining Initiative","at school, HEIs and community levels will be streamlined to enhance youth participation in community activities.",""],[2,"221","3","Youth Civic Education and Patriotism Programme","with the constitutional amendment to lower the voting age to 18 years old, focus will be given to inculcate patriotism, increase awareness on politics as well as improve knowledge on the Federal Constitution and the role of the legislative system in the country's administration.",""],[2,"221","3","Youth Healthy and Active Lifestyle Promotion","Efforts to promote a healthy and active lifestyle among youth with greater emphasis on mental wellbeing will be intensified.",""],[2,"221","3","Youth Digital Ethics Awareness Programme","more awareness programmes will be undertaken to elevate ethical usage of technology, including the digital platform.",""]],"177":[[2,"221","4","Women’s Empowerment and Gender Mainstreaming Framework","Efforts will focus on promoting gender equality, increasing economic participation and enhancing the role of women in decision-making.",""],[2,"221","4","Review of Laws for Women’s Protection","Relevant laws will be reviewed to ensure that women are better protected.",""],[2,"221","4","Gender Mainstreaming Framework for Policy Formulation","The gender mainstreaming20 framework will be introduced to incorporate the gender perspective in formulating policies.",""],[2,"221","4","Institutional Capacity and Evidence-Based Gender Policy Strengthening","Emphasis will be placed on enhancing institutional capacity and evidence-based policymaking, particularly in gender related analysis.",""],[2,"221","4","Women’s Economic Participation Platforms","Women's participation in all sectors will be elevated via multiple economic platforms, including the sharing economy and entrepreneurship development.",""],[2,"221","5","Strengthening Civil and Sharia Laws for Safety and Security","Safety and security issues will continue to be addressed by strengthening both civil and sharia laws",""],[2,"221","5","Women's Rights Awareness and Intervention Programmes","enhancing women's rights awareness and intervention programmes",""],[2,"221","5","Legislation on Sexual Harassment and Gender Inequality","Legislation to address sexual harassment and gender inequalities will be formulated",""]],"178":[[1,"23","3","Connectivity and Transport Infrastructure Enhancement","Four catalytic policy enablers, namely developing future talent, accelerating technology adoption and innovation, enhancing connectivity and transport infrastructure as well as strengthening the public service will support the achievement of these themes.",""],[1,"33","7","Inclusive Transport and Logistics Infrastructure Enhancement","Provision of efficient and inclusive transportation and logistics infrastructure will continue to be the focus by enhancing accessibility to public transport, improving trade facilitation as well as strengthening the institutional and regulatory framework.",""],[1,"33","7","Last-Mile Connectivity Improvement","Measures will be taken to improve last-mile connectivity through the integration of rail and road networks between airports, ports, industrial areas and cities.",""],[1,"33","7","Port Capacity Expansion and Multimodal Cargo Movement","The capacity of ports infrastructure and services will be increased while a multimodal cargo movement approach by the same service provider will be adopted.",""],[1,"33","7","Logistics Ecosystem Transformation Initiative","In addition, transforming the logistics ecosystem for greater efficiency has been identified as a game changer for the logistics sector.",""],[1,"33","7","Logistics Hub Planning Centralization","Initiatives will be taken to centralise planning and development of logistics hub, accelerate digital adoption, encourage mergers and acquisitions among industry players, establish a single border agency and create a national regulatory framework for warehousing and maritime economy.",""],[1,"38","2","Centralised Logistics Hub Planning and Development","In the Twelfth Plan, the Government will transform logistics services by centralising the planning and development of logistics hubs, accelerating digital",""],[1,"38","3","Single Border Agency for Trade Facilitation","A single border agency for trade facilitation will be created",""],[1,"38","3","National Regulatory Framework for Warehousing and the Maritime Economy","a national regulatory framework for warehousing and the maritime economy will be formulated",""],[1,"67","1","Public Infrastructure and Transport Investment Programme","The investment will be largely in infrastructure, transport, utilities as well as the oil and gas industry.",""],[1,"67","1","Major Public Sector Projects Implementation in Phases","Major public sector projects that will be undertaken include the ECRL, Johor Bahru-Singapore Rapid Transit System and Pan Borneo Highway.",""],[1,"69","8","Trade Facilitation Efficiency Enhancement","Efforts to leverage gains from trade will be intensified by further improving the efficiency of trade facilitation at all entry points",""],[1,"70","1","Logistics Services Efficiency Improvement","efforts will be intensified to increase the efficiency of logistics services by streamlining administrative procedures, increasing regulatory compliance and stricter enforcement.",""],[1,"95","7","Logistics Industry Digitalisation and Integrated Supply Chain Platform","The industry will be encouraged to digitalise its operations and connect to an integrated platform in establishing a smart and highly efficient supply chain.",""],[1,"95","7","Warehousing and Distribution Centre Investment Expansion","logistics services providers will be encouraged to increase investment in warehousing and distribution centres to enhance efficiency.",""],[1,"100","8","Regional Logistics Hub Development","Efforts will also be undertaken to position Malaysia as a regional logistics hub, capitalising its advantage of good connectivity in the Asia-Pacific region.",""],[1,"344","3","First- and Last-Mile Connectivity Improvement","Further efforts will be undertaken to improve first- and last-mile connectivity in facilitating trade activities and resolve issues related to governance in transport and logistics.",""],[1,"344","3","Transport and Logistics Infrastructure Efficiency Enhancement","this policy enabler focuses on enhancing the efficiency of transport and logistics infrastructure to provide safe, reliable, affordable and sustainable services.",""],[1,"344","4","Integrated Multimodal Transport Connectivity Improvement","In the Twelfth Plan, the integration of different transport modes will be improved to create seamless connectivity in serving the needs of people and industry.",""],[1,"344","4","Last-Mile Rail-Road Connectivity Enhancement","Concerted efforts will be undertaken to improve last-mile connectivity through the integration of rail and road networks connecting airports, ports, industrial areas and cities.",""],[1,"344","4","Port Infrastructure and Services Upgrading","Meanwhile, the capacity of port infrastructure and services will be increased through the upgrading of facilities and equipment as well as improvement of processes.",""],[1,"345","1","Multimodal Cargo Movement Promotion","In addition, logistics players will be encouraged to adopt the multimodal cargo movement approach to enhance logistics services capability and reduce the cost of distribution.",""],[1,"350","7","Centralised Logistics Hub Planning and Development","Centralising the planning and development of logistics hubs.",""],[2,"33","7","Inclusive Transport and Logistics Infrastructure Upgrade","Provision of efficient and inclusive transportation and logistics infrastructure will continue to be the focus by enhancing accessibility to public transport, improving trade facilitation as well as strengthening the institutional and regulatory framework.",""],[2,"33","7","Last-Mile Connectivity Improvement","Measures will be taken to improve last-mile connectivity through the integration of rail and road networks between airports, ports, industrial areas and cities.",""],[2,"33","7","Logistics Sector Transformation and Governance Reform","Initiatives will be taken to centralise planning and development of logistics hub, accelerate digital adoption, encourage mergers and acquisitions among industry players, establish a single border agency and create a national regulatory framework for warehousing and maritime economy.",""],[2,"38","2","Centralised Logistics Hub Planning and Development","In the Twelfth Plan, the Government will transform logistics services by centralising the planning and development of logistics hubs, accelerating digital",""],[2,"38","3","Single Border Agency for Trade Facilitation","A single border agency for trade facilitation will be created, while a national regulatory framework for warehousing and the maritime economy will be formulated.",""],[2,"38","3","National Regulatory Framework for Warehousing and the Maritime Economy","A single border agency for trade facilitation will be created, while a national regulatory framework for warehousing and the maritime economy will be formulated.",""],[2,"344","3","First- and Last-Mile Connectivity Improvement","Further efforts will be undertaken to improve first- and last-mile connectivity in facilitating trade activities and resolve issues related to governance in transport and logistics.",""],[2,"344","3","Transport and Logistics Infrastructure Efficiency Enhancement","this policy enabler focuses on enhancing the efficiency of transport and logistics infrastructure to provide safe, reliable, affordable and sustainable services.",""],[2,"344","4","Integrated Multimodal Transport Connectivity Improvement","In the Twelfth Plan, the integration of different transport modes will be improved to create seamless connectivity in serving the needs of people and industry.",""],[2,"344","4","Last-Mile Rail-Road Connectivity Enhancement","Concerted efforts will be undertaken to improve last-mile connectivity through the integration of rail and road networks connecting airports, ports, industrial areas and cities.",""],[2,"344","4","Port Infrastructure and Services Upgrading","Meanwhile, the capacity of port infrastructure and services will be increased through the upgrading of facilities and equipment as well as improvement of processes.",""],[2,"345","1","Multimodal Cargo Movement Promotion","In addition, logistics players will be encouraged to adopt the multimodal cargo movement approach to enhance logistics services capability and reduce the cost of distribution.",""],[2,"350","7","Centralised Logistics Hub Planning and Development","Centralising the planning and development of logistics hubs.",""]],"179":[[1,"412","2","Integrated Transport System Improvement","The Twelfth Plan aims to further enhance the efficiency of transport and logistics services by prioritising efforts to provide an integrated, affordable, reliable and seamless transport system.",""],[1,"412","2","Transport and Logistics Sector Competitiveness Enhancement","Additionally, the plan aims to increase industry competitiveness and strengthen the institutional and regulatory framework of the sectors.",""],[1,"413","2","Merger of MAVCOM with CAAM","MAVCOM will be merged with the Civil Aviation Authority of Malaysia (CAAM) to rationalise the aviation sector",""],[1,"415","1","National Transport Policy","Under the NTP, the implementation of various transport initiatives will be guided by five policy thrusts, namely governance, transport infrastructure maintenance, safety, green transport ecosystem and the internationalisation of transport services.",""],[2,"412","2","Integrated Transport System Improvement","The Twelfth Plan aims to further enhance the efficiency of transport and logistics services by prioritising efforts to provide an integrated, affordable, reliable and seamless transport system.",""],[2,"412","2","Transport and Logistics Competitiveness Enhancement","Additionally, the plan aims to increase industry competitiveness and strengthen the institutional and regulatory framework of the sectors.",""],[2,"415","1","National Transport Policy","The NTP was introduced to streamline the fragmented transport initiatives among Federal and state governments, including ministries, agencies and transport authorities to ensure effective and efficient use of resources.",""],[2,"415","3","Regional Highway and Rail Connectivity Expansion","Efforts to enhance connectivity across regions include the construction of highways and rail projects with underserved areas given priority.",""],[2,"415","3","Central Spine Road Construction","The Central Spine Road (CSR), to connect Bentong, Pahang and Kuala Krai, Kelantan, is being constructed in phases.",""],[2,"415","3","Kota Bharu-Kuala Krai Highway Construction","The construction of Kota Bharu-Kuala Krai (KBKK) highway in Kelantan is implemented in phases, where two out of eight subpackages from Pasir Hor to Ketereh were completed in 2019.",""],[2,"415","4","LPT3 Highway Corridor Project","The proposed LPT3 will connect Gemuruh, Terengganu to Tok Bali, Kelantan and is expected to provide a smoother journey to the east coast while boosting economic activities along the corridor.",""],[2,"415","5","Pan Borneo Sabah Highway Construction","The Pan Borneo Sabah Highway was initiated in 2016 to provide road connectivity from Sindumin to Tawau.",""],[2,"415","5","Pan Borneo Sarawak Highway Construction","The Pan Borneo Sarawak Highway from Telok Melano to Miri was 59.4% completed at the end of 2020 and is expected to be ready by 2022.",""],[2,"415","6","Greater Kuala Lumpur/Klang Valley Highway Construction Programme","Five highways are under construction to improve connectivity and ease congestion in the Greater Kuala Lumpur/Klang Valley (GKL/KV).",""],[2,"415","6","West Coast Expressway Completion Project","Meanwhile, West Coast Expressway (WCE) from Banting, Selangor to Taiping, Perak is expected to be completed by 2024.",""],[2,"415","7","Gemas-Johor Bahru Electrified Double Track Rail Extension","For GJB, the final stretch of the electrified double-track from Padang Besar, Perlis to Johor Bahru, Johor, which will offer Electric Train Services (ETS), is projected to be ready by 2023.",""],[2,"415","7","East Coast Rail Link Construction","Meanwhile, the ECRL which re-commenced work in 2019, is currently under construction for the alignment from Dungun to Mentakab and is expected to be completed by 2026.",""],[2,"419","5","Integrated Transport Infrastructure and Logistics Services Programme","The Twelfth Plan will focus on providing efficient and inclusive transport infrastructure and logistics services.",""]],"180":[[1,"422","1","Integrated Public Transport Mobility Measures","Measures will be undertaken to ensure integrated, affordable, reliable and seamless people mobility.",""],[1,"422","4","Public Transport Integration and Transit-Oriented Development","Overall accessibility to public transport will be improved by integrating various modes of transport and encouraging transit oriented development (TOD).",""],[1,"422","5","Integrated Public Transport Coordination Platform","This initiative will be implemented by establishing a platform to coordinate and optimise schedules, whereby minimising the waiting time between different modes.",""],[1,"422","5","Integrated Journey Planner Development","An integrated and reliable journey planner will be developed through this platform.",""],[1,"422","5","Real-Time Public Transport Data Sharing Enhancement","The sharing of real time data among public transport operators will be enhanced to ensure effective utilisation of the platform.",""],[1,"422","7","First- and Last-Mile Public Transport Connectivity Improvement","Continuous efforts will be carried out to improve the first- and last-mile connectivity, particularly in ensuring accessibility to public transport.",""],[1,"422","8","Alternative Transportation and First- and Last-Mile Connectivity Improvement","Efforts to encourage the usage of alternative transportation will be undertaken in improving the first- and last-mile connectivity.",""],[1,"422","8","Micro-Mobility Promotion and Infrastructure Upgrade","The usage of micro-mobility3 vehicles will be increased, while pedestrian lanes in the urban areas will be enhanced to increase the safety and confidence of users as well as promote active mobility.",""],[1,"422","8","Public Transport Node Infrastructure Upgrade","Infrastructure at primary public transportation nodes will also be upgraded to facilitate the use of micro-mobility vehicles for first- and last-mile connectivity.",""],[1,"422","9","Alternative Community-Based Rural Public Transport System","An alternative community based public transport system that offers affordable services will be introduced.",""],[1,"422","9","Dial-a-Ride Door-to-Door Transport Service","One of the options that will be considered is a 'dial-a-ride system', a phone call-based facility, providing door-to-door service for people who do not have access to conventional public transport amenities.",""],[1,"423","1","Inclusive Mixed-Use Transit-Oriented Development","The development of TOD will also incorporate the element of inclusivity.",""],[1,"423","2","Public Transport Promotion and Modal Shift Initiative","Behavioural shift from private to public transport will be encouraged by propelling the usage of public transport as the first choice.",""],[1,"423","2","Inter-Authority Enforcement Coordination for City Centre Vehicle Access","Collaboration between relevant authorities will be enhanced in ensuring effective enforcement of private vehicles entering city centres.",""],[1,"423","2","Transport Mode Matching for Travel Patterns","Suitable transport modes will be identified to match the travel patterns of the rakyat in encouraging the behavioural shift.",""],[1,"423","3","Public Transport Efficiency and Connectivity Improvement","The efficiency and connectivity of the public transport system will be improved in order to propel public transport as the first choice for travel.",""],[1,"423","3","Dynamic Fare Expansion for ETS Services","Dynamic fares will be expanded for ETS services to encourage the usage of inter-city rail transport, where fares will be determined by market demand.",""],[1,"423","3","Unlimited Public Transport Pass Extension","Besides, unlimited passes for train and bus passengers will be extended to further encourage ridership.",""],[1,"423","3","Parking Management for Public Transport Connectivity Areas","Measures such as limiting parking spaces and imposing higher parking charges in areas with good public transport connectivity will also be implemented to manage the inflow of private vehicles into city centres.",""],[1,"423","3","Federal-State-Local Transport Coordination","Collaboration between Federal and state governments as well as the local authorities will be strengthened to facilitate the planning and implementation of these measures.",""],[1,"423","4","Public Transport Demand Analysis and Service Adjustment","Travel patterns of rakyat will be continuously analysed to provide appropriate public transport services.",""],[1,"423","4","Public Transport Usage Promotion Campaign","Initiatives to promote the usage of public transport via mindset and behavioural change to use public transport will be undertaken.",""],[1,"423","4","Integrated Transport Link Feasibility Study for Putrajaya Corridor","A study to review and identify the most efficient and viable integration of other modes of transport to link Putrajaya with Cyberjaya, Bangi and Kajang is currently being conducted.",""],[1,"454","4","Public Transport Enhancement Programme","Public transport will also be enhanced to ensure better access to services and seamless connectivity for the rakyat.",""],[1,"526","8","Stage Bus Services Transformation Programme","Stage Bus Services Transformation Programme",""],[2,"422","1","Integrated Public Transport Mobility Measures","Measures will be undertaken to ensure integrated, affordable, reliable and seamless people mobility.",""],[2,"422","4","Public Transport Integration and Transit-Oriented Development Initiative","Overall accessibility to public transport will be improved by integrating various modes of transport and encouraging transit oriented development (TOD).",""],[2,"422","5","Integrated Public Transport Coordination Platform","This initiative will be implemented by establishing a platform to coordinate and optimise schedules, whereby minimising the waiting time between different modes.",""],[2,"422","5","Integrated Journey Planner Development","An integrated and reliable journey planner will be developed through this platform.",""],[2,"422","5","Real-Time Public Transport Data Sharing Enhancement","The sharing of real time data among public transport operators will be enhanced to ensure effective utilisation of the platform.",""],[2,"422","6","Rail and Road Network Integration for Connectivity","Rail and road networks will also be integrated to provide better connectivity between airports, ports, industrial areas and cities.",""],[2,"422","7","First- and Last-Mile Public Transport Connectivity Improvement","Continuous efforts will be carried out to improve the first- and last-mile connectivity, particularly in ensuring accessibility to public transport.",""],[2,"422","8","Alternative Transportation and First- and Last-Mile Connectivity Improvement","Efforts to encourage the usage of alternative transportation will be undertaken in improving the first- and last-mile connectivity.",""],[2,"422","8","Micro-Mobility Promotion Programme","The usage of micro-mobility3 vehicles will be increased, while pedestrian lanes in the urban areas will be enhanced to increase the safety and confidence of users as well as promote active mobility.",""],[2,"422","8","Public Transport Node Infrastructure Upgrade","Infrastructure at primary public transportation nodes will also be upgraded to facilitate the use of micro-mobility vehicles for first- and last-mile connectivity.",""],[2,"422","9","Community-Based Rural Public Transport System","An alternative community based public transport system that offers affordable services will be introduced.",""],[2,"422","9","Dial-a-Ride Door-to-Door Transport Service","One of the options that will be considered is a 'dial-a-ride system', a phone call-based facility, providing door-to-door service for people who do not have access to conventional public transport amenities.",""],[2,"423","1","Transit-Oriented Development Integration in Rail Project Planning","TOD will be further emphasised to improve accessibility to public transport and provide good connectivity to other amenities.",""],[2,"423","2","Public Transport Promotion and Modal Shift Initiative","Behavioural shift from private to public transport will be encouraged by propelling the usage of public transport as the first choice.",""],[2,"423","2","Inter-Authority Enforcement Coordination for City Centre Vehicle Access","Collaboration between relevant authorities will be enhanced in ensuring effective enforcement of private vehicles entering city centres.",""],[2,"423","2","Transport Mode Matching for Travel Pattern Optimization","Suitable transport modes will be identified to match the travel patterns of the rakyat in encouraging the behavioural shift.",""],[2,"423","3","Public Transport Efficiency and Connectivity Improvement","The efficiency and connectivity of the public transport system will be improved in order to propel public transport as the first choice for travel.",""],[2,"423","3","Dynamic Fare Expansion for ETS Services","Dynamic fares will be expanded for ETS services to encourage the usage of inter-city rail transport, where fares will be determined by market demand.",""],[2,"423","3","Unlimited Public Transport Pass Extension","Besides, unlimited passes for train and bus passengers will be extended to further encourage ridership.",""],[2,"423","3","Parking Management Measures for City Centres","Measures such as limiting parking spaces and imposing higher parking charges in areas with good public transport connectivity will also be implemented to manage the inflow of private vehicles into city centres.",""],[2,"423","3","Federal-State-Local Transport Planning Coordination","Collaboration between Federal and state governments as well as the local authorities will be strengthened to facilitate the planning and implementation of these measures.",""],[2,"423","4","Public Transport Service Planning Based on Travel Pattern Analysis","Travel patterns of rakyat will be continuously analysed to provide appropriate public transport services.",""],[2,"423","4","Public Transport Usage Promotion Campaign","Initiatives to promote the usage of public transport via mindset and behavioural change to use public transport will be undertaken.",""],[2,"423","4","Putrajaya Multimodal Transport Integration Study","A study to review and identify the most efficient and viable integration of other modes of transport to link Putrajaya with Cyberjaya, Bangi and Kajang is currently being conducted.",""],[2,"423","4","Putrajaya Rail Infrastructure Feasibility Assessment","This study will also gauge the feasibility of utilising the rail infrastructure in Putrajaya.",""]],"181":[[1,"350","8","Digital Adoption for Logistics Efficiency","Accelerating digital adoption to enhance efficiency in logistics services.",""],[1,"417","4","Digitalisation of Logistics Services","Measures have been taken to digitalise logistics services to further improve efficiency and competitiveness as well as ensure seamless movement of goods.",""],[1,"423","5","Transport and Logistics Competitiveness Enhancement Initiatives","Initiatives will be introduced to enhance the competitiveness of the transport and logistics sectors.",""],[1,"423","5","Digitalisation and Efficiency Improvement in Transport and Logistics Services","These include enhancing efficiency and leveraging digitalisation in transport and logistics services.",""],[1,"424","1","Transport and Logistics Efficiency Enhancement Initiatives","Initiatives to enhance the efficiency of transport and logistics services focus on raising the capacity of ports infrastructure and services, improving last-mile connectivity, encouraging multimodal cargo movement, upgrading the aviation system and implementing preventive maintenance of roads and bridges.",""],[1,"424","8","Single-Window Transport and Logistics Transaction Platform","A single-window transaction platform will be operationalised and an integrated database will be developed to leverage digitalisation in transport and logistics services.",""],[1,"424","9","uCustoms Single-Window Transaction Platform","The uCustoms, a single-window transaction platform, will be fully operationalised to further improve the ease of doing business by providing a web based, electronic end-to-end solution.",""],[1,"425","1","Integrated Port Community Systems Development","each port authority will develop its own integrated port community system by benchmarking against the Port Klang Net.",""],[1,"425","1","Port Systems Linkage to uCustoms","These integrated systems will be linked to uCustoms, increasing efficiency and productivity as well as ensuring compliance to international standards.",""],[1,"425","2","Centralised Transport and Logistics Database","A centralised database for the transport and logistics sectors will be established.",""],[1,"425","9","Single Border Agency Establishment Study","A study is being undertaken to establish a single border agency to oversee, strengthen and raise the standard of operations and security along national borders and entry points including ports and airports.",""],[1,"425","9","Single Clearance Trade Facilitation Mechanism","The establishment of a single border agency will enhance efficiency in trade facilitation through a single clearance mechanism.",""],[1,"427","1","Transport and Logistics Trade Facilitation and Digitalisation","Emphasis was given to strengthen trade facilitation, improve first- and last-mile connectivity and digitalise logistics services.",""],[1,"454","4","Multimodal Cargo Movement Single Service Provider System","the multimodal cargo movement approach with a single service provider will be adopted.",""],[2,"350","8","Digital Adoption for Logistics Efficiency","Accelerating digital adoption to enhance efficiency in logistics services.",""],[2,"417","4","Digital Logistics Services Modernisation","Measures have been taken to digitalise logistics services to further improve efficiency and competitiveness as well as ensure seamless movement of goods.",""],[2,"423","5","Transport and Logistics Competitiveness Enhancement Initiatives","Initiatives will be introduced to enhance the competitiveness of the transport and logistics sectors.",""],[2,"423","5","Transport and Logistics Efficiency and Digitalisation Measures","These include enhancing efficiency and leveraging digitalisation in transport and logistics services.",""],[2,"424","8","Single-Window Transport and Logistics Platform","A single-window transaction platform will be operationalised and an integrated database will be developed to leverage digitalisation in transport and logistics services.",""],[2,"424","9","uCustoms Single-Window Transaction Platform","The uCustoms, a single-window transaction platform, will be fully operationalised to further improve the ease of doing business by providing a web based, electronic end-to-end solution.",""],[2,"425","1","Integrated Port Community Systems Development","each port authority will develop its own integrated port community system by benchmarking against the Port Klang Net.",""],[2,"425","1","Port Systems Integration with uCustoms","These integrated systems will be linked to uCustoms, increasing efficiency and productivity as well as ensuring compliance to international standards.",""],[2,"425","2","Centralised Transport and Logistics Database","A centralised database for the transport and logistics sectors will be established.",""]],"182":[[1,"231","2","Subregional Connectivity and Border Clearance Improvement","The initiatives focused on enhancing connectivity and facilitating border clearance for the movement of people and goods.",""],[1,"231","2","ICQS Bukit Kayu Hitam and CIQ Sadao Linkage Project","Progress was also made towards connecting ICQS Bukit Kayu Hitam with the Customs, Immigration and Quarantine (CIQ) Sadao, Thailand.",""],[1,"231","3","IMT-GT Physical Connectivity Projects","Connectivity within the subregions was enhanced with the commencement of various projects under the IMT-GT Physical Connectivity Projects (PCPs) and the BIMP-EAGA Priority Infrastructure Projects (PIPs).",""],[1,"231","3","BIMP-EAGA Priority Infrastructure Projects","Connectivity within the subregions was enhanced with the commencement of various projects under the IMT-GT Physical Connectivity Projects (PCPs) and the BIMP-EAGA Priority Infrastructure Projects (PIPs).",""],[1,"231","3","IMT-GT Air Linkages Memorandum of Understanding","The signing of the memorandum of understanding (MoU) on air linkages between IMT-GT member countries further promoted opportunities for business-expansion, including tourism activities.",""],[1,"231","3","Sandakan Airport Upgrading Works","the upgrading works of the Sandakan Airport and the expansion of the Sepanggar Bay Container Port are progressing.",""],[1,"231","3","Sepanggar Bay Container Port Expansion","the upgrading works of the Sandakan Airport and the expansion of the Sepanggar Bay Container Port are progressing.",""],[2,"231","2","ASEAN Subregional Connectivity and Border Clearance Initiative","The ASEAN subregional cooperation under the umbrella of IMT- GT and BIMP-EAGA continued to be leveraged to improve the wellbeing of the rakyat.",""],[2,"231","3","IMT-GT Physical Connectivity Projects","Connectivity within the subregions was enhanced with the commencement of various projects under the IMT-GT Physical Connectivity Projects (PCPs) and the BIMP-EAGA Priority Infrastructure Projects (PIPs).",""],[2,"231","3","BIMP-EAGA Priority Infrastructure Projects","Connectivity within the subregions was enhanced with the commencement of various projects under the IMT-GT Physical Connectivity Projects (PCPs) and the BIMP-EAGA Priority Infrastructure Projects (PIPs).",""],[2,"231","3","Air Linkages Memorandum of Understanding","The signing of the memorandum of understanding (MoU) on air linkages between IMT-GT member countries further promoted opportunities for business-expansion, including tourism activities.",""],[2,"231","3","Sandakan Airport Upgrading Works","the upgrading works of the Sandakan Airport and the expansion of the Sepanggar Bay Container Port are progressing.",""],[2,"231","3","Sepanggar Bay Container Port Expansion","the upgrading works of the Sandakan Airport and the expansion of the Sepanggar Bay Container Port are progressing.",""],[2,"241","6","Subregional Cooperation for Cross-Border Economic Development","Regional development will continue to leverage the subregional cooperation platform to promote and accelerate socioeconomic growth.",""],[2,"242","2","Acceleration of Subregional Connectivity Initiatives","Measures will continue to be undertaken to improve infrastructure accessibility and connectivity by accelerating the implementation of existing subregional initiatives as well as embarking on a new framework to spur economic growth at border areas.",""],[2,"242","2","Implementation of IMT-GT and BIMP-EAGA Connectivity Projects","The implementation of the existing PCPs in IMT-GT and PIPs in BIMP-EAGA will be expedited to boost trade and socioeconomic activities.",""],[2,"242","2","Rantau Panjang-Sungai Golok Bridge Upgrade","the bridge connecting Rantau Panjang, Kelantan and Sungai Golok, Narathiwat will be upgraded.",""],[2,"242","2","Pan Borneo Highway Completion","the completion of more segments of the Pan Borneo Highway project will enhance economic growth across Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[2,"242","3","Enhanced Collaboration and Coordination for Subregional Initiatives","Implementation of subregional initiatives will be further enhanced through better collaboration and coordination among stakeholders for Malaysia to optimise the economic opportunities.",""]],"183":[[1,"244","7","Green Mobility Promotion","The adoption of the green mobility approach to facilitate the movement of people via public transport and active mobility will be promoted.",""],[1,"244","7","Public Transport Accessibility and Connectivity Improvement","Accessibility, connectivity and efficiency of public transport will be improved, including through TOD and first- and last-mile connectivity to attract people to shift from private vehicles to public transport.",""],[1,"244","7","Urban Pedestrian Infrastructure Upgrade","Pedestrian infrastructure in urban areas will be upgraded to ensure that it is safe, user-friendly and connected to public transport nodes to encourage active mobility among urban dwellers.",""],[1,"298","6","Green Mobility and Low-Carbon Cities Initiative","efforts will also be focused on promoting green and resilient cities and townships, enhancing green mobility and augmenting the consumption of low- carbon energy as well as expanding the green market and GGP.",""],[1,"299","4","Low-Carbon Mobility Blueprint","a low- carbon mobility blueprint will be introduced to guide the planning, implementation, monitoring and evaluation of green mobility initiatives.",""],[1,"299","4","Green Public Transport and Active Mobility Upgrade","Accessibility, connectivity, safety and reliability of public transport will be further improved.",""],[1,"299","4","Local Green Mobility Planning and Regulatory Review","master plans and design guidelines for green mobility at the local level will be developed, while relevant legislation at the Federal and state levels will be reviewed.",""],[1,"299","5","Green Vehicle Promotion and Incentives Review","The usage of green vehicles, which reduce air pollution and GHG emissions, and increase energy efficiency, as a preferred mode of transport will be promoted to drive the transition to green mobility.",""],[1,"299","5","Mandatory Energy-Efficient Driving Programme","an energy-efficient driving programme12 for all classes of vehicles will be made mandatory.",""],[1,"299","5","Fuel Economy Standards for New Vehicles","Adoption of fuel economy standards to increase fuel efficiency for new vehicles will also be encouraged.",""],[1,"299","6","B20 and B30 Biodiesel Expansion Programme","The B20 biodiesel programme that contains 20% palm methyl ester will be expanded throughout the country in stages, while the B30 programme will be introduced at the end of the Twelfth Plan to further increase the use of biofuel.",""],[1,"299","6","Alternative Fuel Expansion Initiative","Alternative fuel sources, including compressed natural gas, hydrogen energy and fuel cell will also be expanded.",""],[1,"299","6","Green Vehicle Expansion for Transport and Logistics","The use of green vehicles, particularly for public transport as well as logistics and delivery services will be expanded, while the shift of freight transport mode from road to rail will be further encouraged.",""],[1,"299","6","Transport Sector Carbon Impact Assessment","Carbon impact assessment for the transport sector will be developed.",""],[1,"299","6","Old Vehicle Phase-Out Study","A study to identify mechanisms in phasing out old vehicles in a sustainable manner will also be undertaken.",""],[1,"299","9","Integrated Multimodal Transport Connectivity","The joining of every different form of transport, especially smaller vehicles to ensure quick and easy as possible journeys, particularly for the first- and last- mile.",""],[1,"299","10","Energy-Efficient Driving Training Requirement","Training that incorporates energy-efficient driving techniques as a requirement to obtain driving licenses and permit applications.",""],[1,"300","1","Green Mobility Investment and Incentive Support","The private sector will be encouraged to invest in advancing next generation vehicles, technologies and supporting infrastructure, such as energy-efficient, hydrogen-powered and electric vehicles, and their charging stations.",""],[1,"300","1","Green Mobility Collaboration and Enabling Framework Strengthening","triple-helix13 collaboration will be intensified, while the green-related incentive schemes will be enhanced.",""],[1,"300","1","Green Mobility Regulatory and Standards Framework","The enabling ecosystem, in terms of policies, legislation, standards, incentives and best practices, will be strengthened to facilitate private-driven initiatives and ensure effective implementation of the green mobility agenda.",""],[2,"299","4","Low-Carbon Mobility Blueprint","a low- carbon mobility blueprint will be introduced to guide the planning, implementation, monitoring and evaluation of green mobility initiatives.",""],[2,"299","4","Green Public Transport and Active Mobility Expansion","The blueprint will outline strategies to reduce GHG emissions from the transportation sector as well as accelerate the shift to green mobility, particularly low-carbon public transport and active mobility.",""],[2,"299","4","Public Transport Accessibility and Reliability Improvement","Accessibility, connectivity, safety and reliability of public transport will be further improved.",""],[2,"299","4","Micro-Mobility Services Expansion","Simultaneously, micro- mobility11 services for first- and last-mile connectivity, which enable seamless movement, will be expanded to increase access to public transport.",""],[2,"299","4","Pedestrian and Cycling Infrastructure Enhancement","In promoting active mobility, pedestrian and cycling infrastructure will be enhanced to be user-friendly, connected, safe and comfortable.",""],[2,"299","4","Local Green Mobility Master Plans and Design Guidelines","To ensure effective implementation of green mobility initiatives, master plans and design guidelines for green mobility at the local level will be developed, while relevant legislation at the Federal and state levels will be reviewed.",""],[2,"299","5","Green Vehicle Promotion and Incentive Review","The usage of green vehicles, which reduce air pollution and GHG emissions, and increase energy efficiency, as a preferred mode of transport will be promoted to drive the transition to green mobility.",""],[2,"299","5","Mandatory Energy-Efficient Driving Programme","an energy-efficient driving programme12 for all classes of vehicles will be made mandatory.",""],[2,"299","5","Fuel Economy Standards for New Vehicles","Adoption of fuel economy standards to increase fuel efficiency for new vehicles will also be encouraged.",""],[2,"299","6","B20 and B30 Biodiesel Expansion Programme","The B20 biodiesel programme that contains 20% palm methyl ester will be expanded throughout the country in stages, while the B30 programme will be introduced at the end of the Twelfth Plan to further increase the use of biofuel.",""],[2,"299","6","Alternative Fuel Expansion Initiative","Alternative fuel sources, including compressed natural gas, hydrogen energy and fuel cell will also be expanded.",""],[2,"299","6","Green Vehicle Promotion for Transport Services","The use of green vehicles, particularly for public transport as well as logistics and delivery services will be expanded, while the shift of freight transport mode from road to rail will be further encouraged.",""],[2,"299","6","Transport Sector Carbon Impact Assessment","Carbon impact assessment for the transport sector will be developed.",""],[2,"299","6","Sustainable Vehicle Retirement Study","A study to identify mechanisms in phasing out old vehicles in a sustainable manner will also be undertaken.",""],[2,"299","9","First- and Last-Mile Transport Integration","The joining of every different form of transport, especially smaller vehicles to ensure quick and easy as possible journeys, particularly for the first- and last- mile.",""],[2,"299","10","Energy-Efficient Driving Training Requirement","Training that incorporates energy-efficient driving techniques as a requirement to obtain driving licenses and permit applications.",""],[2,"300","1","Green Mobility Investment and Enabling Ecosystem Strengthening","The private sector will be encouraged to invest in advancing next generation vehicles, technologies and supporting infrastructure, such as energy-efficient, hydrogen-powered and electric vehicles, and their charging stations.",""],[2,"321","3","Cleaner Fuels Promotion Initiative","Cleaner fuels continued to be promoted towards reducing greenhouse gas emissions to combat climate change.",""]],"184":[[1,"245","8","Rural Roads and Bridges Upgrade Programme","The provision of rural infrastructure will be further expanded through constructing and upgrading of roads, bridges and digital infrastructure.",""],[1,"245","8","Rural Street Lighting Installation","These include building and upgrading 2,800 kilometres of paved roads, 100 bridges and installing street lights to ensure the safety of road users.",""],[1,"245","8","Rural Fixed Broadband Expansion","Digital infrastructure will be expanded to increase fixed broadband coverage in rural areas, targeting at least 20% of premises with up to 500Mbps.",""],[1,"246","2","Rural Connectivity and Mobility Improvement","Connectivity and mobility between rural and urban areas will be improved to bridge the development gap and foster greater economic integration.",""],[1,"246","2","Rural Transport Services Enhancement","Transportation services, such as buses, e-hailing and water transportation in rural areas will be enhanced.",""],[1,"246","2","Rural Internet and Telecommunications Expansion","Measures to widen internet and telecommunication coverage will also be undertaken for better connectivity in rural areas.",""],[1,"246","2","eCommerce Programme for Rural Entrepreneurs","The eCommerce programme will be intensified to assist rural entrepreneurs to migrate from traditional business methods to digital platforms for better market access.",""],[1,"246","2","Rural Service Hub Development through PKDs","PKDs will be leveraged to be the hub for services in rural areas in facilitating the delivery of government and business services.",""],[1,"246","2","Digitalisation Promotion through PIDs","PIDs will be enhanced to promote digitalisation among the rural population.",""],[2,"245","4","Rural Connectivity Expansion","Rural areas will be further developed to narrow the development gap between rural and urban areas by upgrading infrastructure and basic amenities, providing better connectivity and expanding socioeconomic activities.",""],[2,"246","2","Rural-Urban Connectivity and Mobility Improvement","Connectivity and mobility between rural and urban areas will be improved to bridge the development gap and foster greater economic integration.",""],[2,"246","2","Rural Transport Services Enhancement","Transportation services, such as buses, e-hailing and water transportation in rural areas will be enhanced.",""],[2,"254","1","Sandakan Airport Runway Extension","The Sandakan Airport is undergoing runway extension works to allow bigger planes to land without weight restriction.",""],[2,"264","2","Public Transport and Logistics Services Improvement","This will be undertaken through improvement of public transport and logistics services, which will spur economic activities, reduce the cost of doing business and enable services to be better delivered to the people.",""],[2,"264","3","RAS Subsidy for Rural Sabah and Sarawak","the Federal Government will continue to subsidise RAS for Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[2,"264","3","Rural Air Service Route Rationalisation and Expansion","The exercise will involve rationalisation of existing routes and the possible introduction of new ones to enhance overall connectivity in rural Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[2,"264","3","STOLport Maintenance Programme","the airport operators will continue to undertake the maintenance of STOLports.",""],[2,"269","11","Rural Connectivity and Mobility Enhancement","Linkages between rural and urban areas will be improved by enhancing connectivity and mobility to foster greater economic integration.",""],[2,"269","11","Rural Transport Services Enhancement","Transportation services in rural areas such as rural buses, water transportation services and e-hailing will be enhanced.",""]],"185":[[1,"264","2","Public Transport and Logistics Services Improvement","This will be undertaken through improvement of public transport and logistics services, which will spur economic activities, reduce the cost of doing business and enable services to be better delivered to the people.",""],[1,"264","4","Logistics Infrastructure and Last-Mile Connectivity Enhancement","The efficiency of logistics services in Sabah and Sarawak will be enhanced by improving existing infrastructure as well as last-mile connectivity.",""],[1,"264","5","Sepanggar Port Upgrading","The upgrading of the Sepanggar Port which commenced in 2020 is expected to be completed in 2024.",""],[1,"264","5","Borneo Trade Connectivity Enhancement","In supporting this, road connectivity to industrial and cargo hubs, as well as the interior of Sabah will be enhanced.",""],[1,"264","6","Bintulu Port Capacity and Service Upgrading","The upgrading of the capacity and services of Bintulu Port is vital in establishing it as one of the main ports of call on Borneo Island.",""],[1,"264","6","Last-Mile Connectivity Improvement","In addition, the last-mile connectivity will be improved to enable efficient and effective delivery of goods to consumers, particularly in the hinterland areas.",""],[1,"264","6","Road Connectivity Improvement","In this regard, road connectivity will be improved.",""],[1,"267","2","Pan Borneo Highway Consolidation Hubs","consolidation hubs will be established along the route to ensure cargo handling efficiency.",""],[1,"267","2","Inland Container Port Development and Improvement","It is also important to develop and improve inland container port facilities to support inland logistics, particularly the Keningau Inland Port in Sabah and the Tebedu Inland Port in Sarawak.",""],[1,"267","2","Targeted Airline Connectivity Incentives","Regional and local airline connectivity will be enhanced by providing incentives to targeted airlines.",""],[1,"267","2","Logistics Supplier Partnership Promotion","logistics services providers will be encouraged to create partnerships with suppliers.",""],[1,"267","5","Mega Projects Construction Programme","The construction of mega projects, such as the Pan Borneo Highway, Sarawak Water Grid Programme and Sabah Seafront will spur the growth of the construction sector.",""],[1,"267","5","Construction Materials Testing Laboratory Upgrade","The laboratory facilities for testing the aforementioned materials will be upgraded to increase capacity and speed up approval processes.",""],[2,"264","4","Logistics Infrastructure and Last-Mile Connectivity Upgrade","The efficiency of logistics services in Sabah and Sarawak will be enhanced by improving existing infrastructure as well as last-mile connectivity.",""],[2,"264","5","Sepanggar Port Upgrading","The upgrading of the Sepanggar Port which commenced in 2020 is expected to be completed in 2024.",""],[2,"264","5","Road Connectivity Enhancement to Industrial and Cargo Hubs","In supporting this, road connectivity to industrial and cargo hubs, as well as the interior of Sabah will be enhanced.",""],[2,"264","6","Bintulu Port Capacity and Service Upgrading","The upgrading of the capacity and services of Bintulu Port is vital in establishing it as one of the main ports of call on Borneo Island.",""],[2,"264","6","Last-Mile Connectivity Improvement","In addition, the last-mile connectivity will be improved to enable efficient and effective delivery of goods to consumers, particularly in the hinterland areas.",""],[2,"264","6","Road Connectivity Improvement","In this regard, road connectivity will be improved.",""],[2,"267","2","Pan Borneo Highway Consolidation Hubs","consolidation hubs will be established along the route to ensure cargo handling efficiency.",""],[2,"267","2","Inland Container Port Development and Improvement","It is also important to develop and improve inland container port facilities to support inland logistics, particularly the Keningau Inland Port in Sabah and the Tebedu Inland Port in Sarawak.",""],[2,"267","2","Targeted Airline Connectivity Incentives","Regional and local airline connectivity will be enhanced by providing incentives to targeted airlines.",""],[2,"267","2","Logistics Supplier Partnership Promotion","logistics services providers will be encouraged to create partnerships with suppliers.",""],[2,"267","3","Road, Last-Mile Connectivity, and Digital Infrastructure Expansion","Roads and last-mile connectivity, as well as digital infrastructure will allow businesses to grow and permeate into rural areas, as well as access to reasonably priced goods and services.",""]],"186":[[1,"268","8","Sabah-Sarawak-Kalimantan Transport Connectivity Improvement","Transport connectivity between Sabah and Sarawak with Kalimantan will be improved.",""],[1,"268","8","Border Town and ICQS Facility Development","To support bilateral economic activities between Serudong and Simanggaris, Immigration, Customs, Quarantine and Security Complex (ICQS) facilities and border towns will be developed in the surrounding areas.",""],[1,"268","8","Cross-Border Road Links and ICQS Facilities Development","Consideration will also be given in developing other potential cross-border road links and ICQS facilities, including in Pegalungan, Nabawan and Long Pasia, Sipitang.",""],[1,"268","8","Sarawak CIQ Facility Upgrading Programme","In Sarawak, Customs, Immigration and Quarantine (CIQ) facilities in Tebedu, Serikin and Telok Melano will be upgraded to cater for the increasing cross-border commercial activities.",""],[1,"268","8","Border Crossing Digital and Utility Infrastructure Upgrade","The digital infrastructure, electricity and water supply in priority border crossings and border towns in Sabah and Sarawak will be upgraded to stimulate growth.",""],[2,"268","8","Sabah-Sarawak-Kalimantan Cross-Border Connectivity Improvement","Transport connectivity between Sabah and Sarawak with Kalimantan will be improved.",""],[2,"268","8","Border Town and ICQS Facility Development","To support bilateral economic activities between Serudong and Simanggaris, Immigration, Customs, Quarantine and Security Complex (ICQS) facilities and border towns will be developed in the surrounding areas.",""],[2,"268","8","Upgrade of Sarawak CIQ Facilities","In Sarawak, Customs, Immigration and Quarantine (CIQ) facilities in Tebedu, Serikin and Telok Melano will be upgraded to cater for the increasing cross-border commercial activities.",""],[2,"268","8","Border Crossing Digital and Utility Infrastructure Upgrade","The digital infrastructure, electricity and water supply in priority border crossings and border towns in Sabah and Sarawak will be upgraded to stimulate growth.",""]],"187":[[1,"415","3","Regional Highway and Rail Connectivity Expansion","Efforts to enhance connectivity across regions include the construction of highways and rail projects with underserved areas given priority.",""],[1,"415","4","LPT3 Highway Project","The proposed LPT3 will connect Gemuruh, Terengganu to Tok Bali, Kelantan and is expected to provide a smoother journey to the east coast while boosting economic activities along the corridor.",""],[1,"415","5","Pan Borneo Sabah Highway Construction","The Pan Borneo Sabah Highway was initiated in 2016 to provide road connectivity from Sindumin to Tawau.",""]],"188":[[1,"415","5","Pan Borneo Sarawak Highway Construction","The Pan Borneo Sarawak Highway from Telok Melano to Miri was 59.4% completed at the end of 2020 and is expected to be ready by 2022.",""],[1,"415","6","Highway Construction and Completion Programme","Five highways are under construction to improve connectivity and ease congestion in the Greater Kuala Lumpur/Klang Valley (GKL/KV).",""],[1,"425","5","Highway Development Restructuring","A governance mechanism will be introduced for the shipping industry and highway development will be restructured to optimise benefits for both customers and industry players.",""],[1,"426","5","Highway Development Model Review and Toll Restructuring","The current model for existing and new highway development will be reviewed to ensure that people will benefit from reasonable toll rates, while ensuring fair returns to investors.",""],[1,"426","5","Highway Concession Restructuring for Operations and Maintenance","The restructuring aims to reduce the risk to the government while enabling concessionaires to undertake operations and maintenance of the highway and generate fair returns from toll collection.",""],[1,"426","6","Highway Project Prioritization and Funding Mechanism","The HNDP 2030 will also provide a mechanism for prioritising new highways and available funding options.",""],[2,"426","5","Highway Development Model Review and Concession Restructuring","The current model for existing and new highway development will be reviewed to ensure that people will benefit from reasonable toll rates, while ensuring fair returns to investors.",""],[2,"426","6","Highway Project Prioritization and Funding Mechanism","The HNDP 2030 will also provide a mechanism for prioritising new highways and available funding options.",""],[2,"427","1","Transport Infrastructure Improvement for Seamless Mobility","The Plan gives priority to improving transport infrastructure in providing seamless people mobility.",""],[2,"427","1","Transport and Logistics Competitiveness and Governance Enhancement","It also focuses on enhancing competitiveness of the transport and logistics industry as well as its governance.",""]],"189":[[1,"416","6","New Kuala Lumpur Airport Traffic Control Centre","the completion of the new Kuala Lumpur Airport Traffic Control Centre in August 2021 is forecasted to increase the number of aircraft movements per hour from 68 to 108.",""],[1,"416","6","Kota Kinabalu International Airport Traffic Control Center Upgrading","Meanwhile, the upgrading of the Kota Kinabalu International Airport Traffic Control Center, which started in 2019 is expected to be completed by 2023.",""],[1,"418","3","Aviation Communication, Navigation and Surveillance System Upgrade","Hence, the system and equipment will need to be updated to ensure efficiency and competitiveness of the aviation services.",""],[1,"424","6","Aviation Infrastructure and Asset Modernization","outdated systems and obsolete equipment will be replaced and infrastructure will be upgraded",""],[1,"424","6","Aviation Infrastructure Maintenance Compliance Mechanism","A mechanism will be established for proper maintenance of infrastructure and assets to ensure that airports and air traffic management systems comply with the International Civil Aviation Organisation (ICAO) standards",""],[1,"424","6","Centralised Aviation Data and Communication System","A centralised system will be developed to improve transmission of data and communication to ensure operational efficiency",""],[1,"426","1","National Airports Strategic Plan","A National Airports Strategic Plan will be formulated to provide policy direction for the development of airports to meet future aviation needs and strengthen the governance of the aviation industry.",""],[2,"413","2","Merger of MAVCOM with CAAM","MAVCOM will be merged with the Civil Aviation Authority of Malaysia (CAAM) to rationalise the aviation sector",""],[2,"418","3","Air Traffic Management System and Equipment Upgrade","Hence, the system and equipment will need to be updated to ensure efficiency and competitiveness of the aviation services.",""],[2,"424","6","Aviation Systems Replacement and Infrastructure Upgrade","In the aviation sector, outdated systems and obsolete equipment will be replaced and infrastructure will be upgraded.",""],[2,"424","6","Aviation Infrastructure and Asset Maintenance Mechanism","A mechanism will be established for proper maintenance of infrastructure and assets to ensure that airports and air traffic management systems comply with the International Civil Aviation Organisation (ICAO) standards.",""],[2,"424","6","Centralised Aviation Data and Communication System","A centralised system will be developed to improve transmission of data and communication to ensure operational efficiency.",""],[2,"426","1","National Airports Strategic Plan","A National Airports Strategic Plan will be formulated to provide policy direction for the development of airports to meet future aviation needs and strengthen the governance of the aviation industry.",""]],"190":[[1,"369","11","Foreign Worker Dependency Reduction Initiatives","New initiatives will be introduced to address the dependency on foreign workers.",""],[1,"370","4","Foreign Worker Dependency Reduction and Local Labour Participation Initiative","Efforts will be undertaken to reduce the dependency on foreign workers and promote greater local participation in the labour market.",""],[1,"370","5","Policy to Reduce Dependency on Foreign Workers","A specific policy will also be introduced to reduce dependency on foreign workers to ensure that they leave the country after a certain period.",""],[1,"370","6","Multi-tier Levy Fund for Local Employment and Skills Upgrading","The excess levy collected through the implementation of multi-tier levy mechanism will be channelled to industry for the purpose of increasing job opportunities and implementing upskilling and reskilling programmes for locals.",""],[1,"370","7","Illegal Worker Deterrence Measures","More deterrent measures will be introduced to reduce the number of illegal workers, where majority of them are over stayers.",""],[1,"370","7","Migrant Deportation Deposit Mechanism","The current insurance guarantee mechanism will be replaced with a new mechanism, which requires deposit equivalent to total deportation",""],[1,"370","8","Foreign Worker Overstay Prevention Enforcement","This effort will be implemented together with the Holistic Enforcement Plan for Illegal Immigrants, the Foreign Workers Action Plan and the Recalibration Plan for Illegal Immigrants.",""],[2,"68","8","Reduction of Dependence on Low-Skilled Foreign Workers","In addition, measures will be taken to reduce dependency on low-skilled foreign workers.",""],[2,"369","11","Foreign Worker Dependency Reduction Initiative","New initiatives will be introduced to address the dependency on foreign workers.",""],[2,"370","4","Foreign Worker Dependency Reduction and Local Labour Market Participation Initiative","Efforts will be undertaken to reduce the dependency on foreign workers and promote greater local participation in the labour market.",""],[2,"370","5","Foreign Worker Dependency Reduction Policy","A specific policy will also be introduced to reduce dependency on foreign workers to ensure that they leave the country after a certain period.",""],[2,"370","6","Multi-tier Levy Fund for Local Employment and Skills Development","The excess levy collected through the implementation of multi-tier levy mechanism will be channelled to industry for the purpose of increasing job opportunities and implementing upskilling and reskilling programmes for locals.",""],[2,"370","6","Industry Automation and Mechanisation Support","Among the initiatives that can be funded include industry automation and mechanisation.",""],[2,"370","6","Employer Incentives for Conducive Workplaces","The fund will also be used to incentivise employers to create a more conducive working environment to attract locals.",""],[2,"370","7","Illegal Worker Deterrence and Deportation Deposit Mechanism","More deterrent measures will be introduced to reduce the number of illegal workers, where majority of them are over stayers.",""],[2,"370","8","Foreign Worker Overstay Prevention Enforcement","This effort will be implemented together with the Holistic Enforcement Plan for Illegal Immigrants, the Foreign Workers Action Plan and the Recalibration Plan for Illegal Immigrants.",""]],"191":[[1,"342","3","Labour Market Realignment and Support System Strengthening","Among the key initiatives to be undertaken to realign the labour market are promoting more equitable CE and higher female labour force participation as well as strengthening the labour market support system.",""],[1,"354","2","Labour Market Realignment for Inclusive Growth","The Twelfth Plan will focus on realigning the labour market for inclusive and sustainable growth as well as developing future-ready talent.",""],[1,"355","1","Labour Market Reform and Human Capital Strengthening","Efforts were undertaken to reform the labour market, improve labour efficiency, provide greater access to quality education and training as well as foster stronger industry-academia linkages.",""],[1,"359","5","Re-employment Placement Opportunity under Active Labour Market Policies","Act 800, which was enforced in January 2018, provides several benefits and a re-employment placement opportunity under active labour market policies for insured persons in the event of loss of employment.",""],[1,"366","9","Future Talent Development for a Dynamic Labour Market","The Twelfth Plan will focus on developing future talent for a dynamic labour market while addressing the employment-related issues caused by the COVID-19 pandemic.",""],[1,"366","9","Labour Market Realignment for Inclusiveness and Sustainability","the labour market will be realigned to be more inclusive and sustainable while future- ready talent will be developed.",""],[1,"366","9","Labour Market Support System Strengthening","Emphasis will be given in promoting equitable CE and labour participation, strengthening the labour market support system, elevating the quality of education, as well as leveraging emerging technologies.",""],[1,"369","1","COVID-19 Job Loss Mitigation Measures","In the immediate term, measures will be introduced to address job losses due to the COVID-19 pandemic.",""],[1,"369","1","Labour Market Policy Realignment","Over the longer term, realignments of current policies and support systems will be undertaken to build an inclusive, resilient and sustainable labour market.",""],[1,"369","1","Equitable Labour Participation Promotion","Among the measures to be undertaken during the Plan period include promoting equitable CE and labour participation as well as strengthening labour market support system, as shown in Exhibit 10-4.",""],[1,"369","1","Labour Market Support System Strengthening","Among the measures to be undertaken during the Plan period include promoting equitable CE and labour participation as well as strengthening labour market support system, as shown in Exhibit 10-4.",""],[1,"369","11","Equitable Circular Economy and Labour Market Strengthening Initiatives","Concerted efforts will be undertaken to promote equitable CE and improve labour participation.",""],[1,"369","11","Female Labour Force Participation Promotion","The participation of more females in the labour force will be encouraged to improve employment sustainability.",""],[1,"370","10","Supportive Social Policies to Increase Female Labour Force Participation","Measures to increase FLFPR will be undertaken by introducing more supportive social policies.",""],[1,"370","10","Home-Based Economic Activities for Women with Secondary Education","Females with secondary educational attainment will be encouraged to participate in labour market through home-based economic activities while continuing with household responsibilities.",""],[2,"342","3","Labour Market Realignment and Support System Strengthening","Among the key initiatives to be undertaken to realign the labour market are promoting more equitable CE and higher female labour force participation as well as strengthening the labour market support system.",""],[2,"354","2","Labour Market Realignment for Inclusive Growth","The Twelfth Plan will focus on realigning the labour market for inclusive and sustainable growth as well as developing future-ready talent.",""],[2,"359","5","Re-employment Placement under Active Labour Market Policies","Act 800, which was enforced in January 2018, provides several benefits and a re-employment placement opportunity under active labour market policies for insured persons in the event of loss of employment.",""],[2,"366","9","Future Talent Development for a Dynamic Labour Market","The Twelfth Plan will focus on developing future talent for a dynamic labour market while addressing the employment-related issues caused by the COVID-19 pandemic.",""],[2,"366","9","Labour Market Realignment for Inclusion and Sustainability","In this regard, the labour market will be realigned to be more inclusive and sustainable while future- ready talent will be developed.",""],[2,"366","9","Labour Market Support System Strengthening","Emphasis will be given in promoting equitable CE and labour participation, strengthening the labour market support system, elevating the quality of education, as well as leveraging emerging technologies.",""],[2,"369","1","COVID-19 Job Loss Response Measures","In the immediate term, measures will be introduced to address job losses due to the COVID-19 pandemic.",""],[2,"369","1","Labour Market Policy and Support System Realignment","Over the longer term, realignments of current policies and support systems will be undertaken to build an inclusive, resilient and sustainable labour market.",""],[2,"369","1","Equitable Labour Force Participation Promotion","Among the measures to be undertaken during the Plan period include promoting equitable CE and labour participation as well as strengthening labour market support system, as shown in Exhibit 10-4.",""],[2,"369","1","Labour Market Support System Strengthening","Among the measures to be undertaken during the Plan period include promoting equitable CE and labour participation as well as strengthening labour market support system, as shown in Exhibit 10-4.",""],[2,"369","11","Equitable Circular Economy and Labour Market Participation Initiative","Concerted efforts will be undertaken to promote equitable CE and improve labour participation.",""],[2,"369","11","Labour Market Strengthening for Worker Welfare and Equal Employment Access","The focus will be on strengthening the labour market to improve the standard of living of workers and provide equal access to employment opportunities.",""],[2,"369","11","Female Labour Force Participation Promotion","The participation of more females in the labour force will be encouraged to improve employment sustainability.",""],[2,"371","12","National Employment Council Coordination Mechanism","initiatives by various stakeholders will be coordinated by the newly established National Employment Council (NEC) chaired by the Prime Minister.",""],[2,"372","1","Employment Creation and Skills Mismatch Strategy Implementation","will oversee the implementation of strategies in creating 500,000 employment opportunities by the end of 2021 as well as in addressing issues related to skills mismatch in the labour market.",""],[2,"372","2","Enhanced Employment Services Portal","The employment services portal will be enhanced to enable redistribution of the workforce disrupted by the COVID-19 pandemic besides redeployment of displaced workers due to automation.",""]],"192":[[1,"70","2","Fiscal Consolidation for Long-Term Sustainability","Fiscal consolidation will resume once the economy is on a better footing to ensure long- term fiscal sustainability.",""],[1,"70","3","Fiscal Responsibility Act","Fiscal governance will be strengthened by institutionalising the fiscal sustainability principles throughccc the introduction of the Fiscal Responsibility Act, which is imperative to ensure long-term fiscal sustainability.",""],[1,"70","3","Revenue Mobilization Reform Package","Revenue will be enhanced by exploring new sources, expanding the revenue base, reviewing tax incentives, strengthening overall tax administration and adopting a medium- term revenue strategy.",""],[1,"70","3","Public Expenditure Management Reform","The management of expenditure will be strengthened by introducing medium-term budgeting and expenditure frameworks, undertaking public expenditure reviews and improving Government procurement management to ensure spending efficiency and effectiveness.",""],[1,"70","3","Debt and Liabilities Management Enhancement","The medium- and long-term debt and liabilities management will continue to be enhanced with the implementation of accrual accounting, introduction of medium-term debt strategy, establishment of the Debt Management Office as well as enhancement of the government guarantees framework.",""]],"193":[[1,"103","3","Third Capital Market Masterplan","The launching of third capital market masterplan and the new blueprint for the financial sector will serve to steer the direction of the overall financial system over the next five years.",""],[1,"103","3","Financial Sector Blueprint","The launching of third capital market masterplan and the new blueprint for the financial sector will serve to steer the direction of the overall financial system over the next five years.",""],[1,"103","7","Financial Ecosystem Strengthening Initiative","Efforts will be undertaken to ensure that the financial ecosystem is able to meet future needs of the economy.",""],[2,"74","5","Financial Intermediation Ecosystem Promotion","an effective financial intermediation ecosystem will be promoted, with a focus on promoting innovation, competitiveness, as well as the Islamic Finance agenda.",""],[2,"82","2","Financial Intermediation Strengthening Initiative","strengthening the effectiveness of financial intermediation ecosystem",""],[2,"103","3","Third Capital Market Masterplan","The launching of third capital market masterplan and the new blueprint for the financial sector will serve to steer the direction of the overall financial system over the next five years.",""],[2,"103","3","New Financial Sector Blueprint","The launching of third capital market masterplan and the new blueprint for the financial sector will serve to steer the direction of the overall financial system over the next five years.",""],[2,"103","7","Financial Ecosystem Strengthening Efforts","Efforts will be undertaken to ensure that the financial ecosystem is able to meet future needs of the economy.",""],[2,"104","2","Financial Services Innovation and Digitisation Initiative","efforts will be focused on facilitating innovation and technological applications in the financial services sector.",""],[2,"104","2","E-Payments Expansion and Acceleration","The adoption of e-payments in the economy for more seamless and secure financial services experience will also be expanded and accelerated.",""],[2,"104","2","Financial Sector Digitisation Measures","measures will be undertaken to facilitate greater industry digitisation to improve overall efficiency of the financial services.",""],[2,"104","3","Market Entry Facilitation for New Digital Financial Players","efforts will be undertaken to facilitate entry of new players such as digital banks, digital insurers, robo-advisors and digital brokers, as well as support market participants in embracing new innovative business models",""],[2,"104","3","Enabling Infrastructure and Regulatory Enhancement","Enhancements to key enabling infrastructure, regulations and practices will also be pursued",""],[2,"104","3","Regional Connectivity and Linkages Enhancement","There will also be continued efforts to enhance regional connectivity and linkages to attract greater foreign capital and knowledge transfer into the country",""],[2,"104","4","Expansion of Market-Based MSME Financing Avenues","Differentiated market-based fundraising avenues will be further expanded to cater to the fundraising needs of MSMEs across their growth cycle, as well as more mature companies seeking regional expansion.",""],[2,"104","4","Development of Alternative Financing for MSMEs","This entails the development of a vibrant alternative financing to complement the banking system, as well as reinforcing consumer protection in the provision of credit, given the growing number of non-traditional entities.",""],[2,"104","4","Expansion of Microfinancing for Enterprises","In addition, efforts to enhance the provision of microfinancing to these enterprises will continue to be pursued.",""],[2,"104","5","Financial System Resilience and Governance Strengthening","Focus will be given on strengthening safeguards for financial stability and enhancing good governance.",""],[2,"104","6","Collaborative Regulatory Enforcement Framework","A more collaborative approach among regulatory authorities within and beyond the country will be adopted to strengthen regulatory enforcement",""],[2,"104","6","RegTech and SupTech Development Initiative","tools and mechanisms relating to regulatory technology (regtech) and supervisory technology (suptech) will also be developed to enhance the effectiveness and efficiency of regulators' role and functions",""],[2,"104","7","Outcome-Focused Financial Sector Regulatory Enhancement","Regulatory and supervisory focus towards inculcating good culture and conduct within the financial sector will be enhanced through more outcome-focused regulatory action to shape market and institutional behaviour.",""],[2,"104","7","Investor Confidence and Directors' Duties Strengthening","This includes greater emphasis on strengthening investor confidence in listed companies through effective discharge of directors' duties and responsibilities.",""],[2,"104","7","Institutional Investor Stewardship and Anti-Corruption Measures","In addition, the role of institutional investors in good governance and stewardship will be enhanced, and holistic anti-corruption measures will be implemented within the capital market.",""],[2,"105","2","Strengthening Islamic Finance Regulation and Supervision","Efforts to consolidate Malaysia's role as a prominent thought leader in Islamic finance, particularly in the areas of regulation and supervision will be intensified.",""],[2,"105","2","Expansion of Value-Based Intermediation Principles","Additionally, the adoption of value-based intermediation (VBI) principles in the provision of finance will be expanded.",""],[2,"105","2","Islamic Social Finance Mobilisation","Islamic financial institutions have been exploring the usage of social finance instruments through blending endowment (waqf), donation (sadaqah) and alms-giving (zakat), to further unlock and more effectively mobilise resources towards provision of financing and financial protection to low income communities.",""],[2,"105","2","Islamic Fintech Market Innovation Mechanisms","In this regard, measures will be undertaken to develop more innovative market- based mechanisms and products, leveraging on Islamic fintech, to better serve the needs of a wider financial market and the economy at large.",""],[2,"105","3","Financial Inclusion Expansion and Innovative Delivery Measures","Advancing the financial inclusion agenda remains a key priority to ensure all Malaysians have meaningful access to quality and affordable financial services, with emphasis on innovative financial solutions, technology-led modes of delivery and assessment tools.",""],[2,"105","3","Micro-Insurance and Micro-Takaful Expansion","The offering of micro-insurance and micro-takaful products will be expanded, while instituting measures to ensure long-term sustainability of medical health insurance and takaful for the",""],[2,"105","4","Financial Inclusion Reform and Structural Issue Resolution","Efforts will also be accorded to expedite reforms and address structural issues that hinder the financial inclusion agenda, such as inadequacy of financial safety nets to buffer B40 households from income shocks.",""],[2,"105","4","National Financial Literacy Strategy","At the same time, initiatives under the National Strategy for Financial Literacy will continue to be pursued to further improve financial literacy among Malaysians.",""],[2,"105","6","Islamic Capital Market Expansion for Social Finance","This will include broadening Islamic capital market products and services to further support social finance activities, such as waqf, for the greater good of society.",""]],"194":[[1,"105","5","Financial Sector Climate Change Action Committee","a committee comprising of Bank Negara Malaysia, the Securities Commission Malaysia and the financial industry, will drive and support climate change actions within the sector.",""],[2,"104","3","Cyber Security Framework Implementation","including implementation of an effective cyber security framework to promote greater efficiency, safety and resilience",""],[2,"105","5","Financial Sector Climate Change Action Committee","a committee comprising of Bank Negara Malaysia, the Securities Commission Malaysia and the financial industry, will drive and support climate change actions within the sector.","Bank Negara Malaysia | the Securities Commission Malaysia"],[2,"105","6","Value-Based Intermediation Framework","Through VBI, Islamic finance will bring various stakeholders together to advance the sustainability agenda.",""],[2,"105","6","Sustainable and Responsible Investment Ecosystem Development","efforts to develop a facilitative Sustainable and Responsible Investment (SRI) ecosystem under the SRI Roadmap will also be intensified.",""]],"195":[[1,"169","3","Prison Management and Rehabilitation Improvement","In addition, prison management and operations will be improved to provide more effective correctional and rehabilitation programmes.",""],[1,"170","3","Prison Management and Operations Improvement","The management and operation of prisons will be improved to enhance service delivery.",""],[1,"170","3","Detention Centre and Correctional Programme Development Plan","A holistic plan will be developed to improve detention centres as well as rehabilitation and correctional programmes.",""],[1,"170","3","Prison Personnel Capacity and Capability Enhancement","In supporting this, the capacity and capability of prison personnel will be enhanced.",""],[1,"170","3","Prison Infrastructure Upgrade for Rehabilitation","Prisons will be upgraded to provide a more conducive environment and adequate space for rehabilitation programmes.",""],[1,"170","3","Segregation of Drug Offenders in Prisons","Drug offenders under Section 15 of the Dangerous Drug Act 1952 will be segregated from other inmates within the prison.",""],[1,"170","4","Expansion of Alternatives to Imprisonment","Alternatives to imprisonment will be expanded by implementing more probation and community corrections programmes.",""],[1,"170","4","Reintegration Partnerships for Ex-Inmates and Parolees","In addition, strategic partnerships among CSOs, volunteers and employers will be enhanced, particularly for the reintegration into society and smart internships with the corporate sector.",""],[2,"169","3","Prison Management and Rehabilitation Improvement","In addition, prison management and operations will be improved to provide more effective correctional and rehabilitation programmes.",""],[2,"170","3","Prison Management and Operations Improvement","The management and operation of prisons will be improved to enhance service delivery.",""],[2,"170","3","Detention Centre and Correctional Programme Improvement Plan","A holistic plan will be developed to improve detention centres as well as rehabilitation and correctional programmes.",""],[2,"170","3","Prison Personnel Capacity Building","the capacity and capability of prison personnel will be enhanced.",""],[2,"170","3","Prison Infrastructure Upgrade for Rehabilitation","Prisons will be upgraded to provide a more conducive environment and adequate space for rehabilitation programmes.",""],[2,"170","3","Segregation of Drug Offenders in Prisons","Drug offenders under Section 15 of the Dangerous Drug Act 1952 will be segregated from other inmates within the prison.",""],[2,"170","4","Expansion of Alternatives to Imprisonment","Alternatives to imprisonment will be expanded by implementing more probation and community corrections programmes.",""],[2,"170","4","Ex-Inmate Reintegration Partnership Strengthening","In addition, strategic partnerships among CSOs, volunteers and employers will be enhanced, particularly for the reintegration into society and smart internships with the corporate sector.",""]],"196":[[1,"230","7","City Competitiveness Master Plan for George Town and Kuantan","The CCMP for George Town and Kuantan is expected to be completed in 2021.",""],[1,"230","7","City Competitiveness Master Plans","Four City Competitiveness Master Plans (CCMPs) were completed for the FT of Kuala Lumpur, Johor Bahru, Kuching and Kota Kinabalu.",""],[1,"237","3","Green City Action Plan Implementation","Implement Green City Action Plan under IMT-GT and BIMP-EAGA Platform",""]],"197":[[1,"238","9","Regional and State Strategic Development Programmes","strategic development programmes at the regional and state levels will be implemented through state-driven initiatives and private sector-led projects.",""],[1,"238","9","Private-Sector-Led New Township Development","The development of new townships led by the private sector, including in the Setia Fontaines, Pulau Pinang as well as Seriemas in Ampangan and Rantau, Negeri Sembilan, are expected to provide additional job and business opportunities.",""],[1,"238","9","Eco-City Township Development at Setia Fontaines","The Setia Fontaines township is expected to leverage the eco-city concept",""],[1,"238","9","Transit-Oriented and Transit-Adjacent Township Development","Seriemas township will focus on Transit Oriented Development (TOD) and Transit Adjacent Development (TAD), thereby encouraging compact development in a high density area.",""],[1,"238","10","Integrated Mixed Development Projects","Integrated and comprehensive mixed development projects, including the catalytic development of Malaysia Vision Valley 2.0 (MVV 2.0) in Negeri Sembilan and the proposed Pagoh Special Economic Zone in Johor will provide new opportunities for growth.",""]],"198":[[1,"242","4","Effective Urban Planning and Governance","Priority will be given in promoting effective urban planning and governance, fostering a sustainable urban economy, prioritising green and resilient urban development as well as developing sustainable urban society.",""],[1,"242","9","Urbanisation Blueprint for Cities","Urbanisation blueprint to be implemented by all cities and its stakeholders, in support of the 2030 Agenda, especially in making cities inclusive, safe, resilient and sustainable.",""],[1,"243","1","Urban Development Data System Improvement","Databases at the urban level will be improved to strengthen urban development planning.",""],[1,"243","1","Sustainable and Smart City Promotion Measures","Measures will also be undertaken to promote sustainable and smart city approaches for better wellbeing of urban dwellers.",""],[1,"243","1","Local Government Law Enforcement and Coordination","Laws relating to local governments will also be further enforced through better coordination.",""],[1,"243","2","Second National Urbanisation Policy Implementation","The Second National Urbanisation Policy (NUP2) will continue to drive the planning and development of urban areas to be more cohesive and effective.",""],[1,"243","2","Urban Profiling Improvement for Local Planning","Urban profiling will be improved based on the findings of the Kajian Penentuan Sempadan Bandar to facilitate better planning at the local government level.",""],[1,"243","2","Malaysia Urban Observatory Data Analytics System","The Malaysia Urban Observatory (MUO), a multidimensional big data analytics system will be introduced as an integrated policy tool for better planning and decision-making.",""],[1,"243","2","Urban Data Sharing and Open Data Initiative","The MUO will enhance urban data collection and data openness as well as promote data sharing among multiple stakeholders for spatial planning at all levels of government.",""],[1,"243","2","Fourth National Physical Plan","Meanwhile, the Fourth National Physical Plan (NPP4) to be launched in 2021 will provide a comprehensive spatial planning framework, which will also cover urban planning.",""],[1,"243","3","MURNInets Adoption by Local Authorities","All local authorities will be encouraged to adopt the MURNInets system.",""],[1,"243","3","MSCF Framework for Smart City Agenda Implementation","The MSCF will be adopted as the framework in implementing the smart city agenda.",""],[1,"243","3","National Smart City Governance Strengthening","Efforts to strengthen smart city governance at the national level will leverage technical experts.",""],[1,"243","3","Smart City Accreditation and Recognition Standards","Assessment indicators will be introduced to set the standard for accreditation, qualification and recognition of smart cities.",""],[1,"243","4","Strengthening National and Local Planning Coordination","The role of the National Physical Planning Council and National Council for Local Government will be enhanced to enable effective planning and implementation of sustainable development through better coordination and cooperation among agencies at Federal, state and local levels.",""],[1,"243","4","Local Government Star Rating System Alignment","The Local Government Star Rating System will be aligned with the 2030 Agenda.",""],[1,"243","4","Local SDG Implementation Promotion","Efforts will also be undertaken to promote the SDGs' implementation at the local level.",""],[1,"243","4","Governance Enforcement and Legislative Reform","Governance mechanisms will be improved by intensifying enforcement and improving the relevant legislations, including the Local Government Act 1976, Town and Country Planning Act 1976 as well as Road, Drainage and Building Act 1974.",""],[1,"397","3","Smart Cities Development Initiative","the development of smart cities will take into consideration these elements in order to address issues pertaining to energy consumption, public transport as well as waste and disaster management.",""],[1,"406","5","Big Data-Powered Urban Planning Optimization","Big-data-powered visualisation and simulation to optimise urban land, space and buildings",""]],"199":[[1,"243","5","Urban Economy Development Promotion","Focus will be given to promote the development of the urban economy by leveraging the potential of cities to attract investment and talent.",""],[1,"243","5","Urban Agglomeration and Ecosystem Enhancement","Efforts will include enhancing urban agglomeration and ecosystem, encouraging the growth of economic activities in urban areas and leveraging city competitiveness.",""],[1,"243","6","Urban Economic Agglomeration and Ecosystem Improvement Initiatives","Identified growth areas, such as urban conurbations6, promoted development zones and catalyst centres, particularly in less developed regions will be leveraged to create economic agglomeration in achieving higher productivity and economic density.",""],[1,"243","6","Urban Infrastructure, Accessibility, Connectivity, and Talent Development Initiatives","Besides, initiatives to improve the ecosystem in urban areas will focus on providing better infrastructure, accessibility and connectivity as well as enhancing talent development.",""],[1,"244","1","Urban Economic Activity Revitalization","Concerted efforts will be undertaken to generate more vibrant and viable urban economic activities, including addressing the impact of the COVID-19 pandemic.",""],[1,"244","1","Urban Digital Ecosystem and eCommerce Support","Efforts will be intensified to improve business activities in urban areas through a better digital ecosystem.",""],[1,"244","1","Commercial Area Planning Guidelines Review","Meanwhile, the Planning Guidelines for Commercial Areas will be reviewed to optimise the utilisation of commercial floor space in urban areas as well as promote mixed-use development and digital ecosystems.",""],[1,"244","2","Land Utilisation Enhancement and Urban Redevelopment","Priority will be given to enhance land utilisation through better zoning and the redevelopment of underutilised land parcels with specific themes and clustering economic activities.",""],[1,"244","2","City Development Based on Specific Characteristics","City development based on specific characteristics will be further pursued to attract quality investment.",""],[1,"244","2","Cyberjaya Revitalisation as a Global Technology Hub","The revitalisation of Cyberjaya as a global technology hub and the development of Bandar Malaysia as an international business hub will promote the Malaysia brand and provide skilled job opportunities for local talent.",""],[1,"244","2","Bandar Malaysia International Business Hub Development","The revitalisation of Cyberjaya as a global technology hub and the development of Bandar Malaysia as an international business hub will promote the Malaysia brand and provide skilled job opportunities for local talent.",""],[1,"244","2","Suburban and Border Town Development Initiative","The development of suburban areas, including border towns will be emphasised to attract more investment and businesses, generating spillover effects to wider surrounding areas.",""],[2,"243","5","Urban Economic Development Promotion","Focus will be given to promote the development of the urban economy by leveraging the potential of cities to attract investment and talent.",""],[2,"243","5","Urban Agglomeration and Ecosystem Enhancement","Efforts will include enhancing urban agglomeration and ecosystem, encouraging the growth of economic activities in urban areas and leveraging city competitiveness.",""],[2,"243","6","Urban Economic Density and Ecosystem Improvement Initiatives","Besides, initiatives to improve the ecosystem in urban areas will focus on providing better infrastructure, accessibility and connectivity as well as enhancing talent development.",""],[2,"243","6","Urban Conurbation and Catalyst Centre Development","Identified growth areas, such as urban conurbations6, promoted development zones and catalyst centres, particularly in less developed regions will be leveraged to create economic agglomeration in achieving higher productivity and economic density.",""],[2,"244","1","Urban Digital Ecosystem and eCommerce Support","Efforts will be intensified to improve business activities in urban areas through a better digital ecosystem.",""],[2,"244","1","Review of Planning Guidelines for Commercial Areas","Meanwhile, the Planning Guidelines for Commercial Areas will be reviewed to optimise the utilisation of commercial floor space in urban areas as well as promote mixed-use development and digital ecosystems.",""],[2,"244","2","Land Utilisation Enhancement through Zoning and Redevelopment","Priority will be given to enhance land utilisation through better zoning and the redevelopment of underutilised land parcels with specific themes and clustering economic activities.",""],[2,"244","2","Place-Based City Development Strategy","City development based on specific characteristics will be further pursued to attract quality investment.",""],[2,"244","2","Cyberjaya Revitalisation and Bandar Malaysia Development","The revitalisation of Cyberjaya as a global technology hub and the development of Bandar Malaysia as an international business hub will promote the Malaysia brand and provide skilled job opportunities for local talent.",""],[2,"244","2","Suburban and Border Town Development Initiative","The development of suburban areas, including border towns will be emphasised to attract more investment and businesses, generating spillover effects to wider surrounding areas.",""]],"200":[[1,"299","2","Green and Resilient City Development Framework","Cities and townships development, including industrial estates, will adopt the green and resilient city concepts, such as the low- carbon city, sponge city9, smart city and equitable transit-oriented development10 (eTOD).",""],[1,"299","2","Green and Resilient City Tools Adoption","As such, green and resilient city tools, including the building information modelling, Malaysian Smart City Framework and Planning Guideline for Disaster Resilient City in Malaysia will be adopted in cities and townships development.",""],[1,"299","2","Low-Carbon Cities Master Plan","A master plan for low-carbon cities will be introduced to guide and coordinate low-carbon initiatives at the local levels.",""],[1,"299","2","Land Use Compliance for Development Projects","In addition, public and private development projects will be required to adhere to the land use policies in designated development areas as prescribed in the National Physical Plan, State Structure Plan, Local Plan or Special Area Plan.",""],[1,"299","2","Sustainable and Resilient Infrastructure and Buildings Initiative","Meanwhile, the development of sustainable and resilient infrastructure and buildings as well as promotion of environment-friendly construction materials will be among the focus areas in the construction sector.",""],[1,"299","3","Expansion of Green Certification Tools for Buildings and Infrastructure","The adoption of green certification tools during the construction and operation phases, such as the Sustainable INFRASTAR, Malaysian Carbon Reduction and Environmental Sustainability Tool (MyCREST) and Malaysia Green Highway Index, will be expanded to more government buildings and infrastructure projects.",""],[1,"299","3","Private Sector Green Certification Adoption Initiative","The private sector will be urged to adopt recognised green certification and performance tools for new development projects as well as renovation and retrofitting works.",""],[1,"299","3","Urban and Communal Farming and Green Space Enhancement","Developers of residential and commercial projects will be encouraged to facilitate urban and communal farming as well as increase, revive and maintain green and blue spaces to regulate microclimate and increase resilience in urban areas as well as promote recreational activities.",""],[1,"299","3","Community Stewardship of Green and Blue Spaces","Sense of ownership and responsibility among the community will be enhanced to jointly create, manage and maintain green and blue spaces as well as public properties.",""],[1,"299","3","Malaysian Urban Observatory System","Malaysian Urban Observatory system will also be introduced to enable integrated town development and improve efficiency in city operations and management.",""],[1,"299","3","Monitoring of Green and Resilient Cities and Townships","The performance of green and resilient cities and townships will be monitored to enable continuous improvement in attaining sustainable development.",""],[1,"299","8","Transit Oriented Development Equity Strategies","Transit Oriented Development (TOD) efforts that are undertaken with an explicit commitment to achieve equity goals through dedicated strategies in ensuring low-income residents benefit from the new development.",""],[2,"299","2","Green and Resilient City Development Framework","Cities and townships development, including industrial estates, will adopt the green and resilient city concepts, such as the low- carbon city, sponge city9, smart city and equitable transit-oriented development10 (eTOD).",""],[2,"299","2","Green and Resilient City Tools Adoption","As such, green and resilient city tools, including the building information modelling, Malaysian Smart City Framework and Planning Guideline for Disaster Resilient City in Malaysia will be adopted in cities and townships development.",""],[2,"299","2","Low-Carbon Cities Master Plan","A master plan for low-carbon cities will be introduced to guide and coordinate low-carbon initiatives at the local levels.",""],[2,"299","2","Land Use Compliance for Development Projects","In addition, public and private development projects will be required to adhere to the land use policies in designated development areas as prescribed in the National Physical Plan, State Structure Plan, Local Plan or Special Area Plan.",""],[2,"299","2","Sustainable and Resilient Infrastructure and Green Construction Materials Promotion","Meanwhile, the development of sustainable and resilient infrastructure and buildings as well as promotion of environment-friendly construction materials will be among the focus areas in the construction sector.",""],[2,"299","3","Expansion of Green Certification Tools for Buildings and Infrastructure","The adoption of green certification tools during the construction and operation phases, such as the Sustainable INFRASTAR, Malaysian Carbon Reduction and Environmental Sustainability Tool (MyCREST) and Malaysia Green Highway Index, will be expanded to more government buildings and infrastructure projects.",""],[2,"299","3","Private Sector Green Certification Promotion","The private sector will be urged to adopt recognised green certification and performance tools for new development projects as well as renovation and retrofitting works.",""],[2,"299","3","Urban and Communal Farming and Green Space Enhancement","Developers of residential and commercial projects will be encouraged to facilitate urban and communal farming as well as increase, revive and maintain green and blue spaces to regulate microclimate and increase resilience in urban areas as well as promote recreational activities.",""],[2,"299","3","Community Stewardship of Green and Blue Spaces","Sense of ownership and responsibility among the community will be enhanced to jointly create, manage and maintain green and blue spaces as well as public properties.",""],[2,"299","3","Malaysian Urban Observatory System","Malaysian Urban Observatory system will also be introduced to enable integrated town development and improve efficiency in city operations and management.",""],[2,"299","3","Monitoring of Green and Resilient Cities Performance","The performance of green and resilient cities and townships will be monitored to enable continuous improvement in attaining sustainable development.",""],[2,"299","8","Transit-Oriented Development Equity Strategies","Transit Oriented Development (TOD) efforts that are undertaken with an explicit commitment to achieve equity goals through dedicated strategies in ensuring low-income residents benefit from the new development.",""]],"201":[[2,"177","5","Community Adoption of National Liveability Best Practices","communities will be encouraged to adopt best practices under the National Community Policy, National Cleanliness Policy and Separation at Source to enhance liveability.",""],[2,"178","1","National Community Policy Rollout","The NCP initiatives will be rolled out nationwide to encourage communities to be more active in keeping the surroundings safe and clean.",""],[2,"178","1","Community Skills and Programme Management Capacity Building","The local communities and residential management bodies will be equipped with the necessary skills to undertake and organise community programmes effectively.",""],[2,"178","1","Strata Management Act Amendment","The roles of joint management bodies and management corporations will be strengthened by amending the Strata Management Act 2013.",""],[2,"178","2","Expansion of Best Practices under the National Cleanliness Policy and Separation at Source","A more conducive living environment will be provided through the expansion of best practices as outlined in the NCP, National Cleanliness Policy and Separation at Source.",""],[2,"178","2","Universal Design Adoption in Housing Projects","Private developers will be encouraged to adopt the universal design concept in housing projects to cater for the needs of specific target groups, particularly PWDs and older persons.",""],[2,"178","2","Environment-Friendly Public Facilities and Green Space Development","Local authorities will also be encouraged to build more environment-friendly facilities, including public parks and recreational spaces, particularly in high-density residential areas.",""]],"202":[[2,"237","3","Green City Action Plan Implementation","Implement Green City Action Plan under IMT-GT and BIMP-EAGA Platform",""],[2,"242","1","Green City Action Plan Expansion","Specific measures will be undertaken to create liveable towns and cities in the subregions.",""],[2,"242","4","Sustainable Urban Development and Governance","Priority will be given in promoting effective urban planning and governance, fostering a sustainable urban economy, prioritising green and resilient urban development as well as developing sustainable urban society.",""],[2,"242","9","Urbanisation Blueprint Implementation","Urbanisation blueprint to be implemented by all cities and its stakeholders, in support of the 2030 Agenda, especially in making cities inclusive, safe, resilient and sustainable.",""],[2,"243","1","Urban Development Data System Improvement","Databases at the urban level will be improved to strengthen urban development planning.",""],[2,"243","1","Sustainable and Smart City Promotion Measures","Measures will also be undertaken to promote sustainable and smart city approaches for better wellbeing of urban dwellers.",""],[2,"243","1","Local Government Law Enforcement and Coordination","Laws relating to local governments will also be further enforced through better coordination.",""],[2,"243","2","Second National Urbanisation Policy Implementation","The Second National Urbanisation Policy (NUP2) will continue to drive the planning and development of urban areas to be more cohesive and effective.",""],[2,"243","2","Urban Profiling Improvement for Local Planning","Urban profiling will be improved based on the findings of the Kajian Penentuan Sempadan Bandar to facilitate better planning at the local government level.",""],[2,"243","2","Malaysia Urban Observatory","The Malaysia Urban Observatory (MUO), a multidimensional big data analytics system will be introduced as an integrated policy tool for better planning and decision-making.",""],[2,"243","2","Urban Data Sharing and Open Data Enhancement","The MUO will enhance urban data collection and data openness as well as promote data sharing among multiple stakeholders for spatial planning at all levels of government.",""],[2,"243","2","Fourth National Physical Plan","Meanwhile, the Fourth National Physical Plan (NPP4) to be launched in 2021 will provide a comprehensive spatial planning framework, which will also cover urban planning.",""],[2,"243","3","MURNInets Adoption by Local Authorities","All local authorities will be encouraged to adopt the MURNInets system.",""],[2,"243","3","Smart City Agenda Implementation Framework","The MSCF will be adopted as the framework in implementing the smart city agenda.",""],[2,"243","3","National Smart City Governance Strengthening","Efforts to strengthen smart city governance at the national level will leverage technical experts.",""],[2,"243","3","Smart City Accreditation and Recognition Standards","Assessment indicators will be introduced to set the standard for accreditation, qualification and recognition of smart cities.",""],[2,"243","4","Strengthening National and Local Planning Coordination for Sustainable Development","The role of the National Physical Planning Council and National Council for Local Government will be enhanced to enable effective planning and implementation of sustainable development through better coordination and cooperation among agencies at Federal, state and local levels.",""],[2,"243","4","Local Government Star Rating System Alignment with the 2030 Agenda","The Local Government Star Rating System will be aligned with the 2030 Agenda.",""],[2,"243","4","Local SDG Implementation Promotion","Efforts will also be undertaken to promote the SDGs' implementation at the local level.",""],[2,"243","4","Governance Enforcement and Legislative Reform","Governance mechanisms will be improved by intensifying enforcement and improving the relevant legislations, including the Local Government Act 1976, Town and Country Planning Act 1976 as well as Road, Drainage and Building Act 1974.",""]],"203":[[1,"240","1","Connectivity and Mobility Improvement Initiative","Connectivity and mobility will be improved to boost inter- and intra-regional economic activities.",""],[1,"240","1","Basic Infrastructure and Services Enhancement","Measures will also be undertaken to enhance the provision of basic infrastructure and services, intensify talent and entrepreneurship development as well as promote collaboration for broader production networks.",""],[1,"240","1","Talent and Entrepreneurship Development Programme","Measures will also be undertaken to enhance the provision of basic infrastructure and services, intensify talent and entrepreneurship development as well as promote collaboration for broader production networks.",""],[2,"240","1","Connectivity and Mobility Improvement Initiative","Connectivity and mobility will be improved to boost inter- and intra-regional economic activities.",""],[2,"240","1","Basic Infrastructure and Services Enhancement","Measures will also be undertaken to enhance the provision of basic infrastructure and services, intensify talent and entrepreneurship development as well as promote collaboration for broader production networks.",""],[2,"240","1","Talent and Entrepreneurship Development Programme","Measures will also be undertaken to enhance the provision of basic infrastructure and services, intensify talent and entrepreneurship development as well as promote collaboration for broader production networks.",""],[2,"240","2","Regional Ecosystem Enhancement","The regional ecosystem will be enhanced to ensure existing industries within the region continue to grow and remain competitive.",""],[2,"240","2","Transport Network Strengthening","The transport network will be strengthened for better connectivity and mobility to boost inter- and intra-regional economic activities.",""],[2,"240","2","Integrated Land-Air-Sea Transport Network Improvement","The integrated transport network connecting land, air and sea will be improved to stimulate economic growth, facilitate the movement of people and goods as well as reduce travelling time and transportation costs.",""],[2,"240","2","Catalytic Transport Projects through Private Initiatives","Meanwhile, the implementation of catalytic projects to improve the transport network through private initiatives, such as the West Coast Expressway and the proposed construction of the Labuan- Menumbok bridge will be encouraged to spur the economy, attract more quality investment and create more job opportunities.",""],[2,"240","3","Basic Infrastructure and Utility Services Enhancement","The provision of basic infrastructure and services, including the supply of water and electricity as well as broadband coverage across regions will be further enhanced.",""],[2,"240","3","Multi-Agency Utility Supply Reliability Coordination","Collaboration with various agencies, including state governments will be strengthened to improve the reliability of water and electricity supply to meet industry requirements.",""],[2,"240","3","Fibre Network Expansion for High-Speed Broadband","The expansion of fibre networks will also provide high-speed and reliable broadband services to support the growing demand of industries.",""]],"204":[[2,"416","3","ETS Service Enhancement","ETS services have been enhanced to meet growing inter-city mobility demand.",""],[2,"416","4","ETS Service Extension to Johor Bahru","ETS is expected to extend the services up to Johor Bahru once the Gemas-Johor Bahru Double Track project is completed in 2023.",""],[2,"417","1","MRT 2 Rail Transit Project","of MRT 2 from Sungai Buloh to Putrajaya, which commenced in 2018, is expected to be completed by 2022.",""],[2,"417","3","Klang Valley Double Track Rail Upgrading Project Phase 1","Measures have been undertaken to enhance intercity rail connectivity, among others, by implementing the Klang Valley Double Track Project (KVDT) Phase 1 from Rawang to Salak Selatan.",""],[2,"417","3","Klang Valley Double Track Rail Upgrading Project Phase 2","Meanwhile, KVDT Phase 2 from Salak Selatan to Seremban and Simpang Pelabuhan Klang to Pelabuhan Klang commenced in 2020 and is expected to be completed by 2026.",""]],"205":[[1,"148","10","Border Security and Anti-Illegal Activity Plan","Implementing a holistic plan in managing security threats and curbing illegal activities at the border.",""],[1,"148","11","Single Border Agency Establishment","Strengthening security management at the border including the movement of people and goods, as well as enforcement, through the establishment of a single border agency.",""],[1,"158","5","Joint Border Control and Patrol Operations","Meanwhile, border controls and patrolling were intensified through joint operations among ATM, PDRM and other enforcement agencies to curb the entry of illegal immigrants and other illegal activities, such as drug trafficking, smuggling and trafficking in persons.",""],[1,"168","5","Illegal Immigration Management Plan","These efforts include developing a holistic plan to manage illegal immigrants, improving border patrols and strengthening defence diplomacy.",""],[1,"168","5","Border Patrol Enhancement","These efforts include developing a holistic plan to manage illegal immigrants, improving border patrols and strengthening defence diplomacy.",""],[1,"168","6","Illegal Immigrant Management Plan","A holistic plan will be developed to manage illegal immigrants, which will cover strategies to improve policy enforcement operations, border control, management of immigrants as well as media reporting and publicity.",""],[1,"168","6","Work Permit Overstay Enforcement Improvement","The plan will include improvement of the enforcement system in dealing with immigrants who entered the country legally but continue working after the expiry of their work permit.",""],[1,"168","6","State Government Cooperation on Illegal Immigrant Information Sharing","The plan will also strengthen strategic cooperation with state governments to ensure increased community participation in channelling information particularly on illegal immigrants.",""],[1,"168","6","Community Leader Empowerment and Public Awareness Programme","Community leaders will be empowered and awareness programmes for the public will be enhanced to assist enforcement agencies in stopping the flow of illegal immigrants.",""],[1,"168","7","Integrated Border Control and Surveillance Enhancement","Border control will be improved through joint operations and border patrolling on land and maritime domains involving ATM and enforcement agencies to prevent any unauthorised entry.",""],[1,"171","5","Single Border Agency and Holistic Border Management Action Plan","In this regard, security management and enforcement, including the movement of people and goods, will be strengthened through the establishment of a single border agency.",""],[1,"171","6","National Digital Identification Policy","A national digital identification policy will be introduced to enable a trusted, secured and transparent movement of data.",""],[2,"168","5","Holistic Illegal Immigrant Management Plan","These efforts include developing a holistic plan to manage illegal immigrants, improving border patrols and strengthening defence diplomacy.",""],[2,"168","5","Border Patrol Improvement Initiative","These efforts include developing a holistic plan to manage illegal immigrants, improving border patrols and strengthening defence diplomacy.",""],[2,"168","6","Holistic Illegal Immigrant Management Plan","A holistic plan will be developed to manage illegal immigrants, which will cover strategies to improve policy enforcement operations, border control, management of immigrants as well as media reporting and publicity.",""],[2,"168","6","Work Permit Overstay Enforcement System Improvement","The plan will include improvement of the enforcement system in dealing with immigrants who entered the country legally but continue working after the expiry of their work permit.",""],[2,"168","6","State Government Cooperation and Community Reporting Mechanism","The plan will also strengthen strategic cooperation with state governments to ensure increased community participation in channelling information particularly on illegal immigrants.",""],[2,"168","6","Community Leader Empowerment and Public Awareness Programme","Community leaders will be empowered and awareness programmes for the public will be enhanced to assist enforcement agencies in stopping the flow of illegal immigrants.",""],[2,"168","7","Integrated Border Control and Surveillance Strengthening","Border control will be improved through joint operations and border patrolling on land and maritime domains involving ATM and enforcement agencies to prevent any unauthorised entry.",""],[2,"171","5","Single Border Agency Establishment","security management and enforcement, including the movement of people and goods, will be strengthened through the establishment of a single border agency.",""],[2,"171","5","Holistic Border Management Action Plan","A holistic border management and operation action plan will be developed to streamline all border enforcement operating procedures.",""]],"206":[[2,"307","8","Strengthened Disaster Response Coordination","Coordination among disaster management-related agencies will be strengthened to further improve the efficiency of disaster response measures, including health-related disasters.",""],[2,"307","8","Disaster Response Technical Training and Simulation Exercises","This will be supported by increasing the number of technical training and simulation exercises, including with regional and international disaster response teams.",""],[2,"307","8","Community-Based Disaster Risk Management and Civil Defence Emergency Response Programmes","Community-based Disaster Risk Management and Civil Defence Emergency Response Team for Community programmes, led by disaster management-related agencies as well as local stakeholders, will continue to be implemented to empower local communities to undertake early disaster response.",""],[2,"307","8","Community Disaster Preparedness Drills and Knowledge Sharing","The capability of communities living in disaster-prone areas will be strengthened through sharing of knowledge and practical approaches as well as by organising more regular drills.",""],[2,"308","1","Build Back Better Disaster Recovery Support","The build back better approach will also be adopted to facilitate affected communities to recover from the aftermath of disasters.",""],[2,"308","1","Alternative Livelihood Income Support","Alternative sources of income will be identified to allow affected communities to sustain their livelihood.",""],[2,"308","1","Counselling Services for Disaster-Affected Communities","In addition, counselling services for the affected communities will be enhanced to help them cope with the trauma.",""]],"207":[[1,"110","2","Industry4WRD-Aligned Industrial Policy and Regulation Reform","Relevant policies and regulations will also be introduced and reviewed in line with the Industry4WRD framework to support growth in the manufacturing sector.",""],[1,"110","2","New Industrial Master Plan Formulation","The new Industrial Master Plan which is being formulated will chart the direction of industry, including reinvigorating private investment.",""],[1,"110","2","Domestic and Foreign Direct Investment Promotion","Efforts will be undertaken to encourage more domestic direct investment as well as quality FDI.",""],[1,"110","2","Emerging Technologies and Intellectual Property Policy Framework","Additionally, policies and regulations will be instituted to cater to the development of emerging technologies and strengthen intellectual property management and protection.",""],[1,"110","2","Catalytic Subsector Roadmap Development","Relevant policies will be reviewed and roadmaps will be developed for the catalytic subsectors, namely E&E, chemical and chemical products, M&E, aerospace, shipbuilding, pharmaceutical and medical devices.",""],[1,"110","2","Automotive Value Chain Blueprint Development","In addition, specific blueprints for the automotive value chain identified under the NAP 2020 will be formulated to promote the adoption of specific technologies and expand market segments.",""],[1,"111","1","Productivity Boost and Market Access Expansion Strategy","Moving forward, the Twelfth Plan will give priority to boost productivity, expand market access, enhance financial intermediation, promote balanced industrial development as well as improve policy and governance.",""],[1,"114","2","Strategic and High-Impact Industries Development Initiatives","During the Twelfth Plan, initiatives will be undertaken to enhance the contribution of strategic and high impact industries in regenerating economic growth.",""],[1,"121","4","Strategic Industry Transformation and Upgrading","In the Twelfth Plan, efforts will be focused on transforming these industries and activities to be more sophisticated and driven by advanced technology.",""],[1,"121","5","Strategic and High-Impact Industries Acceleration","the development of strategic and high impact industries will be accelerated",""],[1,"125","1","Strategic and High-Impact Industry Acceleration","The development of strategic and high impact industries will be accelerated to propel the growth of the economy, particularly in adapting to the changing global supply chain landscape post-pandemic.",""],[2,"110","2","Industry4WRD Policy and Regulatory Support Framework","Relevant policies and regulations will also be introduced and reviewed in line with the Industry4WRD framework to support growth in the manufacturing sector.",""],[2,"110","2","New Industrial Master Plan Formulation","The new Industrial Master Plan which is being formulated will chart the direction of industry, including reinvigorating private investment.",""],[2,"110","2","Domestic Direct Investment and Quality FDI Promotion","Efforts will be undertaken to encourage more domestic direct investment as well as quality FDI.",""],[2,"110","2","Emerging Technologies and Intellectual Property Policy Reform","Additionally, policies and regulations will be instituted to cater to the development of emerging technologies and strengthen intellectual property management and protection.",""],[2,"110","2","Catalytic Subsector Roadmap Development","Relevant policies will be reviewed and roadmaps will be developed for the catalytic subsectors, namely E&E, chemical and chemical products, M&E, aerospace, shipbuilding, pharmaceutical and medical devices.",""],[2,"110","2","Automotive Value Chain Blueprint Formulation","In addition, specific blueprints for the automotive value chain identified under the NAP 2020 will be formulated to promote the adoption of specific technologies and expand market segments.",""],[2,"114","2","Strategic and High-Impact Industries Development Initiatives","During the Twelfth Plan, initiatives will be undertaken to enhance the contribution of strategic and high impact industries in regenerating economic growth.",""],[2,"121","4","Strategic Industry Transformation and Advanced Technology Adoption","In the Twelfth Plan, efforts will be focused on transforming these industries and activities to be more sophisticated and driven by advanced technology.",""],[2,"121","5","Strategic and High-Impact Industries Acceleration","The Twelfth Plan will focus on propelling a number of potential growth drivers leveraging advanced technology and digitalisation in line with the National Fourth Industrial Revolution (4IR) Policy and the Malaysia Digital Economy Blueprint.",""],[2,"125","1","Strategic and High-Impact Industry Acceleration","The development of strategic and high impact industries will be accelerated to propel the growth of the economy, particularly in adapting to the changing global supply chain landscape post-pandemic.",""],[2,"141","1","Strategic and High-Impact Industry Development","Moving forward, efforts will be undertaken to accelerate the development of strategic and high impact industries and enhance the capacity and capability of entrepreneurs as well as enterprises.",""]],"208":[[1,"168","5","Defence Diplomacy Strengthening","These efforts include developing a holistic plan to manage illegal immigrants, improving border patrols and strengthening defence diplomacy.",""],[1,"169","2","Defence Diplomacy and Strategic Security Cooperation","Defence diplomacy will be intensified through bilateral and multilateral collaboration to reduce and avoid conflicts.",""],[1,"169","2","Defence Cooperation MoUs and Joint Exercises Programme","Cooperation with countries and strategic partners will be strengthened through MoUs and memorandum of agreements (MoAs), including in promoting joint exercises and training.",""],[1,"169","2","National Defence and Security Industry Policy","A national defence and security industry policy will be formulated to provide overall direction to reduce dependency on foreign assets and equipment.",""],[2,"168","5","Defence Diplomacy Strengthening Initiative","These efforts include developing a holistic plan to manage illegal immigrants, improving border patrols and strengthening defence diplomacy.",""],[2,"169","2","Defence Diplomacy and Strategic Partnership Cooperation","Defence diplomacy will be intensified through bilateral and multilateral collaboration to reduce and avoid conflicts.",""],[2,"169","2","MoU and MoA-Based Defence Cooperation Framework","Cooperation with countries and strategic partners will be strengthened through MoUs and memorandum of agreements (MoAs), including in promoting joint exercises and training.",""],[2,"169","2","National Defence and Security Industry Policy","A national defence and security industry policy will be formulated to provide overall direction to reduce dependency on foreign assets and equipment.",""]],"209":[[1,"74","5","Financial Intermediation Ecosystem Promotion","an effective financial intermediation ecosystem will be promoted, with a focus on promoting innovation, competitiveness, as well as the Islamic Finance agenda.",""],[1,"82","2","Financial Intermediation Ecosystem Strengthening","the focus will be on boosting productivity mainly through ... strengthening the effectiveness of financial intermediation ecosystem",""],[1,"87","1","Domestic Investment Strategic Fund Matching Grants","technology, upskill workers as well as expand into new markets were also undertaken through the Domestic Investment Strategic Fund (DISF).",""],[1,"90","7","Financial Intermediation Ecosystem Strengthening","This will be achieved by boosting productivity growth, expanding exports markets, strengthening the effectiveness of financial intermediation ecosystem, enhancing the role of industrial estates and food production areas as well as improving governance and policy.",""],[1,"94","1","Financial Capability Strengthening Measures","strengthening financial capability",""],[1,"98","4","Performance-Based Investment Incentives","Incentives and financial assistance in all economic sectors will be enhanced to promote quality investment based on a performance- based approach.",""],[1,"98","4","Performance-Based Subsidy and Incentive Disbursement Reform","The subsidy and incentive disbursement mechanisms will be rationalised from input-based to performance- and output-based.",""],[1,"98","5","Replanting Financing Mechanism Improvement Scheme","established to improve the replanting financing mechanism.",""],[1,"98","6","Performance-Based Incentives for Manufacturing Productivity","performance-based incentives will be emphasised with clear KPI, validity period and exit policy to increase productivity",""],[1,"98","6","Automation Capital Allowance Enhancement","The Automation Capital Allowance will be improved in terms of quantum and mechanism to allow manufacturers to further diversify into high value-added and complex products",""],[1,"98","6","Updated Tax Incentive Promoted List","the promoted list for tax incentives in the Promotion of Investment Act 1986 will be updated to encourage industries to diversify the product base and increase productivity",""],[1,"98","6","Matching Grant Uptake Expansion","measures will be undertaken to increase the uptake of matching grants through collaboration with financial institutions",""],[2,"98","4","Performance-Based Investment Incentives","Incentives and financial assistance in all economic sectors will be enhanced to promote quality investment based on a performance- based approach.",""],[2,"98","4","Subsidy and Incentive Disbursement Rationalisation","The subsidy and incentive disbursement mechanisms will be rationalised from input-based to performance- and output-based.",""],[2,"98","6","Performance-Based Incentives for Manufacturing Productivity","performance-based incentives will be emphasised with clear KPI, validity period and exit policy to increase productivity",""],[2,"98","6","Automation Capital Allowance Enhancement","The Automation Capital Allowance will be improved in terms of quantum and mechanism to allow manufacturers to further diversify into high value-added and complex products",""],[2,"98","6","Updated Tax Incentive Promotion List","the promoted list for tax incentives in the Promotion of Investment Act 1986 will be updated to encourage industries to diversify the product base and increase productivity",""],[2,"98","6","Matching Grant Uptake Expansion","measures will be undertaken to increase the uptake of matching grants through collaboration with financial institutions",""],[2,"98","7","Modern Services Investment Incentive Enhancement","Initiatives to spur growth in the services sector will continue to focus on attracting quality investment, particularly in the modern services subsector by improving existing incentives.",""],[2,"98","9","High-Potential Industries Financing and Incentive Mechanism","A new financing mechanism and incentive structure will be introduced to accelerate the development of high potential industries across the economic sectors, particularly in adopting 4IR technologies.",""]],"210":[[2,"70","1","Logistics Services Efficiency Improvement","efforts will be intensified to increase the efficiency of logistics services by streamlining administrative procedures, increasing regulatory compliance and stricter enforcement",""],[2,"95","7","Logistics Industry Digitalisation and Integrated Supply Chain Platform","The industry will be encouraged to digitalise its operations and connect to an integrated platform in establishing a smart and highly efficient supply chain.",""],[2,"95","7","Warehousing and Distribution Centre Investment Expansion","logistics services providers will be encouraged to increase investment in warehousing and distribution centres to enhance efficiency.",""],[2,"100","8","Digital Supplier-to-Consumer Market Linkage Initiative","Initiatives to improve market efficiency will encompass connecting suppliers directly to consumers through digital platforms and enhancing supply chain sustainability.",""],[2,"100","8","Supply Chain Sustainability Enhancement Initiative","Initiatives to improve market efficiency will encompass connecting suppliers directly to consumers through digital platforms and enhancing supply chain sustainability.",""],[2,"100","8","Malaysia Regional Logistics Hub Development","Efforts will also be undertaken to position Malaysia as a regional logistics hub, capitalising its advantage of good connectivity in the Asia-Pacific region.",""],[2,"101","2","Manufacturing Supply Chain Enhancement Initiative","The manufacturing sector supply chain will continue to be enhanced to produce basic inputs for manufacturing products.",""],[2,"101","2","Manufacturing Supply Chain Gap Mapping and Identification","initiatives will be undertaken in mapping and identifying gaps in the existing supply chain to ensure its sustainability.",""],[2,"101","2","Manufacturing Investment and M&A Promotion","New investment as well as mergers and acquisitions (M&A) will be promoted in addressing the gaps.",""],[2,"101","2","Foreign Company Cooperation for Technology Transfer","Malaysian companies will be encouraged to increase cooperation with foreign companies to facilitate the transfer of technology and knowledge, and develop a skilled domestic workforce.",""],[2,"101","3","Ease of Doing Business and Regulatory Procedure Reform","ease of doing business, including regulatory procedures will be improved to facilitate domestic players as well as attract global players to base their operations in the country",""],[2,"101","3","Supply Chain Management and Regional Distribution Centres","An efficient supply chain management and regional distribution centres will be established to provide comprehensive services to consumers",""],[2,"101","3","Logistics Best Practices and Technology Adoption Programme","Logistics services providers will be encouraged to adopt best practices and emerging technology as well as introduce new ways of doing business",""],[2,"101","4","Logistics Industry Alliance and 4PL Development","form alliances, including through M&A to become fourth-party logistics (4PL) providers to manage and control all activities within the supply chain network and serve as a single point of contact for customers.",""],[2,"101","4","Malaysia Regional Logistics Hub Strategy","Establishing Malaysia as a regional hub will increase the competitiveness of industry players and expand the market share in the region.",""]],"211":[[1,"130","1","Bio-Jet Fuel Prototype Development Programme","a programme to produce Malaysia's first bio-jet fuel prototype using local research and technology will be initiated.",""]],"212":[[1,"139","7","Alternative Financing Mechanisms for Entrepreneurs","A more diversified financing landscape for entrepreneurs will be promoted with greater involvement of the private sector through various alternative financing mechanisms.",""],[1,"139","7","Public-Private Co-Funding Initiative for Innovative Entrepreneurs","Co-funding initiatives between the public and private sectors will be intensified, particularly for high-potential and innovative entrepreneurs and enterprises",""],[1,"140","1","Development Financial Institutions Revitalisation for Inclusive Financing","The role of the Development Financial Institutions (DFIs) will be revitalised to ensure access to financing for different target groups at various stages of growth.",""],[1,"140","2","Startup Financing Access Improvement","Access to financing for new entrepreneurs, especially start-ups, will also be improved to encourage the development and adoption of emerging technology in businesses.",""],[1,"140","2","Entrepreneur Funding Process Simplification","Financing procedures and processes will be simplified to expedite the approval and disbursement of funding to entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"140","2","Failed Entrepreneur Support and Debt Restructuring","In addition, intervention programmes will be introduced to assist failed entrepreneurs and mitigate the risk of bankruptcy.",""]],"213":[[1,"170","2","Holistic Trafficking in Persons Prevention, Prosecution, and Victim Protection Approach","A more holistic approach in curbing trafficking in persons will be adopted in ensuring fair and just treatment.",""],[1,"170","2","Comprehensive Human Trafficking Victim Identification Indicators","Comprehensive indicators will be developed to help with identifying victims and reporting on human trafficking activities.",""],[1,"170","2","CSO and International Organisation Collaboration for Victim Care","Furthermore, strategic collaboration with CSOs and international organisations will be strengthened to provide better care and protection for the victims.",""],[2,"170","2","Holistic Anti-Trafficking Approach","A more holistic approach in curbing trafficking in persons will be adopted in ensuring fair and just treatment.",""],[2,"170","2","Human Trafficking Victim Identification Indicators","Comprehensive indicators will be developed to help with identifying victims and reporting on human trafficking activities.",""],[2,"170","2","Trafficking Victim Care and Protection Collaboration","Furthermore, strategic collaboration with CSOs and international organisations will be strengthened to provide better care and protection for the victims.",""]],"214":[[1,"250","1","Sabah and Sarawak Socioeconomic Development Measures","During the Eleventh Plan, measures were undertaken to accelerate development in Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[1,"250","2","Sabah and Sarawak Regional Inclusion Development Measures","In the Twelfth Plan, socioeconomic development in Sabah and Sarawak will be intensified to promote regional inclusion.",""],[1,"259","6","Sabah and Sarawak Socioeconomic Development Measures","The Twelfth Plan will focus on enhancing socioeconomic development in Sabah and Sarawak to be at par with other states in Peninsular Malaysia.",""],[2,"250","1","Sabah and Sarawak Socioeconomic Development Measures","During the Eleventh Plan, measures were undertaken to accelerate development in Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[2,"250","2","Sabah and Sarawak Socioeconomic Development Intensification","In the Twelfth Plan, socioeconomic development in Sabah and Sarawak will be intensified to promote regional inclusion.",""],[2,"250","2","Infrastructure and Social Services Improvement in Sabah and Sarawak","To do this, the provision of infrastructure will be solidified, economic potential optimised, access to social services improved, inclusive development enhanced and cooperation between the Federal agencies and state governments strengthened.",""],[2,"259","6","Sabah and Sarawak Socioeconomic Development Measures","The Twelfth Plan will focus on enhancing socioeconomic development in Sabah and Sarawak to be at par with other states in Peninsular Malaysia.",""],[2,"263","1","Infrastructure and Connectivity Strengthening in Sabah and Sarawak","The provision of infrastructure and connectivity will be solidified to facilitate economic activities and enable better delivery of social services, particularly in the rural areas.",""],[2,"277","1","Sabah and Sarawak Socioeconomic Development Enhancement","In the Twelfth Plan, greater emphasis will be given in enhancing socioeconomic development in Sabah and Sarawak by providing better infrastructure, optimising economic potential, improving access to social services, enhancing inclusive development and strengthening cooperation between the Federal agencies and state governments.",""]],"215":[[1,"254","6","Civic Outreach Service Expansion","Program Perhimpunan Sivik, an outreach programme introduced in 2016 to enhance access to government services in the rural and remote areas of Sarawak was expanded.",""],[2,"254","6","Civic Assembly Outreach Programme Expansion","Program Perhimpunan Sivik, an outreach programme introduced in 2016 to enhance access to government services in the rural and remote areas of Sarawak was expanded.",""],[2,"272","1","Social Services Access and Safe Environment Improvement","efforts will concentrate on improving access to education, healthcare services and housing as well as enhancing security and public safety.",""]],"216":[[1,"276","9","Strengthening of Native Courts in Sabah and Sarawak","The Mahkamah Anak Negeri Sabah and Mahkamah Bumiputera Sarawak will be further strengthened in the effort to uplift the institution of native courts and uphold native customary rights, culture and practices of the Anak Negeri Sabah and Bumiputera Sarawak.",""],[1,"276","9","Construction and Upgrade of Native Court Buildings","In the Twelfth Plan, the building of Mahkamah Anak Negeri in Tambunan will be continued and completed in 2021, while five new native courts buildings will be constructed in Sabah.",""],[1,"276","9","Upgrade of Mahkamah Bumiputera Sarawak","Meanwhile, 10 Mahkamah Bumiputera Sarawak will be upgraded to provide better services to communities in Sarawak.",""],[1,"276","9","Operationalisation of Native Courts in Sabah and Sarawak","In total, 15 Mahkamah Anak Negeri and Mahkamah Bumiputera in both states are scheduled to be operationalised during the Twelfth Plan.",""],[2,"276","9","Strengthening Native Courts and Customary Rights Infrastructure","The Mahkamah Anak Negeri Sabah and Mahkamah Bumiputera Sarawak will be further strengthened in the effort to uplift the institution of native courts and uphold native customary rights, culture and practices of the Anak Negeri Sabah and Bumiputera Sarawak.",""]],"217":[[1,"310","6","Resource Mobilisation Plan for Sustainable Financing","A resource mobilisation plan will be developed to identify innovative and sustainable financing mechanisms beyond public funding.",""],[1,"310","6","Expansion of Payment for Ecosystem Services Scheme","economic instruments, including the payment for ecosystem services24 (PES) scheme will be expanded.",""],[1,"310","6","Co-management Partnerships for Protected Areas","partnerships between agencies and relevant stakeholders will be expanded to co-manage protected areas.",""],[1,"310","6","Review of Protected Area Entry Fees and Charges","Fees and charges for entry into national and state parks and other protected areas will be reviewed to incorporate the fair value of natural resources and eventually help increase revenues.",""],[1,"311","1","Environmental Financing Mechanism Setup","the EFT implementation mechanism will be set up",""],[1,"311","1","Strengthening of Existing Conservation Trust Funds","The management of existing trust funds, including the National Conservation Trust Fund will also be strengthened",""],[1,"311","1","REDD Plus Mechanism Implementation","the REDD Plus mechanism ... will be implemented",""],[2,"297","5","Sustainable Finance Mobilization for Green Business Practices","In addition, the financial services sector will play a key role in channelling capital to accelerate the adoption of sustainable business practices.",""],[2,"310","6","Resource Mobilisation Plan for Sustainable Environmental Financing","A resource mobilisation plan will be developed to identify innovative and sustainable financing mechanisms beyond public funding.",""],[2,"310","6","Expansion of Payment for Ecosystem Services Scheme","economic instruments, including the payment for ecosystem services24 (PES) scheme will be expanded.",""],[2,"310","6","Co-management Partnerships for Protected Areas","partnerships between agencies and relevant stakeholders will be expanded to co-manage protected areas.",""],[2,"310","6","Review of Protected Area Entry Fees and Charges","Fees and charges for entry into national and state parks and other protected areas will be reviewed to incorporate the fair value of natural resources and eventually help increase revenues.",""],[2,"311","1","Environmental Fiscal Transfer Implementation Mechanism","the EFT implementation mechanism will be set up",""],[2,"311","1","National Conservation Trust Fund Strengthening","The management of existing trust funds, including the National Conservation Trust Fund will also be strengthened",""],[2,"311","1","REDD Plus Mechanism Implementation","the REDD Plus mechanism (Reducing Emissions from Deforestation and Forest Degradation and the Role of Conservation, Sustainable Management of Forest and Enhancement of Carbon Stocks in Developing Countries)25 will be implemented",""],[2,"311","7","Green Financing and Investment Scale-Up","The Twelfth Plan will focus on strengthening environmental governance, scaling- up green financing and investments as well as instilling a sense of ownership and shared responsibility.",""],[2,"313","1","Green Financing Scale-Up for Clean, Green and Resilient Development","Green financing and investments will be scaled-up to support the implementation of the clean, green and resilient development agenda.",""],[2,"313","2","Green Financing for Sustainable Development Projects","The utilisation of green financing and investments will be encouraged for all sustainable and climate- friendly development projects, including projects implemented through the public-private partnerships approach and by the GLCs.",""],[2,"313","3","Sustainable and Responsible Investment Roadmap","The Sustainable and Responsible Investment Roadmap for the Malaysian Capital Market will scale-up capital formation by businesses that adopt sustainable practices and provide green investment opportunities for investors.",""],[2,"313","3","Green and Sustainability Sukuk and Bonds Expansion","The Roadmap will also broaden the use of green and sustainability sukuk and bonds across various economic sectors as well as encourage the use of alternative finance to the underserved segments in the green sectors.",""],[2,"313","3","SDG-Aligned Social and Green Project Financing","Proceeds from this sukuk will be used for eligible social and green projects aligned to the SDGs.",""],[2,"313","4","Sustainable Finance Integration and Scorecard Development","Financial institutions will be encouraged to incorporate sustainability elements into their business portfolios and processes as well as develop scorecards to support sustainable development projects.",""],[2,"313","7","Transparency and Accountability Financing Mechanisms","Therefore, appropriate mechanisms to enhance transparency, accountability and investment worthiness will be strengthened to leverage bilateral and multilateral financing in addressing the domestic financing gaps.",""],[2,"313","7","Centralised Financing Coordination Mechanism","A centralised mechanism will also be established to coordinate and mobilise bilateral and multilateral financing, leverage private sector investments, enhance coordination across sectors, and improve the effectiveness of fund usage.",""],[2,"313","8","Expansion of Environmental Economic Instruments","The application of environmental economic instruments based on the user-pay and polluter-pay principles will be augmented to promote the circular economy, minimise environmental pollution and prevent ecosystems damage.",""],[2,"313","8","Study on Economic Instruments for Environmental Protection","a comprehensive study on the options of economic instruments, including PES and carbon pricing, as well as related costs and benefits will be carried out.",""],[2,"313","8","Revision of Environment-Related Fees and Charges","Existing environment-related fees and charges will also be revised to reflect fair value and the proceeds will be utilised to support environmental protection and conservation efforts.",""],[2,"313","8","Replacement of Environmentally Harmful Subsidies","Meanwhile, environmentally harmful subsidies will be replaced with subsidies that promote environmental sustainability.",""],[2,"314","1","Alternative Disaster Relief Financing Mobilization","Meanwhile, additional financial resources will be sourced from alternative disaster relief funds contributed by the private sector, CSOs and individuals.",""],[2,"314","1","Climate-Resilient Financing and Investment Scale-Up","In addition, climate resilient and environment-friendly financing and investment will be scaled-up to support disaster risk reduction efforts.",""]],"218":[[2,"217","1","Bumiputera Corporate Equity Ownership Strengthening","Bumiputera effective control of corporate organisations will be strengthened to ensure sustainable corporate equity ownership.",""],[2,"217","1","Investment Strategy Review and Investment Literacy Promotion","This will be achieved by revisiting investment strategies and promoting investment literacy.",""],[2,"217","1","SOE Development Enabler Enhancement","Furthermore, the role of SOEs as development enablers in increasing Bumiputera equity ownership will be further enhanced.",""],[2,"217","2","Revision of Bumiputera Institutional Investment Model","The investment model in the Bumiputera mandated institutions will be revisited to ensure optimal returns from strategic investments and divestments to the Bumiputera companies.",""],[2,"217","2","Bumiputera Equity Reallocation and Distribution Mechanism","In ensuring sustainable Bumiputera corporate sector equity ownership, shares of companies divested by Bumiputera mandated agencies will be offered to eligible Bumiputera consortiums and companies.",""],[2,"217","2","Monitoring of Bumiputera Company Disposal","Disposal of Bumiputera-owned companies will be monitored by the sector regulators to maintain the Bumiputera corporate equity ownership.",""],[2,"217","2","Equity Safety-Net Exploration","The possibility of establishing an equity safety-net will be explored to ensure disposal of Bumiputera equity will be made to other qualified Bumiputera individuals and entities.",""],[2,"217","2","Equity Ownership Policy Oversight by EPU, JPM Committee","the Committee on Equity Ownership established under the EPU, JPM will be tasked to oversee the implementation of policies and strategies to further strengthen Bumiputera corporate sector equity ownership.","EPU, JPM"],[2,"217","3","Investment Literacy and IPO Outreach Programme","Bumiputera institutions, such as PNB, MARA and EKUINAS will collaborate with the Securities Commission and Bursa Malaysia in promoting investment literacy.",""],[2,"217","4","Strategic Reallocation of GLC and GLIC Investments","Investment of GLCs and GLICs will be prioritised in the strategic sectors while participation in non-strategic sectors will be gradually reduced.",""],[2,"217","4","Coordinated Disposal of Non-Strategic GLC and GLIC Assets","The disposal of assets owned by the GLCs and GLICs in the non-strategic sectors will be coordinated in ensuring priority will be given to qualified Bumiputera entrepreneurs and entities.",""],[2,"217","4","Bumiputera Corporate Ownership Enhancement Requirement","GLCs and GLICs will be required to enhance the Bumiputera agenda to ensure the sustainability of Bumiputera corporate sector ownership.",""],[2,"217","4","Expanded Bumiputera Company Listing Programmes","Programmes to facilitate more Bumiputera companies to be listed will be expanded through improvements to the existing programmes.",""],[2,"217","4","Strategic Collaboration for Bumiputera MSME and PLC Financing","Strategic collaboration with foreign investors and fund managers will be facilitated to raise funds for Bumiputera MSMEs and PLCs to become global players.",""],[2,"217","5","Digital Financial Planning and Investment Participation Expansion","PNB will facilitate to increase the participation of Bumiputera community in digital-based financial planning and investment services.",""],[2,"217","5","New Unit Trust Product Development","PNB will introduce new unit trust products that have investment exposure in the foreign market.",""],[2,"217","5","Domestic and International Portfolio Diversification","PNB will continue to invest in high performing PLCs in Bursa Malaysia as well as diversify its investment portfolio at the domestic and international market.",""],[2,"217","5","Bumiputera Empowerment Equity Collaboration","Khazanah Nasional Berhad (KHAZANAH), as the national sovereign wealth fund, will also continue to lead collaboration with selected GLCs and GLICs to support and strengthen the Bumiputera Empowerment Agenda in increasing the Bumiputera corporate equity ownership.",""],[2,"217","5","VentureTECH Performance-Based Investment Programme","Bumiputera companies in high value-added, green and emerging industries will be developed through the VentureTECH performance-based investment programme.",""]],"219":[[2,"245","4","Rural Infrastructure and Basic Amenities Upgrading","Rural areas will be further developed to narrow the development gap between rural and urban areas by upgrading infrastructure and basic amenities, providing better connectivity and expanding socioeconomic activities.",""],[2,"245","7","Rural Infrastructure and Basic Services Expansion","These measures include increasing the provision of rural infrastructure, improving basic services and enhancing connectivity and mobility.",""],[2,"245","8","Rural Roads, Bridges and Street Lighting Expansion","The provision of rural infrastructure will be further expanded through constructing and upgrading of roads, bridges and digital infrastructure.",""],[2,"245","9","Rural Water Supply Expansion","The coverage of water supply will be expanded to reach 98% of rural households, including providing alternative water supply and reticulation system.",""],[2,"245","9","Rural Electricity Access Expansion","Electricity supply will be expanded to reach 99% coverage through grid connection and alternative systems, such as small hydro, solar hybrid and solar photovoltaic.",""],[2,"246","1","Rural Basic Services Improvement","The coverage and accessibility to basic services will be continuously improved.",""],[2,"246","1","Rural Waste Management and Sanitation Upgrade","Waste management and sanitation services in rural areas will be enhanced to ensure a sustainable environment.",""],[2,"246","1","Komuniti Sihat Pembina Negara Programme Expansion","The Komuniti Sihat Pembina Negara programme will be expanded to increase health awareness among rural communities.",""],[2,"246","1","Rural Elderly Care Support Services","Rural development planning will also address the needs of older persons, including the provision of healthcare and home caregiver services.",""],[2,"246","1","Program Bantuan Rumah Continuation","The Program Bantuan Rumah will be continued to provide quality and affordable housing in rural areas.",""],[2,"254","2","Basic Infrastructure Improvement Initiatives in Sabah and Sarawak","Access to basic infrastructure in Sabah and Sarawak continues to be improved with the implementation of various initiatives, including the Rural Electricity Supply, Rural Water Supply, as well as Environmental Sanitation and Water Supply programmes.",""],[2,"263","4","Basic Infrastructure Provision and Expansion","The provision of basic infrastructure, including roads, water and electricity supply will continue to be given emphasis.",""],[2,"263","4","Water and Electricity Expansion in Sabah and Sarawak","In addition, coverage of water and electricity supply in Sabah and Sarawak will be further expanded to meet growing demands.",""],[2,"263","5","Basic Infrastructure Upgrading in Sabah and Sarawak","The provision of basic infrastructure will be intensified in Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[2,"263","6","Water Services Infrastructure Construction and Upgrade Programme","new water services infrastructure such as dams, off-river storage, water treatment plants and sewage treatment plants will be constructed, and existing ones upgraded.",""],[2,"263","6","Non-Revenue Water Reduction Programme","allocations will be provided for Non-Revenue Water Reduction Programme in the two states.",""],[2,"269","9","Rural Infrastructure Upgrading and Expansion Programme","The provision of basic infrastructure will be intensified in the rural and remote areas of Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[2,"269","10","Alternative Rural Water Supply Provision","Alternative rural water supply, such as tube wells, gravity feed and rainwater harvesting will be utilised.",""],[2,"269","10","Remote Area Alternative Electricity Supply","Alternative water and electricity supply will be provided in the remote areas.",""],[2,"269","10","Solar Hybrid and Mini-Hydro Microgrid Support","Meanwhile, solar hybrid and mini hydro will be installed to support micro- and pico- grids.",""],[2,"274","7","Basic Infrastructure and Services Expansion for Poor Households","the provision of basic infrastructure and services including roads, treated water, electricity and broadband connectivity will be enhanced.",""],[2,"274","7","Housing Assistance Programme for Poor Households","The housing assistance programme will be continued in building new and repairing dilapidated houses to improve the living conditions of poor households in rural and urban areas.",""]],"220":[[1,"6","1","National Plan Implementation Commitment","The success in implementation and achievement of the Twelfth Plan's objectives and goals is highly dependent on the commitment of each and everyone of us, especially our youth, based on the spirit of Keluarga Malaysia.",""],[1,"7","5","Adaptive Plan Implementation with Regular Reviews","we need to successfully execute this Plan with regular reviews and enhanced flexibility to respond.",""],[1,"35","9","Twelfth Plan Reform and Transformation Agenda","The Twelfth Plan needs to be transformational to overcome global economic uncertainties, domestic structural economic challenges and shortcomings in the development approach.",""],[1,"35","9","Rakyat-First Policy","among the elements to be incorporated into the Twelfth Plan are rakyat- first policy, whole-of-nation approach and political buy-in.",""],[1,"35","9","Whole-of-Nation Implementation Approach","among the elements to be incorporated into the Twelfth Plan are rakyat- first policy, whole-of-nation approach and political buy-in.",""],[1,"35","9","Political Buy-In for Plan Implementation","among the elements to be incorporated into the Twelfth Plan are rakyat- first policy, whole-of-nation approach and political buy-in.",""]],"221":[[1,"32","4","National Defence and Security Strengthening","In ensuring national defence and security, crime prevention efforts as well as rehabilitation and emergency preparedness will be intensified, while the welfare of the Malaysian Armed Forces and enforcement personnel will be improved.",""],[1,"32","4","Security Governance Strengthening","Priority will also be given in strengthening security governance.",""],[1,"32","4","National Unity and Social Cohesion Strengthening","Unity in diversity will be strengthened to maintain a harmonious society and prosperous nation.",""],[1,"32","5","National Security and Unity Strengthening Initiative","Efforts in nation-building and creating a more conducive environment for economic activities as well as a safe and harmonious living for the rakyat will be emphasised by addressing issues on national defence and security as well as the unity.",""],[1,"36","1","Border Illegal Activity Suppression Plan","A holistic plan will be implemented in curbing illegal activities at the border",""],[1,"36","1","National Defence and Security Industry Policy","a new National Defence and Security Industry Policy will be introduced in ensuring a sustainable defence and security capability",""],[1,"36","1","Whole-of-Nation Crime Combatting Approach","wider usage of advanced technology as well as greater involvement by the community will facilitate the whole-of-nation approach in combatting crimes",""],[1,"36","1","Unity Programmes for Social Cohesion","building social interaction among the rakyat will be fostered through unity programmes, sports and religious activities",""],[1,"36","1","Digital Media Patriotism and Volunteerism Campaign","Patriotism and volunteerism will also be strengthened through the utilisation of digital and other media platforms in building social cohesion and fostering greater unity to ensure peace and harmony",""],[1,"144","2","Security Governance Strengthening","Security governance will be strengthened to ensure the nation remains peaceful and public safety is maintained.",""],[1,"154","3","National Security and Sovereignty Strengthening","In the Twelfth Plan, priority will be given to improve national security and safeguard sovereignty in ensuring the nation remains peaceful and prosperous.",""],[1,"164","6","National Security and Sovereignty Strengthening","In the Twelfth Plan, efforts will be intensified in enhancing defence and national security as well as the wellbeing and unity of the rakyat.",""],[1,"168","1","National Security and Sovereignty Protection","National security and sovereignty will continue to be given priority in ensuring a conducive environment for economic activities and safe living as well as maintaining a dignified and resilient nation.",""],[1,"168","1","Security Governance Strengthening","priority will be given in strengthening the security governance.",""],[1,"170","7","Security Governance Strengthening","The governance of security will be strengthened to improve service delivery in upholding public safety and security.",""],[1,"170","7","National Security Council Strengthening","The role and function of the National Security Council (NSC) will be strengthened, several laws on public safety and security will be reviewed and anti- corruption measures will be further enhanced.",""],[1,"170","7","Stakeholder Coordination and Data Integration for Security","Coordination and collaboration among stakeholders as well as data sharing and system integration will be intensified.",""],[1,"171","1","Strengthening NSC Policy Coordination for National Security","The role and function of the NSC as a lead agency in coordinating policies related to national security will be strengthened.",""],[1,"171","1","Enhanced National Security and Public Safety Coordination","The coordination will focus on security issues including cyber security, cross-border crimes, disease outbreak, natural disasters as well as economic and social crises.",""],[1,"171","1","National Operations Management Centre Enhancement","In addition, the National Operations Management Centre will be enhanced through better coordination among relevant stakeholders and connection with all systems related to security, defence and disaster management.",""],[1,"171","2","Public Safety and Security Legal Reform","A number of laws will be amended to ensure relevancy and effectiveness in improving public safety and security.",""],[1,"171","3","Mandatory Job Rotation Policy","Job rotation will also be made mandatory.",""],[1,"171","4","Security and Public Order Consultative Council","A security and public order consultative council will be established to streamline efforts in addressing security threats.",""],[1,"453","2","Border Security Enhancement Action Plan","Focus is given on the implementation of a holistic action plan to enhance security at the border",""],[1,"453","2","Defence and Security Industry Policy","introduction of a new policy for the defence and security industry",""],[1,"453","2","Advanced Technology for Crime Prevention","wider usage of advanced technology in combatting crimes",""]],"222":[[1,"128","2","Upgrade of the National Aerospace Industry Coordinating Office","the National Aerospace Industry Coordinating Office (NAICO) will be upgraded as an agency to create a conducive ecosystem for the development of the industry","Ministry of International Trade and Industry"],[1,"128","3","Upgrading of NAICO for Aerospace Industry Framework Coordination","The upgrading of the NAICO will also strengthen its role to coordinate the implementation of the newly introduced Aerospace Industry Framework, as shown in Exhibit 3-2.",""],[1,"128","3","Aerospace Regulatory Certification One-Stop Centre","A one-stop centre will also be established to coordinate the certification process of various regulatory bodies related to aerospace.",""],[1,"128","7","Aerospace Digital Data Repository System","A dedicated aerospace digital system will be established as a central data repository for aircraft operations, MRO and aerospace manufacturing in Malaysia through a public-private collaborative effort.",""],[1,"129","14","Aerospace Digital Framework","Introduce Aerospace Digital Framework",""],[1,"129","17","Aerospace Certification, Calibration and Testing One-Stop Centre","Establish a one-stop centre at SIRIM for aerospace certification, calibration and testing",""],[1,"129","27","G2B Strategic Engagement Programmes with OEMs","Undertake G2B strategic engagement programmes with OEMs",""],[2,"128","2","Upgrade of the National Aerospace Industry Coordinating Office","the National Aerospace Industry Coordinating Office (NAICO) will be upgraded as an agency to create a conducive ecosystem for the development of the industry.","Ministry of International Trade and Industry"],[2,"128","3","Upgrading of NAICO for Aerospace Industry Framework Coordination","The upgrading of the NAICO will also strengthen its role to coordinate the implementation of the newly introduced Aerospace Industry Framework, as shown in Exhibit 3-2.",""],[2,"128","3","Aerospace One-Stop Certification Centre","A one-stop centre will also be established to coordinate the certification process of various regulatory bodies related to aerospace.",""],[2,"128","7","Aerospace Digital Data Repository System","A dedicated aerospace digital system will be established as a central data repository for aircraft operations, MRO and aerospace manufacturing in Malaysia through a public-private collaborative effort.",""],[2,"129","14","Aerospace Digital Framework","Introduce Aerospace Digital Framework",""],[2,"129","17","SIRIM Aerospace One-Stop Certification Centre","Establish a one-stop centre at SIRIM for aerospace certification, calibration and testing",""]],"223":[[1,"131","4","Art Practitioner Compensation Review","In ensuring the sustainability of the local heritage and culture, compensation and appreciation to art practitioners will be reviewed.",""],[1,"131","4","Agile Tourism Business Model Reform","In this regard, a more agile and effective business model will be introduced to enable the private sector to complement government efforts.",""],[1,"132","6","National Tourism Policy Implementation Acceleration","The implementation of its strategies and initiatives will be accelerated to attain higher industry growth and sustainability.",""],[1,"132","6","National Tourism Steering Committee Strengthening","The national steering committee on tourism development will be strengthened to involve agencies at federal and state levels in providing strategic oversight and coordination.",""],[1,"132","6","Malaysian Tourism Federation Establishment","In addition, a Malaysian tourism federation will be established as a platform for synergistic collaboration between the private and public sectors.",""],[1,"132","6","MOTAC Functions Streamlining and Service Delivery Improvement","Meanwhile, the functions of departments and agencies within the purview of MOTAC will be streamlined and augmented to improve service delivery.","MOTAC"],[1,"132","6","Tourism Agency Redundancy Reduction","Redundancies and overlapping functions will be reduced to improve cost-effectiveness and service delivery.",""],[1,"132","6","Destination Marketing Business Model Restructuring","Keeping abreast with changing trends in travel behaviour, the business model for destination marketing will be restructured.",""],[1,"132","6","Rationalisation of Overseas Tourism Marketing Offices","Malaysian representative offices abroad for marketing and promotion purposes are no longer required and will be rationalised.",""],[2,"132","5","Tourism Data Digitalisation for Planning and Decision-Making","Malaysia will also adopt digitalisation in capturing tourist data and trends in improving planning, resource deployment and decision-making.",""],[2,"132","6","Acceleration of National Tourism Policy Implementation","The implementation of its strategies and initiatives will be accelerated to attain higher industry growth and sustainability.",""],[2,"132","6","Strengthening of the National Tourism Development Steering Committee","the national steering committee on tourism development will be strengthened to involve agencies at federal and state levels in providing strategic oversight and coordination.",""],[2,"132","6","Establishment of Malaysian Tourism Federation","a Malaysian tourism federation will be established as a platform for synergistic collaboration between the private and public sectors.",""],[2,"132","6","Streamlining of MOTAC Functions","the functions of departments and agencies within the purview of MOTAC will be streamlined and augmented to improve service delivery.","MOTAC"],[2,"132","6","Rationalisation of Malaysian Representative Offices Abroad","Malaysian representative offices abroad for marketing and promotion purposes are no longer required and will be rationalised.",""]],"224":[[1,"31","4","Twelfth Plan Game Changers Initiative","game changers that represent the new and innovative ideas will be introduced to shift mindsets and fundamentally change the approach of national development.",""],[1,"31","18","Multi-Stakeholder Collaboration Enhancement","Enhancing collaboration among government agencies, private sector, academia, CSOs and the rakyat.",""],[1,"32","1","Game-Changing and Radical Initiatives for the Twelfth Plan","The Government is committed to delivering game-changing and radical initiatives to ensure that the objectives of prosperity, inclusivity and sustainability are achieved during the Twelfth Plan.",""],[1,"32","1","Economic Reset and Inclusive Sustainability Agenda","Emphasis will be on resetting the economy, strengthening security, wellbeing and inclusivity as well as advancing sustainability.",""],[2,"8","2","Twelfth Plan Transformative Policy Framework","The Twelfth Plan introduces a new transformative approach based on three themes, four catalytic policy enablers and 14 game changers.",""],[2,"23","4","SDG Localisation and CEPA Intensification","localising SDGs initiatives will be intensified, and communication, education and public awareness (CEPA) will be emphasised to enhance understanding and implementation of the SDGs at the local level.",""],[2,"31","4","National Development Game Changers","game changers that represent the new and innovative ideas will be introduced to shift mindsets and fundamentally change the approach of national development.",""],[2,"31","18","Multi-Stakeholder Collaboration Enhancement","Enhancing collaboration among government agencies, private sector, academia, CSOs and the rakyat.",""],[2,"32","1","Game-Changing and Radical Initiatives for the Twelfth Plan","The Government is committed to delivering game-changing and radical initiatives to ensure that the objectives of prosperity, inclusivity and sustainability are achieved during the Twelfth Plan.",""],[2,"35","9","Rakyat-First Policy and Whole-of-Nation Implementation Approach","among the elements to be incorporated into the Twelfth Plan are rakyat- first policy, whole-of-nation approach and political buy-in.",""],[2,"35","9","Political Buy-In for Plan Implementation","among the elements to be incorporated into the Twelfth Plan are rakyat- first policy, whole-of-nation approach and political buy-in.",""]],"225":[[1,"133","2","Halal Talent Development and Occupational Framework Expansion","In this regard, the halal occupational framework will be expanded to include talent requirements in high potential industries such as the pharmaceutical, cosmetics and medical devices industry, through engagement with the industry.",""],[1,"133","2","Halal Course Accreditation and Curriculum Streamlining","The academic programmes and training modules for halal courses will be streamlined and accredited in accordance with the National Occupational Skills Standards (NOSS) and Malaysian Qualifications Framework (MQF).",""],[1,"133","2","Expansion of Halal-Related Higher Education and Skills Training Programmes","Institutions of higher education and skills training institutions will be encouraged to offer more halal-related programmes to produce graduates with holistic halal knowledge and skills.",""],[1,"133","2","Public-Private Halal Research Collaboration","Collaboration between public research institutions and the private sector will be strengthened to create a pool of halal researchers, scientists and engineers, thus increasing the ability to produce high value halal products and services.",""],[1,"133","3","Halal Professional Board Restructuring and Recognition Framework","The Halal Professional Board (HPB) under the Department of Islamic Development Malaysia (JAKIM) will be restructured based on new regulations, which will be formulated, to broaden the accreditation of halal professionals for global markets.","Department of Islamic Development Malaysia (JAKIM)"],[1,"133","3","Halal Professional Standards and Competency Assessment Mechanism","Mechanisms related to halal professional practices standards, codes of conduct and competency assessment will be identified to develop the halal professional recognition framework.",""],[2,"133","2","Halal Talent Development and Occupational Framework Expansion","the halal occupational framework will be expanded to include talent requirements in high potential industries such as the pharmaceutical, cosmetics and medical devices industry, through engagement with the industry.",""],[2,"133","2","Halal Course Standardisation and Accreditation","The academic programmes and training modules for halal courses will be streamlined and accredited in accordance with the National Occupational Skills Standards (NOSS) and Malaysian Qualifications Framework (MQF).",""],[2,"133","2","Expansion of Halal-Related Higher Education and Training Programmes","Institutions of higher education and skills training institutions will be encouraged to offer more halal-related programmes to produce graduates with holistic halal knowledge and skills.",""],[2,"133","2","Public-Private Halal Research Collaboration","Collaboration between public research institutions and the private sector will be strengthened to create a pool of halal researchers, scientists and engineers, thus increasing the ability to produce high value halal products and services.",""],[2,"133","3","Halal Professional Board Restructuring and Recognition Framework","The Halal Professional Board (HPB) under the Department of Islamic Development Malaysia (JAKIM) will be restructured based on new regulations, which will be formulated, to broaden the accreditation of halal professionals for global markets.","Department of Islamic Development Malaysia (JAKIM)"]],"226":[[1,"177","4","Housing Law Revision for Homebuyer Protection","The Akta Pemajuan Perumahan (Kawalan dan Pelesenan) 1966 will be revised to improve existing housing laws and regulations to protect homebuyers.",""],[1,"177","4","Enforcement Against Irresponsible Housing Developers","Stronger action will be taken against irresponsible developers and individuals associated with the companies for abandoning housing projects and treating homebuyers unfairly.",""],[1,"177","4","Commercial Development Protection Act","An act on commercial development will be introduced to protect the interest of small property owners in commercial development projects.",""],[1,"177","4","Residential Tenancy Regulation Act","an act on residential tenancy will be introduced to regulate the rights of proprietors and tenants.",""],[2,"176","2","Affordable Housing Purchase Restriction Regulation","A regulation will be introduced to limit the purchase of only one affordable house per eligible citizen.",""],[2,"176","2","Affordable Housing Secondary Market Price Ceiling","Ceiling prices of affordable housing will also be introduced in the secondary market to control house prices, especially in the urban areas.",""],[2,"176","2","PPR Errant Tenant Exit Enforcement","the exit policy on errant tenants of PPR will be strictly enforced to ensure this programme only benefits deserving households.",""],[2,"177","3","Quality Affordable Housing Standards Enforcement","The Piawaian Perumahan Berkualiti (PPB) will be enforced to ensure the quality of affordable houses.",""],[2,"177","3","Mandatory QLASSIC Housing Quality Assessment","The Quality Assessment System for Building Construction Works (QLASSIC) will be made mandatory under PPB and become a pre-requisite for development approval.",""],[2,"177","4","Housing Development Law Revision","The Akta Pemajuan Perumahan (Kawalan dan Pelesenan) 1966 will be revised to improve existing housing laws and regulations to protect homebuyers.",""],[2,"177","4","Enforcement Against Irresponsible Housing Developers","Stronger action will be taken against irresponsible developers and individuals associated with the companies for abandoning housing projects and treating homebuyers unfairly.",""],[2,"177","4","Commercial Development Protection Act","An act on commercial development will be introduced to protect the interest of small property owners in commercial development projects.",""],[2,"177","4","Residential Tenancy Regulation Act","an act on residential tenancy will be introduced to regulate the rights of proprietors and tenants.",""]],"227":[[1,"178","8","National Public Sports Facilities Management Plan","A national plan will be introduced to provide a comprehensive guideline for the construction, management and maintenance of public sports facilities.",""],[1,"178","8","Centralised Public Sports Facilities Management System","A centralised system will be developed to manage these facilities and ensure optimal utilisation.",""],[1,"178","8","Integrated Online Booking System for Public Sports Facilities","An integrated online booking system, including mobile applications, will be developed to allow greater access to public sports facilities.",""],[1,"178","9","Community-Based Sports Facilities Development","Continuous engagement with local authorities and community leaders will be undertaken to ensure the development of new sports facilities and recreational areas are based on the needs of local communities.",""],[1,"178","9","Public Sports Facility Upgrade and Maintenance Programme","Existing public sports facilities will also be upgraded and properly maintained to optimise usage, while local authorities will be urged to undertake regular maintenance of sports and recreational facilities under their purview.",""],[1,"178","9","Private Sector Sports Facility Provision Initiative","In addition, the private sector and sports bodies will be encouraged to provide more sports facilities for public use.",""],[2,"178","8","National Public Sports Facilities Management Plan","A national plan will be introduced to provide a comprehensive guideline for the construction, management and maintenance of public sports facilities.",""],[2,"178","8","Centralised Public Sports Facilities Management System","A centralised system will be developed to manage these facilities and ensure optimal utilisation.",""],[2,"178","8","Integrated Online Booking System for Public Sports Facilities","An integrated online booking system, including mobile applications, will be developed to allow greater access to public sports facilities.",""],[2,"178","9","Community-Based Sports Facilities Development","Continuous engagement with local authorities and community leaders will be undertaken to ensure the development of new sports facilities and recreational areas are based on the needs of local communities.",""],[2,"178","9","Public Sports Facility Upgrading and Maintenance","Existing public sports facilities will also be upgraded and properly maintained to optimise usage, while local authorities will be urged to undertake regular maintenance of sports and recreational facilities under their purview.",""],[2,"178","9","Private Sector Sports Facility Provision Incentives","the private sector and sports bodies will be encouraged to provide more sports facilities for public use.",""],[2,"179","2","Inclusive Sports Facilities and Participation Programmes","Specific facilities to cater for the needs of target groups such as PWDs, older persons and women will be provided in the development of new sports facilities and recreational areas.",""]],"228":[[2,"208","3","Cost of Living Relief and Purchasing Power Enhancement Initiative","Initiatives to reduce inequality include addressing the rising cost of living and increasing purchasing power as well as strengthening social protection.",""],[2,"208","3","Social Protection Strengthening Initiative","Initiatives to reduce inequality include addressing the rising cost of living and increasing purchasing power as well as strengthening social protection.",""],[2,"208","4","Enhanced Price Control Enforcement","enforcement of price control on goods and services will be enhanced to address price manipulation.",""],[2,"208","4","Food Bank Initiative","The Food Bank initiative and corporate social responsibility (CSR) programmes will help reduce the financial burden of poor households.",""],[2,"208","4","Corporate Social Responsibility Support Programmes","The Food Bank initiative and corporate social responsibility (CSR) programmes will help reduce the financial burden of poor households.",""],[2,"208","4","Financial Education and Literacy Promotion","financial education and literacy will be promoted among all age groups.",""],[2,"210","2","Poverty Reduction and B40 Empowerment Measures","Strategies and initiatives for addressing poverty and empowerment of the B40 will be implemented irrespective of ethnicity.",""]],"229":[[1,"259","4","Special Cabinet Committee on Malaysia Agreement 1963 Review","In September 2018, the Federal Government established the Special Cabinet Committee on Malaysia Agreement 1963 to review the implementation of the Malaysia Agreement 1963 (MA63).",""],[1,"259","4","Transfer of Gas and Electricity Regulatory Powers to Sabah","The Federal Government has agreed in principle on the handing over of regulatory power for gas and electricity supply to the State Government of Sabah.",""],[2,"259","4","Special Cabinet Committee on Malaysia Agreement 1963 Review","In September 2018, the Federal Government established the Special Cabinet Committee on Malaysia Agreement 1963 to review the implementation of the Malaysia Agreement 1963 (MA63).",""],[2,"259","4","Transfer of Gas and Electricity Regulatory Powers to Sabah","The Federal Government has agreed in principle on the handing over of regulatory power for gas and electricity supply to the State Government of Sabah.",""],[2,"275","8","Review of Sabah and Sarawak Rights","the rights of Sabah and Sarawak will be reviewed",""],[2,"275","9","Special Council on Malaysia Agreement 1963","The establishment of the Special Council on Malaysia Agreement 1963 in September 2020 replacing the Special Cabinet Committee further demonstrated the commitment of the Federal Government to ensure that the rights of Sabah and Sarawak under MA63 continue to be protected.",""],[2,"275","9","Coordination of Remaining MA63 Issues","Moving forward, efforts in coordinating and streamlining the remaining issues raised by Sabah and Sarawak will be continued.",""],[2,"275","9","MA63 Coordination Unit in the Prime Minister's Department","The Bahagian Hal Ehwal Sabah dan Sarawak, which was established under the Prime Minister's Department is tasked with coordinating all the issues relating to the implementation of MA63.","Prime Minister's Department"]],"230":[[1,"370","12","Responsive Workforce Training Programme","Systems to support labour market will be strengthened by enhancing labour market information infrastructure and promoting responsive workforce training.",""],[1,"371","9","HRD Corp Levy Reimbursement Revision","The Human Resource Development Corporation levy reimbursement mechanism will be revised to support more training for low- and semi-skilled workers who are susceptible to be displaced with the emergence of 4IR technologies.",""],[1,"371","9","Expanded Micro and Modular Training Programmes","Micro and modularised programmes that target all skill levels, particularly those in the lower skill category, will be expanded.",""],[1,"371","10","National Skills Framework Development and Updating","An extensive review of the current standard classification of occupations to incorporate information on skills requirement will be undertaken to establish a comprehensive and dynamic national skills framework22.",""],[1,"371","10","Government-Industry-Training Provider Cooperation Network","an extensive network of cooperation between the government, industries and training providers will be established.",""],[1,"371","10","Expansion of Training Places for Niche Skills","Additionally, the number of places to train workers who specialise in niche areas and skills will be increased in meeting the new demands from industry.",""],[1,"371","13","National Skills Framework Development","National skills framework will mirror the efforts of the European Commission's European Skills, Competences, Qualifications and Occupation (ESCO) and the US Department of Labor, Employment & Training Administration in developing O*Net.",""],[1,"372","3","Industrial Automation Transition Support","Efforts to move industry to higher value-added activities through automation will be continued.",""],[1,"372","3","Automation-Linked Employee Training Incentives","The related incentives will be reviewed to incorporate components in facilitating necessary training for employees to effectively work with new automation technologies.",""],[1,"372","3","Labour Market Upskilling and Reskilling Support","For employees who are displaced, upskilling and reskilling will be provided through the labour market support system to enable them to remain in the labour market.",""],[2,"342","3","Education and Training Quality Enhancement Initiative","In addition, elevating the quality of education and leveraging emerging technologies will be key initiatives in improving the education and training system.",""],[2,"344","1","Digital Skills and 4IR Talent Development","The supply of talent and skills required to drive both the digital economy and 4IR technology adoption will be increased, while R&D&C&I will be intensified.",""],[2,"354","2","Future-Ready Talent Development Programme","Strategies to produce future-ready talent will include improving the quality of academic and training programmes, ensuring equitable learning outcomes, leveraging on emerging technologies and strengthening the governance.",""],[2,"370","12","Labour Market Information Infrastructure Enhancement","Systems to support labour market will be strengthened by enhancing labour market information infrastructure",""],[2,"370","12","Responsive Workforce Training Programme","promoting responsive workforce training",""],[2,"371","1","Labour Market Data Framework and Analytics Platform","a labour market data framework will be developed to guide planning, development and implementation of labour market policies and initiatives.",""],[2,"371","9","HRD Corp Levy Reimbursement Revision","The Human Resource Development Corporation levy reimbursement mechanism will be revised to support more training for low- and semi-skilled workers who are susceptible to be displaced with the emergence of 4IR technologies.",""],[2,"371","9","Micro and Modularised Training Programme Expansion","Micro and modularised programmes that target all skill levels, particularly those in the lower skill category, will be expanded.",""],[2,"371","10","National Skills Framework Development","An extensive review of the current standard classification of occupations to incorporate information on skills requirement will be undertaken to establish a comprehensive and dynamic national skills framework22.",""],[2,"371","10","Government-Industry-Training Provider Cooperation Network","an extensive network of cooperation between the government, industries and training providers will be established.",""],[2,"371","10","Expansion of Niche Skills Training Places","Additionally, the number of places to train workers who specialise in niche areas and skills will be increased in meeting the new demands from industry.",""],[2,"371","13","National Skills Framework Development","National skills framework will mirror the efforts of the European Commission's European Skills, Competences, Qualifications and Occupation (ESCO) and the US Department of Labor, Employment & Training Administration in developing O*Net.",""],[2,"372","3","Industrial Automation Upgrading and Workforce Transition Support","Efforts to move industry to higher value-added activities through automation will be continued.",""]],"231":[[1,"374","4","School and Vocational College Infrastructure Upgrading","Measures will be undertaken to enhance the infrastructure of schools and vocational colleges in improving the teaching and learning environment.",""],[1,"374","4","Rebuilding Unsafe School Buildings","All schools which are classified under the scale of six and seven in the School Building Condition Index25 and verified as unsafe by the Public Works Department will be rebuilt.",""],[1,"377","10","Disabled-Friendly School Facilities Improvement","The accessibility for students with SEN in schools will be enhanced through improvement of disabled-friendly facilities.",""]],"232":[[1,"374","5","UES Roadmap Strengthening and School Rationalisation","The UES Roadmap Initiative will be strengthened to enhance the management of under enrolled schools and reduce operating expenditure.",""],[2,"374","5","UES Roadmap Strengthening and School Rationalisation","The UES Roadmap Initiative will be strengthened to enhance the management of under enrolled schools and reduce operating expenditure.",""],[2,"374","5","Combined Classes Expansion","The implementation of combined classes will be expanded where Year Two will be merged with Year Three, and Year Four with Year Five.",""],[2,"374","5","UES Rationalisation Criteria-Based Implementation","In addition, continuous efforts will be undertaken to rationalise UES.",""]],"233":[[1,"375","2","University-Industry R&D and Commercialisation Collaboration","HEIs will be encouraged to strengthen collaboration with industry players in research, development, commercialisation and innovation (R&D&C&I) activities.",""],[1,"375","2","Expanded Research Focus on Emerging Technologies","In addition, focus areas in R&D activities will be expanded to meet the industry needs, including emerging technologies such as psychotechnology, robotics and AI.",""],[1,"375","2","Continued Research Grant and Institutional Funding Support","Allocation for RU and HICoE as well as Fundamental Research Grant will continue to be provided to intensify R&D activities as well as develop research-inspired teaching and learning activities.",""],[1,"375","2","Research Management System Development","Furthermore, a research management system will be developed to support research activities in HEIs.",""],[2,"362","8","Industry Centre of Excellence Programme","The ICoE programme provides an avenue for industry players to establish laboratories and teaching facilities within the universities to provide students with exposure to the latest technologies.",""],[2,"375","2","University-Industry R&D&C&I Collaboration Initiative","HEIs will be encouraged to strengthen collaboration with industry players in research, development, commercialisation and innovation (R&D&C&I) activities.",""],[2,"375","2","Expansion of Research Focus Areas for Industry Needs","In addition, focus areas in R&D activities will be expanded to meet the industry needs, including emerging technologies such as psychotechnology, robotics and AI.",""],[2,"375","2","Continued Research Grant and Institutional Support","Allocation for RU and HICoE as well as Fundamental Research Grant will continue to be provided to intensify R&D activities as well as develop research- inspired teaching and learning activities.",""],[2,"375","2","Research Management System Development","Furthermore, a research management system will be developed to support research activities in HEIs.",""],[2,"375","3","Expansion of Centres of Excellence and Centres of Technology","The Centres of Excellence and Centres of Technology will be expanded to spur innovation and knowledge creation as well as enhance technical skills among students.",""]],"234":[[1,"375","5","Education Governance and Coordination Strengthening","Education governance will be strengthened to support the development of future-ready talent.",""],[1,"375","9","Continuous Professional Development for Education Leaders","Continuous professional development will be maintained to improve leadership quality.",""],[1,"375","9","Structured Training Programme for Education Leaders","Education leaders from schools, JPNs, PPDs and divisions will be trained under a structured programme to improve capacity and capability to manage education institutions.",""],[1,"375","9","National Professional Qualification for System Leaders","the National Professional Qualification for System Leaders (NPQSL)26 programme will be introduced.",""],[1,"375","10","NPQSL Training Programme for System Leaders","NPQSL is a training programme for system leaders to ensure officers appointed at district education officers, state officer and division officers are competent.",""],[1,"376","1","Qualification for Educational Leaders (NPQEL) Strengthening and Tailoring Programme","Qualification for Educational Leaders (NPQEL)27 programme will also be strengthened and tailored for different types of schools, particularly Orang Asli, special education, religious schools as well as technical and vocational education.",""],[1,"376","2","Parent-Teacher Association Empowerment for School Governance","The role of Parent-Teacher Associations (PTAs) will be strengthened to play more active role in supporting the school governance.",""],[1,"377","1","PTA Community Monitoring Empowerment","The PTAs will be empowered to assist community monitoring initiatives.",""],[2,"375","5","Education Governance and Coordination Strengthening","Education governance will be strengthened to support the development of future-ready talent.",""],[2,"375","8","Enterprise Data Warehouse and Data Analytics Platform","An enterprise data warehouse as well as a data analytics platform will be established to enable data sharing, support reporting and decision-making across ministries and agencies.",""],[2,"375","8","Private Education Student Data Sharing Initiative","At the same time, private education providers will be encouraged to share data on student enrolment status.",""],[2,"375","8","Comprehensive Student Enrolment Tracking System","This will enable a comprehensive tracking of students' enrolment, including those in private schools.",""]],"235":[[1,"378","3","Bringing School to the Community Programme","A special programme named Bringing School to the Community will be introduced for Orang Asli students to increase their participation in formal learning.",""],[1,"378","4","Expansion of K9 Schools and Transformation into K11 Schools","K9 schools will be expanded and existing K9 schools will gradually be transformed into Comprehensive Special Model School 11 (K11) schools to ensure students complete their 11 years of education.",""],[1,"378","4","Extension of K11 Schools to Orang Asli and Remote Areas","The K11 schools will also be extended to cover not only Orang Asli students but also those residing in remote areas.",""],[1,"378","4","Strengthening TVET Delivery for Orang Asli and Remote Students","Focus will be given to enhance skills development of these students by strengthening the delivery of TVET programmes.",""],[2,"378","3","Bringing School to the Community Programme","A special programme named Bringing School to the Community will be introduced for Orang Asli students to increase their participation in formal learning.",""],[2,"378","4","Expansion of K9 Schools and Transformation to K11 Schools","K9 schools will be expanded and existing K9 schools will gradually be transformed into Comprehensive Special Model School 11 (K11) schools to ensure students complete their 11 years of education.",""],[2,"378","4","Extension of K11 Schools to Remote and Orang Asli Communities","The K11 schools will also be extended to cover not only Orang Asli students but also those residing in remote areas.",""],[2,"378","4","Strengthening TVET Delivery for Orang Asli and Remote Students","Focus will be given to enhance skills development of these students by strengthening the delivery of TVET programmes.",""]],"236":[[1,"382","2","Digital Economy Advancement and Digitalisation Mainstreaming","The focus will be on advancing the digital economy, mainstreaming digitalisation for inclusive development, accelerating R&D&C&I as well as capitalising on the potential of emerging technologies.",""],[1,"389","3","Digital Economy Advancement and Digitalisation Mainstreaming","This will be undertaken by advancing the digital economy, mainstreaming digitalisation for inclusive development, accelerating R&D&C&I and capitalising on the potential of advanced technology.",""],[1,"393","2","Digital Governance Streamlining","Measures will be undertaken to streamline digital governance, accelerate trade through eCommerce, expand the sharing economy and strengthen cyber security.",""],[1,"394","10","Digital Economy Blueprint Implementation","strategies and initiatives will embed Malaysian culture, ethics and values.",""],[1,"395","1","National Digital Economy and 4IR Council Coordination Mechanism","The implementation of digital initiatives will be led by the National Digital Economy and 4IR Council.",""],[1,"395","2","Strategic Change Management Office for Digitalisation","The National Digital Economy and 4IR Council will be supported by the Strategic Change Management Office (SCMO) as a special entity to lead national level change management.",""],[1,"395","2","Digital Economy Change Management Planning and Coordination","The SCMO will develop strategic plans and initiatives, track progress and evaluate performance as well as facilitate coordination of all related committees under the Council.",""],[1,"395","2","National Digital Economy Communication Strategy","This entity will also drive the communication strategy including raising national awareness and branding.",""],[2,"127","7","Malaysia Digital Economy Blueprint Implementation","The implementation of the Malaysia Digital Economy Blueprint is expected to boost Malaysia's digital infrastructure and connectivity.",""],[2,"127","7","5G Network and Cloud Storage Services Development","In this regard, the 5G network and cloud storage services will be a catalyst to create a conducive ecosystem in enhancing Malaysia's attractiveness as an investment destination.",""]],"237":[[1,"393","1","Future-Ready Digital Talent Development","Under the Twelfth Plan, efforts will focus on providing an enabling environment for the growth of the digital economy, strengthening the provision of digital infrastructure and services, developing future-ready digital talent as well as positioning Malaysia as the ASEAN digital centre.",""],[1,"397","5","Digital Talent Development Measures","During the Twelfth Plan, measures will be undertaken to develop digital talent in promoting the digital economy and nurturing future-ready digital talent.",""],[1,"397","6","Digital Skills Ecosystem Enhancement","A conducive ecosystem will be provided to enhance the digital skills of the workforce.",""],[1,"397","6","National Digital Talent Coordination Mechanism","Cross-ministerial collaborations will be strengthened under the National Digital Economy and 4IR Council to ensure the digital talent initiatives are successful.",""],[1,"397","6","Digital Talent Development Strategy Framework","A digital talent development strategy framework will be formulated to address related issues as well as guide and align all digital talent development initiatives.",""],[1,"397","6","Inclusive Funding Facilities for Digital Talent Development","Sustainable and inclusive funding facilities will be provided for this purpose.",""],[1,"398","1","Digital Social Responsibility Promotion Initiative","Digital social responsibility will be promoted to encourage organisations and individuals to contribute towards digital reskilling and upskilling programmes.",""],[1,"398","1","Tax Exemptions and Matching Grants for Digital Training Providers","Incentives such as tax exemptions and matching grants will be introduced to industry players that provide digital education and training programmes.",""],[1,"398","1","Latent Talent Hiring Incentive","In addition, companies will be encouraged to hire latent talent.",""],[1,"398","3","Industrial Training Expansion for Digital Content Talent","Industrial training will be enhanced and expanded to develop more digital content talent.",""],[1,"398","3","Digital Content Upskilling and Reskilling Programme","Upskilling and reskilling programmes will be undertaken, particularly in the areas of animation, games and films that are globally marketable.",""],[1,"398","3","Digital Content Talent Exchange Programme","Talent exchange programmes with established digital content-producing countries will be promoted to strengthen domestic capacity and capability.",""],[1,"408","3","4IR-Related Skills Training Programme","Training for 4IR-related skills will also be provided by various skills training institutions in collaboration with industry players to meet industry demand.",""],[2,"393","1","Future-Ready Digital Talent Development","Under the Twelfth Plan, efforts will focus on providing an enabling environment for the growth of the digital economy, strengthening the provision of digital infrastructure and services, developing future-ready digital talent as well as positioning Malaysia as the ASEAN digital centre.",""],[2,"394","6","Digital Talent Development Initiative","Build agile and competent digital talent",""],[2,"397","5","Digital Talent Development Initiative","During the Twelfth Plan, measures will be undertaken to develop digital talent in promoting the digital economy and nurturing future-ready digital talent.",""],[2,"397","6","Digital Skills Ecosystem Enhancement","A conducive ecosystem will be provided to enhance the digital skills of the workforce.",""],[2,"397","6","Digital Talent Coordination under National Council","Cross-ministerial collaborations will be strengthened under the National Digital Economy and 4IR Council to ensure the digital talent initiatives are successful.",""],[2,"397","6","Digital Talent Development Strategy Framework","A digital talent development strategy framework will be formulated to address related issues as well as guide and align all digital talent development initiatives.",""],[2,"397","6","Sustainable and Inclusive Digital Talent Funding Facilities","Sustainable and inclusive funding facilities will be provided for this purpose.",""],[2,"398","1","Digital Social Responsibility Promotion Initiative","Digital social responsibility will be promoted to encourage organisations and individuals to contribute towards digital reskilling and upskilling programmes.",""],[2,"398","1","Tax Exemptions and Matching Grants for Digital Training Providers","Incentives such as tax exemptions and matching grants will be introduced to industry players that provide digital education and training programmes.",""],[2,"398","1","Latent Talent Hiring Incentive","In addition, companies will be encouraged to hire latent talent.",""],[2,"398","2","Cyber Security Capacity Strengthening Programme","Expertise in cyber security will be strengthened to ensure a trusted, secure and reliable digital ecosystem.",""],[2,"398","2","Local Cyber Security Talent Development Initiative","More local talent will be developed to reduce dependency on foreign cyber security experts.",""],[2,"398","2","Public-Private Cyber Security Collaboration Mechanism","Collaborative efforts between the public and private sectors will be intensified to develop knowledge and skills in cyber security.",""],[2,"398","3","Industrial Training Expansion for Digital Content Talent","Industrial training will be enhanced and expanded to develop more digital content talent.",""],[2,"398","3","Digital Content Upskilling and Reskilling Programme","Upskilling and reskilling programmes will be undertaken, particularly in the areas of animation, games and films that are globally marketable.",""],[2,"398","3","Digital Content Talent Exchange Programme","Talent exchange programmes with established digital content-producing countries will be promoted to strengthen domestic capacity and capability.",""],[2,"398","5","Continuous Professional Development for TVET Instructors","The Continuous Professional Development programmes will be expanded for TVET instructors to obtain professional certificates in digital-related fields.",""],[2,"398","5","Public-Private Partnerships for TVET Industrial Training","Public-private partnerships, including through the teaching factory approach will be encouraged to provide industrial training on the latest technology.",""],[2,"408","3","4IR-Related Skills Training Programme","Training for 4IR-related skills will also be provided by various skills training institutions in collaboration with industry players to meet industry demand.",""]],"238":[[1,"415","7","Electrified Double Track Gemas-Johor Bahru Extension","For GJB, the final stretch of the electrified double-track from Padang Besar, Perlis to Johor Bahru, Johor, which will offer Electric Train Services (ETS), is projected to be ready by 2023.",""],[1,"415","7","East Coast Rail Link Construction","Meanwhile, the ECRL which re-commenced work in 2019, is currently under construction for the alignment from Dungun to Mentakab and is expected to be completed by 2026.",""],[1,"416","3","ETS Service Enhancement","ETS services have been enhanced to meet growing inter-city mobility demand.",""],[1,"416","4","ETS Service Extension to Johor Bahru","ETS is expected to extend the services up to Johor Bahru once the Gemas-Johor Bahru Double Track project is completed in 2023.",""],[1,"417","1","MRT 2 Rail Transit Project","of MRT 2 from Sungai Buloh to Putrajaya, which commenced in 2018, is expected to be completed by 2022.",""],[1,"417","3","Klang Valley Double Track Project Phase 1","Measures have been undertaken to enhance intercity rail connectivity, among others, by implementing the Klang Valley Double Track Project (KVDT) Phase 1 from Rawang to Salak Selatan.",""],[1,"417","3","Klang Valley Double Track Project Phase 2","Meanwhile, KVDT Phase 2 from Salak Selatan to Seremban and Simpang Pelabuhan Klang to Pelabuhan Klang commenced in 2020 and is expected to be completed by 2026.",""],[1,"422","6","Rail and Road Network Integration for Connectivity","Rail and road networks will also be integrated to provide better connectivity between airports, ports, industrial areas and cities.",""],[1,"423","1","Transit-Oriented Development Integration in Rail Planning","TOD will be further emphasised to improve accessibility to public transport and provide good connectivity to other amenities.",""],[1,"454","4","Integrated Rail and Road Connectivity Initiative","This will be achieved through initiatives such as the integration of rail and road networks to provide better connectivity between airports, ports, industrial areas and cities.",""]],"239":[[1,"417","5","Port Real-Time Goods Tracking System","Net, which enables real-time tracking of movement of goods within the port areas.",""],[1,"424","2","Port Maintenance, Repair and Overhaul Service Improvement","Port operators will be urged to provide better services for maintenance, repair and overhaul services (MRO) for ships under the guidance of port authorities.",""],[1,"424","2","Port Infrastructure Capacity Expansion","The port operators will continue to enhance the capacity of ports infrastructure and services to handle larger vessels as well as provide efficient cargo handling facilities.",""],[1,"424","2","Port Congestion Relief Parking Facilities","Proper parking facilities for prime movers will be provided to ease congestion during peak hours in the ports.",""],[1,"424","2","Port Facilities and Process Upgrading Programme","Facilities and equipment of ports will be upgraded while processes will be reviewed to increase overall efficiency and competitiveness.",""],[1,"424","3","Port Last-Mile Connectivity Enhancement","Last-mile connectivity to main ports will be enhanced to address congestion and accommodate future growth in trade.",""],[1,"424","3","Port Rail and Access Road Upgrading","The rail networks within the main ports and access roads to main ports will be upgraded.",""],[1,"424","3","Strategic Cargo Hub Development","Cargo hubs at strategic locations adjacent to the ports will be identified to provide integrated logistics facilities.",""],[1,"424","4","Logistics Connectivity Improvement and Multimodal Cargo Movement","Logistics connectivity between rail, sea and air will be improved to position Malaysia as a vibrant cargo hub.",""],[1,"424","5","Multimodal Cargo Movement Action Plan","To accelerate its implementation, an action plan will be developed to provide clear directives for multimodal cargo movement.",""],[1,"425","7","National Port Committee for Port Development Coordination","A national port committee, which comprises representatives from port authorities and operators, will be established to coordinate the planning of ports development and develop standard operating procedures (SOPs) for port operations.",""],[1,"425","7","Port Regulations Harmonisation and Best Practices Initiative","The committee will also harmonise regulations and share best practices to increase operational efficiency and create a more conducive port environment.",""],[1,"454","4","Port Infrastructure and Services Expansion","In addition, the capacity of port infrastructure and services will be increased",""],[2,"424","1","Transport and Logistics Efficiency Enhancement Initiatives","Initiatives to enhance the efficiency of transport and logistics services focus on raising the capacity of ports infrastructure and services, improving last-mile connectivity, encouraging multimodal cargo movement, upgrading the aviation system and implementing preventive maintenance of roads and bridges.",""],[2,"424","2","Port Service Improvement and Infrastructure Upgrading","Port operators will be urged to provide better services for maintenance, repair and overhaul services (MRO) for ships under the guidance of port authorities.",""],[2,"424","2","Port Capacity Expansion for Larger Vessels","The port operators will continue to enhance the capacity of ports infrastructure and services to handle larger vessels as well as provide efficient cargo handling facilities.",""],[2,"424","2","Port Congestion Relief Parking Facilities","Proper parking facilities for prime movers will be provided to ease congestion during peak hours in the ports.",""],[2,"424","2","Port Facilities and Process Efficiency Upgrade","Facilities and equipment of ports will be upgraded while processes will be reviewed to increase overall efficiency and competitiveness.",""],[2,"424","3","Last-Mile Port Connectivity Enhancement","Last-mile connectivity to main ports will be enhanced to address congestion and accommodate future growth in trade.",""],[2,"424","3","Port Rail and Access Road Upgrading","The rail networks within the main ports and access roads to main ports will be upgraded.",""],[2,"424","3","Strategic Cargo Hub Development","Cargo hubs at strategic locations adjacent to the ports will be identified to provide integrated logistics facilities.",""],[2,"424","3","Port Cargo Consolidation Services","These hubs will reduce the frequency of trucks plying the ports by providing consolidation services for the cargo outside port areas.",""],[2,"424","4","Logistics Connectivity Improvement and Multimodal Cargo Movement","Logistics connectivity between rail, sea and air will be improved to position Malaysia as a vibrant cargo hub.",""],[2,"424","5","Multimodal Cargo Movement Action Plan","To accelerate its implementation, an action plan will be developed to provide clear directives for multimodal cargo movement.",""],[2,"425","6","Centralised Logistics Hub Planning and Development","the planning and development of logistics hub will be centralised at the Federal Government.",""],[2,"425","6","Enhanced Stakeholder Coordination for Project Appraisal and Evaluation","Coordination among the various stakeholders, particularly in project appraisal and evaluation will be enhanced to ensure optimisation of resources in infrastructure development.",""],[2,"425","7","National Port Committee for Port Development Coordination","A national port committee, which comprises representatives from port authorities and operators, will be established to coordinate the planning of ports development and develop standard operating procedures (SOPs) for port operations.",""]],"240":[[1,"421","11","Green Transport Index Formulation","Formulation of Green Transport Index",""],[1,"425","3","Institutional and Regulatory Framework Strengthening for Green Transport","Measures will be implemented to enhance the institutional and regulatory framework.",""],[1,"426","7","Low Carbon Mobility Blueprint Implementation","the Low Carbon Mobility Blueprint action plan will be implemented",""],[1,"426","7","Environmental Standards Mandate for Transport and Logistics","the adoption of environmental standards will be mandated",""],[1,"426","7","Transport and Logistics CEPA Enhancement","communication, education and public awareness (CEPA) will be enhanced",""],[1,"426","8","Low Carbon Mobility Blueprint","The Low Carbon Mobility Blueprint will be implemented to minimise unsustainable movement patterns.",""],[1,"426","9","Mandatory Green Standards for Transport Operators","Mandatory adoption of environmental standards such as the National Green Standards for transport operators will be imposed to expedite the implementation of green practices in the transport and logistics sectors.",""],[1,"426","9","Incentives for Green Transport Standards Adoption","Incentives will be provided to encourage the adoption of these standards.",""],[1,"426","9","Green Transport Index","The Green Transport Index will also be introduced to promote clean and sustainable transport systems as well as resilient infrastructure for efficient mobility.",""],[1,"426","10","CEPA Behavioural Change Programme for Sustainable Transport and Logistics","CEPA programmes will be intensified, targeting transport operators, manufacturers, service providers and users of transport and logistics services.",""],[1,"426","10","Stakeholder Collaboration for CEPA Implementation","collaboration among stakeholders will be strengthened in implementing CEPA to induce green behaviour among users.",""],[2,"426","7","Low Carbon Mobility Blueprint Action Plan","the Low Carbon Mobility Blueprint action plan will be implemented",""],[2,"426","7","Mandatory Environmental Standards for Transport and Logistics","the adoption of environmental standards will be mandated",""],[2,"426","7","Communication, Education and Public Awareness Enhancement","communication, education and public awareness (CEPA) will be enhanced",""],[2,"426","8","Low Carbon Mobility Blueprint Implementation","The Low Carbon Mobility Blueprint will be implemented to minimise unsustainable movement patterns.",""],[2,"426","8","Cleaner Aviation Fuel Standards Development","In the aviation sector, it will include developing cleaner fuel standards, which comply with the Carbon Offsetting and Reduction Scheme for International Aviation (CORSIA) by ICAO.",""],[2,"426","8","Low-Carbon Vehicle Promotion","In the land transport sector, the use of low carbon alternatives such as energy-efficient vehicles, hybrid and electric vehicles will be promoted.",""],[2,"426","9","Mandatory Environmental Standards for Transport Operators","Mandatory adoption of environmental standards such as the National Green Standards for transport operators will be imposed to expedite the implementation of green practices in the transport and logistics sectors.",""],[2,"426","9","Incentives for Green Transport Standards Adoption","Incentives will be provided to encourage the adoption of these standards.",""],[2,"426","9","Green Transport Index","The Green Transport Index will also be introduced to promote clean and sustainable transport systems as well as resilient infrastructure for efficient mobility.",""],[2,"426","10","CEPA Behavioural Change Programme for Sustainable Transport and Logistics","CEPA programmes will be intensified, targeting transport operators, manufacturers, service providers and users of transport and logistics services.",""],[2,"426","10","Stakeholder Collaboration for CEPA Implementation","Therefore, collaboration among stakeholders will be strengthened in implementing CEPA to induce green behaviour among users.",""]],"241":[[1,"419","5","Efficient and Inclusive Transport Infrastructure and Logistics Services","The Twelfth Plan will focus on providing efficient and inclusive transport infrastructure and logistics services.",""],[1,"425","6","Enhanced Inter-Agency Coordination for Transport and Logistics Implementation","Effective policy implementation through better planning and coordination among various agencies is crucial to promote efficiency in the transport and logistics services sectors.",""],[1,"425","8","NLTF Institutional Strengthening and Performance Management","The role of NLTF will be strengthened to ensure effective implementation of policies, strategies and initiatives.",""],[1,"427","1","Transport Infrastructure and Logistics Services Improvement","The Plan gives priority to improving transport infrastructure in providing seamless people mobility.",""],[1,"427","1","Transport and Logistics Governance Enhancement","It also focuses on enhancing competitiveness of the transport and logistics industry as well as its governance.",""],[2,"421","10","Green Transport Index Formulation","Formulation of Green Transport Index",""],[2,"425","3","Institutional and Regulatory Framework Strengthening","Measures will be implemented to enhance the institutional and regulatory framework.",""],[2,"425","3","Governance Strengthening and Green Agenda Promotion","The measures include strengthening governance and promoting the green agenda.",""],[2,"425","3","Green Transport Index Development","The implementation of these measures will improve service delivery and enable the formulation of the Green Transport Index.",""],[2,"425","5","National Warehouse Regulatory Framework","Concerted efforts will be undertaken to improve coordination among stakeholders, enhance enforcement and develop a national regulatory framework for warehouses.",""],[2,"425","5","Shipping Industry Governance Mechanism","A governance mechanism will be introduced for the shipping industry and highway development will be restructured to optimise benefits for both customers and industry players.",""],[2,"425","5","Highway Development Restructuring","A governance mechanism will be introduced for the shipping industry and highway development will be restructured to optimise benefits for both customers and industry players.",""],[2,"425","8","NLTF Strengthening and Performance Management","The role of NLTF will be strengthened to ensure effective implementation of policies, strategies and initiatives.",""],[2,"425","9","Single Border Agency Establishment Study","A study is being undertaken to establish a single border agency to oversee, strengthen and raise the standard of operations and security along national borders and entry points including ports and airports.",""],[2,"425","9","Single Clearance Trade Facilitation Mechanism","The establishment of a single border agency will enhance efficiency in trade facilitation through a single clearance mechanism.",""],[2,"426","3","National Warehouse Regulation and Inventory System","A national warehouse regulation will be developed to ensure uniformity in warehouse development.",""],[2,"426","4","Maritime Economy Governance Mechanism","Efforts will be undertaken to introduce a governance mechanism to facilitate the development of the maritime economy.",""]],"242":[[1,"435","1","Flexible Working Hours for Civil Servants","Measures to improve the work-life balance of civil servants continued to be given emphasis by introducing flexible working hours.",""],[1,"441","1","Flexible Working Arrangements for Public Employees","In retaining and attracting talent, more flexible working arrangements will be introduced to provide options for employees who have constraints in working full time in the office.",""],[1,"441","2","Flexible Working Arrangements Support","In order to support flexible working arrangements, departments and agencies will provide the necessary digital infrastructure.",""],[1,"443","5","Flexible Working Arrangements Policy Enhancement","policies and guidelines for flexible working arrangements will be enhanced.",""],[1,"443","6","Flexible Working Arrangements Policy","A more agile working environment will contribute towards employee retention, boost employee morale and facilitate the achievement of cost-efficient measures.",""],[1,"443","6","Flexible and Trust-Based Work Arrangement Culture","The foundation of an efficient and flexible working arrangement culture is based on trust, effective communication and clear job descriptions.",""],[1,"443","6","Flexible Working Arrangements Implementation","Flexible working arrangements will enable employees to perform better, resulting in increased productivity and quality of work, while work-life balance will be enhanced.",""],[2,"435","1","Flexible Working Hours for Civil Servants","Measures to improve the work-life balance of civil servants continued to be given emphasis by introducing flexible working hours.",""],[2,"441","1","Flexible Working Arrangements for Public Service Talent Retention","more flexible working arrangements will be introduced to provide options for employees who have constraints in working full time in the office.",""],[2,"441","2","Flexible Working Arrangements Support","In order to support flexible working arrangements, departments and agencies will provide the necessary digital infrastructure.",""],[2,"443","5","Flexible Working Arrangements Policy Enhancement","policies and guidelines for flexible working arrangements will be enhanced.",""],[2,"443","6","Flexible Working Arrangements Policy","A more agile working environment will contribute towards employee retention, boost employee morale and facilitate the achievement of cost-efficient measures.",""]],"243":[[2,"382","2","Digitalisation and Advanced Technology Adoption Initiatives","During the Twelfth Plan, initiatives to boost digitalisation and advanced technology adoption will be emphasised.",""],[2,"382","2","Digital Economy Advancement and Digitalisation Mainstreaming","The focus will be on advancing the digital economy, mainstreaming digitalisation for inclusive development, accelerating R&D&C&I as well as capitalising on the potential of emerging technologies.",""],[2,"389","3","Digital Economy and Advanced Technology Advancement","This will be undertaken by advancing the digital economy, mainstreaming digitalisation for inclusive development, accelerating R&D&C&I and capitalising on the potential of advanced technology.",""],[2,"393","1","Digital Economy Enabling Environment","Under the Twelfth Plan, efforts will focus on providing an enabling environment for the growth of the digital economy, strengthening the provision of digital infrastructure and services, developing future-ready digital talent as well as positioning Malaysia as the ASEAN digital centre.",""],[2,"394","1","Cross-Sector Digital Technology Adoption","Further efforts to maximise the potential of the digital economy include the adoption of digital technologies across all economic sectors.",""],[2,"394","10","Digital Economy Blueprint Implementation","In advancing the digital economy, strategies and initiatives will embed Malaysian culture, ethics and values.",""],[2,"399","7","Digitalisation Expansion and Digital Governance Improvement Measures","To mainstream digitalisation, measures will be implemented to expand digitalisation and improve digital governance.",""],[2,"400","1","Digital Inclusion and Online Business Expansion Initiatives","The emphasis will be on facilitating digital opportunities and creating more online business ventures.",""],[2,"409","1","Digitalisation and 4IR Technology Adoption Initiative","During the Twelfth Plan, concerted efforts will be undertaken to boost digitalisation and advance technology adoption to transform Malaysia into a high technology-based economy through, among others, strengthening the basic digital infrastructure with telecommunication services being introduced as a public utility, developing and nurturing future-ready talent to participate in the digital economy as well as increasing the commercialisation of R&D outputs and investments.",""]],"244":[[2,"7","5","Adaptive Plan Execution with Regular Reviews","This measure is in line with the Government's aspiration in ensuring that no one is left behind or neglected in development.",""],[2,"35","9","Implementation of the WKB 2030 and 2030 Agenda","These will ensure the successful implementation of the WKB 2030 and 2030 Agenda.",""]],"245":[[1,"23","4","Whole-of-Nation SDG Implementation Approach","The adoption of the whole-of-nation approach is essential for SDGs implementation.",""],[1,"23","4","Local SDG Localization Initiative","localising SDGs initiatives will be intensified",""],[1,"23","4","SDG Communication, Education and Public Awareness Campaign","communication, education and public awareness (CEPA) will be emphasised to enhance understanding and implementation of the SDGs at the local level.",""],[1,"37","1","SDG and ESG Integration in Decision-Making","The public and private sectors will be encouraged to adopt and integrate the SDGs and ESG principles in their decision-making.",""]],"246":[[1,"32","4","Holistic Sports Ecosystem Promotion","An active lifestyle will be promoted continuously among the rakyat by creating a holistic sports ecosystem.",""]],"247":[[1,"32","6","Integrated Energy and Water Management","Energy and water will be managed holistically and sustainably, taking into account the supply and demand of these resources.",""],[1,"32","6","Energy Trilemma Management","The energy sector will address the energy trilemma",""],[1,"32","6","Universal Water Security Initiative","the water sector will focus on ensuring water security for all.",""]],"248":[[1,"101","1","Agricultural E-Commerce Market Access and Traceability Initiative","farmers will be encouraged to leverage eCommerce platforms to facilitate direct sales and enhance traceability of agricultural products.",""],[1,"101","1","Agricultural Market Infrastructure and Facility Upgrades","related infrastructure and facilities will be improved to enable more farmers to have direct access to market the products.",""],[1,"101","1","Agricultural E-Commerce Partnership and Online Market Expansion","collaboration between eCommerce companies as well as agricultural cooperatives and associations will be established to enable farmers in the rural areas to participate in the online market.",""],[1,"101","1","Agricultural Online Auction Platform","An online auction platform will be developed for a number of agricultural products to facilitate transparent transactions, thus improving the efficiency of the market and eradicating price manipulation by middlemen.",""],[1,"101","1","Agricultural Production Risk Management through Online Trading","Farmers will also be able to better manage production risk through this platform, allowing more contract farming and joint ventures for the supply of agricultural produce.",""],[2,"101","1","Agricultural E-Commerce Market Access and Traceability Initiative","farmers will be encouraged to leverage eCommerce platforms to facilitate direct sales and enhance traceability of agricultural products.",""],[2,"101","1","Online Agricultural Auction Platform Development","An online auction platform will be developed for a number of agricultural products to facilitate transparent transactions, thus improving the efficiency of the market and eradicating price manipulation by middlemen.",""],[2,"101","1","Agricultural Production Risk Management through Digital Market Platform","Farmers will also be able to better manage production risk through this platform, allowing more contract farming and joint ventures for the supply of agricultural produce.",""]],"249":[[1,"86","4","High Value-Added and Complex Product Development Programme","The High Value-Added and Complex Product Development Programme was introduced in 2016 to improve capacities and competencies of industry players in developing high value- added complex products.",""],[1,"86","4","Automotive Vendor Upgrading Programmes","various programmes were implemented to increase the number of vendors that meet the minimum requirements of original equipment manufacturers (OEMs) and participate in the supply chain.",""],[1,"86","4","National Automotive Policy 2020","the National Automotive Policy 2020 (NAP 2020) was launched in February 2020, aiming to propel the country to become a regional leader in automotive manufacturing.",""],[1,"96","5","Automotive Industry High Value-Added Activities Support under NAP 2020","Intensification of high value-added activities in the automotive industry will be supported through the implementation of the NAP 2020.",""]],"250":[[1,"69","8","Industry-Government-Research Collaboration Platform","Collaboration among industry players, government agencies and research institutions will be further enhanced to identify new high value-added products and markets",""],[1,"97","3","Industrial Collaboration Programme Strengthening","The Industrial Collaboration Programme (ICP), a component of the Government Procurement policy will be promoted as a strategic tool to support the effort in moving up the value chain through high technology uptakes and innovation strategies.",""]],"251":[[1,"97","9","Construction Sector Industry-Training Partnerships","Industry players in the construction sector will be encouraged to share resources and partner with training institutions in providing industrial training for workers and students on the latest applied technology.",""],[1,"97","9","University-Industry Linkage Strengthening Initiative","In addition, university-industry linkages will be strengthened by embedding industry input and expertise in the field of study and training to keep abreast with the rapid technological changes.",""],[1,"97","9","Construction Industry Development Board Training and Accreditation Uptake","Industry players will also be encouraged to leverage training and accreditation programmes offered by the Construction Industry Development Board to upskill existing workers, in producing qualified local talent in the sector.",""],[1,"98","1","Industry-Linked Customized Training Programmes","Industries in the manufacturing sector will be encouraged to collaborate with skills training institutions in designing customised training programmes to accommodate their respective needs in moving up the value chain.",""],[1,"98","1","Micro-Credentials Expansion Programme","Efforts to uplift talent will also focus on expanding the provision of micro-credentials programmes to meet the current reskilling and future skills requirements.",""],[1,"98","2","Services Sector Talent Development Strategies","a new SSB will provide the strategies for talent development programmes in the services sector.",""],[1,"98","2","Business and Professional Services Blueprint","A holistic blueprint for business and professional services will also be formulated to guide the relevant stakeholders in upskilling the talent with automation tools and advanced technology in embracing 4IR.",""]],"252":[[1,"98","4","Skim Tanam Semula Implementation","The Skim Tanam Semula (STS)7 will be implemented and an endowment fund will be",""],[1,"98","10","Replanting Scheme (STS)","The Replanting Scheme (STS) is a monthly fixed contribution by smallholders comprising of investment to finance replanting and life insurance elements.",""]],"253":[[1,"100","1","Green Agriculture Practices Adoption Initiative","Efforts to inculcate green practices in the agriculture sector will be intensified by encouraging farmers to adopt good agriculture practices such as myGAP, MSPO and Malaysian Organic (myOrganic).",""],[1,"100","1","Contract Farming Procurement for Green Practices","In addition, agriculture procurement for contract farming will be leveraged to promote adoption of green practices.",""],[1,"100","1","Smart and Environment-Friendly Farming Support","This initiative will enable agricultural cooperatives and associations to facilitate farmers in adopting smart farming and environment-friendly farming practices.",""]],"254":[[1,"101","3","Ease of Doing Business and Regulatory Procedure Reform for Logistics","ease of doing business, including regulatory procedures will be improved to facilitate domestic players as well as attract global players to base their operations in the country.",""],[1,"101","3","Regional Distribution Centres and Supply Chain Management Development","An efficient supply chain management and regional distribution centres will be established to provide comprehensive services to consumers.",""],[1,"101","3","Logistics Best Practices and Technology Adoption Programme","Logistics services providers will be encouraged to adopt best practices and emerging technology as well as introduce new ways of doing business.",""],[1,"101","3","Multimodal Logistics Network Development","Multimodality will be promoted to establish a well-integrated logistics and communication network to ensure an efficient and advanced supply chain.",""],[1,"101","4","Logistics Industry Alliance and 4PL Development","form alliances, including through M&A to become fourth-party logistics (4PL) providers to manage and control all activities within the supply chain network and serve as a single point of contact for customers.",""],[1,"101","4","Malaysia Regional Logistics Hub Strategy","Establishing Malaysia as a regional hub will increase the competitiveness of industry players and expand the market share in the region.",""],[1,"101","5","Industry Capacity Strengthening and Collaboration Initiative","The capacity of industry will be strengthened to enhance competitiveness and sustainability of local industries.",""]],"255":[[1,"102","6","High-Value Agricultural Export Promotion","Export promotion efforts will be enhanced to increase exports of high value products to traditional and new markets.",""],[1,"102","6","Premium Agricultural Produce Promotion Campaign","Premium and high value agricultural produce, such as birdnest, Musang King durian and MD2 pineapple will be actively promoted through various platforms.",""],[1,"102","6","Agricultural Export Standards Compliance Programme","Agricultural exporters will be encouraged to comply with Malaysia's Best standard, which meets internationally recognised myGAP and myOrganic standards, as well as Grading, Packaging and Labelling of Agricultural Products Regulation to ensure market acceptance.",""],[1,"102","6","Agriccommodity Discriminatory Campaign Countermeasures","Meanwhile, concerted efforts to counter the discriminatory campaigns against Malaysia's agricommodity products, particularly on palm oil and timber will be continued.",""],[1,"102","6","MSPO Adoption Programme for Smallholders","These include intensifying programmes to ensure full adoption of the MSPO among smallholders by the end of 2021.",""]],"256":[[1,"104","2","Financial Services Innovation and Digitisation Initiative","efforts will be focused on facilitating innovation and technological applications in the financial services sector.",""],[1,"104","2","E-Payments Expansion Programme","The adoption of e-payments in the economy for more seamless and secure financial services experience will also be expanded and accelerated.",""],[1,"104","2","Financial Sector Digitisation Support Measures","measures will be undertaken to facilitate greater industry digitisation to improve overall efficiency of the financial services.",""],[1,"104","3","Market Entry Facilitation for Digital Financial Services","efforts will be undertaken to facilitate entry of new players such as digital banks, digital insurers, robo-advisors and digital brokers, as well as support market participants in embracing new innovative business models.",""],[1,"104","3","Regional Connectivity and Linkages Enhancement","There will also be continued efforts to enhance regional connectivity and linkages to attract greater foreign capital and knowledge transfer into the country.",""]],"257":[[1,"104","3","Cybersecurity Framework Enhancement","Enhancements to key enabling infrastructure, regulations and practices will also be pursued, including implementation of an effective cyber security framework to promote greater efficiency, safety and resilience.",""],[1,"104","5","Financial System Resilience and Stability Safeguards","Focus will be given on strengthening safeguards for financial stability and enhancing good governance.",""]],"258":[[1,"104","4","Expansion of Market-Based Fundraising and Alternative Financing for MSMEs","Differentiated market-based fundraising avenues will be further expanded to cater to the fundraising needs of MSMEs across their growth cycle, as well as more mature companies seeking regional expansion.",""],[1,"104","4","Consumer Protection Reinforcement for Credit Provision","This entails the development of a vibrant alternative financing to complement the banking system, as well as reinforcing consumer protection in the provision of credit, given the growing number of non-traditional entities.",""],[1,"104","4","Microfinancing Expansion for Enterprises","In addition, efforts to enhance the provision of microfinancing to these enterprises will continue to be pursued.",""],[1,"105","3","Expansion of Micro-Insurance and Micro-Takaful Products","The offering of micro-insurance and micro-takaful products will be expanded, while instituting measures to ensure long-term sustainability of medical health insurance and takaful for the",""],[1,"105","4","Financial Inclusion Reform and Safety Net Strengthening","Efforts will also be accorded to expedite reforms and address structural issues that hinder the financial inclusion agenda, such as inadequacy of financial safety nets to buffer B40 households from income shocks.",""],[1,"105","4","National Financial Literacy Strategy","At the same time, initiatives under the National Strategy for Financial Literacy will continue to be pursued to further improve financial literacy among Malaysians.",""]],"259":[[1,"104","6","Collaborative Regulatory Enforcement Framework","A more collaborative approach among regulatory authorities within and beyond the country will be adopted to strengthen regulatory enforcement",""],[1,"104","6","RegTech and SupTech Development Initiative","tools and mechanisms relating to regulatory technology (regtech) and supervisory technology (suptech) will also be developed to enhance the effectiveness and efficiency of regulators' role and functions",""]],"260":[[1,"104","7","Outcome-Focused Financial Sector Regulation","Regulatory and supervisory focus towards inculcating good culture and conduct within the financial sector will be enhanced through more outcome-focused regulatory action to shape market and institutional behaviour.",""],[1,"104","7","Investor Confidence and Corporate Governance Strengthening","This includes greater emphasis on strengthening investor confidence in listed companies through effective discharge of directors' duties and responsibilities.",""],[1,"104","7","Institutional Investor Stewardship Enhancement","the role of institutional investors in good governance and stewardship will be enhanced",""],[1,"104","7","Capital Market Anti-Corruption Measures","holistic anti-corruption measures will be implemented within the capital market.",""]],"261":[[1,"105","2","Strengthen Islamic Finance Regulation and Supervision","Efforts to consolidate Malaysia's role as a prominent thought leader in Islamic finance, particularly in the areas of regulation and supervision will be intensified.",""],[1,"105","2","Expand Value-Based Intermediation in Finance","Additionally, the adoption of value-based intermediation (VBI) principles in the provision of finance will be expanded.",""],[1,"105","2","Islamic Social Finance Mobilisation","Islamic financial institutions have been exploring the usage of social finance instruments through blending endowment (waqf), donation (sadaqah) and alms-giving (zakat), to further unlock and more effectively mobilise resources towards provision of financing and financial protection to low income communities.",""],[1,"105","2","Develop Innovative Islamic Fintech Market Mechanisms","measures will be undertaken to develop more innovative market- based mechanisms and products, leveraging on Islamic fintech, to better serve the needs of a wider financial market and the economy at large.",""],[1,"105","6","Value-Based Intermediation Framework","Through VBI, Islamic finance will bring various stakeholders together to advance the sustainability agenda.",""],[1,"105","6","Sustainable and Responsible Investment Ecosystem Development","efforts to develop a facilitative Sustainable and Responsible Investment (SRI) ecosystem under the SRI Roadmap will also be intensified.",""],[1,"105","6","Islamic Capital Market Expansion for Social Finance","This will include broadening Islamic capital market products and services to further support social finance activities, such as waqf, for the greater good of society.",""]],"262":[[1,"106","5","Green Industrial Estate Development Programme","the development of industrial estates will be promoted based on the green industry concept.",""],[1,"106","5","Eco-Industrial Parks Guideline Development","A comprehensive guideline on eco-industrial parks will be introduced to be adopted by industrial estates.",""]],"263":[[1,"106","7","Strengthening Dedicated Food Production Areas","The role of dedicated food production areas will be strengthened to increase participation of agropreneurs in modern farming.",""],[1,"106","7","Comprehensive Management Mechanism for Food Production Areas","A comprehensive mechanism in developing and managing these food production areas, such as TKPM, Aquaculture Industrial Zones and Permanent Ruminant Production Parks will be formulated through collaboration between the Federal and state governments.",""],[1,"106","7","Public-Private Collaboration for Modern Farming Technology Adoption","Collaboration between the government, private sector service providers and agropreneurs will be intensified to facilitate adoption of modern technologies.",""]],"264":[[1,"106","8","Industrial Estate Incentives and Financial Assistance Enhancement","The provision of incentives and financial assistance for players in industrial estates, particularly those investing in advanced technology will be enhanced.",""],[1,"106","8","Automation and Technology Utilisation Upgrade Along Value Chains","Greater automation and technology utilisation along the value chain will drive productivity growth and reduce reliance on low-skilled foreign workers.",""],[1,"106","8","Clean Technology Investment Incentive Redesign","Incentives will be redesigned to attract quality investments that utilise clean technology to ensure sustainable practices.",""],[1,"106","8","Smart Farming Financial Assistance Extension","Financial assistance will also be extended to agropreneurs in the food production areas to facilitate the adoption of smart farming practices for higher income and productivity.",""]],"265":[[1,"108","3","Agricultural Coordination Mechanism Strengthening","Existing coordination mechanisms in the agriculture sector will be further leveraged to create better synergy among agencies involved in agricultural development to increase efficiency and effectiveness in service delivery.",""],[1,"108","3","State-Level Agricultural Business Development Centres","Business Development Centre will be set up in all states as a one-stop centre to provide multiple agricultural related services, such as agronomic advisory, licence and permit approvals as well as certification and marketing services.",""],[1,"108","3","Agricultural Marketing Collaboration and eCommerce Promotion","Strategic collaboration among ministries, state governments and agencies will be strengthened to improve efficiency in the marketing of agriculture products.",""],[1,"108","3","Agricultural eCommerce Promotion Platform Use","This will be undertaken by capitalising the existing eCommerce platforms to provide opportunities for farmers to participate in promotion activities and increase visibility of agriculture products.",""],[1,"108","3","Overseas Mission Streamlining for Agricultural Export Promotion","The function of overseas missions will be streamlined to improve coordination in terms of export promotion activities, facilitating market access and dealing with trade-related matters.",""]],"266":[[1,"108","4","Integrated Healthcare Data System","In the healthcare services subsector, an integrated data system encompassing the public and private sector will be developed to capture and manage comprehensive information, including health registries, disease surveillance and economic activities related to healthcare.",""],[1,"108","4","Private Higher Education Institution Resource Sharing Initiative","Meanwhile, collaboration among private HEIs will be promoted in sharing resources, including facility and equipment to improve the quality of teaching and learning.",""],[1,"108","4","Alternative Financing for Private Higher Education Institutions","In addition, the private HEIs will be encouraged to explore alternative financing, including waqf and crowdfunding in ensuring sustainability of the institutions.",""]],"267":[[1,"109","2","Institutional Framework for Professional Services Development","A comprehensive institutional framework for professional services will be formulated to enhance SMPPs capacity and capability in expanding high value-added services.",""],[1,"127","6","Professional and Service Provider Capability Upgrading Programme","To support the operations of global services hubs, the capabilities of professionals and professional service providers need to be upgraded.",""],[1,"127","6","Public-Private Talent Development Partnership","Public- private collaboration in talent development especially upskilling and reskilling will be promoted to ensure a sustainable talent pipeline to meet industry demand.",""],[1,"127","6","Domestic Investment Strategic Fund Support for Digitalisation","existing funds such as the Domestic Investment Strategic Fund (DISF) will be further leveraged to accelerate digitalisation and enhance local GS capabilities.",""]],"268":[[1,"107","8","Stakeholder Coordination and Collaboration Enhancement","Efforts will be undertaken to enhance the effectiveness of existing mechanisms and encourage the sharing of data and resources, which will enable stakeholders to improve quality of outcomes.",""],[1,"109","3","Agency Role Streamlining for Service Delivery Improvement","The roles and functions of relevant agencies will be streamlined to improve service delivery, contribute to effective decision- making and optimise resources.",""],[1,"109","3","Agriculture Sector Agency Realignment and Modernisation","The roles and functions of several agencies in the agriculture sector related to training, research and marketing will be reviewed and realigned in modernising the sector.",""],[1,"109","3","IR4.0 Technology Adaptation and Extension Support","This includes taking into account the needs for IR4.0 technology adaptation, extension services and private sector investment.",""],[1,"109","3","Akademi Binaan Malaysia Capacity Enhancement","In the construction sector, Akademi Binaan Malaysia will be enhanced as an internationally recognised training institution to produce high skilled technical talent.",""],[1,"109","3","Construction Sector R&D Collaboration Streamlining","the roles and functions of the Construction Research Institute of Malaysia and the Centre of Excellence for Engineering and Technology will be streamlined through strategic collaboration to enhance the effectiveness of R&D in the construction sector.",""]],"269":[[1,"107","4","Governance, Policy, and Legislative Strengthening Measures","Measures will be undertaken to strengthen coordination and collaboration for more effective implementation, enhance roles and functions of institutions as well as strengthen policy and legislation.",""],[1,"109","4","Legislative Strengthening and Policy Review","efforts will be undertaken to strengthen existing legislation as well as develop and review relevant policies.",""],[1,"109","4","Conducive Regulatory Environment for Sectoral Transformation","A conducive regulatory environment will facilitate sectoral transformation to move up the value chain.",""],[1,"109","5","Good Regulatory Practices Adoption by Government Agencies","Government agencies will be required to adopt Good Regulatory Practices (GRP) to increase transparency, especially in disseminating information related to changes in law and regulations.",""]],"270":[[1,"109","6","National Agrofood Policy 2021-2030","The National Agrofood Policy 2021-2030 (DAN 2.0), which is being formulated will focus on the application of modern technology in the agrofood subsector to attain higher productivity and income.",""],[1,"109","6","National Food Security Action Plan","An action plan on national food security is also being formulated and is expected to be finalised by the end of 2021.",""],[1,"109","6","Small Farmer Modernisation through Agricultural Cooperatives and Associations","The implementation of DAN 2.0 will enable small farmers, through agricultural cooperatives and associations, to modernise and operate efficiently and effectively.",""],[1,"109","6","National Agricommodity Policy 2021-2030","The National Agricommodity Policy 2021-2030 (DAKN2030) is also being formulated to provide a new direction and targets to increase productivity, enhance downstream activities and promote the growth of new industries.",""]],"271":[[1,"110","4","Agricultural Legislation Modernisation Reform","several rules and regulations will be amended to modernise agricultural activities, increase food safety and nutrition safety requirements as well as address issues that hinder the development of the agriculture sector.",""],[1,"110","4","Mineral Subsector SOP and Guidelines Harmonisation","standard operating procedures and guidelines on best practices for the mineral subsector, particularly on the aspect of enforcement, land rehabilitation and sustainable practices will be reviewed and harmonised for implementation at state level.",""],[1,"110","4","Strategic Minerals Legislative Framework","Related legislations will be formulated and reviewed in developing potential strategic minerals as well as minimising environmental impact from mining and quarrying activities.",""]],"272":[[1,"110","6","Wholesale and Retail Self-Regulation Framework","Self-regulation will be introduced to encourage adherence to legal and safety regulations, particularly in the wholesale and retail subsector.",""],[1,"110","6","Business Association Regulatory Empowerment Amendment","Current regulations will be amended to fully empower the associations and federations to undertake the regulatory responsibility as well as enforce compulsory registration of businesses with the respective associations and federations.",""],[1,"110","6","Private Higher Education Institutions Regulatory Review","Meanwhile, acts and regulations related to private HEIs will be reviewed to align with current developments in the education services subsector.",""]],"273":[[1,"129","16","Domestic Aerospace Supply Chain and Competency Development","Develop domestic supply chain and competencies in the local aerospace manufacturing industry ecosystem",""],[1,"129","23","Aerospace TVET Programme Enhancement","Enhance aerospace TVET programmes for manufacturing, MRO and operations",""],[1,"129","26","Academia-Industry Collaboration for NanoSat and CubeSat Projects","Promote academia and industry collaboration for NanoSat and CubeSat projects",""],[1,"129","28","Aerospace Talent Centre of Excellence","Establish a centre of excellence for aerospace talent",""],[2,"129","16","Domestic Aerospace Supply Chain and Competency Development","Develop domestic supply chain and competencies in the local aerospace manufacturing industry ecosystem",""],[2,"129","23","Aerospace TVET Programme Enhancement","Enhance aerospace TVET programmes for manufacturing, MRO and operations",""],[2,"129","26","Academia-Industry Collaboration for NanoSat and CubeSat Projects","Promote academia and industry collaboration for NanoSat and CubeSat projects",""],[2,"129","28","Aerospace Talent Centre of Excellence","Establish a centre of excellence for aerospace talent",""]],"274":[[1,"132","1","Digital Innovation for Sustainable Tourism Products","Industry players will be encouraged to innovate and adopt digital technology in enhancing the sustainability of tourism products.",""],[1,"132","1","Virtual Tourism and Cultural Promotion Platform","The adoption of digital technology will improve service delivery and enable tourism and cultural products to be better showcased through virtual tours, as well as online cultural shows and handicraft-making.",""],[1,"132","1","Online Marketplace Support for Arts and Handicrafts","Online marketplaces will also be utilised to complement arts and handicraft complexes including Kompleks Kraftangan and Balai Seni to enable wider market access and increase the visibility of local arts and crafts globally.",""],[1,"132","3","National Brand Positioning Strategy","Efforts to enhance Malaysia as a brand that incorporates the identity, essence, image and culture of the nation, will be implemented through distinct brand positioning strategies.",""],[1,"132","3","Malaysia Brand Marketing and Promotion Campaigns","Aggressive marketing and promotional campaigns, which focus on differentiating Malaysia from its competitors and building a distinct market, will be pursued.",""],[1,"132","4","Malaysia Truly Asia Brand Revitalization","The Malaysia Truly Asia tagline will be revitalised to leverage the brand recognition and value built through past efforts.",""],[1,"132","4","Tourism Package Development and Marketing","Attractive tour packages will continue to be developed and marketed, showcasing destinations and activities that include culture, arts and heritage elements to provide a unique experience.",""],[1,"132","4","Digital Tourism Platform Development","Digital platforms will be harnessed to realise tourism-related aspirations.",""],[1,"132","5","Travel Facilitation and Air Connectivity Improvement","travel to and from Malaysia will be made more efficient by improving travel facilitation and enhancing air connectivity.",""],[1,"132","5","Digital Tourism Data and Decision-Support System","Malaysia will also adopt digitalisation in capturing tourist data and trends in improving planning, resource deployment and decision-making.",""]],"275":[[1,"135","4","Agricultural Outsourcing Services Expansion","Efforts in establishing more agricultural outsourcing services will also be intensified to reduce high capital expenditure and the cost of production incurred by farmers.",""],[1,"135","5","Smart Farming Expansion under FELDA Settlements","The smart farming initiatives through technology providers will also be expanded under the FELDA Program Pembangunan Peneroka to increase the productivity and income of settlers.",""],[1,"135","5","FELDA Smart Farming Pilot Expansion","the smart farming pilot project through modern agricultural activities including cash crop, aquaculture and livestock initiated in FELDA Bukit Rokan will be expanded to several other FELDA settlements.",""],[1,"135","5","Modern Farming Information, Capacity Building, and Advisory Support","This expansion will involve dissemination of information on modern technologies as well as capacity building and provision of advisory services to the settlers.",""],[1,"135","6","Community Farming Enhancement Incentives","In this regard, incentives will be provided to assist local communities in intensifying the implementation of community farming.",""],[1,"135","6","Smart Farming Adoption for Community Food Production","Food production through community farming will be enhanced by adopting smart farming.",""],[1,"135","6","Public-Private Smart Farming Advisory Support","In addition, public-private collaboration in providing advisory services and suitable smart farming technology for local communities will be enhanced.",""]],"276":[[1,"137","2","Entrepreneurship Education and Training for Students","Education and training will also focus on developing students with entrepreneurial skills set to produce more job creators among graduates.",""],[1,"137","2","Triple Helix Entrepreneurship Collaboration","Triple Helix collaboration will be encouraged to enable entrepreneurs to acquire the necessary skills and competencies.",""],[1,"137","2","Entrepreneurship Training Modules","Training modules will incorporate skills, such as analytical thinking, emotional intelligence, reasoning, problem- solving, social influence and originality to assist entrepreneurs in their business.",""]],"277":[[1,"138","6","MSME Internationalisation Support Programme","MSMEs that demonstrate high export growth potential will be facilitated through the provision of advisory services, international market intelligence, IP registration as well as brand and product development.",""],[1,"138","6","Trade Facilitation and Regulatory Barrier Reduction Measures","Initiatives will also focus on trade facilitation measures, including reducing regulatory barriers to cross-border trade and business through G2G partnerships and collaboration among countries within ASEAN and APEC as well as with other international organisations.",""],[1,"138","6","FTA Utilisation and MSME Market Access Expansion","Efforts will also be undertaken to leverage the benefits of FTAs in widening market access and accelerating the internationalisation of MSMEs.",""]],"278":[[1,"138","8","Continuous Support for PPK and PNK Entrepreneurship Development","The role of PPK and PNK in developing entrepreneurship among their members will be further enhanced by providing continuous support in the form of inputs, financial assistance, technology uptake and consultation.",""],[1,"138","8","Modern Agro-Food Project Implementation by PPK and PNK","The PPK and PNK will be encouraged to implement modern agro-food projects in partnership with their members to increase productivity and income.",""],[1,"138","8","Agropreneur Programme Expansion for Market Access","This will be undertaken, among others, through the implementation of more agropreneur programmes, which will facilitate wider market access for the members through PPK and PNK.",""]],"279":[[1,"139","3","Entrepreneur Categorisation Review","the categorisation of entrepreneurs, including social entrepreneurs and start-ups, will be reviewed to reflect the current needs and future landscape.",""],[1,"139","3","Startup Cluster Classification Framework","Startups will also be classified under technology and non-technology clusters to align with the current technological advancements and business models.",""],[1,"139","3","Corporate Governance Toolkit for MSMEs","A corporate governance toolkit for MSMEs will be developed to improve business efficiency and performance through fair practices, good ethics and the right corporate and management culture.",""],[1,"139","4","Review and Improve Entrepreneurship Regulations","Existing legislations related to entrepreneurship will be reviewed to enhance the effectiveness and inclusiveness of entrepreneurship development.",""],[1,"139","4","Improve Laws and Regulations for Vibrant Businesses and Cooperatives","relevant laws and regulations will be improved to ensure businesses and cooperatives remain vibrant.",""],[1,"139","4","Informal Sector Business Registration Promotion","Measures will continue to be undertaken to encourage registration of businesses in the informal sector.",""],[1,"139","4","Support Access for Registered Entrepreneurs","This will enable entrepreneurs to have access to necessary supports, such as financing, marketing, and legal protection.",""],[1,"139","5","Small Business Payment Commissioner","A commissioner will be appointed to provide support for small businesses in securing payments on time and will act as a mediator in resolving payment disputes thereby advocating better payment practices among government and businesses.",""]],"280":[[1,"139","6","Centralised Entrepreneurship Information Database","A centralised database will be established to provide comprehensive information on entrepreneurship activities.",""],[1,"139","6","Unified MSME Entrepreneurship Support Portal","A unified portal, MyAssist MSME and a centralised platform that leverage existing one-stop centres such as Pusat Internet Komuniti (PIK) and Pusat Internet Desa (PID) will be further strengthened to facilitate entrepreneurs to acquire knowledge, learn business best practices and obtain essential information on starting a business, market access, human capital development, financial resources and other various business aspects.",""],[1,"139","6","Strengthening and Streamlining Entrepreneurship Development Organisations","the roles and functions of entrepreneurship development organisations (EDOs) will be strengthened and streamlined to improve efficiency and optimise resources.",""],[1,"139","6","Integrated Monitoring Mechanism for Entrepreneurial Development Programmes","a holistic and integrated monitoring mechanism will be introduced to measure the overall impact of entrepreneurial development programmes by EDOs.",""],[1,"140","3","Programme Monitoring and Assessment Mechanism","monitoring of programmes will be enhanced to ensure entrepreneurs are more successful and resilient.",""],[2,"139","6","Centralised Entrepreneurship Information Database","A centralised database will be established to provide comprehensive information on entrepreneurship activities.",""],[2,"139","6","Integrated Monitoring Mechanism for Entrepreneurial Development Programmes","a holistic and integrated monitoring mechanism will be introduced to measure the overall impact of entrepreneurial development programmes by EDOs.",""]],"281":[[1,"146","1","Smart and Cluster Farming Land Optimisation Programme","Rural areas will be transformed by optimising idle land for smart and cluster farming activities, as well as employing advanced technology to increase farm produce.",""],[1,"151","13","Smart and Cluster Farming on Idle Land","Optimising idle land and utilising advanced technology for smart and cluster farming.",""]],"282":[[1,"148","12","National Defence and Security Industry Policy","Introducing the National Defence and Security Industry Policy.",""],[1,"158","2","Training and Capability Upgrading for ATM and Enforcement Agencies","The capacity and capability of ATM and enforcement agencies were strengthened through enhancement of training programmes as well as upgrading of facilities and equipment.",""],[1,"158","2","Specialised Training and Courses for Security Personnel","The competency of personnel in these agencies was improved through systematic training and specialised courses such as strategic joint training, crime analysis and forensic investigation.",""],[1,"158","2","Large-Scale Joint Training for ATM and PDRM","personnel from ATM and PDRM also participated in specialised joint training programmes on a larger scale to enhance skills in interoperability.",""],[1,"169","1","Defence Capacity and Capability Enhancement","Defence capacity and capability will be enhanced in safeguarding national sovereignty as outlined in the Defence White Paper.",""],[1,"169","1","Military Intelligence, Surveillance, Target Acquisition and Reconnaissance Strengthening","military capability will be strengthened in the aspects of intelligence, surveillance, target acquisition and reconnaissance.",""],[1,"169","1","Firepower and Mobility Improvement Measures","Measures will also be undertaken to improve firepower and mobility in enhancing the defence capacity and capability.",""],[1,"169","1","Maritime Security Fortification","maritime security will be fortified, especially in surveillance and enforcement activities as well as showing presence to protect the socioeconomic interest and security of the country.",""],[1,"169","2","National Defence and Security Industry Policy","A national defence and security industry policy will be formulated to provide overall direction to reduce dependency on foreign assets and equipment.",""]],"283":[[1,"169","6","National Action Plan on Preventing and Countering Violent Extremism","A national action plan for preventing and countering violent extremism will be developed as a guide in ensuring rapid response against terrorism and extremism threats.",""],[1,"169","6","Counter-Terrorism Networking and Information Sharing Mechanism","Networking and information sharing with relevant domestic and foreign agencies as well as telecommunication companies, will be strengthened in countering the terrorist movements.",""],[1,"169","6","Awareness and Deradicalisation Programme","In curbing radicalism, awareness and deradicalisation programmes involving relevant agencies will be enhanced.",""],[2,"169","6","National Action Plan for Preventing and Countering Violent Extremism","A national action plan for preventing and countering violent extremism will be developed as a guide in ensuring rapid response against terrorism and extremism threats.",""],[2,"169","6","Counter-Terrorism Networking and Information Sharing","Networking and information sharing with relevant domestic and foreign agencies as well as telecommunication companies, will be strengthened in countering the terrorist movements.",""],[2,"169","6","Awareness and Deradicalisation Programmes","In curbing radicalism, awareness and deradicalisation programmes involving relevant agencies will be enhanced.",""]],"284":[[1,"172","3","Strengthening Healthcare Policy and Disease Control Measures","Measures will focus on strengthening healthcare policy, combatting CDs and NCDs as well as enhancing healthcare programmes for older persons.",""],[1,"172","4","Targeted Health Policy Package","Several policies targeting specific health needs will be introduced, such as oral healthcare, mental health and immunisation policies.",""],[1,"172","4","Food Safety Policy Review","In addition, food safety policies will be reviewed to protect the public against health hazards and fraud in the food supply chain including preparation, sale and use of food.",""],[1,"172","4","Drinking Water Quality Act","The drinking water quality act will also be introduced.",""],[1,"173","3","Regulation of Private Aged Healthcare Facility Design","The design of private healthcare facilities shall comply with the Private Aged Healthcare Facilities and Services Act 2018 and Care Centres (Amendment) Act 2018 to cater for the needs of older persons.",""]],"285":[[1,"179","1","Community-Based Sports Body Strengthening Programme","Community-based sports bodies will be strengthened to conduct sports events and promote an active lifestyle more effectively.",""],[1,"179","1","Sports Body Capacity Building Programme","The management of these sports bodies will be enhanced through capacity building programmes to improve leadership, financial management and administrative skills.",""],[1,"179","1","Community Sports Body Rating System","A rating system will be introduced to promote management excellence among community-based sports bodies.",""],[1,"179","4","Revision of the National Sports Policy","The National Sports Policy will be revised to include, among others, measures to strengthen the administration and management of national sports associations (NSAs).",""],[1,"179","4","Capacity Building for National Sports Associations","The professionalism of NSAs will be enhanced through capacity building programmes.",""],[1,"179","4","Employment of Former National Athletes in NSAs","The NSAs will also be encouraged to hire former national athletes to tap their experience and skills.",""],[1,"179","4","Women in Sports Secretariat Coaching and Leadership Training","The Women in Sports Secretariat will be tasked, among others to ensure more women, particularly former national athletes are trained as qualified coaches and office bearers in HPS entities.",""]],"286":[[1,"180","4","Sports Tourism Promotion and Sports Event Hosting","Sports tourism will be promoted to spur growth in the industry by hosting or organising sports events, such as recreational sports, e-sports and extreme sports.",""],[1,"180","4","International Sports Event Attraction Initiative","efforts will be intensified for international sports events to be held in Malaysia to attract both local and foreign participants and spectators.",""],[1,"180","4","Special Tourism Package Development for Sports Visitors","Special tourism packages will also be developed for them to experience local culture and hospitality.",""],[1,"180","4","Private Investment in International-Standard Sports Facilities","The private sector will also be encouraged to invest in sports facilities that comply with international standards.",""]],"287":[[1,"181","5","Review and Streamline Unity-Related School and Higher Education Programmes","Unity-related syllabus and academic programmes in schools and HEIs will be reviewed and streamlined to enhance effectiveness and relevancy.",""],[1,"181","5","Strengthen Bahasa Melayu Promotion and Proficiency Programmes","Programmes and initiatives to promote the usage as well as to strengthen the proficiency of Bahasa Melayu, as the national language, in society will be further intensified.",""],[1,"181","5","Multilingual Learning and Cultural Understanding Initiative","Efforts will be intensified to encourage the rakyat to learn other local languages such as Mandarin, Tamil and other ethnic languages.",""],[1,"181","5","Digital Language Learning Methods Expansion","Learning methods for other local languages will be diversified by leveraging digital technology.",""],[1,"181","5","Educational Campaigns and Engagements to Cultivate Noble Values","More educational programmes, campaigns and engagements will be undertaken to cultivate noble values.",""],[1,"181","6","Patriotism, Volunteerism, and Values Promotion Measures","Measures will be undertaken to strengthen patriotism and volunteerism as well as leverage the digital platform in instilling noble values.",""],[1,"181","7","Constitutional and Patriotism Awareness Campaigns","Understanding and appreciation of the Federal Constitution and Rukun Negara will be enhanced through wider awareness campaigns by leveraging digital media and other platforms.",""],[1,"181","7","Patriotism Ambassador Appointment Initiative","In addition, constitutional experts and social media influencers will be appointed as icons to raise the level of awareness on patriotism.",""],[1,"181","7","Patriotism Index Development","A new index will also be developed to assess the level of patriotism among Malaysians and assist in designing patriotism programmes.",""],[1,"181","7","National History Dissemination Initiative","Efforts will be intensified in disseminating knowledge on Malaysia's history to every citizen.",""],[1,"181","7","Patriotism Media Content Expansion","Initiatives such as short documentaries and interactive programmes will be increased through collaboration with relevant stakeholders.",""],[1,"181","7","Patriotism Awareness Programmes for Overseas Malaysians","Awareness programmes, including Kelas Bimbingan Malaysia will be expanded to all major diplomatic missions to enhance patriotism and nationalism among Malaysians residing overseas.",""]],"288":[[1,"194","7","Kampung Baru Chinese Community Soft Loan Scheme","Skim Pinjaman Khas Penduduk Kampung Baru Cina was continued during the Eleventh Plan.",""],[1,"210","2","Kampung Baru Business Loan Facility","For low-income Chinese households in Kampung Baru, access to financing facilities will be continued by providing business loans to facilitate their expansion of business.",""],[1,"210","2","Kampung Baru Tourism Promotion and Infrastructure Upgrade","The Skim Pinjaman Khas Penduduk Kampung Baru will be expanded to include the promotion of villages as attractive tourist destinations.",""],[1,"210","2","Kampung Baru Basic Infrastructure and Amenities Upgrading","In addition, basic infrastructure and amenities will continue to be upgraded to enable the Kampung Baru community to enjoy better facilities.",""],[1,"210","3","Priority Support for Low-Income Indian Households","the wellbeing of low-income Indian households will continue to be given priority in line with the Malaysian Indian Blueprint.",""],[1,"210","3","Quality Education Access Improvement for Low-Income Indian Households","Access to quality education will be improved while low education attainment and the issue of dropouts among this community will be addressed.",""],[1,"210","3","Targeted Upskilling and Entrepreneurship Support Programme","Targeted upskilling programmes that match the requirements of industry players will be offered in increasing employment opportunities while entrepreneurship opportunities will be enhanced.",""],[1,"210","3","Parenting Courses and High-Risk Family Support Services","appropriate programmes such as pre- and post-marital parenting courses as well as support services for high-risk families will be provided to holistically address dysfunctional families and youth issues.",""],[1,"210","4","Education Access Improvement for M40 Households","In this regard, access to education will be improved",""],[1,"210","4","Affordable Home Ownership Facilitation","while affordable home ownership will be facilitated",""],[1,"210","4","Health and Employment Insurance Incentive Scheme","In addition, incentives will be provided to encourage them in obtaining health and employment insurance",""],[1,"211","1","M40 Income Support and Entrepreneurship Promotion","The M40 will be supported to boost their income to cope with the high cost of living and prevent them from falling into the vulnerable group.",""],[1,"211","1","M40 Entrepreneurship and Supplementary Income Activities","In this regard, the M40 will be encouraged to be involved in entrepreneurship and supplementary income activities as well as invest in income-generating portfolios.",""],[1,"211","1","M40 Sharing Economy Promotion Through Digital Platforms","The sharing economy will be promoted among the M40 through the use of digital platforms.",""],[1,"211","1","Financial Literacy Programmes and Advisory Services","financial institutions will be encouraged to provide financial literacy programmes and advisory services.",""],[1,"211","2","Affordable Early Childhood Care and Education Expansion","affordable ECCE especially in urban areas and public sector premises will be provided and enhanced",""],[1,"211","2","Workplace Affordable Day Care Incentive","The private sector will be further encouraged to provide affordable day care services at their workplaces",""],[1,"211","3","M40 Health and Employment Insurance Uptake Support","The M40 will be encouraged to subscribe to health and employment insurance to mitigate them from financial vulnerability.",""],[1,"211","3","Tax Relief Review for Health, Life, and Employment Insurance","In addition, income tax relief on health and life as well as employment insurance for the M40 will be reviewed to reduce healthcare costs.",""],[1,"211","4","Affordable Home Ownership Facilitation","Ownership of affordable homes by the M40 will be facilitated.",""]],"289":[[1,"220","1","Target Group Wellbeing and Empowerment Initiatives","Synergistic efforts will be mobilised in empowering specific target groups to improve their wellbeing and achieve a higher standard of living based on the principle of leaving no one behind.",""],[1,"221","1","Strengthening Child Development and Protection Governance Mechanisms","governance and implementation mechanisms for children development and protection will be enhanced",""],[1,"221","1","National Child Development Index Formulation","A national child development index will be formulated as a tool to improve policies related to the biological and psychological growth of children",""],[1,"221","1","Child Justice Process Review","The child judicial process will be reviewed to further strengthen children protection",""],[1,"221","1","Juvenile Offender Separation and Reintegration Programmes","programmes to separate children with minor crimes from those committing more serious offences will be undertaken to assist the reintegration of the young offenders into the community",""],[1,"221","1","National Strategy Plan on Child Marriage","the issue of child marriage will continue to be addressed through the implementation of the National Strategy Plan in Handling the Causes of Child Marriage",""],[1,"221","1","Early Childhood Care and Education Programme Rationalisation","The ECCE programmes will also be rationalised to enhance accessibility and quality of programmes as well as to ensure fees are affordable",""],[1,"221","2","Youth Economic Empowerment Plan","A national plan on youth economic empowerment will be introduced to provide strategic direction in improving youth employability.",""],[1,"221","2","Youth Financial Education Network","a youth financial education network will be initiated as a platform to promote financial literacy and credit management programmes.",""],[1,"221","3","Youth Healthy Lifestyle and Mental Wellbeing Promotion","Efforts to promote a healthy and active lifestyle among youth with greater emphasis on mental wellbeing will be intensified.",""],[1,"221","4","Gender Mainstreaming Framework","The gender mainstreaming20 framework will be introduced to incorporate the gender perspective in formulating policies.",""],[1,"221","4","Review of Laws for Women's Protection","Relevant laws will be reviewed to ensure that women are better protected.",""],[1,"221","4","Women's Economic Participation and Entrepreneurship Support","Women's participation in all sectors will be elevated via multiple economic platforms, including the sharing economy and entrepreneurship development.",""],[1,"221","5","Women's Rights Awareness and Intervention Programmes","Safety and security issues will continue to be addressed by strengthening both civil and sharia laws as well as enhancing women's rights awareness and intervention programmes.",""],[1,"221","5","Sexual Harassment and Gender Equality Legislation","Legislation to address sexual harassment and gender inequalities will be formulated to ensure a safe environment as well as eliminate violence against women and gender-biased discrimination.",""],[1,"222","1","Older Persons Rights Protection Law","This will include introducing laws to protect the rights of older persons, establishing a comprehensive long-term care framework, enhancing quality and services of caregivers as well as invigorating the social care industry.",""],[1,"222","1","Comprehensive Long-Term Care Framework","This will include introducing laws to protect the rights of older persons, establishing a comprehensive long-term care framework, enhancing quality and services of caregivers as well as invigorating the social care industry.",""],[1,"222","1","Healthy Ageing Awareness Campaigns","Awareness campaigns on healthy ageing will be intensified, while care givers for the aged will be promoted as a professional career.",""],[1,"222","1","Caregiver Professionalisation Initiative","Awareness campaigns on healthy ageing will be intensified, while care givers for the aged will be promoted as a professional career.",""],[1,"222","1","Expanded Palliative Care Collaboration","In addition, collaboration between public and private healthcare providers in broadening palliative care services will be strengthened to ensure the effectiveness of intervention programmes.",""],[1,"222","1","IoT-Enabled Homecare Monitoring and Virtual Consultations","New initiatives will also be introduced to modernise healthcare services by utilising internet of things (IoT) in homecare monitoring and virtual medical consultations.",""],[1,"222","2","Youth Financial Literacy Programme Expansion","Programmes to inculcate financial literacy among the younger generation will be amplified to improve financial management skills in preparation for old age.",""],[1,"222","2","Pension System and Retirement Coverage Enhancement","Pension systems and retirement coverage will also be enhanced.",""],[1,"222","2","Private Retirement Scheme Promotion","Private retirement schemes will be promoted to complement existing schemes.",""],[1,"222","2","Social Assistance Streamlining for Older Persons","Current social assistance programmes will be streamlined to strengthen social protection for older persons.",""],[1,"222","2","e-Warga Emas National Database","the e-Warga Emas will be launched as an integrated national database for older persons, to facilitate better policymaking and programme implementation.",""],[1,"222","2","Lifelong Learning and Employment Access Expansion","Accessibility to lifelong learning programmes and employment opportunities will be broadened to improve income and quality of life.",""],[1,"222","2","Elderly-Friendly Physical Planning Adoption","Local authorities will be encouraged to adopt the Physical Planning Guideline for Elderly, while a national framework on Age Friendly City will also be introduced to promote a more conducive environment for the aged population.",""],[1,"222","2","Intergenerational Programme Promotion","Intergenerational programmes will be further promoted to strengthen social interaction among different generations.",""],[1,"222","4","Family Institution Strengthening through Community Empowerment","the family institution will be strengthened through community empowerment",""],[1,"222","4","Pre-Marital Education and Parenting Skills Programme Redesign","Pre-marital education and parenting skills programmes will be redesigned to leverage the digital platform and be more relevant to the current issues and challenges.",""],[1,"222","5","Flexible Working Arrangements Expansion","Work-life balance will be enhanced by promoting flexible working hours.",""],[1,"222","5","Adaptable Working Arrangements Expansion","Adaptable working arrangements will be expanded while the private sector will be encouraged to provide paternity leave and better care centres.",""],[1,"222","5","Private Sector Paternity Leave and Care Centre Promotion","Adaptable working arrangements will be expanded while the private sector will be encouraged to provide paternity leave and better care centres.",""],[1,"222","5","Subfertility Centre Service Expansion","Sexual and reproductive health programmes will be enhanced by expanding the role of Lembaga Penduduk dan Pembangunan Keluarga Negara (LPPKN) Subfertility Centre.",""],[1,"222","5","Financial Literacy and Debt Advisory Services Improvement","Financial literacy and debt advisory services will be improved, particularly for families from the B40.",""],[1,"222","5","Parent Digital Literacy Awareness Expansion","Awareness on digital literacy among parents will be expanded to address digital addiction, while child cyber protection programmes will be incorporated in the school curriculum to increase understanding of cyber threats.",""],[1,"222","5","Child Cyber Protection Curriculum Integration","Awareness on digital literacy among parents will be expanded to address digital addiction, while child cyber protection programmes will be incorporated in the school curriculum to increase understanding of cyber threats.",""]],"290":[[1,"231","6","Stage Bus Services Transformation Programme Expansion","The Stage Bus Services Transformation Programme was expanded to improve connectivity between rural and urban areas as well as to provide scheduled trips for rural communities.",""],[1,"231","6","myBAS Rural Route Expansion","The myBAS service opened up new routes in underserved rural areas, such as Bahau in Negeri Sembilan, Salak Tinggi in Selangor and Chemor in Perak.",""],[1,"231","7","Rural Community Centre Rebranding and Service Delivery Programme","The Rural Transformation Centres (RTCs) and mini RTCs were also rebranded as Pusat Komuniti Desa (PKD) to continue offering key government front line services, business advisory and entrepreneurial skills programmes.",""],[1,"232","1","Rural Economic Activity Intensification Initiative","Initiatives to intensify local economic activities in rural areas were undertaken by encouraging more private sector participation and rural entrepreneurship.",""]],"291":[[1,"239","5","Investment Attraction Incentive Package Enhancement","Measures to attract quality investments, particularly in less developed regions, will be intensified to expedite development.",""],[1,"239","5","R&D&C&I Intensification Initiative","The focus will be on enticing high value-added, advanced technology and knowledge-intensive activities by enhancing competitive incentive packages and intensifying R&D&C&I.",""]],"292":[[1,"240","2","Regional Transport Network Improvement","The transport network will be strengthened for better connectivity and mobility to boost inter- and intra-regional economic activities.",""],[1,"240","2","Integrated Land-Air-Sea Transport Network Upgrade","The integrated transport network connecting land, air and sea will be improved to stimulate economic growth, facilitate the movement of people and goods as well as reduce travelling time and transportation costs.",""],[1,"240","2","Catalytic Transport Projects Through Private Initiatives","Meanwhile, the implementation of catalytic projects to improve the transport network through private initiatives, such as the West Coast Expressway and the proposed construction of the Labuan- Menumbok bridge will be encouraged to spur the economy, attract more quality investment and create more job opportunities.",""]],"293":[[1,"240","3","Basic Infrastructure and Utility Service Enhancement","The provision of basic infrastructure and services, including the supply of water and electricity as well as broadband coverage across regions will be further enhanced.",""],[1,"240","3","Interagency Utility Reliability Coordination","Collaboration with various agencies, including state governments will be strengthened to improve the reliability of water and electricity supply to meet industry requirements.",""],[1,"240","3","Fibre Network Expansion for Broadband Services","The expansion of fibre networks will also provide high-speed and reliable broadband services to support the growing demand of industries.",""]],"294":[[1,"240","5","MSME Integration into Broader Production Networks","MSMEs will be encouraged to increase participation in the broader production networks encompassing large firms and multinational corporations to move up the value chain, open up new business opportunities, increase market access and facilitate the adoption of 4IR technologies.",""],[1,"240","5","Triple Helix Technology Advisory and Consultation Services","The triple helix model2 will be leveraged to provide advisory and consultation services on the application of the latest technologies.",""],[1,"240","5","Data-Driven Decision Support Analytics Tools","Analytical tools will be utilised to assist in providing predictive information for data-driven decision-making.",""]],"295":[[1,"244","8","Expansion of Urban Green and Blue Spaces","Green and blue spaces, such as recreational parks, urban forests and lakes, will be expanded to improve microclimate and enhance biodiversity in urban areas.",""],[1,"244","8","Urban Biodiversity Action Plan","An action plan for urban biodiversity will be developed to guide local authorities in enhancing liveability.",""],[1,"244","8","Urban Green Space Revitalization and Community Farming Support","Developers of residential and commercial projects will be encouraged to revive the green and blue spaces with endemic plant species as well as facilitate community-based urban farming.",""]],"296":[[1,"245","1","Local Agenda 21 Acceleration","Meanwhile, the implementation of Local Agenda 21 (LA21) will be accelerated to achieve the 2030 Agenda.",""],[1,"245","3","Accelerated LA21 Implementation through Local Collaboration","The implementation of LA21 will be accelerated through greater collaboration among local authorities, communities and the private sector in championing urban sustainable development.",""],[1,"245","3","Use of Community Activity Coordination Offices for LA21","The community activity coordination offices in the Program Perumahan Rakyat as well as low- and low medium-cost housing will be further leveraged in accelerating the implementation of LA21 programmes.",""]],"297":[[1,"245","9","Rural Water Supply Expansion","The coverage of water supply will be expanded to reach 98% of rural households, including providing alternative water supply and reticulation system.",""],[1,"245","9","Rural Electricity Access Expansion","Electricity supply will be expanded to reach 99% coverage through grid connection and alternative systems, such as small hydro, solar hybrid and solar photovoltaic.",""]],"298":[[1,"254","1","Rural Air Services Upgrading","Efforts were also undertaken to uplift the Rural Air Services (RAS) by upgrading short take-off and landing airstrips (STOLports) in enhancing connectivity and safety compliance.",""],[1,"254","1","Sandakan Airport Runway Extension","The Sandakan Airport is undergoing runway extension works to allow bigger planes to land without weight restriction.",""],[1,"264","3","RAS Subsidy for Rural Sabah and Sarawak","the Federal Government will continue to subsidise RAS for Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[1,"264","3","Rural Air Route Rationalisation and Expansion","The exercise will involve rationalisation of existing routes and the possible introduction of new ones to enhance overall connectivity in rural Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[1,"264","3","STOLport Maintenance Programme","the airport operators will continue to undertake the maintenance of STOLports.",""]],"299":[[1,"254","2","Basic Infrastructure Improvement Initiatives in Sabah and Sarawak","Access to basic infrastructure in Sabah and Sarawak continues to be improved with the implementation of various initiatives, including the Rural Electricity Supply, Rural Water Supply, as well as Environmental Sanitation and Water Supply programmes.",""],[1,"263","1","Infrastructure and Connectivity Expansion in Sabah and Sarawak","The provision of infrastructure and connectivity will be solidified to facilitate economic activities and enable better delivery of social services, particularly in the rural areas.",""],[1,"263","4","Basic Infrastructure Provision and Expansion","The provision of basic infrastructure, including roads, water and electricity supply will continue to be given emphasis.",""],[1,"263","4","Broadband Coverage Expansion","Besides the expansion of broadband coverage in populated areas, broadband connectivity to rural schools will also be provided.",""],[1,"263","4","Water and Electricity Supply Expansion in Sabah and Sarawak","In addition, coverage of water and electricity supply in Sabah and Sarawak will be further expanded to meet growing demands.",""],[1,"263","5","Basic Infrastructure Upgrading in Sabah and Sarawak","The provision of basic infrastructure will be intensified in Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[1,"263","6","Water Services Infrastructure Construction and Upgrade","new water services infrastructure such as dams, off-river storage, water treatment plants and sewage treatment plants will be constructed, and existing ones upgraded.",""],[1,"263","6","Non-Revenue Water Reduction Programme","allocations will be provided for Non-Revenue Water Reduction Programme in the two states.",""],[1,"269","10","Rural Infrastructure Upgrading and Expansion in Sabah and Sarawak","The provision of basic infrastructure will be intensified in the rural and remote areas of Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[1,"269","11","Alternative Rural Water Supply Provision","Alternative rural water supply, such as tube wells, gravity feed and rainwater harvesting will be utilised.",""],[1,"269","11","Alternative Remote Area Electricity Supply","Alternative water and electricity supply will be provided in the remote areas.",""],[1,"269","11","Solar Hybrid and Mini-Hydro Microgrid Support","Meanwhile, solar hybrid and mini hydro will be installed to support micro- and pico- grids.",""]],"300":[[1,"254","8","Special Pathways to Public Higher Education Institutions","Special pathways to public higher education institutions (HEIs) are provided for students under four categories, namely those with special needs, from B40 households, the Orang Asli community, as well as athletes.",""]],"301":[[1,"263","7","JENDELA Broadband Infrastructure Expansion in Sabah and Sarawak","Broadband coverage in Sabah and Sarawak will be further enhanced under the Pelan Jalinan Digital Negara (JENDELA), to widen the coverage of broadband services in the effort to provide equitable digital opportunities to the population.",""],[1,"263","8","School and Rural Broadband Connectivity Expansion","Measures will be undertaken to improve broadband connectivity in schools, as well as the surrounding areas.",""],[1,"269","12","Rural Broadband Expansion","Broadband coverage in rural areas will be improved to enhance internet connectivity, thus facilitating socioeconomic activities and business expansion through the digital platform.",""],[1,"269","12","Pusat Komuniti Desa Service Hub Upgrading","Pusat Komuniti Desa (PKD) will be upgraded to be hubs for services in rural areas.",""]],"302":[[1,"265","6","Equitable Industrial Development in Sabah and Sarawak","the focus will be given on more equitable industrial development, modernising the agriculture sector, strengthening the oil and gas subsector, enhancing the services",""],[1,"265","8","Industrial Estates Infrastructure Upgrading in Sabah and Sarawak","The development of industrial estates in Sabah and Sarawak will be accelerated through better provision of infrastructure, namely roads, electricity and water supply, as well as internet connectivity.",""],[1,"265","8","National Industrialisation Roadmap Formulation","The formulation of a new national industrialisation roadmap will take into account the local strength of Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[1,"265","8","Review of Investment Incentive Mechanisms","Existing investment incentive mechanisms will be reviewed focusing on selected quality industries and addressing regional imbalance in industrial development.",""],[1,"268","2","Regional Economic Corridor Growth Promotion","efforts will be focused on leveraging regional economic corridors to play a more important role as an engine of growth",""],[1,"268","2","Sabah and Sarawak Investment Destination Promotion","concerted efforts will also be undertaken in making Sabah and Sarawak as preferred investment destinations in BIMP-EAGA by leveraging on comparative advantages in both states",""],[1,"268","3","Strengthening Regional Development Strategies","Measures will be undertaken to strengthen regional development strategies in ensuring a higher development impact.",""],[1,"268","3","Acceleration of Strategic Development Projects","SEDIA and RECODA will intensify efforts in expediting the implementation of strategic development projects.",""],[1,"268","3","Regional Investment Attraction Collaboration","SEDIA and RECODA will be actively collaborating with various agencies to create a conducive environment in attracting quality investment.",""],[1,"268","4","SEDIA Niche Sector Development and Blueprint Review","SEDIA will concentrate on six niche areas, namely oil, gas and energy, tourism, palm oil, manufacturing and logistics, agriculture, as well as education.",""],[1,"268","5","Sarawak Regional Development Area Expansion","In accelerating development in Sarawak, the SCORE area was extended beyond the central region with the establishment of the URDA, HDA and NRDA in ensuring a comprehensive development of the rural and interior areas of Sarawak.",""],[1,"268","6","Acceleration of Strategic Projects in SCORE Growth Nodes","The implementation of strategic projects in the five key growth nodes in the SCORE areas, namely Tanjung Manis, Mukah, Samalaju, Baram and Tunoh will be accelerated.",""],[1,"268","6","Infrastructure and Services Support for Economic Activities","The provision of infrastructure, facilities and services will support economic activities, which in turn will result in spillover effects to the surrounding areas.",""],[1,"268","7","Strengthened Investment Promotion and Facilitation for Sabah and Sarawak","The investment promotion and facilitation functions of the RECs and other investment promotion agencies in Sabah and Sarawak will be strengthened to promote both states as preferred investment destinations for BIMP-EAGA.",""],[1,"268","7","Local Investment Incentives and Business Environment Support","The state governments will play a proactive role in creating a conducive environment for businesses, including efforts to complement national investment incentives with local incentives.",""],[1,"268","7","Industrial Zone Infrastructure and Utility Provision","Measures will be undertaken to ensure adequate electricity and water supply, proper waste management facilities, as well as sufficient digital infrastructure and services at strategic industrial zones and growth nodes.",""],[1,"268","7","Special Fiscal and Non-Fiscal Investment Incentive Schemes","Special fiscal and non-fiscal incentive schemes to attract investment originated from BIMP-EAGA and elsewhere will be explored, particularly schemes that promote green growth and green infrastructure.",""]],"303":[[1,"265","10","MSME Digital Technology Adoption Support","MSMEs will be encouraged to adopt digital technologies in production and business services.",""],[1,"265","10","MSME Digitalisation Training, Mentoring, and Awareness Programme","Training, mentoring and awareness programmes will be implemented for MSMEs in enhancing readiness to digitalise and compete in the local and global market.",""],[1,"265","10","Local MSME One-Stop Support Centres","One-stop centres with connections to other parts of the country will be established to assist local MSMEs to have better access to funding, facilities and stewardship.",""],[1,"265","10","eRezeki and eUsahawan Programme Expansion","The eRezeki and eUsahawan programmes will be improved and expanded to increase the skills and opportunities of the rakyat in Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[1,"265","10","National Digital Economy and 4IR Council Support","The National Digital Economy and 4IR Council, which was established in 2020 will also be leveraged in solving digitalisation issues in Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[1,"268","1","MSME Technology and Digitalisation Adoption Support","MSMEs will be encouraged to increase the sales of products and services through adoption of technology and digitalisation.",""]],"304":[[1,"266","1","Sabah High-Value Agrofood and Aquaculture Development","Agricultural activities in Sabah will focus on producing high value agrofood, aquaculture, deep sea fishing and dairy produce.",""],[1,"266","1","Ranau and Keningau Vegetable and Dairy Production Expansion","Ranau and Keningau will be further developed as the main producer of vegetables and dairy products, while Kota Belud has been identified to undertake large scale paddy and fruit farming.",""],[1,"266","1","Food Production Area Upgrading for Modern Agriculture","Dedicated food production areas such as the Taman Kekal Pengeluaran Makanan (TKPM) and Zon Industri Akuakultur (ZIA) will be upgraded to encourage modern agriculture.",""],[1,"266","1","High-Tech Deep Sea Fishing Promotion","The deep sea fishing industry utilising high-tech fishing vessels will be further encouraged to leverage the availability of resources and competitive advantage.",""],[1,"266","2","Modernisation of Integrated Agricultural Development Areas","The Integrated Agricultural Development Areas of Kalaka Saribas and Samarahan in Sarawak will be transformed into modern agriculture areas.",""],[1,"266","2","Pilot Projects for Modern Agriculture","In this regard, pilot projects will be initiated.",""],[1,"266","2","Upgrade of TKPM and ZIA Facilities","The existing TKPM and ZIA will also be upgraded to encourage modern agriculture.",""],[1,"266","2","Promotion of High-Value Crop Cultivation","High value produce such as durians, pineapples and coconuts will be promoted for large scale cultivation.",""],[1,"266","2","Optimisation of Fishery Complexes for Downstream Development","the utilisation of fishery complexes in Tanjung Manis and Tanjong Bako will be optimised in supporting the development of downstream activities.",""],[1,"266","3","Smart Farming and Precision Agriculture Adoption","The utilisation of digital technology will be enhanced through the application of smart farming and precision agriculture along the production value chain.",""],[1,"266","3","Agricultural Capacity Building and Advisory Services","Capacity building and advisory services will be provided to accelerate the adoption of modern agriculture.",""],[1,"266","3","Promotion of Good Agricultural Practices","In addition, farmers will be encouraged to adopt good agricultural practices such as Malaysian Good Agricultural Practice, Malaysian Sustainable Palm Oil and Malaysian Organic for sustainable agriculture and food safety.",""],[1,"266","3","Strengthening Agricultural Research and Development Capacity","The capabilities of state agricultural departments and agencies in undertaking research and development activities will be enhanced.",""],[1,"266","3","University-Agriculture Research Collaboration","Collaboration with HEIs in the area of research will also be intensified, focusing on soil testing, production of seeds and breeds, as well as biosecurity control.",""],[1,"266","3","Federal-State Agricultural Development Coordination","Meanwhile, to facilitate the adoption of modern technologies, collaboration between the Federal and state governments of Sabah and Sarawak in implementing agricultural development will be strengthened.",""]],"305":[[1,"266","4","Sabah and Sarawak Gas Masterplans","The State Governments of Sabah and Sarawak finalised their gas masterplans in 2020.",""],[1,"266","4","National Natural Gas Roadmap","Initiatives under both plans will be taken into account in formulating the national natural gas roadmap.",""]],"306":[[1,"266","5","MSME Competitiveness Enhancement in Resource-Based Manufacturing","the capabilities and competitiveness of MSMEs in resource- based manufacturing activity will be enhanced with greater adoption of automation and technology",""],[1,"266","5","Industrial Park Promotion and Maintenance Measures","several measures will be undertaken by intensifying promotion activities and improving the maintenance of the industrial parks",""]],"307":[[1,"267","4","Niche Programme Development in Private Higher Education Institutions","Private HEIs in Sabah and Sarawak will be encouraged to introduce niche programmes, such as robotics and artificial intelligence, to attract local and international students.",""],[1,"267","4","Private HEI-Enterprise Skills Partnership Programme","In addition, collaboration between private HEIs and enterprises as strategic partners will be encouraged to provide students with industry skillsets through coaching and mentoring, as well as on-job-training.",""],[1,"267","6","Construction Skills Reskilling and Accreditation Programme","Akademi Binaan Malaysia in Sabah and Sarawak will conduct reskilling, upskilling and accreditation programmes to produce qualified local talent.",""],[1,"273","2","Institution-Industry Lab Upgrade Programme","Existing laboratories and workshops at the institutions will be upgraded as the Institution-Industry Lab (IIL) through shared ownership between selected TVET institutions and industries.",""]],"308":[[1,"270","5","Rural Entrepreneur Digitalisation and Online Market Access Programme","Access to online business platforms will be capitalised to elevate competitiveness and capacity of rural entrepreneurs of Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[1,"270","5","Pusat Internet Optimisation for Rural Digitalisation","The 133 Pusat Internet in Sabah and 138 in Sarawak, comprising of PKD, Pusat Internet Desa and Pusat Internet, will be optimised as platforms to promote digitalisation among rural entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"270","5","DesaMall@KPLB Expansion for Rural E-Commerce","The DesaMall@KPLB programme will be expanded to assist rural entrepreneurs in migrating from traditional business methods to online businesses for better market access.",""]],"309":[[1,"270","6","Urban Development Acceleration Measures","measures to accelerate urban development will focus on improving the development potential of cities, upgrading urban services and enhancing liveability.",""],[1,"270","7","CCMP Action Plan Implementation for Kota Kinabalu and Kuching","Focus will be given to improve the competitiveness of major cities through the implementation of action plans identified under the CCMP for Kota Kinabalu and Kuching.",""],[1,"270","7","Urban Waterfront Tourism and Economic Activity Promotion","The uniqueness of these two cities with a vibrant waterfront area will be leveraged to promote tourism and economic activities.",""],[1,"270","7","Industrial Park Optimization for Job Creation","In addition, measures to increase job opportunities will focus on optimising existing industrial parks, namely the Kota Kinabalu Industrial Park, the Sama Jaya Free Industrial Zone and Samalaju Industrial Park.",""],[1,"270","7","Urban Ecosystem Improvement for Liveability","Meanwhile, the efficiency of the urban ecosystem will be enhanced to promote liveability in the major cities through better access to digital infrastructure, affordable housing and entrepreneurial opportunities.",""],[1,"270","8","Secondary City Economic Development and Investment Attraction Initiative","Efforts to increase the potential of cities in other division areas in the states will focus on enhancing economic activities to spur development.",""],[1,"270","8","City Supporting Ecosystem Coordination Mechanism","efforts to improve supporting ecosystem in these areas will also be given emphasis through collaboration and coordination between Federal and state agencies.",""]],"310":[[1,"271","2","Green City Action Plan Implementation","Measures will be undertaken to enhance the liveability of cities and ecological resilience of Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[1,"271","2","Greenhouse Gas Inventory and Climate Resilience Assessment","Under the GCAP initiative, key cities and towns will be identified for greenhouse gas emission inventory and climate resilience assessment.",""],[1,"271","2","Green Financing and Incentive Scheme for Green Infrastructure","The green financing mechanism will be put in place and innovative incentive schemes will be introduced to promote investment in green infrastructure including energy, transport and housing.",""],[1,"271","2","Renewable Energy and Low-Carbon Infrastructure Expansion","Efforts will be intensified to build or install more renewable energy equipment such as solar photovoltaic, energy-efficient street lighting, low carbon buildings and integrated solid waste management facilities.",""],[1,"271","2","Ecological Fiscal Transfers and Payments for Ecosystem Services","Ecological fiscal transfer measures and payments for ecosystem services will be implemented to ensure the sustainability of the ecosystem services.",""],[1,"271","2","Eco-School Programme Expansion","To instil sustainability awareness among the younger generation, eco-school programmes will be extended across the schools in Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[1,"271","3","Green Growth Promotion and Green Initiatives Acceleration","Green growth will be promoted by accelerating green initiatives and conserving natural capital.",""],[1,"271","4","Green Initiatives Acceleration","Implementation of green initiatives will be accelerated to ensure sustainable, responsible and resilient socioeconomic growth.",""],[1,"271","4","Circular Economy Adoption by Businesses","Businesses will be encouraged to implement the circular economy along their value chain, particularly using recycled materials to produce green products.",""],[1,"271","4","Private Sector Energy Efficiency and Renewable Energy Initiative","The private sector will also be encouraged to implement energy efficiency initiatives in their operation and premises, as well as intensify development and utilisation of renewable energy sources, including hydrogen.",""],[1,"271","4","Government Green Procurement in Sabah and Sarawak","Government green procurement initiative will also be implemented in Sabah and Sarawak as a catalyst in expanding the green market, including the green construction sector.",""],[1,"271","5","Extended Producer Responsibility and Polluter-Pays Promotion","the adoption of the extended producer responsibility approach, user-pay and polluter-pay principles, as well as self-regulation among industries will be further promoted",""],[1,"271","5","Waste Separation and 3R Intensification","Waste separation at source and the reduce, reuse and recycle (3R) initiatives will also be intensified",""],[1,"271","5","Green Financing and Economic Incentives for Business Greening","Economic instruments, environmentally motivated subsidies and the existing green financing incentives will be leveraged to support businesses in greening their activities",""]],"311":[[1,"271","6","Intensified Ecosystem Conservation Programmes","conservation programmes on the terrestrial, inland water, coastal and marine ecosystems will be intensified",""],[1,"271","6","Species Conservation and Sustainable Fisheries Management Programme","the implementation of species conservation programmes including sustainable fisheries management, as well as enforcement activities will be strengthened",""],[1,"271","6","Sustainable Mining Rating Scheme","mining operators will also be encouraged to subscribe to a sustainability rating in ensuring sustainable mining practices",""],[1,"271","7","Community Participation in Protected Area Management","Local communities' participation in protecting and managing protected areas sustainably will be elevated to improve their livelihood.",""],[1,"271","7","Access and Benefit-Sharing Education and Awareness Programme","Education and awareness programmes on access and sharing of benefits will be enhanced.",""],[1,"271","7","Enforcement of the Access to Biological Resources and Benefit Sharing Act 2017","provision of the Access to Biological Resources and Benefit Sharing Act 2017 will be enforced through enactments and ordinances at the state level.",""],[1,"271","7","Payment for Ecosystem Services and Carbon Offset Exploration","payment for ecosystem services including carbon offset will be explored.",""]],"312":[[1,"272","1","Social Services Access and Public Safety Improvement Initiatives","efforts will concentrate on improving access to education, healthcare services and housing as well as enhancing security and public safety.",""],[1,"272","2","Education and Training Access Improvement","efforts will focus on improving access to education and training, as well as enhancing collaboration with industry.",""],[1,"272","2","Industry-Education Collaboration Enhancement","efforts will focus on improving access to education and training, as well as enhancing collaboration with industry.",""],[1,"272","10","Higher Education Access and Infrastructure Improvement in Sabah and Sarawak","Infrastructure, equipment and academic programmes in the existing HEIs in Sabah and Sarawak will be improved according to local needs.",""]],"313":[[1,"274","6","NCR Land Development Facilitation","Efforts will also be undertaken to increase employability and promote entrepreneurship as well as facilitate the development of NCR land.",""],[1,"275","1","NCR Land Development for Income Generation","The development of NCR land will be facilitated to provide income- generating opportunities, particularly in undertaking agriculture activities on a large scale.",""],[1,"275","4","NCR Land Development Acceleration Programme","Ongoing programmes in facilitating the development of NCR land will be accelerated in ensuring the Anak Negeri Sabah and Bumiputera Sarawak have access to opportunities for generating higher incomes.",""],[1,"275","4","NCR Land Surveying and Mapping Acceleration","Hence, the surveying and mapping exercise of the NCR land will be accelerated to facilitate the state governments in gazetting and granting land titles.",""],[1,"275","4","Integrated NCR Land Development Collaboration Mechanism","Collaboration between the state governments, landowners and investors will be strengthened to ensure successful development of the NCR land through an integrated land development approach.",""]],"314":[[1,"276","8","Enhancement of Islamic Training Programmes at Institut Pengajian Islam dan Dakwah Sabah","The role of Institut Pengajian Islam dan Dakwah Sabah in providing more comprehensive Islamic training programmes will be enhanced by upgrading its physical infrastructure.",""],[1,"276","8","Upgrading of Institut Kemahiran Islam Malaysia Sarawak","The ongoing upgrading of Institut Kemahiran Islam Malaysia Sarawak is expected to be completed in 2023.",""]],"315":[[1,"301","1","Circular Economy Transition Initiatives","Among initiatives that will be implemented to expedite this transition include creating an enabling ecosystem, improving design and processes of products and services, extending producer responsibility and strengthening waste management.",""],[1,"301","2","Circular Economy Enabling Framework","an enabling framework will be developed as guidance for the economic sectors to shift to the circular economy.",""],[1,"301","2","Circular Economy Blueprint for Waste and Agricommodities","A blueprint for the circular economy related to solid waste, plastics, scheduled waste and agricommodities will also be introduced to deliver better system-wide economic and environmental outcomes.",""],[1,"301","2","Circular Economy Policy and Instrument Reform","Relevant policies, legislation and economic instruments will be developed to facilitate the transition to the circular economy.",""],[1,"301","2","Circular Economy R&D and Smart Partnership Initiative","Meanwhile, R&D&C&I and smart partnership among stakeholders will be intensified to boost the implementation of the circular economy.",""],[1,"301","3","Sustainable Product Design and Green Labelling Promotion","Therefore, businesses will be encouraged to design products that are more durable, repairable, reusable and recyclable as well as use recycled materials as inputs.",""],[1,"301","3","Green Labelling Uptake Promotion","They will also be encouraged to uptake recognised green labelling.",""],[1,"301","4","Eco-Design Standards Review","reviewed to incorporate eco-design requirements, including the use of recycled materials.",""],[1,"301","4","Green Product and Service Financing Incentives","economic instruments, such as GTFS, GITA and GITE will be leveraged to support businesses in producing green products and services.",""],[1,"301","4","Sharing Economy Model Promotion","More sharing economy models, including product-as-a- service will be introduced to encourage sharing the use of products and services as well as facilities.",""],[1,"301","5","Green Technology Adoption and Circular Economy Measures","Adoption of green technology in industries will result in more efficient resource-use and production cost savings.",""],[1,"302","1","Circular Economy Transition","The circular economy will be achieved through improved product design and manufacturing, innovative sharing economy models2 and enhanced recycling mechanisms.",""]],"316":[[1,"301","6","Extended Producer Responsibility Regulation for E-Waste","In this regard, a new regulation on household electrical and electronic waste (e-waste) will be introduced to implement the EPR for e-waste.",""],[1,"301","6","Extended Producer Responsibility Expansion for Packaging and Single-Use Plastics","The EPR approach will also be extended to cover other types and streams of waste, particularly packaging materials and single-use plastics.",""],[1,"301","6","EPR Regulatory and Monitoring Framework","Accordingly, relevant regulations, economic instruments and monitoring mechanisms will be put in place to enable producers and retailers to implement the EPR for other type of waste.",""],[1,"301","6","Producer Take-Back and Polluter-Pays Support System","Implementation of EPR will be supported through the take-back system by producers or brand owners as well as the adoption of the user-pay and polluter-pay principles.",""]],"317":[[1,"312","4","Strengthening of the One-Stop Environment-Related Data Centre","the one stop environment-related data centre will be strengthened by improving data sharing among various stakeholders, including the private sector and CSOs to support better decision- making.",""],[1,"312","4","Greenhouse Gas Accounting Model and Database","a GHG accounting model and database will be established",""],[1,"312","4","Disaster-Related Repository Enhancement","the disaster-related repository will be enhanced.",""],[1,"312","4","Green Economic Model Development","A green economic model will be developed by leveraging the Green Economy Indicators and the System of Environmental- Economic Accounting for Malaysia to support macroeconomic planning and impact analysis.",""],[1,"312","6","SDG Indicator Data Expansion and Monitoring System","Data for SDG indicators will continue to be expanded and strengthened to monitor progress of the SDGs at the national, state and local levels.",""]],"318":[[1,"312","5","Sustainable Development Talent Development Initiative","Efforts will be undertaken to develop talent that possess knowledge and skills in sustainable development to advance green growth.",""],[1,"312","5","Green Skills Investment Incentive","Both the public and private sectors will be encouraged to invest in developing talent with multiple skillsets, especially in green financing and environmental economy.",""],[1,"312","5","Triple-Helix Academic Programme Collaboration","In addition, triple-helix collaboration will be encouraged to enhance academic programmes in these areas.",""],[1,"312","7","Local Sustainable Development Task Force Establishment","local authorities will be encouraged to establish a task force on sustainable development to mirror the structure at the Federal and state levels.",""],[1,"312","7","Local Authority Capacity Building for Sustainable Development","The capacity and capability of local authorities will be enhanced to enable effective planning, implementation, monitoring and evaluation of sustainable development initiatives.",""],[1,"312","7","Sustainable Development Performance Rating Enhancement","sustainable development elements in the Sistem Penarafan Bintang Pihak Berkuasa Tempatan will be further enhanced to assess the commitments and improve the performance of local authorities.",""],[1,"312","7","Sustainable Development Initiative Financing Mobilization","Local authorities will be encouraged to leverage funding from private and international entities, including matching grants to support the implementation of sustainable development initiatives.",""]],"319":[[1,"312","6","Multi-Stakeholder SDG Engagement and Collaboration Platform","Engagements and collaboration with the private sector, academicians and CSOs will be intensified to ensure there are concerted and accelerated actions by all stakeholders in achieving the 2030 Agenda.",""],[1,"312","6","Regional and International Sustainable Development Policy Dialogue","Cooperation and policy dialogues on sustainable development at the regional and international levels will also be promoted to complement national efforts in accelerating the implementation of the 2030 Agenda.",""],[1,"312","6","ASEAN Net Zero Carbon Emissions Collaboration","In addition, collaboration among ASEAN countries to achieve net zero carbon emissions will be initiated.",""]],"320":[[1,"313","1","Green Financing and Investment Scale-Up","Green financing and investments will be scaled-up to support the implementation of the clean, green and resilient development agenda.",""],[1,"313","2","SDG and ESG Integration in Economic Policy and Public Finance","These include integrating climate change and green growth into macroeconomic policies, fiscal planning, budgeting, investment management and procurement practices.",""],[1,"313","2","Green Financing for Sustainable Development Projects","The utilisation of green financing and investments will be encouraged for all sustainable and climate- friendly development projects, including projects implemented through the public-private partnerships approach and by the GLCs.",""],[1,"313","2","SDG-Aligned Investment Strategy and Performance Monitoring Framework","Targeted strategies with clear accountability to further grow the share of investments that are aligned with the 2030 Agenda will be developed.",""],[1,"313","2","SDG Performance Measurement Framework","Appropriate performance measurement framework will be put in place to monitor and evaluate the implementation of these strategies.",""],[1,"313","2","Public Sector SDG Budget Tagging System","For the public sector, this will also entail developing a budget-tagging system that is linked to the sustainable development objectives.",""]],"321":[[1,"313","3","Sustainable and Responsible Investment Roadmap","The Sustainable and Responsible Investment Roadmap for the Malaysian Capital Market will scale-up capital formation by businesses that adopt sustainable practices and provide green investment opportunities for investors.",""],[1,"313","3","Green and Sustainability Sukuk and Bonds Expansion","The Roadmap will also broaden the use of green and sustainability sukuk and bonds across various economic sectors as well as encourage the use of alternative finance to the underserved segments in the green sectors.",""],[1,"313","4","Sustainable Finance Integration and Scorecard Development","Financial institutions will be encouraged to incorporate sustainability elements into their business portfolios and processes as well as develop scorecards to support sustainable development projects.",""],[1,"313","4","Joint Committee on Climate Change and Taxonomy Support","In supporting this, the Joint Committee on Climate Change, and the climate change and principles-based taxonomy that categorises",""],[1,"313","5","Green Taxonomy for Climate-Aligned Financial Flows","economic activities based on their impact on climate change will be leveraged. This taxonomy will facilitate financial flows to activities that support the advancement of green growth.",""],[1,"313","5","International Climate Finance Networking for Financial Institutions","Financial institutions will be urged to network internationally with relevant platforms and institutions, such as the United Nations Principles for Responsible Investment.",""],[1,"313","5","Climate Risk Disclosure Adoption by Financial Institutions","These institutions are strongly encouraged to adopt recommendations of the Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosures to improve transparency in integrating climate risks for decision-making.",""],[1,"313","5","Green Project Appraisal and Sustainable Practice Capacity Building","Financial institutions will strengthen their capabilities to enable effective evaluation of green project proposals and advocate sustainable practices among clients.",""],[1,"313","6","EPF Sustainable Investment Policy and ESG-Compliant Portfolio Transition","The EPF recently launched its sustainable investment policy and announced its intention to have a fully ESG-compliant portfolio by 2030.",""],[1,"313","6","Bursa Malaysia ESG Adoption Strengthening Efforts","The Bursa Malaysia has also strengthened efforts to bring public listed companies on the ESG journey.",""]],"322":[[1,"313","7","Transparency and Accountability Enhancement for Climate Financing","appropriate mechanisms to enhance transparency, accountability and investment worthiness will be strengthened to leverage bilateral and multilateral financing in addressing the domestic financing gaps.",""],[1,"313","7","Centralised Climate Finance Coordination Mechanism","A centralised mechanism will also be established to coordinate and mobilise bilateral and multilateral financing, leverage private sector investments, enhance coordination across sectors, and improve the effectiveness of fund usage.",""],[1,"314","1","Post-Disaster Liability Management","Post-disaster liabilities will be managed effectively to reduce the financial burden on the government.",""],[1,"314","1","Alternative Disaster Relief Financing Mobilization","Meanwhile, additional financial resources will be sourced from alternative disaster relief funds contributed by the private sector, CSOs and individuals.",""],[1,"314","1","Disaster Risk Transfer Feasibility Study","A study will be undertaken to assess the feasibility of a flexible social protection system through disaster risk transfer26 mechanisms, including disaster risk insurance.",""],[1,"314","1","Climate-Resilient Financing and Investment Scale-Up","In addition, climate resilient and environment-friendly financing and investment will be scaled-up to support disaster risk reduction efforts.",""]],"323":[[1,"314","9","Evidence-Based Inclusive Policy-Making Approach","An inclusive approach to policy-making that combines insights from psychology, cognitive science and social science with empirically tested results to discover how people actually make choices.",""],[1,"315","1","Clean, Green and Resilient Development Agenda","The Twelfth Plan will advance green growth by implementing the clean, green and resilient development agenda through the whole-of-nation approach.",""],[1,"315","1","Climate and Disaster Resilience Enhancement","The key strategies will include increasing resilience against climate change and disasters, embracing the circular economy, mainstreaming SDGs and ESG principles in investment decision, sharing responsibilities in moving towards a low-carbon nation, implementing evidence-based and risk-informed strategies, ensuring equitable benefit sharing and steering behavioural changes.",""],[1,"315","1","Circular Economy Transition","The key strategies will include increasing resilience against climate change and disasters, embracing the circular economy, mainstreaming SDGs and ESG principles in investment decision, sharing responsibilities in moving towards a low-carbon nation, implementing evidence-based and risk-informed strategies, ensuring equitable benefit sharing and steering behavioural changes.",""],[1,"315","1","SDG and ESG Mainstreaming in Investment Decisions","The key strategies will include increasing resilience against climate change and disasters, embracing the circular economy, mainstreaming SDGs and ESG principles in investment decision, sharing responsibilities in moving towards a low-carbon nation, implementing evidence-based and risk-informed strategies, ensuring equitable benefit sharing and steering behavioural changes.",""],[1,"315","1","Low-Carbon Nation Transition","The key strategies will include increasing resilience against climate change and disasters, embracing the circular economy, mainstreaming SDGs and ESG principles in investment decision, sharing responsibilities in moving towards a low-carbon nation, implementing evidence-based and risk-informed strategies, ensuring equitable benefit sharing and steering behavioural changes.",""]],"324":[[1,"319","1","River Management and Coastal Protection Initiatives","a number of physical and non-physical initiatives were implemented to strengthen river management and coastal protection.",""],[1,"337","3","Nature-Based Water Management and Eco-Friendly Construction Policy","Application of nature-based technology in addressing various water-related issues, such as water pollution, floods and droughts will be promoted.",""],[1,"337","3","Constructed Wetlands for Wastewater Treatment","Constructed wetlands (CWs) with appropriate bio-engineering techniques will be built to treat wastewater and water collected in retention ponds as well as improve effluent quality before being released to the river system, as described in Box 9-2.",""],[1,"337","3","Natural Flood Management in Riverine and Coastal Areas","Natural flood management techniques that emulate the regulating function of wetlands will also be adopted in project development planning and design along riverine and coastal areas.",""],[1,"337","4","Constructed Wetlands for Wastewater Treatment","In CWs, specific vegetation will be planted for different treatment purposes, such as for the removal of pollutants, purification of water, control of erosion, filtration of sediments and reduction of water flow.",""],[1,"338","1","Circular Economy Implementation in the Water Sector","The circular economy concept will be implemented in the entire water sector value chain.",""],[1,"338","1","Water Resource Recovery Promotion Initiative","Resource recovery from water and wastewater treatment including sludge, bio-sludge, bio-effluent and biogas will be promoted to create economic opportunities and advance green growth.",""],[1,"338","1","Water Recovery Centres Development","Recovery centres will be built to manage, treat and convert sludge for safe and beneficial use.",""],[1,"338","1","Integrated Wastewater Treatment Plants in Eco-Industrial Parks","Integrated wastewater treatment plants will be built in new eco-industrial parks.",""],[1,"338","1","Promotion of Resource Recovery By-Products","Efforts will also be intensified to promote acceptance and the use of by-products from resource recovery.",""],[1,"338","2","Water-Efficient Product Promotion and Incentive Scheme","The use of water-saving equipment labelled with Water Efficient Product Labelling Scheme (WEPLS) will be scaled up in government premises as well as promoted among domestic and industrial users.",""],[1,"338","2","Green Building Water Efficiency Promotion","The green rating for buildings will be leveraged to encourage water-saving practices and water reuse in commercial premises, including hotels and shopping complexes.",""],[1,"338","3","Smart Water Management and Service Efficiency Upgrade","Smart technologies such as digital meters and sensors, geographic information systems as well as supervisory control and data acquisition system will be incorporated to improve water management and services efficiency.",""],[1,"338","3","Closed-Loop Water Cycle Promotion","Smart technologies will also be utilised to promote the closed-loop water cycle concept which mitigates wastage.",""],[1,"338","3","Smart Water Services Communication Applications","In addition, smart applications will be developed to establish direct and fast communication between water services providers and consumers.",""],[1,"338","3","Pilot Water-Smart City Project","To demonstrate the benefits of smart technology in the sector, a pilot water-smart city project will be implemented.",""],[1,"338","3","Smart Irrigation Modernisation Programme","In the agriculture sector, modern and automatic irrigation systems using smart technologies will be utilised to reduce wastage, improve efficiency, enable more accurate water distribution and increase productivity.",""]],"325":[[1,"343","3","Digitalisation and Advanced Technology Adoption Acceleration","the adoption and application of digital and advanced technology will be accelerated",""],[1,"344","1","Digital Skills and Talent Development","The supply of talent and skills required to drive both the digital economy and 4IR technology adoption will be increased, while R&D&C&I will be intensified.",""],[1,"344","1","Digitalisation Mainstreaming for Inclusive Development","Malaysia will also focus on mainstreaming digitalisation for inclusive development and attracting more investments to become the regional champion in the digital economy.",""],[1,"349","9","Experimental Development Research Funding Allocation","Ensuring 50% of research funding will be focused on experimental development with high commercialisation potential.",""],[1,"349","10","Research Management Unit for Priority-Aligned R&D&C&I","Ensuring R&D&C&I activities are in line with national priorities with the newly established Research Management Unit (RMU).",""],[1,"349","11","Technology Commercialisation and Transfer One-Stop Centre","Establishing a one-stop centre for technology commercialisation and transfer to scale up home-grown technologies.",""],[1,"349","12","Private Sector R&D&C&I Investment and Alternative Financing Support","Increasing investment by the private sector in R&D&C&I and access to alternative financing.",""],[1,"362","8","Industry Centre of Excellence Programme","The ICoE programme provides an avenue for industry players to establish laboratories and teaching facilities within the universities to provide students with exposure to the latest technologies.",""]],"326":[[1,"346","2","Public Sector Digitalisation Acceleration Initiative","accelerating digitalisation and implementation of the Malaysia Digital Economy Blueprint initiatives in the public sector will further enhance public service delivery.",""],[1,"351","7","Digital Technology Adoption Acceleration","Accelerate the adoption of digital technology.",""],[1,"351","15","Public Sector Digitalisation Acceleration","Accelerating digitalisation in the public sector.",""]],"327":[[1,"342","3","Education and Training Quality Enhancement","In addition, elevating the quality of education and leveraging emerging technologies will be key initiatives in improving the education and training system.",""],[1,"347","5","Rural Community Upskilling Programme","Upskill communities in the rural areas.",""],[1,"349","13","Endowment Fund for Education Financing","Establishing an endowment fund to source funds from industry, matching grants, crowdfunding and waqf.",""],[1,"360","7","School Administration Decentralization and Coaching Support","Administration of schools was further decentralised to improve the quality of delivery and governance.",""],[1,"360","12","SISC+ Teacher Coaching Programme","SISC+ is responsible to coach teachers to ensure dimensions of curriculum, assessment and pedagogy are aligned.",""],[1,"360","13","School Leadership Coaching under SIPartner+","SIPartner+ is responsible to coach the school leadership team on effective school administration and management.",""],[1,"361","2","Work-Based Higher Education and Virtual Learning Programmes","Measures were also undertaken to enhance access to quality higher education by introducing diverse learning and teaching approaches.",""],[1,"361","3","MOOC Credit Transfer in Public Universities","Seven public universities agreed to offer MOOCs with credit transfer.",""],[1,"365","13","Early Childhood Education Programmes","20 Education programmes involving preschools for children aged 4+ to 5+ years old and daycare centres for younger children.",""],[1,"366","9","Education Quality Enhancement Initiative","Emphasis will be given in promoting equitable CE and labour participation, strengthening the labour market support system, elevating the quality of education, as well as leveraging emerging technologies.",""]],"328":[[1,"356","9","Labour Law Review","Review Labour Laws: Employment Act 1955, Trade Union Act 1959 and Industrial Relations Act 1967",""],[1,"359","3","Labour Law Amendment Package","The Employment Act 1955 [Act 265] and Trade Union Act 1959 [Act 262] are being amended in line with recent developments in the labour market and to adhere to international labour standards.",""],[1,"369","12","PLWS Method Harmonization and Self-Assessment Framework","Measures will be undertaken to reconcile different methods of calculating PLWS to allow self-assessment by employers.",""],[1,"369","12","PLWS Monitoring Indicators","In addition, new indicators, which measure the linkage between profit, wage and productivity, will be introduced to monitor the effectiveness of this system.",""],[1,"369","13","Guidelines for Worker Welfare and Pay Equity in Firms","For this purpose, guidelines will be developed and disseminated to firms especially micro, small and medium enterprises (MSMEs).",""],[1,"369","13","Employer Work System Reorganisation Support","The guidelines will facilitate employers to reorganise their work systems to improve CE.",""],[1,"369","14","Employee Ownership Trust Model","Firms will also be encouraged to adopt new models for better distribution of profits.",""],[1,"370","1","Employee Ownership Sharing Models","sharing of firms based on a minimum number of employees will be introduced.",""],[1,"370","2","Trade Union Membership Expansion","Efforts to increase membership in trade union will be intensified to enable stronger bargaining power in wage negotiations.",""],[1,"370","2","Co-determination Framework for Worker Representation","Co-determination approach will be introduced to allow worker representatives at the decision-making level.",""],[1,"370","3","National Wage Index Enhancement and Expansion","Continuous efforts to provide wage benchmarking will be undertaken by enhancing NWI.",""],[1,"370","9","Strengthened Labour Rights and Anti-Trafficking Enforcement","Efforts will continue to be undertaken to ensure employers in all economic sectors protect the welfare of the workers and comply with the international obligations related to labour.",""],[1,"370","9","Enhanced Enforcement of Worker Housing Standards","Enforcement under the Employees' Minimum Standard of Housing, Accommodations and Amenities Act 1990 [Act 446] will be enhanced to ensure employers provide safe and suitable accommodation to the workers.",""]],"329":[[1,"322","8","Electricity Bill Rebate Programme","The electricity bill rebate programme was implemented to ease the burden of the rakyat.",""]],"330":[[1,"370","12","Labour Market Information Infrastructure Strengthening","Systems to support labour market will be strengthened by enhancing labour market information infrastructure and promoting responsive workforce training.",""],[1,"371","1","Labour Market Data Framework and Analytics Platform","a labour market data framework will be developed to guide planning, development and implementation of labour market policies and initiatives.",""],[1,"372","2","Enhanced Employment Services Portal","The employment services portal will be enhanced to enable redistribution of the workforce disrupted by the COVID-19 pandemic besides redeployment of displaced workers due to automation.",""]],"331":[[1,"371","12","National Employment Council Coordination Mechanism","initiatives by various stakeholders will be coordinated by the newly established National Employment Council (NEC) chaired by the Prime Minister.",""],[1,"372","1","Employment Creation and Skills Mismatch Implementation Oversight","will oversee the implementation of strategies in creating 500,000 employment opportunities by the end of 2021 as well as in addressing issues related to skills mismatch in the labour market.",""]],"332":[[1,"370","12","Labour Law Compliance Enforcement","Measures will also be undertaken to introduce social protection for gig workers and increase compliance with labour laws and regulations.",""],[1,"372","6","Labour Law Compliance Capacity and Collaboration Strengthening","The capacity of and collaboration among employers, employees and enforcement officers will be strengthened to promote shared responsibility in complying with labour laws and regulations.",""],[1,"372","6","Dedicated Labour Training Hub Upgrade","An existing facility will be upgraded as a dedicated training hub for learning, knowledge sharing, and capacity building for the employers, employees and enforcement officers.",""]],"333":[[1,"370","11","Malaysian Diaspora Talent Mobilization Mechanism","A mechanism to leverage on Malaysian diaspora expertise will be devised.",""],[1,"370","11","Returning Expert Programme Enhancement","The Returning Expert Programme (REP) will be enhanced to make it compulsory for all Malaysians who are working, are going to and are coming back to report to the government.",""],[1,"370","11","Malaysian Diaspora Database Development","A comprehensive database for the Malaysian diaspora will be established to better utilise available talent for the national interest.",""],[2,"370","11","Malaysian Diaspora Talent Mobilization Mechanism","A mechanism to leverage on Malaysian diaspora expertise will be devised.",""],[2,"370","11","Returning Expert Programme Enhancement","The Returning Expert Programme (REP) will be enhanced to make it compulsory for all Malaysians who are working, are going to and are coming back to report to the government.",""],[2,"370","11","Malaysian Diaspora Database Development","A comprehensive database for the Malaysian diaspora will be established to better utilise available talent for the national interest.",""]],"334":[[1,"373","3","Extension of Compulsory Schooling to 11 Years","Compulsory schooling will be extended from six to 11 years by making secondary education compulsory for all Malaysian citizens.",""],[1,"373","6","Student Tracking System Development","A student tracking system from preschool to upper secondary levels will be developed to monitor the mobility of students throughout the school system.",""],[1,"373","6","Student Support Programmes for At-Risk Learners","In addition, student support programmes such as parental and community involvement for poor students and students at risk will be enhanced to ensure students remain in the school system.",""],[1,"373","6","Social and Emotional Support for Students","In this regard, focus will be given in providing social and emotional support for students as well as assisting those with learning difficulties, in order to build an inclusive school environment.",""],[1,"377","1","School Re-enrolment and Zero Dropout Initiative","At the same time, getting children back to school is also important to ensure zero dropout.",""]],"335":[[1,"373","4","Inquiry-Based Teacher Training Programmes","Two teacher training programmes in inquiry-based education, namely Inquiry-Based Science Education (IBSE) and Inquiry-Based Mathematics Education (IBME) will be rolled out to improve teaching and learning approaches.",""],[1,"373","4","STEM Curriculum Modernisation with Digital Technologies","In addition, new and advanced STEM curriculum embedded with digital technologies will be introduced.",""],[1,"373","4","STEM For All School-Industry Linkage Programme","The STEM For All programme will be further promoted by facilitating linkages between schools and industries.",""],[1,"373","4","STEM Per Capita Grant Revision","The per capita grant for subjects under the STEM programme will be revised to provide adequate materials for students to conduct science experiments.",""],[1,"373","4","Science Laboratory Upgrading Programme","The science labs will be upgraded to ensure teaching and learning processes include hands-on science activities, which will be made compulsory.",""],[1,"377","2","RBT Workshop Digital Equipment Upgrade","RBT workshops will be equipped with the required equipment including portable computers and robotics components.",""],[1,"377","2","Hands-on RBT Learning Enhancement","Hands-on activities will be emphasised to nurture creativity and innovative learning among students in carrying out projects and PBS.",""]],"336":[[1,"374","10","HEI Infrastructure and Equipment Upgrading Programme","Various measures will be undertaken to upgrade outdated and unsafe infrastructure and equipment to ensure a conducive environment in HEIs.",""],[1,"377","5","Smart Campus Digital Transformation Initiative","All on-campus activities will also be geared towards creating a smart campus environment which include smart classrooms and labs, interactive learning and teaching using augmented reality (AR) and virtual reality (VR) technologies as well as digital student administration.",""],[1,"377","5","Higher Education Resource Sharing and Co-creation Review","In addition, the usage of learning spaces, including laboratories within HEIs, will be reviewed to promote sharing of resources and co-creation across disciplines and institutions through digital means.",""]],"337":[[1,"373","1","TVET Programme Enhancement and Industry Collaboration","TVET programmes enhanced while industry collaboration and enculturation of LLL strengthened.",""],[1,"375","3","Expansion of Centres of Excellence and Centres of Technology","The Centres of Excellence and Centres of Technology will be expanded to spur innovation and knowledge creation as well as enhance technical skills among students.",""],[1,"375","3","Teaching Factory Rollout for TVET Institutions","the Teaching Factory model that provides real production or manufacturing environment will be rolled out to more TVET institutions to enable students to use industry equipment in campuses.",""],[1,"375","3","Industry Exposure and Experience Linkages for TVET Students","Industry within the proximity of TVET institutions will be leveraged to provide students with better exposure to the latest technology as well as gain industrial experience.",""],[1,"377","6","Technology-Enhanced TVET Pedagogy","The use of emerging technologies such as VR, AR and AI will be leveraged to complement hands-on teaching activities, research and development conducted in laboratories and workshops.",""],[1,"377","6","TVET Curriculum Integration of Emerging Technologies","Pedagogies that embed these technologies will be incorporated in TVET curriculum.",""],[1,"377","6","TVET-Industry Collaboration Expansion","Meanwhile, collaboration between TVET institutions and industry will be intensified to provide more opportunities for instructors and students to apply latest technologies as well as experience actual industry operations and challenges.",""],[1,"398","5","Continuous Professional Development for TVET Instructors in Digital Fields","The Continuous Professional Development programmes will be expanded for TVET instructors to obtain professional certificates in digital-related fields.",""],[1,"398","5","Public-Private Partnerships for TVET Industrial Training","Public-private partnerships, including through the teaching factory approach will be encouraged to provide industrial training on the latest technology.",""]],"338":[[1,"375","8","Enterprise Data Warehouse and Analytics Platform","An enterprise data warehouse as well as a data analytics platform will be established to enable data sharing, support reporting and decision-making across ministries and agencies.",""],[1,"375","8","Private Education Student Data Sharing Initiative","At the same time, private education providers will be encouraged to share data on student enrolment status.",""]],"339":[[1,"378","7","TVET Promotion and Image Enhancement Initiative","Concerted efforts will be undertaken to promote TVET as a preferred choice for students.",""],[1,"378","7","TVET Buddy Programme","the Buddy Programme which leverages successful TVET alumni will be introduced to motivate and guide TVET students and graduates in career, education and business.",""],[1,"378","8","National TVET Brand Introduction","A single TVET brand representing both public and private TVET providers will be introduced.",""],[1,"396","3","Sharing Economy-TVET Training Partnerships","Partnerships between sharing economy players and TVET institutions will be developed to provide training programmes for the rural population",""]],"340":[[1,"396","5","Cyber Security Awareness and Training Initiative","This will include enhancing cyber security awareness initiatives through extensive promotional activities during the cyber security month, develop user guidelines for online and digital applications as well as increase training of the workforce on cyber security through a people-private-public partnership.",""],[1,"396","5","Digital Platform User Guidelines Development","This will include enhancing cyber security awareness initiatives through extensive promotional activities during the cyber security month, develop user guidelines for online and digital applications as well as increase training of the workforce on cyber security through a people-private-public partnership.",""],[1,"396","5","Internet Use Module in School Curriculum","In addition, the school curriculum will incorporate a module on the correct and acceptable ways to use the internet.",""],[1,"398","2","Cyber Security Capacity Strengthening Programme","Expertise in cyber security will be strengthened to ensure a trusted, secure and reliable digital ecosystem.",""],[1,"398","2","Local Cyber Security Talent Development Initiative","More local talent will be developed to reduce dependency on foreign cyber security experts.",""],[1,"398","2","Public-Private Cyber Security Collaboration Initiative","Collaborative efforts between the public and private sectors will be intensified to develop knowledge and skills in cyber security.",""]],"341":[[1,"393","2","eCommerce Trade Acceleration","Measures will be undertaken to streamline digital governance, accelerate trade through eCommerce, expand the sharing economy and strengthen cyber security.",""],[1,"395","7","National eCommerce Strategic Roadmap 2.0 Implementation","The National eCommerce Strategic Roadmap 2.0, 2021-2025 will be implemented to spur eCommerce activities.",""],[1,"395","7","National e-Invoicing Framework Development","A national e-Invoicing framework will also be developed to enable trade partners to seamlessly transact using digital mechanisms, particularly in the export of digital products and services.",""],[1,"395","8","Integrated One-Stop Centre Support for MSME eCommerce","Local MSMEs will be encouraged to increase eCommerce trading through integration of existing one-stop centres to enable better access to funding, facilities and stewardship.",""],[1,"395","8","Digital Business and Cross-Border Trade Coordination","The centre will also coordinate intervention related to digital businesses and cross border trading to encourage local businesses in penetrating the global market.",""],[1,"395","8","Regional Cooperation for Cross-Border Data Flow","Additionally, regional collaboration and cooperation will be leveraged to encourage seamless cross border data flow, without compromising the sovereignty and security of the data.",""],[1,"400","2","eCommerce Expansion for Vulnerable Groups","eCommerce activities will be expanded to scale up digital opportunities for vulnerable groups to exploit digital platforms.",""]],"342":[[1,"393","2","Sharing Economy Expansion","Measures will be undertaken to streamline digital governance, accelerate trade through eCommerce, expand the sharing economy and strengthen cyber security.",""],[1,"395","6","Sharing Economy Regulatory Study","A study will be undertaken to recommend a regulatory framework in providing a conducive ecosystem for the development of the sharing economy including the gig economy.",""],[1,"396","1","Sharing Economy Standards Adoption and Accreditation","To address these challenges and accelerate growth of the sharing economy, standards based on ISO International Workshop Agreement: Guiding principles and framework for the sharing economy (ISO-IWA 27:2017) will be adopted.",""],[1,"396","1","Local Sharing Economy Platform Accreditation Support","In addition, local platforms will be facilitated to be accredited with international sharing economy industry standards and platform certifications, for example ISO TC 324 on Sharing Economy and Fairwork Certification.",""],[1,"396","2","Interregional Sharing Economy Collaboration and Cross-Border Partnerships","The growth of the sharing economy will be further expedited by fostering interregional collaboration and cooperation through cross border partnerships.",""],[1,"396","2","International Knowledge Exchange on Sharing Economy Regulation and Standards","Partnerships with international agencies will also be established for the exchange of knowledge and best practices, especially on regulations and standards.",""],[1,"396","2","Global Expansion Support for Local Sharing Platforms","Local sharing platforms will also be encouraged to go global and attract foreign investment.",""],[1,"396","3","Sharing Economy Awareness and Participation Campaign","efforts to increase awareness and participation of the rakyat in the sharing economy will be intensified",""],[1,"396","3","Industry Adoption of Sharing Economy Models","Industries including tourism, transportation and manufacturing will also be encouraged to adopt and leverage sharing economy models to improve productivity and competitiveness",""],[1,"396","3","Sharing Economy and Gig Economy Promotion Initiatives","Initiatives will also be implemented to promote sharing economy activities, including the gig economy among local communities to supplement their incomes",""],[1,"400","4","Sharing Economy Promotion Initiatives","Several initiatives will be undertaken to facilitate the growth of this economy, including developing standards, setting up new platforms and fostering cross border activities.",""],[1,"400","4","Sharing Economy Awareness Programmes","Awareness programmes will be implemented to further promote participation in the sharing economy, especially among the vulnerable groups.",""]],"343":[[1,"406","10","Intelligent Grid Management System","Intelligent grid management to monitor assets and ensure cost-effective operations",""],[1,"406","10","Advanced Battery Development for Energy Storage and Electric Vehicles","Advanced batteries for energy storage and electric vehicles",""]],"344":[[1,"424","7","Preventive Road and Bridge Maintenance Programme","Preventive maintenance approach will be adopted to extend the lifespan of roads and bridges.",""],[1,"426","2","Weigh-in-Motion Enforcement System","The Weigh-in-Motion (WIM) system will be used to improve enforcement of overloaded movers.",""]],"345":[[1,"425","5","National Warehouse Regulatory Framework","Concerted efforts will be undertaken to improve coordination among stakeholders, enhance enforcement and develop a national regulatory framework for warehouses.",""],[1,"425","6","Centralised Logistics Hub Planning and Development","the planning and development of logistics hub will be centralised at the Federal Government.",""],[1,"426","3","National Warehouse Regulation Development","A national warehouse regulation will be developed to ensure uniformity in warehouse development.",""],[1,"426","3","Warehouse Siting and Approval Process Improvement","In addition, suitable locations will be identified for the development of warehouses, approval processes will be improved and a national warehouse inventory website will be developed.",""]],"346":[[1,"417","5","Marine Resource Management and Vessel Traffic Monitoring Systems","Similarly, the PTP and Johor Port have implemented the Marine Resource Management System and Vessel Traffic Monitoring and Information System since 2018.",""],[1,"425","5","Shipping Industry Governance Mechanism","A governance mechanism will be introduced for the shipping industry and highway development will be restructured to optimise benefits for both customers and industry players.",""],[1,"426","4","Maritime Economy Governance Mechanism","Efforts will be undertaken to introduce a governance mechanism to facilitate the development of the maritime economy.",""]],"347":[[1,"442","1","Civil Servant Digital Acculturation and Change Management Initiative","the digital culture will be inculcated in the early stages of a civil servant's career, while change management initiatives will be introduced to increase knowledge, skills and use of digital services.",""],[1,"442","1","Public Sector Digitalisation Strategic Plan 2021-2025","The successful implementation of initiatives under the Public Sector Digitalisation Strategic Plan 2021-2025 will further enhance digital capabilities and competencies of civil servants.",""],[1,"442","2","Civil Servant Upskilling and Reskilling Programme","The upskilling and reskilling of civil servants will be continuously undertaken to ensure they keep abreast with advancements in technology.",""],[1,"442","9","Digitalisation Initiative Expansion","digitalisation initiatives will be expanded",""],[1,"443","2","Digitalisation of Work Processes","In addition, digitalisation of work processes will further reduce red tape, save resources, enhance accountability and transparency as well as improve public service delivery.",""]],"348":[[1,"443","7","Civil Service Communication and Information Dissemination Enhancement","Communication and dissemination of information within the civil service and to the rakyat will be enhanced to ensure effective service delivery.",""],[1,"446","1","Public Participation Expansion in Decision-Making","Public participation in decision-making processes will be expanded to ensure effective and impactful policies as well as to promote participatory governance.",""],[1,"453","3","Sports for National Unity Initiative","Sports will be leveraged as a platform to build a nation with an active and united rakyat.",""],[1,"453","3","National Unity and Social Cohesion Initiative","Malaysia's diversity and noble values will also be leveraged to strengthen unity in building a prosperous and harmonious nation.",""]],"349":[[1,"444","1","Public Sector and MSME Digitalisation Acceleration","the Government will take the lead in accelerating digitalisation in the public sector and MSMEs.",""],[1,"444","1","National Digital Economy and 4IR Council","the establishment of the National Digital Economy and 4IR Council will strengthen the digital governance structure and spur growth of the digital economy.",""],[1,"444","1","Public-Private Partnerships for Malaysia Digital Economy Blueprint Implementation","More smart partnerships between the public and private sectors will also be forged to boost the implementation of the Malaysia Digital Economy Blueprint initiatives.",""],[1,"453","1","MSME Digitalisation Priority","digitalisation of MSMEs will be a priority to enhance their competitiveness and resilience.",""],[1,"453","1","Entrepreneurship and Enterprise Support Ecosystem","The creation of a conducive and holistic ecosystem to support entrepreneurs and enterprises, as well as expansion of market access and international trade opportunities will enable MSMEs to be global, export-oriented and innovation-driven players.",""],[1,"454","6","4IR Ecosystem Development Strategy","This Twelfth Plan has clearly outlined some of the strategies and initiatives to create ecosystems that are healthy for businesses and individuals to participate in this 4IR era and reap its benefits.",""]],"350":[[1,"522","20","Post-Disaster Volunteer Programme","Post-able Disaster Volunteer Programme",""]],"353":[[2,"33","2","Labour Market Realignment and Support Measures","Among the key initiatives for realigning the labour market are promoting equitable CE and labour participation, as well as strengthening labour market support.",""],[2,"33","2","Education and Training Quality Improvement Initiative","In addition, elevating the quality of education and leveraging emerging technologies will be the key initiatives to improve the education and training system.",""],[2,"33","4","Digital Economy Talent and Skills Development","The talent and skills required to drive both the digital economy and 4IR will be enhanced, while R&D&C&I will be intensified.",""],[2,"34","6","Talent Development for the Digital Economy","Focus will be given to gearing up for the 4IR, providing an enabling environment for the digital economy, intensifying R&D&C&I as well as developing the required talent.",""]],"354":[[2,"32","4","Crime Prevention and Rehabilitation Intensification","crime prevention efforts as well as rehabilitation and emergency preparedness will be intensified",""],[2,"32","4","Armed Forces and Enforcement Personnel Welfare Improvement","the welfare of the Malaysian Armed Forces and enforcement personnel will be improved",""],[2,"32","4","Security Governance Strengthening","Priority will also be given in strengthening security governance",""],[2,"32","4","National Unity and Social Cohesion Strengthening","Unity in diversity will be strengthened to maintain a harmonious society and prosperous nation",""],[2,"32","5","National Security and Unity Strengthening","Efforts in nation-building and creating a more conducive environment for economic activities as well as a safe and harmonious living for the rakyat will be emphasised by addressing issues on national defence and security as well as the unity.",""],[2,"36","1","Border Illegal Activity Curbing Plan","A holistic plan will be implemented in curbing illegal activities at the border",""],[2,"36","1","National Defence and Security Industry Policy","a new National Defence and Security Industry Policy will be introduced in ensuring a sustainable defence and security capability",""],[2,"36","1","Whole-of-Nation Crime Combatting Approach","wider usage of advanced technology as well as greater involvement by the community will facilitate the whole-of-nation approach in combatting crimes",""],[2,"36","1","Unity Programmes for Social Cohesion","building social interaction among the rakyat will be fostered through unity programmes, sports and religious activities",""],[2,"36","1","Patriotism and Volunteerism Strengthening Initiative","Patriotism and volunteerism will also be strengthened through the utilisation of digital and other media platforms in building social cohesion and fostering greater unity to ensure peace and harmony",""]],"355":[[2,"32","4","Affordable Housing Supply Expansion","The supply of quality affordable housing will be increased by improving access to affordable housing and governance as well as ensuring inclusive housing development",""],[2,"32","4","Holistic Sports Ecosystem Promotion","An active lifestyle will be promoted continuously among the rakyat by creating a holistic sports ecosystem",""]],"356":[[2,"67","1","Public Infrastructure Investment Programme","The investment will be largely in infrastructure, transport, utilities as well as the oil and gas industry.",""],[2,"67","1","East Coast Rail Link Project","Major public sector projects that will be undertaken include the ECRL, Johor Bahru-Singapore Rapid Transit System and Pan Borneo Highway.",""],[2,"67","1","Johor Bahru-Singapore Rapid Transit System","Major public sector projects that will be undertaken include the ECRL, Johor Bahru-Singapore Rapid Transit System and Pan Borneo Highway.",""],[2,"67","1","Pan Borneo Highway Project","Major public sector projects that will be undertaken include the ECRL, Johor Bahru-Singapore Rapid Transit System and Pan Borneo Highway.",""],[2,"101","3","Multimodal Logistics Network Development","Multimodality will be promoted to establish a well-integrated logistics and communication network to ensure an efficient and advanced supply chain",""]],"357":[[2,"69","8","Trade Facilitation Efficiency Improvement","Efforts to leverage gains from trade will be intensified by further improving the efficiency of trade facilitation at all entry points",""],[2,"70","1","Internationalisation and Destination Promotion Initiative","measures will be undertaken to reduce the deficit, including greater internationalisation and continued promotion of Malaysia as a preferred destination for tourism, education and healthcare",""],[2,"74","5","Export Market Expansion and Trade Facilitation Measures","The Twelfth Plan also aims to expand export markets by improving market efficiency, empowering the role of industry players and strengthening trade facilitation.",""],[2,"82","2","Export Market Expansion Initiative","expanding market exports",""],[2,"100","4","Domestic and Export Market Expansion Measures","Measures to expand domestic and export markets will focus on improving market efficiency, empowering role of industry players and strengthening trade facilitation.",""],[2,"102","4","Trade Facilitation and Export Promotion Initiative","During the Plan period, focus will be on leveraging trade agreements, and intensifying marketing and export promotion.",""],[2,"102","5","Trade Agreement Utilization Support for MSMEs and Mid-Tier Companies","MSMEs, SMPPs and mid-tier companies in all sectors of the economy will be encouraged to maximise opportunities from existing FTAs, bilateral agreements and economic partnerships with other countries.",""],[2,"102","5","Trade Advisory and Market Intelligence Services","Industry players will be provided with advisory services and comprehensive information relating to foreign market as well as market intelligence.",""],[2,"102","5","New Bilateral and Multilateral Trade Agreement Exploration","In addition, new bilateral and multilateral agreements with potential trading partners will be explored.",""],[2,"102","5","Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Ratification and Implementation","The Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership agreement, which potentially provides preferential market access to 45% of the world's population, is expected to be ratified and implemented in the Twelfth Plan period.",""],[2,"102","5","Negotiation of Potential Free Trade Agreements","Several potential FTAs are currently being negotiated and will be among the priorities to be leveraged.",""],[2,"102","6","Trade Mission Streamlining and Export Promotion","Trade missions will be further streamlined to play an effective role in intensifying marketing and promotion efforts.",""],[2,"102","7","Manufacturing Market Penetration Support","Continuous efforts will be undertaken to facilitate industry players in the manufacturing sector to penetrate into markets of major trading partners.",""],[2,"102","7","National Trade Blueprint","The National Trade Blueprint (RTPN) is designed to improve the business ecosystem and enhance the competitiveness of Malaysian exporting companies by focusing on trade regulations, logistics and market access.",""],[2,"102","7","Mid-Tier Companies Export Development Programme","the Mid-Tier Companies Development Programme and Going Export (GoEx) Programme will be enhanced to enable local companies to export high value-added products.",""],[2,"102","7","National Brand Promotion Initiative","The Malaysian brand will be promoted globally as a brand for quality products.",""],[2,"103","1","Services Export Promotion and Market Expansion","In the services sector, efforts will be undertaken to increase export of local products and services to further reduce the services trade deficit.",""],[2,"103","1","Retail and Food and Beverage Export Initiative Enhancement","Meanwhile, the various export initiatives and programmes in the retail and F&B subsectors, including the Enhanced Franchise Development Programme and the Product Transformation and Distribution Programme will be enhanced to improve their effectiveness.",""],[2,"103","1","Local Product Brand Image Uplift Measures","Measures will also be implemented to uplift the brand image of local products and services to increase international market presence.",""],[2,"103","2","Expansion and Strengthening of the Services Export Fund","The existing services export fund will be expanded to cover the business services focusing on high potential activities, while the implementation and monitoring of the fund will be strengthened.",""],[2,"108","3","Overseas Mission Export Promotion Streamlining","The function of overseas missions will be streamlined to improve coordination in terms of export promotion activities, facilitating market access and dealing with trade-related matters.",""]],"358":[[2,"70","4","Green Economy Economic Model","an economic model on the green economy will be introduced to complement existing macroeconomic planning and impact analysis",""],[2,"70","4","Socioeconomic Impact Assessment for Resource Use","the assessment of socioeconomic impact on utilisation of limited resources such as water, energy, land use and raw materials will be conducted to support the formulation of development policies",""],[2,"77","4","Green Economy Investment Prioritization","Implementing the green economy agenda by prioritising environmental, social and governance (ESG) elements in investment.",""]],"359":[[2,"94","1","Productivity Planning, Evaluation and Monitoring Mechanism Strengthening","Emphasis will be given to strengthening the planning, evaluation and monitoring mechanism, moving up the value chain and strengthening financial capability.",""],[2,"94","1","Productivity Nexus Scale-Up Initiative","In addition, measures will be undertaken to scale up successful initiatives of the Productivity Nexus.",""],[2,"94","7","Evidence-Based Policy Making and Data Sharing Framework","Evidence-based policy (EBP) making will be promoted including, establishing a user-friendly data sharing framework.",""],[2,"94","7","Programme Evaluation and Monitoring Improvement","programme evaluation and monitoring will be improved to increase the effectiveness of productivity initiatives.",""],[2,"94","8","Evidence-Based Policy Adoption Support Network","The adoption of EBP will be supported by establishing a dedicated network to facilitate research on productivity.",""],[2,"94","8","Microdata Compilation and Linked Employer-Employee Dataset Development","In addition, the compilation of microdata will be strengthened, including developing a linked employer-employee dataset, to better identify the diverse and pertinent factors which stifle enterprise- level productivity.",""],[2,"94","8","User-Friendly Data-Sharing Framework for Research","A user-friendly data-sharing framework will also be developed to improve the research ecosystem.",""],[2,"94","9","Structured Programme Evaluation Framework","A structured programme evaluation framework will be developed to assess the effectiveness of all productivity programmes, particularly in ensuring more cost-effective interventions.",""],[2,"94","9","Strengthened Monitoring and Reporting Mechanisms for Productivity Programmes","Monitoring and reporting mechanisms will be strengthened to ensure transparency and sustainability of intervention programmes.",""],[2,"94","9","Evidence-Based Productivity Programme Improvement","the findings from the evaluation and monitoring efforts will be made as references in improving existing and developing new productivity- related programmes.",""],[2,"99","3","Productivity Nexus Implementation and Scale-Up","Under the Twelfth Plan, the Productivity Nexus model will be further leveraged to drive the implementation of productivity initiatives at the sectoral level.",""],[2,"99","4","Expansion of the Productivity Nexus Model","The Productivity Nexus model, where the private sector takes the lead in formulating and implementing productivity improvement programmes at the sector level will be extended to cover more sectors.",""],[2,"99","4","Establishment of New Productivity Nexus in Construction and Logistics","At least two new Productivity Nexus will be established during the Twelfth Plan, namely construction and logistics services.",""],[2,"99","5","Productivity Nexus Programme Review and Rationalisation","A comprehensive review will be carried out to assess the effectiveness of initiatives and programmes under the nine Productivity Nexus.",""],[2,"99","5","Scaling Up Mechanism for Productivity Programmes","A comprehensive mechanism will also be established to facilitate the scaling up of these programmes.",""],[2,"107","8","Stakeholder Coordination and Collaboration Enhancement","Efforts will be undertaken to enhance the effectiveness of existing mechanisms and encourage the sharing of data and resources, which will enable stakeholders to improve quality of outcomes.",""]],"360":[[2,"96","3","Green Construction Practices Promotion","Adopting and implementing green construction practices will create value, improve resource efficiency and cost effectiveness, while reducing environmental impact.",""],[2,"96","3","Green Building Design Uptake Incentive","The industry players in this sector will be further encouraged to uptake green building design that promotes resources, energy and water efficiency as well as incorporates measures to withstand extreme weather patterns and natural disasters.",""],[2,"96","4","Circular Economy Construction Materials Promotion","Implementation of the circular economy6 concept will increase the use of sustainable, durable, biodegradable and recycled construction materials, which will contribute to lower cost and higher product value.",""],[2,"96","4","IBS, BIM, PPVC and Modular Construction Technology Promotion","Its implementation will be promoted through the application of the IBS concept and technologies, BIM, Prefabricated Prefinished Volumetric Construction (PPVC) and Modular Methods.",""],[2,"96","4","Green Procurement Initiative in Construction","The green procurement initiative in the construction sector will promote sustainable resource sourcing and increase demand for high value- added green construction materials.",""],[2,"96","4","Sustainable Construction Certification and Performance Tools Adoption","Developers will also be urged to adopt sustainable certification and performance tools, including the Sustainable Infrastructure Rating Tool (Sustainable INFRASTAR), Green Building Index (GBI) and GreenRE in ensuring environmental sustainability features are incorporated from the beginning of the design and construction phases to operation phase.",""],[2,"100","2","Government Green Procurement Guideline for Works","A short-term action plan and a guideline on government green procurement (GGP) on works will be introduced to encourage green practices in the construction sector.",""],[2,"100","2","Nationwide Green Procurement Implementation for Construction Works","A nationwide implementation of the GGP on works, including procurement of green labelled materials, will catalyse the shift towards more sustainable and green construction practices.",""],[2,"100","2","Green Certification and Performance Tools Adoption Initiative","Industry players will be urged to adopt green certification and performance tools for new development projects as well as renovation and retrofitting works.",""]],"361":[[2,"97","2","Big Data Analytics Adoption and Holistic Private Healthcare Care Enhancement","measures will be undertaken to increase the adoption of BDA as well as strengthen the provision of holistic end-to-end care in the private healthcare subsector",""],[2,"97","2","Premium Healthcare Tourism Package Promotion","exclusive high-end medical tourism packages for premium healthcare travellers will be promoted",""],[2,"97","2","Digital Innovation in Healthcare Delivery and Aged Care Solutions","Emphasis will also be given on digital innovation in healthcare delivery and solutions to ensure better quality of healthcare services including aged care services",""],[2,"97","2","Virtual Teaching and Experiential Learning Strengthening","virtual teaching and experiential learning will be further strengthened to enhance the learning experience",""],[2,"97","2","Education Technology and Learning Materials Innovation","This will drive innovation in the production of education technologies and tools, such as educational applications as well as audio and video materials",""],[2,"97","7","Private Healthcare Subsector Research Collaboration","a more coordinated research in T&CM will be conducted through private sector led collaboration with the research institutions.",""],[2,"98","7","Private Healthcare Tax Incentive Revision for Clinical Research","In the private healthcare subsector, existing tax incentives will be revised to attract involvement of more research-based organisations and increase foreign direct investment (FDI) in clinical research.",""],[2,"98","7","Pharmaceutical R&D Commercialisation for Sustainable Medicine Supply","At the same time, efforts will be undertaken to increase domestic investment in the pharmaceutical industry through commercialisation of R&D findings to secure sustainable medicine supply in Malaysia.",""],[2,"98","8","Digitalisation Support for Private Higher Education Institutions","the private HEIs, particularly MSMEs will be encouraged to utilise existing financing facilities to upgrade and modernise ICT assets as well as digitise teaching content.",""],[2,"99","2","Financial Incentives for Advanced Aged Care Technology Adoption","financial incentives will be introduced to promote adoption of advanced healthcare technology among private aged healthcare facility providers.",""],[2,"103","1","Private Healthcare Brand Promotion Campaign","For private healthcare subsector, Malaysia healthcare brand visibility will be strengthened by intensifying marketing and promotion digitally.",""],[2,"103","1","High-Value Private Healthcare Services Expansion","Moving forward the industry will shift its focus on promotion of high intensity revenue services such as fertility and oncology, as well as strengthening existing network and channels through strategic partners in identified key markets especially ASEAN and Middle East.",""],[2,"103","1","Niche Programme Development for International Students","The potential of private HEIs will be leveraged by introducing niche programmes to attract international students.",""],[2,"103","1","Private HEI-Corporate Strategic Partnership Framework","Strategic collaboration between private HEIs, and large corporations as financial partners, will be encouraged.",""],[2,"108","4","Integrated Healthcare Data System","In the healthcare services subsector, an integrated data system encompassing the public and private sector will be developed to capture and manage comprehensive information, including health registries, disease surveillance and economic activities related to healthcare.",""],[2,"108","4","Private Higher Education Resource-Sharing Collaboration","Meanwhile, collaboration among private HEIs will be promoted in sharing resources, including facility and equipment to improve the quality of teaching and learning.",""],[2,"108","4","Alternative Financing for Private Higher Education Institutions","In addition, the private HEIs will be encouraged to explore alternative financing, including waqf and crowdfunding in ensuring sustainability of the institutions.",""]],"362":[[2,"75","1","Governance and Policy Strengthening for Economic Foundations","the strengthening of the country's economic foundation will be supported by improvement in overall governance and the development of comprehensive policies and legislations",""],[2,"75","4","Business Governance and Facilitative Regulatory Reform","governance and facilitative regulations will be further enhanced to ensure the continuity and sustainability of businesses.",""],[2,"82","2","Governance and Policy Improvement Reform","improving governance and policy.",""],[2,"107","4","Governance, Policy, and Legislative Strengthening Measures","Measures will be undertaken to strengthen coordination and collaboration for more effective implementation, enhance roles and functions of institutions as well as strengthen policy and legislation.",""],[2,"109","4","Legislative Strengthening and Policy Review","efforts will be undertaken to strengthen existing legislation as well as develop and review relevant policies",""],[2,"109","4","Conducive Regulatory Environment for Sectoral Transformation","A conducive regulatory environment will facilitate sectoral transformation to move up the value chain",""],[2,"109","5","Good Regulatory Practices Adoption","Government agencies will be required to adopt Good Regulatory Practices (GRP) to increase transparency, especially in disseminating information related to changes in law and regulations.",""]],"363":[[2,"65","9","Targeted Cash Assistance and Minimum Wage Support","The increase will be supported by higher household income arising from expected stable labour market conditions in tandem with the post-COVID-19 economic recovery, higher minimum wage and cash assistance to the targeted groups.",""]],"364":[[2,"67","4","National Fourth Industrial Revolution Policy Implementation","The implementation of the National Fourth Industrial Revolution (4IR) Policy will be pivotal to boost growth across all sectors.",""]],"365":[[2,"110","4","Agricultural Legislation Modernisation and Food Safety Regulatory Reform","several rules and regulations will be amended to modernise agricultural activities, increase food safety and nutrition safety requirements as well as address issues that hinder the development of the agriculture sector.",""],[2,"110","4","Mineral Subsector SOP and Guideline Harmonisation","standard operating procedures and guidelines on best practices for the mineral subsector, particularly on the aspect of enforcement, land rehabilitation and sustainable practices will be reviewed and harmonised for implementation at state level.",""],[2,"110","4","Strategic Minerals Legislative Development and Environmental Safeguards","Related legislations will be formulated and reviewed in developing potential strategic minerals as well as minimising environmental impact from mining and quarrying activities.",""]],"366":[[2,"110","6","Review of Private Higher Education Institution Laws","Meanwhile, acts and regulations related to private HEIs will be reviewed to align with current developments in the education services subsector.",""]],"367":[[2,"127","8","International Airline Collaboration for Air Connectivity Improvement","In this regard, collaboration with international airlines will be intensified to further improve air connectivity.",""]],"368":[[2,"117","5","MyDigital Content Programme","The MyDigital Content programme has helped local animation companies to market creative products with intellectual properties (IP), such as Upin & Ipin, Ejen Ali, and Didi and Friends in penetrating local and global markets.",""],[2,"117","5","Culture, Arts and Heritage Sector Support Measures","Efforts to boost the culture, arts and heritage segment were undertaken to strengthen the contribution of this segment to support the creative industry.",""],[2,"130","2","Creative Industry Ecosystem Development and Promotion","Measures to accelerate the creative industry growth include developing a holistic ecosystem, upskilling talent to match industry needs as well as strengthening product development and promotion.",""],[2,"130","3","Creative Industry Policy and Governance Framework Review","Existing policies, mainly DIKN and institutional framework will be reviewed to chart a new direction for the industry and support the expansion of local companies into regional and global markets.",""],[2,"130","3","Digital Content Development Framework Enhancement","The framework for digital content development will be improved to increase exports, attract investments, by fully utilising local talent and strengthening public- private partnerships.",""],[2,"130","4","National Creative Industry Development Council","The National Creative Industry Development Council, led by the Ministry of Communications and Multimedia Malaysia and Ministry of Tourism, Arts and Culture (MOTAC), will be the overarching platform to drive the creative industry development.","Ministry of Communications and Multimedia Malaysia | Ministry of Tourism, Arts and Culture (MOTAC)"],[2,"130","4","Creative Industry Satellite Account Development","A satellite account for the creative industry will be developed to facilitate data collection and analysis, further augmenting evidence-based decision-making in realising the industry's potential.",""],[2,"130","4","Creative Industry Database Establishment","A comprehensive database will also be established to facilitate better planning, monitoring and assessment.",""],[2,"130","4","Creative Industry Financing Incentives","Financing mechanisms, including incentives, will be enhanced to accelerate the growth of the creative industry.",""],[2,"130","4","Public Facility Access for Creative Promotion","Existing government facilities, including those for cultural programmes under the Jabatan Kebudayaan dan Kesenian Negara (JKKN) and Istana Budaya, will be made available for private entities to optimise, in promoting and showcasing creative products and services.",""],[2,"130","4","Intellectual Property Awareness Campaign for Creative Content","Concerted efforts will be undertaken to increase awareness of the importance of IP in improving creative content production and protection as well as increasing income-generating capability.",""],[2,"130","6","Creative Industry R&D Capacity Enhancement","R&D capacity will be augmented to ensure sustainability and maximise the potential of creative goods and services.",""],[2,"130","6","Digital Platform Support for Creative Product Development and Promotion","Mobile applications and online platforms will be further leveraged to strengthen product development and promotion.",""],[2,"130","6","Digital Enhancement of Cultural and Heritage Products","Cultural and heritage products, including museums and galleries, will be enhanced by utilising technology, comprising among others, infographics and information-sharing tools, to provide a wholesome experience.",""],[2,"130","6","Digital Promotion of the Malaysian Brand","Digital platforms will be adopted to promote and export the Malaysian brand, capitalising on unique local destinations, food and culture.",""]],"369":[[2,"130","5","Creative Industry Talent Development Programme","more focus will be given to developing talent in the creative space, by aligning it with the national science, technology and innovation agenda.",""],[2,"130","5","Specialised Creative Sector Training and Learning Opportunities","Efforts will include establishing specialised training and learning opportunities that meet industry requirements.",""],[2,"130","5","Creative Talent Upskilling and Reskilling Initiative","Upskilling and reskilling of talent will be accelerated in various areas, including animation, movie-making and gaming.",""],[2,"130","5","Regional eSports and Digital Content Hub","A regional platform for eSports, digital content regional hub and the Creator's Studio will be established to meet the demand of the evolving creative content industry.",""],[2,"130","5","Continuous Updating of Talent Development Training Programmes","institutions related to talent development will be encouraged to continuously update training programmes to produce quality talent in various fields such as music, fashion and design.",""],[2,"130","5","Expansion of Creative Industry Subjects in TVET Institutions","The teaching and learning of creative industry-related subjects, particularly multimedia, digital technology and fashion design, will be expanded to more TVET institutions nationwide.",""]],"370":[[2,"131","3","Ecotourism Destination Monitoring Mechanism","Specific monitoring mechanisms will be established at ecotourism destinations, such as Kilim Geoforest Park in Kedah, Royal Belum State Park in Perak, Danum Valley in Sabah and Mulu National Park in Sarawak to ensure the sanctity and sustainability of these sites.",""],[2,"131","3","Private Sector Ecotourism Management Improvement Measures","Measures will also be undertaken to encourage the private sector to improve management and profitability, and ultimately ensuring the preservation and conservation of such sites.",""],[2,"132","2","Green Tourism and Sustainable Consumption Promotion","Sustainable consumption and production practices, including the adoption of green labels, will be further encouraged.",""],[2,"132","2","Tourism Pricing Mechanism Review","The pricing mechanisms for tourism products and services will be reviewed to commensurate with the value offered.",""],[2,"132","2","Carrying Capacity Limits for Sensitive Tourism Sites","Limits in terms of carrying capacity and LAC for environmentally-sensitive tourism sites, especially those accorded UNESCO Global Geopark or heritage status will be established.",""],[2,"132","2","Cleanliness and Public Amenities Standards at Tourism Sites","In addition, measures will be implemented to maintain high standards of cleanliness and quality of public amenities at these sites.",""],[2,"132","2","Stakeholder Awareness Programme on Maintenance Culture","Concurrently, awareness programmes to instil maintenance culture among stakeholders will be intensified.",""]],"371":[[2,"138","5","Business-to-Business Local Sourcing Expansion","business-to-business (B2B) opportunities will be expanded through initiatives that encourage large companies to source locally from MSMEs.",""],[2,"138","5","Buy Malaysia Campaign Intensification","The 'Buy Malaysia Campaign' will be intensified to support local MSMEs.",""],[2,"138","5","Anti-Monopoly Intervention Programmes","intervention programmes will be undertaken to break unhealthy monopolistic practices in certain industries.",""],[2,"138","7","Malaysian Cooperative Transformation Plan (TRANSKOM) 2021-2025","The governance structure and legal framework that govern the cooperative movement will be improved through the implementation of the Malaysian Cooperative Transformation Plan (TRANSKOM) 2021-2025.",""],[2,"138","7","Promotion of Cooperatives Among B40 and Rural Communities","The cooperative movement among the B40 and rural communities will be further promoted to encourage them to pool their limited resources to achieve economies of scale.",""],[2,"138","7","Extension of MSME Support to Cooperatives","The support provided to MSMEs will be extended to cooperatives, including access to programmes, assistance and business opportunities.",""],[2,"138","8","Continuous Support for PPK and PNK Entrepreneurship Development","The role of PPK and PNK in developing entrepreneurship among their members will be further enhanced by providing continuous support in the form of inputs, financial assistance, technology uptake and consultation.",""],[2,"138","8","Modern Agro-Food Project Implementation with Members","The PPK and PNK will be encouraged to implement modern agro-food projects in partnership with their members to increase productivity and income.",""],[2,"138","8","Agropreneur Programme Expansion for Market Access","This will be undertaken, among others, through the implementation of more agropreneur programmes, which will facilitate wider market access for the members through PPK and PNK.",""]],"372":[[2,"144","2","Crime Prevention, Rehabilitation and Emergency Preparedness Programme","Efforts will be intensified in crime prevention, rehabilitation and emergency preparedness, as well as improve the welfare of security personnel.",""],[2,"144","2","Security Governance Strengthening","Security governance will be strengthened to ensure the nation remains peaceful and public safety is maintained.",""],[2,"148","8","Advanced Technology for Threat Identification and Enforcement","Expanding the use of advanced technology in identifying threats and enforcement activities.",""],[2,"148","9","National Cybersecurity and Cyber Defence Strengthening","Strengthening national cybersecurity and cyber defence.",""],[2,"148","10","Holistic Border Security Management Plan","Implementing a holistic plan in managing security threats and curbing illegal activities at the border.",""],[2,"148","11","Single Border Agency Establishment","Strengthening security management at the border including the movement of people and goods, as well as enforcement, through the establishment of a single border agency.",""],[2,"148","12","National Defence and Security Industry Policy","Introducing the National Defence and Security Industry Policy.",""],[2,"154","1","Strengthening Armed Forces and Enforcement Agency Capacity","the capacity and capability of the Malaysian Armed Forces (ATM) and enforcement agencies were enhanced",""],[2,"154","1","Crime Prevention Programme Improvement","crime prevention programmes were improved",""],[2,"154","3","National Security and Sovereignty Strengthening","In the Twelfth Plan, priority will be given to improve national security and safeguard sovereignty in ensuring the nation remains peaceful and prosperous.",""],[2,"155","1","National Defence and Security Enhancement Initiatives","During the Eleventh Plan, various initiatives were implemented to enhance national defence and security as well as wellbeing and unity of the rakyat.",""],[2,"158","5","Crime Prevention and Police Omnipresence Programmes","Crime prevention efforts were intensified through various programmes involving PDRM omnipresence and public participation.",""],[2,"158","5","Joint Border Control and Patrol Operations","Meanwhile, border controls and patrolling were intensified through joint operations among ATM, PDRM and other enforcement agencies to curb the entry of illegal immigrants and other illegal activities, such as drug trafficking, smuggling and trafficking in persons.",""]],"373":[[2,"144","2","Sports for Active Nation Initiative","Sports will be leveraged as a means to build an active nation, while unity in diversity will be strengthened to create a more harmonious society.",""],[2,"154","3","Sports for Active Nation Initiative","Sports will be leveraged to build an active nation while unity among the rakyat will be enhanced.",""],[2,"155","1","Active Lifestyle and Sports Culture Promotion Programme","Programmes in promoting an active lifestyle were expanded to inculcate sports culture amongst the rakyat.",""]],"374":[[2,"146","1","Less Developed States and Rural Development Acceleration","Efforts will also be intensified to accelerate the development of less developed states and regions, and further narrow the development gap between rural and urban areas.",""],[2,"146","1","Rural Economy Support for Private Sector and Social Enterprises","Private sector and social enterprises will be encouraged to boost the rural economy, while key growth nodes and hotspot areas will be identified to accelerate development.",""],[2,"146","1","Border Area Growth Triangle Cooperation","The subregional cooperation under the Indonesia-Malaysia-Thailand Growth Triangle (IMT-GT) and Brunei Darussalam-Indonesia-Malaysia-Philippines East ASEAN Growth Area (BIMP-EAGA) will be leveraged to catalyse growth in border areas.",""],[2,"146","2","Sabah and Sarawak Regional Inclusion Development Programme","Socioeconomic development in Sabah and Sarawak will be intensified to promote regional inclusion.",""],[2,"146","2","Federal-State Programme Coordination Mechanism","Cooperation between Federal agencies and state governments will be strengthened to effectively implement programmes and projects.",""],[2,"146","2","Infrastructure and Connectivity Enhancement","The provision of infrastructure and connectivity will be enhanced, while economic potential optimised by creating a conducive ecosystem for economic growth.",""],[2,"146","2","Social Services Improvement Initiative","Access to better social services will be enhanced by improving educational infrastructure, healthcare services and housing, while security and public safety will be strengthened in ensuring a safer environment.",""],[2,"151","6","Preferential Allocation of Basic Development Expenditure to Less Developed States","Allocating at least 50% of Total Basic Development Expenditure1 for the six less developed states, especially Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[2,"151","9","Investment Incentive Package for Target States","Providing attractive incentive packages to entice investments to these states.",""],[2,"151","11","Green City Action Plan Expansion","Promoting sustainable cities by extending the Green City Action Plan (GCAP).",""],[2,"151","12","Rural Industrial Park Development and Revitalization","Intensifying rural industrialisation by developing new industrial parks and reinvigorating existing ones.",""]],"375":[[2,"164","6","National Security and Sovereignty Strengthening","In the Twelfth Plan, efforts will be intensified in enhancing defence and national security as well as the wellbeing and unity of the rakyat.",""],[2,"168","1","National Security and Sovereignty Protection","National security and sovereignty will continue to be given priority in ensuring a conducive environment for economic activities and safe living as well as maintaining a dignified and resilient nation.",""],[2,"169","1","Defence Capacity and Capability Enhancement","Defence capacity and capability will be enhanced in safeguarding national sovereignty as outlined in the Defence White Paper.",""],[2,"169","1","Military Intelligence, Surveillance, Target Acquisition and Reconnaissance Strengthening","military capability will be strengthened in the aspects of intelligence, surveillance, target acquisition and reconnaissance.",""],[2,"169","1","Firepower and Mobility Improvement Measures","Measures will also be undertaken to improve firepower and mobility in enhancing the defence capacity and capability.",""],[2,"169","1","Maritime Security Surveillance and Enforcement Enhancement","maritime security will be fortified, especially in surveillance and enforcement activities as well as showing presence to protect the socioeconomic interest and security of the country.",""],[2,"183","1","National Defence and Security Strengthening","In the Twelfth Plan, efforts will be intensified to strengthen national defence and security.",""]],"376":[[2,"169","3","Welfare Support for ATM and Enforcement Personnel","The welfare of ATM and enforcement personnel will be taken care off to enhance personnel performance in implementing duties.",""],[2,"170","6","Personnel Housing Construction, Upgrade and Maintenance","the quarters will be built, upgraded and maintained to create a condusive environment for the personnel.",""],[2,"170","6","Healthcare Programme Improvement for ATM and Enforcement Personnel","Meanwhile, healthcare programmes for ATM and enforcement personnel will be improved to increase health and fitness.",""]],"377":[[2,"168","1","Security Governance Strengthening","priority will be given in strengthening the security governance.",""],[2,"170","7","Security Governance Strengthening","The governance of security will be strengthened to improve service delivery in upholding public safety and security.",""],[2,"171","1","Strengthening NSC National Security Coordination","The role and function of the NSC as a lead agency in coordinating policies related to national security will be strengthened.",""],[2,"171","1","Enhanced National Operations Management Centre","In addition, the National Operations Management Centre will be enhanced through better coordination among relevant stakeholders and connection with all systems related to security, defence and disaster management.",""],[2,"171","2","Public Safety and Security Legal Reform","A number of laws will be amended to ensure relevancy and effectiveness in improving public safety and security.",""],[2,"171","4","Security and Public Order Consultative Council","A security and public order consultative council will be established to streamline efforts in addressing security threats.",""]],"378":[[2,"176","2","Affordable Homeowner Database","A comprehensive database of affordable homeowners will be established to monitor home ownership.",""],[2,"176","6","Waqf Land Development Law","A law on waqf land development will be introduced at the Federal level which will serve as a guide for waqf land development throughout the country.",""],[2,"176","7","Housing Redevelopment Guideline","A housing redevelopment guideline will be formulated, using the public-private partnership model, to rebuild public housing, especially dilapidated flats, and old or abandoned government quarters that are beyond economic repair.",""],[2,"176","7","Affordable Housing Near Transport Terminals","In addition, affordable housing will be built close to transport terminals to improve mobility and connectivity.",""],[2,"176","7","Affordable Housing in New Township Planning","the provision of affordable housing will be included in the development planning of new townships.",""],[2,"177","1","Affordable Housing Governance Enhancement","The governance of affordable housing will be enhanced to improve planning, coordination and execution of affordable housing projects at the Federal, state and local levels.",""],[2,"177","1","Affordable Housing Institutional Capacity Strengthening","Institutional capability in building affordable houses, enforcing houses standards, and strengthening rules and regulations to safeguard homebuyers and tenants will be enhanced.",""],[2,"177","2","Housing Data Centre Establishment","A data centre on housing, integrating relevant data from the Federal and state governments as well as private developers will be established to strengthen the institutional capability.",""],[2,"177","2","Evidence-Based Housing Policy Formulation Using BDA","BDA will be leveraged to facilitate evidence-based policy formulation in developing housing projects.",""],[2,"177","2","Housing Integrated Management System","a housing integrated management system will be developed to serve as a single-entry platform for the application and processing of advertisement and sale permits.",""],[2,"177","6","National Affordable Housing Guideline for State Governments","A national guideline will be formulated to serve as a reference for state governments in the development of affordable housing in new townships.",""]],"379":[[2,"179","2","Dedicated Sports Participation Programmes for Target Groups","Sports event organisers will also be required to organise dedicated programmes to encourage participation of these target groups.",""],[2,"179","2","Community-Level Sports Activities for Target Groups","Local authorities will also be encouraged to organise more sports activities for these groups at the community level.",""],[2,"179","2","National Plan of Action for Women in Sports","a national plan of action to boost participation of women in sports will be introduced.",""],[2,"179","2","School and Higher Education Sports Culture Promotion","Intensive efforts will also be undertaken to instil sports culture among children and youth by improving sports programmes and syllabi in schools and HEIs.",""],[2,"179","2","Sports Participation Awareness Campaigns","Awareness campaigns, particularly through digital platforms and sports events will be implemented to encourage sports participation among the targeted groups.",""],[2,"179","4","Revision of the National Sports Policy","The National Sports Policy will be revised to include, among others, measures to strengthen the administration and management of national sports associations (NSAs).",""],[2,"179","4","Capacity Building for National Sports Associations","The professionalism of NSAs will be enhanced through capacity building programmes.",""],[2,"179","4","Women in Sports Coaching and Leadership Training","The Women in Sports Secretariat will be tasked, among others to ensure more women, particularly former national athletes are trained as qualified coaches and office bearers in HPS entities.",""]],"380":[[2,"205","1","Enhanced Social Welfare Programmes for the Hardcore Poor and Poor","Existing social welfare programmes for the hardcore poor and poor will be enhanced.",""],[2,"205","1","Need-Based Cash Transfers and Healthcare Support","Assistance such as cash transfers and healthcare support will continue to be provided on a need basis.",""],[2,"205","1","Productive Welfare, Entrepreneurship and Microfinance Support","Productive welfare programmes, including entrepreneurship and micro financing will be intensified to provide economic opportunities for the poor.",""],[2,"205","1","Training and Upskilling for Poor Households","In addition, training and upskilling will be strengthened among members of poor households to increase employability and capacity in venturing into income-generating activities.",""],[2,"205","1","Basic Financial Education for Poor Households","Basic financial education will be enhanced to improve their financial literacy.",""],[2,"205","2","Structured Private Sector Support for Poor Households","The private sector will be encouraged to offer structured and targeted assistance to poor households by providing scholarships and training, entrepreneurship and job opportunities as well as organising public benefit programmes through in situ development.",""],[2,"205","2","Promotion of Social Enterprises and Cooperatives","Social enterprises and cooperatives will be further promoted among the poor to increase household income.",""],[2,"205","2","Community-Based Economic Activities Programme","Community-based economic activities will be pursued as part of income-generating programmes.",""],[2,"205","2","Inclusive Business Approach for Poor Supply Chain Participation","The inclusive business approach15 will be introduced to increase the involvement of the poor in the supply chain.",""],[2,"205","6","Base-of-the-Pyramid Inclusive Business Engagement","Businesses that engage people living at the base of the economic pyramid (B1) to provide goods and services, making them part of the value chain.",""]],"381":[[2,"205","3","Improved Access to Quality Education and Skills Training","improving access to quality education and skills training",""],[2,"205","3","Improved Healthcare Services","improving healthcare services will be given priority",""],[2,"205","4","Expanded Quality Education Support for Poor Households","Provision for quality education will be expanded to enhance the education level among members of poor households.",""],[2,"205","4","Subsidised Early Childhood Care and Education Expansion","subsidised ECCE will be continued and expanded to offer more affordable and high-quality childcare services for the poor.",""],[2,"205","4","Universal Early Childhood Education Provision","Steps will be taken to provide early childhood education for all, while efforts will be intensified to ensure children from poor families will complete compulsory schooling of 11 years.",""],[2,"205","4","Scholarships to Reduce School Dropouts","targeted interventions such as scholarships will be provided to reduce the number of school dropouts among poor households.",""],[2,"205","4","Scholarship Support for Skills Training and Higher Education","Scholarship opportunities will also be provided in easing the financial burden to pursue skills training, TVET and higher education.",""],[2,"205","5","Expanded Community Health Outreach for the Poor","Efforts to uplift the health of the poor will focus on improving the outreach of pre-natal care to geriatric services to the community.",""],[2,"205","5","Balanced Nutrition Awareness Promotion","In addition, awareness of the importance of good health will be further promoted by ensuring balanced nutrients intake at all stages of life.",""],[2,"205","5","Food Basket Programme for the Poor","Initiatives will be intensified to promote a balanced diet through the food basket programme for the poor according to the optimum minimum requirement based on the Malaysia Food Pyramid.",""]],"382":[[2,"204","1","Service Delivery Mechanism Strengthening","The strategies include improving access to essential services, increasing income and uplifting the standard of living of the poor, addressing urban poverty, strengthening the service delivery mechanism and narrowing household inequality.",""],[2,"206","1","Basic Amenities and Housing Improvement for the Poor","These efforts include improving basic amenities and infrastructure as well as upgrading the living conditions of the poor.",""],[2,"206","2","Systematic Garbage Collection and Transportation Service Improvement","Access to systematic garbage collection and transportation services will be improved.",""],[2,"206","2","Basic Utilities and Broadband Access Expansion in Remote Areas","Basic utilities and communication services such as treated water, electricity and broadband connectivity will be enhanced, particularly in remote areas.",""],[2,"206","3","Housing Assistance Programme for Poor Households","In ensuring the adequate supply of affordable housing for poor households, the housing assistance programme will be continued.",""],[2,"206","8","Service Delivery Mechanism Strengthening","The service delivery mechanism will be strengthened by enhancing the delivery system, improving poverty measurement and policy implementation as well as exploring new funding mechanisms.",""]],"383":[[2,"204","1","Urban Poverty Reduction Measures","The strategies include improving access to essential services, increasing income and uplifting the standard of living of the poor, addressing urban poverty, strengthening the service delivery mechanism and narrowing household inequality.",""],[2,"206","4","Urban Poverty Support and Wellbeing Programme","Efforts to address urban poverty will focus on improving access to social support in maintaining a certain level of quality of life and uplift the wellbeing of urban poor communities.",""],[2,"206","5","Entrepreneurship Training and Microfinancing Expansion for the Urban Poor","Access to entrepreneurship training and microfinancing will be expanded to increase and diversify income of the urban poor.",""],[2,"206","5","Social Enterprise Initiatives for the Urban Poor","SE initiatives will be promoted to address social and economic issues faced by the urban poor.",""],[2,"206","5","Community-Based Urban Livelihood Activities","Community-based activities in producing goods and services such as urban farming,",""],[2,"206","6","Childcare Services and Home-Based Food Business Promotion","childcare services and home-based food business will also be promoted to generate additional income.",""],[2,"206","6","Urban Poor Gig Economy Job Access Initiative","the urban poor will be exposed to job opportunities in the gig economy.",""]],"384":[[2,"206","7","Expanded Early Childhood Care and Education Access for Urban Poor Households","Early childhood programmes will be made more accessible for children from urban poor households.",""],[2,"206","7","Community-Based ECCE Facilities in Low-Cost Housing Areas","CBOs will be encouraged to provide ECCE facilities at public and private low-cost housing areas.",""],[2,"206","7","Enhanced Tuition Support for Urban Poor Students","the provision of tuition classes to the urban poor students residing in low-cost housing projects will be enhanced.",""],[2,"206","7","Online Tuition Delivery Through Digital Platforms","Digital platforms will be leveraged to provide online tuition.",""],[2,"206","7","Child Nutrition Awareness and Balanced Diet Promotion","A balanced nutrient intake will also be promoted to address malnutrition issues among children.",""],[2,"206","7","TVET Awareness Campaign for Urban Poor Youth","awareness of TVET programmes will be intensified among youth from urban poor households.",""]],"385":[[2,"192","6","Young Agropreneur Financial Assistance and Training Programme","Program Agropreneur Muda has provided financial assistance and training to entrepreneurs to venture into farming, livestock, fisheries and agro-based activities.",""],[2,"192","6","Urban Farming Programme","Meanwhile, urban farming programmes have been conducted in 4,556 locations involving 111,486 participants, generating an additional average monthly income of at least RM300.",""]],"386":[[2,"194","7","Kampung Baru Chinese Community Soft Loan Scheme","Skim Pinjaman Khas Penduduk Kampung Baru Cina was continued during the Eleventh Plan.",""]],"387":[[2,"196","2","Family and Community Empowerment Programme","The Family and Community Empowerment (FACE) programme was introduced in 2016 to promote parenting awareness and skills.",""],[2,"196","2","Parenting and Family Wellbeing Education Programmes","Programmes such as Parenting@Work, SMARTbelanja@LPPKN and FamilyEducation@LPPKN were undertaken to provide knowledge and skills related to marriage, parenting and family wellbeing, benefitting 907,100 family members as of 2020.",""],[2,"196","2","Maternal Mortality and Unwanted Pregnancy Prevention Services","Various programmes were also carried out to address issues concerning maternal mortality and unwanted pregnancies.",""],[2,"196","2","Family Support and Reproductive Health Services","A total of 1,065,301 family members particularly women benefitted from family support programmes such as family planning, mammograms, cervical cancer screening and subfertility treatment.",""]],"388":[[2,"210","2","Kampung Baru Business Loan Facility","For low-income Chinese households in Kampung Baru, access to financing facilities will be continued by providing business loans to facilitate their expansion of business.",""],[2,"210","2","Kampung Baru Village Tourism Promotion Scheme","The Skim Pinjaman Khas Penduduk Kampung Baru will be expanded to include the promotion of villages as attractive tourist destinations.",""],[2,"210","2","Kampung Baru Basic Infrastructure and Amenities Upgrading","basic infrastructure and amenities will continue to be upgraded to enable the Kampung Baru community to enjoy better facilities.",""]],"389":[[2,"210","3","Targeted Education, Skills, Entrepreneurship, and Family Support Programmes for Low-Income Indian Households","In pursuing inclusive development, the wellbeing of low-income Indian households will continue to be given priority in line with the Malaysian Indian Blueprint.",""]],"390":[[2,"210","4","M40 Support and Social Mobility Measures","Concerted efforts to support the M40, especially the M117 income decile will be undertaken to attain more equitable economic gains and improve their standard of living.",""],[2,"210","4","Insurance Incentive Support for M40 Households","In addition, incentives will be provided to encourage them in obtaining health and employment insurance.",""],[2,"211","1","M40 Income Support and Entrepreneurship Promotion","The M40 will be supported to boost their income to cope with the high cost of living and prevent them from falling into the vulnerable group.",""],[2,"211","1","M40 Entrepreneurship and Supplementary Income Activities","In this regard, the M40 will be encouraged to be involved in entrepreneurship and supplementary income activities as well as invest in income-generating portfolios.",""],[2,"211","1","M40 Sharing Economy Promotion Through Digital Platforms","The sharing economy will be promoted among the M40 through the use of digital platforms.",""],[2,"211","1","Financial Literacy and Advisory Services for M40","In addition, financial institutions will be encouraged to provide financial literacy programmes and advisory services.",""],[2,"211","3","M40 Health and Employment Insurance Subscription Incentives","The M40 will be encouraged to subscribe to health and employment insurance to mitigate them from financial vulnerability.",""],[2,"211","3","Tax Relief Review for Health, Life, and Employment Insurance","In addition, income tax relief on health and life as well as employment insurance for the M40 will be reviewed to reduce healthcare costs.",""]],"391":[[2,"211","2","Affordable Early Childhood Care and Education Expansion","affordable ECCE especially in urban areas and public sector premises will be provided and enhanced.",""],[2,"211","2","Workplace Affordable Day Care Incentive","The private sector will be further encouraged to provide affordable day care services at their workplaces.",""],[2,"221","1","ECCE Programme Rationalisation","The ECCE programmes will also be rationalised to enhance accessibility and quality of programmes as well as to ensure fees are affordable.",""]],"392":[[2,"212","1","Bumiputera Socioeconomic Development Support","Bumiputera socioeconomic development will be given priority through enhancing the governance, service delivery and human capital development as well as strengthening access to education.",""],[2,"213","1","Basic Necessities Assistance for Poor Bumiputera Households","Assistance in the form of basic necessities such as housing, education and health will continue to be provided to poor Bumiputera households.",""],[2,"213","1","Income Diversification Training for B40 Bumiputera Households","Furthermore, the B40 Bumiputera households will be encouraged to diversify their sources of income to improve their standard of living through the provision of appropriate training.",""],[2,"213","2","M40 Bumiputera Household Empowerment Programme","The M40 Bumiputera households will continue to be empowered towards increasing their potential to attain a better standard of living.",""],[2,"213","2","T20 Bumiputera Community Contribution Initiative","The T20 Bumiputera households will be encouraged to actively contribute back to the Bumiputera community.",""]],"393":[[2,"214","3","Bumiputera Human Capital Development Initiatives","Efforts will be intensified in expanding educational access and opportunities, improving the quality of skills programmes, increasing the participation in certified professional programmes as well as improving huffaz skills and marketability.",""],[2,"214","4","Bumiputera Future Skills Education Programme","MARA education institutes will be leveraged to equip Bumiputera human capital with skills of the future including artificial intelligence (AI), advanced digital skills, critical thinking as well as spiritual and positive values to enhance creativity and competency.",""],[2,"214","4","Bumiputera Nurturing and Development Programmes","The Bumiputera education institutions will also be encouraged to implement the nurturing and development programmes18 in complementing the academic and technical training received by students and trainees.",""],[2,"214","5","Intensified Structured TVET Skills Training","Structured skills training in TVET programmes will be intensified by MARA to increase the supply of Bumiputera talents in meeting industrial demands as well as to address the high Bumiputera unemployment rate particularly among youth.","MARA"],[2,"214","5","HEI-Industry Digital Employability Platform","a digital platform will be developed through collaboration between HEIs and industry to improve the employability of Bumiputera graduates.",""],[2,"214","5","New Skills Development Programme for Emerging Jobs","a programme to develop new skill sets related to the solution of complex problems, technology design and programming will be introduced to equip the Bumiputera for newly emerging skilled jobs.",""],[2,"214","6","Bumiputera Graduate Professional Support Programme","More eligible Bumiputera graduates will be supported to increase the number of Bumiputera professionals such as accountants, architects and engineers.",""],[2,"214","6","Bumiputera Future Careers Strategy","specific strategies will be formulated to increase Bumiputera participation in future careers such as analysts, data scientists and big data experts through strategic collaboration with industry and skills training institutions.",""],[2,"214","6","Bumiputera Specialist Training Programme","more Bumiputera professionals will be trained to become specialists in various fields such as medicine and engineering.",""],[2,"214","6","Bumiputera Professional Financing Diversification Mechanism","Funds will be sourced from SOEs and the private sector as well as individuals through crowdfunding to reduce dependency on government.",""],[2,"214","7","Student and Trainee Skills and Values Development Programme","This programme will help students and trainees to acquire relevant skills and values such as industry relevant soft skills, financial literacy, employment readiness, leadership and spiritual values to complement technical competencies in creating balanced and competitive individuals.",""],[2,"215","1","Tahfiz Programme Accreditation and Curriculum Alignment","Concerted efforts will continue to be implemented to accredit tahfiz19 programmes, particularly in private institutions to provide better routes for huffaz to enter into mainstream education.",""],[2,"215","1","Huffaz Technical and Professional Training and Lifelong Learning","In addition, YPPB and MARA will continue to train more huffaz in technical and professional fields as well as program pembelajaran sepanjang hayat (PSH) in enhancing their employability.",""]],"394":[[2,"215","6","Vendor Development Programme Expansion","The involvement of Bumiputera MSMEs in the Vendor Development Programme will be further intensified.",""],[2,"215","6","Carve-Out and Compete Initiative Expansion","Meanwhile, the carve-out and compete initiative will be extended to various sectors in increasing effective Bumiputera participation in the economy.",""],[2,"215","6","Bumiputera MSME Consortium and Cooperative Formation Support","Bumiputera MSMEs will also be encouraged to form consortiums and cooperatives in enhancing their capacity and capability to compete along the supply chain.",""],[2,"215","6","VentureTECH Capital Injection for Bumiputera Companies","Meanwhile, VentureTECH will be injecting capital into Bumiputera companies with potential.",""],[2,"215","6","Bumiputera MSME Exit Policy Framework","A clear exit policy will be formulated to encourage successful Bumiputera MSMEs to be more independent and resilient.",""],[2,"215","7","SOE Partnership Support for Bumiputera MSMEs","SOEs will enhance collaboration with MNCs and global companies in identifying and assisting potential Bumiputera MSMEs.",""],[2,"215","7","Smart Partnership Commercialisation Initiative","Smart partnerships between SOEs, R&D institutions and Bumiputera MSMEs will be intensified to develop and commercialise IPs as well as innovative products and services to penetrate new markets.",""],[2,"215","7","Bumiputera Business Promotion in New Growth Areas","Bumiputera businesses will be promoted in new growth areas across the country, while Development Financial Institutions (DFIs) will be urged to expand financial assistance, coaching and mentoring to support potential Bumiputera entrepreneurs venturing into high value-added activities.",""]],"395":[[2,"215","7","Bumiputera MSME Global Market Expansion Support","Bumiputera MSMEs will be encouraged to grow and penetrate the global market.",""]],"396":[[2,"212","1","Wealth Creation and Waqf Instrument Optimization","concerted efforts will be undertaken in increasing wealth creation, optimising TRM and waqf instruments as well as ensuring sustainable corporate equity ownership.",""],[2,"216","4","TRM and Waqf Development Optimisation","the development of TRM and waqf instruments will be optimised.",""],[2,"216","4","Collaborative Development of TRM and Waqf Lands","state authorities will be encouraged to develop TRM and waqf lands through collaboration with the Federal agencies.",""],[2,"216","4","Integrated Master Plan for TRM and Waqf Development","An integrated master plan on the development of TRM, waqf land and waqf instruments will be formulated to provide a framework for socioeconomic development at state and local levels.",""],[2,"216","4","Expanded Land Data Management Committee Mandate","The role and scope of the Jawatankuasa Pemandu Pengurusan Data Tanah Rizab Melayu Semenanjung Malaysia will be expanded to provide guidelines relating to land development and value creation.",""],[2,"216","5","Waqf Land Development Coordination Committee","A committee comprising representatives of Federal and state governments will be set up to provide overall direction in planning, implementation and monitoring of waqf land development.",""],[2,"216","5","Expansion of Waqf for Socioeconomic Development","the possibility of expanding the concept of waqf as an instrument for broader socioeconomic development will be explored.",""],[2,"216","5","Federal Waqf Fund Establishment","A waqf fund at the Federal level will be established to mobilise resources from individuals and corporate bodies to fund socioeconomic activities.",""]],"397":[[2,"218","4","Orang Asli Education Access Improvement Programme","Access to education will be improved to facilitate social and economic mobility of Orang Asli.",""],[2,"218","5","Education Programme Streamlining and Access Improvement for Orang Asli","Efforts in strengthening ongoing programmes on education will be streamlined.",""],[2,"218","5","Orang Asli Early Childhood Education Access Expansion","Access to ECCE for the Orang Asli community will be improved to better prepare them in acquiring the basic skills of reading, writing and counting (3M).",""],[2,"218","5","Orang Asli Student Retention and Learning Improvement Initiative","Student dropouts during the transition from ECCE level to primary and from primary to secondary will be reduced while teaching and learning methods will be improved to ensure that Orang Asli students remain in school and progress towards higher levels of education.",""],[2,"218","5","TVET and Tertiary Education Enrolment Expansion","In addition, enrolment in TVET programmes and tertiary education will be increased.",""],[2,"218","6","Community-Based Student Attendance and Literacy Improvement Programme","The Program Jom Belajar will be further expanded within the community to improve student attendance through innovative teaching and suitable learning methods in reducing illiteracy.",""],[2,"218","6","Teacher Decent Accommodation Provision","In ensuring a conducive living environment for the teachers, adequate decent accommodation will be provided.",""],[2,"218","6","Community Basic 3M Skills Programme","The Program Kelas Komuniti will continue to ensure the community is able to master the basic 3M skills.",""],[2,"219","1","Expanded Access to Orang Asli Education","Access to education will be improved to encourage social and economic mobility of Orang Asli.",""],[2,"219","1","Comprehensive Special Model School 9 Expansion","The Comprehensive Special Model School 9 (K9) which offers schooling up to Form 3 will be made accessible to more Orang Asli students in facilitating the transition from primary to secondary schools.",""],[2,"219","1","Comprehensive Special Model School 11 Programme","A Comprehensive Special Model School 11 (K11) that provides 11 years of schooling will be implemented to ensure Orang Asli students remain in school until they sit for the SPM examination.",""],[2,"219","1","TVET-Oriented K11 School Curriculum","K11 schools will focus on TVET programmes with specific training skills taking into account the local as well as national requirements.",""],[2,"219","2","Bringing School to Community Programme","a special programme, Bringing School to Community, will be introduced through collaboration between government, universities and CSOs.",""]],"398":[[2,"219","4","Income-Generating Poverty Eradication Programme","Poverty eradication programmes will focus on income-generating activities.",""],[2,"219","4","Commercial Crop and Traditional Handicraft Development","Potential crops that have commercial value and traditional handicrafts will be further developed to fully exploit their potential.",""],[2,"219","4","Orang Asli Microfinance and Skills Training Support","microfinancing facilities and skills training will be provided for Orang Asli to become entrepreneurs, particularly in ecotourism, agrotourism as well as arts and handicrafts.",""],[2,"219","4","State Land Gazettement for Economic Activities","State governments will be encouraged to enhance the gazettement of land for economic activities.",""]],"399":[[2,"222","2","Financial Literacy Programmes for Young People","Programmes to inculcate financial literacy among the younger generation will be amplified to improve financial management skills in preparation for old age.",""],[2,"222","2","Pension System and Retirement Coverage Enhancement","Pension systems and retirement coverage will also be enhanced.",""],[2,"222","2","Private Retirement Scheme Promotion","Private retirement schemes will be promoted to complement existing schemes.",""],[2,"222","2","Social Assistance Streamlining for Older Persons","Current social assistance programmes will be streamlined to strengthen social protection for older persons.",""],[2,"222","2","e-Warga Emas National Database","the e-Warga Emas will be launched as an integrated national database for older persons, to facilitate better policymaking and programme implementation.",""],[2,"222","2","Lifelong Learning and Employment Access Expansion","Accessibility to lifelong learning programmes and employment opportunities will be broadened to improve income and quality of life.",""],[2,"222","2","Physical Planning Guideline for Elderly Adoption","Local authorities will be encouraged to adopt the Physical Planning Guideline for Elderly, while a national framework on Age Friendly City will also be introduced to promote a more conducive environment for the aged population.",""],[2,"222","2","Age-Friendly City National Framework","a national framework on Age Friendly City will also be introduced to promote a more conducive environment for the aged population.",""],[2,"222","2","Intergenerational Programmes Promotion","Intergenerational programmes will be further promoted to strengthen social interaction among different generations.",""]],"400":[[2,"231","6","Stage Bus Services Transformation Programme Expansion","The Stage Bus Services Transformation Programme was expanded to improve connectivity between rural and urban areas as well as to provide scheduled trips for rural communities.",""],[2,"231","6","myBAS Rural Route Expansion","The myBAS service opened up new routes in underserved rural areas, such as Bahau in Negeri Sembilan, Salak Tinggi in Selangor and Chemor in Perak.",""],[2,"231","7","Rural Basic Services Expansion Programme","Access to basic services in rural areas, such as primary healthcare, education and affordable housing was further enhanced.",""]],"401":[[2,"239","3","MSME Value Chain Upgrading Support","Industry players, especially MSMEs in the key growth nodes and hotspot areas, will be encouraged to move up the value chain and participate in high value-added activities.",""],[2,"239","3","Industry 4IR Adoption Facilitation","Efforts will be undertaken to facilitate industries to embrace the 4IR through the adoption of technology, automation and innovation, particularly in complex industrial processes.",""],[2,"239","4","Green Growth Initiatives for Industry","Industries will also be encouraged to implement green growth initiatives by adopting green technology and best practices.",""],[2,"239","5","Quality Investment Attraction Measures","Measures to attract quality investments, particularly in less developed regions, will be intensified to expedite development.",""],[2,"239","5","Competitive Incentive Package Enhancement","The focus will be on enticing high value-added, advanced technology and knowledge-intensive activities by enhancing competitive incentive packages and intensifying R&D&C&I.",""],[2,"239","6","High-Value Economic Transformation and Industry Facilitation","efforts will be undertaken to move away from low-end economic activities to high value-added, advanced technology and knowledge-intensive activities.",""],[2,"239","7","Enhanced Investment Incentive Packages","Incentive packages will be enhanced to attract more quality investment to catalyse key economic activities across key growth nodes and hotspot areas.",""],[2,"239","8","R&D&C&I Intensification for MSME Productivity","Efforts to enhance R&D&C&I will be intensified to increase productivity, particularly among MSMEs.",""],[2,"239","8","Industry Collaboration with Higher Education and Research Centres","Industries will be encouraged to collaborate with HEIs and research centres to embark on research that focuses on the specific needs of the industries and communities in each region.",""],[2,"239","8","Anchor Company Support for MSMEs in Less Developed Regions","Anchor companies will be identified to assist MSMEs in the less developed regions.",""],[2,"239","8","Agribusiness Anchor Company Technical Assistance and Market Access","In the agribusiness industry, anchor companies will take up an active role in providing technical assistance and greater market access to small scale agropreneurs to provide wider growth opportunities to MSMEs.",""],[2,"240","5","MSME Integration into Broader Production Networks","MSMEs will be encouraged to increase participation in the broader production networks encompassing large firms and multinational corporations to move up the value chain, open up new business opportunities, increase market access and facilitate the adoption of 4IR technologies.",""],[2,"240","5","Triple Helix Technology Advisory and Consultation Services","The triple helix model2 will be leveraged to provide advisory and consultation services on the application of the latest technologies.",""],[2,"240","5","Analytical Tools for Predictive Decision Support","Analytical tools will be utilised to assist in providing predictive information for data-driven decision-making.",""]],"402":[[2,"247","1","Regional Economic Development and Balanced Growth Initiative","The Twelfth Plan will optimise regional economic potential, develop sustainable cities and transform rural areas to bridge the development gap.",""],[2,"276","3","Priority Development Allocation for Less Developed States","The Federal Government is committed to ensuring the less developed states are given priority in the development allocation.",""]],"403":[[2,"267","8","Special MSME Financing Fund for Sabah and Sarawak","Access to financing will be improved for MSMEs by allocating a special fund for Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[2,"267","8","MSME Financing Awareness Programmes","Special programmes will be implemented to increase awareness of available financing for MSMEs.",""],[2,"267","8","Mobile Banking Expansion for MSME Financing Access","In addition, mobile banking will be expanded to provide better access to financing.",""],[2,"274","9","Entrepreneurship Ecosystem Strengthening for Community Development","The entrepreneurship ecosystem such as financing assistance and marketing through digital platforms will be strengthened to facilitate entrepreneurs in accelerating the socioeconomic development of these communities.",""]],"404":[[2,"266","6","Sabah Aerospace Industry Development","Thus, the development of the aerospace industry in Sabah will focus on maintenance, repair and overhaul (MRO), as well as becoming centre of excellence for skilled training.",""],[2,"266","6","Sarawak Helicopter Operations and MRO Development","Due to Sarawak's frequent use of rural air transportation for the provision of basic social services, such as mobile healthcare services and RAS, the focus for Sarawak will be on helicopter operations and MRO.",""],[2,"267","4","Niche Programme Development in Private Higher Education Institutions","Private HEIs in Sabah and Sarawak will be encouraged to introduce niche programmes, such as robotics and artificial intelligence, to attract local and international students.",""],[2,"267","4","Private HEI-Enterprise Skills Partnership Programme","In addition, collaboration between private HEIs and enterprises as strategic partners will be encouraged to provide students with industry skillsets through coaching and mentoring, as well as on-job-training.",""],[2,"267","6","Construction Workforce Reskilling and Accreditation Programme","Akademi Binaan Malaysia in Sabah and Sarawak will conduct reskilling, upskilling and accreditation programmes to produce qualified local talent.",""],[2,"273","2","Institution-Industry Lab Upgrading Initiative","Existing laboratories and workshops at the institutions will be upgraded as the Institution-Industry Lab (IIL) through shared ownership between selected TVET institutions and industries.",""],[2,"275","8","Talent Strengthening Initiative","talents will be strengthened",""]],"405":[[2,"267","5","Mega Project Construction and Laboratory Upgrade Programme","The construction of mega projects, such as the Pan Borneo Highway, Sarawak Water Grid Programme and Sabah Seafront will spur the growth of the construction sector.",""],[2,"267","5","Construction Materials Testing Laboratory Upgrade","The laboratory facilities for testing the aforementioned materials will be upgraded to increase capacity and speed up approval processes.",""],[2,"267","6","Construction Technology Adoption Incentives","In this regard, incentives will be introduced to encourage more industry players to adopt the latest construction technologies.",""]],"406":[[2,"274","8","Expanded TVET Upskilling Programme","The upskilling programmes, especially TVET, will be intensified.",""],[2,"274","8","Customised Community Skills Training","Untapped ancestral skills and talent of local communities will be unleashed by providing customised skills training.",""],[2,"275","3","Human Resources Development Fund Access Improvement for Youth Employability","Access to the human resources development fund programmes will be improved to enhance the employability of youth by providing dedicated reskilling and upskilling programmes to leverage local economic opportunities.",""],[2,"275","3","Youth Soft Skills Training Programme","Youth will also be provided courses on self- discipline, interpersonal and communication skills, adaptability and self-confidence to better compete with more experienced workers.",""],[2,"275","3","Youth Entrepreneurship Support Programme","In addition, youth who are inclined towards entrepreneurship will be channelled to specific programmes in developing their ability to venture into business.",""]],"407":[[2,"275","1","NCR Land Development for Agricultural Income Generation","The development of NCR land will be facilitated to provide income- generating opportunities, particularly in undertaking agriculture activities on a large scale.",""],[2,"275","4","NCR Land Development Acceleration Programme","Ongoing programmes in facilitating the development of NCR land will be accelerated in ensuring the Anak Negeri Sabah and Bumiputera Sarawak have access to opportunities for generating higher incomes.",""],[2,"275","4","NCR Land Surveying and Mapping Exercise","Hence, the surveying and mapping exercise of the NCR land will be accelerated to facilitate the state governments in gazetting and granting land titles.",""],[2,"275","4","Integrated NCR Land Development Collaboration Mechanism","Collaboration between the state governments, landowners and investors will be strengthened to ensure successful development of the NCR land through an integrated land development approach.",""]],"408":[[2,"271","2","Ecological Fiscal Transfer and Ecosystem Services Payments","Ecological fiscal transfer measures and payments for ecosystem services will be implemented to ensure the sustainability of the ecosystem services.",""],[2,"271","2","Eco-School Programme Expansion","eco-school programmes will be extended across the schools in Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[2,"271","6","Ecosystem Conservation Programme Intensification","conservation programmes on the terrestrial, inland water, coastal and marine ecosystems will be intensified.",""],[2,"271","6","Species Conservation and Sustainable Fisheries Management","the implementation of species conservation programmes including sustainable fisheries management, as well as enforcement activities will be strengthened.",""],[2,"271","6","Sustainable Mining Rating Adoption","mining operators will also be encouraged to subscribe to a sustainability rating in ensuring sustainable mining practices.",""],[2,"271","7","Community Participation in Protected Area Management","Local communities' participation in protecting and managing protected areas sustainably will be elevated to improve their livelihood.",""],[2,"271","7","Access and Benefit-Sharing Education and Awareness Programme","Education and awareness programmes on access and sharing of benefits will be enhanced.",""],[2,"271","7","State-Level Enforcement of the Access to Biological Resources and Benefit Sharing Act 2017","the provision of the Access to Biological Resources and Benefit Sharing Act 2017 will be enforced through enactments and ordinances at the state level.",""],[2,"271","7","Payment for Ecosystem Services and Carbon Offset Exploration","payment for ecosystem services including carbon offset will be explored.",""],[2,"289","1","Protected Areas Conservation and Ecosystem Rehabilitation","There was greater emphasis placed on conserving protected areas and rehabilitating degraded ecosystems of terrestrial and marine areas as well as enhancing the livelihood of indigenous and local communities (ILCs).",""]],"409":[[2,"291","2","Climate Change Taxonomy Development","the climate change and principles-based taxonomy is being developed to enhance understanding and assessment of the risks.",""],[2,"298","6","Climate Action Enabling Instruments and Carbon Pricing","the focus will be on developing enabling instruments for climate action, including carbon pricing.",""],[2,"298","7","Nationally Determined Contribution Roadmap","a Nationally Determined Contribution roadmap will be developed to devise specific mitigation action plans in fulfilling the country's commitment to the Paris Agreement.",""],[2,"298","7","Low-Emission Development Strategy Studies","Multi-scenario analyses and detailed studies will also be undertaken to formulate long-term low emission development strategies as well as assessing the cost and implications to the country in achieving carbon neutrality.",""],[2,"298","7","Carbon Pricing Feasibility Study","a feasibility study will be conducted on carbon pricing, such as carbon tax and the Emission Trading Scheme.",""],[2,"299","1","Carbon Trading and Green Finance Instruments","carbon trading. These instruments will also help mobilise investments required in stimulating the development and utilisation of green technologies as well as green market innovation, thus promoting low- carbon economic growth.",""],[2,"313","5","Climate-Related Financial Taxonomy and Green Finance Mobilization","economic activities based on their impact on climate change will be leveraged. This taxonomy will facilitate financial flows to activities that support the advancement of green growth.",""],[2,"313","5","Climate Risk Disclosure and Responsible Investment Alignment","These institutions are strongly encouraged to adopt recommendations of the Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosures to improve transparency in integrating climate risks for decision-making.",""],[2,"313","5","Green Project Appraisal and Sustainable Finance Capacity Building","Financial institutions will strengthen their capabilities to enable effective evaluation of green project proposals and advocate sustainable practices among clients.",""]],"410":[[2,"301","1","Circular Economy Transition Initiatives","Among initiatives that will be implemented to expedite this transition include creating an enabling ecosystem, improving design and processes of products and services, extending producer responsibility and strengthening waste management.",""],[2,"301","1","Whole-of-Nation Circular Economy and SDG Integration","As Malaysia embraces the circular economy, adoption of the whole-of-nation approach, and integration of the SDGs and ESG principles into decision-making will be promoted.",""],[2,"301","2","Circular Economy Transition Framework for Businesses","Businesses, especially MSMEs, will be encouraged to adopt the circular economy concept in the design, production, logistics, consumption and waste management of products and services.",""],[2,"301","2","Circular Economy Enabling Framework","In this respect, an enabling framework will be developed as guidance for the economic sectors to shift to the circular economy.",""],[2,"301","2","Circular Economy Blueprint for Waste and Agricommodities","A blueprint for the circular economy related to solid waste, plastics, scheduled waste and agricommodities will also be introduced to deliver better system-wide economic and environmental outcomes.",""],[2,"301","2","Circular Economy Policy and Economic Instruments Package","Relevant policies, legislation and economic instruments will be developed to facilitate the transition to the circular economy.",""],[2,"301","2","Circular Economy R&D, Commercialisation and Innovation Partnership","Meanwhile, R&D&C&I and smart partnership among stakeholders will be intensified to boost the implementation of the circular economy.",""],[2,"301","3","Sustainable Product Design and Green Labelling Promotion","Therefore, businesses will be encouraged to design products that are more durable, repairable, reusable and recyclable as well as use recycled materials as inputs.",""],[2,"301","3","Green Labelling Uptake Promotion","They will also be encouraged to uptake recognised green labelling.",""],[2,"301","4","Eco-Design Standards Review","reviewed to incorporate eco-design requirements, including the use of recycled materials.",""],[2,"301","4","Green Business Tax Incentive Support","economic instruments, such as GTFS, GITA and GITE will be leveraged to support businesses in producing green products and services.",""],[2,"301","4","Sharing Economy Model Promotion","More sharing economy models, including product-as-a- service will be introduced to encourage sharing the use of products and services as well as facilities.",""],[2,"301","5","Green Technology Adoption and Circular Economy Measures","Adoption of green technology in industries will result in more efficient resource-use and production cost savings.",""],[2,"301","6","Extended Producer Responsibility Regulation for E-Waste","a new regulation on household electrical and electronic waste (e-waste) will be introduced to implement the EPR for e-waste.",""],[2,"301","6","Extended Producer Responsibility Expansion to Packaging and Single-Use Plastics","The EPR approach will also be extended to cover other types and streams of waste, particularly packaging materials and single-use plastics.",""],[2,"301","6","EPR Regulatory and Monitoring Framework","relevant regulations, economic instruments and monitoring mechanisms will be put in place to enable producers and retailers to implement the EPR for other type of waste.",""],[2,"301","6","Producer Take-Back System and Polluter-Pays Support","Implementation of EPR will be supported through the take-back system by producers or brand owners as well as the adoption of the user-pay and polluter-pay principles.",""],[2,"304","1","Circular Economy Regulatory and Economic Instruments Framework","The circular economy promotes, among others, eco-design, ban of single-use plastics and utilisation of biodegradable plastic bags for organic waste.",""]],"411":[[2,"305","4","Review of Waste Import and Export Enforcement Legislation","Existing legislation, including Act 127 and the Customs Act 1967, will be reviewed to enable stringent and robust enforcement, monitoring and control of waste imports and exports.",""],[2,"305","5","Transboundary Waste Import Control and Enforcement","Following this, exporting countries will have to attain prior informed consent from importing countries before transboundary shipping of waste takes place.",""],[2,"305","5","Imported Waste Inspection and Verification Enhancement","In addition, on-site inspections and verification for all types of imported waste will be enhanced.",""],[2,"305","5","Illegal Waste Operator Tracking and Penalty Enforcement","Simultaneously, efforts to track and weed out illegal waste operators will be escalated and stiffer penalties imposed to curb illegal operations.",""]],"412":[[2,"305","6","Planetary Health Mainstreaming in Policy and Planning","planetary health will be mainstreamed in policies, and development planning and implementation",""],[2,"305","6","Environmental Health Prioritisation and Hazardous Substances Management","efforts will be intensified to prioritise environmental health as well as implement environmentally sound management of chemical and hazardous substances",""],[2,"305","7","Environmental Health Regulatory Review and Strengthening","In addressing environmental issues effectively, including emerging issues, Act 127 will be reviewed.",""],[2,"305","7","Household E-Waste Regulation and Clean Air Planning","These include the introduction of regulation on household e-waste, master plan on clean air and guidelines for managing end-of-life vehicles as well as green practice modules for chemical and scheduled waste industries.",""],[2,"305","7","Smart Environmental Enforcement Systems","Environmental enforcement efforts will be intensified and improved through smart surveillance and enforcement systems, online system for self-regulation among industries, hydrocarbon fingerprinting to address marine oil spills and environment geospatial information system.",""],[2,"305","7","Empowerment of Environmental Enforcement Task Force","the task force will be empowered to enforce Act 127 and the Water Services Industry Act 2006.",""],[2,"305","7","Pollution Carrying Capacity Studies","studies to determine the carrying capacity of the atmosphere, river and soil in absorbing pollutants, particularly in high-risk areas will be undertaken to facilitate enforcement efforts.",""],[2,"306","1","Environmental Impact Assessment Enhancement","The prescribed activities under the Environmental Impact Assessment (EIA) will be enhanced to strengthen environmental management.",""],[2,"306","1","Strategic Environmental Assessment Studies","studies on the effectiveness of the EIA and the introduction of the Strategic Environmental Assessment17 (SEA) will be undertaken.",""],[2,"306","1","Fisheries Act Revision for Coastal Impact Assessment","The Fisheries Act 1985 will be revised to incorporate impact assessment of coastal area development on the fisheries ecosystem.",""],[2,"306","1","Health and Social Impact Assessment Enhancement","health and social impact assessments will be enhanced to support evidence-based and risk-informed decision-making.",""],[2,"306","2","Cleaner Production Pollution Prevention Requirements","premise owners and developers will be required to prevent pollution or reduce its emissions at source through better preventive and emission control measures.",""],[2,"306","2","Industry Environmental Compliance Reporting Requirements","They will also be required to submit regular reports to the relevant authorities.",""],[2,"306","2","Environmental Standards and Compliance Training Programme","technical training in relevant fields as well as professional certification programmes for the industry players will be enhanced.",""]],"413":[[2,"307","4","National Disaster Risk Management Policy","A national policy on disaster risk management and multi-level disaster resilience plans as well as a national adaptation action plan will be developed.",""],[2,"307","4","Multi-level Disaster Resilience Planning","A national policy on disaster risk management and multi-level disaster resilience plans as well as a national adaptation action plan will be developed.",""],[2,"307","4","National Adaptation Action Plan","A national policy on disaster risk management and multi-level disaster resilience plans as well as a national adaptation action plan will be developed.",""],[2,"307","4","Integration of Climate and Disaster Measures into Development Plans","These will be integrated into the local, structural and sectoral development plans to improve planning and implementation of appropriate measures.",""],[2,"307","4","Geological Hazard Adaptation and Risk Reduction Framework","A framework will be developed to outline adaptation and risk reduction measures for geological hazards, including earthquake and submarine landslides.",""],[2,"307","4","Revision of Spatial Plans for Risk Reduction","These measures will be incorporated in the revision of all relevant spatial plans.",""],[2,"307","4","Integration of Scientific and Indigenous Knowledge","In addition, scientific and indigenous knowledge will be assimilated to improve planning and implementation of measures, which will address the complexity and dynamicity of the impact of climate change and disasters.",""],[2,"307","5","Integrated Resilience and Sustainability Approaches","Adoption of integrated approaches, combining structural and non- structural initiatives, will be expanded to enhance resilience as well as ensure sustainability and cost effectiveness.",""],[2,"307","5","Developer Hazard Mapping and Disaster Preparedness Requirements","developers will be further encouraged to include site hazard mapping, disaster preparedness plans and disaster insurance in project implementation.",""],[2,"307","5","Climate and Disaster Socioeconomic Impact Assessment","the socioeconomic impact of climate change and disasters will be quantified to better understand and manage the implications of such events.",""],[2,"307","6","Climate Adaptation and Disaster Risk Reduction Measures","based adaptation and risk reduction measures will also be enhanced through green cover expansion and coastal improvement as well as watershed, wetlands and river conservation.",""],[2,"307","9","Build Back Better Disaster Recovery Approach","The build back better approach will continue to be adopted as one of the disaster preparedness and recovery measures in enhancing resilience against climate change and disasters, hence protecting development gains.",""],[2,"307","9","Resilient Reconstruction and Development Standards","the reconstruction of damaged buildings and infrastructure as well as new developments will be required to adhere to the planning and development guidelines as well as resilient construction guidelines and building standards.",""],[2,"307","9","Regulation of Development in High-Risk Areas","new developments in high-risk, flood-prone and environmentally sensitive areas, including highlands will be strictly regulated.",""],[2,"307","9","Review of Building Codes and Retrofitting of Critical Infrastructure","existing building codes will be reviewed, while critical buildings and infrastructure will be retrofitted.",""]],"414":[[2,"311","2","Enforcement of Access and Benefit-Sharing Act 795","Act 795 will be enforced to ensure revenues generated from the commercialisation of biological resources and traditional knowledge are fairly and equitably shared among resource providers.",""],[2,"311","2","Capacity Building for Competent Authorities on Access and Benefit Sharing","the capacity and capability of the Competent Authorities at all levels will be enhanced.",""],[2,"311","2","Access and Benefit-Sharing Education and Awareness Programme","education and awareness programmes on access and benefits sharing will be enhanced for ILCs.",""],[2,"311","2","Traditional Knowledge Documentation Initiative","Existing traditional knowledge will be documented to safeguard the rights of the ILCs, while R&D&C&I and investment in bioprospecting activities will be encouraged to realise the value of traditional knowledge.",""]],"415":[[2,"296","8","Integrated River Basin Management Plan Implementation","Implementation of the Integrated River Basin Management (IRBM) Plans",""],[2,"311","4","Water Catchment and Riparian Habitat Protection","The gazetting and protection of water catchment areas will be intensified, while riparian forests and wetland habitats will be conserved and protected to ensure sustainability of water resources as well as reduce disaster risks.",""],[2,"311","4","Integrated River Basin Management Acceleration","Furthermore, the adoption of the IRBM approach will be accelerated in line with the Integrated Water Resources Management (IWRM) to maximise socioeconomic benefits, while conserving the freshwater ecosystem.",""],[2,"311","4","State Water Legislation Harmonisation","states will be encouraged to review and harmonise their respective water- related legislation based on the Water Resources Bill 2016 to ensure coherence and comprehensiveness of water resources management.",""],[2,"311","4","Federal Water Agency Governance Improvement","Governance of water-related agencies at the Federal level will be improved to strengthen the implementation of IWRM.",""],[2,"318","2","Integrated Water Resource Management Adoption","Accelerating the adoption of the Integrated Water Resource Management (IWRM) will be the foundation in transforming the water sector.",""],[2,"326","2","Water Sector Management Improvement","Management of the water sector will be improved by encompassing multidimensional approaches.",""],[2,"326","2","Stakeholder Participation and Water Governance Strengthening","Measures will be undertaken to enhance stakeholder participation, governance and decision-making as well as financial and infrastructure sustainability.",""],[2,"328","10","Integrated Centre for Water Data and R&D&C&I","Establishment of an Integrated Centre for Water Data and R&D&C&I",""]],"416":[[2,"311","7","Shared Responsibility for Green Growth Initiative","The Twelfth Plan will focus on strengthening environmental governance, scaling- up green financing and investments as well as instilling a sense of ownership and shared responsibility.",""],[2,"312","3","State Sustainable Development Task Forces","State governments will be recommended to establish a task force on sustainable development to monitor, assess and report the implementation and performance of sustainable development initiatives, including conserving biodiversity, addressing climate change and pollution as well as reducing disaster risks.",""],[2,"312","3","Environment and Climate Change Centres of Excellence","Centres of excellence on environment and climate change as well as biodiversity will be established by leveraging existing institutions.",""],[2,"312","4","Strengthening of the One-Stop Environment-Related Data Centre","the one stop environment-related data centre will be strengthened by improving data sharing among various stakeholders, including the private sector and CSOs to support better decision- making.",""],[2,"312","4","Greenhouse Gas Accounting Model and Database Establishment","a GHG accounting model and database will be established, while the disaster-related repository will be enhanced.",""],[2,"312","4","Disaster-Related Repository Enhancement","a GHG accounting model and database will be established, while the disaster-related repository will be enhanced.",""],[2,"312","4","Green Economic Model Development","A green economic model will be developed by leveraging the Green Economy Indicators and the System of Environmental- Economic Accounting for Malaysia to support macroeconomic planning and impact analysis.",""],[2,"312","5","Sustainable Development Talent Development Initiative","Efforts will be undertaken to develop talent that possess knowledge and skills in sustainable development to advance green growth.",""],[2,"312","5","Green Skills Investment Incentive","Both the public and private sectors will be encouraged to invest in developing talent with multiple skillsets, especially in green financing and environmental economy.",""],[2,"312","5","Triple-Helix Academic Programme Collaboration","In addition, triple-helix collaboration will be encouraged to enhance academic programmes in these areas.",""],[2,"312","6","Multi-Stakeholder SDG Engagement and Collaboration Platform","Engagements and collaboration with the private sector, academicians and CSOs will be intensified to ensure there are concerted and accelerated actions by all stakeholders in achieving the 2030 Agenda.",""],[2,"312","6","Regional and International Sustainable Development Policy Dialogue","Cooperation and policy dialogues on sustainable development at the regional and international levels will also be promoted to complement national efforts in accelerating the implementation of the 2030 Agenda.",""],[2,"312","6","ASEAN Net Zero Carbon Emissions Collaboration","In addition, collaboration among ASEAN countries to achieve net zero carbon emissions will be initiated.",""],[2,"312","6","SDG Indicator Data Expansion and Monitoring System","Data for SDG indicators will continue to be expanded and strengthened to monitor progress of the SDGs at the national, state and local levels.",""],[2,"312","7","Local Sustainable Development Task Force Establishment","local authorities will be encouraged to establish a task force on sustainable development to mirror the structure at the Federal and state levels.",""],[2,"312","7","Local Authority Capacity Building for Sustainable Development","The capacity and capability of local authorities will be enhanced to enable effective planning, implementation, monitoring and evaluation of sustainable development initiatives.",""],[2,"312","7","Sustainable Development Performance Rating Enhancement","sustainable development elements in the Sistem Penarafan Bintang Pihak Berkuasa Tempatan will be further enhanced to assess the commitments and improve the performance of local authorities.",""],[2,"312","7","Sustainable Development Financing Mobilization for Local Authorities","Local authorities will be encouraged to leverage funding from private and international entities, including matching grants to support the implementation of sustainable development initiatives.",""],[2,"313","2","SDG and ESG Mainstreaming in Economic Management","The public and private sectors, including financial institutions will be encouraged to adopt the SDGs and ESG principles.",""],[2,"313","2","Targeted SDG-Aligned Investment Strategy","Targeted strategies with clear accountability to further grow the share of investments that are aligned with the 2030 Agenda will be developed.",""],[2,"313","2","SDG Performance Monitoring Framework","Appropriate performance measurement framework will be put in place to monitor and evaluate the implementation of these strategies.",""],[2,"313","2","Public Sector SDG Budget Tagging System","For the public sector, this will also entail developing a budget-tagging system that is linked to the sustainable development objectives.",""]],"417":[[2,"314","2","Behavioural Change and Stakeholder Collaboration for Environmental Conservation","efforts will focus on steering behavioural changes, including adopting the behavioural insights27 approach.",""],[2,"314","3","CEPA Initiatives for Environmental Awareness and Behaviour Change","Communication, education and public awareness (CEPA) initiatives will be intensified to encourage mindset and behavioural changes as well as enhance shared responsibility in environmental protection, biodiversity conservation and disaster risk reduction.",""],[2,"314","3","Environmental Champions Empowerment Initiative","environmental champions will be identified and empowered as agents of change.",""],[2,"314","3","Environment-Related Curriculum Expansion","Experiential learning among students will be enhanced through the expansion of environment-related curriculum",""],[2,"314","4","Youth Environmental Awareness and Sustainability Participation Programme","Youth will be encouraged to actively participate in advocating environmental awareness and sustainability programmes",""],[2,"314","4","Training of Trainers for Teachers and Community Leaders","teachers and local community leaders will be equipped with appropriate skills through training of trainers' programmes",""],[2,"314","5","Amanah Lestari Alam Environmental Education Support Initiative","Amanah Lestari Alam, a company limited by guarantee, will be leveraged to support the implementation of environment and sustainability-related education initiatives in schools and higher education institutions as well as awareness programmes.",""],[2,"314","6","Behavioural Insights for Environmental Awareness and Sustainable Lifestyles","The behavioural insights approach will be adopted to steer mindset and behavioural changes, mainly through the provision of appropriate facilities, product labelling and reward system as well as incorporation in faith practices.",""],[2,"314","6","Stakeholder Collaboration for Behavioural Insights Adoption","Collaboration with various stakeholders will be strengthened to promote the adoption of behavioural insights.",""],[2,"314","7","Environmental Protection Dialogue and Knowledge-Sharing Platforms","Existing dialogues and knowledge-sharing platforms will be enhanced, and new ones will be created to promote a shared vision on environmental protection and conservation.",""],[2,"314","7","Community and Private Sector Environmental Participation Initiative","the involvement of communities and the private sector in environmental protection and conservation programmes will be further encouraged, including via technological innovations and social media.",""],[2,"314","7","Community-Based Resource Monitoring and Citizen Science for ILCs","The ILCs will also be empowered in the conservation of natural areas through community-based resource monitoring and citizen science28.",""],[2,"314","7","Friends of River Initiative Replication","The success of the Friends of River initiative by the community in supporting the protection, restoration and sustainable use of rivers will be replicated.",""],[2,"314","7","Private Sector Coordination for Conservation Financing","Contributions from the private sector, including financial institutions will be better coordinated to support efforts in implementing various conservation activities.",""]],"418":[[2,"318","2","Gas Market Liberalisation","In the Twelfth Plan, the sustainability of the energy sector will be further enhanced through the liberalisation of the gas market.",""],[2,"319","1","Energy Sector Sustainability and Diversification Measures","Efforts were undertaken to ensure sustainability of the energy sector through resource diversification, continuous investment in new infrastructure and technology enhancement.",""],[2,"326","2","Sustainable Energy and Water Utilisation Initiative","In the Twelfth Plan, emphasis will be given to the sustainable utilisation of energy and water to ensure security of supply as well as to create more economic opportunities.",""],[2,"326","2","Energy and Water Institutional and Regulatory Reform","Efforts will be undertaken to improve institutional and regulatory frameworks.",""],[2,"326","2","National Energy Policy Development","A comprehensive national energy policy will be introduced to strengthen the oil and gas and electricity ecosystems.",""],[2,"328","4","OGSE Industry Blueprint","Establishment of OGSE Industry Blueprint",""],[2,"329","1","Energy Sector Sustainability Initiatives","Initiatives will be focused to enhance the sustainability of the energy sector.",""],[2,"329","1","Oil and Gas Industry Growth Support","This will include ensuring the healthy growth of the oil and gas industry.",""],[2,"329","1","Electricity Supply System Reinforcement","The reinforcement of generation, transmission and distribution systems will further strengthen the electricity supply industry.",""],[2,"329","1","Market Liberalisation Communication Plan","A comprehensive communication plan on market liberalisation will also be developed to provide clear information to the energy fraternity and the rakyat.",""],[2,"329","5","Comprehensive Single Energy Policy","Two key initiatives will be implemented to address the energy cross-sectoral predicaments, namely the formulation of a comprehensive single energy policy",""]],"419":[[2,"319","1","Water Service Provider Financial Sustainability Strengthening","In the water sector, the financial sustainability of service providers was strengthened.",""],[2,"319","1","Water Infrastructure Upgrading and Expansion","Existing infrastructure was upgraded, while new ones were built to support increasing demand and improving access in rural areas.",""],[2,"319","1","River Management and Coastal Protection Initiatives","Furthermore, a number of physical and non-physical initiatives were implemented to strengthen river management and coastal protection.",""]],"420":[[2,"334","1","Public Consultation Platforms for Water Sector Transformation","Rakyat will be empowered to drive the transformation through the establishment of public consultation platforms, implementation of awareness-raising, advocacy and capacity-building (AACB) programmes as well as expansion of community-driven conservation activities.",""],[2,"334","1","Awareness-Raising, Advocacy and Capacity-Building Programmes","Rakyat will be empowered to drive the transformation through the establishment of public consultation platforms, implementation of awareness-raising, advocacy and capacity-building (AACB) programmes as well as expansion of community-driven conservation activities.",""],[2,"334","1","Community-Driven Water Conservation Activities","Rakyat will be empowered to drive the transformation through the establishment of public consultation platforms, implementation of awareness-raising, advocacy and capacity-building (AACB) programmes as well as expansion of community-driven conservation activities.",""],[2,"334","2","Public Consultation Platforms for Water Management","Public consultation platforms will be established at the state and district levels for active engagement as part of the water management system.",""],[2,"334","2","Capacity Building for Water Consultation Platform Members","Capabilities and skills of members will be enhanced, particularly in conflict resolution and negotiation to ensure the effectiveness of the platforms.",""],[2,"334","2","Strategic Communication Plan for Water Sector Transformation","A strategic communication plan will also be developed for the effective implementation of the water sector transformation.",""],[2,"334","3","Comprehensive AACB Programmes for IWRM","Efforts to enhance understanding of the IWRM will be intensified through the implementation of comprehensive AACB programmes.",""],[2,"334","3","Structured IWRM Training Modules","To ensure its effectiveness, structured modules will be developed for specific target groups.",""],[2,"334","3","Farmer Participation in Irrigation Infrastructure Management","In the agricultural sector, farmers' involvement in water resource management will be enhanced through their participation in the operation and maintenance of irrigation infrastructure.",""],[2,"334","3","AACB Support for Land-Use Decision-Making","The implementation of AACB programmes will help in decision-making for development, particularly in land- use change.",""],[2,"334","5","Environmental Education and Experiential Learning Enhancement","Environmental-related education, especially experiential learning, will be further enhanced through collaboration among educational institutions, civil society organisations (CSOs), the private sector and government agencies.",""]],"421":[[2,"334","4","Community-Driven Environmental Conservation Programmes","Community-driven programmes in environmental conservation will be increased to empower people to protect and conserve water resources as well as create socioeconomic activities.",""],[2,"334","4","Expansion of Tagal and FoR Initiatives","Various successful initiatives including the Tagal system and FoR programmes will also be expanded.",""],[2,"334","4","Water-Saving Behavior Campaigns","Campaigns to inculcate water-saving habits and precise water use among domestic users",""],[2,"334","5","Periodic Water Resources Status Reporting","Reports on the status of water resources will be published periodically.",""],[2,"336","3","Ecological Fiscal Transfer Mechanism Institutionalisation","The ecological fiscal transfer mechanism will be institutionalised by providing adequate funds and introducing an appropriate distribution mechanism.",""],[2,"336","3","River Ecosystem Services Assessment Requirement","state governments and local authorities will be encouraged to conduct assessments of the river ecosystem services8 before decisions are made on land-use change.",""],[2,"336","3","Payment for Ecosystem Services Mechanism","a mechanism will be established to ensure the payment for ecosystem services commensurates with the benefits derived and costs incurred from the services.",""],[2,"336","3","Green Technology Financing Scheme for Water Saving and Circular Economy","The existing Green Technology Financing Scheme will also be leveraged to inculcate water saving habit and promote circular economy practices among water-intensive industries.",""]],"422":[[2,"338","1","Circular Economy Implementation in the Water Sector","The circular economy concept will be implemented in the entire water sector value chain.",""],[2,"338","2","Scale-Up of Water-Efficient Product Use","The use of water-saving equipment labelled with Water Efficient Product Labelling Scheme (WEPLS) will be scaled up in government premises as well as promoted among domestic and industrial users.",""],[2,"338","2","Fiscal Incentives for Water-Efficient Products","Fiscal incentives and rebates will also be considered to further encourage usage of water-efficient products.",""],[2,"338","2","Green Building Water-Saving and Reuse Promotion","The green rating for buildings will be leveraged to encourage water-saving practices and water reuse in commercial premises, including hotels and shopping complexes.",""],[2,"338","3","Smart Water Management and Service Efficiency Upgrade","Smart technologies such as digital meters and sensors, geographic information systems as well as supervisory control and data acquisition system will be incorporated to improve water management and services efficiency.",""],[2,"338","3","Smart Water Applications for Provider-Consumer Communication","In addition, smart applications will be developed to establish direct and fast communication between water services providers and consumers.",""],[2,"338","3","Pilot Water-Smart City Project","To demonstrate the benefits of smart technology in the sector, a pilot water-smart city project will be implemented.",""],[2,"338","3","Smart Irrigation Modernisation Programme","In the agriculture sector, modern and automatic irrigation systems using smart technologies will be utilised to reduce wastage, improve efficiency, enable more accurate water distribution and increase productivity.",""]],"423":[[2,"346","2","Public Service Institutional Streamlining and Professionalisation Reform","the structures and functions of ministries and agencies will be reviewed and streamlined to establish a flatter organisation and reduce bureaucracy in the government administration.",""],[2,"346","2","Public Service Act for Clear Separation of Powers","A public service act will be introduced to ensure a clear demarcation of powers between Members of the Administration and civil servants.",""],[2,"346","2","Public Service Leadership Selection and Recruitment Improvement","strengthening the mechanism for the selection of key leaders will improve the overall performance of the public service.",""],[2,"351","5","Clarification of Roles and Responsibilities Between Political Leaders and Civil Servants","Ensure the delineation of roles and responsibilities between Members of the Administration and civil servants.",""],[2,"351","6","Key Leader Selection Mechanism Strengthening","Strengthen the mechanism for the selection of key leaders in ensuring a more effective public service delivery.",""],[2,"351","11","Public Sector Administrative Streamlining Reform","Reviewing and streamlining structures and functions of ministries and agencies to establish a flatter organisation, reduce bureaucracy, increase transparency and optimise the use of resources.",""],[2,"351","12","Public Service Act for Checks and Balances","Introducing a public service act to ensure more effective checks and balances between executive, legislative and judicial powers.",""],[2,"351","13","Key Leader Selection Mechanism Strengthening","Strengthening the mechanism for the selection of key leaders.",""],[2,"351","14","Professional and Managerial Officer Recruitment Mechanism Improvement","Improving the mechanism for recruitment of professional and managerial officers in various schemes in attracting the best talents.",""],[2,"351","22","Civil Service Resource Optimization and Rights Preservation","Optimisation of existing resources as well as preservation of rights and obligations of civil servants.",""]],"424":[[2,"349","13","Endowment Fund for Education Financing","Establishing an endowment fund to source funds from industry, matching grants, crowdfunding and waqf.",""]],"425":[[2,"369","12","PLWS Method Harmonization and Self-Assessment Framework","Measures will be undertaken to reconcile different methods of calculating PLWS to allow self-assessment by employers.",""],[2,"369","12","PLWS Monitoring Indicators Development","In addition, new indicators, which measure the linkage between profit, wage and productivity, will be introduced to monitor the effectiveness of this system.",""],[2,"369","13","Guidelines for Worker Welfare and Pay Equity in Firms","For this purpose, guidelines will be developed and disseminated to firms especially micro, small and medium enterprises (MSMEs).",""],[2,"369","13","Work System Reorganization Support for Firms","The guidelines will facilitate employers to reorganise their work systems to improve CE.",""],[2,"369","14","Employee Ownership Trust Adoption","Firms will also be encouraged to adopt new models for better distribution of profits.",""],[2,"370","1","Employee Ownership Sharing Models","sharing of firms based on a minimum number of employees will be introduced.",""],[2,"370","2","Trade Union Membership Expansion","Efforts to increase membership in trade union will be intensified to enable stronger bargaining power in wage negotiations.",""],[2,"370","2","Co-determination for Worker Representation","Co-determination approach will be introduced to allow worker representatives at the decision-making level.",""],[2,"370","3","National Wage Index Enhancement and Expansion","Continuous efforts to provide wage benchmarking will be undertaken by enhancing NWI.",""]],"426":[[2,"369","11","Female Labour Force Participation Promotion","The participation of more females in the labour force will be encouraged to improve employment sustainability.",""],[2,"370","10","Supportive Social Policies to Increase Female Labour Force Participation","Measures to increase FLFPR will be undertaken by introducing more supportive social policies.",""],[2,"370","10","Home-Based Economic Activities for Women with Secondary Education","Females with secondary educational attainment will be encouraged to participate in labour market through home-based economic activities while continuing with household responsibilities.",""],[2,"370","10","Mandatory Childcare Facilities for Employers","a new law will be introduced to mandate employers to provide childcare facilities, of which penalties will be imposed for those who failed to comply.",""]],"427":[[2,"373","4","Inquiry-Based STEM Teacher Training Programmes","Two teacher training programmes in inquiry-based education, namely Inquiry-Based Science Education (IBSE) and Inquiry-Based Mathematics Education (IBME) will be rolled out to improve teaching and learning approaches.",""],[2,"373","4","Digital-Enabled STEM Curriculum Reform","new and advanced STEM curriculum embedded with digital technologies will be introduced.",""],[2,"373","4","STEM For All School-Industry Linkage Programme","The STEM For All programme will be further promoted by facilitating linkages between schools and industries.",""],[2,"373","4","STEM Per Capita Grant Revision","The per capita grant for subjects under the STEM programme will be revised to provide adequate materials for students to conduct science experiments.",""],[2,"373","4","Science Laboratory Upgrading Programme","The science labs will be upgraded to ensure teaching and learning processes include hands-on science activities, which will be made compulsory.",""]],"428":[[2,"374","2","School Quality Assurance Enhancement","Quality assurance will be enhanced to ensure effective delivery of teaching and learning in schools.",""],[2,"374","2","School Inspectorate Autonomy Reform","The inspectorate of schools will be given greater autonomy to increase operational flexibility.",""],[2,"374","2","School Inspection Process Improvement","The current inspection processes will be improved to ensure every school is inspected at least once in every two years.",""],[2,"374","2","Inspectorate Training Expansion to Early Childhood and Community Agencies","The training of trainers for inspectorate will be extended to Taman Bimbingan Kanak-kanak (TABIKA) under the Community Development Department (KEMAS), Department of National Unity and Integration (JPNIN) and Department of Orang Asli Development (JAKOA) to ensure consistency of student outcomes.",""],[2,"374","4","School and Vocational College Infrastructure Upgrading","Measures will be undertaken to enhance the infrastructure of schools and vocational colleges in improving the teaching and learning environment.",""],[2,"374","4","Reconstruction of Unsafe School Buildings","All schools which are classified under the scale of six and seven in the School Building Condition Index25 and verified as unsafe by the Public Works Department will be rebuilt.",""]],"429":[[2,"374","3","Values-Based Teaching and Character Development in Schools","good values will be incorporated in all subjects beyond Islamic Education, Moral Education as well as Civic and Citizenship Education.",""],[2,"374","3","Value-Based Teaching for Student Character Building","Value-based teaching will be applied to inculcate character building and social interaction among students.",""],[2,"374","3","Review of Strategic Plans for Holistic Student Values Development","the related short- and long-term strategic plans will be reviewed to instil values and develop student character holistically.",""],[2,"374","3","Student Participation in Sports and Associations Promotion","Student participation in sports, associations and uniform bodies will be promoted to foster greater unity and understanding among students.",""]],"430":[[2,"376","7","TVET Digital Learning Strengthening Programme","During the Twelfth Plan, initiatives to leverage emerging technology in education will focus on optimising the digital learning ecosystem, strengthening TVET through digital learning and strengthening industry collaboration for greater innovation.",""],[2,"376","7","Industry Collaboration for Innovation Initiative","During the Twelfth Plan, initiatives to leverage emerging technology in education will focus on optimising the digital learning ecosystem, strengthening TVET through digital learning and strengthening industry collaboration for greater innovation.",""],[2,"377","4","Remote Learning Strengthening and Digital Skills Development for HEIs","The HEIs will strengthen remote learning approaches to ensure continuity in learning and teaching.",""],[2,"377","4","Digital Skills Upgrading for Higher Education Staff and Students","Academic staff and students of HEIs will be equipped with digital skills to further improve learning outcomes.",""],[2,"377","4","Higher Education Quality Assessment Reform","Measures will also be undertaken to improve the Rating for Higher Education Institutions (SETARA) and Malaysian Quality Evaluation System for Private College (MyQUEST), by incorporating technology indicator in the assessment criteria.",""],[2,"377","5","Smart Campus Development Initiative","All on-campus activities will also be geared towards creating a smart campus environment which include smart classrooms and labs, interactive learning and teaching using augmented reality (AR) and virtual reality (VR) technologies as well as digital student administration.",""],[2,"377","5","Shared Learning Spaces and Digital Resource Co-creation Review","In addition, the usage of learning spaces, including laboratories within HEIs, will be reviewed to promote sharing of resources and co-creation across disciplines and institutions through digital means.",""],[2,"377","6","Technology-Enhanced TVET Pedagogy","The use of emerging technologies such as VR, AR and AI will be leveraged to complement hands-on teaching activities, research and development conducted in laboratories and workshops.",""],[2,"377","6","TVET Curriculum Integration of Emerging Technologies","Pedagogies that embed these technologies will be incorporated in TVET curriculum.",""],[2,"377","6","TVET-Industry Collaboration Expansion","Meanwhile, collaboration between TVET institutions and industry will be intensified to provide more opportunities for instructors and students to apply latest technologies as well as experience actual industry operations and challenges.",""]],"431":[[2,"378","10","TVET Database Development Platform","A TVET database will be developed to enable BDA to support effective policy formulation and programme development and delivery.",""],[2,"379","1","Future Talent Development through Labour Market Realignment","The Twelfth Plan will focus on developing future talent by realigning the labour market and improving the quality of education and training programmes.",""],[2,"379","1","Education and Training Quality Improvement Programme","The Twelfth Plan will focus on developing future talent by realigning the labour market and improving the quality of education and training programmes.",""]],"432":[[2,"395","6","Data Sharing Regulatory Framework","Relevant regulations pertaining to data sharing will be put in place to address concerns relating to system interoperability, cyber security and technical standards.",""],[2,"395","6","Cyber Security Policy Streamlining","The cyber security ecosystem will be strengthened by reviewing and streamlining policies and initiatives across authorities.",""],[2,"395","6","Risk-Based Digital Technology Assessment","A risk-based approach in the development and acquisition of digital technologies, including network-ready products and solutions, will be adopted to identify potential risks and undertake mitigation measures.",""],[2,"395","6","Sharing Economy Regulatory Study","A study will be undertaken to recommend a regulatory framework in providing a conducive ecosystem for the development of the sharing economy including the gig economy.",""],[2,"396","4","Malaysia Cyber Security Strategy Implementation","the Malaysia Cyber Security Strategy (MCSS) will be implemented to spearhead efforts to manage cyber threats.",""],[2,"396","4","Strengthening of the Cyber Security Legal Framework","The cyber security legal framework will continue to be strengthened and the Cyber Security Act will be enacted.",""],[2,"396","4","MSME Cyber Security Adoption Support","During the Twelfth Plan, MSMEs will be encouraged to adopt cyber security measures and a secure digital environment in line with increasing digital adoption to grow businesses.",""],[2,"396","5","Cyber Security Awareness and User Guidance Initiative","This will include enhancing cyber security awareness initiatives through extensive promotional activities during the cyber security month, develop user guidelines for online and digital applications as well as increase training of the workforce on cyber security through a people-private-public partnership.",""],[2,"396","5","Internet Use Curriculum Module","the school curriculum will incorporate a module on the correct and acceptable ways to use the internet.",""],[2,"400","7","National Digital Identification Policy","A national digital identification policy will be developed to provide a comprehensive framework for building trust and security for digital transactions and movement of data.",""],[2,"400","7","Personal Data Protection Act Review","The Personal Data Protection Act will be reviewed to provide greater rights and control over personal data as well as clarity on personal data management using technology.",""],[2,"401","2","National Digital Identification Roll-out","The NDI will also enable innovative and value-added digital services that facilitate end-to-end business processes with digital signing.",""],[2,"408","4","Open Data Sharing Infrastructure Upgrade","Open data sharing infrastructure will be upgraded to enable accessibility of digital information by the public and private sectors, academia and the rakyat.",""],[2,"408","4","Personal Data Protection and Data Sharing Regulation Strengthening","Meanwhile, guidelines and regulations on personal data protection and data sharing will be strengthened to ensure data is safeguarded against cyber-attacks and unethical uses.",""],[2,"408","4","Ethical Framework for Technology Development and Use","An ethical framework and standards on technology development, deployment and utilisation will also be introduced to ensure responsible use of technology.",""],[2,"408","4","National Cyber Security Response Strengthening","The implementation of the national cyber security response, surveillance and supervision will also be strengthened to protect the nation against any possible cyber threats.",""]],"433":[[2,"417","5","Port Marine Resource and Vessel Traffic Monitoring Systems","Similarly, the PTP and Johor Port have implemented the Marine Resource Management System and Vessel Traffic Monitoring and Information System since 2018.",""],[2,"424","7","Preventive Road and Bridge Maintenance Programme","Preventive maintenance approach will be adopted to extend the lifespan of roads and bridges.",""],[2,"424","7","Pilot Preventive Maintenance Projects Using Advanced Materials","A number of pilot projects on preventive maintenance using advanced materials and innovative technology have proven that can increase the lifespan of roads.",""],[2,"424","7","Ultra-High Performance Concrete Bridge Upgrading","The UHPC will be used mainly in replacing and upgrading aged and narrow bridges.",""],[2,"426","2","Weigh-in-Motion Enforcement System","The Weigh-in-Motion (WIM) system will be used to improve enforcement of overloaded movers.",""]],"434":[[2,"434","7","Full-Pay Study Leave and Scholarship Programme","Continuous learning and capacity building among employees under the support group were encouraged through the introduction of a full-pay study leave with scholarship programme in 2017.",""],[2,"440","7","Civil Servant Training Module Enhancement","Moving forward, the training modules for civil servants will be further improved to ensure civil servants possess the traits of excellence required in effectively managing domestic and global challenges.",""],[2,"440","7","Civil Servant Leadership and Skills Development Programme","The training programmes will include aspects of grooming, inculcating positive attitude, developing leadership skills as well as knowledge enhancement and exposure to ensure civil servants stay relevant and competitive.",""],[2,"440","7","Civil Service Digital Literacy Initiative","With the acceleration of digital adoption, every civil servant is expected to be digitally literate by 2025.",""],[2,"441","5","Advanced Professional Development Training for Future Leaders","existing programmes to nurture future leaders such as the advanced professional development training will be strengthened",""],[2,"441","6","Civil Service Values and Ethics Training","The good values, patriotism and preparedness to serve beyond expectations will be instilled in the early stages of recruitment and periodically through-out the service.",""],[2,"442","1","Civil Servant Digital Acculturation and Change Management Initiative","the digital culture will be inculcated in the early stages of a civil servant's career, while change management initiatives will be introduced to increase knowledge, skills and use of digital services.",""],[2,"442","1","Public Sector Digitalisation Strategic Plan 2021-2025","The successful implementation of initiatives under the Public Sector Digitalisation Strategic Plan 2021-2025 will further enhance digital capabilities and competencies of civil servants.",""],[2,"442","2","Civil Service Upskilling and Reskilling Programme","The upskilling and reskilling of civil servants will be continuously undertaken to ensure they keep abreast with advancements in technology.",""],[2,"442","3","Specialized Expert Development Programmes","More programmes will be undertaken to produce experts in specialised areas, such as in economic planning, finance, international relations and negotiations, procurement as well as project planning and management.",""],[2,"442","3","Customised Training and Secondment Programme","customised training and secondment programmes will be provided to enhance exposure and enable these personnel to acquire technical skills in the relevant areas.",""],[2,"442","3","Public-Private Cross-Fertilisation Programme","cross-fertilisation programmes between public and private sector personnel will be expanded to broaden knowledge-sharing and develop subject matter experts.",""],[2,"442","4","Civil Service Future-Readiness Training Programme","Appropriate training will be provided to enable civil servants to be future-ready especially in performing new tasks and responsibilities arising from the advancement of technology.",""],[2,"442","4","Centralised Civil Service Upskilling and Reskilling Coordination Platform","all existing upskilling and reskilling training initiatives by different agencies will be regulated and coordinated by a single agency using a centralised platform.",""]],"435":[[2,"444","3","Cybersecurity Strengthening for Online Transactions","cyber security will be strengthened for all online transactions.",""],[2,"444","3","National Digital Identification Project","the national digital identification project will be introduced in early 2022 to accelerate the realisation of digital governance, promote inclusivity, reduce cost of access to services and enhance service delivery to the rakyat.",""],[2,"444","3","Government Digital Footprint Enhancement","The digital footprint will also be enhanced to ensure integrity, accountability and transparency are not compromised while accessing and sharing government documents online.",""],[2,"444","4","Local Authority Digital Service Delivery Upgrade","Local authorities will be encouraged to leverage on the existing MyGovernment portal to improve service delivery.",""],[2,"444","4","Local Authority Digital Infrastructure and Online Services Upgrade","it is important for local authorities to upgrade their digital infrastructure and online services.",""],[2,"444","4","Public Sector E-Payment Adoption","Agencies at both the federal and state levels will be encouraged to adopt e-payment methods.",""],[2,"444","4","Cashless Transaction Security Awareness Campaign","awareness on the security of cashless transactions will be enhanced to gain public trust.",""]],"436":[[2,"453","2","Holistic Border Security Action Plan","Focus is given on the implementation of a holistic action plan to enhance security at the border, introduction of a new policy for the defence and security industry, as well as wider usage of advanced technology in combatting crimes.",""],[2,"453","2","Defence and Security Industry Policy","Focus is given on the implementation of a holistic action plan to enhance security at the border, introduction of a new policy for the defence and security industry, as well as wider usage of advanced technology in combatting crimes.",""],[2,"453","2","Technology-Enabled Crime Prevention Initiative","Focus is given on the implementation of a holistic action plan to enhance security at the border, introduction of a new policy for the defence and security industry, as well as wider usage of advanced technology in combatting crimes.",""]],"437":[[2,"447","8","High-Impact Development Expenditure Prioritisation","Government allocations will prioritise high impact projects that generate higher multiplier effects in the economy.",""],[2,"447","8","Balanced Regional Development Allocation","At least 50% of the development expenditure will be allocated to six less- developed states, namely Sabah, Sarawak, Kelantan, Terengganu, Kedah and Perlis, to ensure a more balanced regional growth and reduce development gaps.",""],[2,"447","8","Connectivity and Basic Infrastructure Improvement","Most of the allocations will be channelled to improve connectivity and provide better access to basic infrastructure, amenities and services.",""],[2,"453","5","Regional Inclusion Funding Prioritization for Less Developed States","In allocating Federal Government funds, special attention will be given to Sabah, Sarawak and other less developed states to promote regional inclusion.",""],[2,"453","5","Infrastructure, Connectivity, and Social Services Upgrading","The provision of better infrastructure and connectivity, as well as improved access to social services and enhancement of defence, security and public safety will contribute towards uplifting the socioeconomic status of the rakyat.",""]],"438":[[2,"454","4","Rail-Road Network Integration for Multimodal Connectivity","This will be achieved through initiatives such as the integration of rail and road networks to provide better connectivity between airports, ports, industrial areas and cities.",""],[2,"454","4","Port Infrastructure and Services Capacity Expansion","In addition, the capacity of port infrastructure and services will be increased and the multimodal cargo movement approach with a single service provider will be adopted.",""],[2,"454","4","Multimodal Cargo Movement Single-Service Provider Model","In addition, the capacity of port infrastructure and services will be increased and the multimodal cargo movement approach with a single service provider will be adopted.",""],[2,"454","4","Public Transport Enhancement Programme","Public transport will also be enhanced to ensure better access to services and seamless connectivity for the rakyat.",""]],"439":[[2,"447","9","Government Asset Management and Maintenance Roadmap","A new roadmap and action plan will be formulated to improve asset management and maintenance of government infrastructure and facilities.",""],[2,"447","9","Strengthening of the JKR Facility Management Unit","the existing Facility Management Unit in JKR will be strengthened to coordinate maintenance initiatives across ministries and agencies as well as ensure compliance with asset maintenance standards.",""],[2,"447","9","Priority Funding for Public Asset Maintenance","allocations for the maintenance of roads, buildings and other public assets will be given higher priority.",""],[2,"447","9","Expanded Opportunities for Small Contractors in Maintenance Projects","more opportunities will be provided to small contractors.",""]],"440":[[2,"516","16","Integrated Weather and Flood Forecasting and Early Warning System","Integrated weather and flood forecasting and early warning system",""]]}});